window.FWN_NECROPOLIS_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_NECROPOLIS_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":2201,"title":"Chapter 2201: Chapter 2156.1: Heavenly Dao As Master","paragraphs":["Chapter 2156.1: Heavenly Dao As Master","“Have you really decided?” Motong asked solemnly.","Lu Yun nodded—he had no other choice. Even though he’d built a new world and even if he killed the will of nothing, that would still not fully resolve everything.","Only when he became the heavenly dao could he safeguard the world of immortals!","He didn’t know how the heavenly dao in that world of immortal dao civilization had been murdered, but he knew that he didn’t fight alone. When he returned as the heavenly dao, Qing Yu, the little fox, Pangu, Hongjun, Daoist Yuyu, Fuxi, and the others would all come to him to protect him.","The heavenly dao needed heirs as well.","However, he would lose everything before fully awakening as he underwent the baptism of three thousand reincarnations.","“This is the way left by the mistress,” Motong took a deep breath. It was thanks to everything left by Mo Yi that she was able to break through the will of nothing during this time on the Origin Continent and find herself again.","“Thanks to certain powers that you command through the Tome of Life and Death, the heavenly dao might pass its legacy onto you through other means. But no matter what, you must hold on. Make sure you do not break through ahead of time and find yourself again, no matter the cost!”","Otherwise, the heavenly dao would see the various karmic ties on Lu Yun and treat him as a threat to that world. It would swiftly kill him without second thought!","Lu Yun nodded. “Can I ask... how does Ouyang Du end up?”","That was the only person he cared about in this world. Perhaps his ending had long been written, but Lu Yun still couldn’t help but ask.","Motong sighed heavily. “Ouyang Du... is the Darkness city lord.”","Lu Yun paused, then silently nodded with a smile.","“Then, I shall follow in the mistress’ footsteps. I hope... that you can protect my home.” Tears flowed from Motong’s eyes as the black power of reincarnation blossomed out of her body. She turned into reincarnation and scattered upon the wind, erased from existence. There was only an innocent and kind little girl left in the world—Xiangliu Yunge—one who held endless hopes and dreams for the future.","The power of reincarnation swallowed Lu Yun and turned him into different people again and again. He endured life after life until his core essence was sealed by the three thousand iterations of reincarnation. It sank into a deep sleep and awaited a far off awakening.","When he left, the original Yushi Moli began to recover. The power of reincarnation resurrected him, and he lived out his life as he would’ve before.","......","Waves of incredible pain assaulted Lu Yun’s nerves like the tides. He looked dumbly at the ceiling and didn’t move.","“Where am I? Why does it seem so familiar...” He stared off into space, feeling that something extraordinarily important to him was slipping through his fingers. Deep sorrow bloomed in his heart, but it was quickly swept away by something that couldn’t be explained.","“Ah! You’re awake, young master! I’ll tell milord!” A surprised voice that was mostly filled with disappointment echoed in his ears, followed by a pitter-patter of hurried footsteps.","“Was that Lan’er? Mm, yes, that was my maid Lan’er!” Lu Yun’s mind began to clear up. “So it was all a dream! It was all an absolutely ridiculous dream!”","He shook his head and propped himself up, wanting to shift to a seated position. Pain drummed into his head as he did so and he flopped back onto the bed.","“Oh yeah, I fought Ouyang Shenghe yesterday and he beat me up before I had a chance to hit him...” Still a bit out of sorts, Lu Yun raised his arm with effort and gently patted his head, trying to pat his memories back into order.","BOOM.","The exquisite, yet fragile door to Lu Yun’s meditation chamber split open, raining down as a pile of shards as a tall and muscular figure appeared in front of him. Towering at a little over two meters with broad shoulders and a sculpted back, the figure carried itself with an authoritative bearing. He looked forty years old, but there was an indescribable look in his eyes, one that spoke of witnessing many years.","He was the strongest powerhouse in Darklake Cultivation Empire and Lu Yun’s grandfather—Lu Tianling.","“Ah!!” Lu Yun first paused blankly when his grandfather arrived, then howled with indignity. “Grandfather!! My door was made of rosewood and it cost me ten upper rank spirit stones! Ten upper rank spirit stones!!”","He bounced upright with a surge of strength from somewhere and shook with outrage as he stared at Lu Tianling.","The man froze sheepishly. Although he was the strongest in the empire, he doted on his grandson without limits. Nothing was too much for Lu Yun and the sky was the limit.","But he suddenly recalled something the next second and glared, “Are, are you trying to send me to an early grave?! You only possess seven levels of qi refinement, but you fought Ouyang Shenghe! Have you had too much of life?!”","“Hehe, grandpa, aren’t I just fine?” Lu Yun reached out a shaky hand and rubbed his face with a grin.","“Just fine?!” Lu Tianling snorted explosively. “Do you know that you’ve been in a coma for three months?!”","Lu Yun blinked when he heard “three months” and quieted down. Light sparkled in his eyes as he thought over something.","“Your meridians have been shattered and your dantian broken. You’re not much better than your second uncle now. His Majesty pities you for being the only heir to the Lu Clan and sent us a Nineturns Profound Life Pill. You will recover from all of your wounds if you take it,” Lu Tianling sighed and took out a jade bottle, tossing it onto the bed before he left.","......","Lu Yun stared motionlessly at the jade bottle on his bed.","Lu Tianling was the strongest heavyweight within Darklake Cultivation Empire; he was their battle god. His cultivation was latter nascent spirit and he dominated the lands, intimidating neighboring countries so much that they didn’t dare attack.","Lu Yun was the family's only male heir. At sixteen years old, his potential was stunning and he possessed a constitution perfect for cultivation. Unfortunately, he was by nature lazy, negligent, and good-for-nothing. Instead of focusing on cultivation, he was much more fascinated by affairs in the bedroom and idled on the streets all day to bully others.","In other words, he was a bonafide hooligan, thug, and scoundrel.","Lu Yun’s parents passed away when he was young and he was Lu Tianling’s only grandson. The old master spoiled his grandson to the extreme. While he immensely disliked Lu Yun’s typical behavior, he very rarely reined it in. He chose to overlook what he could and only occasionally lectured a few words.","That served to encourage Lu Yun’s indolence and troublemaking, until he grew into a young man completely out of control.","Three months ago, he ran into the Ouyang young master on the streets of the capital. The Ouyangs were one of the seven greatest families of the capital and Ouyang Shenghe beat Lu Yun within an inch of his life after a verbal altercation. If it wasn’t for the Lu experts arriving in the nick of time, Lu Yun would’ve died in that fight.","As it were, Lu Tianling had to exhaust the family wealth to save a grandson whose meridians were broken and dantian crippled. Even so, Lu Yun spent three months in a coma until he awoke today.","“I’ve been out for three months?” Lu Yun raised his eyes to look at a fearful maid off to the side.","“Yes, yes. Young master’s been unconscious for three months. Today is the last day of the third month...” Lan’er squeaked back.","“Good, good, very good!” Lu Yun nodded with a smile. Lan’er wished she could faint dead away.","“My cultivation has been crippled, my meridians are severed, and my dantian has been shattered, correct?”","“Yes... that is what imperial physician Yuan from the palace said...” Lan’er was almost in tears. This charmingly handsome gentleman who seemed he should be cultured and considerate was anything but with how he treated people. Lan’er was fifteen this year and had served Lu Yun for three years. After three years of being cursed at and hit, she had a bone deep fear of the young master.","“Good, very good, fantastic!” Lu Yun nodded and his smile deepened. “Take this Nineturns Profound Life Pill and give it to your father.”","He picked up the jade bottle and threw it at Lan’er. She froze on the spot after catching it, not knowing what to do.","Has Ouyang Shenghe beaten the young master into an idiot..? Wild thoughts ran through her mind. Her father He Wuhen was once the grand steward of the Lu complex. His cultivation was latter golden core. Someone had shattered his golden core three years ago when he protected Lu Yun and he was crippled forevermore.","The Nineturns Profound Life Pill was divine medicine for wounds. All injuries were immediately healed with it and a crippled cultivation would recover in a short period of time. It was priceless and without a market in Darklake.","“I told you, take it,” Lu Yun said lazily, but Lan’er heard a bizarre note of barely suppressed... joy? in her master’s voice.","Dazed by the turn of events, she left the room clutching the bottle with her hands.","......","“Is it all true?” Lu Yun sank into deep thought.","In the three months that he’d been unconscious, he’d dreamed an enormous dream. In that dream, he experienced three thousand reincarnations and journeyed three thousand worlds. He fully underwent all of the love, hate, joy, and grief to be found in those worlds, as well as a variety of successes and failures.","After three thousand worlds, he came to a strange place and saw a person in white—one who called himself heavenly dao!","Experiencing three thousand reincarnations and traveling through three thousand worlds had all been his work. In that strange place, Lu Yun hailed the heavenly dao as his master and became his disciple!","Lu Yun had believed everything without question when in the dream. Who else would have the ability to send him through three thousand reincarnations in three months, but still ensure that he retained his sense of self if not the mythical and transcendent heavenly dao?","He’d thought it all just a dream when he first awoke, but when he heard the timeframe of three months and his crippled cultivation, he truly believed that everything in the dream was real.","The heavenly dao had reminded him when he left that, “Thou hast slept for three months and thy cultivation ended. When thou awakes, cultivate the ‘Nine Chapters of Dao’. Remember to abstain from any healing pills or medicines, remember that most urgently!”","Lu Yun then returned to reality with a flash of golden light, but he somehow thought that he’d experienced more than three thousand lifetimes. There’d been another, a critical three thousand and one!","But as soon as the thought of a three thousand and one reincarnation rose in his mind, an agitation deep within his heart brewed and suppressed the notion, expunging it.","Lu Yun was still Lu Yun, the sole grandson of the battle god of the Darklake Cultivation Empire.","He wasn’t the Lu Yun from the future, here in this world with a mission.","“The Nine Chapters of Dao? The cultivation method that the heavenly dao practices?” A trace of anticipation rose in his heart. The previous Lu Yun had hated cultivation. He meditated a few times a year only because his grandfather forced him to.","Seventh level qi refinement at sixteen years old was just run of the mill. If it wasn’t for his astounding potential, he would only be third level. Darklake was an empire of cultivators, even the regular people knew how to refine qi. Seven levels of qi refinement was nothing to write home about.","But now, Lu Yun had journeyed three thousand worlds and experienced three thousand lives. Though his core essence didn’t change, his heart and mind were greatly tempered. He was no longer the lackadaisical son of a rich family that he once was, he knew the importance of cultivation.","Thus, he remained curled up in bed and slowly closed his eyes.","Golden light sparkled in and out of sight in his sea of consciousness. Although his cultivation was crippled, his consciousness as a cultivator was still present. When his consciousness touched the golden light, a mental explosion of sound echoed through his mind."]},{"number":2202,"title":"Chapter 2202: Chapter 2156.2: Heavenly Dao As Master","paragraphs":["Chapter 2156.2: Heavenly Dao As Master","The Nine Chapters of Dao!","There were nine chapters to dao and nine revolutions to dao. The dao heart was eternal and the great dao traversed through all!","Kaboom!","The golden light exploded and emanated an extremely profound presence. A cultivation method slowly unfurled in Lu Yun’s mind.","The Nine Chapters of Dao were the chapters of Seeing Dao, Knowing Dao, Questioning Dao, Understanding Dao, Obtaining Dao, Becoming Dao, Executing Dao, Heavenly Dao, and Great Dao!","The first chapter of Seeing Dao abruptly expanded into strange runes hovering in front of him and filtered into Lu Yun’s mind.","Unbidden, his hands formed a hand seal and the energy of heaven and earth roiled soundlessly toward him. They created a massive vortex of energy that surged into Lu Yun’s body. Once inside of them, they turned into murky air currents that circulated through the air. His shattered meridians and dantian were repaired and made whole through the air currents.","Not only that, but his repaired meridians were wider, bigger, stronger, and more durable than before. The remnants of medicines within him were fully refined by the air currents.","As the grandson of the strongest powerhouse within Darklake, Lu Yun normally ate various pills and medicines like he would candy. But as his cultivation was subpar, he was unable to refine their effects and they accumulated in his body.","Not that these gray air currents swept through his body, they completely refined the lingering medicines and expelled what they could not.","......","The Lu complex, Lu Tianling’s residence.","A seventy year old elder who could only be described as haggard knelt on the ground in doddering fashion. He held a jade bottle in his hands.","“Milord, this old servant has erred!” The elder raised the jade bottle high and placed his forehead on the ground, not daring to raise his head.","Lu Tianling sighed. “Old He, you’ve accompanied me on and off the battlefield for at least one hundred years.”","“This old servant is fortunate enough to follow the lord!” He Wuheng raised his head and panted for breath.","He was originally one of Lu Tianling’s generals and dominated the battlefields with his lord. When the borders of Darklake Cultivation Empire quieted down twenty years ago, he returned home to be the Lu Clan’s family steward.","“You wouldn’t have become like this if it wasn’t for you protecting Yun’er three years ago,” Lu Tianling intoned. “I send Lan’er to follow at Yun’er’s side as a way to protect her.”","As the Lu grand steward, He Wuheng had possessed immense authority backed by unquestionable strength. Since Lan’er was his daughter, she was the recipient of endless attention and favor. But after losing his cultivation, it was only a matter of time before varying thoughts brewed in the motley crew of people intermingled with the family.","Lu Yun was eccentric and tyrannical—though sending Lan’er to him consigned her to certain suffering, it also meant that no one in the household would dare think of taking any action against her.","“This old servant thanks milord!” He Wuheng kowtowed again.","“Since Yun’er gave you this pill, you should take it. You’ve laid low for three years. If you can recover overnight and attain a nascent soul, that will be an immense help to the family.” Lu Tianling waved the old servant off.","“But...” He Wuheng protested.","“There is no but.” Lu Tianling fixed his eyes on the southeastern skies over the Lu complex. An imperceptible vortex of spirit energy was slowly gathering there. That was where Lu Yun’s residence was.","Hu Weheng looked in the same direction as well. Though his cultivation was crippled, his consciousness remained and thus he could still sense the abnormalities in that direction.","“Yun’er does not need this pill.” Lu Tianling smiled with great happiness.","“But the second master...” He Wuheng paused before finishing his sentence.","“Chi’er’s injuries are the result of an extraordinarily malicious restriction. His body cannot endure the medicinal effects of the Nineturns Profound Life Pill.” Sorrow flashed through Lu Tianling’s eyes.","......","Lu Yun remained lying on the bed in the same position as before. One hand flitted through various hand seals while the other held a piece of upper rank spirit stone. Tendrils of white air currents flowed from the spirit stone down Lu Yun’s arm, entering his body to bolster the gray currents within.","The gray currents inside Lu Yun had formed a complete circulation that were perfectly cycled rebirth and decline.","Pfft!","Lu Yun’s left hand was suddenly empty as the fist-sized spirit stone crumbled away into dust. The remnants floated to the bed while his storage ring flashed another upper rank spirit stone into his hand.","Upper rank spirit stones were exceedingly valuable spirit stones in a world of cultivation. Golden core cultivators ordinarily trained with mid rank spirit stones. One upper rank stone was sufficient for one month’s worth of cultivation.","But Lu Yun had demolished an upper rank spirit stone in less than one hour! Thus, the terrifying might of the Nine Chapters of Dao were readily apparent.","Humm.","The gray energy within his body shuddered when Lu Yun digested his second spirit stone and surged toward his dantian.","Whoosh!","The golden light that’d hovered in his consciousness all this time also shot into his dantian and became one with the gray currents. An enormous “dao” character appeared in his dantian. This was a sign that the first turn of the first chapter of the Nine Chapters of Dao—Seeing Dao—was well underway.","His cultivation was fully recovered to his previous seven levels of qi refinement. Lu Yun took a deep breath and jumped down from the bed.","Glittering illumination from the stars poured through the windows and reflected off of Lu Yun’s face. A handsome and charming young man, his eyebrows were straight and angled sharply upward. Bright eyes twinkled like the night sky and a finely pronounced nose hung in the center of his face. A smile that carried hints of laziness constantly played on his thin lips.","But at the moment, sharp killing intent glared out of his eyes.","“Ouyang Shenghe... The Ouyangs and other families in Darklake have schemed against the Lus for a very long time. A few dozen Lu golden core experts have all had their cultivation crippled because of me—some even died on my behalf. This young master will take these up against all of you one by one!”","The current Lu Yun was no longer the spoiled young master from three months ago. After traveling through three thousand worlds in his dreams, he carried the memories of three thousand lives on him—all of their relationships, grudges, successes, triumphs, and suffering. He’d experienced all that life had to offer in all its iterations, which made the schemes of his current life easy to decipher.","Anyone in the Lu Clan could see through them, but Lu Yun had bumbled ignorantly through life and was constantly used by others. He sapped the clan’s resources for his unawareness and brought down a fatal blow to the family three months ago!","Lu Tianling had certainly paid more than just a bit of wealth to heal his grandson’s wounds and retain his life.","“In that case, this young master will keep you company and see who gets toyed to death first,” Lu Yun breathed out portentously and calmed himself. He sat down cross-legged again and slowly circulated the gray air currents within his body.","These currents weren’t the true qi of cultivators in the qi refinement stage, nor were they the true origin of cultivators in the foundation establishment stage. Rather, they were the more sophisticated level of Hongmeng true qi.","Hongmeng true qi was much higher quality than true origin. After all, Lu Yun’s Nine Chapters of Dao were an unparalleled method from the heavenly dao itself.","Rumble!","The hazy character in Lu Yun’s dantian trembled and emanated a current of profound presence. Something new appeared in his mind—combat art of heavenly dao, Petrification!","Those with weaker cultivation levels than the user were frozen forever. Those on the same level were frozen for three breaths. Those stronger than the user, but less than two levels higher, were frozen for a breath. Those stronger than two levels over the user would not be affected.","The two levels meant two cultivation stages!","“Doesn’t... doesn’t this make me invincible? I can kill people stronger than me!” Lu Yun’s eyes widened with incredulity. Two cultivation stages!","This was most definitely a combat art from the heavenly dao!","However, he didn’t let it go to his head. After journeying through three thousand worlds and equipped with the memories of three thousand lifetimes, he wasn’t so immature as to think that a single combat art made him unmatched in the world.","Any sort of existence would have its flaws. That applied without exception to the combat arts of heavenly dao. He could already think of it being possibly negated if his opponent wore a powerful defensive treasure on them.","“Darklake Cultivation Empire is just a third rank cultivation empire. That makes it a primitive backwater in a corner of the world. Thus, Petrification is enough to make me undefeated in this land...” A keen light shone in Lu Yun’s eyes as he analyzed the situation. “So there are nine turns each to the nine chapters. Each breakthrough I make results in a turn, and each turn will grant me a new combat art of the heavenly dao.”","He calmly assessed the situation, refraining from letting his astounding gains go to his head. All things in life were equal—as strong as the heavenly dao combat arts were, they also consumed an incredible amount of energy.","Lu Yun sat down cross-legged and reentered meditation, seeking to increase his store of Hongmeng true qi.","......","When the sun rose in the east, Lu Yun emerged from meditation and shook out his clothes. He summoned Lan’er to help him wash up and walked out of his residence.","The maid looked at him with a complicated expression. Her father had taken the Nineturns Profound Life Pill and fully recovered from his injuries.","Whoosh!","A black figure flashed to his side when he strode out of his yard and took a ramrod straight stance next to him. It was a new guard that his grandfather had arranged for him—Lu Xian. Initial golden core, that was the core battle strength of the empire since Darklake was a third rank cultivation empire. Their strongest powerhouses were nascent soul, but those were few and far in-between in the land.","Many golden core guards had once followed by Lu Yun’s side, but they were all dead or injured. Lu Xian looked roughly twenty years old and wore no expression on his stiff face. A sharp air wrapped around him, like he was a newly sheathed sword that could emerge at any second to kill.","At the same time, Lu Yun’s powers of observation were far more than what they used to be. He could tell with a quick glance that Lu Xuan’s cultivation was the result of a secret art. If no other fortuitous opportunities found him, this would be the limits of his cultivation in this life.","He paused, inclined his head at Lu Xuan, and headed for the family vaults.","“Lu Yun? You’ve just recovered from your injuries. What are you doing out and about instead of resting?” An elder named Lu Jiu stood guard at the vaults. At latter golden core, he frowned when he saw the young man.","“Thank you for your concern, elder. I have fully recovered.” Lu Yun smiled and headed into the vaults.","“Halt!” Lu Jiu interposed himself between Lu Yun and the doors. “Everything of value has been sold off. What are you doing here for?”","He spoke stiltedly and with great sorrow. Lu Yun was an unvarnished wastrel in everyone’s eyes. Lu Tianling had established the clan one hundred years ago and it’d once been the most glorious, greatest family of the empire!","But thanks to Lu Yun’s youthful ignorance and ludicrous behavior, he was constantly used by their enemies. The magnificent family swiftly declined over a handful of years.","Lu Yun glared at Lu Jiu and ignored the elder, walking straight into the vaults. They were protected by an enormous formation that attacked anyone who approached it—even nascent soul stage cultivators. But since he was Liu Tianling’s beloved grandson, he naturally knew how to bypass it.","Lu Xuan stood guard outside.","“The Ouyangs, Yuwens, and Chus... I am not Lu Yun if I don’t rip all of you up by the roots!” Lu Yun clenched his fists as he looked at the empty shelves.","The vaults were tremendous and used to be filled with countless treasures, spirit herbs, medicines, ores, and natural resources. But now, only a few dimly glowing things were left on a few racks."]},{"number":2203,"title":"Chapter 2203: Chapter 2157.1: Lu Second Master","paragraphs":["Chapter 2157.1: Lu Second Master","All of the spirit herbs, medicines, and pills within the vaults had been consumed. The rest of the rare ingredients and materials had been sold off. As for spirit stones, only a diminutive pile of one hundred upper rank spirit stones were left in a corner.","Lu Yun sighed and placed the stones in his storage ring. He surveyed the shelves and transferred a few more things to his ring before walking out of the vaults.","Lu Jiu looked on lividly outside. The vaults had been empty enough already, but were completely bare after Lu Yun picked over them. There was nothing left anymore.","Ultimately, the elder sighed and departed without another word. However, Lu Yun fully registered his look of disappointment before he left.","......","When Lu Yun returned to his meditation chamber, he shut the door tight and took out a few items from his storage ring. Pelts of monster beasts, spirit cinnabar, and a spirit qi brush. These materials that he’d just retrieved from the vaults were low level ingredients for talismans.","He’d found great success in some of his three thousand lifetimes and stood at the peak of his world. He’d also met with incredible failures and died to enemies, or lived out his life in mediocrity. But in each of the worlds and lifetimes, he’d mastered a skill or gained precious experience.","In one of his lifetimes, he stood at the top of a world as its talisman grandmaster, making talismans his great dao.","Lu Yun held an upper rank spirit stone with one hand and the brush in the other, swishing graceful runes onto the monster beast pelts.","There were four levels to the dao of talismans. Fourth and lowest level utilized red ink and yellow paper—those were ordinary talismans.","Third level was his current creations. It required spirit cinnabar ink, a spirit qi brush, and runes written into the pelts of monster beasts. These could be called spirit talismans.","Second level was jade talismans, using jade and spirit stones as their base. They were incredibly powerful talismans that Lu Yun could not attempt to make with his current cultivation level.","First level was the legendary talismans from the void—it used the energy of heaven and earth to create talismans in the air. This was a mythical ability that not even the Lu Yun of three thousand worlds ever accomplished.","He focused solely on directing his Hongmeng true qi to etching talisman after talisman. Sweat beaded his forehead and soaked through his back. Being seventh level qi refinement, he was far from adequate for creating spirit talismans. His Hongmeng true qi, however, was of such high quality that it made up for this shortcoming.","Crack!","The upper rank spirit stone in his hand cracked with a crisp sound and trickled to the ground as a pile of shards. Expressionless, he summoned another upper rank spirit stone into his hand with a flash from his ring.","A full day passed; Lu Yun didn’t stop until the sun set in the west. There were five hundred talismans in his storage ring and he wouldn’t have stopped if he hadn’t run out of ingredients.","“Just a few hundred low level spirit talismans are enough to exhaust me. If Shan Quan and Yu Lei found out about this, they’d laugh their heads off at me.” Lu Yun gave a long exhale as he wiped off his forehead and took off his drenched shirt. “Ai, worlds in dreams... worlds in dreams. Were they just fantasies of my dreams or real worlds?”","He looked out the window at the night sky, a forlorn expression on his face. Another memory struggled deep in his heart. However, it couldn’t shift the slightest bit due to being strictly sealed away.","That memory brought not loneliness, but sorrow.","......","Another night passed and a new morning dawned.","Lu Yun fully recovered after a night of rest and took a deep breath when he opened his door, gazing upon the rising sun. He expelled putrid air from his stomach.","“Time to collect some debts.”","The second he walked out of his yard, Lu Xuan appeared by his side like a ghost. Lu Yun remained oblivious as he headed out of the Lu residence.","\"And where is the great young master Lu off to?” sounded a sarcastic voice.","Lu Yun stopped, turning around to beam at a man in white who’d emerged from the inner residence. “Aiya, it’s second master Lu! What brings you here, second uncle?”","The man looked to be thirty years old and of thin frame. His complexion was pale and his steps unsteady. He was plainly a mortal.","He was the second master of the Lu Clan—Lu Xiaochi. His name had once been known throughout the empire as a stunning genius and he’d coalesced a nascent soul at thirty years old. He was the foremost genius of Darklake Cultivation Empire.","Lu Xiaochi was Lu Tianling’s foster son and Lu Yun once loathed the sight of the man. He didn’t think Lu Xiaochi was part of the family at all. Yet, three years ago, when he antagonized a rival that he couldn’t afford to offend, Lu Xiaochi had laid down his life to protect his nephew when the rival came knocking. His meridians were broken and he lost all of his cultivation after that.","If it hadn’t been for the emperor issuing a decree, both Lu Xiaochi and Lu Yun would’ve been beaten to death from that encounter.","But what kind of person was Lu Yun? The previous Lu Yun had been a complete ingrate without a conscience to speak of. Not only was he not thankful for his uncle’s help, but he frequently cursed at Lu Xiaochi for being crippled trash after the fact.","“Second uncle?” Lu Xiaochi blinked with incredulity. “Did you just call me second uncle?”","“You’re my grandfather’s son, not his daughter. Am I supposed to call you second aunt instead?” Lu Yun shrugged and headed for the main doors.","“Stop right there!” Lu Xiaochi couldn’t resist stopping the boy. Lu Yun’s altercation with Ouyang Shenghe three months ago had gravely set the family back and shaken its foundations. Lu Tianling used qi from his nascent soul to yank Lu Yun back from the jaws of death.","Now that the boy had recovered, he was certainly going out to cause more trouble. The current Lu Clan was full of holes and weaknesses—they couldn’t endure any more problems!","Lu Yun stopped and looked at Lu Xiaochi with bafflement.","“Did you take all of the remaining things from the vaults yesterday?” the Lu second master demanded lividly.","“Well, how can one do business without some capital?” Lu Yun responded as flippantly as usual.","“Do business? You’re going to the Ruyi Club, aren’t you?” Lu Xiaochi snorted.","The Ruyi Club was the capital’s largest gambling den. Frequented by idle wealthy scions like Lu Yun, it was one of the three biggest money making operations in the city. The other two—Rouge Pavilion and Beast Colosseum—also counted Lu Yun among their frequent customers.","“Ahem...” Lu Yun coughed awkwardly and responded seriously, “Second uncle, I’m the family’s eldest young master at the end of the day. How would I go to a place like that? Your nephew is indeed going out to do business today!”","“Do business? Very well, your second uncle will accompany you and see just how you do business.” Lu Xiaochi enunciated his title, feeling that the sun would rise in the west tomorrow. How was Lu Yun calling him his second uncle?","“Ah, that would be wonderful!” Lu Yun grinned broadly and didn’t decline. He gestured for his uncle to go first.","Lu Xiaochi brandished his sleeves and swept out the door.","......","Being the capital of Darklake Cultivation Empire, Dark City bustled with activity on a daily basis. Given its name, the empire was filled with cultivators. However, setting foot on the path of cultivation was easy, but building one’s foundations was difficult. Most of the cultivators in Darklake were of the qi refinement stage—the lowliest of societal castes.","Only when one reached the foundation establishment stage could one ride a sword and shake off the identity of a civilian. One could join the army and achieve great deeds in battle, receiving rewards of spirit stones and pills to win further glory with cultivation.","The castes were strictly defined and closely adhered to within the empire. If a civilian didn’t meet with unique opportunities, they would be a civilian for the rest of their lives and spend their days toiling away.","Hence, most citizens focused on cultivating and accumulating wealth. They typically bought a Foundation Establishment Pill when they reached ninth level qi refinement and joined the army after breaking through.","They were now in times of peace after Lu Tianling led the one million strong army in battle twenty years ago, butchering Tianlong Empire’s army of one million and two hundred thousand soldiers at Tiger Suppression Pass. His might traveled to the four corners of the land and no one dared raise the banner of war on Darklake Empire anymore.","Peace and prosperity was upon Darklake. Its population numerous, hale, and hearty. Dark City thronged with people and overflowed with activity.","Lu Yun wore white robes and waved around a gentleman’s fan of pale gold. He seemed urbane and genteel at a glance, but all that changed when he expanded his fan. A scene of pornography was drawn on the instrument—quite vivid and lifelike in its reproduction.","Lu Xiaochi ground his teeth when he saw the fan, but the little bastard waved it around proudly on the streets. Completely oblivious, he was patently very satisfied with the picture.","A vibrant market was located on a street not too far from the Lu residence. All sorts of wares and trades abounded, but a hush stole over it when the Lu young master sauntered in. Smiles froze on everyone’s faces, merchants and customers alike.","“What’s this doombringer doing out here? Didn’t the Ouyang second master beat him to death?”","“I thought so too! Old general Lu stormed the Ouyang residence because of him, killing one of their nascent soul experts and two of the latter golden core powerhouses!”","“Did he come back from the dead?”","“Nah, Ouyang Shenghe probably showed him mercy and didn’t beat him to death...” Gossip flurried through the crowd as people parted ways like the tides. The past three months had been the happiest of their lives in the capital.","“Heh heh, it looks like this young master still commands quite some respect from people,” Lu Yun chuckled with his nose in the air.","Meanwhile, Lu Xiaochi wanted to find a hole to crawl into. Couldn’t the kid see the looks of disgust that the crowd was sending him? The Lu second master knew a bit of Lu Yun’s actions, but it was another thing to witness his nephew’s behavior for himself.","“You, the one selling flame fruits. Come here.” Lu Yun randomly crooked his finger at a middle-aged man with an honest look on his face and a carrying pole across his shoulders.","etvolare's Thoughts","My sanity was severely tested in May. I spent a very good portion of it cussing behind the screen. Please review, leave comments, get a random person on the street to read NECRO or otherwise Imma chuck my head lol. Not only have we gotten the second reset in 20(?) chapters, chapter lengths are about to get RIDICULOUS."]},{"number":2204,"title":"Chapter 2204: Chapter 2157.2: Lu Second Master","paragraphs":["Chapter 2157.2: Lu Second Master","The middle-aged man could do nothing but present himself in front of Lu Yun as ordered. The young man reached out and took a flaming red fruit from the baskets hanging off the carrying pole. He crunched noisily after taking a bite.","“Although this flame fruit isn’t a spirit fruit, it tastes not bad.” A nodding Lu Yun smacked his lips.","“If the gentleman likes, this humble one can give you all of these fruits,” the trembling man offered with fear and reluctance.","“Lu Yun!” hectored the Lu second master, unable to accept what was happening in front of him.","Lu Yun paid his uncle no mind and cocked his head, sizing up the seemingly honest and simple man. A gentle smile played on his lips. “Yo, you’d win an Oscar if you were on Earth.”","“An Oscar? What is that?” Both the Lu second master and middle-aged man blinked when they heard the unfamiliar word.","Lu Yun reached out and gently caressed the man’s face.","Smack!","He suddenly wound his hand back and slapped the man across the face. How could the latter stand up to Lu Yun when he was only six levels qi refinement? Not to mention that he didn’t dare offer any resistance.","He spun around on the spot and spat out several teeth before falling to the ground. Lu Yun swiftly followed up with a few vicious stomps on the downed man.","“How dare you piece of shit try to fool this young master with a flame fruit?! Do you really think I’m a beggar??” Lu Yun cursed as he kicked and beat the man.","“Mercy, mercy, sir! This humble one will never dare do so again, never!” the man wailed as he suffered a torrent of blows.","“Lu Yun!” The Lu second master could no longer bear what he was seeing and ran forward to stop his nephew. He wasn’t the only one, many cultivators in the surroundings also itched to rush forward and teach the bully a lesson.","But they all quieted down when they saw Lu Xuan standing ramrod straight next to Lu Yun. That was a golden core powerhouse!","Lu Yun stopped when he saw Lu Xiaochi draw near. Having lost all of his cultivation, his second uncle was less than a cultivator now and could not withstand the strength of someone at seven levels qi refinement.","“You may go,” Lu Xiaochi said with a frown when he saw Lu Yun pause his abuse.","“Yes, yes, yes, thank you second master! Thank you!” The middle-aged man forfeited his carrying pole as he scrambled off to the side.","“Halt! Did I say you could go? Lu Xuan!” Lu Yun tilted his head back and called out lazily. His guard flashed out like a ghost, returning with the middle-aged man dangling from his hand like a dead dog.","Lu Xuan was a deathsworn raised by Lu Tianling to be Lu Yun’s guard. He obeyed the young man’s commands without question or an inkling of hesitation.","“This young master is too poor these days. Hand over your storage bags, rings, or whatever.” Lu Yun cocked his head like a ruffian and lazily regarded the honest man.","The Lu second master’s expression was wooden. As they said, to know a man by reputation was not as good as meeting him face to face. It was always far better to see someone in person than to hear of them from others.","Lu Yun was called the pestilence of Dark City and he well deserved the title. But when Lu Xiaochi heard his nephew demand the vendor’s storage bags and rings, he sighed all the same.","Lu Tianling was wise and awe-inspiring, yet his only grandson failed so spectacularly to live up to expectation and was so magnificently incompetent!","Storage bags were regarded as more precious items in Darklake Cultivation Empire. How would a civilian of the qi refinement stage afford one? Storage rings were even more valuable, not even wandering cultivators of golden core might possess them.","Only children and disciples of powerful families such as Lu Yun would own them, yet he was demanding them from a qi refinement civilian?? This nephew of his was beyond ridiculous!","What the Lu second master failed to notice was a hint of true panic that flashed through the man’s eyes when he heard the demand.","“You’re not going to hand them over, are you?” Lu Yun cackled and smacked the vendor again, then manhandled him roughly in search of the items. When he fished out a storage bag the size of a palm from the man’s robes, he lightly slapped the latter’s dantian.","Color drained from the man’s face as his dantian was destroyed and his cultivation crippled.","“Lu Xuan, throw him into the sewers.” Lu Yun waved the man away with distaste. “The fuck, you hollered and danced in front of me with a pole of flame fruits for four years. Do you really think this young master’s gone senile and lost my memory, that I can’t remember you? You may enjoy the act, but I’m completely over it.”","There was no light left in the man’s eyes anymore. Lu Xuan grabbed him and vanished with a quick jump.","“Don’t you think you’re out of line, Lu Yun??” Lu Xiaochi shook with fury. Seeing that Lu Yun had retrieved a storage bag from the man’s robes, he thought that Lu Yun had done the deed because he desired the man’s wealth.","“The dude was pretty rich—there’s a storage ring inside his bag. Tsk tsk,” Lu Yun clucked his tongue when he found a stage ring inside the bag.","“What a pity that the man was only one step away from establishing his foundations. He was fortunate enough to obtain a senior’s storage ring and could’ve joined the army, but it’s all empty dreams after encountering a hooligan like you,” Lu Xiaochi sighed when he saw the ring.","Meanwhile, Lu Yun chuckled at his second uncle’s words.","“Second uncle, this thing’s interesting. You can have it.” Lu Yun retrieved a blue stone the size of a fist from the ring and tossed it at Lu Xiaochi. The man blinked as he reflexively caught the stone.","“This is... a communication stone?” Lu Xiaochi paused. When he looked up again, he saw only Lu Yun’s back and Lu Xuan sticking to him like a shadow.","“Lu Yun, do you know what this is?” Lu Xiaochi quickly caught up to his nephew.","“That was the only thing inside the storage ring apart from spirit stones. I have no use for it, so you can have it, second uncle,” Lu Yun said casually.","Lu Xiaochi sighed inwardly. He’d thought that his nephew had suddenly grown a brain, but it seemed to be pure coincidence. Communication stones were exceedingly rare and, in fact, restricted items within the empire. Only the army could use them; it was an incredible crime for civilians to possess them. Ordinary families wouldn’t pass messages through communication stones.","It was normal for a sheltered noble scion like Lu Yun not to recognize it. But since Lu Xiaochi had followed Lu Tiangling since he was a child and fought by the war god’s side, he naturally recognized the communication stone.","“It’s just a rock, there’s no need to make a big deal out of it.” Lu Yun waved him off. “If second uncle likes it, you can have it. There are only a few mid rank spirit stones inside the storage ring... Man, even the storage bag is more valuable...”","Lu Xiaochi smiled wryly at Lu Yun’s sigh and placed the stone inside his robes. He was certain now that it was a happy coincidence that his nephew had crippled the vendor. The vendor was also a spy that an enemy family had planted near the Lus.","“I’m so hungry, let’s go eat at Immortal Gathering.” Lu Yun rubbed his stomach and looked at the sun in the sky.","Another wave of resignation struck Lu Xiaochi. Immortal Gathering was Dark City’s biggest restaurant and it belonged to one of the seven great families—the Mo Clan. The Mos were, without a doubt, the foremost family in the city. They were the largest beneath the imperial family.","The Lus were able to meet them toe-to-toe, and more, when the former was in its prime. But the Lu Clan now boasted of only Lu Tianling and no other nascent soul powerhouses. If it wasn’t for Lu Tianling hanging on for dear life, the Lus would likely immediately collapse and become a third-rate family.","“Huh? What’s that?” Lu Yun’s eyelids jumped when they took a few steps out and saw a pill pavilion of immense scale. Its signboard proclaimed it to be the “Lingtian Pill Pavilion”.","“When did this Lingtian Pill Pavilion appear?” Lu Yun frowned.","“This pavilion belongs to the Ling Clan, they opened shop when you were unconscious,” Lu Xiaochi explained when he saw Lu Yun’s expression. “Your grandfather is heavily depleted right now, so don’t provoke the Lings.”","He couldn’t help warning since the Lings were also one of the seven great families and stronger than the Lus.","“Pfft,” Lu Yun curled his lip. “My grandfather is called Tianling, but this pavilion is Lingtian. They’re doing this on purpose! Hmph!”","He snapped open his pornographic fan with a loud crack and sauntered into the pill pavilion.","Behind him, Lu Xiaochi smacked himself on the forehead. What was the point of saying all that to the kid? The Lings and Lus didn’t have a conflict of interest and appeared to be friendly with each other on the surface, but Lu Yun had secretly clashed with many of their sons under the table.","There was no one apart from Lu Tianling who could keep this young master in check. The Lu second master absolutely lacked that ability.","......","The general manager of Lingtian Pill Pavilion started when Lu Yun sauntered in, then smirked with barely imperceptible derision.","“Look who’s arrived, it’s young master Lu! Come in, come in! Ah Lian, serve tea!” He quickly welcomed their latest guest with a wide smile.","“You’ve got some nerve calling yourself the Lingtian Pill Pavilion,” Lu Yun said leisurely as he looked around.","There were quite a few cultivators in the pill pavilion, but they scattered like startled birds when they saw Lu Yun. He was the only customer left in the massive hall within the blink of an eye.","“Not at all, not at all. Young master Lu is always so humorous.” The general manager smiled a smile that didn’t reach his eyes.","“Alright then, give me five hundred of the third rank King Qi Pill,” Lu Yun demanded after brief thought."]},{"number":2205,"title":"Chapter 2205: Chapter 2158.1: Prodigal","paragraphs":["Chapter 2158.1: Prodigal","There were nine ranks to pills and medicines—first rank was the lowest, ninth rank was the highest.","Third rank was already a premier rank in Darklake Cultivation Empire. Being able to come up with five such pills would be an enormous feat, to say nothing of five hundred pills. Thus, Lu Yun’s demand was the height of unreasonableness.","“Five hundred third rank pills? Sir Lu and young master Lu, do you have too much time on your hands? Surely you have better things to do,” the general manager's sneer deepened. He might show some respect for Lu Yun’s identity in ordinary times, but Lu Tianling had just exhausted his nascent soul to save Lu Yun. The old general was gravely injured, and if this only pillar of strength fell, then the entire Lu Clan was done for.","“I just happen to have a ton of time and energy on my hands today, what of it?” The petulant tyranny of a prodigal scion appeared on Lu Yun’s face when he saw the general manager’s expression.","Lu Xiaochi closed his eyes when the general manager talked back to his nephew. As he thought, the kid was here to pick a fight.","“Lingtian Pill Pavilion sure speaks loudly, huh!” Lu Yun suddenly darted forward and slapped the manager across the face.","The grand manager was latter foundation establishment, but he registered with shock that his body seemed to be gripped by an invisible hand. He couldn’t move and his internal energy was completely confined. Even his thoughts seemed to be grinding to a halt!","Smack!","All he could do was watch as Lu Yun’s hand descended on his cheek. Without the protection of internal force, his left cheekbones shattered and he spewed out all of his teeth.","Then, the grand steward flopped to the ground without another word and fainted dead away.","“How dare you offend this young master?! You’ve plainly had enough of living! Lu Xuan, smash everything!” Lu Yun surreptitiously took out a few talismans from his storage ring and flung them into the surroundings. The talismans twinkled and vanished out of sight.","Bam bam bam!","Several nearly imperceptible explosions later, the defensive formations surrounding Lingtian Pill Pavilion fell without resistance.","Since Lu Xuan had been given orders, he immediately leapt into action. His fingers formed a hand seal, shooting out a bolt of radiant sword brilliance that rampaged through the spacious structure.","“Lu Xuan, you blithering idiot!” Lu Yun shrieked with pain. “Just smash the restrictions and whatever around the shelves, what are you doing destroying the pills and medicines for?! They’re all spirit stones!”","Lu Xuan’s eternally stoic expression flickered when he heard his master’s anguished howl. He quickly adjusted his actions and redirected his sword light to attacking the restrictions around the pills instead.","Lu Yun relieved the general manager of his storage ring and placed it into his own. He then swiftly collected the exposed pills and medicines on the shelves.","Hovering outside the door, Lu Xiaochi’s jaw dropped. His nephew really was out to do business, but the business of beating and robbing others!","Lingtian Pill Pavilion had swiftly expanded after its grand opening three months ago and was one of the top five pill pavilions in the capital. It boasted of unfathomable pills and wealth—its general manager’s storage ring was a miniature walking treasury.","“Who is the cretin that dares stir up trouble in my clan’s pill pavilion?!” A furious roar echoed throughout the building as a flying sword shot out of the air, aimed at Lu Xuan.","The deathsworn remained expressionless as his hands flickered through sword seals. His careening sword light immediately altered direction to block the flying sword and dueled it in a nearby corner.","A middle-aged man swiftly charged out of an inner office. Bearing a cultivation level of initial golden core, he was the family steward in residence at the Lingtian Pill Pavilion.","Dark City was the capital of Darklake and innumerable heavyweights walked its streets. No one could’ve ever imagined that anyone would brazenly commit robbery in open daylight. Lu Yun was likely making history with his visit to the Lingtian Pill Pavilion!","There was only an initial golden core steward holding down the fort and the building’s defensive formations were casually installed. Given that it hadn’t been long since the pavilion’s opening, much of its protective measures were incomplete.","“Stop wasting time, kill him!” Lu Yun shouted at his guard while busily collecting everything he laid eyes on. He ignored the Ling steward after casually pointing at him.","Pfft!","Lu Xuan’s sword light crashed through the steward’s sword and chopped his head off. Lu Xuan himself blinked at the outcome, unable to comprehend what had just happened. They were of the same cultivation level, so how had his opponent died so easily?","Lu Tianling had employed secret arts to raise Lu Xuan’s cultivation to golden core—it was an entirely different notion compared to the steward’s cultivation. The Ling steward was a core figure of the Ling Clan and had solidly walked the path of cultivation to reach his current heights. His foundations were solid and he bore a very high likelihood of rising further.","Even Lu Xuan knew that if the fight dragged on, it would be he who died, not the steward.","Despite the unexpected, Lu Xuan remained composed. He was just Lu Yun’s guard and the family’s deathsworn. There were many things that he didn’t need to think too deeply about.","Lu Xiaochi’s heart sank to see Lu Xuan execute a golden core Ling steward. There was no redeeming the relations between the two families now. The Lus had just expanded their family fortune and was making enemies everywhere. Lu Yun well deserved his reputation of being the scourge of Dark City!","Lu Xiaochi’s lips trembled and he shook from fury, but found nothing to say.","Nothing held Lu Yun back after he disposed of the steward. He likewise relieved the other of his storage ring and then charged into the inner offices of the pill pavilion.","Lu Yun departed from Lingtian Pill Pavilion after one hour passed, stroking his storage ring with immense satisfaction. The city guards were dispatched during this time and rushed to the scene. Upon seeing the livid Lu second master, however, they quietly returned to their posts without taking any action.","Although Lu Xiaochi’s cultivation was crippled, he still commanded high respect in the army. Not to mention, they were located near the Lu family residence and the Lu second master was also here. There was nothing that the city guards dared undertake.","By the time the Ling Clan received word of the day’s happenings, their Lingtian Pill Pavilion was a pile of rubble.","“Lu Yun, are you trying to destroy the Lus?!” Lu Xiaochi shuddered as he looked at his highly self-satisfied nephew.","“Eh? Destroy the Lus? Why do you say that, second uncle?” Lu Yun blinked. “Your nephew’s come into a huge sum of wealth and will be using it to replenish our vaults. How is that destroying the family?”","“You...” Lu Xiaochi bit off with frustration, “You’ve fully offended the Lings! There will never be peace between the Lings and Lus now!”","“Was there peace between us before?” Lu Yun raised his eyebrows. “Second uncle, how were you crippled?”","Lu Xiaochi paused.","“You were injured by the Nineheavens Pagoda—the foremost faction of the fourth rank cultivation empire, the Dark Orchid Empire. I’m not idiotic enough to provoke someone like that,” Lu Yun shrugged.","His second uncle stared wordlessly at him.","“But an easy target? Let’s hit ‘em where it hurts! That’s how your nephew is—I pick on the weak and avoid the strong, hehe.” Lu Yun grinned broadly.","“Hoi, young master Lu! There you are, I’ve finally caught up to you!” A young man a few years older than Lu Yun huffed and puffed up to them. Two servants were hot on his heels.","“Haha, Yu Shuai! It’s been a while, but you look as good as ever!”","The young man was second master Yu Shuai of the Yu Clan, one of the seven great families of the capital! Just as the “shuai” character of his name encompassed good looks, he was as handsome as he was named. A strapping young man, it wouldn’t be hyperbole to call him the best looking of the capital.","There were seven great families of Darklake Empire that ranked beneath the imperial family—the Mo, Ouyang, Yuwen, Ling, Zhao, Yu, and Lu Clans. There were six to begin with, the Lu Clan was a later addition and Lu Tianling its first patriarch.","As good-for-nothing as Lu Yun usually was, he still had a few close friends that they all got up to no good with. Second young master Yu Shuai of the Yu Clan, for one, and third young master Zhao Chenguang of the Zhaos","However, birds of a feather flock together and like begets like. Seeing Lu Yun’s character was to know the character of his friends. Lu Yun, Yu Shuai, and Zhao Chenguang were categorized as the three pestilences of Dark City.","“Hahaha!! I’m nothing compared to young master Lu!” Yu Shuai stuck his thumb up at Lu Yun. “You keep the lowest of profiles at home, but kick in the Lings’ shitty pavilion as soon as you walk out! Come come come, I hear that you’ve recovered. These are the medicines that I’ve prepared for you!”","Yu Shuai waved his servants forward; they placed a massive chest taller than their master in front of Lu Yun.","Yu Shuai had received word when Lu Yun woke up, yet Lu Tianling wasn’t the sort to welcome the profligate friends of his grandson. He’d refused to let Yu Shuai into the residence, so when Yu Shuai heard that Lu Yun was out on the streets, he’d quickly come with the chest.","“Um, eh, uh...” It felt like something was stuck in Lu Yun’s throat. “My dear Yu Shuai, why don’t you put these things in a storage ring? What are you hauling them around for?”","He didn’t know what to say when he looked at the chest several heads taller than his friend.","“Heh, this makes my present much more sincere!” Yu Shuai guffawed.","Lu Yun laughed as well and waved the chest into his storage ring, then cracked the pornographic fan open again.","“C’mon, Chenguang’s set up a banquet at Rouge... uh... Immortal Gathering.” A proud Yu Shuai spontaneously thought better of their destination when he saw the foreboding Lu second master off to the side. One of his servants slipped off toward Rouge Pavilion when he cast meaningful glances at them."]},{"number":2206,"title":"Chapter 2206: Chapter 2158.2: Prodigal","paragraphs":["Chapter 2158.2: Prodigal","Although Lu Xiaochi’s cultivation had been crippled and his consciousness mostly gone, he still exerted a certain degree of authority when it came to the prodigal sons of the capital. He was once the legend of the empire, after all, whether in terms of cultivation or other areas.","While Lu Tianling was the commander-in-chief of three armies at the battle of Tiger Suppression Pass twenty years ago, it’d been Lu Xiaochi who was the vanguard and led the armies from the front!","He was the executioner of the million strong army from the Tianlong Empire!","Thus, Lu Xiaochi’s influence in Darklake was unquestionable, particularly among the younger generation. Even devoid of his cultivation, he remained still the idol of many.","A renowned thug of Dark City, Yu Shuai was as docile as a kitten in front of Lu Xiaochi. Likely the only person who dared disrespect the man was his treasure of a nephew.","“C’mon, let’s walk around! Us brothers haven’t seen each other in a few months, we’re in no hurry to go to Immortal Gathering!” Lu Yun flung his arm around Yu Shuai’s shoulders like he hadn’t seen anything. The two pounded each other in the back as they strolled through the city’s streets.","But with Lu Xiaochi present, Yu Shuai refrained from putting a toe out of line. He was deeply terrified of earning the once legendary character’s disgust. Lu Yun, however, didn’t care at all. He behaved the same as usual and did whatever he wished. He was even more over the top than he typically would be.","The two finally turned to the direction of Immortal Gathering when the south soared high in the southern sky.","Bam!","A figure bounced out of the restaurant’s front doors when they reached it.","Bam bam bam!","Another three were kicked out.","“The fuck, how dare a couple small fry run afoul of me! I’ll have your entire family’s heads for this!” A slightly juvenile, but highly arrogant voice traveled out of the door. A muscular man nearly three meters tall darted out of Immortal Gathering.","His thick arms and legs rippled with muscles, his back and shoulders were equally broad. He was like a moving mountain and his height nearly twice that of Yu Shuai’s. But when one looked at his face, one was greeted with a strange dissonance.","Large, limpid eyes were set in a fair face that tapered off at the chin. Faint eyebrows arched over thin lips that were set in a natural pout. The tender face seemed to default to a shy smile...","If this face was found in a young boy, that would make for a charming young man. If it was found in a young girl, she would grow up to be a stunning beauty of the nation. But in a strapping man the size of a building... It was a very odd sight that couldn't be put in words.","He was one of the three scourges of the capital—the Babyfaced Hulk, Zhao Chenguang.","“Mercy, Master Zhao! Mercy!” The people who’d been kicked out of the restaurant scrambled back to the young man and hugged his boots, bursting into loud tears.","He kicked them away again when he saw Lu Yun and the others, cursing irritably, “Get out of here and don’t cross my path again!” Zhao Chenguang let them off the hook so easily because his friends were here. Otherwise, this would’ve been only the beginning.","“Heh, young master Lu and Yu Shuai, you guys are finally here. I’ve been waiting for a long time!” He snuck a careful look at Lu Xiaochi and didn’t dare greet the Lu second master.","“C’mon c’mon, let’s go eat! I’m starving!” Lu Yun grabbed Zhao Shenguang’s arm without further ado and dragged his two friends upstairs, wholly ignoring his uncle.","......","Immortal Gathering was the foremost restaurant of Dark City. It belonged to the Mo Clan and other branches could be found in other empires.","Although cultivators had no need for food, the dishes served by a renowned restaurant such as Immortal Gathering were no ordinary fare. They offered spirit beasts seasoned with spirit medicines—their cuisine could increase a cultivator’s internal force and consolidate their cultivation.","Cultivators did not eat in the higher ranked empires, instead partaking of spirit grains. Those were coalesced from the energy of heaven and earth and further made into spirit cuisine. That was immensely helpful for cultivation, making the act of eating another act of cultivation.","However, Darklake Empire lacked both spirit grain and cuisine.","There were three floors to Immortal Gathering. The first and second were mass seating, the third was private rooms. Lu Yun and his companions were the most noble of personages in the empire, so they naturally wouldn’t mix with the general public in the first two floors. They headed straight for the third floor.","Private rooms filled the third floor. The surroundings were elegant and spirit qi abounded. Graceful young women flitted through the hallways to bring dishes to the customers.","Bam!","A human-shaped object rolled down the stairs when Lu Yun and the others reached the stairway to the third floor.","“Who did it?! Who dares hit one of mine?!” Zhao Chenguang flew into a rage when he identified that it was one of his followers.","“Young master, young master, someone’s taken our room!” someone wailed from upstairs before they were also thrown downstairs. It was Zhao Chenguang’s other follower.","“Bastard!” he roared and charged up the stairs.","Lu Yun and Yu Shuai looked at each other, a hint of cruelty appearing in the latter’s eyes. He followed close behind Zhao Chenguang and charged up to the third floor. Meanwhile, Lu Yun remained uncommonly quiet, but he frowned.","“Hahaha, your room? Zhao Chenguang, I saw it with my own eyes that you weren’t the person originally sitting here!” rang another more tyrannical voice.","“Yuwen Chenghu!” Lu Yun’s brows snapped together and he quickly followed his friends.","Yuwen Chenghu was the second young master of the Yuwen Clan, one of the seven great families of the Darklake Empire. He was quite strong, having reached initial foundation establishment at eighteen years old. At the very least, he was far superior to the half-hearted cultivator that was Lu Yun.","Yuwen Chenghu was also a major prodigal scion of the capital, but even the good-for-nothings had their own cliques. Yuwen Chenghu, the Ling Clan, and Ouyang Clan stood allied with each other. They caused no end of trouble for Lu Yun’s clique in regular times. Even some of his previous guards had been crippled over the course of clashing against them.","Of Lu Yun’s friends, Yu Shuai was eighth level qi refinement, Zhao Chenguang ninth level, and Lu Yun was the weakest at seventh level. None of them had reached foundation establishment, so none of them would be a match for Yuwen Chenghu if it came to a fight.","Lu Xiaochi rubbed his temples, finally understanding how his nephew spent most of his days. It was a mixed assortment of lawlessness on the streets, bullying others, and fighting the other profligates in town. It was an endless repeat of ludicrous actions that never stopped.","How was this thug descended from the wondrous Lu Tianling? What would his elder brother and sister-in-law think if they could see how their son was?","Lu Yun set foot onto the third floor with Lu Xuan in tow. Yu Shuai and Zhao Chenguang stood side by side, their difference in height starkly contrasting each other. They faced off against a room full of people.","A gentleman in white held a folded fan outside of it. Elegantly poised, he was Yuwen Chenghu, the second young master of the Yuwen Clan.","“Zhao Chenguang, Yu Shuai. How dare two pieces of trash dare raise your hands against me?” Yuwen Chenghu snorted when he saw Lu Yun arrive. “So young master Lu is here too. The Dark City’s three pieces of trash are here!”","“You’re fucking asking for it!” Zhao Chenguang possessed an explosive temper and was about to rush forward, but Lu Yun forcefully stopped him in his tracks.","“Who you calling trash?” Lu Yun cocked his head.","“Trash means you three, of course.” Yuwen Chenghu’s white robes shifted gracefully in the air, their finesse an easy complement to his pride.","“Oh,” Lu Yun nodded. “I think you’re trash too, but why are you referring to yourself in the second person?”","“I... what?? You!!” Yuwen Chenghu understood the insult this time and turned bright red with fury.","“You called yourself trash, not us. You admitted it yourself.” Lu Yun shrugged.","Yu Shuai and Zhao Chenguang roared with laughter when they grasped the joke.","“It’s interesting that a cripple like you can still be so cocky,” came another voice from the room. “What, did my second brother not beat some sense into you three months ago? Look at you running around again and yapping your head off.”","“So you’re the blockhead who’s inside.” Lu Yun raised an eyebrow. The other person inside was the third young master of the Ouyang Clan—Ouyang Shengmu.","Ouyang Shenmu was a remarkably talented cultivator who was a similar age to Lu Yun. He was already at foundation establishment and could very likely reach golden core before twenty years old. Ouyang Shenmu was a bonafide genius and a leading example to the rest of the Darklake youngsters.","“Heh heh, that’s true. Lu Yun, you were a dead dog after second brother Ouyang beat you up three months ago. How dare you show your face around here? Take a piss and check out your reflection in it!” Ouyang Chenghu jerked and quickly piped up when he thought of something.","Ouyang Shengmu was a promising talent, but Ouyang Chenghu was just a pretty facade. His cultivation level was slightly higher, but he was no different from the Lu Yun of old.","“Heh heh heh heh,” Lu Yun burst into chuckles before his friends could explode. “Dying for the sake of a beauty is a worthy death and a story to be recounted!”","Whoosh!","He snapped his fan open and raised his head jauntily, a look of unfulfilled satisfaction on his face.","His words caused both Ouyang Shengmu and Ouyang Chenghu to pause with incomprehension, not knowing where he was going with them.","“Ai, Ouyang Shengxiang is a connate constitution indeed! That fair skin, the soft and tall peaks, a tender butt, and a willowy waist... Most importantly is that red dot of a birthmark on her left butt cheek—that’s the most beguiling part of them all...” Lu Yun drooled as he recounted the scene in an ardent murmur.","Zhao Chenguang and Yu Shuai stared wide-eyed at Lu Yun, not knowing what in the heavens he was talking about.","A clash between some of the most famous noble sons of the capital had drawn a crowd. Those who could stand on the third floor instead of being kicked out by Zhao Chenguang were those with certain lofty identities to them. They were happy to watch the show, and they did so with dawning looks of understanding.","No wonder the Ouyang second young master had erupted with fury. It looked like the greatest pestilence of Dark City had certain relations with the Ouyang pearl!"]},{"number":2207,"title":"Chapter 2207: Chapter 2159.1: Saint? Saaaaaint?","paragraphs":["Chapter 2159.1: Saint? Saaaaaint?","Dead silence reigned on the third floor of Immortal Gathering. Only Lu Yun’s lip smacks and lascivious chortling could be heard.","“Hahaha, well done! As expected of young master Lu, you are the glory of our generation!” Yu Shuai broke into loud applause and threw knowing winks at his friend.","No one knew why Ouyang Shenghe had beaten up Lu Yun. The noble sons of the capital frequently clashed with each other, but they never sought to kill one another. If it wasn’t for the Lu experts arriving in the nick of time three months ago, Lu Yun wouldn’t have made it out alive.","Even so, he’d barely survived. So this was the reason why!","Ouyang Shengxiang was the apple of the Ouyang eye, a connate fragrance constitution that appeared once in a thousand years. Wreathed by a natural fragrance, someone of her constitution progressed extremely slowly at the start of their cultivation journey. At fifteen years old, she was only third level qi refinement.","But once she established her foundations, her cultivation speed could only be described as terrifying. Forming a nascent soul was simply a matter of time.","Dark Orchid Empire—Darklake’s superior nation—had also noted Ouyang Shengxiang’s existence. They were waiting for her to reach latter nascent soul before moving her to Dark Orchid Empire for further training.","She was the Ouyang Clan’s little princess and Lu Yun had unspeakable relations with her! No wonder the Ouyangs had gone so mad that they were willing to provoke Lu Tianling—the strongest of the empire.","A faintly smiling Lu Yun took in the laughter and chatter around him, but current happenings somehow seemed very unreal, like this wasn’t his life.","However, the thought recoiled in his mind as soon as it formed, as if it was unwilling to touch something. An enormous instinct wanted to awaken the past him, but his subconsciousness told that instinct that this was to be avoided at all costs. He couldn’t do that, no matter what!","Right now, he was Lu Yun of Darklake Empire, Lu Tianling’s grandson!","The past... he couldn’t have a past!","“Lu Yun, you spew nonsense!” Inside the room, Ouyang Shengmu shot to his feet with a look of fury.","Ouyang Shengxiang was betrothed to the crown prince of Dark Orchid Empire and the clan had finally managed to attach itself to a tremendous backer! The clan would also be dragged into things if her reputation suffered!","“This young master is spouting nonsense?” Lu Yun waved his graphic fan and flicked a sidelong glance at Ouyang Shengmu when the young man walked out. “Do you not know about the red mole on your sister’s left butt cheek?”","“This, this is nonsense! Sheer ridiculousness! There is no red mole on my sister’s bottom!” As Ouyang Shengmu was only nineteen years old, he immediately lost his composure when Lu Yun provoked him in this manner. Who would’ve thought that the trash in front of him would be so out of line?? He had to say something to protect his younger sister’s reputation!","“What, have you seen Ouyang Shengxiang’s butt with your own eyes?” Lu Yun shook his head and clucked his tongue.","“You!!” Ouyang Shengmu turned bright red. “Why would I ever do that?? Stop it with your lies!”","Lu Yun was an old monster who’d weathered three thousand reincarnations; he’d fully experienced all of the vicissitudes of life. Although Ouyang Shengmu was very promising, he was just a baby in Lu Yun’s eyes.","Additionally, there seemed to be something that’d left an even deeper impression than the three thousand reincarnations. It was the life that’d been covered by his various lifetimes, the one that he couldn’t remember.","“Then of course you don’t know about the red mole,” Lu Yun cocked his head. “Or maybe you already know about it, but you’re just pretending not to... Rumors say that the three Ouyang brothers are very close with their baby sister. Do the four of you often hide together and play some special games...” he mused with a knowing expression on his face. These shameless speculations were the height of insolence!","“Bastard, you little bastard!” Ouyang Shengmu squawked with outrage.","Yuwen Chenghu was stiff with surprise next to him. Things were developing in a completely different direction from what they thought. Their plans had said that the one hollering with anger and in complete mental disarray would be young master Lu. So why were things turning out like this?","Yuwen Chenghu was a complete buffoon who’d been taken in by Lu Yun. His thoughts proceeded down strange directions after hearing the wild speculations. Meanwhile, Yu Shuai and Zhao Chenguang snickered without mercy.","Paused at the head of the stairs all this time, Lu Xiaochi assessed the situation with a strange light in his eyes. He dipped his head in thought, then left Immortal Gathering. He knew what would happen next.","“Slap him, Ouyang Feng!” roared Ouyang Shengmu, rage boiling over at the leer on Lu Yun’s face. A stony faced middle-aged man rushed out of the room behind him. Dressed in black, the man reached for Lu Yun’s face.","“How dare a pathetic servant raise his hand against me?! I’ll have your entire family killed for this!” Enormous killing intent rose between Lu Yun’s brows when he registered Ouyang Feng’s emergence. His killing intent was the culmination of three thousand reincarnations, the dignity of a lofty personage that could not be disrespected.","Ouyang Feng was Ouyang Shengmu’s personal guard. Despite being mid golden core, he faltered when met with Lu Yun’s overwhelming glare.","“Ouyang Feng, you piece of trash, hurry up and hit him!” Ouyang Shenmu cursed when he saw his guard hesitate.","“Hold!” A mollifying voice tinged with authority rang out. A slightly chubby, middle-aged man dressed in golden robes had appeared at some point on the third floor. “It would be untoward for an altercation to develop in Immortal Gathering, young sirs.”","He was the general manager of Immortal Gathering and his cultivation had reached latter golden core.","“This young master will pay ten times whatever we break! Ouyang Feng, slap him!” Ouyang Shengmu snarled, incensed by Lu Yun’s last words. They were a fatal blow to Ouyang Shengxiang’s reputation and the entire Ouyang Clan!","What special games between the Ouyang siblings?? What kind of sheer utter tripe was that?! Even his eldest brother Ouyang Shengtian, hailed as the foremost genius of the capital, would be enraged, to say nothing of Ouyang Shengmu.","Ouyang Feng regained his bearings—he was an Ouyang deathsworn and his mental state as solid as a rock. He found solid footing against the Lu young master again. Thus, he raised his enormous hands and slammed them toward Lu Yun’s cheeks.","“Lu Xuan, kill him!” Lu Yun sneered to see a mere servant raising a hand against him.","Whoosh!","Lu Xuan’s sword light was already rushing toward Ouyang Feng before his master finished his command. Ouyang Feng jerked with surprise and hastily backed up.","“Kill Lu Xuan!” Ouyang Shengmu calmed down and barked out a frosty command.","Yuwen Chenghu shook his head with confusion, wondering how things had progressed like this. Although the results were the same, it was Ouyang Shengmu who’d taken action first.","According to their plans, Lu Yun would make the first move while Ouyang Shengmu and Yuwen Chenghu followed his lead. They would kill Lu Yun’s guard in the ensuing fight and then cripple Lu Yun again, just like things had occurred three months ago!","Although some mishaps had occurred along the way, the final outcome should still be the same.","“Yujin, you go as well,” Yuwen Chenghu directed as Lu Xuan clashed with Ouyang Feng. Another golden core expert bounded out of the private room.","“Yuwen Chenghu, you’re just a piece of trash to your clan. How come you have a golden core guard by your side??” Yu Shuai and Zhao Chenguang squawked with surprise when they saw another golden core guard rush out.","Yuwen Chenghu’s status in his family was similar to theirs in their families. Although the former was initial foundation establishment, he was much older than Zhao Chenguang and the others, so he wasn’t highly regarded by his clan.","He would never be assigned a golden core guard!","Ouyang Shengmu was different, he was a treasured genius of his clan. It was entirely reasonable that the Ouyangs would send a golden core powerhouse to protect him.","Two golden core cultivators fought each other—one initial golden core and one mid stage. Sword light flashed like dragons and churned toward Lu Xuan.","“Lu Xuan, kill those two scum!” Lu Yun snarled. Everyone blinked when they heard his words. Didn’t the ignorant prodigal know that his opponent’s guards were stronger than his deathsworn?","Kill the two? Lu Xuan wouldn’t even be able to hold his own.","Stunned expressions crossed their faces the next second.","Pfft!","Ouyang Feng and Yujing’s heads soared into the air with two neat moves. Two headless bodies stumbled back and crashed to the ground.","Dead silence reigned.","Everyone was shocked. Two golden core powerhouses had died in a split second!","One had to know, the Ouyangs and Yuwens were in a different league compared to the Lus. The Lus had risen to prominence in the last one hundred years and possessed shallow foundations. The other two were illustrious cultivation families in Darklake Empire. Their roots ran deep and their deathsworn were not like Lu Xuan, forced to their level through secret arts. They’d cultivated every step of the way to attain their strength.","Lu Xuan raised his sword expressionlessly, majestic and proud. Although he was only initial golden core, he seemed mysterious and inscrutable in this moment.","“You lil piece of shit wanted to slap me?!” Lu Yun paled for the briefest of seconds before erupting with domineering fury. He scowled and charged up to Ouyang Shengmu, delivering a hearty slap across the face.","Slap me?!","The old Lu Yun wouldn’t have stood for it and the new Lu Yun would respond in an even more overbearing fashion! No one could even think about it!","Smack!","Ouyang Shengmu flew backward from the ringing blow, his left cheek swollen. Since his cultivation was much stronger than Lu Yun’s, he didn’t suffer much injury.","“How dare you hit me?!” Ouyang Shengmu reeled with surprise and snarled before throwing himself at Lu Yun. He was stronger than Ouyang Shenghe—Shenghe had been able to beat Lu Yun to an inch of death. He could more than manage the same deed!","“Help him!” Yu Shuai and Zhao Chenguang looked at each other before leaping forward. However, Yuwen Chenghu stopped them from helping their friend."]},{"number":2208,"title":"Chapter 2208: Chapter 2159.2: Saint? Saaaaaint?","paragraphs":["Chapter 2159.2: Saint? Saaaaaint?","“Lu Xuan, confine his cultivation for me!” Lu Yun yelled, drawing a blank stare from his guard.","Confine the opponent’s cultivation? He knew how to kill people, but confine their cultivation?","He didn’t know how!","But before he could do anything, he saw Ouyang Shengmu stiffen, like he was a wooden log. Face contorted in a fiendish grin, Lu Yun pressed his palm on Ouyang Shengmu’s dantian.","Pfft!","Ouyang Shengmu spat out a mouthful of blood amid a look of incredulity. His dantian had been shattered and his meridians crumbled from the impact of Lu Yun’s savage blow! He was in the same ghastly condition that Lu Yun had been three months ago!","Yuwen Chenghu, Yu Shuai, and Zhao Chenguang paused with shock.","The four children of Ouyang Baitian were renewed throughout Darklake. Even the least accomplished Ouyang Shenghe was a latter formation establishment cultivator. Ouyang Shengmu was already peak formation establishment, one step away from golden core. But Lu Yun had just crippled him!","Ouyang Shengmu might have a chance to recover if he came in possession of a miracle pill like the Nineturns Profound Life Pill, but those were impossible to find, even with money. Lu Tianling had rendered such services to the empire and had only one grandson. That was why the emperor had bequeathed him a pill.","But for the Ouyangs, they had Ouyang Shengtian, Ouyang Shenghe, and Ouyang Shengxiang to carry on the family name. It didn’t matter that Ouyang Shengmu was out of the picture.","Additionally, it was likely that the imperial family didn’t have a second pill to give.","“Y-y-y-y-you, Lu Yun, you crippled Ouyang Shengmu! Do you have a death wish?! Do you know the disaster you’ve created for yourself?? The Ouyangs will not forgive you for this!” Yuwen Chenghu gasped when he saw Ouyang Shengmu gurgle bloody foam.","“Won’t forgive me?” Lu Yun tilted his head to the side without a care in the world. “So what? This young master dares touch even Ouyang Shengxiang. Who cares about an Ouyang Shengmu? So he’s crippled. If you keep running your mouth, I’ll have you join him...”","Violence brewed from his bones. Cripple Ouyang Shengmu? How dare the idiot go by the name of Shengmu?! That was the same pronunciation as the characters for saint! Is he mocking me with that name?!","No, wait, when did the scourge of the capital turn into a saint?","Lu Yun shook his head rapidly, still quite irritated by the name. And why did the idiot have to be named Ouyang?!","Ouyang...","Yuwen Chenghu shuddered, subconsciously glancing at the ramrod straight Lu Xuan standing behind Lu Yun. He turned on his heel and left without a word.","Lu Yun shook and nearly fell to the ground. Yu Shuai and Zhao Chenguang quickly helped him up.","“Are you alright, Lu Yun?” Zhao Chenguang asked.","“I’m fine, just not fully recovered from my injuries yet. I’ll be fine with a bit of rest,” Lu Yun waved them off.","“Young masters, you’ve destroyed three private rooms with your fight. Are you going to just leave after the deed?” The restaurant’s grand steward appeared again.","“Didn’t the one on the floor say that he’ll pay ten times over for whatever breaks? Send him the bill,” Lu Yun huffed with a sideways glance at the man.","......","After departing Immortal Gathering, Lu Yun went straight home with Lu Xuan. The Lu servants knew that their ashen-faced young master had come off worse for the wear after an encounter with others and didn’t dare get on the baleful young man’s bad side.","“Lu Xuan, stand guard at the door. Don’t let anyone in before I come out!” Lu Yun panted. His guard stood silently at the door, as expressionless as always.","Lu Yun took out five upper rank spirit stones and waved them into the void. They transformed into a miniature Five Elements Exclusion Formation that isolated the room’s energy ripples from the outside.","He took out another upper rank spirit stone and gripped it, silently replenishing some of the Hongmeng true qi that had been depleted.","Lu Yun had consecutively deployed Petrification today in order to kill four golden core powerhouses and crippled two foundation establishment cultivators. Unfortunately, it resulted in his remarkable stores of energy being consumed.","The limits of Petrification were significant. Although it could freeze cultivators two realms higher than him, it consumed his Hongmeng true qi at a pace that could only be described as colossal.","Hongmeng true qi is used up pretty quickly... Hellfire is way more useful.","“Eh? What’s hellfire?” Lu Yun blinked as the question flashed through his mind. It was quickly suppressed by his subconsciousness and he didn’t dare think further.","He closed his eyes to meditate, slightly recovering his store of Hongmeng qi after four hours.","“Time to see what I got today.” He eagerly took out three storage rings from his own—they were from the general manager of the Lingtian Pill Pavilion, the Ling family steward, and Ouyang Shengmu.","These three occupied high positions in their families and as such, there were quite a few treasures in their rings. Lu Yun erased their owner brands and emptied them of their contents, filling his meditation chamber with a dazzling assortment of glittering, twinkling magnificence.","A myriad of spirit medicines, pills, ores, ingredients, and spirit stones piled up in his room. Just the fortune held in the three rings eclipsed the Lu Clan’s former family wealth by more than ten times.","“Hmm? The fourth rank Grand Unity Pill?” Lu Yun discovered with surprise when he opened a jade bottle and sniffed the dense fragrance emanating from it. “But there’s an additional ingredient of Extreme Flame Grass in it, so it’s actually a poison pill...”","His expression darkened.","The Grand Unity Pill was a fourth rank pill that replenished qi and healed internal injuries. Since Lu Tianling had exhausted his nascent soul and was beset with internal injuries, he needed a pill like this the most.","However, the one from the Lingtian Pill Pavilion was a poison pill! It would heal his injuries in the short term if he took it, but once he used too much internal force, he would shatter all of his meridians.","Lu Yun had stood at the peak of the four supplemental daos at different times in his journey through the three thousand worlds. He constantly innovated and defined new disciplines. The sabotage within a mere fourth rank pill wouldn’t escape his eyes.","Although he didn’t know what the Ling Clan had planned, he was well aware that this poison pill would eventually make it into his grandfather’s hands!","But... wasn’t formula dao the king of supplemental dao?","Huh? What’s formula dao?","Lu Yun blinked when a new thought entered his mind, one that was swiftly destroyed with a rumble.","A certain heavenly dao: Formula dao cannot appear in this era! If it does, what will you utilize in the future?? You would be boxed in by the will of nothing from day one!","“It looks like there’s no use for the Immortal Talisman of Water and Sky that I spent all of my effort etching yesterday. The Grand Unity Pill is far more valuable than it.” A smile curved his lips as Lu Yun rifled through a heap of spirit herbs and medicine.","“As precious as Skystar Grass and Nineleaves Root are, they’re not rare. But there’s none here...?” He frowned slightly. “Oh, right. Yu Shuai gave me a chest of ingredients today.” He summoned the chest back out with a wave of his hand. Throwing the lid back, Lu Yun scanned the tall pile of spirit herbs within.","“Skystar Grass, Nineleaves Root!” He brightened. “The Grand Unity Pill, Extreme Flame Grass, Skystar Grass, and Nineleaves Root can be combined to create the medicinal properties of the ninth rank spirit grass—Violet Orchid Ganoderma!”","Medicinal properties reformation.","In Lu Yun’s eyes, other than the mythical spirit roots of legend, he could recreate the medicinal properties of any immortal pill or grass so long as he had sufficient ingredients. He could do so even with much lower level components.","In the three thousand worlds, he once used the lowliest spirit herbs to recreate the effects of a legendary immortal pill. Far from being limited to pills and medicines, his skills extended to crafting high level talismans, treasures, and formations from lower level inputs as well.","“I think there’s more to this... When I traveled through the three thousand worlds, it felt like I knew all of this to begin with. But when did I learn everything?” Lu Yun tilted his head to the side, unable to come to an answer.","He waved out a small pill cauldron from one of the storage rings—formerly the possession of the golden core general manager of Lingtian Pill Pavilion. Given his place of residence, he was naturally practiced in refining pills.","As it’d been three months since the pill pavilion’s opening, they’d yet to build rooms dedicated to pill refinement. Thus, the general manager carried a pill cauldron on him—a habit that benefited Lu Yun handsomely.","He tossed a handful of spirit herbs into the pill cauldron and set them on fire with a hand seal. He lacked an internal fire of his own as his cultivation was only seven levels qi refinement. Thus, he could only use external fires to refine his pills.","However, he was likely the only one in the entire cultivation world who would use spirit herbs as fuel for his refinement flame!","His hands continued to flicker through seals as the fire blazed. When the cauldron stabilized at the appropriate temperature, he tossed in the Grand Unity Pill, Skystar Grass, and Nineleaf Root. Hongmeng qi swept out of his body and entered the pill cauldron through his hand.","......","Lu Tianling’s residence.","Lu Tianling frowned as he read the report from a subordinate.","“What do you make of it, Old He?” He handed a jade slip to He Wuheng—it contained a detailed recounting of Lu Yun’s dealings of the day.","He Wuheng had fully recovered from his injuries after refining the Nineturns Profound Life Pill. He would return to his former cultivation given enough time and reach even further.","“The young master’s cultivation has fully recovered. Even this old servant needs some time to recover after refining the Nineturns Profound Life Pill...” He Wuheng paused.","Lu Tianling nodded wordlessly.","“The Nineturns Profound Life Pill is a spirit pill beyond ninth rank. But a spirit pill cannot restore a crippled cultivator to their former strength within two days,” the old servant concluded. “However, the young master’s change in personality is the key!” A keen light shone in his eyes. “What seemed to be preposterous speech just so happened to jab at the listener’s weak spot. It flustered and discomfited Ouyang Shengmu, throwing him off balance.”","Lu Yun had fallen into an Ouyang scheme three months ago and spent three months in bed. Lu Tianling had exhausted the family fortune to save his grandson’s life, so how could he not take some precautions after the fact?","Everything that Lu Yun had committed was done under Lu Tianling’s watchful eye.","“The flame fruit vendor... wasn’t a coincidence. The young master knew who he was targeting.” Being Lu Tianling’s right hand man both on and off the battlefield, He Wuheng possessed equal parts valor and intelligence. He was no simple steward."]},{"number":2209,"title":"Chapter 2209: Chapter 2160.1: Severed Meridians","paragraphs":["Chapter 2160.1: Severed Meridians","“What do you think of this matter?” Lu Tianling asked instead of offering his own views.","“There’s two possibilities...” He Wuheng mused. “The first is that the young master has finally learned a painful lesson from his last run-in and matured during the three months.”","“The other?” Light glinted in Lu Tianling’s eyes.","“...a powerhouse has possessed his body...”","Lu Yun had not been reborn through possession. Just as the Tome of Life and Death had once brought him to the world of immortals through the power of reincarnation, he was well and truly in this world. He really was Lu Yun, like he’d been reincarnated into the boy.","The past him was completely sealed beneath three thousand reincarnations. He wouldn’t fully awaken until he became the heavenly dao. At that point, he would travel through space and time to return to his home and safeguard his homeland.","Everyone had a past life—the past Lu Yun was the equivalent of his past life. Everything he possessed now was a result of three thousand worlds and three thousand lifetimes.","......","Dark City, the Ouyang Clan.","Ouyang Shengmu was pale as a sheet and his life hung by a thread. An Ouyang elder with an initial nascent soul cultivation exhausted his qi to keep Ouyang Shengmu alive, but was also grievously injured for his efforts.","A domineering man of roughly forty years old stood in front of Ouyang Shengmu’s bed. Killing intent shown out of his eyes. He was the current patriarch of the Ouyang Clan—Ouyang Baitian!","At latter nascent soul, he was one of the strongest in Darklake Empire.","The Ouyang Clan had existed in Darklake for thousands of years. Its foundations ran deep and the authority that Ouyang Baitian commanded was nothing that an upstart like Lu Tianling could compare to.","If it wasn’t for Lu Tianling possessing unparalleled strength and being the absolute strongest within the empire, the Lus wouldn’t have been able to establish themselves as a clan. The other six families would’ve razed it to the ground long ago.","Even so, the formation of the Lu Clan severely threatened the profits of the old cultivation families. They ostracized the newcomer at every turn, with the Ouyangs and Yuwens openly hostile to the Lus.","“The Lus are becoming ever more recklessly wanton. Ouyang Shengmu looks to be completely crippled,” a man dressed like a scholar said softly next to Ouyang Baitain.","“You Lings have suffered quite a loss too. That family of trash wrecked your Lingtian Pill Pavilion.” Ouyang Baitian smiled a smile that didn’t reach his eyes when he looked at the man.","The scholarly man was the patriarch of one of the seven great families—Ling Chongxiao.","“It’s just a pill pavilion, it doesn’t matter if it’s gone.” Ling Chongxiao didn’t mind in the slightest. “But since the poison pill has landed in Lu Tianling’s hands, our plan can commence ahead of time.”","“The Lings should not take action openly,” rang a third voice—patriarch of the Yuwens, Yuwen Zonglin. “The Lings look to be friendly with the Lus on the surface and it’s the Lus who’ve seized the pill from you. It has nothing to do with your clan. If the emperor is involved again this time, he will be wary of you even if the Lus don’t die.”","“Hmph! That Lu Tianling is just a genius from one of Darklake’s vassal nations, a second rank cultivation empire! How dare a bumpkin establish a clan in Darklake?!” Ling Chongxiao snorted.","Darklake Empire possessed two major second rank vassals—Dark Empire and Wing Empire. Lu Tianling came from Dark Empire.","Second rank cultivation empires saw golden core cultivators as their strongest citizens. But in Dark Empire, when one reached peak golden core, their superior nation took the cultivator away, no matter what their identity was.","When it came to the reasons... a primary one was that a superior state would never permit a vassal nation to grow stronger and possibly out of control. The second was that resources were limited in a second rank nation. Even if the cultivator in question broke through to nascent soul, they would be hard pressed to take another step forward.","Darklake Empire brimmed with rich resources, enough to help a nascent soul cultivator continue on their path. The strongest of the empire were nascent soul cultivators. Any who made it to the empire were treated graciously and bestowed a high position.","But one such as Lu Tianling, establishing a great clan on equal footing with the other six blue bloods of the nation... Well, that was unheard of.","Of course, once Lu Tianling or the three patriarchs reached latter nascent soul and seemed ready to break through to soul projection, Darklake’s superior nation—Dark Orchid Empire—would take the cultivator away.","There had been some cultivators among the six families or imperial family who reached the soul projection stage. They’d all joined Dark Orchid factions to become their subordinates or guest elders.","“The emperor is biased, what can we do?” Ouyang Baitian shook his head.","Due to a misunderstanding that Lu Yun had died three months ago, Lu Tianling stormed the Ouyang Clan with incandescent rage. Despite being surrounded by Ouyang experts, he killed one nascent soul powerhouse and two latter golden core ones before retreating at leisure.","After he was injured to save Lu Yun, the Ouyangs led their people to exterminate the Lu Clan. Emperor Situ Wenxian had stopped them, and that was the end of the matter.","“We can now visit him with the same excuse that Lu Tianling used against us. Let’s see what the emperor has to say this time!” Yuwen Zonglin snorted. If the emperor stopped them again, that would truly weaken the loyalty of the old families.","“But we must be on our guard still no matter what. The Lings cannot take action. Baitian and I are sufficient.”","None of the patriarchs mentioned Lu Yun from beginning to end. In their eyes, that was just Lu Tianling using his grandson to take revenge on the Ouyang Clan. What’d happened at Lingtian Pill Pavilion was a coincidence. It was precisely the type of behavior expected from Lu Yun as he’d committed no end of acts like these before.","......","The sun set in the west. Inside his meditation chamber, Lu Yun wiped off his forehead and slowly stood up, his footsteps a bit unsteady.","“I’m going to have a tough time explaining myself when grandfather asks about this,” Lu Yun sighed as he looked at the jade green pill in his hands. He felt that he had nothing to hide, but it was still more than a bit ludicrous to speak of taking the heavenly dao as his master and undergoing three thousand reincarnations.","Lying would be more believable, and for some reason, Lu Yun felt that becoming the heavenly dao’s disciple was a significant matter for more reasons than one. It had to do with an enormous plan that required proceeding with extreme caution.","“Mm, let’s just say that I’ve taken a stunning powerhouse as my master. That’s not really a lie as I really do have a stunning master.” Lu Yun swallowed a qi replenishment pill he’d brought back from Lingtian Pill Pavilion. His exhausted stores of Hongmeng qi recovered somewhat.","He naturally knew that his doings of the day wouldn’t escape his grandfather’s notice. He could even guess Lu Tianling’s reaction. It would be very alarming if Lu Tianling was unmoved, so it was to be expected that his grandfather would have certain questions. If nothing else, he would ask because he cared about his grandson.","The situation was similar to a student who always failed his tests suddenly testing full marks. The first thing that the parents and teacher needed to do wasn’t to praise the student, but to wonder if he’d cheated.","It was only logical.","More importantly was that Lu Yun knew today’s events were a scheme set up by the Ouyangs, Yuwen, and the Lings in the shadows. It wasn’t aimed at him, but at his grandfather.","If it’d looked like his defeat was imminent, Lu Tianling’s contingency plan would activate. Of course, the Yuwens and Ouyangs were no fools. They certainly had their preparations ready as well.","In that case, Lu Yun decided to go on the offensive and ensure that he occupied the moral high ground. He played along with their plans, and he foresaw that the two families would attempt to kick in their door in a few more days. They wanted to make use of him taking the poison pill, if nothing else.","......","When Lu Yun walked out of his room, he saw his second uncle sitting grumpily on a stone stool in the yard. The man’s cheeks were puffed out like an irate toad.","“Aiyo, what’s brought second uncle to my residence?” Lu Yun asked merrily.","“You’re finally willing to come out, huh?” Lu Xiaochi snorted. “What evil doings have you gotten up to in your room?”","“Um...” Lu Yun scratched his nose with embarrassment. “I was tired after making some money today so I... took a nap.” He stretched and yawned to punctuate his words.","Lu Xiaochi rolled his eyes. “What are you trying to do?”","“What do you mean, second uncle?” Lu Yun was the perfect picture of baffled innocence.","“How do you explain what happened today??” Lu Xiaochi sniffed. “The vendor on the street was at least eighty years old. Why did you rob him?”","“Eh, didn’t I say? That guy yelled into my ears for quite a few years. He was annoying me to tears and I was incredibly irritated. Who else would I take it out on, if not him?” Lu Yun curled his lip.","Lu Xiaochi’s baleful expression deepened as he had no response to that.","“Immortal Gathering? How do you explain yourself there?”","“Huh? Immortal Gathering?” Lu Yun blinked.","“Ouyang Shengxiang!” Lu Xiaochi ground his teeth.","“Oh... um... surely you jest, second uncle,” Lu Yun coughed awkwardly. “She’s one of the three great beauties of the capital and the lover of my dreams, the goddess of my heart. Your nephew simply spoke of what we all want. Ouyang Shenghe beat me up because I took a peek at her bathing. Um... the red mole really is very charming!”","Lu Xiaochi gaped, Lu Xuan remained as expressionless as always, and Lan’er covered her mouth.","“Er, you are dismissed, Lan’er. What we’re going to talk about is not fit for children.” Lu Yun waved her off.","Lan’er reddened and quickly retreated.","“Second uncle, I know you have certain thoughts about Ouyang Shengxiang, so your nephew will describe her beauty to you. She has curves in all the right places, whatever should be big is big and whatever should be small is small. Especially her... just a hair bigger would be too big, just a tad smaller would be too small...”","“Enough!”"]},{"number":2210,"title":"Chapter 2210: Chapter 2160.2: Severed Meridians","paragraphs":["Chapter 2160.2: Severed Meridians","Lu Xiaochi was roughly eighty years old. Although cultivators possessed long lifespans, making it so that eighty years old was the start of one’s life, he was an upright and honest individual who wouldn’t mix with a hooligan like Lu Yun.","Livid, he said stiffly, “Your grandfather wants you.”","“Okay.” Lu Yun nodded, on a roll. He licked his lips and left the yard.","Lu Xiaochi’s cross expression turned into a rueful chuckle as he watched Lu Yun go. That bout of ridiculousness had prevented him from asking some questions that he’d wanted answers to.","“It looks like there is definitely more than meets the eye for this nephew of mine... And is there really a red mole on Ouyang Shengxian’s bottom?” He suddenly stroked his chin thoughtfully.","......","The Lu complex was a massive park forested by various individual residences, each protected by individual formations. Lu Tianling’s residence sat in the middle of the complex and was the eye of the major protection formation—the Major Cycle Nebula Formation.","As a direct lineal descendent of the patriarch, the eldest grandson, and the future heir, Lu Yun could come and go through the formation’s clusters at will.","“Grandfather!” He bowed respectfully to the towering man when he reached Lu Tianling’s residence.","“Mm.” Lu Tianling nodded, a trace of unnatural white marking his face. Lu Xiaochi was close on Lu Yun’s heels.","“Yun’er, it isn’t that grandfather and your second uncle doubt you, but that your change truly makes us worry,” Lu Tianling said after a long moment of silence.","Lu Yun nodded. He would also be suspicious if it were him. After all, Lu Tianling and Lu Xiaochi had watched him grow up. They were well aware of what his personality was like. It would be absolute bullshit to spin a story that he’d purposefully created a facade of being good-for-nothing and treating the world as his stage.","It also wouldn’t make any sense that he’d stepped out of concealment and revealed his true self when the family was in danger, because he was the sole reason that they were in these straits!","Their enemies had used him again and again, leading Lu Tianling around by the nose and forcing the great general to give way again and again for his grandson. Lu Yun’s title of the number one prodigal of Dark City was well rooted in reality.","Lu Xiaochi also looked at Lu Yun with blazing eyes.","“Grandfather, it’s not like I’ve been possessed by another.” Lu Yun took out a piece of inky-green jade hanging from his neck. “This is called the Soul Extendere Jade, right? It’s the bane of the souls of cultivators. Without the protection of a physical body, even the soul of an immortal will be crippled if it draws near the jade...”","Lu Tianling’s eyes opened wide and he gasped, “You recognize the Soul Extendere Jade!”","The Soul Extendere Jade wasn’t something that should be found in a third rank empire like Darklake. Possibly even the emperor of Dark Orchid might not know about its existence. It was considered a priceless treasure that was many times more precious than the Nineturns Profound Life Pill.","Being effective against souls, there was only one use for it—preventing cultivators from being possessed by another.","Powerhouses abounded in the world of cultivation. Where there were people, there was conflict. When cultivators died, it was very possible that fragments of their souls remained. Those fragments retained sufficient strength to seize the body of another and be reborn.","Possession took an enormous toll on the invader—oftentimes, the invader’s own soul fragmented and died in the process. But if one chose a victim with shallow cultivation foundations or someone who was already gravely injured, then the chances of success were somewhat higher.","Lu Tianling had seen his fair share of old monsters taking possession of youngsters, so when Lu Yun fell into a coma for three months, he brought out his treasured Soul Extendere Jade to shelter his grandson’s soul and prevent a possession.","It wasn’t that Lu Yun had taken possession of the body he’d reincarnated into it. It was a karmic tie from the womb and he was Lu Yun the moment he was born. It just so happened that the heavenly dao took him as a disciple at an appropriate time.","Lu Yun nodded. “The Soul Extendere Jade is uncommonly precious and can damage souls to prevent cultivators from being seized by another. But the greatest effect of this item is to nurture the soul, not to harm it. Immortals would fight over it if they saw it.”","Lu Tianling and Lu Xiaochi looked at each other with astonishment.","“Grandfather, your grandson’s soul was not harmed. In the three months that I spent unconscious, I gained a powerful master and traveled with him, learning by his side,” Lu Yun explained with all seriousness.","“Dream Sutra, propagating dao in dreams?” Lu Tianling shot to his feet. “Teaching through dreams is the capability of high-level immortals! Is your master a mighty immortal? No wonder... no wonder your injuries and cultivation fully recovered without needing a Nineturns Profound Life Pill!”","Both cultivators and immortals existed in a world of cultivation! Cultivators set reaching immortality as their goal on their path of cultivation. The Dream Sutra that Lu Tianling spoke of was a method unique to immortals, and not that of ordinary immortals.","Golden immortal? High immortal? Or...","“Did you go to the Celestial Realm Battlefront during these three months? That would make sense, only a place like the battlefield can make you swiftly grow up,” Lu Xiaochi interjected.","“The Celestial Realm Battlefront...” A sharp light flashed through Lu Yun’s eyes when he heard these words. It seemed to be the key of everything and the future source of destruction for this world of immortal dao civilization.","Lu Tianling and Lu Xiaochi no longer doubted Lu Yun. No one would be able to possess the young man when he wore the Soul Extendere Jade. The treasure could harm even the souls of immortals. All of Darklake Empire would suffer tremendous disaster if it was widely known that the Lus possessed one such treasure.","It was an item that immortals would fight over!","Owning the Soul Extendere Jade and being able to establish a clan through his own strength... Grandfather also possesses many secrets. Lu Yun thought silently to himself.","Lu Yun gaining an immortal for a master, leaning through the Dream Sutra, and being sent to the Celestial Realm Battlefront was the only explanation for his changes. Lu Tianling breathed a long sigh of relief and smiled. “As long as you’re fine, as long as you’re fine. If anything happened to you, grandfather would dismantle the Ouyangs and Yuwens.”","“And the Lings,” Lu Yun grumbled.","Lu Tianling inclined his head. “So you see things clearly too. Although the Ling Clan has not erupted in open hostility against us, they’ve done many things from the shadows.”","“The Ouyang Clan will not easily let us off the hook,” Lu Xiaochi said with an uneasy look at Lu Tianling.","The patriarch waved him off.","“Grandfather.” Lu Yun walked up and took out a jade bottle from his storage ring. “This is a pill that master gave me to replenish qi and heal internal injuries.”","The bottle contained the pill that he’d formulated with the properties of the Violet Orchid Ganoderma.","He didn’t say it was his work as it wasn’t yet time to speak of this. If Lu Tianling learned that his grandson was this capable, he would immediately cocoon the young man with protection and prevent any word from getting out.","Lu Yun being a prodigal son was the only opening that their enemies could use against the Lu Clan. Once they discovered that the family trash had become an unparalleled genius, they would immediately seek to kill him. Lu Tianling would never permit this to happen, so he would certainly confine Lu Yun to the residence and forbid him from taking a single step through the front doors.","The young man was safe if he was remained an incompetent wastrel.","In Lu Tianling’s eyes, it must be his grandson’s master directing Lu Yun’s actions earlier in the day. It wasn’t his grandson’s own inspiration, so Lu Yun had concealed things.","“Grandfather, you should refine the pill. We haven’t seen the last of the Ouyangs and neither are the Yuwens the peaceful sort. They’ll probably come calling over the next few days,” Lu Yun said.","Lu Tianling’s expression changed dramatically when he opened the jade bottle for a sniff. “This is a pill refined from the ninth rank spirit grass Violet Orchid Ganoderma...” A crafty smile spread across his face like a wily old fox. “I would fear them somewhat before today, but now?”","Lu Yun cackled as well, the spitting image of a young fox.","......","“I say, kid, you hide things well,” Lu Xiaochi snapped when the two of them left Lu Tianling’s residence. The patriarch had gone into closed door cultivation to refine the pill. Lu Yun and Lu Xiaochi took their leave at the same time.","The two adults didn’t ask why the immortal had accepted a good-for-nothing like Lu Yun as their disciple. The thoughts of immortals were not for mortals to conjecture.","“Eh? What have I hidden?” Lu Yun looked innocently at his second uncle.","“Didn’t you say you didn’t recognize this?” A fist-sized stone appeared in Lu Xiaochi’s hand—the communication stone.","“Huh? When did I say that? I said I have no use for it,” Lu Yun pouted.","Lu Xiaochi paused, recalling what their conversation had been. That... was true, that was indeed what his nephew had said.","“Alright, second uncle, let me take a look at your injuries and see if there’s any way to help you recover your cultivation,” Lu Yun said solemnly.","Lu Xiaochi froze, then asked hopefully after a long pause, “Yun’er, is your master going to help me himself?”","“Master has left and is not in Dark City anymore,” Lu Yun shook his head. “But I’ve learned a bit of his abilities and should be able to handle second uncle’s injuries without difficulty.”","Lu Xiaochi smiled ruefully. He knew his injuries very well and that there was no one in this world who could heal him. His nephew had neither learning nor art and was just seven levels qi refinement. Though he had an immortal for a master, how much of his master’s skill could he have learned in three short months?","He didn’t hold out any hope.","Lu Yun grabbed his uncle’s wrist and sent his consciousness into the man’s body. The Lu second master had been latter nascent soul and the foremost genius of the empire. Although his cultivation had been crippled and his consciousness suppressed, his physical body remained incomparably strong. Having been baptized by the energy of heaven and earth, he kept a youthful appearance.","“Severed Meridians Hold! It’s the Severed Meridians Hold!” Lu Yun’s expression shifted as he muttered lowly.","Lu Xiaochi frowned, but didn’t say a word.","“The Severed Meridians Hold is known as the most vicious restriction there is. It leaves cutting points within a cultivator’s meridians. If one tries to force medicines through, it will immediately shatter the meridians and have the victim die an explosive death!” Lu Yun explained in a frosty voice. “How can a mere Nineheavens Pagoda, a sect of a fourth rank empire, possess such a cruel restriction?!”","Lu Xiaochi’s eyes widened—his nephew had just voiced the same thing as Lu Tianling once said. But Lu Tianling had only said it was a vicious restriction he’d never seen before, he hadn’t been able to identify it."]},{"number":2211,"title":"Chapter 2211: Chapter 2161.1: Senior Brother","paragraphs":["Chapter 2161.1: Senior Brother","The Severed Meridians Hold... I would be able to break it if I reached the second turn of Seeing Dao and ascended to foundation establishment... Lu Yun mused inwardly. That seemed to be the case, yet also not the case. He seemed to be able to break it even without reaching the second turn, but that ability had been... sealed away?","Lu Yun hesitated, but his instincts hid the thought as soon as the notion rose in his heart. As baffled as he was, he wasn’t willing to pursue the matter further.","Something else must’ve happened beyond the three thousand reincarnations! As for what he’d sealed away, there must be a reason for it since he instinctively didn’t wish to recall it. Therefore, he wouldn’t think more on it.","Lu Xiaochi smiled wryly when he looked at his nephew’s expression and shook his head. He left without saying a word.","“Second uncle... believe me...” Lu Yun said slowly as he watched Lu Xiaochi’s departing back.","The man paused, then nodded gently.","......","The moon was high in the night—it was another night of the full moon.","Lan’er had gone to bed and Lu Yun sat alone in the yard, holding a wine jug made of white jade and filling his cup to the brim.","“A jug of warm wine enjoyed beneath the moonlight, paired with a serving of life as I drink...” Lu Yun murmured to himself. “Were the three thousand worlds and reincarnations a dream or reality? What is the sealed experience beneath the three thousand?”","He raised his cup and toasted the night sky before tossing its contents back with a gulp.","Although he’d gained a great many skills, abilities, and experience throughout the three thousand worlds and reincarnations, he’d also formed too many emotional ties and relationships. Somehow, the deepest of them all was what he wished least to forget, yet had to forget it for now. It was what affected him sleeping and waking.","He exhaled a mouthful of turbid air and continued drinking as he cultivated.","The Nine Chapters of Dao were from the heavenly dao and nature—it was the closest cultivation method there was to the great dao. Lu Yun’s Hongmeng qi circulated at every second, ensuring that he cultivated when he ate, slept, and walked. If he wanted to, he could prevent any energy ripples from arising when he cultivated.","In contrast, cultivators had to sit cross-legged with their eyes closed, clearing their mind of all thought when they cultivated. They had to reach a mentally empty state before entering meditation.","“My cultivation level is at the first turn, the second turn is nowhere in sight. Although the Nine Chapters of Dao are a cultivation method of the heavenly dao, it consumes too much energy to train...”","A piece of upper rank spirit stone crumbled in his hand and drifted to the ground. Upper rank spirit stones could no longer satisfy his needs. If word of that got out, it would shock a large group of cultivators.","One upper rank spirit stone was sufficient to support a golden core cultivator for half a month. How had a weakling of only seven levels qi refinement absorbed all of the energy from a spirit stone in one hour?!","“It looks like I need to take some time to collect a few paramount rank spirit stones.” Another upper rank stone appeared in his hand with a twinkle from his storage ring.","The Lu Clan originally possessed a decent store of paramount rank spirit stones, seeing as it was one of the seven great families of the capital. But Lu Tianling had expended the entire family fortune to save his grandson three months ago because Lu Yun had been too gravely injured. He’d employed countless medicines and spirit herbs to do so—otherwise, his own nascent soul might not have been sufficient.","That matter three months ago had delivered a fatal blow to the family. The Lu Clan was now outwardly strong, but inwardly brittle. It would never be able to lay hands on another paramount rank spirit stone.","“Hmm?” Lu Yun furrowed his brow as he was shocked to discover that the hazy “dao” character in his dantian, the source of the “Seeing Dao” chapter, was shaking violently. Jade-green light exploded from his body.","Humm!","The scene in front of his eyes changed before he had a chance to react; he arrived in a void that was both familiar and unknown. An endless expanse of brilliant stars filled the area. A silver patch of land made from stars could be found in its center. This was where Lu Yun had met the heavenly dao and been accepted as a disciple.","The silver patch that was but thirty meters across held a flawless stone table in its center. Pristinely white, two stone stools were placed next to it. Lu Yun hadn’t seen this table on his first visit. Someone was sitting on one of the stools.","It was a man dressed in simple blue robes and a meter of blue hair reaching waist-length in a casual manner. He looked to be in his twenties and appeared rather ordinary, but a few hints of detachment could be read in his face.","He smiled broadly to see Lu Yun arrive and the young man felt great happiness blossom in his heart as well. Unbidden, he responded with a faint smile.","“Aha, hello junior brother. Sit.” The man in blue robes gestured at the other stool.","“Junior brother?” Lu Yun blinked, but took a seat without hesitation.","“Allow me to introduce myself, I am your eldest senior brother—the sky.” The man looked affably at Lu Yun. [1]","“Eldest senior brother?” Lu Yun blinked. He’d thought that the heavenly dao only had him for a disciple, but here was an eldest senior brother! Did this mean there was a second and third senior brother too?","Sky seemed to see through Lu Yun’s bafflement and smiled. “Don’t be confused, you’re the only living disciple that master has. However, I don’t know why he accepted you as one.”","Lu Yun remained quiet and waited for his senior brother to continue.","“I and your other senior brothers are not living beings. We are the manifestations of rules that possess our own independent thought. We come from the same origins as master.”","Lu Yun blinked again, but it made sense, considering what his senior brother’s name was. The sky wasn’t a deity in the world of cultivation, but it was one in many of the worlds that he’d traveled to and his temples could be found in quite a few of them.","He was in the presence of a literal deity! And the deity was his senior brother!","“Eh... um... senior brother, since you’re a rule, how have you taken physical form? Do rules have their own consciousness as well...?” Lu Yun frowned, feeling that this question was very important.","A smiling Sky shook his head. “The rules are the rules. We are without beginning or end, without desire or emotion. We cannot form a consciousness. The heavenly dao and I are the manifestation of the emotions of life, the thoughts of the living. We are dead beings if we take shape as the rules—we would lack our own mind. If we take physical form, we do so with the will of the living as our basis.”","“The will of the living?” Lu Yun nodded, seeming to grasp something, but not knowing what he grasped. “What instructions might senior brother have for me with this visit? Are you going to give me a greeting gift? I happily welcome all connate treasures or connate supreme treasures!”","The young man fully relaxed. He was the heavenly dao’s disciple too, so his identity was the same as the sky’s. His character had long been tempered into a firm and unyielding state. Thus, he was able to face the deity in front of him with ease.","As he spoke, he smiled bashfully and shyly reached out his hand.","Sky paused, dazed. He was a rule and had taken physical form due to the will of life. He’d never interacted with living beings before, so he didn’t know how to respond to Lu Yun’s rascally attitude.","“You’re a lazy one, kid.” He shook his head with a rueful smile. “Well, a connate treasure is too powerful for you right now. You won’t be able to use it. I have a leaf here that you can use to defend yourself with.”","Sky probed the air with his right hand and gently closed his hand on it, summoning an oval shaped leaf of jade green into his hand.","“A... leaf? That’s so miserly,” Lu Yun grumbled, but quickly took the leaf. Even a piece of leaf from the sky was incredibly precious.","“What do you know? This leaf is from the first spirit root of the three realms—the Builder Tree. With this leaf on you, it will safeguard your life so long as your soul isn’t shattered by the attack.”","Lu Yun closed his hand around the leaf as Sky spoke. Dense vitality flowed out of it and into his body. The leaf then vanished into his body like it was a drop of water.","“I am the disciple of the heavenly dao, is there anyone in existence who can touch me?” he muttered.","“It is true that you are a disciple and favored by the heavenly dao,” Sky chuckled wryly. “But there are plenty of people who do not respect the sky and earth, who seek to defy the heavens. There are many, many of them who hold not the slightest hint of respect toward me or our master. You would just be an ordinary human in their eyes. For them, defying the heavens and slaughtering the heavenly dao is their aim.”","“Defy heaven?” Lu Yun snorted. “Why would they want to do that?”","A strange ripple agitated in his mind. The future of this world of immortal cultivation... would be one of life waging war on the heavens and causing their own destruction. The heavenly dao was the will of life. To defy the heavens... was to defy life.","Sky blinked as Lu Yun stretched. When the young man saw a pot of tea and two teacups on the stone table, he poured a cup for himself and sipped at it leisurely.","“Those so-called defiers are the most idiotic of them all. Their goal is to defy the heavens? Them? Defying the heavens is more like a slogan from those who’ve failed in life.”","When some failed to achieve what they wished despite a forceful effort, they felt that it was the heavens that denied them accomplishment. When some failed to properly grasp what they had, they felt that it was the heavens that stripped it from them. And thus, defying the heavens became a rallying call.","If the heavens dare obstruct me, then I will defy the heavens!","But please, the heavenly dao was very busy and had no time to spare for individual people, whether to obstruct them or strip them of certain things. Failure and loss was just a matter of one’s personal failing. In Lu Yun’s eyes, those who failed were worthy of sympathy, but if one didn’t understand why one had failed and assigned the reason to someone else—or even the heavens...","Then. Well. That was the height of idiocy.","Fate? That was always under one’s control. Destiny? That was just smoke and mirrors. To Sky, even a disciple of the heavenly dao like Lu Yun might die in someone else’s hands. Nothing was guaranteed and it was up to the young man whether or not he would come into his own.","Having experienced three thousand reincarnations and worlds, Lu Yun had long since ceased to fixate on anything. Although heavenly dao was the intangible overlord of all, it was also just a rule. It lacked emotions and desire. It would still exist if life ceased to be.","Everything was equal beneath the heavenly dao and to the heavenly dao, there was no life. Those who fancied themselves abandoned by the heavens were even more ridiculous. They were the ones who’d abandoned themselves.","Lu Yun had never thought much of those who said they would defy the heavens. Why would he think of someone who didn’t believe in themselves as a major enemy?","1. His name literally means the blue sky, that thing up there when we look up. ☜"]},{"number":2212,"title":"Chapter 2212: Chapter 2161.2: Senior Brother","paragraphs":["Chapter 2161.2: Senior Brother","There was an interesting saying in the three thousand worlds.","Catching strays.","Indeed, the current heavenly dao and Lu Yun’s three senior brothers had caught strays. They were denounced by tongue and pen for no reason at all.","In contrast, Lu Yun admired those who respected neither heaven nor earth—they believed in only themselves. Those kinds of people possessed enormous confidence and felt that they could overcome everything with personal strength alone. They would never grouse about defying the heavens.","Although they held no heavenly dao in their minds and followed their own hearts, their wills were resolute. They would never blame others for their difficulties.","Sky shook his head with a smile. “There are some things that you’ll only understand later on.”","“Senior brother, you didn’t bring me here just to say these things, did you?” A merry Lu Yun sipped the paramount rank immortal tea and shoved the full jade pot into his storage ring.","Sky pretended not to see Lu Yun’s motions.","“Of course not.” He changed to a solemn expression. “The Dao Chapters are a cultivation method from the great dao. Progressing through all nine chapters will enable you to perfect your own great dao.”","“So it’s about cultivation!” Lu Yun brightened. The Dao Chapters that the sky spoke of were the Nine Chapters of Dao that he practiced. It was quite a perverse method as the Hongmeng qi that resulted from training its first chapter was much higher quality than the true origin of cultivators. However, the cultivation process was exceedingly hard.","Lu Yun’s current cultivation was but the initial first turn of the Seeing Dao chapter. He’d need to toil for at least ten years if he wished to break through to mid first turn, and that was just the three minor levels of the first turn!","The rest of the cultivation to come didn’t bear thinking about.","Having experienced three thousand worlds, Lu Yun wouldn’t run into bottlenecks when it came to cultivation experience and the understanding of various cultivation realms. The key issue was that the amount of energy it took to practice all nine chapters was too enormous to consider.","“You are a physical body and a mortal soul in the end. Although you possess a heavenly spirit root, you will fail to reach the second chapter of Knowing Dao without outside aid,” Sky said slowly.","A heavenly spirit root was Lu Yun’s spirit root. It wasn’t a perversely strong one, but it was the only instance to ever appear within the world of cultivation and all three realms.","A heavenly spirit root was named after the heavens. The Lu Yun of three months ago had never truly tried to cultivate, but his cultivation level steadily grew nonetheless until he reached seventh level qi refinement. This ludicrous feat would cause an uproar through the world if anyone else knew of it.","This was the reason that the heavenly dao gave when it wanted Lu Yun for a disciple. Of course, Lu Yun understood that there must be other reasons for the heavenly dao to physically manifest and take a human mortal for a disciple. It couldn’t just be for a rare spirit root.","He looked raptly at Sky, silently waiting for his senior brother to continue.","Sky lifted his right hand in the void, slowly coalescing a green seal that was one meter long on each side.","“This is the Seal of the Multitude. It is a treasure formed of the will of all people. Although it isn’t a connate treasure, it might possibly be stronger than one,” Sky explained solemnly. “The seal can collect the will of the people and help you with cultivating the Dao Chapters. You will see twice the results with half the effort.”","“A treasure stronger than a connate treasure?” Lu Yun beamed at it.","Sky said no more and waved it into his junior brother’s body in a streak of green light.","“Remember, the rules cannot be flouted. I will be returning to my place now.” As Sky looked at Lu Yun, he suddenly said, “I know that you’re very interested in the memories sealed at the bottom of your heart and wish to delve into them—but remember, you’re the one who sealed them away!","“You don’t wish to recall those memories at present and they will resurface when the time is right. You will know the cause and effect of everything then. The answer lies within you.”","Lu Yun started, then quickly nodded with gravity. He was indeed very curious about what the three thousand reincarnations had sealed away and wanted to break through the seal, but a certain instinct always kept him at bay.","It must be the past him who’d personally set the seal.","Lu Yun could be much more relaxed when it came to facing his senior brother. As the physical manifestation of the rules, Sky wouldn’t harbor so many layers of thought. If he’d brought out the Seal of the Multitude when Lu Yun asked for a greeting gift, he would’ve saved the expenditure of a leaf from the Builder Tree.","The young man well understood how precious the leaf was; it was likely on par with the seal. The Builder Tree was rumored to be the first spirit root among the six realms and six daos, the unparalleled divine tree that connected the realms. It’d disappeared from existence, however, and no one knew where it’d gone. Even the mightiest immortal would fight over one of its leaves.","Sky’s body began to fade away and the scene morphed in front of Lu Yun’s eyes again. He returned to his little yard, whereupon Sky rematerialized where they’d just conversed.","“Indeed, the greatest worry of living beings is wisdom, and the source of wisdom is thought.” Sky smiled ruefully as he looked at where Lu Yun had vanished. “The heavenly dao wished to give him the seal and the last leaf of the Builder Tree, but I gave him the leaf as a greeting gift and made it so that he owes me a favor...","“Ai, worries, thoughts, and wisdom. It’s better to be an emotionless rule that lacks desire...” The man faded away again.","......","The moon’s radiance spilled forth like water, the night was as silent as a dream.","Lu Yun sat quietly in his yard, having kept the same position as before. If it wasn’t for the appearance of a tremendous amount of vitality in his body and the Seal of the Multitude in his dantian, he would’ve thought everything was just a dream.","He slowly closed his eyes and focused on his dantian.","A hazy “dao” character still occupied the center, emanating a marvelously profound presence. The green seal hovered silently beneath it, as if it was an altar table hoisting the character up for worship.","Lu Yun’s consciousness could clearly sense a green current flowing from the seal into the character.","“My senior brother... really gave me the seal and didn’t tell me how to use it. Collecting the will of the people can help with my cultivation? What is the will of the people?” Lu Yun chuckled ruefully. Regardless, the addition of the seal caused a bizarre power to form within his body. It came from the seal and melded into the Hongmeng true qi of his body. When stimulated by the burst of new power, his Hongmeng qi of initial first turn seemed ready to enter mid stage.","Lu Yun still didn’t know how to use the seal after he studied it for a bit. Meanwhile, the leaf from the Builder Tree completely disappeared after entering his body. Apart from a massive vitality coursing through his being, he couldn’t find any trace of it.","Lu Yun sighed and took out a piece of upper rank spirit stone from his spirit stone, returning to his usual schedule of cultivation.","Dao methods followed nature, which was why Sky hadn’t told his junior brother how to use the seal. He wanted Lu Yun to progress naturally and to come to results as a matter of course.","As for the memories that’d been sealed away, Lu Yun felt that his senior brother made a lot of sense. It was highly likely that he was the one who’d sealed them away. Otherwise, his instincts wouldn’t react like they did whenever he tried to access them.","......","Dawn. The first rays of sunlight in the east.","Bam!","A terrible collision broke the tranquility of early morning.","“Hand over Lu Yun and pay for my son’s life, old fart Lu, or I—Ouyang Baitian—will raze your complex today!” A commanding shout erupted in the air as a golden hammer the size of a house descended from the sky. It smashed into the defensive formation around the Lu residence and made the entire complex shudder.","Lu Yun was startled awake from his meditation and lifted his eyes to see three towering bodies standing in the air.","“Ouyang Baitian?” Lu Tianling gracefully rose into the air. He was dressed in blue robes with white hair framing a face that was forty years old. “You’re here for your son, but what are you here for, Yuwen Zonglin?”","“Shengmu and my daughter are betrothed. I see him as my son-in-law, so why do you think I’m here?” Yuwen Zonglin snorted and unsheathed his sword. “Hand over Lu Yun, old fart, or Brother Ouyang and I will see what the strongest of Dark City is capable of!”","Lu Yun couldn’t help but snort with laughter as he listened on the ground. Yuwen Zonglin wouldn’t even dare breathe too loudly in front of a Lu Tianling in perfect condition. Kick in the Lu front door? Why, of course when the old man was gravely injured!","Of the seven families in the city, Yuwen Zonglin was the weakest out of all the patriarchs.","“Hahaha, how dare a mere Yuwen Zonglin talk to me like this!” Lu Tianling threw his head back with laughter and waved a ray of fiery sword light at the patriarch.","Whoosh!","Although he was the weakest, Yuwen Zonglin was still a latter nascent soul cultivator. He sneered at Lu Tianling’s attack and sent out an answering ray of sword radiance to intercept it.","“Hahaha, Lu Tianling, your lower rank spirit weapon Brightfire Slayer is unmatched in third rank cultivation empires. Why don’t you bring it out now?”","Spirit weapons were a rarity in third rank cultivation empires. Even lower ranked ones were exceedingly valuable. The ultimate treasure of the Darklake imperial family was also a lower rank spirit weapon.","The other six families only possessed ordinary paramount rank treasures, yet a newly risen clan possessed a spirit weapon! It made them green with envy and was the reason why the Yuwens, Ouyangs, and Lings hidden in the shadows were so eager to attack the Lus.","Ouyang Baitian beckoned and sent his hammer streaking toward Lu Tianling.","“Since you wish to see Brightfire Slayer, I’ll show you its capabilities!”","Ouyang Baitian and Yuwen Zonglin brightened. If the old man used his spirit weapon, he would have to call upon his full force. Whether or not he’d taken the poison pill, it was beyond what his current condition could endure.","Lu Tianling placed his hands together and summoned a shining swortsword between them. It blazed with fire and affected the flow of qi in the environment around it. The air exuded a suffocating heat.","Spirit weapons shouldn’t appear in third rank cultivation empires. Not even Dark Orchid Empire—a fourth rank one—often saw one!","Whoosh!","Brightfire Slayer abruptly transformed into a massive blade nine meters tall and shot at the golden hammer."]},{"number":2213,"title":"Chapter 2213: Chapter 2162.1: I Dug This Hole","paragraphs":["Chapter 2162.1: I Dug This Hole","An enormous blade of fire smashed into the massive hammer.","Pfft!","Standing at the front, Ouyang Baitian spat out a mouthful of blood as his weapon was likewise sent flying.","“How is this possible?!” Ashen-faced, the shocked Ouyang Baitian never dreamed that he wouldn’t be able to take even one of Lu Tianling’s moves.","“How is it not possible?!” Lu Tianling sneered and struck with Brightfire Slayer again.","Boom!","Another heat wave exploded through the air as Ouyang Baitian flew out like a kite on a broken string. He smashed viciously into the ground. Next to him, Yuwen Zonglin didn’t even have a chance to react before fire filled his field of view.","......","Lu Tianling was slightly pale and a tiny dribble of blood trickled out from the corner of his mouth, but his expression remained unchanged. He looked down at the two patriarchs that he’d smashed into the ground, then streaked back into the Lu complex in a ray of fiery sparks. He couldn't be bothered with saying more to them.","“Grandfather... really is a wily old fox. He was putting on a weak act before!” Lu Yun chuckled when he saw the old man disappear. He knew the effects of his pill. The Violet Orchid Ganoderma was a ninth rank spirit grass that was very rare in the world. However, a simple spirit grass was still worth less than the Nineturns Profound Life Pill.","All medicines were part poison and part cure. Spirit grasses contained other impurities in addition to their medicinal effects. Only when they were refined into pills could they be absorbed by cultivators.","What Lu Yun had created was a complete Violet Orchid Ganoderma that was pure medicine. It neared an immortal grass rank with no impurities and was more unadulterated than some pills.","As a latter nascent spirit cultivator, Lu Tianling easily absorbed the pill’s effects after one night of refinement.","......","Lu Yun could understand why his grandfather played the pig to eat the tiger and didn’t say anything to expose him. Instead, he called Lu Xuan to him and exited a back door while humming a small ditty.","He suddenly halted.","Humm!","The green Seal of the Multitude in his dantian burst with scintillating light. The entire seal began trembling as an inexplicable strength surged into it. The seal shuddered once more and released a vast amount of energy that surged into the “dao” character within his dantian.","That character was Lu Yun’s core origin and the heart of the Nine Chapters of Dao. The intangible character threw off radiance as the mysterious strength surged into it and solidified a tiny bit more.","Hongmeng qi circulated rapidly through Lu Yun’s body and he spontaneously broke through to mid stage first turn. His cultivation also rose to eighth level qi refinement.","All of this happened in a split second, leaving him stunned and dazed.","“What, what just happened?” he gasped.","Was this goodwill from the masses? He seemed to have... experienced such a cultivation method before. But the previous instance seemed to have something to do with a tree.","It has to do with that sealed experience again. Just what did I undergo before?","But where did this goodwill come from?","Another voice sounded at this time and interrupted his thoughts. “Young master, young master, milord wants you!” It was slightly shaky.","Lu Yun turned around to see grand steward He Wuheng running toward him. The man had shaken off his typical despondency and blazed with high spirits. His dantian and meridians were fully repaired. He would return to his previous cultivation level given enough time and break through to nascent soul.","Gratitude shown between his brows and sudden inspiration struck Lu Yun.","The will of the people... goodwill from the people... Is that what this is about?","His thoughts spun rapidly as something familiar seemed to dawn on the horizon. Raising an eyebrow, he smiled at the man. “First of all, congratulations to Uncle He for making a full recovery!”","“It’s all thanks to young master! If it wasn’t for young master’s favor, this old servant would be a cripple for the rest of my life!” He Wuheng answered in a shaking voice and took a deep breath. He knew everything that’d happened to Lu Yun during this time, how the young man had gained a powerful immortal for his master and traveled to the Celestial Realm Battlefront. He had greatly matured from the irredeemable thuggishness of before.","“Ah, yes, grandfather wants me? I’m not going yet.” Lu Yun blinked. “I have something more important to do. Come help me, Uncle He!”","“Huh?” He Wuheng paused.","“We’re gonna get rich!” Lu Yun grabbed the steward without further explanation and left through the back door.","There was nothing that He Wuheng could do about the young master not answering his grandfather’s summons. Although the grand steward was initial golden core, he was aways at a loss when facing the young man.","Lu Tianling was likely the only person in the entire clan who could exercise some control over Lu Yun, not to mention that He Wuheng owed a great debt of gratitude to the young man at present.","......","Being early morning, there were few people out on the streets. Additionally, three nascent soul powerhouses had just battled in mid air, so most of the cultivators in the city were cowering at home. They didn’t want to be affected by the backlash.","Thankfully, powerful formations were in place in the city. Their clash hadn’t resulted in tangible damage.","Even so, natural qi within several kilometers of the Lu residence was in complete disarray. It blocked the probing consciousnesses of others so no one knew what’d occurred.","Three talismans appeared in Lu Yun’s hands as they stood in a quiet alley. He slapped them onto himself, He Wuheng, and Lu Xuan. The three changed drastically with an accompanying mist of hazy radiance.","He Wuheng turned into a burly man, Lu Xuan was a middle-aged scholar, and Lu Yun looked like a different nobleman’s son.","“Transformation Talismans!” He Wuheng gasped. These were extraordinarily precious in the world of immortal cultivation as they fully transformed a cultivator’s presence and aura for six hours. Regular cultivators couldn’t see through their disguise—only cultivators who reached the soul separation stage and possessed thousands of strands of nascent spirit could see through such a talisman.","Soul separation cultivators were only found in fifth rank empires. In other words, Lu Yun’s talismans enabled him to do what he wished in third and fourth rank empires without running the risk of being exposed by anyone.","Hu Wuheng’s heart ached. Three Transformation Talismans were worth literal cities!","Lu Yun didn’t care in the least and rushed them along, “C’mon, let’s go let’s go. We’re gonna get rich!”","Get rich?! Do you know the three talismans that you just threw out are the riches?! He Wuheng howled inside.","Lu Yun took the lead and surreptitiously brought them to the street not too far from the Lu residence. Two massive potholes marked it and furious fire energy raged within them, burning down the houses closest to it.","As this was Lu territory, the cultivators that’d lived inside had hurriedly evacuated when the fight broke out. Two charcoal figures tried to climb out of the potholes. They looked at each other when their heads poked out and exchanged wry smiles.","“Hoi!!” rose a cruel, peevish voice. “I paved this road and I dug this hole. Leave behind your storage rings if you want to get out of it!”","Startled, their grips slackened and they rolled back down. They were Ouyang Baitian and Yuwen Zonglin that Lu Tianling had blasted down from the sky.","With the old general’s strength, he had no problem beating the two of them by himself. He didn’t even need his spirit weapon. So when Brightfire Slayer was deployed, the two were instantly defeated.","Although they were all latter nascent soul, he was the undisputed strongest of Dark City!","Lu Tianling was truly enraged this time. The two families had set aside dignity and propriety to use his grandson as an excuse for hostilities. He certainly wouldn’t show them any mercy. Thus, the two noble patriarchs were heavily injured and their nascent souls damaged as well.","The two had come with utmost confidence and full preparation, so they hadn’t brought any servants or followers. It was already unreasonable enough that they were attacking a grievously injured Lu Tianling. If they brought more men, it might alarm the imperial family and the emperor would involve himself.","Thus, it was the perfect set up for an opportunistic noble scion to take advantage of their injuries."]},{"number":2214,"title":"Chapter 2214: Chapter 2163.1: Explosion","paragraphs":["Chapter 2163.1: Explosion","The five paramount rank spirit stones came from the storage ring of the Lingtian general manager, back when Lu Yun robbed the Lingtian Pill Pavilion. There were only two dozen of them, so he used them very sparingly.","When the five spirit stones sank into the air, they formed a miniature Reverse Five Elements of Absolute Slaughter Formation after a series of ripples.","He Wuheng’s jaw dropped. Creating a formation with a wave of the hand? How did one characterize this kind of ability?","What happened next sent him into a daze.","Countless spirit talismans flew out of Lu Yun’s hands and vanished into the air. Next thing the Lu steward knew, the formation that’d just been created also winked out of sight. He couldn’t find it, no matter how he swept the air with his consciousness.","Lu Yun’s fingers flickered through hand seals as gray air currents gathered in his hands. Slowly, ever so slowly, the exquisite Reverse Five Elements of Absolute Slaughter Formation enveloped all of Black Maple Peak.","When he waved his hand again, the remaining paramount rank spirit stones sank into the grand formation.","“This... young master...” He Wuheng swallowed hard.","“Just a few tricks up my sleeves,” Lu Yun grinned brilliantly. Man, why can’t I call upon formula dao? Things wouldn’t be such a hassle if I could use formula dao!","Huh? Wait, what’s formula dao?","He couldn’t help but think of formula dao and it seemed to be tied to... someone. Someone he never wanted to forget, but had no choice but to temporarily forget...","Meanwhile, Lu Xuan relieved Yuwen Zonglin and Ouyang Baitian of their storage rings. He collected their personal weapons as well and handed them to his young master.","“You guys take these two.” Lu Yun tossed Ouyang Baitian’s Mountain Shaker and Yuwen Zonglin’s Turquoise Willow to He Wuheng and Lu Xuan.","For once, a trace of hesitation showed on the eternally expressionless Lu Xuan’s face. He Wuheng didn’t even dare catch the treasure. These were the personal weapons of two patriarchs—two upper rank treasures! Only the patriarch of a family had the right to use them. Others of the clan, even nascent soul elders, wielded only mid rank treasures.","“Well? Take them already, stop dragging your heels. It’s annoying.” Lu Yun chucked them to the ground and ignored the two. He focused on examining the two storage rings. “Tsk tsk tsk, it looks like these two families are very rich. Maybe ten thousand paramount spirit stones was too little to ask?”","He emptied their contents, transferring them to his own ring, then threw the now-awake and glaring patriarchs into the Reverse Five Elements of Absolute Slaughter Formation. They were unable to put up any resistance given that they were suppressed by his talismans and heavily injured.","“Who are you?” Ouyang Baitian ground out through a bleeding mouth.","“Heh heh heh heh heh, since when did nascent soul small fry have the privilege of knowing this gentleman’s name?” Lu Yun cackled, then fetched some treasures of the five elements from his storage ring and threw them into the formation. It spontaneously increased in strength.","He didn’t possess much in the way of resources, but thanks to the contents of the patriarchs’ rings, the formation was swiftly made complete.","Lu Yun was a formation grandmaster. While his cultivation level wasn’t high, he could more than handle a few nascent soul cultivators if he employed a formation. A true formation grandmaster could call upon the full defenses of heaven and earth with just a hundredth of the power of a formation.","Nascent soul small fry... just listen to him! He Wuheng’s cheek spasmed, but he was able to come to terms with his young master’s words when he thought of Lu Yun’s master.","What did a nascent soul cultivator count for?","“Young master, will we cause any trouble if we refine these treasures?” He Wuheng’s personal treasure had broken when he was crippled, so the upper rank Mountain Shaker was a perfect replacement.","“Trouble?” Lu Yun curled his lip. “How many of the Ouyangs and Yuwens sport treasure that was originally from us Lus? I’m just collecting some interest from them.”","Lu Xuan had already erased Yuwen Zonglin’s brand from Turquoise Willow and claimed it with his own blood. He made a cursory refinement of the item and stored it within his body.","Just as the patriarchs hung onto life by a thread, so were the brands on the treasures extremely weak. Lu Xuan alone was sufficient to erase the one on the sword. When He Wuheng saw what the guard had done, he hesitated no longer and refined Mountain Shaker as well.","Lu Yun sent two more talismans flying out with a gentle prod in the air. They sank into Ouyang Baitian and Yuwen Zonglin’s foreheads, vanishing without a trace.","......","The Ouyang and Yuwen representatives were quick onto the scene. It took less than an hour for one hundred combined experts to rush to Black Maple Peak. They were led by four nascent soul cultivators, twenty golden core experts, and the remaining of latter foundation establishment. Arriving in streaks of sword light, they swiftly surrounded the mountain that was fifteen kilometers across.","“Patriarch!”","“Elder brother!”","Nascent soul elder Yuwen Tuo led the Yuwen Clan, whereas Ouyang Baiyi led the Ouyang contingent. He was Ouyang Baitian’s younger brother. The two leaders were both mid nascent soul and followed by an initial nascent soul elder.","Since Darklake Empire was a third rank cultivation empire, latter nascent soul counted as a supreme powerhouse. There weren’t that many of them in the entire nation. The Ouyang had possessed more, but Lu Tianling killed one of them when he rushed their residence three months ago.","That these two clans could summon four nascent souls and twenty golden cores in an hour was quite remarkable. It went without saying that the foundation establishment cultivators were just cannon fodder.","Yuwen Tuo and Ouyang Baiyi almost wept blood when they saw their patriarchs.","“Save the patriarch!” Yuwen Tao possessed a fiery temper and sent his sword diving into Black Maple Peak.","“Formation!” Ouyang Baiyi kept more of his cool and roared for one hundred rays of sword light to surround the mountain. No one dared make any brash moves since both patriarchs were held below them. Otherwise, the joint offensive would’ve blown the mountain up as soon as they arrived.","Rumble!","Enormous ripples oscillated through the mountain when Yuwen Tuo entered it, as if it was an enormous lake. And then, the man disappeared from sight.","Within Black Maple Peak, Yuwen Zonglin and Ouyang Baitian sagged like shapeless sacks of potatoes.","“A formation!” Ouyang Baiyi jerked with surprise.","They’d scanned the entire peak with their consciousness before taking action and hadn’t discovered anything out of the ordinary. To think that this entire mountain would be ensconced by a huge formation!","Ruuuuumble.","Terrifying rumbles and Yuwen Tao’s furious roars echoed from the formation below.","“I say, that was fast! Have you guys prepared all of the spirit stones?” A cocky and unctuous voice sounded in the air over the mountain. “Twenty thousand paramount rank spirit stones... And now I’ve captured another one of your nascent soul elders. The Yuwens can pay another five thousand spirit stones!”","“You court death!” shouted the remaining nascent soul cultivator from the Yuwen Clan.","“Let's see who it is that courts death.”","RUMBLE!!","The formation stirred to motion again and hid the entire mountain from sight.","Someone challenging two of the seven major families already shocked the capital. Many of them wanted to watch the show at Black Maple Peak, but the Yuwen and Ouyang Clan didn’t permit an audience to form. They chased away any stranger who showed up. However, many powerhouses were sweeping the premises with their consciousness and had a full read on what was occurring.","The only ones who dared do so with impunity were the other major families of the city.","The enemy in the formation below was targeting only the Yuwens and Ouyangs. Those two had long allied with each other, so the other families were just watching the show. They wouldn’t interfere.","As for the Lus... Lu Tianling’s old wounds had flared up after that battle and he’d gone into closed door cultivation to recover. There was no one else worthy of note in that family apart from the old general. They had few golden core cultivators and thus no ability to kidnap the patriarchs. Therefore, no one suspected them and felt that it was the two families’ enemies taking advantage of the situation.","“You court death!”","Whoosh!","Ouyang Baiyi made the formation shudder when he struck it with a ray of sword light.","“What, you don’t want your patriarchs alive anymore?!” The voice inside the formation grew flustered.","“The position of patriarch goes to those with ability! There are heirs for the position if our patriarch dies! The dignity of the Ouyangs, however, cannot be sullied!” Ouyang Baiyi roared. His flying sword was also a mid rank treasure and it raised sword light several dozen meters tall that crashed down on the formation.","The formation trembled violently once more, but one set up by Lu Yun utilized endless power of heaven and earth and wouldn’t be broken by a nascent soul cultivator.","In a small forest fifty kilometers outside Black Maple Peak.","Lu Yun leaned against a tree in complete relaxation. Meanwhile, Lu Xuan and He Wuheng stood guard for each other as they refined the two upper rank treasures.","......","“That person is in the formation! We break the formation together!” Ouyang Baiyi became the rallying point, given that Yuwen Tuo was caught inside the formation. The ambitious Ouyang Baiyi had long wanted to be the patriarch, but never had a chance to since Ouyang Baitian was an intrepid, domineering strategist. If he could use this opportunity to eliminate Ouyang Baitian, the next Ouyang patriarch would be him!","The Ouyang and Yuwen Clans had been thoroughly humiliated this time. Their patriarchs had been kidnapped and held for ransom. Even if Ouyang Baitian and Yuwen Zonglin returned safely to their families, they wouldn’t have the face to continue in their respective positions.","However, a living Ouyang Baitian was also a threat to Ouyang Baiyi. A plethora of intrigues and plots surged beneath the surface in families as large as the two clans.","Though the Yuwen Clan hesitated, they knew they could not dither in a matter that involved family pride. In the eyes of the great families, face was more important than anything!","No one would respect the clan if they lost face, eventually resulting in a gradual drifting away of the family’s descendants and disciples. The clan would inevitably decline.","Thus, gains and losses of the moment didn’t mean anything. Not to mention, if the enemy really did kill the two patriarchs, that would ignite a blood feud. The two clans were so influential in the empire that they could even borrow the imperial family and use the entire nation’s might to hunt down the perpetrator.","A joint offensive of one hundred cultivators created a massive crack in the formation. Within it, Yuwen Tuo brightened and added his power to the attack.","Rumble!!","Black Maple Peak shuddered and the formation in the air shattered with immense energy ripples."]},{"number":2215,"title":"Chapter 2215: Chapter 2163.2: Explosion","paragraphs":["Chapter 2163.2: Explosion","In the clearing of Black Maple Peak, Yuwen Zonglin and Ouyang Baitian weakly lifted their heads. They sighed in unison when they saw one hundred cultivators in the air.","“The opponent is too arrogant. This formation seems dominating, but it couldn’t withstand a single combined blow from three nascent souls and twenty golden cores!” Ouyang Baiyi descended from the sky and loftily looked down at his older brother sprawled on the ground.","“Where is he?” Ouyang Baiyi looked down his nose at Ouyang Baitian.","The man shook his head.","“He should be somewhere in the mountain. Fan out!” Yuwen Tuo shouted to his men as he helped up Yuwen Zonglin.","......","“Oh? They broke the formation? That was a bit slower than I thought.” Fifty kilometers away, Lu Yun took a bite out of a spirit fruit and crushed two spirit talismans he’d placed next to him.","......","Within Black Maple Peak.","Ouyang Baitian paled as he looked at Ouyang Baiyi and opened his mouth, seeming to want to say something. He flushed unnaturally before he could get a word out and golden light burst out of his dantian.","“No!” Being mid nascent soul powerhouses, Ouyang Baiyi and Yuwen Tuo sensed something off about the situation and immediately rose into the air on the back of sword light.","Humm!","A second formation snapped into place outside the mountain and prevented them from leaving.","Boom!","Boom!","Yuwen Zonglin and Ouyang Baitian detonated their nascent souls!","Power sufficient to destroy heaven and earth filled the vicinity, obliterating the fifteen kilometers of Black Maple Peak.","The entire world fell silent.","......","The power generated by the self-denotation of one nascent spirit cultivator was unfathomable. A cultivator of the same level would die if they were caught in the center of the explosion. There were two such cultivators self-detonating at the same time in the mountain!","Although Yuwen Zonglin and Ouyang Baitian were heavily injured and their nascent souls impacted, their core origin was unharmed. The explosion of two nascent souls at the same time was enough to level Black Maple Peak.","If it wasn’t for a protective formation around the mountain keeping the recoil in, the shockwaves might’ve even reached Dark City fifty kilometers away.","All that was left of the mountain now was a massive pit that stretched thirty meters across. It was a pit that buried the Ouyang and Yuwen Clans.","......","“Alright, show’s over, time to go home.” Lu Yun stretched lazily and jumped down from the tree.","Lu Xuan and He Wuheng stood up at the same time. They sensed startling energy ripples from fifty kilometers out, but didn’t know what’d happened.","“Young master, don’t we want the twenty thousand ransom anymore?” He Wuheng hesitated.","“Twenty thousand paramount spirit stones?” Lu Yun snorted with laughter. “We’ll take it from their family mines if we want spirit stones. We don’t need to go to the trouble of kidnapping their people.”","Get rich?","To Lu Yun, the lives of the one hundred powerhouses were the real wealth!","Paramount rank spirit stones?","Just a small trick to provoke the enemy into losing their temper. It was their fault for valuing their dignity so much.","......","The capital was in an uproar by the time Lu Yun returned. First Ouyang Baitian and Yuwen Zonglin jointly challenged the strongest of Dark City—Lu Tianling—and were soundly defeated.","Then, the two patriarchs were kidnapped and held for ten thousand paramount rank spirit stones each. It stunned the city’s cultivators when the word spread. Capturing two mighty patriarchs and extorting payment from their families... The world had gone mad!","What happened next overwhelmed the city and sent the other four families and imperial family into raging fury!","The latter had been watching on the sidelines and even with some schadenfreude. However, news of the complete demise of Ouyang Baitian, Yuwen Zonglin, and the one hundred cultivators sent to rescue them took the empire by storm.","It wasn’t just a loss to the two families, but a loss to Darklake Cultivation Empire at large! That was one hundred powerful cultivators and a handful of nascent soul experts!","It rocked Darklake and even alarmed some of her neighbors. Nascent soul powerhouses were the pillars of third rank cultivation empires. These empires were deemed third rank due to the presence of nascent soul heavyweights.","In the world of cultivation, cultivation empires were divided into nine ranks. First rank empires were deemed thus if they possessed foundation establishment cultivators, second rank if they had golden core, and so on and so forth.","Foundation establishment, golden core, nascent soul, soul projection, soul separation, combination, tribulation, and awakened. There were eight ranks in total that corresponded to eight ranks of cultivation empires. The legendary ninth rank empire boasted of wandering immortals.","Destruction of the physical body and reassembly of the nascent soul made one a wandering immortal.","Being a third rank empire, nascent soul cultivators were the foundation of Darklake Empire. Every nascent soul powerhouse was extremely precious to Darklake, and now six had died in one fell swoop—including two patriarchs of the seven great families! Twenty golden core cultivators had died along with them, an enormous loss that cut to the heart of even Darklake—first among the third rank empires.","Not to mention, their strongest Lu Tianling was heavily injured at the moment!","Fear and danger were found around every corner in Darklake and every blade of grass and tree was a potential enemy. The Ouyang and Yuwen Clans were nearly mad with fury.","......","Meanwhile, the source of the kerfuffle sauntered back home like none of this had anything to do with him. At a time like this, no one paid attention to a useless noble son loitering on the streets.","Lu Xuan and He Wuheng naturally knew what’d happened when they returned to the capital with their young master. As strong as their composure was, they were also immensely startled by the turmoil. They finally understood just what they’d accomplished on this trip outside the residence.","What did Lu Yun care about the commotion? Those were people who wanted him dead. Why would he keep himself in check if he had a chance to eliminate the enemy?","He wasn’t a saint—he’d fight anyone who called him a saint!","And it was just a few nascent soul cultivators. If it really ended up threatening Darklake’s security... he’d just compensate the empire then.","“Lu Yun, where have you been all morning?”","The young man was greeted by a brooding Lu Xiaochi as soon as he entered the front door.","“Eh, nothing much. Just went out for a walk,” Lu Yun glossed things over.","“Second master...” He Wuheng swallowed hard and found it difficult to say more.","Lu Xiaochi nodded at the grand steward and proclaimed righteously, “Spies from our enemies have infiltrated Darklake—the Ouyangs and Yuwens have suffered much from it. Even their patriarchs are dead, so you should stay home for a while.”","The seven great families were starting to suspect that the disaster that’d visited their brethren was the work of Darklake’s number one enemy—the Tianlong Empire.","“You are an important person of the Lu Clan and your grandfather’s biggest treasure. Keep in mind that they may very well target you to threaten your grandfather!” Lu Xiaochi declared solemnly.","Lu Yun bobbed his head up and down, the very image of a biddable child.","......","Lu Xiaochi breathed out much more easily when he watched Lu Yun’s departing back. This young master was the clan’s only weakness.","“How are you, Uncle He?” He smiled gently at the recovered He Wuheng.","“Second master... this old servant has a report to make to the patriarch!” He Wuheng took a deep breath.","“Foster father?” Lu Xiaochi frowned. “Foster father entered closed door cultivation after the fight this morning.”","Lu Tianling had sent He Wuheng to tell the young man to curtail his activities because his grandfather was entering closed door cultivation. Who would’ve thought that the steward would be commandeered into other tasks instead?","Lu Tianling had no choice but to enter closed door cultivation before receiving a response.","“Closed door cultivation?” He Wuheng smiled with resignation. “Second master, let us go to a secret chamber!”","......","“What?!” Lu Xiaochi gaped at the family steward, his mind buzzing and not knowing what to say.","“You mean everything that happened today is a result of that little bastard?” Lu Xiaochi heaved for breath and stared wide-eyed. His voice trembled from the news.","He Wuheng nodded ruefully and manifested a golden hammer in his hand. It was Ouyang Baitian’s personal treasure—upper rank Mountain Shaker.","“This... this...” Lu Xiaochi was so shocked that his mind went blank. “This kid really knows how to get himself into trouble.”","\"Second master, we must let the patriarch know. It would result in the extermination of our clan if someone else finds out,” He Wuheng said worriedly.","“Extermination of the clan...?” Lu Xiaochi cocked his head as a meaningful smile appeared on his lips. “Darklake is small puddle—how much trouble can there be even if it’s turned upside down? Who would dare exterminate us? There’s no need to bother foster father with this kind of matter.”","A mysterious expression on his face, Lu Xiaochi waved off the steward’s concerns.","......","\"Young master young master, bad news! Bad news!” Lan’er hurriedly ran up to Lu Yun when he returned with Lu Xuan.","“What is it?” Lu Yun smiled to see his maid.","“Miss Fengwu is trapped inside the Ascella Formation!” she said urgently. [1]","Lu Tianling had turned the entire Lu complex into a Major Cycle Nebula Formation. It was comprised of multiple smaller formations and the Ascella Formation was one of them. Being one that trapped its targets, even golden core cultivators would find it difficult to escape once they were caught within.","“Miss Fengwu?” Lu Yun blinked, then smiled as a beautiful form flashed through his mind. “Let’s go and see this Miss Fengwu!”","Fengwu was a girl traveling by herself that Lu Yun had encountered on the streets of Dark City half a year ago. She was so captivating that the number two beauty of the city—Yuwen Shengxiang—paled far in comparison to her.","As the greatest pestilence of the capital, Lu Yun naturally captured her and brought her home when he saw her. When he wanted to defile her, Lu Tianling stopped him and almost broke his legs.","Lu Yun had yet to undergo reincarnation then and was not the current Lu Yun that he was now. His grandfather had warned him that he was not allowed to lose his virginity before he reached foundation establishment. If he did, he would be exiled from the family.","Lu Yun conducted all manner of wild escapades and was the height of lawlessness, but his grandfather kept him strictly in check when it came to affairs between man and woman. He was so strict that Lu Yun didn’t dare try to touch his grandfather’s bottom line.","Fengwu’s face drained of color when she heard Lu Tianling’s words. She’d thought she’d escaped calamity, but after the young man reached foundation establishment...","Therefore, she spent the past half year trying to escape from the Lu residence. Layered with protection as it was from the Major Cycle Nebula Formation, there was nowhere she could go.","The great formation had shook this morning when Ouyang Baitian’s hammer came down. She’d thought her chance had arrived and tried to make a run for it, but ended up trapped in the Ascella Formation.","1. Ascella is a star located in the Sagittarius constellation. ☜"]},{"number":2216,"title":"Chapter 2216: Chapter 2164.1: Fengxian Wu","paragraphs":["Chapter 2164.1: Fengxian Wu","A lithe woman wearing a red silk dress and a thin veil across her face ran in circles inside the Ascella Formation, trying to find the exit. It was only three meters wide, but she couldn’t walk out of this range no matter how she tried.","Lu Yun stood outside the formation and sized up its prey.","“No wonder grandfather didn’t allow me to touch her, but wouldn’t let her go either. She’s not an ordinary person.” He cocked his head as his fingers flew through a few hand seals, making the smoothly operating Ascella Formation to grind to a temporary halt.","Grandfather wouldn’t let him touch her before, and now he wasn’t the slightest bit interested in her. Not because of the three thousand reincarnations, but because there were two faint figures at the bottom of his heart. Even though he’d forgotten them for now, they still left an imprint on his heart.","It seemed that everything he did now, including forgetting them... was for them. He did so in order to remember them anew in the future.","“Hmm?” The woman in red frowned and spun around, facing a Lu Yun who wore an amused expression on his face. “Lu Yun!” Her voice was cold and her fingers twitched, as if wanting to attack the young man.","However, she subconsciously glanced at the ramrod straight Lu Xuan next to him, then at the formation around her. There was nothing else she could do but sag with resignation.","“It’s been a while, Miss Feng. Have you been well?” Lu Yun’s gaze brazenly roved over her body. A meaningful upturn curved his lips.","Fengwu's face turned stiff and she snorted frostily, “Thanks to young master Lu’s care, everything is well.”","“That is good...” He continued scanning her body, particularly the especially sensitive areas. The bottom of his eyes, however, were as clear as water. There was no lustfulness to be found there.","“Lu Yun!” Fengwu couldn’t flounce off, but neither could she just stand there for Lu Yun to look his fill. She was incredibly irritated—although the young man had stopped the formation, he hadn’t opened it to let her out.","“Eh? What are you still doing here, Miss Fengwu? Grandfather’s gone into closed door cultivation, so the formation is operating on its own. While I can pause it, I can’t hold it like this for long.” Lu Yun looked at Fengwu with equal parts surprise and bafflement.","“How, how am I supposed to leave when you haven’t opened it?!” Fengwu snapped.","She’s a child, alright, that’s all it took to make her angry. Although a golden core cultivation level isn’t weak, how did she make it to Dark City without getting captured along the way? Lu Yun smirked to see Fengwu turn beet red with anger. “Aiyaya, just look at me. How come I haven’t opened the formation yet?”","And yet, he did nothing and remained sizing up Fengwu.","Lan’er burst into snorts of laughter; she could sense Lu Yun’s changes over this period of time. The previous young master had either hit her or beat her, but while his general behavior remained the same after waking up, he was much more caring toward her than before.","Lan’er was a fourteen year old girl with a simple nature. She could discern who was good to her and who wasn’t. Right now, she could tell that although Lu Yun’s gaze was aggressive, it was more teasing than anything else. But as someone bogged down by the details, Fengwu naturally missed the change.","“You!” Fengwu ground her teeth, but could do nothing about her situation.","Lu Yun normally fawned over her and curried favor with her. Other than a lack of personal freedom, her treatment was on par with the young master in the Lu residence. She’d thought she could escape thanks to the enormous upheaval today. Who would’ve thought that a mere Ascella Formation would trap her?","Lu Yun judged it a good stopping point for his teasing and waved his hand, allowing Fengwu to walk out.","“Aren’t you something, Lu Yun!” Fengwu bit off and turned to leave.","“Aiyaya, why are you leaving just like this, Miss Fengwu? It’s been so long since we’ve seen each other. Come, let us have a good chat.” Lu Yun shamelessly followed after her and kept up a litany of ingratiating remarks while he focused on her chest.","Fengwu’s face twisted with distaste—she felt like there were countless ants crawling over her body. It was the worst possible feeling.","“Lu Yun, I can dig your eyes out, you know!” she spat out with a sudden stop.","“Eh?” The young man played innocent. “What makes you say that, Miss Fengwu?”","His eyes remained busy looking at her chest.","Fengwu wanted to cry. No one had ever treated her with such disrespect in her entire life! The men she normally met either treated her as a goddess or at the very least, with extreme respect. Even the previous Lu Yun only had fawning smiles for her when he saw her. Although his gaze was lecherous, he’d only dared sneak peeks, not brazenly disrespect her like he did now.","Apparently, someone had sent this kid into a coma for three months—why hadn’t they just beaten him to death?!","“Oh, yes,” Lu Yun suddenly thought of something. “The third rank pill that I gave Miss Fengwu last time—the Origin Nurturing Pill. I would request that the miss return it, please.”","He suddenly stepped in front of her and blocked her way.","“You...” Fengwu paused, not knowing how to react. Although it’d only been a third rank pill, it had been very useful to her. She’d refined it the day he gave it to her.","Lu Yun had given it to her because he wanted to find favor in her eyes; he’d forced her to accept it, but now wanted it back after so much time had passed? That was... the height of shamelessness!","It was her first time encountering such a situation, so she didn’t know what to do.","“Miss Feng knows the current circumstances of the Lu Clan as well, we’re very tight on funds! The Origin Nurturing Pill is a third rank pill. There’s not that many third rank pills in the empire, so... ai!” Lu Yun sighed heavily despite himself. “Please return it, miss!”","“You’re completely shameless!” was all that Fengwu managed after grinding her teeth.","Amusement sparkled deep in Lu Yun’s eyes while he answered carelessly, “Shameless? Miss Feng, how am I shameless? Please return it to me!”","“You... I’ve already eaten and refined it!” Fengwu ground her teeth even harder.","“Huh? Refined it?” Lu Yun lifted his head blankly and stared at Fengwu’s face veil, as if wanting to lift it through the sheer force of his gaze. “I remember Miss Feng said that she would rather die than ever eat my pill? Did it taste good?”","“You...” Fengwu flushed bright red and her eyes seemed ready to spit fire. How dare this kid toy with her like this?! Thank goodness only Lan’er and the wooden Lu Xuan were around. I just need to have a thick enough face to brush this off!","Lu Yun remained expressionless, like he hadn’t heard anything. Lan’er’s eyes were curved into crescents and her shoulders shook from the force of her laughter. She’d been present when the young master gave the pill to Fengwu. The maid completely remembered what the woman had said back then.","“Stop wasting your time and efforts. I would rather die here than eat a pill from a evildoer like you!”","Lu Yun... had put the pill down and left sheepishly.","So it turned out that the proud Miss Feng had refined it as soon as they’d left!","“I’m sure you’re joking, Miss Feng.” Lu Yun stroked his chin. “How would someone as proud as you go back on their word? The pill must be stored on you somewhere and you’ve said all this to anger me. How about this, permit me to search your body?”","He reached out with both hands before she could respond and reached for her chest.","“Get away from me!” Fengwu shrieked and released a burst of true origin from her body. It immediately sent Lu Yun flying and she quickly backed up, staring coldly at the Lu young master.","Lu Xuan looked sharply at her and snowy radiance rose from his form. He shifted forward and stabbed at the center of her forehead.","Fengwu sniffed coldly and quickly made some hand seals. As she moved, the image of a kaleidoscopic phoenix appeared behind her and shifted ethereally according to her movements.","Bam!","Lu Xuan was also sent flying, along with his sword. He remained unmoved and called upon his sword, sending a ray of turquoise sword light out from his hand.","“An upper rank treasure? How does a deathsworn of a minor Lu Clan own an upper rank treasure?” Fengwu was startled to see the sword light, but burst into laughter. “So what if you have an upper rank treasure? Your skill with the sword... Bah, can this even be called skill?”","Instead of responding herself, the phoenix behind her rebuffed Lu Xuan’s sword light and sent Turquoise Willow flying.","Lu Xuan spat out a mouthful of blood.","“Enough,” Lu Yun said.","A pale Lu Xuan returned to his post behind the young master like nothing had happened. Turquoise Willow vanished as a streak of light into his body.","“Hahaha, there is much more to Miss Feng than meets the eye! A qi refinement fellow like me was able to take a golden core powerhouse alive? Tsk tsk, should I shower myself with some compliments?” Lu Yun stroked his chin and smirked at Fengwu.","She stared frostily back at him and it seemed like her body was bathed in a pillar of flame. “How would you have possibly captured me if not for the fact that I was gravely injured?”","“Oh I see,” Lu Yun nodded. “So you owe me a great debt of gratitude instead? I am actually your savior?”","“Shameless!” Fengwu’s eyes nearly spat fire.","Lu Yun continued as if he hadn’t heard a thing. He shook his head and said with great self-satisfaction, “Miss Feng is a stunning beauty and was heavily injured... If it wasn’t for this young master bringing you home with me and ensuring your safety... you would be in very ghastly straits now.","“Uh uh uh, don’t be in a rush to refute me. There are more noble scions than this young master in Dark City. If you’d met Zhao Chenguang or Yu Shuai, you’d already be their bedwarmers.”","Fengwu’s eyes blazed when she heard the term bedwarmer, but Lu Yun spoke the truth. If it hadn’t been for Lu Tianling, she would already be a toy for Lu Yun’s lustful whims.","The elders of the other great families rarely interfered with the activities of the good-for-nothings in their clans."]},{"number":2217,"title":"Chapter 2217: Chapter 2164.2: Fengxian Wu","paragraphs":["Chapter 2164.2: Fengxian Wu","“Besides, didn’t Miss Feng recover from your wounds because of the Origin Nurturing Pill? Just this alone means that Miss Feng should be properly thanking this young master.” There was no sign of lasciviousness to be seen in Lu Yun now.","Fengwu had been hiding her strength all along; she’d perfectly concealed her cultivation at foundation establishment. Perhaps Lu Tianling had seen through her, but everyone else in the Lu residence thought she was just initial foundation establishment.","Who would’ve fathomed that this fragile woman would turn out to be an initial golden core powerhouse?","Although this was within Lu Yun’s expectations, she likely would’ve played the pig to eat the tiger to the very end if he hadn’t thrown her off balance and forced her to reveal her trump cards. Fengwu was inexperienced in the ways of the world—her experience was essentially zero—but she maintained an airtight lock on her privacy.","Regardless, such a person was essentially defenseless in front of Lu Yun. The personal capabilities that she’d hide for half a year were quickly revealed in full.","Fengwu knew that she’d fallen for a trap when she saw Lu Yun’s expression. She retracted the phoenix image and said coldly, “There’s nothing I wouldn’t like more than to kill you right now.”","“Kill me?” Lu Yun snorted with laughter. “Lan’er, Lu Xuan, did you guys hear that? This woman wants to kill me!”","Lan’er’s head alertly bobbed up and down while sword light appeared in Lu Xuan’s hand again. He stared intently at the woman, ready to leap into action at any time.","“The Ouyangs and Yuwens died to spies from an enemy nation earlier today, they even lost their patriarchs. Miss Feng is a cultivator not from Dark City. This young master strongly suspects that you are that hand in the shadows! Do you know the magnitude of your crimes?! Not even the emperor can save you now!” Lu Yun hectored righteously.","The typically aloof Lu Xuan’s face began spasming when he heard this. Meanwhile, Fengwu’s jaw dropped. She’d been trapped in the formation all morning and hadn’t known about any of this.","“Nonsense! Your grandfather injured the two patriarchs, what does it have to do with me!?” Fengwu was well aware of her current straits. Although her background was impressive and the deaths of a few nascent soul cultivators didn’t mean much, she would be in for some trouble if she didn’t handle this matter properly.","“My grandfather? My grandfather is a valued subject of Darklake Empire and colleagues with the patriarchs of the Ouyang and Yuwen Clans. They jointly protect the nation, so how would he cut off his own arms?!” Lu Yun pressed his position and didn’t cede any mental ground.","Lu Xuan watched with a strange expression—the two patriarchs and nearly one hundred powerhouses from the two families had died to his own young master’s machinations. So why was he assigning all the blame to a young woman...?","As devoutly loyal as Lu Xuan was to the Lus, wholly without question, even he had to marvel at how thick-skinned his young master was.","Fengwu was speechless. She’d developed a deep understanding of Lu Tianling’s character over the past six months. He was a just, aboveboard, and selfless individual who would never shake Darklake’s foundation for personal reasons.","The only exception was when he charged into the Ouyang residence three months ago because he’d thought Lu Yun was dead. If no one had later notified him that his grandson was still alive, he likely would’ve stomped the entire clan into the ground.","Other than that, he only lectured the two patriarchs when they came calling and threw them out. He didn’t seek to kill them.","In Lu Yun’s words, his grandfather was too good for his own good.","“I was trapped in that formation all morning! How could I have done anything?!” fumed Fengwu.","“Maybe you have co-conspirators?” Lu Yun leaned against a pillar and proposed lazily.","“Co-conspirators?? If I did, would I be here?!” Fengwu had ground her teeth so much by this point that they were on the verge of cracking.","“Haha!” Lu Yun barked with laughter. “This young master is the only grandson of the war god of Darklake. Who knows, maybe you let yourself be captured so you could gather intel at the Lu residence?”","“Y-you-you...” Fengwu was nearly crying with anger. The kid was too infuriating! The entire complex was surrounded by the Major Cycle Nebula Formation. It was a premier formation even in her homeland, so what intel was she supposed to gather??","The Lu residence was Lu Tianling’s territory. No other faction dared send even the hint of a spy. The other six clans had tried their best when the clan was first established, but their people either vanished from existence or turned into deathsworn devoted to the Lus.","A sudden thought struck Fengwu.","“What if I tell you that I can break the restriction on your second uncle?”","“Oh?” Lu Yun blinked. This was wholly unexpected!","“Your second uncle has fallen victim to the most vicious Severed Meridians Hold! There is no answer for it in the entire world, much less a third rank cultivation empire!” Fengwu stuck her nose in the air. “But I know how!”","The second Lu master and Lu Yun had been like fire and water before—they either jeered at each other when their paths crossed or completely ignored the other’s presence. Lu Yun’s","complete attitude change upon awakening had long become the talk of the complex.","“If you don’t hand over the way to cure second uncle, I will defile you first and then kill you, then defile and kill you again!” Lu Yun cackled and bore down on Fengwu.","“Hmph!” Fengwu no longer doubted anything when she saw the young man’s expression. The kid was irredeemable trash! She’d thought that he was possibly provoking her on purpose to force her secrets out of her... but it looked like she’d thought too highly of the kid.","Off to the side, Lu Xiaochi and He Wuheng were hidden in another formation and watching the scene play out.","“What is this kid trying to do?” Lu Xiaochi didn’t know whether to laugh or cry as he watched the two youngsters hurl insults at each other.","“Miss Fengwu is no ordinary person. Milord saw it long ago, so I’m sure the young master sees it too.” He Wuheng practically worshiped the ground that Lu Yun walked on now. The young man had eliminated one hundred powerhouses from the Ouyang and Yuwen Clans with a wave of his hand. Who in the Lu Clan didn’t want to do something like this?","No one could’ve fathomed that their good-for-nothing young master would manage the deed!","“This Fengwu is very likely from an upper rank cultivation empire. Her dao method of Unmoving Phoenix isn’t something that an ordinary family would possess. But she knows about the Severed Meridians Hold and has a way to break it?” Lu Xiaochi frowned slightly.","Severed Meridians Hold was a restriction that someone from the foremost sect of the Dark Orchid Empire—the Nineheavens Pagoda—had planted in him. As a sect of a mere fourth rank empire, it was impossible for the Nineheavens Pagoda to own such a vicious restriction.","Lu Xiaochi was beginning to suspect this Miss Fengwu, and he still hadn’t determined what his nephew wanted with her after ruffling her feathers for so long.","The kaleidoscope phoenix formed behind Fengu again and circled in the air.","“Unmoving Phoenix?” Lu Yun grinned. “Don’t forget, Fengwu, this is the Lu residence. The entire complex is enclosed by a formation. It would be such an easy task if this young master wished to kill you or make you streak in front of everyone.”","He flicked his finger and sent a ray of light out of it.","Rumble!","Seven scintillating stars winked into existence in the sky—the Big Dipper. Somehow, Lu Yun had brought Fengwu within range of the Big Dipper Formation!","The Ascella Formation trapped while the Big Dipper Formation killed.","“You!” Fengwu looked around with shock. She could easily sense the vast might of pressure from heaven and earth. As domineering as her Unmoving Phoenix was, to the point of sweeping all opponents on the same level as her, it was weak to the point of insignificance when up against the Major Cycle Nebula Formation.","Not to mention, Lu Yun didn’t desire to kill her. He wanted to make her run naked through the residence!","“I’ll tell you how!” Fengwu wanted to slap herself across the face. Wasn’t this just making trouble for herself??","Lu Yun seemed to have become a completely different person after he woke up. She could easily beguile him before, but although he appeared just as lascivious as ever, his attitude had undergone a complete change.","He’d been a mean dog three months ago. Although cruel, he would heel and obey if she waved a bone in his face. Lu Yun now? He was a starving wolf. If she waved a bone at him now, he would gobble her and the bone!","It was the first time that Fengwu made a concession.","Lu Yun smiled. Someone from a lofty, noble family like Fengwu despised a grassroots cultivator like him from the bottom of her heart. Indeed, to someone like her, all of Darklake Empire was just a remote backwater.","The initial concession was the start of a slippery slope—and that was Lu Yun’s goal.","There was much to be harvested from Fengwu and he would take full advantage of the rich pickings close at hand. At the same time, he was well aware that someone like her was immensely proud. If he wanted to smoothly benefit from her presence, then he needed to dull the edge of her pride.","“Give me a jade slip.” Fengwu’s expression was foreboding beneath her face veil and her tone could freeze water.","Lu Yun retrieved a blank jade slip from his storage ring and tossed it over.","She filled it with her consciousness, etched some material, then returned it to him.","“I would also request the privilege of knowing Miss Fengwu’s name.” Lu Yun crooked his finger when he accepted the jade slip, making the Big Dipper Formation tremble.","“Compound surname Fengxian, single character Wu.” Fengwu... Fengxian Wu glared viciously at Lu Yun before stomping off.","Lu Yun ignored her, focusing instead on the jade slip that he put into his storage ring.","......","“Damned thief and blasted ugly! How would I be in these straits if it wasn’t for you?! I’m being thoroughly insulted and bullied by a country bumpkin!” Fengxian Wu had destroyed a veritable army of tables and chairs in an exquisite residence.","“What ‘I only take wealth and not your body, or I’ll only take your body but not your life’?! You took all of my belongings and smashed the Transformation Jade. I wouldn’t be so poorly off if it wasn’t for you!” She plopped to the ground in an angry huff, angriest not at Lu Yun, but at the robber that’d robbed her clean of everything she’d owned!"]},{"number":2218,"title":"Chapter 2218: Chapter 2165.1: Shengxiang","paragraphs":["Chapter 2165.1: Shengxiang","“Just what are you doing, Lu Yun? What did you provoke that Fengxian Wu for?” Lu Xiaochi appeared soon after Lu Yun returned to his yard. He called their guest Fengxian Wu, not Fengwu. Plainly, he’d overheard their conversation.","The second master was accompanied by a rather large surge of goodwill.","“Goodwill?” Lu Yun ignored his uncle and looked behind Lu Xiaochi.","He Wuheng followed the second master’s footsteps and looked at Lu Yun with both adoration and his usual respect.","Oh? Does collecting goodwill mean more than making people thankful? Is goodwill also created when I do something that makes them think highly of me?","Goodwill resulted from the strength absorbed by the Seal of the Multitudes. Any positive emotion tied to Lu Yun, such as gratitude or adoration, created a mysterious power that was goodwill. This seemed a bit different from the tree of his subconscious memories.","He Wuheng’s goodwill toward Lu Yun lasted only a few breaths before vanishing. Yet the Hongmeng qi created from that momentary goodwill was the equivalent of ten days worth of cultivation! Although he was far from reaching latter first turn, it shone light on another avenue for Lu Yun.","“If one He Wuheng is enough to help me break through to mid first turn and save me ten days of hard cultivating... The what about ten, one hundred, or one thousand He Wuhengs...?” A radiant smile rose on Lu Yun’s face.","Lu Xiaochi snorted to see his nephew pause, then grin the same way the boy had when speaking with Fengxian Wu—lewd and utterly debauched.","“Ahem...” Lu Yun returned to his senses and looked at his second uncle with confusion. “What might second uncle need?” He was in a very good mood and greeted Lu Xiaochi merrily.","“I asked you, what were you doing provoking Fengxian Wu?” Lu Xiaochi huffed back.","“Eh... to get the way to break the Severed Meridians Hold?” Lu Yun still wore a devil-may-care smile that made Lu Xiaochi’s hand itch to slap him.","“Didn’t you say that you’d be able to do it once you reached foundation establishment?” the man frowned.","“I did and I can, but so can Fengxian Wu’s method,” Lu Yun responded in a lackadaisical manner.","Bright light shone out of Lu Xiaochi’s eyes.","“While her method can also break the restriction, it will end uncle’s path to becoming an immortal. Once we break the Severed Meridians Hold using her way, your path to immortality will come to an end,” Lu Yun said solemnly as the smile dropped off his face.","Lu Xiaochi, He Wuheng, Lu Xuan, and Lan’er’s expressions froze.","Becoming an immortal?","There were indeed immortals in the world of immortal dao civilization, and quite a few of them. But one from a third rank Darklake Empire? This was the stuff of legends!","It’d never happened before in the nation’s history.","Breaking through nascent soul to reach soul projection was already a tremendous feat that came about once in a hundred years. No one had ever heard of someone from Darklake ascending to immortality!","If there was such a lucky soul, they would immediately be freed of Dark Orchid Empire’s constraints. Even a soul projection powerhouse wouldn’t be subject to that empire’s whims.","“You can’t possibly think that I can become an immortal after my restriction is broken,” Lu Xiaochi said ruefully. Although his potential was unparalleled and he’d coalesced a nascent soul at thirty years old—an incredible achievement in Darklake Empire—that was still nothing if viewed from the lens of some of the higher level cultivation empires.","“You can.” Lu Yun nodded.","Lu Xiaochi paused, dazed.","“Don’t forget who my master is,” Lu Yun continued proudly.","“An immortal...” Lu Xiaochi took a deep breath, hope gleaming at the very bottom of his eyes.","“Second uncle, you have a high status in the family. Although you’re grandfather’s foster son, you’re a core figure of the clan. It won’t stay a secret for long if the restriction on your body is broken. Our enemies will investigate, but all we have to do then is attribute everything to the wondrous Fengxian Wu,” Lu Yun said casually.","Lu Xiaochi inclined his head, upwardly revising his opinion of the young man. There was no solution to the Severed Meridians Hold to be found in a third rank empire. If it was suddenly undone, the family’s enemies would send people to look into things and potentially discover clues that things were not as they were supposed to be.","Although Lu Yun had an immortal for a master, his master was not here for the moment. It would be exceedingly easy for their enemies to kill him.","What surprised Lu Xiaochi was that his nephew had guessed that the family had enemies, and that they weren’t the other families of Darklake Empire.","“Is there anything else, second uncle?” Lu Yun asked again.","Lu Xiaochi shook his head. “Since you know that the family has enemies, you should rein yourself in a little. Your grandfather doesn’t think much of the families in the empire. Although they attack us using you as an excuse, your grandfather pays them no heed so long as you’re alright.” Lu Xiaochi paused, then said, “This is just trials and tests for you.”","“Trials and tests?” Lu Yun chuckled. “Then let them continue. Your nephew is unwise in the ways of the world and needs a great deal of tempering.”","Lu Xiaochi rolled his eyes. “Unwise in the ways of the world? You were so unwise that you ensured the deaths of the Yuwen and Ouyang patriarchs—do you need more tempering?”","Lu Yun nodded. He seemed to have come to this world for this particular trial.","“Whatever, do as you wish. Just don’t go overboard and give our enemies something to threaten your grandfather with,” Lu Xiaochi smiled with resignation.","“Young master...” Lan’er looked weakly at Lu Yun. Their conversation touched upon the classified affairs of the Lu Clan and she was only a mere servant girl.","“It’s fine, don’t speak of today’s events with anyone else,” Lu Yun smiled gently.","“So the young master is this handsome when he’s not busy being mean...” Lan’er’s heart was aflutter.","“Ai... second uncle, although there are rules in place for the world of cultivation so that many can’t openly move against us, what are the rules? They’re meant to be broken.” Lu Yun stretched lazily. He didn’t ask who their enemies were as Lu Xiaochi wouldn’t tell him if he did. Lu Yun’s parents had died when he was young—not on the battlefield, but to those unknown enemies.","The Ouyangs and Yuwens, as well as the Lings in the shadows, attack us so blatantly probably because they’ve been infiltrated by our enemies. The Nineheavens Pagoda from Dark Orchid is also likely one of their pawns...","But who are our enemies? The Severed Meridian Hold? Only an awakened cultivator who’s passed through their tribulation can deploy it.","Lu Yun shuddered when he thought of one such cultivator he’d angered a few years ago. That’d been a true brush with death!","......","The one hundred and fifty kilometers of Dark City’s northern quadrant was the poorest district of the entire capital. Some of the lowest portions of society congregated here. As powerful and prosperous Darklake Empire was, it had its shady parts. One such area was the slum district of the northern quadrant in its capital that was one thousand kilometers across.","Lu Yun was dressed as he usually was—long white robes, fine jade dangling from his waist, and the very graphic fan in his hand. He sauntered through the streets with Lan’er and Lu Xuan flanking him.","Being of noble bearing, they immediately drew general attention when they entered the district. It was mostly qi refinement cultivators who lived in this district, so they quickly dodged out of view when they saw the Lu young master’s arrival. No one wanted to run afoul of this pestilence!","“Young master, what are we doing here?” Lan’er didn’t understand it. Lu Yun typically spent his days in the eastern or southern quadrants. That was where the capital’s most prosperous districts were located. The northern quadrant... she recalled that the young master had only ever been here once before.","“Just taking a walk,” Lu Yun smiled faintly. He’d been ten years old when he first visited six years ago. Arrogant, tyrannical, and overweening, he’d caused no end of trouble for the residents when he was here.","He was bored after that trip and never came again.","A lifeless atmosphere ruled the northern quadrant. The other three were protected by powerful formations—only the northern quadrant wasn’t. Even its Qi Accumulation Formation had been out of circulation for an indeterminate period of time.","Bam!","A grayish figure landed by Lu Yun’s feet.","“You cretin! I will cripple you if you dare show your face around here again!” A gentle voice shouted loudly with denunciation and a faint fragrance drifted through the air. A young woman dressed in white with a veil across her face charged out of a simple shack.","“Ouyang Shengxiang?” Lu Yun raised an eyebrow when he saw the girl.","“You’re the one who came and threw your weight around in my northern quadrant! Just you wait, woman, just you wait!” The grayish figure—an initial foundation establishment cultivator scrambled out of sight.","“Ouyang Shengxiang is only three levels of qi refinement. How was she able to send an initial foundation establishment flying?” Lu Yun mused as he watched the man run away.","“Lu Yun?!” Ouyang Shengxiang flew into a rage when she saw the young man.","What he’d said at Immortal Gathering had naturally made its way into her ears; it was the talk of town now. She was unable to refute it, and most awkward of all; there was indeed a red mole on her bottom!","Now that she saw him here, she couldn’t resist charging forward to teach him a lesson.","Lu Yun met her in kind to see Ouyang Shengxiang charge at him.","“Aiyaya my dear! Though we are born a thousand miles apart, souls that are one will always meet. To think that we’d encounter each other here—it’s destiny!”","Whoosh!","He snapped his fan open, making Ouyang Shengxiang halt in her tracks when she saw the pornographic depiction. His fan was more than an ordinary folding fan—it was a paramount treasure. Its images could move, so Lu Yun could turn it into a walking show as soon as he infused it with his Hongmeng qi."]},{"number":2219,"title":"Chapter 2219: Chapter 2165.2: Shengxiang","paragraphs":["Chapter 2165.2: Shengxiang","Ouyang Shengxiang was an unmarried girl of fifteen years old and lacked a firm grasp of the matters between men and women. Mortified, she didn’t know what to do when suddenly presented with this kind of view.","“Who is your dear?!” Her eyes spat fire, but she didn’t dare look in Lu Yun’s direction.","“How is father-in-law?” Lu Yun approached merrily. Lan’er and Lu Xuan followed him alertly—Ouyang Shengxiang had just sent an initial foundation establishment cultivator flying with one kick!","“Who, who’s your father-in-law?!” Ouyang Shengxiang angrily stomped her foot, then grew snappish when she thought of how her father had just died yesterday.","“Your dad is my father-in-law, of course,” Lu Yun chortled.","“I’ll kill you!” Ouyang Shengxiang couldn’t keep herself in check anymore and raised her hand, shooting out a watery ripple of sword light from her fingertips. It beelined toward Lu Yun.","Clang!","Turquoise light flashed by and blocked the sword light. Lu Xuan stood stiffly upright with enormous killing intent emanating from his body. He leveled a cold glare at Ouyang Shengxiang.","“Sword mastery? Ouyang Shengxiang’s only three levels of qi refinement, how can she deploy qi through a sword?” Lu Yun jumped with surprise. Only when cultivators reached foundation establishment could they begin to master a sword. Those below that level couldn’t fully utilize one.","Although Lu Yun practiced the Nine Chapters of Dao and possessed unquestionably strong Hongmeng qi, his own cultivation was only eighth level qi refinement. He was unable to deploy qi out of a sword.","“Turquoise Willow!” Ouyang Shengxiang’s expression turned chilly when she saw the sword light.","“Who are you and how dare you bully Miss Xiang!” rang a furious roar as the slums boiled over with activity. Nearly eight hundred people waving clubs or blunt instruments flooded out of nowhere, surrounding Lu Yun and his people. The ones closer to Ouyang Shengxiang clustered protectively around her.","“Get out of the northern quadrant if you’re going to bully Miss Shengxiang!”","“That’s right, get out of here! You’re not welcome here!”","The strongest of them was sixth or seventh level qi refinement. Ambient qi in the northern quadrant was very lacking due to a dearth of resources, so ascending to seventh level qi refinement here was quite an accomplishment.","Most people hovered around first or second level qi refinement.","“Hey, take a closer look, alright? She’s the one who struck first, I’m the victim here,” Lu Yun protested with resignation as he faced a menacing crowd of cultivators.","“We don’t care if you struck first or Miss Xiang did. Whoever is an enemy of Miss Xiang is nothing good! The northern quadrant doesn’t welcome you!” A teenager waving a kitchen knife glared hotly at him.","I wonder what she’s done to win over all of the residents. Lu Yun smiled. “Oh, is that so?”","He took out a vermilion command token from his storage ring, one etched with a vermilion bird ready to take off in flight.","“I am the commander of the Vermilion Bird troops in Darklake Empire and am here on secret orders to investigate the deaths of the Ouyang and Yuwen patriarchs. Are all of you co-conspirators to keep me here?” Lu Yun drawled as he held the command token high.","Lu Tianling commanded four major troops of Azure Dragon, White Tiger, Vermilion Bird, and Black Tortoise. The Azure Dragons were valiant and skilled in battle, the domineering White Tigers acted as shock troops, the Black Tortoises were unparalleled in defending cities, and the Vermilion Birds were once their strongest member!","Not only were the Vermilion Birds first among the four troops, they were the foremost battle force of Darklake. However, they were fully lost in battle at the battle of Tiger Suppression Pass twenty years ago.","Although they’d been eliminated, their designation remained. Lu Tianling had given the command token to Lu Yun after the boy’s birth, hoping that he could inherit the Vermilion Birds and return them to glory.","Sadly, Lu Yun had been unsalvageable trash before and the Vermilion Bird was never reformed. Up till now, the troop listed only Lu Yun on its rolls. Its command token, however, contained immense authority. It represented the strongest of the empire—Lu Tianling!","But who were those in front of him? The lowest of the low in the world of cultivation. Lu Tianling and the four great troops were too far removed from them. It’d been twenty years since the Vermilion Birds were wiped out—they were less important than a piece of lower rank spirit stone to these people.","Although Lu Yun was dressed opulently and carried himself with an uncommon air, the cultivators didn’t have the capacity to consider those details as their Miss Xiang was being bullied.","“Alright back off now, back off now. What are you people doing crowding around here?? Are you trying to raise a rebellion?” A stern voice came from the sky, followed shortly by a ray of sword light. A middle-aged man in black stood in the air and surveilled the crowd below.","“Master Yu...” The cultivators paled to see the man.","Yu Qianhua was latter foundation establishment and part of the city guard. He was in charge of the northern quadrant, so naturally needed to pay a visit when nearly eight hundred cultivators congregated on the same spot.","“Hoi, so it’s Master Yu Qianhua! I was wondering why I hadn’t seen you in a while, so you’ve come to the northern quadrant!” Lu Yun put away the command token when he saw the man and tilted his head back. “Get your ass down here, this young master isn’t used to talking to people standing over me.”","“Um...” The cultivators wanted to faint when they heard Lu Yun loftily address Master Yu Qianhua. Yu Qianhua and the city guard of this quadrant were their gods and the goal of all of the denizens.","If they were able to establish their foundations, they would be able to join the city guard and become someone like him. That would bring honor to their families, but their idol, their goal in life, was currently being hollered at by someone else!","Yu Qianhua was about to erupt with anger when he took a closer look at the speaker. He quickly changed his expression and landed on the ground.","“So the august young master Lu has come to visit... I have failed to welcome you properly, please forgive me.” Yu Qianhua bowed repeatedly while cursing inwardly. What was this spoiled brat doing here?? He wouldn’t have come if he’d known that Lu Yun was here!","Being less than fifty years old, yet having already reached latter foundation establishment, Yu Qianhua counted among the upper echelon of talent in Darklake. Unfortunately, he came from a humble background and lacked a patron. Although he’d joined the city guards, he was assigned to a place like the northern quadrant.","Ambient qi was so sparse \\ that cultivators progressed slowly when they were based in the area. But since his duties lay here, Yu Qianhua didn’t dare leave.","“I remember you were in charge of the southern quadrant and you were a captain there. What are you doing here?” Lu Yun asked with every semblance of confusion.","Yu Qianhua looked at the young man and hesitated before responding, “The Ouyang young master—Ouyang Shenghe—broke through to latter foundation establishment. He’s joined the city guards for training and has become captain of the southern quadrant. Qianhua was reassigned to the northern quadrant due to lack of skill.”","“Ouyang Shenghe huh...” Lu Yun turned back to look at Ouyang Shengxiang. She and her brother had plotted against Lu Yun to beat him up. Events of the day were still fresh in his mind.","“Hmph!” Ouyang Shengxiang snorted coldly to see Lu Yun look at her. “What does it have to do with my older brother that you’ve been reassigned to the northern quadrant? It’s your own fault for slacking on your duties and nothing to do with my brother.”","“Your brother?” Yu Qianhua blinked before realizing that the renowned benefactor of the northern quadrant was the young miss of the Ouyang Clan!","The cultivators around them exchanged glances of disbelief with each other. How noble was the young miss of the Ouyang Clan? Yet here she was, helping impoverished cultivators!","No wonder the two noble scions had been at odds with each other as soon as they met. It was no secret that the Ouyangs and Lus did not get along.","“What do you know, Ouyang Shengxiang?” Lu Yun snorted and showed the girl no face. “Yu Qianhua comes from purely civilian roots and established his foundation at twenty years old. He joined the Black Devils, a troop that set foot on the battlefield no less than twenty times. He accomplished innumerable achievements and is latter foundation establishment at forty-five years old. His abilities are nothing that your brother can measure up to!”","The Black Devils were a star troop that answered to the imperial family. They rivaled the four troops under Lu Tianling’s command.","“Hmph, foundation establishment at forty-five years old? He’s just trash and not worthy of being mentioned in the same breath as my brother,” Ouyang Shengxiang sniffed dismissively.","“Hahahaha!” Lu Yun roared with laughter. “Foundation establishment at forty-five years old? You come from a major family, Ouyang Shengxiang, and have rich resources to draw on. You have absolutely no idea about the hardships of the poor!”","He swept a look around the surroundings. “Master Yu comes from a purely civilian background and had no spirit stones to use. He utilized the qi of heaven and earth to slowly make his way to foundation establishment at twenty years old. He traded accomplishments in battle for cultivation resources to reach his current heights. It is a long and difficult process that a coddled noble miss like you knows nothing about!","“To be blunt, if Ouyang Shenghe and Yu Qianhua were to fight each other, Ouyang Shenghe would be terminated in less than three moves!","“Hmph, Master Yu has rendered great service to the empire and should’ve had a promising future after making captain. But your useless flop of a brother has destroyed his future!”","City guards were as good as exiled after they were sent to the northern quadrant. If no fortuitous opportunity came to them, they would stay here until they retired.","Off to the side, Yu Qianhua trembled. Lu Yun clearly sensed goodwill flow from him, a surge on par with what he’d felt from He Wuheng during the second time."]},{"number":2220,"title":"Chapter 2220: Chapter 2166.1: Human Demon","paragraphs":["Chapter 2166.1: Human Demon","And that wasn’t all of it!","Five more surges of goodwill appeared in the surroundings, though they weren’t as pronounced as what came from Yu Qianhua.","Bolstered by the additional sources, Lu Yun’s Hongmeng qi circulated at a faster speed and the dao character within his dantian blazed with light.","Boom!","A shackle seemed to snap in his mind as he ascended to latter first turn of the Seeing Dao chapter. He was now ninth level qi refinement!","Six combined forces of goodwill had propelled him into breaking through! Lu Yun made sure to keep his composure and ensure that no one could detect the abnormalities in his body.","The Nine Chapters of Dao were peculiar and close to nature. Although he couldn’t fully conceal his cultivation and return to his original state, he could fully hide the energy ripples caused by a breakthrough.","So while he’d broken through, Lu Yun’s expression remained the same as before. The only thing he felt was that this kind of cultivation via goodwill was very familiar—so familiar that he wanted to recover the sealed him right this second!","But... he couldn’t.","“Useless flop?” Ouyang Shengxiang sneered at Lu Yun. “My brother is no useless flop compared to young master Lu Yun. So what if my second brother has destroyed this Yu Qianhua’s future? How many families have you destroyed?”","The crowd reacted with surprise when the girl named Lu Yun. Although Yu Qianhua had said young master Lu earlier, there were many Lu surnamed families in the city. However, there was only one who dared bicker with an Ouyang!","Despite the Ouyangs being gravely set back, having lost three nascent soul cultivators in one fell swoop, they were still a premier family of the nation.","When the crowd heard the name Lu Yun, they felt like they’d stepped into a large pile of fecal matter. They were so disgusted that they wanted to throw their shoes away.","“Hahaha!” Lu Yun rocked back and forth with laughter when he heard Ouyang Shengxiang. “To think that I, Lu Yun, would one day be considered on the same level as the second Ouyang young master! Hahahaha!!”","“Hmph!” Ouyang Shengxiang glowered. Lu Yun was indeed unfit to be mentioned in the same breath as her brother!","Ouyang Shenghe was renowned throughout the capital not only for his stunning potential, but also his upright character. He loved taking a stand for justice and was second only to the three gentlemen of Dusk City.","Those three gentlemen weren’t the likes of Lu Yun, Yu Shuai, and Zhao Chenguang. Rather, they were truly three gentlemen who were the leading figures of the empire’s younger generation. All of them were less than fifty years old, but they’d reached nascent soul and were the pillars of the next generation.","“I say, Miss Xiang, how is your third brother?” Lu Yun chuckled.","“Thanks to young master Lu, my third brother is very well.” Ouyang Shengxiang’s face darkened when she heard Lu Yun mention Ouyang Shengmu.","A sudden thought struck Lu Yun and he looked on with interest, but his mind was rapidly sorting through certain thoughts.","His random string of sarcasm had fully irritated Ouyang Shengxiang. She didn’t want to stay here any longer, especially as Lu Yun was known for being an absolutely shameless cad. How would a girl hold her own against him?","Thus, she spun on her heel and stalked off.","“Ai ai ai, I say Miss Xiang, we haven’t sorted out our marriage yet. Why don’t I find some time to pay a visit to my father-in-law?” Lu Yun called out when he saw the girl leave.","Ouyang Shengxiang glowered. Father-in-law? Her father? Ouyang Baitian? He’d just died yesterday! Lu Yun was picking at scabs while her family was still setting up for a funeral!","“If you continue this nonsense, Lu Yun, I won’t mind beating you unconscious for another three months!” Ouyang Shengxiang sniffed and quickly ran off. She wanted to teach Lu Yun a lesson, but she would come off worse in the exchange if she remained any longer.","She was here alone!","“Interesting.” Lu Yun narrowed his eyes as he looked at the girl’s departing back. Such a grave matter had happened to the Ouyang Clan and her father was dead, but she had the presence of mind to visit the northern quadrant?","There was no way she was here to commit good deeds or acts of service!","“Young master...” Yu Qianhua hesitated.","“Alright, that will be all. You guys can all go now.” Lu Yun waved off the cultivators around them and swiftly dispersed the crowd.","“Yu Qianhua, your potential’s not bad. You should follow me.” Lu Yun cocked his head at the man and smiled meaningfully.","Follow Lu Yun? Yu Qianhua’s expression shifted. One of the seven major families of the capital stood behind Lu Yun and their patriarch was the city’s strongest powerhouse, Lu Tianling. However, very few who followed by Lu Yun’s side met with a good end.","The young man’s guards were all golden core powerhouses, but they were either crippled or dead after a few days. The one next to him now seemed to be in fine fettle, but he’d probably be comatose or dead with another few days.","“And the five over there, stop hiding. Come on out.” Lu Yun was much more relaxed after breaking through and reaching latter first turn. He pointed in a certain direction, prompting five soldiers similar to Yu Qianhua to walk out with resignation.","They were all mid foundation establishment and had been greatly touched by the young master’s words. The city guard of the northern quadrant was almost exclusively staffed by those who’d offended nobility. There was nothing wrong with their character, so what Lu Yun had just said made them grateful to the young man.","“Greetings to young master Lu!” they chorused.","“You five and Yu Qianhua shall follow this young master in the future. I’ll show you the good life! It’ll be one hundred times better than staying in this forsaken place.” Lu Yun stuck his nose up in the air.","Yu Qianhua and his men looked at each other, not knowing how to respond.","Lu Yun sneered and took out the Vermilion Bird command token again. “This general recruits you for the Vermilion Birds! What, do you want to defy its commander?”","“But, young ma—General Lu,” Yu Qianhua modified his honorific as he continued to look at Lu Yun. “This humble soldier is already part of the third major troop of the city guards and answers to Master Sun Shengsun’s banner...”","“Shengsun, huh,” Lu Yun nodded. “Just a mere commandant. Would he dare fight this general for men? It is his honor that this general wants some of his people!”","Yu Qianhua and the others paused, only now recalling that it was Marshal Lu Tianling behind the young man. He was the leader of the empire’s armies! Commandant Sun Shengsun did indeed not count for much compared to this one.","“Alright, take off your city guard uniforms. They’re so ugly—do you really think it’s acceptable to walk around in public wearing those?” Lu Yun curled his lip at the black armor on the six.","The armor was made from ordinary refined iron and etched with a few defensive runes. They would be treasures in a world of mortals, but were trash to cultivators.","Yu Qianhua and his men had no other choice; they had to obey Lu Yun’s orders. Everyone knew that the greatest scourge of Dusk City was an eccentric fellow. He might be smiling one second and drawing his sword on the audience the next.","Thus, the six men took off their armor and stood helplessly next to Lu Yun.","Some of the cultivators peeping from the shadows found this incredulous. The mighty city guards had taken off their uniforms and joined this young master, just like that?","It was unbelievable!","“General, if the six of us are gone, then the safety of the northern quadrant...” Yu Qianhua asked carefully.","“The safety of the northern quadrant?” Lu Yun’s lip curl deepened. “What does that have to do with me?”","His newest subordinates looked wryly at each other. It appeared that the rumors were true—young master Lu was an absolutely lawless good-for-nothing who never thought about the consequences.","“Enough, enough, don’t think so highly of yourselves,” Lu Yun harrumphed. “Dusk City will not fall to enemies without you and Sun Shengsun will send someone else here tomorrow.”","He waved them off and sauntered toward an alley.","Lan’er and Lu Xuan were used to his antics, so they followed close behind their young master. It would be weird if Lu Yun had a sudden change of heart and actually cared about the livelihood of the people.","Yu Qianhua and the other five sighed. They were in for it now. Not only did they have to be this young master’s cannon fodder, but they would go down in history as infamous characters. They’d thought that being assigned to the northern quadrant was suffering enough, but now they realized their previous life had been a slice of paradise."]},{"number":2221,"title":"Chapter 2221: Chapter 2166.2: Human Demon","paragraphs":["Chapter 2166.2: Human Demon","......","“This should be it.” Lu Yun’s nose twitched as he followed the cloud of fragrance left behind by Ouyang Shengxiang. They stopped in front of an ordinary looking house that appeared the same as its neighbors, but the young man looked at it with interest.","“Lu Xuan, destroy the tuft of grass at the top of the wall.” Lu Yun pointed at a withering handful of grass on the wall.","Whoosh!","The tuft was gone after a flash of light.","“Yu Qianhua, break the second to last brick next to the door from the right.” Lu Yun pointed at a floor tile.","Yu Qianhua didn’t understand the order, but he followed suit when he saw how Lu Xuan had responded. He directed his sword light to smash the brick in.","Bam!","A muffled sound rang from the house and ripples undulated through the air in front of it.","“Well well, a Mirage Formation with complementary wood and earth,” Lu Yun snorted with laughter and casually threw a talisman through the front door.","Bam!","The house trembled and the void shifted, vastly changing the ordinary-looking house in front of them.","“What... this spirit qi is so dense! It’s on par with some of the houses that belong to the cultivation families in the southern district!” Yu Qianhu exclaimed as he took in the wave of qi that wafted toward them.","“Wood and earth complement each other in this Mirage Formation. But if it lacks water, then the earth would be fully constrained by the wood. The power of the formation would be immensely diminished then,” Lu Yun chuckled. HIs talisman had happened to destroy one of the ponds in the corner of the yard.","He could dismantle a formation like this with a quick wave of his hand. And if he could use formula dao... Oh, what the fuck, get out of my head. I don’t want to remember formula dao right now!","“Ahem...” a weak cough rang from the yard. “The lad outside the door is young, but your experience is vast. You are ten times stronger than the three gentlemen of the capital.”","It was hoarse, aged, and tinged with a weak feebleness.","“Senior praises me too highly, that was just a small trick.” Lu Yun smiled and stepped into the yard. Ten times stronger than those idiots? Are you insulting me? He remained smiling, however, and didn’t mind the exchange.","“Young master!” Lan’er cautioned urgently.","“It’s fine, you can all come in,” Lu Yun responded without turning around.","Lu Xuan was already at his master’s heels while Yu Qianhua and the others looked around with surprise. They’d never expected such a place in the northern quadrant of the capital. If it hadn’t been for Lu Yun breaking the outside formation, they would’ve never discovered the truth behind this locale.","Their view of the young man was undergoing some slight changes, but they also weren’t too surprised by the happenings. After all, Lu Yun’s grandfather was Lu Tianling, the greatest of the nation.","The house was of moderate size, but seemed to be another world. Birdsong and flowers abounded and its ambient qi was overwhelming. In fact, it provided nearly the same level of comfort as Lu Yun’s own house.","“The qi of the northern quadrant is scarce, yet there is so much here! There is either a high level qi accumulation formation at play or there’s a small qi energy vein below!” Lu Yun narrowed his eyes as his mind spun rapidly through various possibilities.","An elder with an otherworldly air laid on a reclining chair in the middle of the yard. His hair and beard were white and he was dressed in long blue robes. His pale face and weak aura indicated severe injuries.","“My name is Lu Yun, greetings to this... senior?” Lu Yun merrily tilted his head to the side. Despite calling the other his senior, there was no trace of respect on his face.","“You’re Lu Yun?” Startled, the elder opened his eyes slightly. “The legendary Lu Yun is rumored to be an unlearned and incompetent wastrel. He is a thorough scoundrel and unredeemable scum. But judging from your actions moments ago, you are very different from hearsay.”","Whoosh!","Lu Yun tilted his head back and snapped his fan open.","“An unlearned and incompetent wastrel?” he said proudly. “A thorough scoundrel and unredeemable scum? Slander, utter slander! I am genteel, refined, and poised with dashing grace. I hold a hundred disciplines in my mind and instruct the mountains and rivers. I am the epitome of being free and restrained!","“Is there any in the entire world that is more stunning than me, much less Darklake?”","That was the truth.","Yu Qianhua and his men looked skeptically at each other.","“So one is indeed invincible after setting aside considerations of face,” mumbled a soldier called Chu Zhaoyang. The elder, however, nodded in agreement with Lu Yun’s words.","“The formation I set up outside the door consists of complementary wood and earth. Although some formation grandmasters can see through a Mirage Formation, the Illusory Killing Formation of Water is not something identifiable by ordinary formation masters,” the elder declared solemnly in a self-assured manner.","“Hahaha!” Lu Yun roared with laughter. “An Illusory Killing Formation of Water? I think there’s more to it than that!”","The elder’s eyes brightened as the young man sent out another talisman.","Rumble!","Lightning the width of a finger flashed by with a loud rumble. It struck a wood chopper resting on some firewood and sent it flying.","Humm!","The yard trembled again as the uncommonly dense heavenly qi turned even heavier. Some inexplicable killing intent that’d floated through the surroundings also vanished without a trace.","“A Reverse Five Elements of Absolute Slaughter formation is something beyond the capabilities of formation masters in even fourth rank cultivation empires. I am ever more curious about your identity, senior.” Lu Yun snapped his fan shut and crossed his arms with a half smile.","“Who would’ve thought that someone would recognize and break my formation in a mere third rank cultivation empire?” The elder narrowed his eyes. Although he seemed to be complimenting Lu Yun, a hint of killing intent traced his words. “As for this old man’s identity, it’s better that you don’t know.”","“You’re teaching the three Ouyang brothers and Ouyang Shengxiang, aren’t you?” Lu Yun asked after a moment’s pause.","“You possess some knowledge. Apart from Ouyang Shengtian and Ouyang Shengxiang, everyone else in the Ouyang Clan is trash,” the elder nodded.","“No wonder Ouyang Shengxiang can defeat a foundation establishment cultivator when she’s only three levels qi refinement herself. She doesn’t use the methods of a low-ranked cultivation empire,” Lu Yun mused.","“Oh, does young master Lu wish to take this old man for a master?” the elder curved his lips upward. “As much potential as Ouyang Shengtian possesses to be listed as first among the three gentlemen, your potential isn’t the slightest bit lesser than his.”","Lu Yun wordlessly curled his lip. Ouyang Shengtian? Lu Yun could have him ascend to the heavens in one second! [1]","Yu Qianhua, Chu Zhaoyang, and the others looked on with mouths agape.","This old man heaving for breath was the master of the four Ouyang geniuses? And what else had he said, that the renowned wastrel Lu Yun was just as promising as Ouyang Shengtian??","Who was Ouyang Shengtian? The number one genius of Dark City and the leader of the three gentlemen of the capital! His cultivation had already reached nascent soul! A nascent soul cultivator was a mighty personage on high. How was he being compared to Lu Yun??","“Let me think—why has someone like you been deposited in someplace like this?” Lu Yun slowly paced through the yard and sized up the surroundings. “There’s not a single maid or servant here.”","“I like quiet,” the elder retorted.","“More like the Ouyangs don’t dare give you any servants,” Lu Yun snorted. “They put you here and have you teach Ouyang Shengtian and the others, but don’t invite you to their home. They don’t even give you a servant... So let me think about your identity.”","The old man’s expression began to turn ugly.","Lu Yun walked up to him and scanned the old man’s body with his consciousness. “Your bones are brittle and your nascent soul is close to collapse. You’ve suffered a grave blow at some point in the near past. Oho, I know who you are.” The young man winked at the elder.","Brooding, the elder’s face was dark.","“Bloodbath.” Lu Yun took a few steps back. “To think that the human demon who once slaughtered one million cultivators from the fifth rank Barren Empire, the one who almost caused the empire’s downfall, would be here!”","“The human demon Bloodbath!” Lu Xuan, Lan’er, and Yu Qianhua gasped in unison.","Bloodbath had once roamed the world of cultivation as a mythical personage. Legend had it that Bloodbath wore red, possessed red hair, red eyes, and caused bloody light to appear around his body when he deployed his cultivation methods. He was an exceedingly horrifying figure who did not belong to any sect or clan. He also wasn’t part of any empire either.","For reasons unknown, he’d clashed with the fifth rank Barren Empire one hundred years ago and slaughtered one million of its citizens in three days. Even their emperor was a victim; a vast fifth rank empire teetered on the edge of disintegration within half a month.","But after that, Bloodbath vanished from public view.","“How is that possible?!” Yu Qianhua denied. “They say that Bloodbath was killed after the three ninth rank empires issued arrest warrants for him!”","But judging from the elder’s expression, he was silently admitting to things!","“Let me think about this,” Lu Yun continued as he watched the elder remain silent. “It’s said that Bloodbath’s cultivation methods are unique and require a supply of fresh blood. If you can access fresh blood, you instantly recover no matter how severe your injuries are. The Ouyangs must have placed you here and refused to give you any servants because of that.”","1. Shengtian is wordplay for ‘sacred sky’ (the young man’s name) and ‘die’. They are pronounced the same. ☜"]},{"number":2222,"title":"Chapter 2222: Chapter 2166.3: Human Demon","paragraphs":["Chapter 2166.3: Human Demon","“What makes you think that this old man is Bloodbath?” The corner of the elder’s eyes twitched as he made one final struggle.","Lu Yun chuckled, “As marvelous as the Transformation Jade is, it does not pull the wool over my eyes.”","The elder’s—Bloodbath’s—expression shifted.","“Indeed, I am Bloodbath. Do you want to bring me to a ninth rank cultivation empire to collect the bounty now?” A bloody light flashed through the depths of his eyes when he raised his head.","“Even the Ouyangs know to treat you as an honored guest for their own use. I am no fool.”","Although Lu Yun didn’t know what the Ouyang Clan had done to make Bloodbath bow his head, it marked the start of many more submissions. Having dictated their terms to Bloodbath once, it wouldn’t be hard for the Ouyangs to do so again.","Those behind Lu Yun widened their eyes. This was the human demon Bloodbath! He was a name that parents used to scare their children into not crying, and he was sitting right in front of them!","“You want to recruit me as your subordinate?” Bloodbath’s voice changed from hoarse and wizened to that of a young man’s. Somehow, it was also tinged with a trace of unnatural entrancement.","“What else? Am I supposed to invite you to be my ancestor?” Lu Yun chortled.","“Hahaha! Even Ouyang Baitian doesn’t dare invite me home—he’s terrified that I’ll recover through the aid of fresh blood. How does a kid wet behind the ears like you dare bring me home?” Bloodbath sneered. “Your grandfather may be the strongest of Darklake, but he’s nothing but an ant to me.”","“Recover through the aid of fresh blood? Do the Ouyangs really believe that bullshit?” Lu Yun snorted. “As uncanny as the Method of Blood Shadows is, it’s not to those levels.”","“You...” Bloodbath paused, startled that the young man knew what his cultivation method was.","The Method of Blood Shadows was a cultivation method from a demonic sect that existed ten thousand years ago—the Blood Demons. Bloodbath had obtained it by accident and it was the reason why his cultivation had taken a massive leap forward.","The Method of Blood Shadows required irrigation of fresh blood throughout the process of cultivation and constant slaughter. That was how Bloodbath earned his nickname of “human demon”.","However, training with the method was an exceedingly painful process that twisted one’s personality. Bloodbath was rumored to be an eccentric with wild mood swings, someone who slaughtered entire cities at the drop of a hat. This was due to his practice of the Method of Blood Shadows.","This cultivation method had been infamous ten thousand years ago, leading to its progenitor—the dominant Blood Shadows—being jointly eliminated by the three ninth rank cultivation empires. To this day, the Method of Blood Shadows was still forbidden.","“The Method of Blood Shadows?” Bloodbath blinked, then sneered. “Would I be in these straits if that was what I practiced?”","Lu Yun nodded. “That’s true, even the Blood Shadows ten thousand years ago didn’t own the full Method of Blood Shadows. They only possessed fragments, and what you practice is likely pieces of fragments.”","Bloodbath’s expression stilled.","“Don’t be in a rush to refute me. Being wanted by the ninth rank empires, it’s not like your reputation is any better than the Blood Shadows of old,” Lu Yun chuckled. “I happen to have the complete Method of Blood Shadows.”","The old man trembled.","“As for the injuries on senior’s body—the wounds inflicted by others? Just mere scratches. The worst of them is from a cultivation deviation.” Lu Yun looked straight into Bloodbath’s eyes. The old man narrowed his eyes in return and didn’t say a word.","Those next to Lu Yun gaped and stared incredulously as the young man.","Was this the legendary good-for-nothing who didn’t know anything? If he was a bumbling fool, then what did that make Ouyang Shengtian? Or the three gentlemen of Dark City? Who in the capital had possessed knowledge like Lu Yun’s?","At the same time, Yu Qianhua and his men exchanged rueful smiles. Lu Yun was talking of this so openly in front of them and keeping nothing from them. It would be one thing if young master Lu was an ordinary prodigal and spent his days in a hazy daze of debauchery, but this fellow had plainly fooled everyone.","“This young master is able to heal your injuries,” Lu Yun said.","“You are but ninth level qi refinement. You haven’t even reached foundation establishment, so how can you heal my injuries?” Bloodbath had lived for hundreds of years, after all. He’d fully recovered his composure.","“My cultivation?” Lu Yun cocked his head. “Lan’er, tell him what this young master was at two days ago.”","Lan’er was goggling at her young master. Ninth level qi refinement? Hadn’t the young master always been at seventh level? She blinked and asked blearily, “Young master, you were at seven levels two days ago. When did you break through to nine levels?”","“Eh...” Her baffled answer dealt a heavy blow to the hearts of everyone present. Seven levels two days ago? This...","“So now, you have two options available.” Lu Yun wagged a finger in front of the elder. “First, this young master will kill you and trade your head for the bounty from the ninth rank empires. Second, follow this young master’s banner. After I help you recover from your injuries, I will teach you the complete Method of Blood Shadows.”","A talisman appeared in his hand. Lightning sparkled over it as it emanated ponderous energy ripples.","Bloodbath’s eyes darted around. “The Method of Blood Shadows requires human blood. Is young master Lu proposing to supply me with the blood that I need?”","“Human blood?” Lu Yun burst out laughing. “The Method of Blood Shadows is the foundational method of the Canon of the Blood God. What does the Canon of the Blood God want with human blood?”","The Blood God... Lu Yun paused briefly. He’d known someone like this during his three thousand reincarnations. As evil as that person’s cultivation method had been, he didn’t make use of mortal blood.","Bloodbath reeled from the response.","“In that case, I, Bloodbath, will follow you. Answering to Lu Yun’s banner is better than being grounded by the Ouyangs,” Bloodbath made up his mind.","“Swear on your blood demon,” Lu Yun turned into a picture of seriousness.","“Very well, upon my blood demon,” Bloodbath sighed.","A blood demon oath for a demonic dao cultivator was the equivalent of a heavenly dao oath for an immortal cultivator. If it was violated, it altered one’s tribulation and made success nigh impossible.","Swearing upon a blood demon or heavenly dao was a joke in a small place like Darklake. It was enough for cultivators to reach nascent soul. Undergo one’s tribulation? That was the stuff of myths and legends.","But for Bloodbath, he wouldn’t dare break a promise made with his blood demon. He’d reached the combination cultivation level when he slaughtered the fifth rank cultivation empire hundreds of years ago—his tribulation was close at hand.","Lu Yun was well aware of that as well. Additionally, someone as proud as Bloodbath would never renege on his word after bowing his head to Lu Yun and deciding to follow the young man.","Making the elder swear on his blood demon was just a precaution. Lu Yun had one hundred ways to control a mere combination cultivator, ways that would ensure the cultivator offered up his full devotion.","He didn’t care about Bloodbath’s past. So he’d exterminated an empire? So what? All Lu Yun knew was that he was very weak and urgently needed to strengthen himself.","Bloodbath was like a blade left by the side of the road, one already covered in blood. All the young man was doing was picking it up and using it to protect himself and those around him.","And to finish what his sealed self needed to do.","“Those who are smart will always meet with a good end,” Lu Yun chuckled.","“This subordinate swears fealty to young master Lu. You have our undying loyalty!” Yu Qianhua and his men immediately sank to their knees when they heard the young man. They were all shrewd people who knew how to assess the situation, seeing as they’d been able to survive the battlefield and join the city guards.","Lu Yun had just recruited a heavily wanted criminal right in front of their eyes. These six men would either become the young master’s direct subordinates, or they would be silenced in death. There was no other outcome.","Lu Yun nodded with satisfaction.","“You six take Senior Blood and follow me back to the residence,” he commanded after momentary thought.","“Understood!” the six chorused.","......","Although endless experience and knowledge filled Lu Yun’s mind, he was far too weak himself. The Lu Clan also swayed and teetered in the wind. Despite sensing that his family wasn’t all that it appeared on the surface, that his grandfather was hiding many secrets, it also seemed that his family had to face something that was many times more frightening than imagination might indicate.","Lu Yun had experienced three thousand lifetimes and had the heavenly dao as his master, but he was a puny ant at the moment and had to do everything he could to strengthen himself.","Although he’d forgotten everything of the past, a sense of urgency and danger existed deep within his heart. He needed to face something that was much more terrifying and bigger than all of this. The addition of a personage like Bloodbath was most timely assistance."]},{"number":2223,"title":"Chapter 2223: Chapter 2166.4: Human Demon","paragraphs":["Chapter 2166.4: Human Demon","Bloodbath had lost all of his cultivation for the moment and was nearly paralyzed, making him much worse off than Lu Xiaochi. Despite that, Lu Yun still had his ways of quickly recovering some of the senior’s cultivation level.","Lu Tianling was still in closed door cultivation after the earlier fight and Lu Xiaochi had completely relaxed upon learning that his nephew could heal his injuries and break the Severed Meridians Hold. He filled his days with planting flowers, raising birds, and living a completely carefree life.","Dark City had been engulfed in pandemonium since disaster beset the Ouyang and Yuwen Clans. A tense atmosphere filled the air and everyone looked fearfully over their shoulders.","None of this mattered to Lu Yun. After he brought Bloodbath back to the Lu residence, he arranged a house for all seven people to live together.","“Yu Qianhua, Chu Zhaoyang, Yin Tingyu, Chen Li, Huo Haoran, and Qiu Yuan, you six are the first batch of soldiers in the Vermilion Bird.”","The six men stood in a line in front of Lu Yun.","“Senior Bloodbath is your drillmaster.”","“Drillmaster?” Bloodbath stirred with interest from his soft chair.","“Indeed, drillmaster,” Lu Yun nodded. “Teach these six how to cultivate and turn them from six wusses into true soldiers.”","Drillmaster... What a far off title. It seemed to cross endless space and time to reappear here, like a dream. Lu Yun pursed his lips and suppressed the odd feeling rising in his heart. He also prevented himself from thinking further and avoided the impulse to break the seal.","Yu Qianhua and his men flushed with outrage.","“Now now, don’t be angry—the city guards are just the last of the army’s pickings. The true elites who survive the battlefield are snapped up by the imperial family and sent elsewhere,” Lu Yun murmured to himself and didn’t look at the six.","“Interesting.” Bloodbath had returned to his original appearance of long blood-red hair, bloody eyes, and long white robes. His features made him seem quite otherworldly. “If my guess is right, although the Vermilion Bird answers to Lu Tianling, it belongs to the Darklake imperial family.”","“I have my ways to take care of that, it’s just an empty military designation.” Lu Yun didn’t care in the slightest. Darklake was just a mere cultivation empire. So what if it was even the reigning dynasty of the world of immortals?","“What do you think, second uncle?” Lu Yun turned around and asked empty air.","“Hahaha, I knew I couldn’t fool you!” Lu Xiaochi walked through the door. “Junior Lu Xiaochi greets Senior Bloodbath.”","“You’re the legendary first genius of Darklake—Lu Xiaochi?” Bloodbath tilted his head and looked at Lu Xiaochi. “The Severed Meridians Hold?”","While he lacked all cultivation, the consciousness of a combination cultivator was still present in his body.","“Precisely.” Lu Xiaochi nodded with a smile.","“It looks like the waters are deep at the Lu Clan,” Bloodbath chuckled.","“As deep as they are, they won’t drown the senior,” Lu Yun interjected.","“Who knows?” A worried expression appeared on Bloodbath’s face. “I’ll be able to help if you can restore my cultivation sooner rather than later. Otherwise, I may very well drown in these waters.”","“Heh, all in due time,” Lu Yun chuckled. Old fox! You want some benefits before we’ve gotten anything from you?","“Do you want to reform the Vermilion Bird?” Lu Xiaochi asked solemnly.","“Yes.” Lu Yun nodded and didn’t say anything further.","There shouldn’t be any difference between the Lu’s Vermilion Bird and Darklake’s Vermilion Bird. Given Lu Yun’s capabilities and some time, it wouldn’t be hard if he wanted to claim Darklake Empire for himself. However, it seemed that his grandfather and the emperor shared a deeper than expected relationship.","Lu Xiaochi fell silent.","“No worries, I’ll meet with some people later on and reclassify the Vermilion Bird designation as my private army. If worst comes to worst, I’ll just discard the designation,” Lu Yun grinned.","The Vermilion Bird was an obsession of Lu Tianling’s, one that had formed after the entire crew was wiped out twenty years ago. It was clear from him gifting the designation to Lu Yun at birth just how fixated he was on the name.","Lu Yun naturally understood his grandfather’s point of view. The Lu Clan was attributed to fire and there were two such talents in each generation. Lu Tianling and Lu Yun possessed fire spirit roots. Lu Xiaochi was a foster son and also possessed a fire spirit root. The family’s cultivation methods were fire attributed and the Vermilion Bird was the legendary fire god of the south.","“Discard it? Your grandfather will never agree to that,” Lu Xiaochi sighed. “The Lus share an uncommon relationship with the Darklake imperial family.”","“I know,” Lu Yun nodded. “How else would Situ Wenxian have so easily given us the Nineturns Profound Life Pill?”","Situ Wenxian was the name of the Darklake emperor.","......","Ten golden cores and three nascent souls had died within the span of a day. This was a tremendous blow to the Ouyang Clan, one that nearly plunged them into the depths of despair. Yet, what happened next sunk the senior council into unprecedented levels of panic.","Bloodbath went missing!","When the last patriarch, Ouyang Baitian, encountered the heavily injured Bloodbath, he’d grounded the old man inside the northern quadrant. But now, the crippled Bloodbath without any cultivation to call upon had gone missing!","Bloodbath was a demon that killed without blinking an eye. The clan’s original plans were to have him teach those of the younger generation with sufficient potential, then send him to the ninth rank empires for the reward once all value had been extracted from him.","As plentiful as the bounty was, the ninth rank empires would never send a combination cultivator to teach the Ouyang’s younger generation. Although Bloodbath’s sins were monstrous and flagrant, he was still an ant in their eyes.","Within the Ouyangs, Ouyang Shengtian had coalesced a nascent soul at a young age and was a stunning genius of the third rank empire. All the same, he would be mediocre beyond belief in a ninth rank empire.","Ninth rank empires were the apex of the world of cultivation. They couldn’t be bothered to nurture the so-called geniuses of third rank empires. The Ouyangs were well aware of this, which was why they’d kept Bloodbath to nurture their most promising.","He was the reason why Ouyang Shengxiang was able to defeat a foundation establishment cultivator when she was only third level qi refinement.","Ouyang Shengmu and Ouyang Shenghe didn’t count for much in the old man’s eyes, so they didn’t receive his true teachings. If it wasn’t for the fact that they were Ouyang Baitian’s children, they wouldn’t even have the right to learn of the elder’s presence.","Thus, Bloodbath was behind the creation of these two genius young masters. His disappearance sent the family’s senior council into complete panic. They hadn’t been this thrown off-balance when Ouyang Baitian and two of their nascent soul elders died!","Once Bloodbath recovered, he was definitely the sort to slaughter the entire Ouyang Clan for revenge. No one would be safe.","“Bloodbath is severely injured and can’t even move. He can’t get out of Dark City, maybe he’s hiding in a corner somewhere,” said Ouyang Zhen, one of the few remaining nascent soul elders of the family.","An extraordinary young man of twenty-some years old stood in front of him with a noncommittal expression. He was the leader of the three gentlemen of Dark City—Ouyang Shengtian.","Dressed in long blue robes, he possessed natural grace beyond his years.","“My father’s death likely has something to do with Bloodbath.” Ouyang Shengtian’s upward slanting eyebrows slightly knit together.","Although he’d been taught by Bloodbath, the old man was just a tool in Ouyang Shengtian’s eyes. There was no affection of master and disciple between them. Bloodbath had decided to teach them only to ensure his own survival. The two sides were just using each other.","“Does Bloodbath belong to a sect?” Ouyang Zhen’s face suddenly shifted. “If he does...”","“No,” Ouyang Shengtian shook his head. “What kind of person is the legendary Bloodbath? He is completely lawless, as evidenced by his slaughter of the fifth rank empire one hundred years ago. If he really does have a sect supporting him, we would’ve been razed to the ground long ago.","“He must’ve secretly used some methods to recruit a few cultivators for his use. He is a mythical combination cultivator, after all. No one knows what he’s capable of.” Ouyang Shengtian shook his head.","The Ouyangs and Yuwens didn’t know how their patriarchs and powerhouses had died, even now. The power from an exploding nascent soul had been so domineering that Black Maple Peak was leveled and all traces erased.","The power from the explosions had also erased Lu Yun’s formation. All that was left were traces of a grand formation being destroyed. The presence of self-detonating nascent souls were dispelled by the formation’s destruction.","“Hmm?” Ouyang Shengtian frowned and brooded.","“What is it?” Ouyang Zhen asked. The genius had plainly received a secret transmission.","“How interesting, Lu Yun is robbing Ouyang storefronts?” Ouyang Shengtian breathed out heavily. “Whether or not Lu Tianling is truly in closed door cultivation to recover, it is true that Lu Yun has gone out of control. Since he’s delivered himself on an empty platter, we will take full advantage of it. I want Lu Tianling’s life this time!","“Elder Zhen, you are the Ouyang patriarch from now on.” Ouyang Shengtian’s eyes blazed with sharp light, making Ouyang Zhen shudder in spite of himself.","The two clans suspected that Lu Yun had engineered the last incident, with Lu Tianling pulling the strings from the shadows. They’d created an enormous trap for Ouyang Baitian and Yuwen Zonglin to set foot into.","etvolare's Thoughts","So what if they did, you're the ones who set foot into it lawl. So very \"look what you made me do\" vibes.","Yes, that's four parts for a chapter. You guys see what I've been dealing with?"]},{"number":2224,"title":"Chapter 2224: Chapter 2167.1: Seeing Dao","paragraphs":["Chapter 2167.1: Seeing Dao","The southern quadrant of Dark City was the capital’s center of commerce. Filled with shops and vendors, it thronged with boisterous crowds. Nearly half of the capital’s shops were concentrated in the southern quadrant; it was also the commercial hub for Darklake Empire as a whole.","Apart from the Lu Clan, the other six major families all had storefronts in the quadrant.","Bam!","A muffled explosion rang from a magnificent pagoda that seemed more like an abode for fairies than a shop. Its lavish doors blew out in an explosion of shards as a person sailed through them, shocking the passersby on the streets.","“Ah, isn’t that the general manager of the Ouyang trading company? Who’s beat him up like this?” someone gasped when they recognized the man.","“As much as the Ouyangs have suffered over the past few days, they still possess deep foundations and are one of the seven great families of the empire. Who dares stir up trouble in their storefront and cripple their general manager?” A crowd gathered and registered the scene with shock and surprise.","They could clearly see a large hole in the general manager’s dantian. His golden core was broken and his cultivation of latter golden core was no more.","The demise of Ouyang Baitian and the others was no small blow to the family, but they were a massive entity in the empire at the end of the day. Their business ran back thousands of years and no one knew how many nascent soul powerhouses existed among the clan.","“This young master just wants to start a tab for a few million upper spirit rank stones. How dare you hem and haw and not jump to it? Have you had enough of living?!” A lordly voice echoed from the headquarters of the Ouyang trading company. “Damn you’re poor. How does the vaunted general manager of the Ouyang trading company have only two thousand paramount spirit stones in his storage ring?”","The crowd collectively shuddered when they heard the imperious voice.","“Lu Yun? Has he lost his mind? How dare he start things in the Ouyang headquarters? Is Marshal Lu Tianling declaring war on the Ouyang Clan?” Hard swallows could be heard throughout the assembly.","“What’s going on here?!” A contingent of soldiers dressed in black armor cut through the crowd. They were led by a handsome man in his early twenties; there was a swipe of blue in the center of his forehead.","Twenty-three soldiers followed behind him—the city guards of the southern quadrant. Their leader was Captain Ouyang Shenghe.","He flew into a rage to see his family’s own trading headquarters be smashed in and the general manager crippled. However, he didn’t rush into brash action. Ouyang Xuan, the general manager, had been latter golden core. If someone of that caliber had been crippled, this was no place or time for him to charge in without second thought.","“Lu Yun!” He found the scavenging Lu Yun in the center of the storefront when he swept it with his consciousness.","“Aiyoyo, I wondered who’d come! So it’s the honorable Master Ouyang Shenghe of the city guards! This young master has failed to welcome you properly, please don’t fault me for it,” Lu Yun responded jeeringly as he continued to search through the wreckage.","Formations and restrictions abounded in the building, but this level of deterrence was as good as nothing to Lu Yun. A few simple hand seals were sufficient to dismantle formations that could withstand a full strength blow from a latter golden core powerhouse.","“Oh? A Profound Exalted Stone? This is fifth rank material, nice!” Lu Yun waved aside a restriction and took out a jade-green stone the size of a fist. He grinned merrily at it.","“Go, stop them!” Ouyang Shenghe set aside caution when he saw that it was Lu Yun. He charged in with his men, fully on guard against the young man’s deathsworn. Both the Ouyangs and Yuwens knew that his bodyguard was playing the pig to eat the tiger—he was at least latter golden core!","Ouyang Shenghe rushed in to find almost pure rubble. The first floor had been decimated and some of the storage rooms had been blown out. If it wasn’t for a powerful formation protecting the entire building, the Ouyang trading headquarters might already be level ground by now.","It’d been Ouyang Baiyi holding down the fort at headquarters. With his demise a few days ago and the rest of the nascent soul Ouyang elders preoccupied elsewhere, the clan was yet to assign someone to take his place. Thus, Lu Yun sauntered in to take advantage of the opening.","More than thirty percent of the clan’s wealth was concentrated at these headquarters—and that was just in terms of spirit stones! Its stores of natural treasures, precious ores, weapons and equipment, talismans, and pills were too precious to be assessed.","Lu Yun rushed in like a starving wolf in a herd of sheep and plundered everything he set eyes on, leaving nothing behind.","“Good thing this young master brought enough storage rings today! Just one wouldn’t be enough to hold so much stuff!” Lu Yun gleefully strung a bunch of storage rings together and hung them around his neck.","Storage ring capacity was limited and his were the most premier of their kind in Darklake. They held nine meters worth of stuff at most, but how could nine meters contain all of the treasures and wealth at the Ouyang trading headquarters?","Ouyang Shenghe’s eyes spat fire. There were five floors to the building and three of them had been emptied out. Not even a feather was left on the ground! He finally saw Lu Yun when he raced to the fourth floor with his men. The Lu young master was dressed in white robes and directed six inscrutable cultivators dressed in black in destroying the restrictions on the fourth floor.","Lu Xuan stood behind his master, the hint of a smile playing on his aloof face.","“Stop!” Ouyang Shenghe was about to lose his mind. He was grinding his teeth so hard that his gums were nearly bleeding.","The family could recover the lost wealth if they took a stand. If they demanded justice from the imperial family, they could wrest it all back from the Lu Clan. But the formations and restrictions being destroyed were the product of thousands of years of painstaking work. The methods for some of their formations had been lost to time!","“Continue, ignore him,” Lu Yun waved at his men.","“You court death!” Enormous energy ripples burst out of Ouyang Shenghe and he pushed off both feet, barreling toward Lu Yun.","“Piss off!” Lu Yun snorted and slightly shifted to the side, adroitly evading his attacker. He kicked out his leg and stomped on Ouyang Shenghe’s face.","Pfft!","Ouyang Shenghe flew back just as swiftly as he came, nose bleeding and teeth broken.","“A puny latter foundation establishment dares throw his weight around this young master? That old fellow was right, Ouyang Shenghe is trash.” Lu Yun lifted his head proudly while the remaining twenty-three city guards looked on with shock.","Three months ago, Ouyang Shenghe had beaten young master Lu to the point of the latter being unable to get up. His life hung by a thread, but now he was able to send Ouyang Shenghe flying with one kick?","Ouyang Shenghe was latter foundation establishment, but Lu Yun was just qi refinement!","“There’s no need to be so surprised. If Ouyang Shengxiang can beat up a foundation establishment cultivator, there’s no reason why a stunning genius such as this young master cannot.” Lu Yun flipped his long hair and flicked out a talisman. It streaked into a ray of yang metal energy and smashed into a critical node of the wood attribute formation in front of him. The active formation shattered with a roar.","Dressed in black outfits and equipped with Transformation Jade, Yu Qianhua and the others curled their lips. Ouyang Shengxiang had been personally tutored by Bloodbath and hailed from an august clan. Of course she was no ordinary person.","The foundation establishment cultivator she’d beaten up was just a northern quadrant civilian. He’d been lucky enough to establish his foundations, but remained at initial foundation establishment without any cultivation methods. His usage of true origin was crude and he knew only the most basic of techniques. How was he a match for Ouyang Shengxiang?","Meanwhile, Lu Yun’s opponent was Ouyang Shenghe, a latter foundation establishment who’d received tempering in the army.","Yu Qianhua and the others understood that this seemingly useless wastrel was actually a genius who’d hidden himself well. They’d committed to memory Bloodbath’s assessment of Lu Yun.","After breaking the final formation of yi wood, the fourth floor was open to their plundering. All of the rooms were leveled and Lu Yun even located some hidden formations.","“Let’s go to the fifth floor.” Lu Yun peered down his nose at the bedraggled Ouyang Shenghe, struggling to crawl up from the ground.","Revenge? Of course he was going to have his revenge. But so what if he crippled the Ouyang young master or even killed him? Having him wish for death was the true revenge.","Plus, it was more useful to have him alive for the moment.","“Captain...” The twenty-three city guards didn’t know what to do as they watched their leader crumple into a heap on the ground.","“Stop them and kill the six in black. As bold as Lu Yun is, he doesn’t have the guts to attack the city guard!” A few more teeth fell out of Ouyang Shenghe’s mouth as he spoke.","The city guards looked at each other with rueful smiles. Didn’t dare attack the city guard? Then what was with the teeth that just fell out of your mouth, second young master Ouyang?","However, they didn’t dare defy direct orders. Shoving and pushing each other, they came to the fifth floor as well.","“I recommend that none of you stick your noses in this,” Lu Yun said coldly, casting sidelong glances at the twenty-three guards that’d just come upstairs."]},{"number":2225,"title":"Chapter 2225: Chapter 2167.2: Seeing Dao","paragraphs":["Chapter 2167.2: Seeing Dao","“Young master Lu, you are of noble status, but you are currently disrupting public order...” A middle-aged man at latter foundation establishment offered hesitantly.","“Disrupting public order?” Lu Yun chuckled. “Got it, I won’t disrupt public order then. You guys can return to your posts.”","“Um...” The group looked carefully at the stoic Lu Xuan next to his master, set their jaws, and left.","“Smart people live longer,” Lu Yun laughed.","He let Yu Qianhua and his men have the run of the place after breaking the formations and restrictions on the fifth floor. Lu Yun himself returned to the fourth floor and leered at the grimacing Ouyang Shenghe.","“So we meet again, second young master Ouyang...” Lu Yun stalked over to his fallen opponent.","“What do you want?” Ouyang Shenghe scooted over to the stairs. He hadn’t thought that his men would be scared off with just a few words and quite hated them at the moment. If he could stall for a little bit of time, he would be able to take out Lu Yun once his family’s experts arrived.","“To beat you, of course!” Lu Yun tightened his fists.","“Let’s see who beats who!” Ouyang Shenghe didn’t think he was weaker than Lu Yun. He was just caught off guard earlier. His fingers flickered through a sword seal and sent a ray of sword light at Lu Yun’s head.","The Lu young master tilted his head, evaded the light, and flashed to Ouyang Shenghe. He kicked his opponent in the dantian, making Ouyang Shenghe curl up like cooked shrimp in the middle of the floor.","Lu Yun bent down with delight and patted the ashen face. “Second young master Ouyang, who did you say would be beating the other up?”","He took out a blood-red talisman from his storage ring and slapped it into the other’s forehead.","“What, what did you just do to me?!” Ouyang Shenghe struggled with fear.","“It’s a secret!”","......","Lu Yun barging into the Ouyang trading headquarters alarmed quite a few people, but many more—including the Ouyangs themselves—didn’t think much of it.","Their trading headquarters was heavily fortified. Once the formations were in operation, not even Lu Tianling would be able to break them, to say nothing of other nascent soul powerhouses.","The entire building was protected by yet another formation, its power one of the strongest among all of the third rank cultivation nations.","Lu Yun was just a mere qi refinement cultivator. Even if he had a golden core guard by his side, he might be stymied by one of the formations of illusion alone. He might even be trapped or suffer severe injuries.","Thus, Ouyang representatives didn’t arrive until an hour after Lu Yun left. A very bizarre sight greeted them.","“Eh? What’s that? It looks like sausage links.” Thirty were in the Ouyang contingent led by a golden core family steward. He rubbed his eyes and took another dumbfounded look at their trading headquarters.","Harmony reigned outside the building, as if nothing had taken place. The only sign of anything out of the ordinary was a crowd gathered in front of the doors. People pointed and laughed at the links of something up in the air.","“Let’s take a closer look at what Lu Yun has up his sleeve.” The steward sped up his pace.","“Um...” Astounded expressions appeared on the Ouyang representatives when they drew closer. Those weren’t sausage links—those were people stripped of their clothes and hung outside the building!","Their clothes were the rope stringing them together and they didn’t have an undergarment to their name!","“What... is... going... on?” The group froze, not knowing what to do.","“That’s... that’s general manager Ouyang Xuan!”","“Wait, that’s the second young master! It’s the second young master! Save him!”","Nonchalantly at ease seconds ago and ready to take Lu Yun into custody, the Ouyang contingent panicked and flew on their swords, frantically helping down the human sausages in the air.","Lu Yun had stripped everyone from the general manager to the errand boy naked, hanging them outside of the building. As for the maids and serving girls... he lived up to his reputation and took them all back to the Lu residence.","“Who did this?!” the golden core steward shrieked with outrage. Ouyang Shenghe’s meridians were fractured and his dantian heavily injured, but his cultivation remained. The young man hadn’t been crippled.","The twenty-three city guards cowering a few streets away looked fearfully in the direction of the Ouyang trading company, their hearts in their throats.","“Young master Lu is vicious! Taking revenge on Ouyang Shenghe like this is worse than killing him!”","“The struggles between the rich and powerful aren’t things that minor characters like us can be involved in.”","“But we ignored Ouyang Shenghe’s orders and left. His clan will take us to account for it, no?”","“Better that than dead,” the twenty-three guards conversed among themselves.","“Although Ouyang Shenghe is well known in the city, his righteous exterior hides a cruel heart. Yun Mo, all of you will certainly feel his wrath,” came another voice at this time.","“Captain?!” Vice captain Yun Mo trembled and he looked at the newcomer with shock.","“It’s been two months since I left, Yun Mo. How has your cultivation not progressed at all?” Yu Qianhua revealed his original appearance and smiled benignly.","Yun Mo looked at the outfit that his former captain wore and lowered his head in thought, understanding certain things.","“The young master wanted to eliminate all of you, but I begged for mercy since we’re brothers through life and death,” Yu Qianhua sighed.","Lu Yun had easily broken the formations within the building with his methods. This troop of city guards was the only witness apart from Ouyang Shenghe. The Lu young master naturally had his ways to ensure that Ouyang Shenghe kept his mouth closed.","“We don’t know anything,” one of the guards responded with difficulty. Although they faced only Yu Qianhua, their former captain represented Lu Yun and possibly even Lu Tianling. If Lu Yun wanted to silence them, he had a thousand ways to ensure that they disappeared forever.","The Ouyangs and Yuwens had suffered immense disaster and their patriarchs were dead. No one would pay attention to a few city guards that went missing at this time.","“You do know,” Yu Qianhua shook his head. “Take off your armor and change into what I’m wearing. You will be part of the Lu Clan from henceforth. Your families will receive their protection as well.”","Twenty-three identical outfits appeared in Yu Qianhua’s hands. These were all his men and they’d endured life and death on the battlefield together. He knew their backgrounds well.","“You can choose to accept with false pretenses, but the young master says that only smart people deserve to live long.” Yu Qianhua looked in another direction. There was a coolly detached man dressed in a black combat outfit, standing stiffly upright like a spear.","“Captain, we’re willing to follow you. I trust that you won’t harm us.” Yun Mo raised his head and looked at Yu Qianhua.","His captain sighed with immense relief. “My good brothers!”","......","In an exquisite private room on the third floor of Immortal Gathering.","Lu Yun sat primly in his seat, a rare expression of seriousness on his face. Across from him was a young man in white robes. He was calm with a pleasant smile.","“Brother Situ, Prince Situ, Your Highness the ninth prince. How long has it been since our last meeting?” Lu Yun subconsciously scooted his seat cushion closer to Situ Yun.","The prince smiled wryly.","“I say, old brother Lu. Why did you call upon me today? You’re being so mysterious.” Situ Yun looked to be a young man, but he was actually in his forties. He was a nascent soul cultivator and one of the three gentlemen of the capital. He was also the greatest genius of the imperial family.","The Darklake imperial family possessed an uncommon relationship with the Lus. If it wasn’t for their help, Lu Tianling wouldn’t have been able to establish the Lu Clan. He would’ve long been swallowed by the other six families.","Lu Yun and Situ Yun were on good terms, but they weren’t as close as he was with Zhao Chenguang and Yu Shuai. Prodigals of a feather flocked together; Situ Yun was too upright.","Ninth prince Situ Yun had trained with Lu Tianling from an early age. He could be considered the marshal’s disciple, even though they hadn’t formally cemented that relationship.","“Ahem...” Lu Yun coughed dryly. “It’s nothing major. You know how I have the Vermilion Bird command token, Brother Situ?”","“You want to rebuild it?” The prince assessed Lu Yun like he was meeting the Lu young master for the first time.","“You know as well as I do that things are a bit chaotic in the capital right now. I might die anytime I set foot outside my front door, so it’ll be a lot safer if I have some men around me,” Lu Yun tried to gloss things over with this excuse.","“Using an entire army troop as your bodyguard...” Situ Yun looked strangely at the other. “You only need to submit a report to the Ministry of Military Affairs if you want to rebuild the Vermilion Bird, but you’ve come to me...”","“I want to ask Brother Situ for a favor. Can you reassign the Vermilion Designation to my personal name?” Lu Yun finally revealed his true intentions.","“You want to build a private army?” Situ Yun immediately understood.","Lu Yun nodded."]},{"number":2226,"title":"Chapter 2226: Chapter 2167.3: Seeing Dao","paragraphs":["Chapter 2167.3: Seeing Dao","Each of the major Darklake families possessed a private army. They were formed at the clan’s behest to safeguard important territory such as the family mines or clan headquarters. The Lu Clan also possessed its own army.","“That’s easy,” Situ Yun smiled. “It’d be slightly out of the question if you want to turn the Darklake army into your private army, but the Vermilion Bird is no more. Only its military designation remains, so I can make the call and give it to you if you wish.”","Situ Yun was the imperial family’s foremost genius and his words carried a certain weight in the family. Emperor Situ Wenxian doted on him, so he did indeed possess this level of authority.","“My thanks to Brother Situ,” Lu Yun smiled.","“Situ Yun, my ninth younger brother, you’ve got some nerve to casually give away military designations like this. Our royal father didn’t give you this kind of authority!”","Bam!","The door to their private room exploded and its defensive formation likewise shattered. A burly man charged in with a few other people.","Lu Yun frowned and glanced at Situ Yun—the prince looked on with an unpleasant expression.","“Crown Prince.” Situ Yun addressed the newcomer. The intruder was the crown prince of Darklake Empire—Situ Jie—the heir to the throne.","With Situ Jie’s cultivation and acumen, he was sure to ascend to the throne when the emperor ascended beyond nascent soul and left for a fourth rank cultivation empire. The unexpected appearance of Situ Yun posed no small threat to him. His younger brother was backed by Lu Tianling and the throne would be unequivocally his if the old marshal fully supported Situ Yun.","The other six families of Darklake Empire very rarely involved themselves in the matter of succession. It was why they’d prospered for such a long period of time.","The Lus, however, were different. It’d been less than one hundred years since their founding and their roots did not run deep. If they supported Situ Yun and he became the emperor, he would most certainly wholeheartedly reinforce the Lu Clan. The family might advance by leaps and bounds in a very short period of time.","This kind of win-win situation was what Situ Jie was most concerned about.","“It looks like the crown prince has brought the Mo Clan to your side and won their support.” Lu Yun relaxed his straight posture and laid back on the seat cushion.","Situ Jie blinked.","“That does indeed look to be the case,” Situ Yun frowned. “Immortal Gathering’s private booths are isolated by formations, preventing consciousness and sound from piercing them. How would big brother know of my conversation with young master Lu if not for the support of the Mo Clan?”","“It’s just a parlor trick not worth mentioning,” came another voice behind Situ Jie. A small, thin man with a squirrelly expression on his face darted out.","“Indeed, just a parlor trick not worth mentioning!” Situ Jie burst into laughter when he saw the man.","“You are the genius of Profound Wing Empire, Yong Heyu?” Situ Yun lowered his voice.","“Yong Heyu greets Your Highness the ninth prince,” the man responded with a smile.","Profound Wing Empire was one of Darklake’s two major vassals and a second rank cultivation empire. Yong Heyu was its foremost genius and had come to Darklake after coalescing his nascent soul. He’d joined the crown prince’s faction and became Situ Jie’s strategist.","The resources of a second rank cultivation empire were insufficient to support nascent soul cultivators from advancing further. If they wished to progress, they needed to move to a more sophisticated nation. Most nascent soul cultivators from second rank empires voluntarily joined third rank nations.","As for fourth rank... nascent soul cultivators from second rank empires would not be highly valued in a fourth rank empire and wouldn’t receive many resources. They would be far more important in a third rank empire.","“You can see through Immortal Gathering’s formations? Or do you have a special treasure on you?” Lu Yun asked lazily as he sprawled on his cushion.","“That’s for me to know,” Yong Heyu huffed while he cast a sidelong glance at Lu Yun. “Young master Lu, His Highness the crown prince is here, but just look at you. Did your parents not teach you manners? Or were you born out of a trash heap and your parents didn’t want you?”","Irritation brewed in Yong Heyu’s heart when he saw Lu Yun’s attitude and expression. He’d conducted an in-depth investigation of the Lu Clan before this. Lu Tianling was a genius who rose to prominence in Darklake Empire and was formerly the greatest in the Wing Empire. He’d been born a few hundred years earlier than Yong Heyu.","In Yong Heyu’s world, there would be the Yong Clan in Darklake Empire and not the Lu Clan if they’d been born at the same time!","He’d thrown himself under the crown prince’s banner because he wanted to borrow the future emperor’s strength to establish a Yong Clan!","“Yong Heyu?” Lu Yun raised his head with a supercilious smile. “This young master doesn’t care if you’re a number one genius or number two idiot. I don’t care whose dog you are, but since you’ve bitten me, this young master will have you die.”","Parents would always be his weak spot! It was a pain that overrode everything, one beyond the three thousand lifetimes...","Lu Yun had reincarnated three times—from earth to the world of immortals and then to this world. In all of his lifetimes, he’d never had parents.","It hadn’t been his reincarnation when he became Yushi Moli—he’d just been borrowing the young man’s body. That was entirely different from him becoming the Lu Yun of this world through the cycle of reincarnation.","He was newly arrived when his parents in this world met with disaster and died. His ludicrous acts and utter depravity since childhood were a form of trauma expression. Killing intent rose in his heart to hear Yong Heyu bring up a pain point.","“You’re Lu Tianling’s grandson, aren’t you? I’d like to see who is it that dies today!” Yong Heyu grinned savagely in his anger and raised his hand, throwing himself at Lu Yun’s neck. Situ Jie smirked and didn’t stop the man.","Bam!","Thump!","Yong Heyu flew backward like a cannonball, plowing through the wall and crashing to the street outside. He broke an untold number of things on his way out.","An aloof young man dressed in long ivory robes and a beautiful piece of jade hanging from his waist had appeared at some point in time.","“I show you mercy today on behalf of the crown prince. If you, Yong Heyu, dare set foot in any Mo business in the future, I will kill you.” The young man’s voice spread through the vicinity, clearly audible throughout Immortal Gathering and the streets adjacent to it.","Yong Heyu scrambled up from the ground and glared at the restaurant with seething resentment.","“The three gentlemen of Darklake? Heh heh heh heh heh...” he leered.","......","“Yong Heyu violated the privacy of Immortal Gathering’s guests, so we must offer an explanation. No one will dare patronize our establishment in the future if we do not. I trust you do not mind, Your Highness?” The young man remained just as aloof while addressing Situ Jie.","“He’s just a dog. You’re saving this prince a bit of effort, young master Yue.” Nothing flickered through Situ Jie’s expression and he responded pleasantly, but Lu Yun could read the lurking brutality hidden behind it.","“Very well,” the young man nodded.","How is Mo Qiyue’s cultivation this terrifying? Isn’t he supposed to be the weakest of the three gentlemen? The energy ripples he gave off earlier put him on par with number nine. Situ Jie seethed inwardly, but there was nothing he could do. The young man in front of him was the most mysterious of the three gentlemen—Mo Qiyue.","Mo Qiyue kept to himself and rarely appeared in the public eye. He never displayed his cultivation in front of others. Although people knew he was a nascent soul cultivator, no one knew how strong he was.","Of the three gentlemen, Ouyang Shengtian had been the first to break through and form his nascent soul. Situ Yun was second, and Mo Qiyue the last. Situ Yun had once said that he was less than Ouyang Shengtian, so the hierarchy of the three was deemed in the order that they broke through.","Situ Jie inclined his head at Mo Qiyue and took a deep look at Lu Yun before whirling around to leave.","“Brother Situ, young master Lu, what happened just now was our oversight. Your meal is on the house today.” Mo Qiyue spoke in indifferent, emotionless tones. He nodded at Lu Yun and Situ Yun before drifting away.","“Mo Qitian... tsk tsk, he hid things well. He’s no simple character.” An amused smile played on Lu Yun’s lips as he watched Mo Qitian’s departing back.","“No simple character?” Situ Yun curled his lip. “That’s an enormous understatement. I think Ouyang Shengtian became very satisfied with himself when I said I was less than him and he actually thinks he is the greatest among the younger generation.”","“Oh?” Lu Yun smiled.","“I battled Mo Qitian once,” Situ Yun took a deep breath. “Three moves. I lost in three moves.”","Lu Yun raised an eyebrow.","“We were both golden core at the time and haven’t sparred since we coalesced our nascent souls. I don’t know how strong he is now,” Situ Yun chuckled. “The Mo Clan has been around longer than Darklake Empire has. You can’t possibly think that Admiral Lu’s clan once really did eclipse the Mo Clan. I’d believe it if it was said that the Mos have soul projection cultivators!”","etvolare's Thoughts","Why the author decided to do this with the lengths and new worlds at the end of the series really baffles me. How is this enjoyable for anyone? You guys got answers? I got none."]},{"number":2227,"title":"Chapter 2227: Chapter 2167.4: Seeing Dao","paragraphs":["Chapter 2167.4: Seeing Dao","Lu Yun first shook his head, then nodded solemnly.","Situ Yun smiled. “It looks like your reputation of a bumbling prodigal who knows nothing is the furthest thing from the truth.”","“Bumbling? Prodigal? Know nothing? That’s a load of nonsense from other people,” Lu Yun curled his lip. “Brother Situ, you can’t possibly think that a mere Lu Yun could be the downfall of the mighty Lu Clan?”","Situ Yun nodded solemnly without missing a beat.","Lu Yun rolled his eyes and didn’t want to talk to the prince anymore. It was... true.","......","Night, the Lu residence.","Lan’er was asleep. As he watched her, Lu Yun felt that she reminded him of someone. A name that shouldn’t exist popped into his mind.","Wanfeng.","The name flashed through his thoughts and dissipated upon the night air. Lu Yun was sitting in his yard and thinking over a few things from the day.","“Mo Qiyue is much stronger than Ouyang Shengtian and Situ Yun. His methods are beyond the world of cultivation.” Lu Yun frowned, finding the Mo Clan a bit mysterious.","He was familiar with Situ Yun’s strength because his grandfather had taught the prince. Of crows, he’d further studied the genius prince because he wanted to locate a strong backer for himself.","“The Mos... I hope you’re not what I think.”","The Lus had enemies and their enemies came from a strong background. His parents had died to those enemies. When Mo Qiyue struck earlier in the day, the energy ripples coming from him had made Lu Yun’s heart sink. It wasn’t the strength that a cultivator from a third rank empire should possess.","Lu Yun was even beginning to suspect that the Mos had something to do with his family’s enemies, or if they’d been infiltrated by the enemy.","“Oh?” His lips curved upward as a large surge of goodwill came from the south. The Seal of the Multitudes exploded with scintillating light, converting the enormous sum of goodwill into Hongmeng true qi. The converted energy surged into the “dao” character of Lu Yun’s dantian.","“I am now peak first turn and a half step away from second turn... What a pity that I didn’t break through,” Lu Yun exhaled after twenty breaths of time. “Bloodbath has finally truly given his allegiance to me. If goodwill still hadn’t sparked from him after this time, there would be nothing for me to do but kill him and take his head to collect the bounty.”","He stood up and looked to the south.","Goodwill carried the emotions of their originator, enabling Lu Yun to confirm if the other was truly loyal to him or building a relationship under false pretenses.","These methods... were so similar to the tree of his subconscious.","After robbing the Ouyang trading headquarters earlier in the day, Lu Yun spent the afternoon refining a pill from a large sum of looted ingredients and gave it to Bloodbath.","The elder’s wounds began healing after he took it, which was why he’d generated so much goodwill. He was genuinely thankful to Lu Yun from the bottom of his heart.","If his injuries had taken a turn for the better, but he still wasn’t grateful to the Lu young master, that would mean he was a heartless wretch who could very possibly stab the young man in the back at any time. After all, he’d sworn fealty to Lu Yun, but he was yet to do anything for the young man.","If it was Lu Tianling or Lu Xiaochi in Bloodbath’s position, neither of the two would be grateful to Lu Yun. They were family, so whatever action was taken was only to be expected.","Bloodbath was once a combination powerhouse. The higher the cultivation level, the stronger the goodwill. Just his alone was sufficient to bring Lu Yun to the brink of breaking through.","“It’s up to me to actually ascend.” Lu Yun wasn’t in a hurry to seek out the elder. He knew that his pill was sufficient to reconnect meridians and restore Bloodbath’s freedom of movement. It could even help his true origin operate again, but it couldn’t address the root of his injuries.","A paramount rank spirit stone appeared in Lu Yun’s hand and he slowly closed his eyes. The amount and quality of qi contained within a paramount rank stone was far in excess to an upper rank stone.","Dense qi flooded his body and assimilated into the Hongmeng true qi. The first turn of the Seeing Dao chapter operated furiously, pulling him in a state of zen.","Lu Yun’s mind and heart were free of all thought. An extremely profound ripple grew in all directions and he felt that his mind and body were fully clear.","“Is this dao?” He felt that he was floating in the cosmos and among the brilliant splendor of the stars. In this moment, he seemed to see the dao that countless cultivators and living beings yearned for.","Such was the meaning of the first of the Nine Chapters of Dao—to see dao.","It was an indescribable presence that could not be put into words, as if all of the meaning of life was contained in that paradoxical dao.","Dao was dao, but it was not eternally dao. Lu Yun was proceeding down this path step by step. His ultimate goal was to become heavenly dao. He would cultivate the heavenly dao as a living being, then become the guardian of all existence and battle the will of the nothing.","Thus, he had to forget his past for now and devote himself to becoming dao. He possessed his own daos in the past. He’d mastered the nothing and reincarnation—these were completely different paths with heavenly dao and great dao.","Unexpected consequences would arise if he remembered everything from before, to say nothing of the heavenly dao expelling him.","Rumble!","A radiant star burst in his mind and his eyes shot open. A meter of brilliance shot out, dismissing the illusions in front of him. His Hongmeng qi churned and charged in another direction, setting off a chain reaction that gradually solidified the ethereal energy.","The second turn of Seeing Dao.","Lu Yun remained seated and summoned another paramount rank spirit stone into his hand. His Hongmeng qi circulated furiously as he absorbed energy from the stone.","Hummm!","A ponderous will came from Lu Yun’s mind as five ripples wavered in and out of sight in the five carnival directions. The Connate Great Dao of the Five Elements.","The second heavenly dao combat art of the Seeing Dao chapter had appeared. It differed from the previous Petrification art as the latter came from the character in Lu Yun’s dantian. The Connate Great Dao of the Five Elements came from heaven and earth—a vastly different concept.","Petrification required the user’s own Hongmeng qi as the base and consumed an enormous amount of energy. The Connate Great Dao of the Five Elements, however, required no Hongmeng qi and needed only intent.","The stronger one’s mind was, the greater the power behind this combat art.","Lu Yun suddenly reached toward the south and materialized a dancing red flame in his palm.","“This is connate fire origin,” he murmured to himself. He probed the north and collected a sample of glistening water origin energy. “Another familiar combat art... I seem to have commanded something like this before. It’s more comfortable to use than that Petrification.”","As he muttered to himself, he knew that this was a combat art once controlled by his sealed memories.","“My cultivation is too weak at the moment. Even though Hongmeng qi isn’t needed for the Connate Great Dao of the Five Elements, I’m still limited in how much connate origin energy I can retrieve.” He dismissed the two samples of connate energy with a clap of his hands.","“But the Connate Great Dao of the Five Elements should be different from the one sealed in my memories. It’s just the same basics. I can borrow the five elements, but I can’t use them in any art.” Lu Yun cocked his head in thought. “And yet, that’s enough. The connate five elements are not to be trifled with. I need to coalesce my nascent soul first before I can use the connate elements as a foundation for some simple arts.”","He regained his cool and sat cross-legged, consolidating his new cultivation level of second turn Seeing Dao.","“I’ve finally established my foundation and can get rid of that restriction for second uncle. But I still need to make some preparations. Establishing the foundations for immortality is a very crucial step of cultivation.” Lu Yun swallowed a pill from his storage ring and grasped in the southern void, summoning a ball of fire origin into his hand.","He slowly refined it, strengthening his spirit root—a fire spirit root.","The cultivators of the world of cultivation were categorized by spirit roots of the five elements. During foundation establishment, they refined the appropriate element to enhance their spirit root. Someone like Lu Yun who refined the connate five elements during his foundation establishment was likely unheard of.","“I wonder how the Ouyangs will respond to me plundering their trading headquarters. The formations and restrictions have been erased and Ouyang Shenghe has turned into an idiot. They won’t dare take any brash action, will they?","“It’s the Yuwens’ turn next tomorrow, even if I fall flat on my face.”","etvolare's Thoughts","So that's what he did to Ouyang Shenghe."]},{"number":2228,"title":"Chapter 2228: Chapter 2168.1: Cerulean Sword Dragon, Suppressed Memories","paragraphs":["Chapter 2168.1: Cerulean Sword Dragon, Suppressed Memories","Lu Yun ultimately left the Yuwen trading headquarters alone. When the Yuwen Clan learned of what transpired at the Ouyang Clan, they sent three nascent soul elders to stand guard and moved most of the treasure at their trading headquarters.","Lu Yun pouted when he received the news and said nothing.","Meanwhile, the Ouyangs came by a few times, but were stopped outside the front door with the excuse that the patriarch was in closed door cultivation.","......","“In the three thousand reincarnations, one of my ultimate accomplishments was to use spirit herbs and medicines of the mortal realm to create the medicinal effects of the ninth legendary spirit herb of the world of immortals—the Shennong Grass. I then refined it into an immortal pill when I was just a cultivator.”","Lu Yun faced the pile of spirit herbs and medicines that he’d taken from the Ouyang headquarters and mused over them.","“These aren’t enough for the Shennong Grass. Its effects are also fierce—any below the soul separation level might immediately explode if they took it.” Lu Yun stroked his chin. “An immortal pill is a good bet, but if an immortal pill appears in a world of cultivation, it will trigger a pill tribulation. And once a pill tribulation arrives, that will lead all manner of riffraff to us.","“Besides, I’m so pathetically weak right now that I can’t refine an immortal pill. Mm, I’ll assemble some concoctions first and make preparations to resolve second uncle’s Severed Meridians Hold.”","His fingers fluttered through a few hand seals and propelled gleaming specimens of ingredients into the air. They landed in the pill cauldron in front of him, whereupon Lu Yun summoned a red flower of fire origin energy from the south. He directed it into the pill cauldron in the form of a scintillating blaze of flame.","Connate fire incinerated a multitude of ingredients and turned them into pure medicinal strength. They were continuously disassembled and reassembled through his manipulation.","Creating new medicinal attributes out of different ingredients was more than just mixing them together. Special methods were required in the process, making it much more complicated than simply refining pills or medicines.","Crack!","Lu Yun’s ears twitched as he caught a tiny disturbance. A fine crack had splintered the exquisite pill cauldron in front of him. Frowning, he changed his hand seals and dismissed the connate fire.","“This pill cauldron’s from the Ling Clan’s Lingtian Pill Pavilion. It’s just an upper rank treasure, no wonder it can’t withstand a connate flame.” He looked at the minute crack with frustration.","“This is my oversight. Grandfather has a lower rank pill cauldron, so it won’t hold up under a connate flame either. The Ling Clan is the pill refinement family of Darklake. It’s said that their clan treasure is a paramount rank pill cauldron. If I can get my hands on that...” Lu Yun was sorely tempted and couldn’t silence the urge.","“I might be able to modify a paramount rank treasure into a lower rank spirit treasure if I add a few things to it. A spirit rank pill cauldron should be able to hold a connate flame.” Lu Yun waved his hand and stowed the liquid in the broken cauldron, then left his residence.","......","“Senior Blood, how are you recovering?”","Bloodbath was dressed in long ivory robes and wore his dark-red hair loosely down his back. He sat in a small house located in the southern quadrant of the Lu residence, taking deep breaths as he faced the morning sun. Blood-red radiance sparkled around him.","Yu Qianhua, the five originally assigned to the city’s northern quadrant with him, and the later twenty-three city guards stood in the yard with their eyes closed in meditation. They were positioned in a bizarre formation.","“Latter golden core.” Bloodbath’s voice floated in and out of the air—a marked contrast to his previous feebleness. “I can immediately return to nascent soul if you can give me a spirit crystal.”","“A spirit crystal? Darklake Empire doesn’t have such things. Dark Orchid might, but they won’t easily take it out.” Lu Yun shrugged.","Spirit stones were spirit crystals, but spirit crystals were much more valuable. The qi contained within one lower rank spirit crystal was the equivalent of one hundred paramount rank spirit stones. However, no one was willing to trade one lower rank crystal for one hundred stones.","If spirit stones were defined as stones containing qi, then spirit crystals were crystalline structures formed from qi. There was nothing else in them apart from qi.","Spirit crystals were used by cultivators of high ranked cultivation empires. It would be an incredible treasure if anyone in a third or fourth rank empire laid hands on one.","“Then give me ten thousand paramount rank spirit stones. I want to set up Qi Accumulation Formation to recover my cultivation,” Bloodbath changed his request.","Lu Yun sniffled noisily, recalling the elder’s prowess. Ordinary objects were sufficient for him to set up a Reverse Five Elements of Absolute Slaughter. If he had ten thousand paramount rank spirit stones... he might redirect all of the capital’s qi into his formation.","“Latter golden core is enough, you don’t need to be stronger for now.” Lu Yun ignored the elder’s request.","Bloodbath looked at him.","“Do you remember the Canon of the Blood God that I talked about?” Lu Yun smiled.","Blood trembled and jerked his head up. The young man took out a jade slip from his ring and tossed it to the old man.","“This is the first half of the canon. It’s at least one hundred times stronger than that Method of Blood Shadows you’re currently practicing.”","Bloodbath infused the jade slip with his consciousness to study its contents.","“Did you create this?” He looked askance at Lu Yun.","The young man nodded. “The Canon of the Blood God is a very important affair. Although this is just its first method, it’s still much more important than you might think. Destroy the jade slip after you’ve committed it to memory.”","Jade slips were a way to ensure the succession of cultivation methods in the world of cultivation as there were many things that could not be captured by words or text. Only higher level methods were recorded in jade slips.","The heritage of cultivation methods was more so a heritage of great dao and an incomparable mentality.","Two people practicing the same method might find themselves proceeding in vastly different directions and reaping immensely different results. That was due to each person comprehending dao in different ways.","Text records in books and on papers were applicable for only lower level cultivation methods. Some of the larger families and sects recorded all of their cultivation methods in jade slips. They were locked by restrictions, making perusal impossible unless special methods were used to access them.","Bloodbath nodded and swiftly memorized the jade slip’s contents. He reduced it to dust with a clap of his hands. At his level, he could naturally tell how terrifying the Canon of the Blood God was and how much more sophisticated it was compared to the Method of Blood Shadows.","At the same time, he discovered that one had to use the Method of Blood Shadows as the foundation for the Canon of the Blood God, first reaching golden core with the former before moving on.","Bloodbath gave a long exhale and raised a cupped fist salute to Lu Yun. A moderate surge of goodwill rushed out of him and into the seal in the young man’s body. It wasn’t as large as the surge from yesterday, but it was still sufficient to consolidate Lu Yun’s foundations after setting foot into initial second turn.","There were limits to the amount of goodwill generated from one person unless Lu Yun became their god and the beholder of their faith. Otherwise, one person’s goodwill would steadily diminish even if they were increasingly grateful to him.","Gratitude, admiration, and faith—those were the three ways of obtaining goodwill that he’d identified. Gratitude and admiration were temporary, only faith was forever and would continue to produce goodwill. However, it was nigh impossible to inspire faith from a cultivator.","This seemed to be another difference from the tree of his memories. That tree collected the power of emotions, whereas the seal compelled living beings to worship the holder.","“Senior Blood, you are now latter golden core. If you use this method from the Canon of the Blood God, then you’re...” Lu Yun smiled at Bloodbath.","“Do you ask about my strength?” Bloodbath responded calmly. “Although I am just latter golden core for the moment, I still reign invincible in this nation even without the Canon of the Blood God.”","He spoke matter-of-factly as a combination level powerhouse, even if their strength had receded for the moment, was still invincible in a third rank nation. There was nothing to be proud of as it was only to be expected.","“Very good.” Lu Yun broke out into a large grin. “The Ling Clan possesses a pill cauldron as their family treasure. I would ask that Senior Blood pay them a visit and take the pill cauldron.”","“Take the Ling family treasure from their home?” Bloodbath blinked.","“Yes,” Lu Yun chuckled.","“That’s... that’s going to be a bit difficult,” Bloodbath frowned slightly. “I’m not afraid of anyone in single combat, but it will be tricky to visit a clan and seize their family treasure.”","Lu Yun looked at him wordlessly.","“Ah forget it, I’ll go. I just need some time to prepare,” Bloodbath chuckled ruefully. He’d received benefits from Lu Yun, so he couldn’t very well turn down the young man’s first request now, could he?","That would be too embarrassing."]},{"number":2229,"title":"Chapter 2229: Chapter 2168.2: Cerulean Sword Dragon, Suppressed Memories","paragraphs":["Chapter 2168.2: Cerulean Sword Dragon, Suppressed Memories","As savage as Bloodbath was, he was a principled person. Yu Qianhua and the others paused their training, looking at Lu Yun with surprise. It was understandable that the young master had robbed the Ouyang trading headquarters, but now he wanted to seize the Ling family treasure?","That was... that was so exciting!","A family’s ultimate treasure was the basis of their existence. The clan wouldn’t be far from destruction if it was lost.","He was going to uproot the Lings!","“Is this how you train in the army?” Lu Yun turned around and barked at the men. The twenty-nine jerked with dismay and calmed their hearts again, reentering meditation.","“Do you trust them so easily?” Bloodbath asked faintly with a glance at the young man.","Lu Yun nodded wordlessly. The goodwill from them was pure and genuine. They could be trusted. Plus, he believed his own eye for people—it was developed over three thousand reincarnations. Additionally, there was that even more mysterious lifetime that’d been sealed away.","Although it was inaccessible, he retained some instincts from it.","“This is a Stillness Talisman. It will quiet the energy ripples on you when active and conceal you from even nascent soul cultivators.” Lu Yun handed a talisman to Bloodbath.","The elder placed it in a storage ring and sat down cross-legged. Bloody radiance winked in and out of sight around him as he practiced the Canon of the Blood God.","......","“Do you trust them so easily?” A scholarly Lu Xiaochi appeared after Lu Yun left the house, holding a book and posing the same question as Bloodbath had. He, however, included the old man in his questioning.","“Use not people you suspect and suspect not people you use,” Lu Yun quoted with a smile.","“Very good! You possess the same charisma as your grandfather!” Lu Xiaochi roared with laughter.","Lu Yun pursed his lips and didn’t say anything. This was a walk in the park after three thousand reincarnations and three thousand worlds of experience recruiting people. When it came to Bloodbath... he’d fully lashed the old man to the Lu war chariot with the Canon of the Blood God.","“Aren’t you afraid of Bloodbath capturing you and forcing you to give the rest of the canon to him?” Lu Xiaochi stopped laughing.","“Only smart people live longer. Bloodbath being able to survive the joint search of the three ninth rank cultivation empires means that he is a smart person,” Lu Yun responded solemnly.","Lu Xiaochi blinked, not knowing what to say next.","“Bloodbath will visit the Ling Clan after a while and take their pill cauldron. I’ll be able to break your Severed Meridians Hold then, second uncle,” Lu Yun changed the topic.","Lu Xiaochi trembled and he whispered, “You mean... you’ve established your foundations?”","Lu Yun nodded.","“Your grandfather was right! Your potential is unparalleled and had you been willing to train since childhood, there would be four gentlemen of the capital!” The Lu second master smiled with gratification.","Lu Yun was only sixteen, which placed him on par with Ouyang Shengmu and Ouyang Shenghe. Ouyang Shengtian had established his foundations at ten years old and Lu Xiaochi... when he was six.","Four gentlemen of the capital? Are you insulting me, uncle? Lu Yun curled his lip.","“Right then, come with me.” Lu Xiaochi suddenly thought of something and walked toward the family vaults. Lu Yun seemed to grasp something as he watched his uncle and followed the man.","Latter golden core elder Lu Jiu was on duty and walked out when he saw Lu Xiaochi. He frowned and huffed disapprovingly when he saw Lu Yun.","“Uncle Jiu, please open the secret vault. Yun’er has established his foundations,” said Lu Xiaochi.","“Established his foundations?” Lu Jiu looked with surprise at Lu Yun and nodded slightly. “So you’ve finally lived up to the patriarch’s care. Come with me.”","“Secret vault?” Lu Yun blinked.","“We have the external vaults and a secret vault,” Lu Xiaochi explained. “What you see normally is our external vaults. The real treasure is kept within the secret vault, and I’m only letting you know about this because you’ve finally matured.”","Lu Yun smiled wryly. With his previous personality, he’d rush in and empty the secret vault if he’d known of it.","An expressionless Lu Jiu walked into the empty external vault and formed a few hand seals, sending a slight tremor through the structure.","Rumble!!","The formation guarding the vaults cracked open and the floor slowly split beneath them, revealing a long stairway that stretched into the ground.","“The secret vault is beneath. Second master, I will remain on guard outside while you enter with Lu Yun,” Lu Jiu said.","Lu Xiaochi nodded and strode to the staircase. Lu Yun quickly took out a storage ring from his own and tossed it to Lu Jiu.","“Elder Jiu, I’ve been a bit busy these days and didn’t have time to give these to you. I leave their contents in your hands.” He quickly shuffled after his second uncle.","Lu Jiu looked at the ring and curiously scanned it with his consciousness.","“Storage rings? What did he give me a storage ring worth of storage rings for?” Lu Jiu didn’t know whether to laugh or cry. There were more than fifty storage rings inside, enough to make a small pile.","“Storage rings are immensely valuable to ordinary cultivators, but they are nothing to the seven great families...” He took out a ring at random and sent his consciousness into it, wanting to see how much space there was inside. Subconsciously, he felt that the good-for-nothing young master of his family knew so little of the world that the boy thought even storage rings were precious.","“Um? Hmm? Hmm hmm?!” Lu Jiu squawked like a choking duck and made strange gurgling noises.","The storage ring was only nine meters wide, but it was filled to the brim with upper rank stones the size of a fist. There were at least one hundred thousand spirit stones in here!","Even with Lu Jiu’s cultivation of latter golden core, his heart couldn’t help but spasm painfully. When he recovered from his daze, he hastily took out all of the rings and scanned each of them.","“The wealth in these rings is more than what we had in our prime! Where did the young master get all of this from?” Lu Jiu stared fixedly at all of them and murmured, “As I thought, the young master of old was an act...”","......","“What did you just give Uncle Jiu?” Lu Xiaochi asked curiously when his nephew caught up to him.","“Whatever I don’t need from the Ouyang trading headquarters,” Lu Yun responded casually.","“The Ouyang trading headquarters?” Lu Xiaochi blinked. “You really robbed them?!”","Although he’d heard rumors of the Lu young master seizing everything from the Ouyang trading headquarters, he’d snorted and thought nothing of the wild stories. He knew what Lu Yun was capable of. Plundering wealth that’d been accumulated for over thousands of years? Even ten nascent soul powerhouses would be beaten to death and thrown out if they attempted to do so, to say nothing of his nephew!","“What, is there anyone else who can do the deed?” Lu Yun smirked.","“I thought the Ouyangs had released the rumors on purpose as a pretext to move against us again,” Lu Xiaochi said dazedly.","The Ouyangs had sent people to kick in their doors during the past two days, but Lu Xiaochi once again paid them no heed. He thought the family was using Lu Yun embarrassing them as an excuse to stir up trouble. Who would’ve thought that his nephew really had looted their trading headquarters?","It’d only been a few days, but the number one prodigal of Dusk City had committed numerous stunning acts. First he’d robbed the Lingtian Pill Pavilion, one of the top five in the capital, then killed the Ouyang and Yuwen patriarchs. And now he’d cleaned out the Ouyang trading headquarters!","“This is wealth that the Ouyangs have accumulated over thousands of years...” Lu Xiaochi’s heart clenched painfully.","“Pfft, oh ye of little experience in the world.” Lu Yun shook his head. This level of wealth was insignificant in his view. He’d only handed over part of his gains. Thousands of years of accumulation meant just the spirit stones at the headquarters was a fully thirty percent of the Ouyang Clan’s wealth. The pills, medicines, treasures, ingredients, and materials that he’d collected were far greater than the spirit stones.","Lu Yun had taken such a bite out of the family that he’d half crippled them.","Uncle and nephew reached the end of the staircase. They were three hundred meters below the ground in a space one hundred and twenty meters wide. Protected above and below by a formation of earth origin, night pearls were embedded in the walls. It was filled with incredibly precious treasures."]},{"number":2230,"title":"Chapter 2230: Chapter 2168.3: Cerulean Sword Dragon, Suppressed Memories","paragraphs":["Chapter 2168.3: Cerulean Sword Dragon, Suppressed Memories","“I wanted to see you surprised, but I guess I won’t be seeing that today,” Lu Xiaochi chuckled wryly.","“A spirit crystal??” Lu Yun saw a fist-sized, crystalline object at the center of the room.","“That’s right, a spirit crystal!” His uncle nodded. “That’s your grandfather’s most precious treasure and the last wealth of the family.” He paused, recalling what was in the ring that Lu Yun had just offered. “Erm... at least it was before.”","Lu Yun took a deep breath and inclined his head. It was just a lower rank spirit crystal, but it was probable that even the imperial family didn’t have something like it.","“There used to be more in the secret vault, but your grandfather used half of it to save you,” Lu Xiaochi continued.","Lu Yun understood. What the Ouyangs had done to him three months ago was mostly to exhaust the Lu family fortune and Lu Tianling’s nascent soul.","Lu Xiaochi walked up to a rack and took down a box made of jade. He gave it to his nephew.","“This is the inner core of the seventh rank spirit beast Aureate Seraph Bird.”","“A seventh rank spirit beast!” Lu Yun raised an eyebrow. That was the equivalent of a combination cultivator! This inner core would be priceless even in a ninth rank cultivation empire. The Aureate Seraph Bird was a premier existence among seventh rank spirit beasts.","“Your grandfather hunted the bird for you when you were born.” Lu Xiaochi looked meaningfully at Lu Yun.","“What?!” Lu Yun was finally startled. “Grandfather personally hunted down an Aureate Seraph Bird for me?!”","Being a premier existence among seventh rank beasts, it took a tribulation level cultivator to hunt one!","Lu Xiaochi was immensely satisfied to finally see shock and surprise on his nephew’s face.","“Yun’er, it is time to let you learn of some things since you’ve taken an immortal to be your master,” he sighed. “Your grandfather’s true cultivation is indeed tribulation level.","“He was attacked by our enemies when he weathered his tribulation and failed his attempt. But he survived, thanks to an extraordinary treasure on him. He was in similar condition to Bloodbath—he lost all of his cultivation.","“But your grandfather has now returned to latter nascent spirit and can easily take care of combination level spirit beasts. He thinks nothing of these great clans in Darklake,” Lu Xiaochi recounted, lost in recollection.","“Who are our enemies?” Lu Yun frowned. Tribulation level... was a peak powerhouse of the world.","“I don’t know, your grandfather never spoke of it to me,” his uncle smiled ruefully. “The less you know about some things, the better.”","Lu Xiaochi understood Lu Yun’s temper. If the young man knew who the enemy was, he would immediately take action. That would be bad for the current Lu Clan.","Lu Yun inclined his head. If his grandfather could kill a seventh rank spirit beast sixteen years ago, just imagine how strong he’d been in his prime! That also indicated how strong their enemy was.","“Your grandfather once said,” Lu Xiaochi enunciated carefully as he looked into Lu Yun’s eyes. “Is a ninth rank cultivation empire supposed to be strong? That is a title given by others.”","“That, I know.” In Lu Yun’s journeys through the three thousand worlds, though he didn’t spend any of them in this world, he’d gone to the world of immortals and some other worlds associated with this one.","He also knew that in the sealed experience, he’d visited even grander, more magnificent worlds that... made one despair.","“This universe is vast and without end. The world of cultivation is but the tip of the iceberg.”","And it is not the only world.","“Good, so long as you know.” Lu Xiaochi nodded with peace of mind. “Your grandfather exposed his whereabouts when he hunted the beast sixteen years ago, resulting in our enemies coming for us. Your parents died because of it and your grandfather was heavily injured. His cultivation is much less than before.”","“Grandfather is injured?” Lu Yun’s frown deepened. “He’s in closed door cultivation now, trying to refine all of the effects of the Violet Orchid Ganoderma. Ah, no wonder...”","“The enemy has infiltrated the great clans of Darklake. The Ouyang, Yuwen, and Ling Clan biding their time in the shadows have become their pawns. They are the shears with which to clip your grandfather’s wings.” This was when Lu Xiaochi looked oddly at Lu Yun. “Your grandfather and I both know about this, but there’s nothing we can do if the other only grasps you in their hand and does nothing.”","Lu Yun coughed awkwardly. His grandfather had once grounded him for a period of time, saying something about enemies of the family. However, he’d resisted in a very violent fashion and even protested by fasting.","In his eyes, Lu Tianling was the strongest in the capital and his greatest backer. All enemies would be reduced to dust in the face of his grandfather’s invincible might!","Lu Tianling doted on his grandson and could do nothing but give way. He had to watch as Lu Yun gradually wasted the accumulation of family strength that he’d built over one hundred years.","“What you’ve done recently is earthshaking enough. Although the world of cultivation has its rules, preventing the enemy from taking direct action against you, you should keep a lower profile. Otherwise, they will stop at nothing to kill the last heir of the Lus,” a solemn Lu Xiaochi concluded with a note of warning.","“Why should I keep a low profile?” Lu Yun asked with surprise. “Would I be me if I kept a low profile?”","Stop at nothing? Let’s see who stops less at nothing! I am the biggest prodigal now, not the saint of the past—hang on. What saint? Why do I think I’m a saint?","Lu Yun shook his head fiercely while his uncle stared dumbly at him.","“Don’t worry, second uncle, I know what I’m doing. Plus, I have master,” he chuckled.","“Your master? An immortal?” Lu Xiaochi chuckled ruefully. “Immortals are also restricted in the world of cultivation.","Lu Yun shrugged. Immortals were, but not the heavenly dao. Not to mention, he had a senior brother, the sky!","“Alright, alright, I know I can’t keep you in check.” A resigned Lu Xiaochi gave the inner core to Lu Yun. “You’re at foundation establishment now and as such, a perfect time to refine the five elements. Don’t waste this inner core, make sure to consolidate your foundations with it.”","Lu Yun solemnly received it and carefully put it into his storage ring. There was too much associated with this inner core.","........","Uncle and nephew met the stern Lu Jiu when they emerged aboveground. The elder was bouncing around like a happy gardener, merrily placing treasures on the shelves.","“Second master, young master, you’ve come out.” Lu Jiu gleefully hopped over to them. “Young master, where did you get all this? This sum of wealth is much more than what we had in our prime!”","“Haha, would the elder believe me if I said I robbed all of it from someone else?” Lu Yun roared with laughter.","Lu Jiu nodded emphatically. “When shall we commit another robbery?”","Lu Xiaochi: ......","......","Lu Yun kept to himself over the next month, not doing anything out of bounds.","Although the Ouyang trading headquarters robbery raised some waves, nothing else happened after that. The Ouyang Clan swiftly recalled some of their members and a tense atmosphere settled over the great family.","But apart from those actions, they didn’t seem inclined to pursue things further. Everyone could tell that they were planning to just let it go.","Lu Yun understood their frame of mind. They couldn’t hide that Bloodbath had escaped, followed shortly by their trading headquarters being attacked. Although they said that the Lu young master was responsible, who would believe that?","The Ouyang Clan couldn’t endure revenge from Bloodbath, so an investigation? That would be courting death. Bloodbath wouldn’t care about rules set by ninth rank empires if he started killing.","......","Dark City quieted down on this cloudy night.","Rumble!","An enormous disturbance rang from the city’s western front. The center of the Ling residence exploded.","“Who are you and how dare you touch our family treasure?!” A furious roar split the air as endless rays of sword light shot at the intruder.","“Hmph! You wish for death!” came a frosty response.","The clouds in the sky abruptly parted and revealed a bright, pristine moon. A fey young man dressed in long ivory robes and hair as dark as night stood in the air. He raised his arms and embraced the moon in the sky, summoning endless rays of moonlight into his hands."]},{"number":2231,"title":"Chapter 2231: Chapter 2168.4: Cerulean Sword Dragon, Suppressed Memories","paragraphs":["Chapter 2168.4: Cerulean Sword Dragon, Suppressed Memories","“Moon Slayer!” roared the young man as he chopped the air with his right hand. Rays of moonlight swiftly gathered in an enormous blade of light and smashed downward.","RUMBLE.","The countless rays of sword light immediately shattered and their owner spat out blood, falling to the ground. The blade of light continued unabated and crushed the Ling residence.","“Patriarch!!” Screams of woe and terror rang from the complex. The blade of light had split apart the patriarch of the Ling Clan, Ling Chongxiao, and their family home!","“This seat is but selecting a treasure today, so how dare a mere Ling Clan resist! This transgression cannot be pardoned. Killing only your patriarch is already an act of mercy, so you should be grateful!” The fey young man sniffed and headed to the outskirts of the city, sword light beneath his feet.","Humm!","A second ray of sword light rose from another direction as soon as he turned and shot straight at him.","“Another fool who’s had enough of living.” The young man turned around and sent out a blade of light, immediately shattering the sword light. However, it did its job and kept him where he was. A thin cultivator in gray robes appeared in front of him.","“How dare a mere golden core run rampant through Darklake Empire? Do you think there is no one left in Dark City?” Gray Robes was wrapped in a thin layer of mist, his features impossible to make out.","“No one in the vast Dusk City has stepped forward but you. You seek to make a name for yourself through me, don’t you?” The young man in white stared coolly at Gray Robes, derision playing on his lips.","The various sects and factions of the world of cultivation kept to themselves and very rarely stuck their nose in other people’s affairs. Although the Ling Clan was under attack, cultivators from the other families wouldn’t make a move unless the Lings requested help.","“Hahaha, make a name for myself through you? Is there anything about you that would help me?” Gray Robes roared with laughter. “You’re just golden core, but you were able to kill the latter nascent soul patriarch. You must have come into enormous fortune, so if I kill you, that fortune will be mine!”","Several nascent soul powerhouses flew out of the Ling complex as they spoke.","“Fellow daoist, thank you for stopping this cretin. The Lings will remember this debt of gratitude.” Senior elder Ling Tianfeng raised cupped fists at the stranger, then shouted, “Set up the formation!”","Seven nascent soul elders assembled into formation and blocked the young man’s avenue of retreat.","“Kill!” Gray Robes went on the offensive as soon as he saw the formation snap into place. His bright yellow sword exploded with sword light that was a few dozen meters tall and he directed it at the young man’s head.","His opponent also sensed that Gray Robes was different from his opponents thus far and took the oncoming conflict more seriously.","......","Lu Yun stood on the roof of his house and looked to the western sky.","“Bloodbath seriously thought way too highly of himself. He said that no one in Darklake is a match for him, but just a few nascent soul cultivators are keeping him in place!” He curled his lip and slapped a Transformation Talisman onto himself, flying toward the west in a streak of dull sword light.","The disguised Bloodbath was battling Gray Robes. Although he absolutely held the upper hand, his opponent was no pushover. The formation of seven Ling elders was in full operation and helped Gray Robes fight Bloodbath to a standstill.","Thousands of Ling cultivators stood on the ground, calling energy from the surroundings as they set up a certain formation. There were also numerous cultivators from other factions watching the fight—in particular a few nascent soul elders from the Ouyang Clan. They trembled with fear when they saw the young man in white robes.","Bloodbath, that has to be Bloodbath! Ouyang Zhen shrieked inwardly. Although his appearance and aura has changed, he’s definitely Bloodbath! Why has he gone for the Lings? He must have co-conspirators!","“Go home, the Ouyangs will not be involved with this.” Ouyang Shengtian was acquainted with Bloodbath since childhood. He recognized the figure in the air with a single glance and immediately called for a retreat.","He was deeply afraid that the old man would discover their presence.","Ouyang Shengtian wasn’t the type to let impulse take control; he possessed absolute calm. Bloodbath’s existence severely threatened the family, but he wasn’t naive enough to think that this was a good time to get rid of the old man.","The three ninth rank cultivation empires had posted a bounty on Bloodbath’s head for one hundred years, but the old man was still hale and hearty. If it wasn’t for him taking a wrong turn on his own cultivation and subsequently losing all of it, the Ouyangs wouldn’t have captured him.","Now recovered from his paralyzed state, he wasn’t someone that a third rank empire could contain—even if he was only golden core. Bloodbath escaping from their hands meant that he certainly had someone helping him.","However, inspiration struck Ouyang Shengtian. He had a wonderful idea to alleviate pressure on his clan.","......","“What is Bloodbath doing?” Lu Yun looked askance as he flew with dull sword light. The old man was starting to lose ground and his movements were turning messy. There were even sword marks on his pristine white robes!","“The Lings have lost a patriarch? That’s far from enough. If the Ouyangs decide to kill the Lings en masse...” It took only a brief moment for Lu Yun to understand what the elder intended. The more bedraggled he became, the more his original moves reverted to what Ouyang Shenghe and Ouyang Shengxiang would utilize.","Bloodbath suddenly formed a hand seal and created a massive wave behind him. Terrifying aura spread in all directions and the wave grew into a ball thirty meters across.","“The ultimate art of the Ouyang Clan—Waves Breaking The Heavens! You’re an Ouyang!” Ling Tianfeng cried out with shock when he saw the ball of water.","“Retreat!” Gray Robes also reacted with unwelcome surprise. “So you’re an Ouyang... hmph!” He snorted and raised his sword light to leave.","BOOM!","The cerulean water ball exploded into a mighty torrent that rushed toward the Ling residence below.","A Ling elder was obliterated upon being struck by the torrent. The nascent soul elder only had time for one agonized scream before he flew to pieces. The golden core and foundation establishment cultivators were even worse off. They stood no chance and were vaporized to the person.","“Heh heh heh, the Ouyang Clan? This seat is no Ouyang, I am their enemy! I purposefully learned their ultimate art to frame them!” Bloodbath cackled as he gazed down over the heavily damaged Ling residence.","Who would believe him now? Whatever he said was just an attempt to cover up the truth. How would an outsider learn the ultimate art of a clan?!","“No matter who you are, you will die tonight! A treasure that enables a latter golden core to wield so much power... I will have it!” Gray Robes erupted with a powerful aura and collected a dense array of sword light around him. He transformed into a sixty meter long dragon that twisted in Bloodbath’s direction.","“What kind of technique is this?!” Bloodbath gasped, sensing how terrifying the dragon of sword light was.","“The Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons!” Lu Yun also gasped. He’d seen this technique in his travels through the three thousand worlds—when he reincarnated through the world of immortals. It was a premier art in that world.","“No, wait!” Something seemed to explode in his mind. The Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons?! Vast Dragon Seaturner?!","This thing doesn’t belong to the three thousand worlds, it doesn’t! I have to suppress it, I have to keep it down! I can’t let the sealed off memories awaken!!","“I must have it, I must have the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons!” Lu Yun stared fixedly, a new obsession brewing in his heart. It was very important to him! He took a deep breath and tamped down the agitating memories in his mind.","“Freeze!” He pointed at the enormous dragon.","Pfft!","Lu Yun’s eyes widened with surprise as the dragon only stuttered momentarily before continuing toward Bloodbath.","“A spirit treasure level defensive item!” he frowned. Based on the Petrification art that he could deploy now, his opponent had to be three cultivation levels higher than him or equipped with a defensive item that was spirit treasure and above. The other wouldn’t so easily overlook the art otherwise.","At his current cultivation level, he could petrify nascent soul cultivators for a single breath.","Gray Robes was just initial nascent soul, but could ignore Lu Yun’s Petrification. That meant there was at least one spirit treasure level defensive item on him.","“Who is Gray Robes... He seems familiar...” Lu Yun rushed toward the man without any hesitation."]},{"number":2232,"title":"Chapter 2232: Chapter 2169.1: Sol Truefire","paragraphs":["Chapter 2169.1: Sol Truefire","Bloodbath was Bloodbath, after all. He was a legendary character who defined his generation. The elder shifted slightly and twisted nine times in a bizarre fashion, smoothly evading the enormous dragon of sword light.","Lu Yun came up to him, wrapped in a haze of dull sword light.","“I want this person alive!” he stated.","“Too hard.” Bloodbath recognized Lu Yun with a single glance, despite the young man’s aura and appearance being different. “He’s obviously reaped the inheritance of some powerhouse and he didn’t use his full strength just now.”","One who Bloodbath would call a powerhouse was at least tribulation level.","“He probably obtained the inheritance of some stunning heavyweight for the ages, which is why I want him alive!” Lu Yun cackled.","Bloodbath blinked. You want him alive? Get him yourself!","Massive chaos had engulfed the Ling cultivators; countless Ling disciples and descendants were injured or dead. Their complex lay in ruins as Bloodbath’s blow had shattered their defensive formation.","“Hmph!” Gray Robes erupted again and recollected his sword light. Two dragons hovered in the air this time and threw themselves at Bloodbath.","“Stay over there. As strong as this person is, he’s no match for me.” Bloodbath shoved Lu Yun aside and formed several hand seals, manifesting more cerulean waves from his body and ensconcing himself in a huge whirlpool.","“The Primordial Floods! It’s the Ouyang Primordial Floods technique! Ouyang Clan, do you intend to exterminate the Lings?!” Ling Tianfeng keened with the sorrow of seeing his family die in front of him.","Rumble!!","Bloodbath exploded with another wave that was three hundred meters tall and smacked it down on the sword dragons churning toward him.","RUMBLE!!","Two overwhelming forces crashed into each other in the air, scattering sword qi and waves everywhere. Their energy rampaged through the capital, eliciting shrieks and screams from the bystanders. Some didn’t have time to react before they were torn to pieces by the energy’s vibrations.","Whether it was Bloodbath or Gray Robes, both of them deployed power that was far in excess of nascent soul. Bearing the brunt of the fallout, countless Ling disciples flew apart as ashes and neighboring houses also suffered for their proximity. Their inhabitants wailed and screamed in agony.","Lu Yun frowned slightly, a trace of pity stirring in his heart. Was this his latent saint tendencies?","“As much of a bastard I am, I haven’t completely lost my conscience!” The young man set his jaw and flung out countless talismans. Each of them lit up and eroded the terrifying power unleashed in the air.","“Hah!” He took out a jade-green pill from his storage ring and crushed it, scattering its powder in jade-green arcs over the earth.","The Lu Yun of three months ago would’ve gleefully watched devastation run wild in the surroundings. No matter how many died, they were just numbers and nothing to do with him.","But after journeying through three thousand worlds and living endless lives, his mentality had undergone a tremendous shift. The more he experienced, the more he understood how precious life was, as opposed to becoming more detached.","Most important were his sealed memories. It seemed that he also fought for the good of all during that time. The Ling Clan was the enemy, but not everyone was at fault. There were also innocents among them.","Their disaster arose because of him, so he wouldn’t idly sit by. But neither did he feel much guilt because he wasn’t a good person to begin with.","Humm!","His eyes widened as the Seal of the Multitude flared with magnificent blue light. Goodwill streamed into it, originating from the ten thousand cultivators beneath him. The Ling Clan was among them as he’d blocked the terrifying energy ripples for them and showered restorative medicine on them. Goodwill from such a large sum of people was heaven-shaking for the current Lu Yun.","“They would probably hate me if they knew the truth...” The thought flashed through his mind.","Goodwill from the seal flooded into the dao character of his dantian, causing it to flare in turn and spontaneously raise his cultivation to mid foundation establishment.","“Stop!” He frowned and suppressed his raging cultivation. Goodwill was just a supplement. He would easily destabilize his foundation if he depended on it too much and create issues for later cultivation.","Lu Yun had already used goodwill to reach mid second turn. He needed to take some time to thoroughly temper his foundation and cultivate by himself. More importantly, he needed to fully understand every cultivation level to come in the first chapter and make preparations for the future.","Thus, Lu Yun was in no hurry to break through and stored the incredible amount of goodwill deep within the seal.","......","Up in the sky, the battle between Bloodbath and Gray Robes reached its peak. Gray Robes fully released his hidden strength and displayed the might of his spirit rank treasure. He had another spirit rank defensive treasure on his body, so the two combined made it impossible for Bloodbath to defeat him.","The elder’s flying sword was just a lower rank treasure that he’d obtained from Lu Yun. Other than that, his personal treasure was sealed in his dantian and inaccessible before he recovered his previous cultivation.","Gray Robes had two spirit rank treasures on him as well as the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons. The latter was a preeminent sword technique from the world of immortals. Although Gray Rovers couldn’t fully utilize its might, it was sufficient to help him fight the gravely restrained Bloodbath to a standstill!","“I always thought that I only needed to be wary of Lu Tianling, but to think that there’s someone like this in Darklake! He commands this level of battle strength at golden core. He can’t be allowed to develop further!” Gray Robes set his jaw. “The second move of the Cerulean Sword Dragons, Abyss Rising!”","He twisted and shrank the ponderous dragon of sword light, but his speed was more than three times before.","“Primordial Floods!” Bloodbath sneered and sent floodwaters cascading again.","RUMBLE!","A pillar of fiery light descended from the sky, heralding the arrival of an enormous bird of fire. It easily dispelled both the second move of the Cerulean Sword Dragons and the Primordial Floods.","“Daoists, please exit the city if you wish to do battle,” came a stately voice of imposing majesty.","“A replica beyond the body—a second nascent soul.” Bloodbath blinked when he saw the odd bird, then emitted a long peal of laughter. “As expected of the Darklake emperor, you refined the spirit beast Inferno Swan as a second nascent soul! It’s part of the divine Bi Fang beast’s bloodline—with it as your nascent soul, you stand a chance of becoming an immortal!”","“The bloodline of the divine Bi Fang beast...” Gray Robes’ heart clenched when he heard the identification. Jealousy, fury, and greed rose in his heart. All good things should be his! All fortuitous encounters should be his!","“Please exit the city.” The Inferno Swan looked coldly at the two combatants.","Back in the palace, Situ Wenxian looked on with resignation. These two fought with abandon in the capital and were beginning to threaten the entire city’s safety. They would level half of the city if they weren’t kept in check.","But all of the great families kept to themselves and no one was willing to take a stand. Thus, it was up to the emperor to take the field. His Inferno Swan was extremely strong as it possessed a divine beast’s bloodline. It easily broke up the fight for the time being.","“Hmph, it’s your lucky day.” A variety of expressions flickered through Gray Robes’ face with the Darklake emperor’s involvement. He grit his teeth and left amid sword light.","There was no sign of Lu Yun to be seen.","Bloodbath raised cupped fists at the emperor’s replica and followed Gray Robes out.","“Your Majesty, please administer justice on behalf of the Lings!” Ling survivors wailed on the ground, kowtowing fervently to the Inferno Swan in the sky.","One of the seven great families of the capital was no more after today. Their family treasure—the Wovenfire Cauldron—had been stolen. Half of the complex’s defensive formation was broken after Bloodbath pierced it through with Moon Slayer.","The energy ripples from the battle between Bloodbath and Gray Robes shook the rest of the complex into rubble. Many of their nascent soul powerhouses were dead. There were too many dead golden core and foundation establishment cultivators to be counted. A thousand years of accumulation had been destroyed in one night.","This kind of loss was far worse than what the Ouyangs and Yuwens had suffered.","Pity appeared in the fiery bird’s eyes before it sighed and vanished in the air, not saying anything else.","......","Lu Yun and Bloodbath flew through the western city gates, speeding toward a certain location.","“What, you couldn’t bear their suffering?” Up ahead, Bloodbath slowed down to keep pace with Lu Yun.","“Couldn’t bear their suffering?” Lu Yun blinked. “Why would I?”","“Then why did you save them?” Bloodbath snorted with laughter.","“Because I wanted to?” Lu Yun sniffed.","“Um...” Bloodbath paused, not knowing what to say.","“It looks like your mindset hasn’t reached perfection yet.” Lu Yun cast a sidelong glance at him. “Killing people, saving people, all are a function of my wishes. To think is to take action, my heart and mind are one.”","In other words, your daddy felt like it!","Bloodbath rubbed his nose wordlessly.","“Heh heh heh, you don’t let up, do you? And a tiny foundation establishment fellow came to watch the show as well?” A sinister ran in the air as Gray Robes had come back. He stood in front of Lu Yun and Bloodbath."]},{"number":2233,"title":"Chapter 2233: Chapter 2169.2: Sol Truefire","paragraphs":["Chapter 2169.2: Sol Truefire","“So it’s Yong Heyu.” Lu Yun raised a brow when he got a clear look at Gray Robes. The mysterious person who could fight Bloodbath to a standstill was the crown prince’s hanger-on!","“Yong Heyu keeps his cards close to his heart. He is an extremely calculating person and bided his time after Mo Qitian kicked him out of Immortal Gathering...” Lu Yun jerked with astonishment. He hadn’t thought that the powerhouse to deploy the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons would be Yong Heyu!","“Die!” Bloodbath wasted no time and struck.","“Aoou!” A spirited dragon croon exploded from Yong Hey’s body as a white dragon shadow materialized behind him. “Heh heh heh, no matter who you two are, both of you will die today.”","Yong Heyu crossed his arms in front of his chest as the dragon behind him flared with light. The light manifested as a terrifying ray of dragon-shaped sword qi that enveloped Lu Yun and Bloodbath.","“A dao weapon!” Shocked out of his usual composure, Bloodbath’s expression changed drastically.","Treasures were divided into five ranks of qi treasure, fine treasure, spirit treasure, dao treasure, and immortal treasure.","Dao treasures, even lower rank ones, were as rare as phoenix feathers and dragon scales in fifth and sixth rank empires. Bloodbath only possessed a paramount spirit treasure in his prime—he hadn’t owned a dao treasure either.","He never dreamed that a dao treasure would appear in a tiny third rank cultivation nation!","Its might could be described as cataclysmic. Yong Heyu had been able to match him when he wielded a spirit treasure. Now that he brought out a dao weapon? Bloodbath grew wary.","He has a dao weapon! Right, the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons is the ultimate technique of the Mindful Immortal Potentate of the world of immortals. He must’ve obtained parts of the potentate’s legacy, but what is the potentate’s legacy doing here?","The Mindful Immortal Potentate likely had much to do with Lu Yun’s sealed memories.","As his thoughts spun rapidly, Lu Yun quickly backed away. An enormous ball of sword light exploded from the flying sword beneath his feet and hurtled toward the sword dragon, attempting to offset it.","Wham!","A muffled feeling hit him in the chest as his lower fine-rank sword smashed to smithereens. He twisted several times in bizarre fashion, defusing the titanic power and borrowing it to retreat far away.","Rays of ominous bloody radiance sparkled around Bloodbath. They were now thousands of kilometers away from Dark City and there was no one around in the dead of the night. He didn't need to hide his strength anymore.","His energy of true origin from the Method of Blood Shadows had long since transmuted to true origin of the Canon of the Blood God.","“Hand Seal of the Blood God!” Bloodbath slapped his palm out, forming a blood-red palm sixty meters across. It loomed over the dragon figure and the ray of dragon-shaped sword light.","“As strong as a dao weapon is, you’re just initial nascent soul. Much of its power is inaccessible to you.” Bloodbath recovered his calm and snorted dismissively.","His palm and sword light negated each other in the sky. However, his face was pale from exertion and blood trickled out of the corner of his mouth. He was only latter golden core—withstanding a dao weapon also inflicted significant damage on him.","“Hahaha, I’m just initial nascent soul? And you’re just a golden core cultivator, listen to you talk!” Yong Heyu wiped away the blood from his lips and suddenly took on a startled expression. “Well well, it’s your lucky day, I will show you mercy for now.”","He transformed into a streak of dragon-shaped sword light and vanished swiftly in the night sky.","“Someone’s coming,” Lu Yun said with regret as he joined Bloodbath in the air.","“He bears a dao weapon. It’s impossible for us stop him if he wants to run,” the elder remarked faintly.","Sword light flashed as a man in white robes appeared before them.","“As I thought, there is the presence of a dao weapon here.” The man in white possessed dashing flair and looked around sharply, standing in the air with his sword grasped tightly. “Where is he?”","“You scared him off.” Lu Yun shrugged at White Robes.","“Do you know who he is?” White Robes flicked an aloof look at Lu Yun.","“Heh, you’re an interesting fellow. We’re the ones who destroyed the Ling Clan, but you make trouble for a righteous cultivator who sought to stop us,” Lu Yun smiled faintly.","“The Ling Clan? They have nothing to do with me,” White Robes responded calmly. “A dao weapon matters a great deal more and is the most important issue at hand. What does a traitorous Ling Clan have to do with me?”","“Are you the nation’s secret force?” Bloodbath murmured as bloody light receded from his eyes.","Every empire retained some hidden aces that were the foundation of their being. When Darklake triumphed over Tianlong Empire twenty years ago, it vaulted them to the strongest of third rank empires.","Given how strong Darklake was, it naturally had its trump cards.","White Robes looked at Bloodbath. “Your foundations are powerful to have such strength at golden core. If you join the Hidden Dragons, Darklake will have a chance of rising to a fourth rank empire.”","“Rise to fourth rank...” Lu Yun’s eyes gleamed.","White Robes remained looking at Bloodbath, waiting for his answer.","“Ask him. If he wants me to go, I’ll go.” Bloodbath carelessly pointed at Lu Yun with his chin.","Startled, White Robes turned to Lu Yun.","“We are all part of Darklake. All of her people have a responsibility to invigorate our nation!” Lu Yun declared righteously. “But we can forgo joining the Hidden Dragons.”","The Hidden Dragons was one of Darklake’s strongest armies. They once reigned triumphant everywhere they campaigned and vanished from the public eye after Darklake defeated Tianlong twenty years ago.","Who would’ve thought that they’d been concealed from the public and underwent secret training? They were the secret weapon that Darklake sought to use in their bid for fourth rank status!","But it made sense, Darklake Empire was already the strongest third rank cultivation empire. It naturally possessed ambitions to break free from Dark Orchid’s control and become a fourth rank in its own right.","Lu Tianling was a tribulation cultivator! He cowered in this third rank empire only because of his enemies. Everything was possible if Lu Tianling was present in Darklake. Lu Yun had also long sensed that the empire’s true foundations were likely far in excess of what was on display.","“Then I’ll kill both of you. The plans of Darklake cannot be exposed,” White Robes pivoted coldly. A flying sword appeared in his hand, illuminating the surroundings with frosty glare.","He was exceedingly strong, but it’d been Situ Wenxian’s second nascent soul who took action earlier in the capital. White Robes hadn’t appeared because the imperial family didn’t want to reveal Darklake’s secrets.","“His cultivation is soul projection. There’s a treasure on him concealing his true strength.” Bloodbath frowned as a keen light glinted in his eyes.","“Uncle Wu, grandfather said you were dead. You’ve actually ascended to soul projection, huh, and joined the Hidden Guards?” Lu Yun rubbed his nose. Feeling that there was no other way to resolve the situation, he removed his Transformation Jade.","“Young master? What are you doing here?” White Robes blinked.","Wu Wei and He Wuheng were Lu Tianling’s left and right arms in battle. Wu Wei set foot into nascent soul first and mysteriously vanished ten years ago. The outside world understood that his old injuries had flared up and died as a result.","Lu Yun had met Wu Wei when he was young, having a very deep impression of the stone faced, yet unexpectedly dashing Uncle Wu.","It looks like the Hidden Dragons are grandfather’s secret force. What is the relationship between grandfather and Darklake Empire?","Tribulation cultivator Lu Tianling was likely the only one who was able to pull the wool over Dark Orchid’s eyes and secretly raise a force like the Hidden Dragons. The Dark Orchid Empire was a fourth rank empire of long standing. It kept Darklake under close surveillance; the affairs of tonight and a dao weapon appearing in Darklake would likely make its way to Dark Orchid in the morning.","“What happened tonight involves the safety of the Lu Clan. Please keep this a secret for your nephew, Uncle Wu,” Lu Yun articulated carefully.","“Don’t worry, no one will know of anything tonight.” Wu Wei inclined his head. “Including the emperor.”","In his eyes, the Lu Clan came first, then Darklake. He was loyal to the empire only because of Lu Tianling’s order.","A smile appeared on Lu Yun’s face.","“Very well, this matter is at an end. I will return to make my report now.” Wu Wei suddenly thought of something as he was about to turn around and said, “Don’t try to shake the nation’s foundations. Darklake is the foundation of the family.”","He vanished amid a streak of sword light. Although he was a subject of Darklake Empire, he was loyal to the Lu Clan.","“To think that the waters would run so deep at a mere Darklake Empire! Even the fifth rank Barren Empire all those years ago didn’t possess this many layers to them,” Bloodbath sighed with emotion as he watched Wu Wei depart.","“Oh?” Lu Yun looked at the elder with interest. “Are a few soul projection cultivators sufficient for this level of judgment?”"]},{"number":2234,"title":"Chapter 2234: Chapter 2169.3: Sol Truefire","paragraphs":["Chapter 2169.3: Sol Truefire","“What do you know?” Bloodbath snorted. “Security is highly emphasized in the empires of the world of cultivation. With the three ninth rank empires at the head, each layer beneath them is subject to heavy surveillance. You aren’t able to picture the level of control that each higher rank empire exerts over its vassals! If word got out that a soul projection cultivator had appeared among Darklake’s Hidden Dragons, it would shock the entire world.”","Lu Yun remained silent, memories of the three thousand reincarnations playing out in his mind.","“Do you know the Celestial Realm Battlefront?” Bloodbath took a deep breath.","“The Celestial Realm Battlefront...” Lu Yun ducked his head, an expectant, yet also despairing feeling blossoming in his heart.","Disaster would come from the Celestial Realm Battlefront.","“The Celestial Realm Battlefront exists in an odd void, but it encompasses the entire world of cultivation. There is a heavenly book in its center. It is the basis by which all higher rank empires control lower rank empires. Whenever a powerhouse appears in a lower rank empire that should only appear in a higher rank, their name appears in the book.” Bloodbath looked into Lu Yun’s eyes. “There is a soul projection cultivator in Darklake, but you have somehow evaded the heavenly book’s senses.”","The elder paused when he saw Lu Yun’s expression and smiled. “That’s right, cultivators from lower ranked empires do not have the right to enter the battlefront. Only those from mid rank and above have the right to know about its existence and enter it.”","“Can you talk to me about the Celestial Realm Battlefront?” Lu Yun asked after a long period of silence.","The old man nodded as he sensed something off about the young man. “The Celestial Realm Battlefront is a magnificent existence. No one knows what kind of world it is and no one knows how it formed. Resources are plentiful, treasures are untold, and anything that cannot be found in the world of cultivation can be found there.","“Inheritances and dao weapons from primordial times, even immortal weapons, are available there. That is where I found my Method of Blood Shadows, not in the Blood Shadows sect of ten thousand years ago.","“Any cultivator or immortal who wishes to visit the Celestial Realm Battlefront can only do so through their consciousness. Physical bodies are barred from entry. After setting foot in that world, cultivators receive a new body that is limited to initial nascent soul.","“Thus, immortals who enter the Celestial Realm Battlefront will see their cultivation spontaneously decline to nascent soul. But resources, treasures, and opportunities are so plentiful in the battlefront that many are those who soar to new heights during their trials.”","Lu Yun nodded silently and indicated for Bloodbath to continue.","“But since everyone’s cultivation is the same in the Celestial Realm Battlefront, many cultivators keep themselves in check when they enter the world. Only the true geniuses who are invincible among their peers walk around with impunity and temper themselves.","“That world is incredibly vast, so vast that our world of cultivation is just a corner of it. The Celestial Realm Battlefront is the true stage for the strong. Humans, demons, monster spirits, and all manner of strange and exotic races can be found there. We fight over resources and treasures. The world of cultivation we are in is called the Jade Ruins World of Immortal Cultivation. The part of the battlefront that we occupy is the Jade Ruins Battlefront.","“True origin cannot be honed in the Celestial Realm Battlefront, but dao methods can be tempered. One can sense the great daos of the world and accumulate experience. When one dies in the battlefront, one’s spirit returns to the body instead of being lost in death. But an enormous blow is delivered to the spirit, resulting in injuries to the heart and mind at best, or being crippled at worst.” Bloodbath paused for air after he sketched the general contours of the marvelous world.","“So this is the Jade Ruins...” Lu Yun hummed in thought. “Do you know Slaughterless?”","“Slaughter... less?” Bloodbath blinked and rummaged through his memories. “Do you mean the powerhouse who swept the battlefront eight thousand years ago, Slaughterless?”","“Eight thousand years ago?” Lu Yun paused. Eight thousand years? It looks like master didn’t put me through imaginary reincarnations, but had me travel through space and time through real worlds.","Slaughterless was a name he knew from one of his lifetimes. There was a Celestial Realm Battlefront in that world and he was basically certain that it was the same as the Jade Ruins Battlefront.","In the Celestial Realm Battlefront that he knew of, Jade Ruins was renowned for being extremely weak.","One of Lu Yun’s burning questions was finally resolved. Everything he’d experienced in his reincarnations was real! Since all of those people existed, he could find them again! And when he did so, he could recover his forgotten memories...","That was his true goal.","Another point that Lu Yun was very certain of was that the heavenly dao had only sent him to the past. It hadn’t sent him to the future at any point. That would run the risk of the present Lu Yun meeting himself.","Lu Yun coming across Lu Yun? The heavenly dao would never create such a mess.","An unsettled feeling had sparked in his heart the first time he heard “Celestial Realm Battlefront” from his grandfather. In all of his reincarnations, he always ended up at the battlefront.","The journeys of three thousand lifetimes had created too many ties and concerns for him to sever. The battlefront was the only connection between his dreams and the current world. Only through the Celestial Realm Battlefront could he determine whether the worlds he’d traveled to were real or illusion.","He also knew that the battlefront was tied to a certain disaster—a disaster he could not prevent. He could only watch it happen to avoid repeating the past.","It’d hung over his mind after he awoke, and now the knot in his heart was no more. He even felt that he was breathing much more easily.","“Haha, time to go back, Bloodbath! That dao weapon and the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons will all be mine!” Lu Yun roared with laughter and summoned six meters worth of sword light, racing back to the capital.","Bloodbath gaped, having no idea what flight of fancy had just seized the young master.","“Slaughterless is a legendary figure on the battlefront and he disappeared after a battle eight thousand years ago. Does Lu Yun have something to do with Slaughterless?” the elder mumbled to himself. “That makes sense, the kid is quite mysterious and owns methods such as the Canon of the Blood God. Is it Slaughterless behind him?”","......","Early next morning.","Bam!","Someone kicked in Lu Yun’s doors startling Lu Yun, Zhao Chenguang, and Yu Shuai.","A glowering Lu Xiaochi roared at the latter two, “You two, get out!”","Zhao Chenguang and Yu Shuai shrank in on themselves and scrambled out of Lu Yun’s yard.","“Brother Zhao, Brother Yu, remember what I just said. Don’t share with anyone what I just gave you!” Lu Yun called out to their fleeing forms.","“Don’t worry, young master Lu! Only us two will know about it, no one else will!” Yu Shuai’s voice came back on the wind.","“Lu Yun, young master Lu, you’re quite a character, huh!” Lu Xiaochi took out a jade talisman after the two had left and covered Lu Yun’s house with a restriction. “Do you know how many cultivators died in the western district last night?!” His eyes nearly spat fire.","“Three to five thousand?” Lu Yun asked carefully.","“Three thousand five hundred and eighty-one!” Lu Xiaochi yelled. “Three thousand five hundred and eighty-one lives extinguished forever because of your decision!”","Lu Yun hadn’t kept his commands to Bloodbath a secret from his uncle, so Lu Xiaochi was nearly beet-red with fury.","“So what?” Lu Yun tilted his head. “The three thousand five hundred and eighty-one includes the Ling Clan, doesn’t it?”","“They are the vast majority.” Lu Xiaochi managed to bring himself slightly under some semblance of control.","“The other victims could’ve fled far away when Bloodbath fought Gray Robes, but they chose to draw closer to the action. Why is that?” Lu Yun raised his head. Although he did have a tendency to act like a saint, he didn’t have an overabundance of compassion.","Lu Xiaochi blinked.","“The dozen meters around the Ling residence is all Ling territory. Those people ran over because they wanted to see the Lings be destroyed and scavenge through the ruins,” Lu Yun snorted with laughter. “Since they wanted to be vultures, they needed to run the risk of dying. There are no free lunches in this world.”","Lu Xiaochi plopped on a stone stool and refused to listen to his nephew talk circles around him.","“Besides, tragedy wouldn’t have occurred if Gray Robes didn’t stop Bloodbath. If you want to assign responsibility, second uncle, I’ll have the elder come there.” Lu Yun moved to stand up.","“There’s no need.” Lu Xiaochi thought things through and quickly waved the lad off. Bloodbath? That was a perverse god of slaughter who’d killed a million cultivators by himself and almost ended a fifth rank empire. What did three thousand people matter to him?"]},{"number":2235,"title":"Chapter 2235: Chapter 2169.4: Sol Truefire","paragraphs":["Chapter 2169.4: Sol Truefire","“You should make some preparations, second uncle. I will remove the Severed Meridians Hold from you after three days.” Lu Yun took out a tea leaf the size of a fingernail. “Steep this leaf with fifty kilograms of water. Drink all of it within three days.”","“A single piece of leaf? Fifty kilograms of water?” Lu Xiaochi’s eyes widened as he stiltedly took the plain leaf. It looked like it’d already been brewed for a pot of tea before. He had no idea what to say.","“Remember, second uncle, at least fifty kilograms of water from a clear spring. Otherwise, you might explode after drinking the tea,” Lu Yun reminded solemnly.","“What kind of tea is this?” Lu Xiaochi asked dumbly.","“I got it from my senior brother. You won’t be able to find it in the world of immortals, much less the world of cultivation,” Lu Yun harrumphed mysteriously.","A light sparkled in the Lu second master’s eyes as he took a deep breath and carefully stowed the leaf. Lu Yun has a senior brother?","“You should put things out of your mind, second uncle. It was my lack of foresight last night. I’ll be sure to make a comprehensive plan next time there is an operation.” Lu Yun smiled at his uncle.","“Next time?” Lu Xiaochi harrumphed. “Next time??”","......","Unrest had shaken the capital again, but its residents seemed to be numb to shocking news. The Ling Clan had been razed to the ground, their patriarch was dead, and even their family treasure had been stolen. On top of it all, it was the Ouyang Clan responsible for the deed!","However, this occurrence seemed trivial compared to two other pieces of news.","Human demon Bloodbath had reappeared in the world of cultivation! He was behind the deaths of the Ouyang and Yuwen patriarchs one month ago. Neither was the white-robed young man who attacked the Lings last night from the Ouyang Clan. He was Bloodbath!","The second piece of news further stunned the nation. There was a dao weapon in Darklake! A treasure of such level might not be seen in even fifth and sixth rank empires, so to think that it would appear in a minor third rank empire!","Dusk City and the entire nation was thrown into an uproar.","“Wovenfire Cauldron, paramount fine rank treasure.” Lu Yun sat cross-legged in the center of the Lu Clan’s pill room and contemplated a small red cauldron in his hand. The affairs of the outside world didn’t concern him. “It falls a bit short compared to where I want it to be. It’ll be hard for me to refine it into a spirit treasure with my current strength.”","He frowned, then focused his mind. Probing the south with his bare hand, he grasped a ball of flames.","“Combine!” Lu Yun threw the ball of connate flames into the Wovenfire Cauldron and poured in other paramount rank ingredients that he’d already prepared off to the side.","“Grandfather hunted down the Aureate Seraph Bird to harvest its inner core for me and paid an incredible price...” An inner core the size of a fist appeared in his hand. “Today, this core will create a half-step spirit rank pill cauldron for my family!”","He threw the inner core into the cauldron as well.","Out of all possible treasures, offensive types were most commonly found. Defensive treasures were much fewer in number, and the rarest were pill cauldrons. Spirit rank pill cauldrons were extremely rare in fourth rank cultivation empires.","There was a mid fine rank cauldron in the palace, whereas the ones remaining in the nation were lower fine rank. There wasn’t even an upper fine rank. The Lings were hailed the greatest pill refinement family of Darklake because they possessed a paramount fine rank.","Whoosh!","A ball of red flames shot out of the Wovenfire Cauldron as soon as the inner core was added—it was the ball of connate flames that Lu Yun had melded into it. A bright red shadow that quite resembled a strange-looking bird circled over it.","Hand seals for treasure refinement streamed into the Wovenfire Cauldron. The circling shadow solidified until it was almost ready to take tangible form.","Humm!","Lu Yun’s heart and mind trembled as Hongmeng qi surged out of his body to combine with the cauldron.","Hongmeng qi was exceedingly pure energy that far exceeded the true origin of cultivators. It advanced further after Lu Yun set foot into the second turn of the Seeing Dao chapter. So long as he refrained from deploying arts from the heavenly dao, ordinary arts and methods were a walk in the park for him and didn’t consume anything.","Rays of Hongmeng qi flowed into the Wovenfire Cauldron, igniting the ball of connate flame inside.","Chirp!","The fiery shadow of a bird crooned loudly, causing the entire cauldron to shrink rapidly.","“Erm...” Lu Yun’s hands paused from forming more hand seals and he stared dumbly at the tiny cauldron that was now three inches tall. “It looks like... I underestimated the combination of Hongmeng qi and connate flames. Although I have the experience of a refinement grandmaster, I am not the me of reincarnation. The Aureate Seraph Bird contains the bloodline of the divine Three-Footed Aureate Bird. Being burned by connate flames and fed by my Hongmeng qi was sufficient to fully awaken that bloodline.”","The young man swallowed hard. The inner core of the Aureate Seraph Bird, connate flames, and Hongmeng true qi had jointly raised the Wovenfire Cauldron into a mid rank spirit treasure!","It’d gone from a paramount rank fine treasure to a mid rank spirit treasure!","It wildly exceeded his expectations. He’d thought it would be wonderful if he could turn the Wovenfire Cauldron into a half-step spirit treasure with the ingredients on hand. Lu Yun had forgotten about his own attributes as this was indeed the expected outcome if any other master refiner had attempted the same task. However, he possessed connate flames and Hongmeng qi!","“The experience from my reincarnations is valuable, but I must remember to look at it through the lens of my own abilities.” A smile floated onto Lu Yun’s face. He practiced the Nine Chapters of Dao—they were so much stronger than the cultivation methods he’d known before that they couldn’t be considered on the same playing field.","There were also his forgotten memories to consider.","Lu Yun looked at the tiny cauldron—it’d been three meters tall previously, but was now three inches in height. It also looked vastly different from before. There was a golden bird about to leap into flight etched in miniature on the cauldron. It possessed three feet—the image of the Three-Footed Aureate Bird.","“The Wovenfire Cauldron... needs a name change. From henceforth, your name is the Aureate Bird Cauldron.” Lu Yun beckoned the tiny cauldron into his hand. “Oh? It’s more than just a pill cauldron now, it can also attack with the Aureate Bird Truefire?”","His eyes brightened.","“Wonderful!” Lu Yun roared with laughter.","The inner core of the Aureate Seraph Bird had awakened its Three-Footed Aureate Bird bloodline after being refined by connate flames and Hongmeng true qi. It now possessed the Three-Footed Aureate Bird’s flame—Aureate Bird Truefire.","Although it was less than a connate flame, the Three-Footed Aureate Bird was a divine beast born of the sun. Its fire was also known as Sol Truefire!","......","Whoosh!","A gust of golden-red flames rose out of the Aureate Bird Cauldron as the shadow of a Three-Footed Aureate Bird circled over them.","“It is Sol Truefire!” Lu Yun breathed a long exhale and calmed himself.","Although Sol Truefire was far less than a connate flame, it was still exceedingly domineering. He was limited in the amount of connate fire he could summon—he couldn’t even use it in an attack.","The Aureate Bird Cauldron had become a spark for the Aureate Bird Truefire. The flames were endless so long as the spark was not extinguished, and they possessed high offensive capabilities.","Lu Yun had lacked a handy treasure ever since awakening. With his establishment of foundations, he could send his energy through treasures. This mid rank spirit treasure was the perfect tool for the occasion.","He was in no rush to walk out after the cauldron took shape. Rather, the young man sat down and carefully refined the small cauldron, gaining a deep understanding of its capabilities.","......","Three days passed.","On this day, an agitated Lu Xiaochi arrived early at Lu Yun’s yard. Flushed and in good health, immense energy ripples percolated through his body. He would be mistaken for a human-shaped paramount spirit crystal if he set foot out of the Lu residence in his current state. There was so much qi in him that it’d melded into every inch of his flesh and blood.","His meridians were fragile due to being afflicted by the Severed Meridians Hold. He couldn’t refine qi, but the qi in his body wasn’t damaging his meridians. Instead, they were absorbed into his being.","The tea leaves that Lu Yun had filched from his senior brother had been far from ordinary tea leaves.","“You’re here early, second uncle.” A yawning Lu Yun walked out of his house and took a look around. “Grandfather’s not at home, is he?”","Lu Xiaochi paused, then nodded. “Your grandfather made a trip out after fighting Yuwen Zonglin and Ouyang Baitian.”","Lu Tianling’s declaration of heading into closed door cultivation to recover from his injuries was just smoke and mirrors. Lu Yun had also thought he was in seclusion at first, but grew suspicious when he didn’t see his grandfather for a month.","“Uncle He, please have the defensive formation operate at full strength,” Lu Yun said to He Wuheng. The steward had followed the second master to the young master’s abode."]},{"number":2236,"title":"Chapter 2236: Chapter 2170.1: Connate Spirit Root","paragraphs":["Chapter 2170.1: Connate Spirit Root","He Wuheng had reached peak latter golden core; he was half step away from nascent soul. He nodded when he heard Lu Yun’s words and left to oversee the Major Cycle Nebula Formation.","Lu Yun and Lu Xiaochi headed for the secret vault. It was the quietest and most secure spot in the Lu residence. Lu Yun could not afford any interruptions if he was to break the Severed Meridians Hold on his uncle.","Whoosh!","The hovering Aureate Bird Cauldron slowly expanded with Lu Yun’s wave. It grew from a flaming red cauldron three inches tall to one that was three meters in height. As Lu Xiaochi watched on dazedly, his nephew threw various spirit herbs and ingredients into the cauldron, refining them into red medicinal liquid.","Thinking for a moment, Lu Yun retrieved another small tea leaf from his storage ring and carefully ripped off a piece that was half of a thumbnail. He likewise threw it into the pill cauldron.","The addition of the tea leaf turned the flaming red liquid in the color of jade green. Refreshing tea fragrance wafted out of it. When Lu Yun next beckoned, the piece of lower rank spirit crystal floated to his hand.","“Please enter the cauldron, second uncle.” He smiled calmly at Lu Xiaochi.","“Alright.” The man took off his clothes without a word and jumped into the Aureate Bird Cauldron.","“The process will be extremely painful, please bear with it.” Lu Yun flipped his hand and clapped the lid onto the cauldron before his second uncle could respond. Both of his hands fluttered in a hand seal and summoned a reddish-gold shadow of a Three-Footed Bird. It circled over the cauldron as Aureate Bird Truefire blazed to life.","“The Severed Meridians Hold... has no solution,” Lu Yun sighed softly.","The Severed Meridians Hold was regarded as the most evil restriction in the three realms and six great daos. Although there was supposed to be a solution somewhere, it only treated the symptoms and not the cause. Breaking it meant that the victim would never stand a chance of becoming an immortal. They would also be the weakest of any cultivation level they advanced to.","All meridians were ruined with the Severed Meridians Hold, so what Lu Yun sought to do was reforge the meridians!","Refine a person as a pill!","He would refine a living being as he would a pill!","One of his disciples in the three thousand lifetimes had also been afflicted with the Severed Meridians Hold. Being a pill refiner fanatic, Lu Yun had thrown his disciple into a cauldron and refined him. He’d used an unparalleled combat art to reforge all of that disciple’s meridians, thereby breaking the restriction.","However, it wasn’t a method available to just anyone. It required someone whose pill dao had reached wondrous, undefinable peaks, or the victim would die in refinement.","Not only did the process require stunning skill, but it necessitated crazed fervor. No normal person would throw a beloved disciple into a pill cauldron, but Lu Yun had been a madman in that lifetime.","Aureate Bird Truefire jumped and flickered while Lu Xiaochi clenched his teeth in the cauldron. He bled through his lips, but didn’t make a sound. Breaking the meridians to reforge them anew was pain worse than being drawn and quartered or flayed alive.","Lu Yun’s hands flicked through hand seals, making the cauldron shake. Suddenly, he paused and probed in the cardinal directions. The connate powers of earth, air, wood, metal, and fire gathered together and surged into the pill cauldron.","“In that world, I used the inner core of a divine beast that took snake form to reforge my disciple’s spirit root. That gave him the talents of the divine beast. This time, I will use the powers of the five elements to forge a spirit root of the five elements for my second uncle!”","Lu Yun set his jaw and formed a very strange hand seal. He then bit his tongue and spat out a mouthful of essence blood, melding it into the Aureate Bird Cauldron.","“Come out, leaf of the Builder Tree!” Keen light shone from his eyes as the shadow of a leaf flickered in and out of sight on him.","His current cultivation level was second turn of the Seeing Dao chapter. Thus, he was able to force the leaf from the Builder Tree out if he needed to.","Lu Yun quickly waved his hand when the leaf appeared and directed a large current of vitality from the leaf into the cauldron. Apart from using his own blood as a catalyst, he was unable to use the leaf’s power. Only then could he guide the leaf’s power into the cauldron for his second uncle to absorb.","Crack!","A tiny crack snaked through the lower rank spirit crystal that he cradled in his arms. Refining a person as a pill was such an enormous drain on resources that even Lu Yun couldn’t support the endeavor for too long with Hongmeng true qi. Thus, he had to use the lower rank crystal.","He didn’t dare use the Qi Accumulation Formation when they were in the secret vault. It would cause an enormous disturbance and easily expose the family vault secret.","The cauldron gradually settled down and the golden bird shadow in the air silently circled over it. The lower rank spirit crystal was no more—there weren’t even shards of it left. Lu Yun took out one hundred paramount rank spirit stones from his storage ring as his hands continued to form hand seals.","......","Seven days later, Lu Yun carefully let his fingers stop.","“It’s finally done.” There was no Hongmeng qi left in his dantian and his meridians were empty. A suffocating sense of emptiness rose in his heart.","Humm!","Blue light flared brilliantly from the Seal of the Multitude in his dantian. The goodwill stored within flooded out, transmuting into Hongmeng qi.","“What a pity that I didn’t have the attention to spare for the seal when I was breaking the Severed Meridians Hold. I would’ve been able to save the lower rank crystal and all these paramount rank stones.”","The seal contained enormous goodwill, but Lu Yun had to actively communicate with it to touch the energy. There was also a transmutation process—all things that Lu Yun hadn’t dared split his concentration for when he was dissolving the restriction. He’d been completely focused on the task at hand.","If the slightest hint of anything had gone wrong, Lu Xiaochi would’ve either turned into a pill or been decimated to ashes.","After recovering his Hongmeng true qi, Lu Yun probed to the south and grabbed a handful of connate flames. He casually tossed it into the cauldron to replace the Aureate Bird Truefire. Once the flames burned down, that would be when his second uncle emerged from the cauldron.","Mission accomplished, the young man sat down to make the best use of time. The methods of the second turn operated slowly and he grabbed a handful of connate fire origin from time to time, refining it as he cultivated.","Another seven days passed before the connate flames inside the cauldron fully dwindled away. The Aureate Bird Cauldron ceased to operate and its lid shot upward, giving way for a naked Lu Xiaochi.","He jumped out of the cauldron with gleaming, flawless skin. He’d looked to be in his thirties to begin with and was exceedingly handsome. Now he looked younger than thirty and shone with a heroic air.","“Tsk tsk, second uncle, your manhood is a sight to behold. When are you going to give me a second aunt, eh?” Lu Yun waggled his eyebrows suggestively.","“Shut up, brat,” Lu Xiaochi cursed teasingly and grabbed a set of long white robes next to him. “Many thanks to you this time.”","He took careful stock of himself. Although his internal force was as empty as ever and he completely lacked cultivation, the frail feeling that’d plagued him before was gone. It was replaced by a vibrant vitality.","This was a sign that his Severed Meridians Hold was no more.","“What’s a little thing between family?” Lu Yun smiled. He was at ease once there was no goodwill coming from Lu Xiaochi. Anything that family did for each other was only to be expected. If gratitude resulted from any actions... that would mean there was still a certain distance between the two.","“Second uncle,” Lu Yun turned serious. “I modified your spirit root as I broke the restriction, changing your fire spirit root into one of the connate five elements.”","“A spirit root of the connate five elements?” Lu Xiaochi blinked. He’d never heard of it before, but being named connate must mean that it was extraordinary. Spirit roots were the foundation of a cultivator and the determinant of their future accomplishment. He’d once possessed a paramount rank fire spirit root, so his cultivation speed was far faster than others.","“My master says that spirit roots are divided into five ranks,” Lu Yun explained matter-of-factly. “Ordinary roots of the five elements, paramount rank of the five elements, immortal spirit root, connate spirit root, and chaos spirit root. I used some special methods to change yours of the paramount fire root to the fourth highest—one that encompasses all five elements.”","“Ah...” Lu Xiaochi stared at Lu Yun like he was seeing a ghost.","He knew the divisions of the spirit roots, but only knew about the ordinary, paramount, and immortal spirit roots. He didn’t know anything that came after.","Cultivators absorbed their respective element to strengthen their spirit root when they reached foundation establishment, but strengthening was all they could do. Enhancing the rank of a spirit root was unheard of!"]},{"number":2237,"title":"Chapter 2237: Chapter 2170.2: Connate Spirit Root","paragraphs":["Chapter 2170.2: Connate Spirit Root","“Don’t get agitated, second uncle. As strong as the potential of connate spirit roots are, they require significant personal effort too,” Lu Yun smiled faintly. “Here, this is the Major Five Elements Demolition Godslayer Record. It’s an impressive method even in the world of immortals. If you’re interested in becoming a sword immortal, second uncle, you can try practicing this method.”","Although the Severed Meridians Hold had been broken, Lu Xiaochi had still lost all of his cultivation. He was an ordinary person with the ponderous consciousness of a nascent soul cultivator. Everything had to be started anew.","“The cultivation methods from the world of immortals!” Lu Xiaochi shook. His nephew had given him so many surprises that, despite being mentally prepared, he was still shocked.","“Is your master an immortal of the world of immortals instead of the world of cultivation?” he asked in a trembling voice.","“The world of immortals...” Lu Yun frowned. The Major Five Elements Demolition Godslayer Record was a method that he’d obtained in his first reincarnation. He’d found it in a secret locale in the world of immortals and rose to the top of the world with it.","But in his remaining reincarnations, he never took the ascent protocol to the world of immortals, despite becoming an immortal many times. He didn’t even know where it was.","The world of immortals seemed to have become a legend in stories shared between cultivators.","The Mindful Immortal Potentate was a heavyweight in the world of immortals. His inheritance appearing in the Jade Ruins World of Immortal Cultivation is a sign that many things have gone wrong. Or have the gates to the world of immortals closed for some reason?","His mind flew rapidly through various possibilities as he’d dwelled in the world of immortals when it was at its most prosperous. Innumerable cultivators took the ascent protocol to the world. However, each of his reincarnations resulted in the memories of an individual personality that weren’t connected to each other. Hence, he didn’t have much to draw off of.","Had the disaster of his subconscious already begun?","Forget it, I’m putting all of this out of my mind for now. I’m just small fry at foundation establishment, what do the problems of the world of immortals have to do with me? Lu Yun shook his head with a smile.","Lu Xiaochi rubbed his nose—he’d asked one question. Why had that caused Lu Yun to frown in thought, then mumble to himself? He was growing ever more mystified by his nephew.","“I don’t know the particulars about my master either. He sent my senior brother with a lot of things and had me take care of them myself,” Lu Yun quickly responded when he saw that his uncle had more questions. “Second uncle, although your restriction’s been broken, your spirit root is not very stable yet. There’s still plenty of medicine left in the Aureate Bird Cauldron. You should make good use of it and consolidate your spirit root. I’m heading out now.” Lu Yun turned and left.","......","Being an energetic person, staying inside a small room for seven days had nearly suffocated Lu Yun.","Rumble!!","He’d just exited the secret vault when a terrifying explosion went off outside the Major Cycle Nebula Formation. The formation shook like a leaf.","“Lu Xuan!” Lu Yun frowned and summoned his guard to him. “What’s going on?”","“It’s the Nineheavens Pagoda.” Rather wounded, Lu Xuan was unnaturally pale. “They came three days ago and started attacking the formation. All guards that are golden core and above have entered the formation to support it.” Pausing, he added, “Senior Blood has not gone.”","In the entire residence, only Lu Yun could command Bloodbath. The old man wouldn’t make a move even if the complex was breached and everyone slaughtered. Lu Xuan had suffered his injuries through the course of supporting the formation.","“Recover from your wounds first.” Lu Yun flicked a pill into Lu Xuan’s hands. “Uncle He, open the formation!”","Standing in the center of the Major Cycle Nebula Formation, He Wuheng started when he heard the young master’s voice. Thinking of Yuwen Zonglin and Ouyang Baitian’s ending, he quickly let the formation go.","Those outside stopped attacking when they saw the formation grind to a halt.","BOOM!","The Lu residence doors exploded in a shower of shards.","“Hahahahaha!! How dare a puny Lu Clan stand in this young master’s way? You seek death!” came an uncommonly cocky voice from the door. A handsome young man roughly the same age as Lu Yun walked through the broken doors. Clad in turquoise robes, he was followed by two dozen cultivators.","The weakest of the two dozen was nascent soul and the strongest was soul projection.","“Lu Yun, get your ass out here! We’re going to fight in single combat!” he bawled as soon as he entered.","“I wondered who it was, so it’s Sir Cloudexit. It’s been three years since we last saw each other, has all been well?” Lu Yun immediately recognized the young man.","Sir Cloudexit, young lord of the Nineheavens Pagoda, had visited Darklake three years ago. He’d bumped into Lu Yun and the two started fighting when the verbal exchange turned ugly. Although he was from the foremost sect of a fourth rank empire, Cloudexit himself was an utter bumpkin and less than Lu Yun of the time.","He suffered an enormous beating at Lu Yun’s hands, resulting in representatives from the Nineheavens Pagoda visiting a few days later and crippling Lu Xiaochi right in front of Lu Tianling.","This time, other cultivation empires had come after hearing news of a dao weapon appearing in Darklake. As the superior nation to its vassal, Dark Orchid would certainly send someone.","Sir Cloudexit had nursed a grudge ever since he’d suffered a beating three years ago. Revenge was constantly on his mind, so he would fully seize this chance now that it’d come by!","“Hahaha, just in time, Lu Yun! I’ve already taken care of the trash that is Zhao Chenguang and Yu Shuai. You’re the only one left!” Cloudexit roared with laughter when he saw Lu Yun and took a step forward, slamming his palm at Lu Yun’s chest.","“You’ve gone from third level qi refinement to golden core in three years. Looks like you’ve been diligently cultivating these years!” Lu Yun swiftly retreated when the other advanced.","Humm!","Cloudexit brayed with amusement to see Lu Yun back away and manifested a longsword in his hand. It exploded with radiance that reached nine meters long and crashed down on Lu Yun’s head.","Lu Yun frowned and quickly moved his feet, his body twisting and turning agilely to easily dodge the domineering sword light.","“Sir Cloudexit’s cultivation is run-of-the-mill as his golden core level is just the result of pills and medicines. The longsword in his hand, however, is a lower spirit rank weapon!","“Niiiice, it’s mine!” Lu Yun beamed. He typically wouldn’t want something like this, but he didn’t have anything like it at the moment.","“Hahaha, you didn’t think that I would coalesce my golden core after only three years, did you now? You’re just a foundation establishment, let’s see how you’ll fight me!” Sir Cloudexit strutted proudly to see his old enemy on the receiving end of what he’d once suffered.","Meanwhile, those of the Nineheavens Pagoda suppressed eye rolls. What was there to be proud of when a golden core cultivator equipped with a lower spirit rank weapon beat a foundation establishment cultivator?","All this talk of fighting and enmity? Everyone knew that Lu Yun was unworthy to be Sir Cloudexit’s enemy!","It was the young lord of the greatest sect in a fourth rank empire on one side and the noble scion of a third rank empire on the other. The difference in their status was stark. It was as if the young lord of a rich merchant family had charged into the marketplace to match a successful vendor in a contest of wealth.","“Heh heh heh, if I could beat you as a dead dog three years ago, I will still beat you as a dead dog three years later!” Lu Yun cackled as he rapidly retreated.","“Shut up, you little piece of shit!” Cloudexit flew into a rage.","“Hmph, am I supposed to fight you just because you want me to fight? Your Nineheavens Pagoda bullied us through superior force three years ago and crippled my second uncle. He’s a cripple even now, so who knows what you guys will do this time if I fight you again?!” Lu Yun complained loudly, the very picture of being cautious of the sect, but not thinking much of Cloudexit.","“It’s not up to you if we fight or not!” Cloudexit was a renowned prodigal of Dark Orchid. Tyrannical, egotistical, ludicrous, and lascivious. Lu Yun’s retort instantly stoked his temper.","“Then this young master will sit here and let you beat me! You have the strength in numbers, so it’s a dishonorable victory no matter what!” Lu Yun curled his lip and plopped on the ground, ready to let his opponent beat him however he wished.","That made Cloudexit pause. He wanted to grind Lu Yun’s face into the ground with his cultivation, but it meant nothing if the other didn’t resist at all.","“You over there, this is between me and Lu Yun! Don’t interfere!” Cloudexit suddenly turned around and roared as his entourage."]},{"number":2238,"title":"Chapter 2238: Chapter 2170.3: Connate Spirit Root","paragraphs":["Chapter 2170.3: Connate Spirit Root","“You’re golden core, young lord. You can do whatever you want to a foundation establishment cultivator from a lower empire. What do we need to interfere for?” the soul projection powerhouse smiled fawningly.","Cloudexit nodded with satisfaction. “Lu Yun, you heard him too. My people will not interfere in our matter!”","“What, is your word final?” Lu Yun cocked his head in a flippant way. “My family cannot afford to suffer vengeance from the Nineheavens Pagoda after the fact. Please, my uncle is still crippled after we exchanged two moves three years ago!”","“Right then, listen up, all of you! This is a matter between Lu Yun and I. It does not involve the Nineheavens Pagoda. I will show no mercy to anyone who dares repeat previous actions!” Cloudexit felt that Lu Yun made a lot of sense and hollered at his men.","“Do not worry, young lord! We will not interfere!” shouted the soul projection cultivator with an expansive air of being responsible for everything.","Please, all of Lu Yun’s actions and behavior had been within their grasp since he was a child. Who didn’t know how ridiculous and useless he was? Even though he was foundation establishment now, he was absolutely no match for a golden core cultivator. Foundation establishment cultivators of his age could be found in large handfuls on the street in Dark Orchid Empire!","“Very good, I hope all of you will refrain from eating the shit that you’ve just pushed out of your asses.” Lu Yun stood up and dusted himself off. “C’mon, let’s go outside. Don’t break my house.”","Ignoring the group, he sauntered out to the streets.","Cloudexit was enormously proud that Lu Yun had agreed to his terms, whereas his entourage looked on with stiff expressions. Refrain from eating the shit that they’d pushed out of their asses? Did the Lu young master have to speak in such a manner?","Lu Tianling’s house being under attack raised attention from all of the cultivators in the capital, but all manner of people were also in the city these days. Cultivators from fourth, fifth, and even sixth rank empires could be found in the capital.","A dao weapon was too relevant—only the imperial families of sixth rank empires might possess one. Other clans and sects would never own one if they didn’t encounter fortuitous occurrences. Hence, none of them could sit idly by if there was a possibility that a dao weapon had appeared in a mere third rank empire.","There was no one on the streets, but countless minds swept the area. A fight between two prodigals wasn’t worth watching, but some wanted to see how Lu Tianling, the strongest in Dark City, would react.","Of course, those from the fourth, fifth, and sixth rank empires didn’t care, but those from other third rank or elsewhere in the empire had to show some respect for Lu Tianling.","“Hahaha, Lu Yun, this time I’ll beat you like the dog you are!” Standing in the middle of the street, Cloudexit brandished his longsword and leered provocatively at the Lu young master. Suddenly, he went slack jawed. Abruptly ignoring Lu Yun, he shifted to stare fixedly in a certain direction.","“What a stunning jade beauty! No, that’s insufficient to describe her. Is she a fairy from the heavens?” he murmured with a hard swallow.","A woman in white had appeared by the Lu residence doors at some point. Slender, yet curvaceous, she emanated a breathtaking aura despite her face being covered by a veil. The woman was fatally alluring to a hotblooded young man like Cloudexit.","She was Fengxian Wu.","“Ahem!” Lu Yun coughed loudly. “Sir Cloudexit, are we fighting or not?”","“Fight? Yeah!” Cloudexist snapped back to his senses, but he was very distracted and his eyes kept drifting to the doors.","“Die, Lu Yun!” He pointed with his sword and sent out light nine meters long. However, everyone could tell that this blow was far lacking compared to before. His mind wasn’t in the fight at all.","Lu Yun chuckled and evaded the sword light. He took out a stack of talismans from his robes and threw them in the air.","Rumble!!","Rocks, blades of wind, lightning, spears of ice, blades of metal, wood, and nearly one hundred types of low level techniques smashed into Cloudexit. He swiftly gave the fight his full attention again and hastily operated true origin, wanting to defend against them.","But it was too late. While the techniques were only the level of initial foundation establishment, they filled the sky and were everywhere. A buffoon like Cloudexit couldn’t possibly handle them all.","Bam!","They smashed into Cloudexit and elicited a pale-yellow dome of light around him. The light persisted for a few seconds before it shattered.","Charred and smoking, Cloudexit flew backward with a loud wail.","Those from the Nineheavens Pagoda were extremely frustrated. They could tell that these talismans wouldn’t break the young lord’s defensive treasure in ordinary times. However, Cloudexit had been so distracted moments ago that he’d forgotten to activate his treasure. It’d raised automated defenses on its own.","“So he has a spirit rank defensive treasure on him!” Lu Yun walked up to Cloudexit and grabbed the other’s longsword. “Hahaha, this sword bears a Lu surname now!” He roared with laughter.","“Lu Yun, you court death!” the soul projection cultivator shouted. He jumped into the air and brought his palm down on Lu Yun.","The Lu young master jerked with surprise and brought the longsword up in front of him.","Wham!","He spewed a mouthful of blood and flew out like a kite on a broken string.","“Are you alright, young lord?” The soul projection cultivator arrived in front of Cloudexit and helped him up, shoving a variety of pills and medicines into the young man’s mouth like they didn’t cost anything.","“How dare you ambush me, Lu Yun!” Cloudexit howled after he took the pills and recovered slightly from his injuries.","“Hahahaha!!” Lu Yun stood up shakily and shoved He Wuheng aside. The steward had run out to help him up. “So the Nineheavens Pagoda does like to eat shit that you’ve pushed out of your asses!”","“You!” The disciples’ faces burned hotly; Cloudexit was almost spitting fire from his eyes. The impudent brat was weaker than him, but Lu Yun had beaten him into such a bedraggled state. Honor? That didn’t exist among good-for-nothings.","“Ambush?” Lu Yun wiped off the blood at the corners of his mouth. “You wield a spirit rank flying sword and possess a spirit rank defensive treasure. I’m just foundation establishment, how can I ambush you?”","“Shut up!” Cloudexit shoved aside the soul projection cultivator and pointed at Fengxian Wu. “Miss, you’re part of the Lu Clan, aren’t you? You will follow me back to the Nineheavens Pagoda if you don’t want the complex to be razed to the ground and everyone in the family die. Well?”","Busy watching the show, Fengxian Wu blinked and cast a startled glance at Cloudexit. So this young lord had designs on her? This was most unexpected!","Ever since awakening and obtaining a method to break the Severed Meridians Hold, Lu Yun had treated Fengxian Wu politely. He placed no limits on her whatsoever.","The method she’d handed over was supposed to break the restriction, but no one knew if it could really do the deed. All Lu Yun needed was a reason for the change in his family. Otherwise, he’d never be able to explain why his uncle was no longer crippled.","The more Fengxian Wu grew accustomed to the Lu residence, the more her dislike abated. Her wounds had mostly healed after a month’s recovery.","“The Nineheavens Pagoda?” Although her tone was chilly, it was still as melodious as a mountain creek. Cloudexit found his very bones relaxing.","“Why should I go to Nineheavens Pagoda?” Fengxian Wu looked unblinkingly at Cloudexit.","The young lord completely forgot about the situation he’d been in moments ago when he saw a beauty paying attention to him. He flipped his hair dashingly and whoosh! sent his long, charred hair drifting to the ground in pieces.","“Pfft!” Fengxian Wu couldn’t but help laugh when she saw this.","Cloudexit’s dark face turned even darker. He knew what had happened, but wasn’t at liberty to erupt in fury in front of a beauty.","“The Nineheavens Pagoda is the greatest sect in the Dark Orchid Empire. My father is a soul projection powerhouse and I am its future leader. If you go back with me, you would be the sect’s future mistress. It’s a life a thousand times better than being in a minor Lu Clan!” Cloudexit said proudly as he stroked his bald head."]},{"number":2239,"title":"Chapter 2239: Chapter 2170.4: Connate Spirit Root","paragraphs":["Chapter 2170.4: Connate Spirit Root","“Future mistress?” The smile slipped off Fengxian Wu’s face. “You can’t even beat Lu Yun. It looks like there’s not much to the future sect leader of the Nineheavens Pagoda.”","She snorted and looked at Lu Yun again. He’d already put the flying sword into his storage ring. The Nineheavens Pagoda? He truly wasn’t concerned about them.","“Sir Cloudexit, I admit that I won through a fluke just now. It was because you were distracted,” he said cheekily. “If we were fighting in earnest, I would be no match for you.”","That slightly mollified Cloudexit, whereas the cultivators behind the young lord looked on darkly. However, they didn’t dare say anything. Everything the Lu young master said happened to land precisely on what the young lord cared about. Whoever dared interject now would face their young lord’s wrath.","Forget it, we’re just here to ensure that the young lord is safe. He can do whatever he’d like as long as he’s not in imminent danger.","The soul projection expert exchanged glances with the people behind him. Sir Cloudexit was the sect leader’s only son and his doting on the young lord knew no bounds. There was once a latter nascent soul disciple who refused to obey the young lord. For that, the sect leader crippled him and threw him in the dungeons.","Everyone in the entourage was of important standing, but they were here only as the young lord’s guard. Of course, they weren’t the only ones from the sect in the city since a dao weapon was at stake.","“But, although this young lady lives at my residence, she is not part of the Lu Clan. She has nothing to do with my family.” Lu Yun was unable to conceal the apprehension within his tone despite attempting to appear calm.","A self-sure smile immediately spread across Cloudexit’s face.","“Heh heh, miss, you heard that. Now go back with me.” He walked up and reached for Fengxian Wu’s hand.","Off to the side, He Wuheng closed his eyes. This Cloudexit was about to be struck with incredible misfortune. The cocky young lord of the greatest sect in a fourth rank empire had just provoked someone he really should’ve left alone.","A frosty demeanor crept over Fengxian Wu’s face.","“Lu Yun, I’ll make you pay for this later.”","Smack!","She raised her hand before she spoke and drew an agonized yelp from Cloudexit, sending him flying. His left cheek was immensely swollen and he spat out all of his teeth as he tumbled.","“How dare you?!” gasped some cultivators by the young lord’s side. Who would’ve imagined that a woman in the Lu residence would dare harm the young lord?!","They hadn’t taken action earlier because they’d backed themselves into a corner. If they acted against Lu Yun, that would be eating their own waste matter.","Whoosh!","An initial nascent soul cultivator snorted coldly and dashed to Fengxian Wu. He grabbed for her neck.","Smack!","The nascent soul cultivator also went flying with a crisp slap. He ended up in similar straits as Cloudexit—teeth spewing from a bloody mouth and half of his face caved in.","Dead silence reigned. Everyone looked at the beautiful fairy like they’d seen a ghost. An initial golden core cultivator had sent an initial nascent soul cultivator flying! This was beyond flabbergasting in a low rank empire!","In the meantime, a trembling Cloudexit came back to his senses. Fengxian Wu had clearly shown him mercy or he’d be missing his entire head if she’d used full force.","The woman wore an aloof expression behind her face veil. She glanced at Lu Yun, but didn’t say anything.","He Wuheng swallowed hard. He’d l knew that Miss Feng was very strong, but who would’ve thought that she’d be this strong? She’d sent a nascent soul cultivator flying with her cultivation of initial golden core!","Nascent soul was unbeatable in a third rank nation.","“You didn’t let me down,” Lu Yun quirked his lips upward. “Saving you with a Violet Orchid Ganoderma Pill was well worth it.”","“Take her!” snarled the soul projection cultivator. He sent the other nascent soul cultivators forward with a wave of his hand.","“You seek death!” Fengxian Wu sneered and moved lightly, dancing around like a lithe flame.","Smack smack smack!","Each of the seven cultivators, including two latter nascent soul cultivators, suffered a slap to the face and was thrown backward. Fengxian Wu returned to where she stood before, as if she hadn’t taken a step away.","“How dare a paltry Nineheavens Pagoda throw its weight around in front of me. I can exterminate you for this offense!” She lifted her chin upward while she spoke calmly, like she was describing an ordinary occurrence. Exterminating the Nineheavens Pagoda seemed as commonplace as eating and drinking to her—not something worth taking note of.","Fear dawned in Cloudexit’s eyes and his guards sucked in sharp breaths. They’d truly provoked someone they couldn’t afford to, someone they should’ve avoided at all costs.","“Exterminate my Nineheavens Pagoda? This young lady speaks bold words!” sounded another voice as sword light flashed through the air. A bulky man arrived on the scene; he brimmed with unbounded aura that pounced viciously on Fengxian Wu.","“Second senior brother!” Cloudexit called out when he saw the man.","“What a disgrace,” snorted his senior brother in complete lack of consideration. Cloudexit ducked his head, resentment flashing through his eyes.","This second senior brother was initial soul projection, but the aura he exuded far outstripped that of the soul projection cultivator next to Cloudexit.","“Young lady, no matter who you are, Darklake is Dark Orchid property because it is a vassal nation. It is untoward that you show no face to the Nineheavens Pagoda.” The senior brother turned around and stared straight at Fengxian Wu.","“A mere Nineheavens Pagoda is nothing to me,” she snorted.","“Hahahahahaha!!” the second senior brother roared with laughter. “You may have an impressive background, but you’re just a grounded phoenix at the moment. Will anyone know if I capture or kill you?”","His aura suddenly expanded balefully. “If my guess is right, not even the Lus know your true identity. You will die in ignominy if you die here.”","A shrewd light glinted in his eyes. “You have insulted my Nineheavens Pagoda and the Lu Clan are accomplices. Men, kill everyone from the Lus, including this woman!”","Humm!","Sword light shimmered in the air as a dense net of energy came down from above, encircling the entire Lu residence.","“The Nineheavens Pagoda and others laid their plans long ago. Cloudexit was just a pawn.” Lu Yun immediately detected that the sect was fully prepared to eliminate his family. The Darklake emperor was likely distracted by other matters at the moment and had no attention to spare for the Lus.","Rumble!!","The Major Cycle Nebula Formation activated in the air and enveloped the residence in a layer of scintillating starlight.","“Kill!” The sect had been stymied by this formation when they attacked three years ago and the Darklake emperor had further appeared to smooth over matters. The same would not happen again today.","Lu Yun took Fengxian Wu and He Wuheng back into the complex. As domineering as the sword light was outside, they could not break the formation.","“So it is the Major Cycle Nebula Formation.” Emotion flickered over Fengxian Wu’s face as she looked up at the formation as brilliant as the night sky. “Lu Yun, I never would’ve thought that a small family like yours would possess this formation.”","Lu Yun blinked. “Is it famous?”","“Not here,” Fengxian Wu shook her head. “But it surpasses the ancients and amazes the contemporaries where I am from.”","“Where you are from?” Lu Yun brightened, subconsciously thinking of his grandfather and wondering if they were from the same place.","She refused to speak more on that matter. “If my guess is right, you used my presence to divert some of the attention from the Lus. You’re going to make me the cause of all the recent changes in the family, aren’t you?”","“Oh?” Lu Yun sized up Fengxian Wu and stopped on her chest. “They say that big breasts compensate for small brains, but Miss Feng has both breasts and brains.”","Fengxian Wu was very uncomfortable with how Lu Yun was looking at her. “I recommend you to not try the same tactics on me, they won’t work.”","“Is that so?” He smiled, but retracted his gaze. Now wasn’t the time to tease the young lady.","The Nineheavens Pagoda had assembled three soul projection and dozens of nascent soul cultivators in a massive sword formation that attacked the complex. The Major Cycle Nebula Formation trembled successively, ripples undulating through its surface.","“Why are you so calm? Are you not afraid they’ll break the formation?” Fengxian Wu suddenly asked.","“Why should I be afraid when you’re not afraid?” Lu Yun shrugged. “You said so yourself that this formation surpasses the ancients and amazes the contemporaries. It would fail to live up to its reputation if a few soul projection small fry could break it.”"]},{"number":2240,"title":"Chapter 2240: Chapter 2171.1: Law Enforcer","paragraphs":["Chapter 2171.1: Law Enforcer","“Soul projection small fry?” Fengxian Wu blinked. “If I’m seeing things correctly, you’re foundation establishment yourself, aren’t you?”","“That’s right, I’ve established my foundations!” Lu Yun chortled. “I don’t need to be a virgin anymore, so you...”","Although he leered like a pervert, he didn’t nurse the slightest desire in his heart. Two people had lived in it all this time and filled it to the brim.","Fengxian Wu flushed bright red.","RUMBLE!","The formation groaned as individual clusters within extinguished one after another. An enormous opening punched through the Major Cycle Nebula Formation. Within the Lu residence, the golden core cultivators overseeing the formation spat out mouthfuls of blood and fell to the ground.","“What?!” Lu Yun’s brows creased.","A man dressed in black combat armor stood proudly in the air. He wielded a longsword and looked imperiously over the complex. Not only had the Major Cycle Nebula Formation been pierced through, but so had the sword formation set by the Nineheavens Pagoda.","“An awakened cultivator!” The second senior brother reeled with shock. “How is there an awakened cultivator here??”","Awakened cultivators were peak existences among cultivators. They’d passed their tribulations and could ascend to immortality in a cloud of radiance. What was an awakened cultivator doing in a mere third rank empire??","“A law enforcer for the Jade Ruins Realm?” Fengxian Wu looked at the armored man with interest.","“Who is the lord of the Lu Clan?” The man spoke gruffly with a manner of eternal ice that would never melt.","“This humble one is Lu Yun and greets the senior.” Lu Yun remained where he was as no one dared move given the aura draped over the area. He raised cupped fists inside a halted Major Cycle Nebula Formation.","“I am a law enforcer from the Xuanhuang Empire. I wish to know if the human demon Bloodbath in the Lu residence.” The armored man ignored the gesture.","“He is not.” Lu Yun connected the dots. A few days ago, the Ouyang Clan spread word that Bloodbath was in Silver City. This law enforcer had likely come to verify the rumors.","The dao weapon? Would an enforcer from one of the three ninth rank empires lack for dao weapons? His longsword and black armor were all upper dao rank treasures!","“Milord, the Lus cannot be trusted to answer. An investigation must be made!” Another voice rang out as soon as Lu Yun finished speaking. Ouyang Shengtian arrived in a streak of sword light.","“Hmph!” snorted the armored man as he swept out with an incomparable consciousness.","“Milord enforcer, we are entertaining an honorable guest. Milord will not be able to afford the consequences if you run afoul of this noble guest!”","The law enforcer frowned when a voice sounded in his ears.","“Milord most likely knows a little about Miss Fengxian, if she is offended...” Lu Yun continued.","“Fengxian...” The enforcer trembled and looked deeply at Fengxian Wu next to Lu Yun. He swiftly calmed down. “Bloodbath is not in the Lu residence. I take my leave.”","He vanished on the spot with a turn of his body.","Fengxian Wu glared at Lu Yun. She’d identified the newcomer in a moment of interest, but that gave an opportunity for the young man to use her again.","I suspected that Fengxian Wu was the young miss of some clan from a ninth rank empire, but it looks like I’ve underestimated her still. Lu Yun’s lips curved upward. What she’d called out was “a law enforcer for the Jade Ruins Realm”, not of the Xuanhuang Empire or a ninth rank empire.","Most important was his earlier observation of her fighting skill. It went without saying how precious her identity was if an initial golden core cultivator could easily trounce several nascent soul powerhouses.","But a law enforcer has come and the Ouyangs are using him as their weapon. It would be a fatal blow to both the family and nation if he really does discover the tie between Bloodbath and us.","It looks like the Ouyangs have gotten an inkling of the truth behind events of that day. Lu Yun’s thoughts flew rapidly.","Due to the law enforcer breaking the Major Cycle Nebula Formation, the three soul projection and dozens of nascent soul cultivators from the Nineheavens Pagoda streamed into the complex.","“Hahaha, Lu Yun, I’d like to see how you strut around now! And you, woman! How dare you hit me?! I’m going to drag you back and turn you into my sex slave! I’ll have you know what wishing for death feels like!” A cackling Cloudexit leered threateningly and looked Fengxian Wu up and down.","The young woman looked on solemnly while a phoenix shadow flickered behind her. Lu Yun didn’t care about the intruders.","“Sir Cloudexit, do you really intend to eat the shit that you’ve pushed out your ass?” Lu Yun smiled superciliously at his opponent.","“Shut up!” he roared back.","“Don’t bother arguing, just slaughter the entire clan down to the last chicken!” roared his second senior brother Xu Lang. The nascent soul cultivators erupted in unison and sent terrifying rays of sword light at Lu Yun.","Boom!","Another tremble shook the air and dispersed the cascade of sword light. A magnificent black figure descended from the sky.","“You know that this seat is here, yet persist in conducting affairs that anger the heavens and vex the people. Do you lack all respect for this seat?” The black armored enforcer had come back and coolly regarded Cloudexit, Xu Lang, and their people.","“Mi, milord...” Xu Lang stammered with shock. He hadn’t thought that the venerated enforcer would interfere in a low ranked cultivation empire! “Mi-milord, Darklake is a vassal of my Dark Orchid Empire. This is an internal affair, so I would request that milord not interfere.”","It was a perfect opportunity to get rid of the Lus! Once the clan was done and that person’s task was complete, the entire sect would receive untold benefits and even become a sect of a fifth rank empire!","Bam!","Xu Lang flew backward. He was devoid of life signs when he crashed to the ground.","“Get out,” the enforcer grunted.","The rest of the Nineheavens Pagoda cultivators scrambled for dear life. They ran off without even retrieving Xu Lang’s corpse.","Hiding in the shadows, Ouyang Shengtian quickly scuttled off when he saw that the wondrous personage he’d arranged for had somehow become a guardian for the Lu Clan and seemed to be in a strange mood.","“Our deepest thanks to milord enforcer for saving us!” Lu Yun bowed to the law enforcer.","Fengxian Wu retracted her phoenix shadow and looked noncommittally at the man. He’d taken action purely on account of her.","“Unmoving Phoenix... You are indeed a Fengxian...” The enforcer looked on with agitation.","“It’s enough to simply know of certain things, you don’t need to speak of them,” Fengxian Wu’s voice echoed in the man’s mind, calming his expression.","“Miss Fengxian, why have you come to the Jade Ruins Cultivation World? Do you wish for me to contact... so they can bring you back?” he transmitted back.","“No need, I have my reasons for being here. Do not reveal my presence to anyone.”","“Understood!” the enforcer responded solemnly.","The Fengxians were a stunning family that could destroy this entire world if they were angered. The Unmoving Phoenix that Fengxian Wu displayed was their ultimate art. Only someone of their bloodline could learn it.","While the black armored man was a law enforcer of the Jade Ruins Realm, he was also acquainted with the formidable clans outside the realm. Most important was that their world and the three ninth rank empires were just a tiny corner of the faction that the Fengxian Clan belonged to.","The world was vast—the Jade Ruins Realm and its associated faction were but a speck of dust.","Lu Yun knew that the enforcer was conversing with Fengxian Wu when he didn’t receive a response. His eyes moved rapidly in thought.","“Milord enforcer, please forgive this humble one for lying earlier,” he suddenly said.","“Eh?” Both Fengxian Wu and the enforcer started.","“Senior Bloodbath is indeed in the residence.”","The law enforcer was a bit bemused. He was primarily here to arrest Bloodbath, but things took on a different cast after he met a Fengxian young miss.","Was Bloodbath important anymore?","Not being a Jade Ruins inhabitant, Fengxian Wu raised a quizzical eyebrow when she heard the name Bloodbath.","“The one who used the pill to heal Miss Fengxian’s injuries was Senior Bloodbath,” Lu Yun solemnly explained.","Fengxian Wu had been gravely injured before. Although she’d suppressed her injuries with secret arts, making everything seem normal on the surface, she was so deeply hurt that her golden core had cracked.","It’d taken Lu Yun’s pill with the properties of the Violet Orchid Ganoderma and Bloodbath’s combination-level methods, as well as a tea leaf from Sky, to fully heal her. It was for this reason that she was willing to stay at the Lu residence and didn’t mind how Lu Yun had fully used her just now."]},{"number":2241,"title":"Chapter 2241: Chapter 2171.2: Law Enforcer","paragraphs":["Chapter 2171.2: Law Enforcer","One month ago, Fengxian Wu was wary of a Lu Xuan at initial golden core. One month later, she was able to defeat numerous golden core cultivators with a sweep of her arm. The contrast was stark.","“Miss Fengxian was once injured?” Terror appeared on the enforcer’s face. He knew full well how precious each member of the Fengxian bloodline was. If this young lady suffered an accident whilst in the Jade Ruins Realms, even Xuanhuang Empire would be her burial goods.","“It is of no matter. The Lu young master and Senior Bloodbath have healed my injuries. I have made a full recovery.”","The man breathed out more easily after hearing Fengxian Wu’s response. “Then it seems that Bloodbath’s merits are more than his faults. They negate his previous crimes. Upon my return, I will request that the chief enforcer pardon Bloodbath.”","“In that case, my gratitude to the venerated chief enforcer.” Lu Yun smiled with a glance at Fengxian Wu.","The black armored man also looked at Lu Yun with a much more gentle expression.","“It is best that as few know of my affairs as possible. Don’t send people to disturb me or reveal my movements. Your chief enforcer won’t be able to shoulder the consequences. You should go back now,” Fengxian Wu transmitted once more.","“Understood,” the man took a deep breath. “Then I trouble young master Lu to look after Miss Fengxian while she is here.”","He raised cupped fists to Lu Yun.","“Naturally, if I might know the senior’s name...?”","The man blinked, then smiled faintly. “Helian Shan.”","“Please be at ease, Senior Helian. No one will touch Miss Fengxian while she resides at the Lu residence. But the Nineheavens Pagoda...” Lu Yun paused meaningfully.","“I will take care of them, don’t worry.” Helian Shan stopped, then continued, “As Bloodbath is a combination level cultivator, his presence here violates the rules. He should stay in the shadows whenever he moves around.”","The enforcer had a good impression of Lu Yun and thus exchanged a few more words with the young man before leaving in a ray of sword light.","“Miss Fengxian’s identity is indeed extraordinary. Even an enforcer whose word is law in the world of cultivation bows and scrapes in front of you. He was worried about breathing too loudly!” Lu Yun said cheekily to Fengxian Wu after Helian Shan left.","A proud smile appeared reflexively on Fengxian Wu’s face, but she blinked in the next second. Was it worth boasting about that Lu Yun admired her?","“This young lady saved your life this time—it counts as returning your favor for helping me recover.” Fengxian Wu lifted her chin. “But you then struck a connection with Helian Shan through me, so you owe me one.”","Lu Yun nodded and replied solemnly, “Miss Fengxian speaks truly. The Lu Clan was saved this time purely thanks to Miss Fengxian. They say that words are too paltry when it comes to gratitude too great to be repaid. If Miss Fengxian needs help with anything in the future, I will do my utmost to fulfill your need so long as it is within the scope of my abilities.”","He spoke with an earnest look in his eyes—there was none of his usual craftiness or lewdness to be found. Fengxian Wu’s eyes widened when she saw his expression.","She’d gotten to know the young man better after spending a month together. Although he was an unmitigated good-for-nothing bastard, he was extremely principled when it came to certain things.","He always returned kindness tenfold, repaying a drop of dew with a lively spring.","As a wily old fox of three thousand lifetimes, Lu Yun knew that sometimes friendship was much more important than profit or gain. He was very pointed in his actions—Fengxian Wu would treat him as a friend and never think of him as anything more than that.","It wasn’t narcissistic for him to say that he needed to carefully maintain this boundary. He was too exemplary and easily attracted attention. However, he wasn’t interested in anyone. Lu Yun wanted to save himself for the two who were sealed away in his memories.","......","The appearance of a law enforcer daunted some of the unstable elements in Darklake Empire. Currents of trouble that’d been ready to overtake the capital settled down for a few days. Although representatives of the Nineheavens Pagoda were still present in Dark City, they were uncommonly law-abiding.","They said nothing when Lu Yun threw Xu Lang’s corpse into the streets—even when the second senior brother had been stripped naked.","The law enforcer had killed without another word on behalf of the Lu Clan. That was sufficient for everyone to understand that the current Lus were a faction not to be touched.","Lu Yun gained the most out of the incident. Thanks to Helian Shan’s appearance, the family remained as solid as Mount Tai in the furor raised by the dao weapon. More importantly, the three ninth rank empires withdrew their arrest notice for Bloodbath. It took only a few short days for the elder to no longer be a fugitive.","The news sent all of Jade Ruins Cultivation World into an uproar while the Ouyang Clan viewed it with quiet dread. Never had they fathomed that they’d make such a mess of things. The family was doomed if Bloodbath came looking for revenge!","However, another piece of gossip swiftly made the rounds—the powerhouse that’d wielded the dao weapon was a cultivator from Wing Empire, one of Darklake Empire’s two major vassals. His name was Yong Heyu.","Attention that’d been gathered on Darklake Empire immediately shifted to Wing Empire. As Yong Heyu’s previous master, Crown Prince Situ Jie was quickly identified and prodded to find Yong Heyu.","......","The Lu residence.","Patriarch Lu Tianling was absent and no one knew where he was, the second master was in closed door cultivation below ground, which left Lu Yun the only one in charge.","“You spread the news, didn’t you?” Bloodbath had reverted to his original appearance—long, dark red hair, blood-red eyes and white robes. He sprawled comfortably on the chair in front of Lu Yun.","The cancellation of his arrest warrant allowed him to relax greatly. He made enormous daily progress in the Canon of the Blood God after recovering from his injuries; he was almost nascent soul now. The goodwill emanating from him was so strong that he almost nursed a remarkable faith in Lu Yun.","The Ouyang Clan had taken advantage of him for numerous years, but everything changed after he met the young man. He’d lost his home a long time ago—the Lu residence was his home now.","“No,” Lu Yun shook his head. “It was just impossible to conceal Yong Heyu’s involvement. How are the twenty-nine getting along?”","“Their willpower is decent, but their potential is subpar. Their cultivation hasn’t grown much—a twenty percent increase in strength at most,” Bloodbath sighed.","“Twenty percent? That’s not bad.” Lu Yun nodded. He’d yet to resolve the Vermilion Bird affair because Situ Yun was distracted by the crown prince’s machination these days.","“I will have to continue to trouble the senior in matters to come,” the young man said. “Although these people come from the army and have experienced life and death, they are still yet to reach my standards.”","“What are you looking for?” Bloodbath frowned.","“Senior, please take these people to the Great Wilderness Mountain for further training,” Lu Yun said carefully.","“What?!” Bloodbath went slack jawed. The Great Wilderness Mountain was a zone of immense danger in the Jade Ruins Realm. There were countless spirit beasts and even monster spirits there.","“This is the Four Divisions of Heaven Formation, a combined force formation. I leave it in the senior’s hands.” Lu Yun handed a jade slip to the elder.","“The Four Divisions of Heaven Formation?” Bloodbath scanned it curiously. “Ah...”","He was stunned. Being a formation master himself, he easily saw how powerful this one was. It used the four symbols and twenty-eight mansions of the sky to summon the power of the stars from the four cardinal directions. Its might was unparalleled.","“As strong as this formation is, those people still need to practice it. How about this, I’ll teach it to them first and have them practice for a bit before heading to the mountain.” A strange smile curved Bloodbath’s lips.","Lu Yun blinked, then quickly understood that the elder wanted to make a move against the Ouyangs.","“However, this formation requires only twenty-eight. You’ve given me twenty-nine.” Bloodbath didn’t know what Lu Yun was planning.","“Yu Qianhua’s cultivation is the highest among the twenty-nine, I’m tapping him to be the commander of the Vermilion Guard. The other twenty-eight will be hidden guards concealed in the shadows. The Vermilion Guard will also fall to the senior.” Lu Yun smiled gently.","“You brat, you’ve got designs on me!” Bloodbath cursed with a chuckle. He understood what the young man intended.","Although they were out to train, it was also a recruiting drive. This was a trip to truly reassemble the Vermilion Bird—what Lu Yun meant by the Vermilion Guard. Given Bloodbath’s finesse, it was no problem for him to recruit some men. The senior also understood that by giving the Vermilion Guard to him, he was tied to the Lu Clan in the future.","To be honest, he hadn’t thought of any other possibility after Lu Yun took out the Canon of the Blood God. That wasn’t a method that belonged to the world of cultivation.","......","Bloodbath left with the men; Lu Yun didn’t care to inquire what his exact plans were.","“Are you not interested in the dao weapon?” Fengxian Wu grew much more lively after seeing Helian Shan. A small smile could often be found in her frosty expression.","“Dao weapon?” Lu Yun had obtained a lower spirit rank sword from Cloudexit. He’d just refined it, so he smiled with amusement at Fengxian Wu’s question.","“It’s one thing if we secretly stole it from him. If we blatantly take it by force, we’d just be creating trouble for ourselves.” He waved her off. “The aura of a dao weapon is too great. Everyone without five hundred kilometers would be aware whenever we used it. If we lack sufficient strength to retain it, it would only be inviting disaster to take it.”","etvolare's Thoughts","One thing I will say, I am very happy that the author has been recycling just enough of the old names that naming hasn't been a complete hassle. Then again I suppose coming up two entirely different worlds, cultivation systems, family backgrounds, treasures and methods over the span of 30 chapters was too much, even for him. = ="]},{"number":2242,"title":"Chapter 2242: Chapter 2171.3: Law Enforcer","paragraphs":["Chapter 2171.3: Law Enforcer","“Miss Feng, you’ve visited the capital for half a year now and have been in the Lu residence the entire time. You’ve yet to take a good look at Dusk City. Why don’t I show you around?” Lu Yun and Fengxian Wu were more like friends these days; the young lady lit up at his suggestion.","Although she came from a large faction that lived in a place a thousand times more prosperous than Dusk City, there was a different kind of joy to be found in the Darklake capital.","Lu Yun brought Fengxian Wu, Lan’er, and Lu Xuan out of the residence with him.","Lan’er and Fengxian Wu had befriended each other long ago. The two chattered happily as they strolled down the street, each holding two sticks of candied spirit fruits. They made for quite a pleasing sight.","“My dear young master Lu, you’ve finally come out! Your brothers have missed you terribly!” Two figures came into view—one tall, one short. The short one was beautiful, urbane, and debonair—his only disadvantage his height. The other one was nearly three meters tall with rippling muscles—just one of his arms was as thick as a regular person’s waist. His body was paired with a youthful looking face that appeared fourteen years old.","It was Zhao Chenguang and Yu Shuai.","“Eh? What happened to you, Brother Zhao? Oh right, I hear that someone beat you guys up?” Lu Yun couldn’t help but laugh when he saw the two.","Yu Shuai was well enough, but Zhao Chenguang’s face was mottled black and blue. He’d plainly suffered a thorough beating.","“Don’t mention it. When that so-called Sir Cloudexit couldn’t find you, he came for us because he heard we’re your friends. Our families didn’t dare offend the Nineheavens Pagoda and handed us over. Ai, it’s a long story!” Yu Shuai sighed mournfully.","“Cloudexit, again?” Fengxian Wu frowned slightly when she heard the name. Plainly, she had a very bad impression of the man. Zhao Chenguang and Yu Shuai shrank in on themselves.","“Miss Feng Wu, you must take a stand for us brothers! That Sir Cloudexit is an animal!” Zhao Chenguang sniffled.","Zhao Chenguang and Yu Shuai often called upon the Lu residence over the past month and were well acquainted with “Miss Feng Wu”. They didn’t have any designs on her because they thought she was Lu Yun’s woman. When stories spread of a stunning beauty worth nations easily beating seven nascent soul powerhouses, as well as the cocksure Sir Cloudexit, they immediately thought of Feng Wu.","“Has he not left the capital yet?” Fengxian Wu asked warningly. She’d nursed a grudge ever since he said he wanted to make her a sex slave.","No one bore a grudge like a woman.","“Sir Cloudexit is in the Beast Colosseum!” Yu Shuai quickly said.","“He seems to be enjoying life, what’s he doing there?” Lu Yun chuckled.","“You’d think he’s there to watch beasts fight. But no, he’s there to make people fight!” Zhao Chenguang spat out.","“Make people fight?” Lu Yun’s group paused, startled.","“Cloudexit’s captured a few qi refinement cultivators from the northern district and tied them together with metal chains. He’s gambling large sums at the Beast Colosseum, saying that whoever’s beast pet can beat his human pets wins ten paramount rank spirit stones!” Yu Shuai explained.","“What?!” Lu Yun’s anger flared. Although he was a good-for-nothing and spent his days being a pestilence upon others, he would never do something so out of line. Treating humans as pets? Forcing them to fight other beasts? That was a depraved loss of humanity!","“And? Are there people betting with him?” Fengxian Wu’s face darkened.","“Yes.” Yu Shuai’s chest heaved. “Not cultivators of Darklake, however. All foreigners. Chenguang spoke up against it and got completely beaten up.”","“Let’s go to the Beast Colosseum!” Fengxian Wu possessed a high sense of justice and couldn’t sit still after hearing of the ludicrous situation.","Meanwhile, Lu Yun sank into deep thought.","“Lu Xuan, take Lan’er home. Miss Feng and I will go to the Beast Colosseum,” Lu Yun said to his guard.","“Young master...” Lan’er was reluctant.","“Go home, things aren’t as simple as they seem. Lu Xuan, protect Lan’er well.”","“Yes, young master.” Lu Yun’s wish was Lu Xuan’s command and he hurried back to the residence with the maid.","“Things aren’t as simple?” Fengxian Wu blinked when she heard Lu Yun.","“Given my temper, I would definitely show myself after Chenguang suffered a beating. Heh heh heh, nice move, Cloudexit. I’d like to see what you’re up to.”","The Lu Yun of four months ago wouldn’t think much of treating qi refinement cultivators as human pets. He’d even find it novel and only pay attention to Zhao Chenguang being beaten.","“Yu Shuai, who’s there other than Sir Cloudexit?” Lu Yun asked.","“A few other noble sons, probably from Dark Orchid Empire. Their background is on par with that Cloudexit.” Yu Shuai paid much more attention to detail compared to Zhao Chenguang. Although the latter possessed a youthful face, he was ruled by the muscles on his body.","“Is there anyone from Darklake Empire with them?” Lu Yun pressed.","“Ouyang Shengtian!” Zhao Chenguang quickly responded. “Just him. Not only does he not stop them, but he goads them onward!”","......","The Beast Colosseum sat in the southwest of the capital and occupied a dozen kilometers. It rivaled the family complex of a large clan, but was the trade of an external faction as opposed to a local family business.","Its buildings were grand and magnificent. The four sacred beasts of azure dragon, white tiger, vermilion bird, and dusk tortoise stood in the four corners. It was divided into four major areas inside, likewise named after the four sacred beasts. Each of the areas was further split into seven sections and populated with numerous observation pavilions.","Noble scions loved coming to the Beast Colosseum for entertainment. They spent their days taming spirit beasts, bringing them to the colosseum, and taking wagers as they pitted the beasts against each other in fights.","“Hahaha! Brother Lin, your Fire-Eye Wolf King is a second rank spirit beast alright! It easily tore my human pet to pieces! Here you go, ten paramount rank spirit stones!”","“Brother Xu is indeed trustworthy!” the so-called Brother Lin laughed raucously when he received the stones.","Brother Xu was Sir Cloudexit. His surname was Xu and the characters of his name were chuyun, meaning “out cloud”. Hence, he was called Sir Cloudexit.","“Why are the cultivators of Dark City so weak? They’re all dead after an hour. Li Wei, go capture some foundation establishment cultivators. I can’t keep losing like this,” Cloudexit said to a guard next to him.","“Yes, young lord.” Li Wei was initial nascent soul. He responded to his orders and left the pavilion.","“I happen to lack a spirit beast—this Li Wei can be my human pet!” Lu Yun and the others naturally overheard the conversation in the azure dragon area. When they saw Li Wei walk out, Lu Yun approached him without a word.","“Petrify!” he shouted softly. The guard’s cultivation was completely confined after he slapped a talisman on the man.","“Yu Shuai, Chenguang, prepare some metal chains and tie this fellow up for me. Hahaha, so human pets are in fashion now! I want to join in the fun!” Lu Yun’s arrogant glee echoed through the area.","“Lu Yun!” Cloudexit jumped up like a cat whose tail had been stepped on and he rushed out of the pavilion.","......","Yu Shuai and Zhao Chenguang looked at each other, both swallowing hard in unison. They hadn’t even gotten a clear look at how Lu Yun had subdued Li Wei. This was a nascent soul cultivator, a preeminent existence in Darklake Empire!","They subconsciously looked at Fengxian Wu, relaxing somewhat when they confirmed her presence.","“Aha, so it’s Sir Cloudexit! It’s only been a few days, but your hair is looking ever fuller!” Lu Yun burst into laughter when he saw Cloudexit’s head. He’d burned Cloudexit bald with several hundred talismans when they fought. The young lord had only managed to grow a thin layer of hair after a period of time.","The young masters next to Cloudexit couldn’t help but frown when they saw Lu Yun. They were all in their twenties, but all golden core cultivators. That would make them incredible geniuses in Darklake. However, being from a different level of cultivation empire, golden core at twenty-some years old was a common occurrence to them.","“You are Lu Yun?” The Lin surnamed young master tilted his chin upward and looked down at Lu Yun. “I can make the call and show you mercy if you release Guard Li.”","“Heh heh heh heh heh...” Lu Yun chortled. “Aren’t you interesting. This nascent soul cultivator is my new human pet. I’m about to show my dominance in the Beast Colosseum and earn some spirit stones to spend. If I release him just because you say so, won’t that be an incredible loss of face for me?”","“Who do you think you are, Lu Yun?!” Cloudexit’s eyes spat fire and he only just managed to keep himself under control when he saw Fengxian Wu by Lu Yun’s side. “You’re just someone who likes to hide behind a woman!”","Cloudexit and his friends were convinced that it’d been Fengxian Wu who took down Li Wei."]},{"number":2243,"title":"Chapter 2243: Chapter 2172.1: Face Slapping","paragraphs":["Chapter 2172.1: Face Slapping","Where did that woman come from? She’s only golden core, but she easily defeats numerous nascent soul opponents... Young master Lin’s thoughts flew rapidly.","The other two noble scions with Cloudexit also had their misgivings and didn’t say anything.","“Hide behind a woman?” An astonished Lu Yun turned around to look at Fengxian Wu. “I’m obviously standing right in front of her, is Sir Cloudexit’s head screwed on right?”","“You...” Cloudexit turned beet red.","“Cut the crap, this young master is here to watch beasts fight. Eh, no, I’m here to watch people fight, not argue with you guys.” Lu Yun held his hand out for a metal chain that Zhao Chenguang passed over to him. He casually tied it to Li Wei’s neck and kicked the man in the back of the knees.","Li Wei thumped to a kneeling position on the ground, unable to resist because his cultivation was sealed by Lu Yun’s talisman.","“I hear that human pets are all the rage these days, so here is mine. Which one of you guys wants to put him through his paces?” Lu Yun kicked Li Wei in the butt and punted him into the ringed enclosure.","Cloudexit was nearly apoplectic with fury. Li Wei was a Nineheavens Pagoda disciple and currently his guard. A nascent soul cultivator enjoyed decent status in a fourth rank empire!","If it wasn’t for the sect leader doting on his son so much, he wouldn’t have sent so many nascent soul cultivators as Li Wei’s guard. Lu Yun treating one of them as a human pet was a vicious slap at the sect’s face.","But after the Nineheavens Pagoda crippled Lu Xiaochi three years ago and given how they plainly wanted to eliminate the Lus this time, Lu Yun couldn’t be bothered to put on an amiable facade for them.","At the same time, Helian Shan’s interference and killing of Xu Lang proved quite deterring for the Dark Orchid cultivators. The other three young masters from that nation looked at each other, reading gravity in their peers’ eyes.","“I’d like to see who dares bet against Lu Yun!!” Cloudexit’s infuriated voice rang out clearly.","“Hahahaha, isn’t this the nascent soul powerhouse Li Wei of the Nineheavens Pagoda? When did he become a human pet? How interesting. I happen to have a second rank blaze lion with me today. Why don’t I take Sir Lu Yun up on your offer?” another voice sounded immediately after.","A young man dressed in long ivory robes with a beautiful piece of jade around his waist strolled out of another pavilion, entering the one that Lu Yun and the others were in.","“This must be Miss Feng Wu. Greetings, I am Yang Qing.” The young man swept a genteel bow at Fengxian Wu as soon as he walked in.","Fengxian Wu glanced at him and ignored the young man. Yang Qing rubbed his nose, not minding the snub.","“Yang Qing! How dare people from the Ascension Sword Sect show their face in a Dark Orchid vassal nation?!” Cloudexit roared when he saw the young man.","“Only trash like you would ask such an idiotic question, Xu Chuyun.” Yang Qing cast a sidelong glance at Cloudexit.","Lu Yun’s eyes darted rapidly between them as he grasped what was playing out before him. The matter of the dao weapon had raised a great furor in the fourth and fifth rank empires. All manner of great factions had sent their disciples to investigate. Leading the delegations were the most accomplished of the younger generation. It was plainly also a journey to temper the younger disciples.","There were no dao weapons in fourth and fifth rank nations. The appearance of one was sufficient to tilt the balance of power between the cultivation empires. The older generation checked each other and had reached an agreement that the younger generation should take point this time. Thus, Sir Lin and Yang Qing were the unofficial heirs to their faction since they captained their delegations.","Cloudexit was an exception.","“Sir Lu, I’ll bet against you. How about it?” Yang Qing smiled faintly at Lu Yun.","“Don’t you dare, Lu Yun!” Cloudexit jumped out while everyone else looked on coldly. “Yang Qing is from Skypine Empire, the enemy of Dark Orchid! You’d be a traitor if you dare take the bet!”","“What an idiot,” Lu Yun snorted. “Since you are from Skypine, Sir Yang, then I cannot back down! Beating you would be winning glory for Dark Orchid!”","Yang Qing blinked, then smiled radiantly. “Good, good, very good! Although Sir Lu is young, your aspirations are great. Here, I will bet one hundred paramount rank spirit stones against you. They are yours if you win!”","Cloudexit glowered, but there was nothing he could say to Lu Yun. Everything the latter said made sense. As for Li Wei, he’d kept up a litany of curses ever since being thrown into the enclosure.","“Aiya, one hundred paramount rank stones...” A conflicted expression spread across Lu Yun’s face. He had quite a few paramount rank stones after robbing the Ouyang Clan, but they were very useful to him. He wasn’t willing to waste even one out of his tens of thousands.","“How about this, I have a lower spirit rank flying sword here. Will this work as my forfeit?” Lu Yun summoned a cerulean flying sword with a flip of his hand.","It was the one he’d taken from Cloudexit.","“A spirit weapon?” Yang Qing brightened.","“I’m going to kill you, Lu Yun!” Cloudexit bawled with fury. Lu Yun had delivered slap after slap to his face. He was completely humiliated, but couldn’t erupt with fury given that Fengxian Wu was present.","“I’ll take you as my human pet next and bet you against Sir Yang if you keep running your mouth, do you hear me?” Lu Yun suddenly hectored with a chill in his expression.","“You...” Cloudexit had never suffered this kind of humiliation before! It was one thing to be beaten by Lu Yun; how was he supposed to endure repeated degradation?","But when he looked at the deeply amused Fengxian Wu behind Lu Yun, someone who’d stayed silent the entire time, he chose to be quiet. Baleful resentment bloomed in the bottom of his eyes.","“That’s more like it.” Lu Yun cockily shook his head.","Cloudexit nearly spat blood; this was the straw that broke the camel’s back.","“I’m going to kill you, Lu Yun!!” Cloudexit was another unequivocal prodigal who spent his days terrorizing others. He possessed a deeply tyrannical streak, one that was fully aroused by Lu Yun’s last word.","Humm!","His true origin surged as he slammed a palm down on Lu Yun’s chest.","Smack!","The crowd only saw a shadow flash in front of their eyes before Cloudexit spun on the spot. A purplish handprint was as clear as day on his cheek.","“I said that I would take you as a human pet if you kept running your mouth!” Lu Yun flashed behind Cloudexit and grabbed the other’s collar.","“How dare you hit me?!” Cloudexit shrieked incredulously.","“How dare you!” gasped another nascent soul guard next to Cloudexit. Everything happened too quickly for him to react. When he gathered his senses, the young lord was already in Lu Yun’s hands.","“This is bad!” Sir Lin and the other two young masters also reacted with dismay, but Yang Qing was one step ahead of them.","“Gentlemen, I won’t move if you don’t move. If you move... Do you think you’ll be a match for Miss Feng?”","The three trembled like they’d been doused in cold water.","“No, it’s not Feng Wu taking action, but Lu Yun!” Sir Lin realized with shock.","Cloudexit’s other guard was already subdued and wore a talisman on his forehead. No one could tell how Lu Yun had accomplished the deed. A foundation establishment cultivator taking down a golden core and nascent soul cultivator by himself? It would be one thing if Lu Yun came from a higher rank empire, but he was just a good-for-nothing from a third rank empire!","“Alright, Sir Yang. I now have three human pets and can bet against you.”","Cloudexit and his other guard were frozen by talismans. Their eyes bulged with fury as Lu Yun treated them as human pets.","“Well...” Yang Qing hesitated. As lofty as Li Wei and the other fellow was, they were just disciples of the Nineheavens Pagoda. But Xu Chuyun was different, he was the sect leader’s only son and deeply beloved. If Yang Qing really treated him as a human pet, he wouldn’t make it out of Darklake alive!","“Lu Yun, you’re creating trouble for your clan!” Sir Lin took a stilted step forward.","“Creating trouble?” Lu Yun blinked. “If I might know your name...”","“Dark Orchid, the Lin Clan, Lin Qi,” the young man snorted.","“So you’re from the Lins of Dark Orchid?” Lu Yun cocked his head with a supercilious smile. “I wonder what is this trouble that Sir Lin speaks of?”","“Lu Yun, don’t presume that the law enforcer will always protect the Lu Clan after intervening once!” The other two Dark Orchid young masters took a step forward and stood side by side with Lin Qi. Unlike Cloudexit, they were elites of their family instead of prodigals. While they were sometimes up to no good, they were completely different from Cloudexit.","“What, do the three of you wish to interfere in the feud between the Nineheavens Pagoda and my family?”","Smack!","Lu Yun turned back and slapped Cloudexit across the face, making his other cheek swell up.","“You!” shouted the three to see Lu Yun slap Cloudexit again.","Yang Qing backed away, regarding the situation with a cold eye. Skypine and Dark Orchid were opposing nations; he was delighted to see an enemy beset with internal strife."]},{"number":2244,"title":"Chapter 2244: Chapter 2172.2: Face Slapping","paragraphs":["Chapter 2172.2: Face Slapping","This Lu Yun is incredibly strong... He’s very different from what the stories say, but his style is a perfect match. A sharp light glinted in Yang Qing’s eyes as he made certain calculations.","“What about me?” Lu Yun sniffed. “Stand over there like good little boys if you don’t want to be my pet!”","“Good, very good!” laughed the young master dressed in traditional clothing. “Adversity from the heavens can be accepted, but mishaps of one’s own making cannot be endured! I, Wen Qiushui, would like to see how you’d turn me into a human pet!”","“Are you sure you want to be my pet?” Lu Yun glanced at Fengxian Wu. “Miss Feng, we should have a good time on your first visit to the Beast Colosseum. How about I give these three and their guards to you as pets?”","“Very well,” Fengxian Wu smiled. Although her face was covered by a veil, the young masters—including Yang Qing—paused in a daze. “But I can’t be bothered to catch them myself. You do it for me, Lu Yun,” she giggled.","A wry smile spread across Lu Yun’s face—and it wasn’t an act. He was confident against golden core opponents, but nascent soul would be difficult without using the Petrification art. Not to mention, each of the three were accompanied by two guards that were also nascent soul. He could handle one or two of them, but would be able to do nothing other than run if all six mobbed him at the same time.","The three glared with livid expressions, but didn’t dare refute Fengxian Wu. She’d defeated a dozen nascent soul cultivators by herself, including latter nascent soul powerhouses. None of them were a match for her.","“Lu Yun, I recommend you release Sir Cloudexit and apologize properly to him. Otherwise, your two servants will become my human pets,” came another voice at this time.","A handsome young man dressed in long blue robes walked in with two followers. Each of them carried a person in their hands.","“Ouyang Shengtian?” Lu Yun raised an eyebrow, then swiftly regained his calm. His men were carrying an unconscious Lu Xuan and Lan’er. “It looks like you want to die, Ouyang Shengtian.”","“Oh?” The Ouyang young master hauled Lan’er in front of him. “This He Lan’er is General He Wuheng’s daughter, isn’t she? Oh, he’s your family servant now after stepping down from his post. Isn’t he a loyal one? If you want Lan’er to live, you will release Sir Cloudexit. That would be good for both of us.","“And Miss Feng Wu, I recommend you to not do anything. Since I’ve come here with the two of them, it naturally means that I’m fully prepared.” Ouyang Shengtian glanced at Fengxian Wu.","She did indeed want to spring into action as she was good friends with Lan’er and wouldn’t stand to see her friend in these straits.","Smack!","A crisp face slap jarred everyone out of their thoughts. The pitiful Cloudexit had suffered another heavy blow. Being frozen by a talisman, the brooding young lord couldn’t move or talk.","“Let them go,” Lu Yun demanded.","Ouyang Shengtian paused, shocked.","Smack!","“Let them go!”","“You...”","Smack!","“Let them go!”","......","Everyone’s jaw dropped. It was incredible that Lu Yun would act like this! One slap after another rained down on Cloudexit’s face. He suffered a dozen slaps in short order and his handsome face turned as swollen as a pig’s head.","“I will kill Xu Chuyun if you don’t let them go. All of it will be the Ouyang Clan’s fault then,” Lu Yun paused and sneered at Ouyang Shengtian.","Cloudexit was still conscious despite suffering a dozen hearty slaps. He glared at Ouyang Shengtian with eyes of fire. Why would he be suffering such humiliation if it wasn’t for this kid interfering?!","No one really thought that Lu Yun would use him as a human pet, including Yang Qing. Whoever dared put their beast in a ring with Sir Cloudexit was looking to die. And even if Lu Yun really did lose his mind, Yang Qing wouldn’t dare bet against him!","Dark Orchid’s enemy nation would be very careful to avoid doing so. Something seemingly inconspicuous could cause war to break out between the two sides. No one could afford such consequences, and Xu Chuyun most certainly occupied that kind of status in his father’s heart.","But now, Lu Yun had been goaded into smacking Cloudexit again and again. Ouyang Shengtian was furious and subconsciously looked at Xu Chuyun, but didn’t release Lan’er.","Ouyang Shengtian wants to force my hand. No wonder he put on this show today, he’s the one behind everything. The thought flashed through Lu Yun’s mind and he chuckled, “What, are you still not releasing them, Ouyang Shengtian? Are you trying to force me into killing Xu Chuyun?”","Terror appeared on Cloudexit’s face.","“Hurry up and let them go!” Lin Qi frowned and shouted.","Ouyang Shengtian remained unmoving and stared frostily at Lu Yun. “I don’t think you have it in you to kill Sir Cloudexit.”","“Heh heh heh,” Lu Yun chuckled. “You don’t believe me? Then let me show you!”","He raised his hand, drawing horrified expressions from Lin Qi, Wen Qiushui, and Luo Hongfei. But before they could move, Lu Yun reached back with his hand and scratched his head.","“Don’t worry, it’s just a joke,” he smirked.","The group felt like they were on the verge of heart attacks. This kid... truly had no limits!","“But it does seem that Ouyang Shengtian would be very happy to see me kill Sir Cloudexit...” Lu Yun continued calmly.","Ouyang Shengtian’s expression shifted, yet he remained blithely unconcerned. “Sir Cloudexit is noble and lofty, you are but the young master of country bumpkins. Hurry up and release him!”","“Country bumpkins? Noble and lofty?” Lu Yun shook his head and stomped on Xu Chuyun’s back, kicking him to the ground and resting one foot on his head.","“I don’t know why you’re trying to provoke me, Ouyang Shengtian. You must know that one tends to lose reason when one is upset. Losing reason often leads to unreasonable action. Is that what you want to see?” Anger dawned on Lu Yun’s face.","Lin Qi, Wen Qiushui, and Luo Hongfei had also realized something was amiss and looked unpleasantly at Ouyang Shengtian.","“Oh... oho!” Lu Yun scratched his cheek with a look of dawning understanding. “Your baby sister, the Ouyang Shengxiang who’s been in this young master’s bed, is said to be engaged to the Dark Orchid crown prince. Is this what you’re counting on? The Lus will suffer revenge if Xu Chuyun dies, but the Ouyangs will remain safe due to your relationship with the Dark Orchid crown prince. What a lovely move of killing with a borrowed blade!”","Sprawled on the ground, deep resentment flashed through Xu Chuyun’s eyes. In this moment, he hated Ouyang Shengtian more than he did Lu Yun.","“Aiya, I wonder if the Dark Orchid crown prince knows that Ouyang Shengxiang has a red mole on her butt...” Lu Yun licked his lips.","Ouyang Shengtian’s face drained of color. Lin Qi, Wen Qiushui, and Luo Hongfei’s expressions also turned odd. Ouyang Shengxiang was a connate fragrance constitution and the crown prince had decided long ago that she would be his future empress. Yet, Lu Yun was saying that she’d been in his bed?","What did that mean?","And there was a red mole on her butt?","Um...","The three found things very strange indeed when they looked at Ouyang Shengtian’s pallor.","“Sir Cloudexit, my human pet, it looks like someone really wants you to die.” Lu Yun leaned over and patted Xu Chuyun’s swollen cheek.","Xu Chuyun’s eyeballs were about to fall out from the force of his glare, but there was nothing he could do since he was under Lu Yun’s foot and immobilized by a talisman.","“Young master Lu, will you release Xu Chuyun on my behalf?” sounded a new voice. A young man roughly twenty years old had walked into the pavilion at some point.","“Very well, this young master will show mercy today on behalf of Sir Yue.” Lu Yun recognized the newcomer in long ivory robes as one of the three gentlemen of the capital—Mo Qiyue.","Despite his words, he didn’t move his foot. “Ouyang Shengtian, you should release my two servants.”","Ouyang Shengtian took a long look at Mo Qiyue before throwing Lan’er and Lu Xuan over. Zhao Chenguang and Yu Shuai frantically caught Lu Xuan while Fengxian Wu held up Lan’er.","Lu Yun snorted and snapped his fingers, dispersing the talisman on Xu Chuyun’s head. He removed his foot and kicked the young man to Lin Qi and the others.","“But now I lack a human pet without Sir Cloudexit.” His next words caused the atmosphere to tense up again."]},{"number":2245,"title":"Chapter 2245: Chapter 2173.1: Challenge","paragraphs":["Chapter 2173.1: Challenge","After being rescued, Xu Chuyun looked at Lu Yun with eyes full of fear. He didn’t dare say anything anymore. What if Lu Yun changed his mind and grabbed him again?","“Ouyang Shengtian, how about you be my human pet?” Lu Yun cocked his head at the Ouyang young master; the latter’s face darkened.","“Don’t you go too far, Lu Yun.” Ouyang Shengtian took two steps back. Cloudexit’s two nascent soul guards were still in Lu Yun’s hands.","“Hahahaha!! Sir Ouyang of the three gentlemen is scared off by one word from me? Insignificant little me? Looks like I command quite a bit of respect!” Lu Yun roared with laughter to see the other’s expression.","The corner of Mo Qiyue’s lips tugged upward. “What three gentlemen of Dusk City? It’s just a trite title given by bored people.”","Ouyang Shengtian’s face darkened further when he heard the response. Plainly, the Mo young master didn’t think much of the moniker, but Ouyang Shengtian did and cared quite a great deal.","“But Sir Ouyang counts the title among his treasures...” Lu Yun snorted. Mo Qiyue wordlessly curled his lip.","Ouyang Shengtian glowered ominously.","Lu Yun waved him off. He was just scaring the Ouyang young master. These wouldn’t be the tactics he’d employ if he wanted to take action. He’d make sure that Ouyang Shengtian yearned for death.","“Sir Yang Qing, my lower spirit rank longsword is worth at least a million paramount rank spirit stones, is it not? Betting one hundred against it seems too few.” Dismissing what’d just happened, Lu Yun focused on haggling instead.","“The Arcturus Sword is well known in fourth rank empires. Mighty without parallel, it’s worth at least two million paramount stones,” Yang Qing assessed honestly.","“Then you should also bring out something on the same level to bet against me.” Lu Yun had wanted to befriend this exemplary disciple of the Ascension Sword Sect, thereby creating a strong helper for the Lu Clan, but his attitude earlier changed Lu Yun’s mind.","Lu Yun’s earlier actions probed Yang Qing’s attitude. Since the latter had kept himself out of the affair and refused to be involved, there was no need for Lu Yun to extend a friendly gesture to him.","Yang Qing’s attitude was an indicator that he wasn’t an ideal ally. Although he’d stopped Lin Qi and the others for Lu Yun, he’d done so to sit on his hands and watch others fight. He wanted to set the snipe and clam at each other and take advantage of both. His calculations were fully evident to Lu Yun.","“Ah...” Yang Qing blinked.","“I have a mid spirit rank sword called Riversurge. Why don’t I bet it against young master Lu?” A young man wearing long emerald robes and a beautiful piece of jade across his forehead stepped into the pavilion.","Yang Qing, Lin Qi, Wen Qiushui, and Luo Hongfei frowned. They didn’t recognize the newcomer in green. But judging from his bearing and the spirit rank weapon he’d brought it, he came from uncommon origins.","“If I might know this gentleman’s name...?” Lu Yun raised cupped fists to the young man.","“Jiang Feng,” the young man offered.","Yang Qing and the others continued to regard him blankly, unable to place him. His cultivation was greater than theirs at initial nascent soul—the same as Ouyang Shengtian and Mo Qiyue.","Fengxian Wu’s eyes narrowed ever so slightly when she heard the name.","“Is this Jiang Feng from a sixth rank empire?” Yang Qing mumbled to himself. He knew all of the fifth rank factions and fourth rank disciples by heart. If he didn’t know the stranger, that made him someone from a sixth rank empire.","As for seventh rank or above... a dao weapon wouldn’t draw their attention.","“So it’s Sir Jiang,” Lu Yun grinned. “But your Riversurge is a mid rank weapon while my Arcturus is only lower rank. We’re one level apart and I don’t have any more treasures to offer.”","“That may not be the case,” Jiang Feng smiled faintly, merriment in his eyes. “Didn’t you claim the personal wealth of Xu Lang from the Nineheavens Pagoda? Just take out a few items from your vault.”","The recovering Xu Chuyun nearly spat a mouthful of blood when he heard this.","“Alright then,” Lu Yun agreed reluctantly. “But I left all that at home, so if I lose, Brother Jiang will have to make a trip with me.”","“Hahahaha!” Jiang Feng laughed heartily. “You jest, Sir Lu. It’s not a given who will win or lose, there’s no need to come to conclusions so quickly.”","“Do my two human pets look like they stand a chance of winning?” Lu Yun cast a dismissive glance at the two in the ring. Xu Chuyun’s two guards were ashen faced and prepared to die. They were nascent soul disciples of the vaunted Nineheavens Pagoda, yet were subject to such intense humiliation in a third rank empire! Did they have it in them to continue living?","“That’s up to Sir Lu’s ingenuity,” Jiang Feng smiled uncaringly.","Lu Yun blinked, then suddenly shifted in front of Ouyang Shengtian.","“Ouyang Shengtian, our families have been enemies for a while and there’s no changing that. You can be my human pet and fight for me this time!” Sparks flared from Lu Yun’s hand as he grabbed for Ouyang Shengtian’s head.","Frowning, the Ouyang young master swiftly backed away. A flying sword shot out of his mouth and made for Lu Yun’s head in a streak of light.","Lu Yun shuffled his feet and gently shifted his body, easily evading the ray of light.","“Kill!” Killing intent flooded Ouyang Shengtian’s face. The flying sword exploded into dozens of light rays that rained down on Lu Yun.","“Interesting.” Lin Qi and the others watched the fight with interest, not inclined to stop the two. Their guards stood firmly in front of them.","Hummm.","Lu Yun’s Arcturus blazed with green light and projected a ray of sword light three meters long.","“Fire Slay!” he shouted, eliciting a sheen of fiery sparks from his sword light. They climbed up the radiance like a fire dragon.","Rumble!","The fire dragon and Ouyang Shengtian’s sword light smashed into each other in a shower of brilliance.","Pfft!","Ouyang Shengtian spat out a mouthful of blood—his personal treasure, the upper fine rank flying sword, clanged to the ground as scrap metal. Connected as he was to the weapon, he also suffered greatly from the damage.","A talisman shimmered in Lu Yun’s hand as he brought it down on Ouyang Shengtian’s head.","“Blood Shadow Flight!” Ouyang Shengtian ground his teeth and raised a ball of bloody light around him. He was gone when it cleared.","“That’s the human demon Bloodbath’s technique!” gasped Lin Qi and the others. Who would’ve thought that Ouyang Shengtian would deploy it?","“Wait, it was the Ouyang Clan who spread word that Bloodbath is in the capital. What is the truth of the situation?”","The Beast Colosseum was protected by formations, so nothing spilled over to the outside no matter how intense the fights inside were. In fact, no one beyond their pavilion would notice the scuffle unless someone was specifically keeping an eye on them.","“Ai, the only human pet that could win has run off,” Lu Yun sighed with resignation, inwardly cursing Bloodbath and all of his ancestors. The Ouyangs treated you like that, but you still taught them your ultimate protection techniques?","Jiang Feng shrugged without a word. The other noble scions were numb to the sight of Lu Yun easily defeating an initial nascent soul cultivator. That was how he’d subdued Xu Chuyun’s two nascent soul guards, wasn’t it?","Just as the group relaxed, Lu Yun darted forward and grabbed Xu Chuyun amid the latter’s ghastly howls.","“Hey, listen up, you two! You will win no matter what or I’ll turn your young lord into a human pet and match him against Sir Jiang next, do you hear me?” Lu Yun sealed off Xu Chuyun’s cultivation and hauled him up by the collar.","Xu Chuyun’s two guards had been ready for death, but stirred to life again when they saw their master in Lu Yun’s hands.","“Do whatever you want to me, but let go of the young lord!” Li Wei roared within the enclosure. Although they’d been assigned as the young lord’s guards, they were still deeply loyal to the Nineheavens Pagoda.","“Beat Sir Jiang’s battle pet for me and I’ll let your young lord go,” Lu Yun chuckled.","Li Wei’s eyes spat fire.","“In that case, let us begin.” Lu Yun turned with a smile.","“Yang Qing, is it? I’m going to borrow your blaze lion.” Jiang Feng nodded and pointed at Yang Qing.","A displeased look appeared in Yang Qing’s eyes, but he had no choice and handed over the blaze lion since he was unfamiliar with Jiang Feng’s background.","Xu Chuyun was nearly sobbing—Lu Yun treated him as nothing more than a toy and didn’t give him a chance to fight back.","A blaze lion was a second rank spirit beast, the equivalent of a foundation establishment cultivator. Although Li Wei’s cultivation was sealed off, he still possessed the immense physique of a nascent soul cultivator.","Human and beast faced off in the enclosure that ran thirty meters across.","The Beast Colosseum was where rich scions came to while away the time. Each pavilion saw its regulars and they typically didn’t interfere with each other. Only when there was a site-wide event did everyone head to the larger enclosures, so no one knew that Lu Yun and the others were in this pavilion. Otherwise, the four Dark Orchid gentlemen wouldn’t be acting like this.","All the same, there was certainly going to be revenge taken after the fact."]},{"number":2246,"title":"Chapter 2246: Chapter 2173.2: Challenge","paragraphs":["Chapter 2173.2: Challenge","Lu Yun didn’t care that trouble was incoming after today. The Nineheavens Pagoda had plainly come to Dark City to eliminate the Lu Clan. Since there were open hostilities between the two, there was no need for any restraint in his actions.","Fights within the Beast Colosseum were unusually brutal. As human and beast grappled with each other, Li Wei paid the price of an arm to crush the blaze lion’s head.","It was a pyrrhic victory made possible through the physique of a nascent soul cultivator.","Emotion flickered over Fengxian Wu’s face—she couldn’t bear the sight.","“Aiyaya, Brother Jiang, it looks like I’ve won,” Lu Yun said merrily.","“Ole brother Lu’s human pet is extraordinary indeed. I wholeheartedly accept my defeat.” Jiang Feng and Lu Yun’s honorifics for each other had changed at some point in time. “This Riversurge is my dear younger brother’s.” Jiang Feng casually handed the sword to Lu Yun.","Off to the side, Lin Qi and the other noble sons swallowed hard. A mid spirit rank weapon was exceedingly rare even in fourth rank empires. It was typically wielded only by the various patriarchs and sect leaders of the major factions.","“Brother Jiang, Brother Mo, I see that it’s almost noon. Why don’t I prepare a banquet at my residence and invite the two brothers for a visit?” Lu Yun looked around and addressed Mo Qiyue and Jiang Feng.","Jiang Feng nodded with a faint smile while Mo Qiyue first blinked with astonishment, then nodded as well.","“Yu Shuai, Chenguang, c’mon. We’re drinking at my place,” Lu Yun called out to his friends. He always included them as they were his brothers for life.","Meanwhile, Lu Xuan and Lan’er recovered through Fengxian Wu’s efforts. Lu Xuan was once more expressionless as he marched the one-armed Li Wei and Xu Chuyun’s other guard, Cheng You, back to the Lu residence.","......","“Eldest senior brother, you must uphold justice for me!” Xu Chuyun had fully recovered in a Dark City inn. Apart from his hair needing time to grow back, all was as it should be with him.","A handsome young man in pale blue robes sat in front of him. Naturally graceful, he emanated an ethereal air. He was much weaker than Xu Lang at only latter nascent soul, but as the senior disciple of the Nineheavens Pagoda, his methods were much superior to Xu Lang’s.","“You can ignore the Lu Clan going forward. Our mission centers on the dao weapon,” Xu Youyuan said faintly.","“But...”","“There are no buts.” Xu Youyuan flicked a glance at the young lord. “Nothing is an issue so long as you are alive. We only had one chance to eliminate the Lu Clan. Things are over since we missed it.”","Enormous reluctance colored Xu Chuyun’s face, but he didn’t dare protest.","Xu Youyuan and Xu Lang were the senior and second disciples of the Nineheavens Pagoda. They stood head and shoulders above their peers in the younger generation of Dark Orchid Empire; someone as useless as Xu Chuyun couldn’t begin to measure up to them.","His father had raised them from youth and they occupied the same status as Xu Chuyun in the sect. However, since it was a law enforcer from the ninth rank empires that’d kill Xu Lang, there was nothing that anyone dared say. They would have to accept it if even their emperor was executed by a law enforcer.","“Li Jian, have you determined where that Yong Heyu is yet?” Xu Youyuan asked another disciple who’d walked through the door.","“Yes,” Li Jian smiled faintly. “He was at the Iron Pagoda Mountain in the western territory of the Profound Wing Empire three days ago. He left ripples of a spirit weapon behind—it seems likely that he fought someone there.”","“Profound Wing Empire, the Iron Pagoda Mountain.” Xu Youyuan shot to his feet. “We go to the Profound Wing Empire!”","......","All of the factions in a holding position at Dark City mobilized for the mountain in the western quadrant of Profound Wing Empire. Many of Darklake’s own factions joined the hustle and bustle as well.","The Lu residence.","“Are you going to Iron Pagoda Mountain as well, Brother Jiang?” Lu Yun looked curiously at Jiang Feng, easily discerning that the young man possessed an incredible background. He was most probably from an upper rank cultivation empire, so why did he care about the dao weapon?","“Ask Mo the Second. I go if he goes, I won’t go if he doesn’t.” Jiang Feng used his chin to point at a Mo Qiyue sipping tea.","Lu Yun had been very surprised to find out that the two knew each other. He already knew that the Mo Clan wasn’t as simple as it appeared and that Mo Qiyue hid his strength deep, but who would’ve thought that he’d have a relationship with someone like Jiang Feng?","Jiang Feng had stayed at the Lu residence ever since their meeting at the Beast Colosseum, which often brought Mo Qiyue to the complex.","What stoked Lu Yun’s curiosity was that Mo Qiyue was an only child. So why did Jiang Feng call him “the second” in a way that indicated he was the second child of his family?","“It’ll be interesting to watch the proceedings.” Mo Qiyue put down his teacup with a smack of his lips. “Ole brother Lu, your tea tastes very special. I wonder what kind of tea leaves are these.”","“They’re just some trifles. I’ll give Brother Mo a few kilograms if you like it,” Lu Yun smiled. He’d concocted this tea with the medicinal properties of numerous spirit herbs, it wasn’t the tea leaf that he’d obtained from his senior brother. That leaf was too potent—Lu Yun could drink it at will because he was protected by the laws of heavenly dao. But here, even a tea leaf the size of a fingernail needed to be brewed with hundreds of liters of water.","“That would be wonderful.” A faint smile spread across Mo Qiyue’s face.","“Honestly, he needs to do a better job of showing his emotions.” Jiang Feng rolled his eyes.","Humm!","A sharp sword whistle echoed from the depths of the Lu residence, followed shortly by vast sword qi that shot into the clouds. The whistle shocked the city.","“This is... the ripples of latter nascent soul! Most of the foreigners have left Dusk City, so who do these belong to??” Within the Ouyang residence, Ouyang Zhen rose with a start and looked to the east.","Many nascent soul cultivators within the Yu, Zhao, Mo, Yuwen, Ling Clans, and even the palace, opened their eyes to look to the east.","“Another latter nascent soul powerhouse has appeared in Darklake Empire!” Emperor Situ Wenxian smiled from his throne.","The air over the Lu residence.","Lu Xiaochi stood proudly in the air with sword qi raging around him. Undeniably glorious, he wore a black combat outfit and seemed like a sharp sword that’d shot out of its scabbard.","“This is...” Jiang Feng stood up. “Such incredible sword intent! An incredible sword immortal has appeared in this nation!”","Fervor flashed through Jiang Feng’s eyes. Mo Qiyue glanced at his friend and shook his head.","“Ah, it’s the Lu second master. Has your cultivation recovered?” An elder with graying hair appeared in the skies outside the complex with a flash of sword light. He was very startled by what he found.","“Hahaha, greetings to Senior Zhao Xuanfeng, senior elder of the Zhao Clan.” Lu Xiaochi held himself with confidence and assurance. Not only had his cultivation fully recovered, but it’d taken a step forward and reached latter nascent soul.","The Major Five Elements Demolition Godslayer Record that Lu Yun had given him was a premier sword method recorded in the world of immortals. Combined with the tea leaves that Lu Yun had taken from his senior brother, it ensured that Lu Xiaochi easily returned to a nascent soul cultivation level.","“Pity, I need a decent weapon,” Lu Xiaochi found this sole lacking regretful. His personal treasure had been a flying sword before he was crippled, but enemies had shattered it.","“Second uncle, catch!” Lu Yun took out the Riversurge that he’d just won from Jiang Feng and threw it to Lu Xiaochi.","“A mid spirit rank weapon!” Eyes brightening, Lu Xiaochi laughed happily. “What a fine sword! Senior Zhao, dare you spar with me?” He pointed the sword at Zhao Xuanfeng.","The elder smiled ruefully.","“How do the Lus have a mid spirit rank weapon? When did they become as common as cabbages?” Zhao Xuanfeng could fight Lu Xiaochi if the latter didn’t have his new weapon, but the emergence of the mid spirit rank weapon meant that his own upper fine rank weapon would be ruined after one blow.","“So it was the Lu second master who broke through to latter nascent soul after recovering his cultivation. This unaccomplished junior would be happy to spar!” Sword light flashed through the sky as a young man in long green robes arrived atop a flying sword.","“You are the current foremost genius of the capital, Ouyang Shengtian?” Lu Xiaochi looked at the newcomer.","“Indeed, that is this junior!” A keen light glinted in Ouyang Shengtian’s eyes.","“Didn’t you defeat this guy? How dare he challenge your second uncle?” A surprised Jiang Feng gazed at the young man in the sky.","“The Ouyang Shengtian in front of us is more than what he seems.” Lu Yun shook his head. He, too, rose into the air with a flash of sword light beneath his feet.","“Ouyang Shengtian, my vanquished opponent—how does trash like you want to challenge my second uncle? Come come, this young master will meet you in battle,” Lu Yun roared with laughter as he soared on the back of Arcturus.","Ouyang Shengtian looked at him unpleasantly.","Lu Xiaochi paused, turned his head stiltedly, and almost had his eyeballs fall out to see his nephew join him with a lower spirit rank weapon.","“Did you just say... Ouyang Shengtian is your vanquished opponent?” he asked hesitantly.","“Heh heh heh heh heh,” Lu Yun cackled.","There were numerous people gathered below; all of them rolled their eyes when they heard Lu Yun. You’re just a handful of dog shit, Lu Yun. How dare you shamelessly boast that one of the three gentlemen lost to you? You’ve lost your mind!","The four gentlemen from the Dark Orchid Empire had locked down the happenings at the Beast Colosseum. No one dared speak about it, and although some rumors circulated, most dismissed the hearsay as jokes.","Initial nascent spirit Ouyang Shengtian losing to Lu Yun? Never. No one paid any attention to the Lu young master’s cultivation. What difference was there between foundation establishment and qi refinement to a nascent soul powerhouse?","“Ouyang Shengtian, you’ll have to get through me first if you want to challenge my second uncle. Don’t even think of fighting my uncle if you can’t defeat me.” Killing intent shimmered in Lu Yun’s eyes. Ouyang Shengtian gave him a very strange feeling—a very uncomfortable feeling. Thus, he’d changed his mind. He was going to send Ouyang Shengtian to the afterlife as soon as possible.","The Ouyangs had undoubtedly been infiltrated by the enemy. Judging from the Ouyang young master’s performance at the Beast Colosseum, he’d coordinated his actions with the real enemy.","Since Lu Yun was just foundation establishment, he couldn’t fly through the air. He had to use Arcturus to face Ouyang Shengtian in the sky. A fiery light flashed by when he assembled his hands into a seal and a miniature pill cauldron appeared in his dantian.","“Then I will help you along since you wish to die so badly,” Ouyang Shengtian said woodenly as his expression returned to normal."]},{"number":2247,"title":"Chapter 2247: Chapter 2174.1: Possession","paragraphs":["Chapter 2174.1: Possession","Lu Xiaochi recovering his cultivation and advancing one step further alarmed many people. All of the great families in Dusk City and numerous hidden experts turned their attention to the Lu Clan.","Apart from Jiang Feng and a few others, most outsiders had gone to the Profound Wing Empire. The allure of a dao weapon was undeniable for fourth and fifth rank empire cultivators. No one expected that Ouyang Shengtian, mere initial nascent soul, would think of challenging the newly ascended Lu Xiaochi at this time. Even more surprising was that Dusk City’s number one prodigal was taking the fight for his second uncle!","It was so inconceivable that heads spun, but many were happy to watch the show. They wanted nothing more than for Ouyang Shengtian to kill Lu Yun and cleanse the capital of its greatest pestilence. It was a common sentiment despite Lu Yun only bothering some of the great families after he’d woken up.","Ouyang Shengtian remained expressionless as his aura increased. Pale-gold true origin surged out of his body like a ball of golden flames.","Lu Yun didn’t care. He formed a sword seal with his hands and split out numerous rays of sword light from the sword beneath his feet. They shot for Ouyang Shengtian.","“A lower rank empire is a lower rank empire after all. You still rely heavily on supplemental dao.” Derision played at the corners of Ouyang Shengtian’s lips.","What was known as supplemental dao were the great daos involving treasure, pill, formation, and talisman. Cultivation was intricately tied to them, hence they were known as the four great supplemental daos.","“Supplemental dao?” Lu Yun’s lips turned upward. Supplemental dao was king.","No one had a clear line of sight into Ouyang Shengtian’s movements. They simply saw radiance fill the sky. Lu Yun’s lower spirit rank weapon exploded with sword light that dispersed as soon as it appeared. The result was normal to the crowd as the Lu young master was just foundation establishment. How could he possibly withstand a nascent soul cultivator?","“Die, Lu Yun!” Ouyang Shengtian shouted coldly and pitched forward, nearly melding into this part of the world.","A ray of sword light abruptly appeared in front of Lu Yun—the will of devastation suddenly filled the land.","“Be careful!” Lu Xiaochi warned his nephew with dismay, but Ouyang Shengtian was moving so quickly that he didn’t have time to maneuver.","Clang!","A ringing from the soul echoed through the air as the terrifying sword light was rebuffed.","“You blocked it! How did you do that?!” Zhao Xuanfeng yelled. Even he wouldn’t have been able to avoid that strike; his upper fine rank weapon would be severely damaged as well.","Lu Yun dismissed the power of yang metal at his fingertips and responded with a slightly wan face, “You aren’t Ouyang Shengtian.”","“That’s not up for you to decide,” Ouyang Shengtian sneered. He raised his sword high again and brought it down on Lu Yun.","Humm!","Ambient energy within the surroundings oscillated with a massive hum as the enormous ray of sword light shot with unstoppable momentum.","It was strength—pure and absolute strength!“Hmph!” Lu Yun snorted, silver radiance once more shooting out of his hand. He waved it into a silver line, one that embedded itself into the void.","Boom!","The tremendous ray of sword light collided with the silver line and caused both to vanish. Lu Yun paled and backed away.","“Ouyang Shengtian does not possess this kind of ability.” Lu Yun calmed the roiling qi inside his body and looked directly at the Ouyang young master.","“Who would’ve thought that the biggest trash of Dusk City would be a hidden expert? I’m rather curious now what kind of person Lu Tianling, the greatest of Dusk City, is.” Ouyang Shengtian was slightly surprised, but didn’t display much emotion on his face. “I am Ouyang Shengtian now.”","Lu Yun regarded the person solemnly. He looked the same as Ouyang Shengtian, but exuded a completely different air. Plainly, someone had taken possession of the young master.","“You strut around in public instead of keeping a low profile after taking Ouyang Shengtian’s body. What, do you think no one can do anything to you?” Lu Yun transmitted contemptuously.","The two had been conversing via transmission, leaving the crowd in the dark about their conversation. It would rock the nation if people knew that the greatest genius of the younger generation had been taken possession by another.","Since he wasn’t Ouyang Shengtian, this person did not have a conflict with Lu Yun. Thus, there was no need for Lu Yun to expose his secret. The new Ouyang Shengtian had likely come with another goal in mind.","“It hasn’t been long since I’ve taken possession of this body. I need a massive fight to grow accustomed to it,” Ouyang Shengtian responded candidly.","Ouyang Shengtian suffered incredible injuries when he activated Bloodbath’s Blood Shadow Flight to flee from the Beast Colosseum. Added to that his defeat at Lu Yun’s hands, an indelible blow had been dealt to his will. That gave this person the chance to swoop in and claim Ouyang Shengtian for himself.","“That’s easy, I’ll keep you company. My second uncle is no match for you.” Lu Yun looked at Lu Xiaochi with a wide grin.","“Are you that confident in yourself?” Ouyang Shengtian blinked. This kid was just foundation establishment. Even if his potential was stunning without parallel, he could at most fight a normal nascent soul cultivator. That wasn’t rare in the world that “Ouyang Shengtian” came from.","The current Ouyang young master was possessed by an unmatched powerhouse. His battle experience was sufficient to sweep nascent soul and soul projection cultivators alike. It was a case similar to Bloodbath. The elder was just latter golden core, but he would trounce soul projection cultivators if the mood seized him.","“I would naturally be no match for you if you’d grown comfortable in this body, but right now, I can provide some amusement,” Lu Yun answered. Since the real Ouyang Shengtian was dead and the person in front of him wasn’t the family’s true enemy, then none of this mattered.","While he couldn’t beat the Ouyang young master in combat, it was an easy thing to scheme the other to death if he wished to.","“That is just as well.” Ouyang Shengtian looked around. Since he’d yet to recover his strength, it was better not to be in the public eye too often.","“Let’s fight outside the city.” Lu Yun set foot onto his flying sword and shot out of the city, Ouyang Shengtian close behind him.","That left Lu Xiaochi standing dumbly where he was, not knowing what to do. His nephew had transmitted a message before he left, telling him not to follow them.","“Don’t worry, second uncle, Lu Yun will be fine.” Mo Qiyue flew up from Lu Yun’s house and smiled at Lu Xiaochi. The Lu second master shook his head ruefully and didn’t say anything.","The disturbance raised by Lu Xiaochi recovering his cultivation was over as swiftly as it arose. Nothing came of it. The law enforcer killing Xu Lang had intimidated both the outsiders and Darklake’s own factions. The Ouyang, Ling, and Yuwen Clans didn’t dare harbor further ulterior motives.","So they said law enforcers wouldn’t deign to move against weaklings? Who were they kidding? Was there a difference between third and fourth rank empires to an awakened cultivator? No one wanted to gamble with their own life.","In this way, some of the latent threats pointed at the Lu Clan were thus erased, but danger was not yet over.","......","One thousand kilometers to the east of Dusk City, a minor mountain now razed to the ground.","Ouyang Shengtian sprawled on the ground and breathed heavily. “Damn, nice kid. If it wasn’t for your core origin and aura being one and the same, I would suspect that you’re also possessed by another immortal.”","The two had fought to a standstill after two hours. It almost made Ouyang Shengtian doubt himself.","Lu Yun’s robes were likewise disarrayed and he responded weakly, “You’re not bad yourself. The nascent soul of a wandering immortal seizing possession of someone else is damned impressive.”","Lu Yun had utilized the power of reincarnation, not possession, to become the Lu Yun of this world. After he lived through three thousand lives, the Lu Yun of this world was his starting point.","Ouyang Shengtian’s expression shifted drastically. Wandering immortals were those whose body had been destroyed and their nascent souls gravely injured. Death was final in that state, so how would they have the chance to seize possession of another?","But Ouyang Shengtian was plainly an exception. He’d come across a fortuitous opportunity and retained a sliver of nascent soul after his body was destroyed, then successfully took possession of another.","The wandering cultivators of the cultivation empires would be thrown into a frenzy if word of this got out. Wandering cultivators were failed immortals—they endured tribulations every thousand years. Each was worse than the one before until the immortal died.","But wandering cultivators... somehow, Lu Yun felt that there shouldn’t be wandering immortals beneath immortal dao. Mm, I need to remember this, I’m sure I can use them somehow in the future. Maybe I can perfect another immortal dao through them.","Lu Yun waved the other off when he noted his expression. “Be at ease. As shocking as possession is, that’s all there is to it.”","Ouyang Shengtian blinked, then roared with laughter. The discomfort he’d felt seconds ago dispersed.","Wandering immortals? Just failures to many people and not worth paying attention to. There was nothing in it for Lu Yun if he spread word of this. Wandering immortals were lofty individuals in the Jade Ruins Realms, but the lowest on the totem pole elsewhere.","Lu Yun being only foundation establishment, but able to evenly match the possessed Ouyang Shengtian answered a lot of questions.","“How comfortable are you with this body now?” Lu Yun changed the topic.","“Eighty percent. Ouyang Shengtian’s foundations are good and I stand a chance of becoming a full immortal with him” The other didn’t give his true name as he was Ouyang Shengtian now.","Lu Yun nodded. Ouyang Shengtian did indeed possess strong potential to receive Bloodbath’s approval and be on par with a connate fragrance constitution.","“As for you... a mere Jade Ruins Realms is no stage for you,” said Ouyang Shengtian.","Lu Yun smiled noncommittally. Although the current Ouyang Shengtian possessed the boy’s memories, he was in essence, a different person. The Ouyang and Lu Clans were enemies, but the Ouyang Shengtian in front of him was not.","“I’ve discovered some interesting things in Ouyang Shengtian’s memories,” the young man smiled mysteriously at Lu Yun.","“It has to do with some powerful faction who has my family in their sights, doesn’t it?” Lu Yun curled his lip.","“So you know,” Ouyang Shengtian paused."]},{"number":2248,"title":"Chapter 2248: Chapter 2174.2: Possession","paragraphs":["Chapter 2174.2: Possession","“How would I not know about the family’s enemy? I just don’t know where they’re from. Trust me, Ouyang Shengtian doesn’t know either.” Lu Yun rubbed his forehead with resignation. Weakness was the original sin. Although he’d been very powerful in the past, he was very weak now.","“The past Ouyang Shengtian didn’t know, but the present Ouyang Shengtian does,” the young man grinned.","“Who?” Lu Yun brightened.","“I can tell you,” Ouyang Shengtian raised a brow. “But you need to tell me who your master is.”","His expression turned solemn. He’d thought that Lu Yun was a simple genius, but the young man’s battle technique showed signs of being tempered and forged endless times. He was no different from the genius disciples of some of the most stunning clans or sects.","Lu Yun would not have this level of accomplishment if it wasn’t for a powerful master giving him pointers.","“My master?” Lu Yun’s lips turned upward and he pointed his right hand at the sky.","“As I thought, an immortal.” Ouyang Shengtian looked grave. “He must be an immortal from a domineering faction. In that case, I can tell you.”","Although he’d once been a wandering immortal, he hadn’t been a true immortal. He was stronger than awakened cultivators, but would be no match for a regular immortal. There was a wide chasm between immortals and mortals. Failing to reach true immortality meant that one could not vie with immortals, even if one was a wandering immortal.","“Great Xia, the Origin Sect,” Ouyang Shengtian uttered.","“Great Xia?!” Lu Yun trembled, a strange look appearing in his eyes.","“You know Great Xia?” Ouyang Shengtian remained calm. Since it was an immortal behind Lu Yun, it wasn’t that surprising that the young man knew about Great Xia.","“To think that it still exists!” A smile floated onto Lu Yun’s face.","“Great Xia has stood for one hundred thousand years and boasts of three thousand cultivation worlds beneath its banner. It rules over one hundred and eight thousand cultivation empires and dominates the four lands. How would it not exist?” Ouyang Shengtian spoke of Great Xia with immense reverence. That was the master of this land and the Jade Ruins Realm just one of its worlds.","Lu Yun nodded without protest.","“If my guess is right, the Miss Feng residing as your guest also hails from Great Xia. She looks to be a member of the royal family.” Ouyang Shengtian looked at Lu Yun again.","“That’s my guess as well,” Lu Yun nodded. How else would he have been able to go head-to-head with the Nineheavens Pagoda if not for Fengxian Wu’s presence? One had to know that the Nineheavens Pagoda was more than what it seemed. The Origin Sect backed it.","Ouyang Shengtian couldn’t tell what the Lu young master was thinking.","“The Ouyang Clan has suffered significant blows in recent times,” he suddenly brought up. “I know it’s your people taking action from the shadows. Now that I’ve taken possession of Ouyang Shengtian, I will become him and the leader of the clan. I wish for you to stop targeting the Ouyangs.”","No matter who Ouyang Shengtian had once been, he’d formed a karmic tie to the boy after taking possession of him. He would be struck with future misfortune if he didn’t repay the debt. He had his own enemies as well and needed to hide from them with a new identity.","“That’s simple enough. I will not move against the Ouyangs so long so you are not my enemy.” Lu Yun nodded after thinking it over. Ouyang Shengtian was extremely frightening after being taken possession by a wandering immortal. It would be unwise to be enemies with him—it was always better to have an additional friend as opposed to an enemy.","“Be enemies with you?” Ouyang Shengtian shrugged. “It’s the Origin Sect on one side and an overwhelming immortal on the other. It would be very painful to be caught between the two of you, so I might as well stay out of it.”","Lu Yun could already match him at only mid foundation establishment. There weren’t many characters like him to be found in even Great Xia. Would an immortal not value a genius that they’d invested so much into developing?","As for the Origin Sect... Worlds of cultivation had their own rules. Any sect powerhouse that dared break the rules would have to endure Great Xia’s fury. Otherwise, the Origin Sect would’ve openly moved against Lu Tianling when they discovered where he was.","Lu Yun nodded and took out a transmission spirit stone from his storage ring, sending a message to Bloodbath. That finally set Ouyang Shengtian at ease. To be honest, he wasn’t very confident in his chances against Bloodbath.","The two conversed a while longer before Ouyang Shengtian left in a streak of sword light.","......","“Great Xia... so it’s still there! Grandfather comes from Great Xia too! But I’ve never heard of the Origin Sect—it’s probably a newly risen sect,” Lu Yun murmured to himself as he looked to the northern sky. That was one of the worlds that he’d been born into among the three thousand.","“I wonder if they’re still there... As for Ouyang Shengtian... heh.” Lu Yun sat quietly on the ground, a paramount spirit stone in his hand as he slowly recovered his Hongmeng qi.","Hongmeng qi was so pure that only thirty percent of it had been exhausted in his two hour battle with Ouyang Shengtian.","Lu Yun slowly opened his eyes after four hours. The sun hung in the west and dusk shrouded the land. An enormous aura suddenly descended from the sky and a figure of pale blue arrived over Lu Yun’s head.","“You’re finally here. You’re much slower than I expected.” Lu Yun remained cross-legged on the ground and didn’t lift his head.","“You knew I was going to come?” The newcomer blinked.","“Didn’t I do everything to ensure that you’d come?” Lu Yun raised his head with a radiant grin.","The newcomer was a middle-aged man in his thirties. Fair skinned and clean shaven, his aura was so domineering that the qi in the surroundings were forced away. He was a soul separation powerhouse.","Soul separation cultivators were also hailed as gods of the land. They were half step immortals and could split their consciousness into multiple strands, coalescing images of themselves to walk the land. They were heavyweights of fifth rank cultivation empires.","“A little boy at foundation establishment,” frowned the man. “Even geniuses need time to develop, but you don’t have any anymore.”","He sent a ray of sword light at Lu Yun’s head.","A casual blow from a soul separation powerhouse could obliterate ten Ouyang Shengtians after possession. Although what Lu Yun had done in the Beast Colosseum wasn’t widely known through Darklake, the Nineheavens Pagoda had reported it to the Origin Sect. Once the sect learned of everything, they set their sights on Lu Yun.","This soul separation powerhouse was from the origin Sect. He wasn’t a direct subordinate, but from a fifth rank empire.","“What a pity that they sent only a soul separation cultivator. It’d be more worth it if they sent an awakened cultivator or wandering immortal.” Reluctance shone in Lu Yun’s eyes. He’d put on such a heaven defying display—capturing nascent soul cultivators at foundation establishment—but attracted only a soul separation cultivator.”","That level might be enough to overwhelm most, but it was far from sufficient in his eyes.","Wham!","A blue wind gusted around Lu Yun’s body as a blue seal flickered in and out of sight. It crushed the domineering ray of sword light.","The Seal of the Multitude!","The enormous goodwill that he’d absorbed at the Lings was stored within the seal; he hadn’t used it to elevate his cultivation. It was also impossible for him to use a connate treasure at his current level.","But there were always exceptions. If he burned some of the goodwill and used it to compel the rest of the reserves, he was able to call upon part of that strength.","Everything he did was for this one blow.","Bam!","The Seal of the Multitude hovered over the powerhouse’s head after destroying his sword light.","“What is this?!” he gasped with horror. The suffocating feeling of death loomed over him and he couldn’t move. Never had he guessed that an ant he could’ve snuffed out with a finger would suddenly turn into a massive dragon!","The seal froze him in the sky, enabling Lu Yun to approach him.","“It doesn’t matter who you were before. From now on, you are Lu Yi,” Lu Yun cackled and sent a talisman into the center of the man’s forehead. Hand seals flying, Hongmeng qi streamed out of his body and into the runes etched into the powerhouse.","The soon-to-be Lu Yi stared with eyes wide open, terror filling them. His life force blazed vibrantly.","“Mm, initial soul separation. That’s sufficient.” When Lu Yun tapped the man’s forehead with his finger, Lu Yi’s eyes instantly dulled and he seemed to be more like a walking dead. “Not bad, not bad. The body of a soul separation cultivator retains some of its sentience when it’s turned into a talisman puppet! Now that’s a happy surprise.”","He drifted to the ground after withdrawing his hand seals. Up in the sky, the look in the soul separation cultivator’s eyes returned to normal and he landed expressionlessly next to Lu Yun. His runes vanished with a shimmer, making him appear the same as an ordinary person.","Talisman puppets were one of his most marvelous inventions as a talisman grandmaster. They refined the living alive, making them wish for death. It was a most cruel act that retained all of their cultivation, memories, and experience. The victim became an invincible pawn and did not know fear or pain.","While it was a heartless invention, Lu Yun never showed mercy to his enemies. Since the soul separation cultivator had decided to kill a stranger, he had to be ready to be killed at any time.","“That used up one third of the goodwill in the seal!” Lu Yun lamented. It’d been a slight waste to burn goodwill for a soul separation cultivator, but he hadn’t had any better options.","“I’m in no hurry to enhance my cultivation. Refining the five elements to consolidate my foundation is the most pressing task at hand. If my guess is right, part of the Mindful Immortal Potentate’s treasure is in Yong Heyu’s hands. The treasure of an immortal potentate is enough to send even immortals into a frenzy.” Lu Yun licked his lips.","The Mindful Immortal Potentate was a famous sword immortal in the world of immortals. His Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons had been unmatched. Additionally, Lu Yun somehow felt that the technique had a lot to do with him. He had to lay hands on it no matter what.","As for the dao weapon? Given enough time, he’d forge one for himself.","“Since Great Xia still exists, then what I’ve left there should also still remain.” The look in his eyes grew deep."]},{"number":2249,"title":"Chapter 2249: Chapter 2175.1: Tiger Suppression Pass","paragraphs":["Chapter 2175.1: Tiger Suppression Pass","Things were calm over the subsequent days and nothing of note took place.","With Lu Xiaochi emerging from seclusion to take the helm, Lu Yun couldn’t be bothered exerting the same effort as before for the family’s affairs. He spent his days in his typical indolence and lackadaisical pleasure seeking.","Nor did the Origin Sect send more people against him. In their view, a soul separation powerhouse was more than enough for a foundation establishment boy.","Jiang Feng and Mo Qiyue headed for the Profound Wing Empire.","......","It was a starry night with no sign of the moon, Lu Yun sat in his yard with a jar of wine. The bleak autumn wind howled through the trees—mid autumn was upon the world.","“What a pity that the memories of my three thousand lifetimes are independent of each other. It would be so helpful if they were interconnected and could be referenced against each other.” Lu Yun’s straight brows drew together as he laughed ruefully at himself.","In his current state, he was just the collection of memories from three thousand powerhouses. While they were rich in experiences, they could not be overlaid on each other.","Storing the memories of three thousand people in one mind was a vastly different concept to one person retaining their own memories and reincarnating three thousand times. The horrors of the latter far exceeded the former.","Each of Lu Yun’s three thousand lifetimes saw different accomplishments that were for better or worse. More important was the cultivation of his mind and heart. He brought back only an additional portion of experience from each of his reincarnations—his mind and heart didn’t undergo any changes. It was like he’d experienced three thousand dreams. He still needed to cultivate from the beginning.","However, he instinctively sensed that the memories of three thousand lifetimes were to suppress his initial memories. Their purpose was to turn him into a pristine sheet of paper and forget about the past.","Each lifetime left a mark of reincarnation that stamped another seal over his past.","If he wanted to connect all of the memories to each other, that would be the mental equivalent of yet another reincarnation. It wouldn’t help his sealed memories at all.","The three thousand reincarnations were the heavenly dao’s tutelage for its newest disciple. All of Lu Yun’s skills were a function of the heavenly dao passing them to him through the reincarnations.","“It’s time that I broke through.” Lu Yun slowly refined a ball of connate fire origin in his hand and called upon the Seal of the Multitude. A moderate surge of goodwill flowed out of it and melded into his dantian.","Boom!","His Hongmeng qi trembled and turned viscous while his dantian and meridians enlarged.","Latter foundation establishment.","“I can use goodwill to raise my cultivation however I like when I’m foundation establishment, but I probably won’t be able to do that when I’m golden core and nascent soul.” Lu Yun knew where his limits would be after taking stock of his condition.","As marvelous as goodwill was, it was fundamentally different from the energy of heaven and earth. Based on what his senior brother had said, goodwill was just a supplemental force as it still fell to Lu Yun himself to break through the bottlenecks.","Of that, Lu Yun was well aware. He could even vaguely sense that he’d cultivated in a similar way in his sealed memories.","Qi refinement and foundation establishment were the accumulation of strength. Golden core, nascent soul, and above focused on the comprehension of heavenly dao.","Such was Lu Yun’s underlying goal.","“Looks like I need to find a time to visit Great Xia. The Jade Ruins Realm is just fringe territory, one of the most impoverished worlds of cultivation there is. It’s a ninth rank world that requires the administration of wandering immortals. I bet there aren’t any wandering immortals in Great Xia,” Lu Yun mused to himself as he toyed with his wine cup.","One of the major benefits of practicing the Nine Chapters of Dao was that anything he did was the natural course of nature. Even drinking wine in his yard was following the heavenly dao and enabled him to break through.","“Hmm? Seven Kills, Greedy Wolf, Army... And there’s the Taisui and Yinghuo...” Lu Yun bounced up from his stool and stared at the night sky.","Seven Kills, Greedy Wolf, Army, Taisui, and Yinghuo were the five stars of disaster and ill omen. Normally unobservable and hidden deep within the cosmos, the appearance of a single one heralded inauspicious tidings. All five appearing at the same time shocked Lu Yun beyond belief.","“Wait, no, no. The five stars counter and complement each other. If only four were present, then this world or Great Xia would soon be rocked by unrest. But with five appearing, they maintain a delicate balance that ensures everything is fine.” Lu Yun made swift calculations as he tilted his head up at the sky.","Appearance of the five unpropitious stars wouldn’t raise a disturbance in the world. Not many cultivators nursed this kind of interest.","“Hmm?” Lu Yun narrowed his eyes. “Didn’t the Mindful Immortal Potentate in the world of immortals gain a treasure that was coveted by the immortal emperor in the central celestial court? The five immortal kings of Seven Kills, Greedy Wolf, Army, Taisui, and Yinghuo deployed their respective star’s power to suppress the potentate. What the Mindful Immortal Potentate obtained was a tower... The Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons, Iron Pagoda Mountain, the five stars...”","!!!","Lu Yun nearly leapt to his feet.","“No way! Can it be that the Iron Pagoda Mountain of the Profound Wing Empire is the potentate’s treasure?! Although he wasn’t an immortal king, he caused the mutual destruction of five immortal kings with the pagoda. After his demise, the pagoda vanished as well...","“That’s right, the five stars in the heavens must be attracted to the residual power of the five immortal kings around the treasure. Yong Heyu has revealed the dao weapon at this precise moment so he can lure powerful cultivators to the mountain. He wants to use their strength to cut through the power of the immortal kings and claim the pagoda!”","Lu Yun strung everything together. The era that he’d once reincarnated into could not be determined. In this day and age, the entire world of immortals had vanished and been reduced to a myth, so it was logical that the power of its immortal kings had been degraded through the long passage of time.","“Even if the Iron Pagoda Mountain isn’t the one that killed the Mindful Immortal Potentate, it must be related. It looks like I'm headed there after all.” Lu Yun licked his lips. “Power leaking from the immortal kings has called the five stars to reveal themselves. Looks like we’re not far from the treasure truly coming out into the light.”","Lu Yun craved everything about the Mindful Immortal Potentate, whether it was the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons or the Iron Pagoda Mountain. While the Mindful Immortal Potentate’s title was immortal potentate, he’d defeated numerous immortal kings in his time. He was the greatest immortal potentate of the world of immortals in both deed and name.","The central immortal emperor had had to send out the five most premier immortal kings of the world to bring him down. They only completed their mission through dying with the immortal potentate. Even the immortal emperor was gravely injured after the fact.","......","The second day.","“Lu Xuan, what are your thoughts now?” Lu Yun asked his guard while he ate breakfast in the yard.","“I have thought it through. Lu Xuan is willing to give up his cultivation to practice the young master’s methods.” Lu Xuan looked firmly back at the young man.","Lu Xuan’s potential was extremely poor; he’d made it to golden core purely through Lu Tianling’s secret arts. Although his battle strength was on par with a golden core cultivator, there was no possibility for him to ever advance again.","Lu Yun constantly wanted to increase the cultivation of those around him, including Lu Xuan. But Lu Xuan was utterly loyal to Lu Yun, so he hesitated when he heard that the requirement was to sever his previous cultivation.","After he saw the young master defeat nascent soul powerhouses with a few simple moves, however, he hesitated no longer. He was Lu Yun’s guard, but he wouldn’t be able to do anything if they met real danger, due to his cultivation of initial golden core.","“This is the Sword of Slaughter Record, it walks the path of slaughter. Train in it and go to Bloodbath when you reach foundation establishment. He’ll make further arrangements for you.” Lu Yun handed a jade slip to Lu Xuan and dismissed the guard.","“Are you leaving Dark City?” A Lu Xiaochi in high spirits came to Lu Yun after Lu Xuan left.","Upon breaking the Severed Meridians Hold and advancing in his cultivation, the Lu second master issued a series of challenges throughout the capital. He fought every latter nascent soul powerhouse in the great families, apart from the Lings that’d been nearly exterminated.","He only lost to the newly possessed Ouyang Shengtian by half a step, making him top three in nascent spirit powerhouses of Darklake Empire. And this was simply due to his lack of familiarity with the Major Five Elements Demolition Godslayer Record.","“I want to go stretch my legs,” Lu Yun nodded and didn’t answer with the truth. He didn’t want his second uncle to go to the Profound Wing Empire. It was highly likely that it would be a very perilous and bloody trip given the background behind the Iron Pagoda Mountain. Great Xia experts might even appear at the end.","“Oh right, second uncle, if you feel that there’s not enough of a challenge in Darklake powerhouses, you should visit the Celestial Realm Battlefront. That’s where all of the geniuses in the worlds are gathered.”","“The Celestial Realm Battlefront!” Lu Xiaochi took a deep breath and smiled wryly, “I’d have to join a mid rank empire faction if I want to visit the Celestial Realm Battlefront.”","“That’s easy enough, we’ve got a mover and shaker living at home. Ask her.” Lu Yun pointed at the house next door.","“You mean Miss Fengxian? She’s just golden core,” Lu Xiaochi blinked.","Apart from being part of a fourth rank or above cultivation empire, one needed to be stronger than nascent soul. Golden core cultivators were prohibited from entry into the Celestial Realm Battlefront.","“She may just be golden core, but her identity is sufficient to take you into the battlefront,” Lu Yun smiled.","“Alright, I’ll ask her for help.” Lu Xiaochi turned on his heel and left.","“The Fengxians... so Fengxian Wu is from that family,” Lu Yun sighed with emotion.","When he reincarnated into Great Xia, the Fengxians were just a tiny family content with their tiny part of the world. Who would’ve thought that they’d grow to the point where a single disciple could lay down the law in a world of cultivation?","While the law enforcers of the Jade Ruins Realm were scattered throughout the three ninth rank empires, they were subordinates of the Great Xia royalty and the true masters of the Jade Ruins Realms.","Any of them, even an ordinary enforcer, had no need to bow and scrape before an ordinary Great Xia faction. Only the dynasty’s most supreme forces inspired fear and reverence. Ouyang Shengtian had said that it was highly likely Fengxian Wu was from the royal family.","A family that called itself royal required the presence of titled kings.","“With the world of immortals gone missing, who bestows titles now?” Lu Yun curled his lip. But the process of conferring titles... seemed a bit familiar.","etvolare's Thoughts","Lol I'm guessing immortal king > immortal potentate. Yay shoving an entire backstory of new characters into the middle of a chapter."]},{"number":2250,"title":"Chapter 2250: Chapter 2175.2: Tiger Suppression Pass","paragraphs":["Chapter 2175.2: Tiger Suppression Pass","Lu Yun left Dark City after three more days and some preparation.","Fengxian Wu was wholly unconcerned with affairs in the world of cultivation. She normally stayed in and refused to set foot through the Lu front doors. Instead of a tourist, she seemed more like a young lady sheltered from the world.","Only Lu Yun made the trip this time.","Profound Wing Empire was located to the north of Dark Empire; the two were the greatest vassals of Darklake Empire. However, Profound Wing was less than Dark as the latter boasted of Lu Tianling.","Lu Tianling had fled to Dark Empire when he was gravely injured and hid his cultivation while he recovered. Dark Empire became his springboard into Darklake Empire. After arriving in Darklake, he leveraged his new position to secretly develop his faction and take revenge.","Lu Tianling exercised utmost prudence and avoided entering a higher level cultivation empire because those were directly controlled by the heavenly book in the Celestial Realm Battlefront. It would be very difficult for him to do anything under those circumstances.","While Darklake also fell under its purview, the book was weaker here and Lu Tianling could hide from its detection through special methods.","Since Dark Empire sheltered Lu Tianling in his time of need, he naturally returned the favor in kind. Dark Empire and Profound Wing Empire were the two major vassals of Darklake Empire, but they shared an adversarial relationship with each other.","This was purposefully fostered by Darklake. For one, it was a constant drain on both sides and ensured that neither would ever be able to challenge Darklake’s control. Secondly, continuous warfare facilitated the rise of genius talent in both nations. Once they grew into their power, they were retrieved by Darklake to enhance the empire’s own strength.","As for how to keep these people in check and ensure that they swore fealty to Darklake—that was up to the methods and charisma of those who ruled.","Nascent soul cultivators were few and far in between in second rank nations. There were no more than five or six in the past thousand years.","Lu Yun’s goal was very apparent—the Iron Pagoda Mountain in the western reaches of the Profound Wing Empire. He flew on the back of his sword and barged about madly, making no effort to cover his tracks. The young man rather hoped that he’d run into more Origin Sect powerhouses along the way. More talisman puppets were always welcome.","Profound Wing Empire was five hundred thousand kilometers west of Dark City. Cultivators traveled fifty kilometers in one breath when they utilized a flying sword, so they covered thousands of kilometers a day in this transport mode.","Lu Yun’s Hongmeng qi was many times higher quality than regular true origin and could be expended without reservation. Thus, his speed was on par with latter golden core powerhouses.","Ordinary golden core experts needed roughly a month to travel from Dark City to Profound Wing Empire. Lu Yun was close to the western border of Darklake after approximately twenty days; he flew over mountain ranges that stretched on without end.","It was a barren place with few signs of inhabitation. Even qi was sparse in the surroundings. The frontier was often hard and desolate territory, a far cry from the prosperity of the heartland.","“Oh?” Lu Yun paused in mid air.","Humm!","A loud hum exploded in the void as soon as he stopped and a strong surge of power gathered from all sides.","“Hahaha, little boy, didn’t your parents tell you that you can’t fly around in the mountains of Tiger Suppression Pass?” sounded an extremely rough force. Following that, more than one hundred cultivators appeared out of nowhere and blotted out the sky. A brute in black and sporting a curly mustache laughed loudly at Lu Yun.","“Oh? Tiger Suppression Pass?” Lu Yun blinked. “This is Tiger Suppression Pass, where the Darklake army slaughtered Tianlong’s million-strong armies?”","Tiger Suppression Pass was the site of the final battle between the Darklake and Tianlong Empire. There were nearly two million combined fatalities of cultivators over foundation establishment, which meant the pass should’ve been drowning in resentment. Contrary to expectation, all it was was just a little more barren than usual.","“Chief, the child seems scared stiff. Look at his clothes—they’re all fine rank treasures! He must come from a big family and they must be rich! He’s a fat sheep!” A middle-aged man with a sharp chin and hollow cheeks sized up Lu Yun, clucking his tongue with appreciation.","“Little boy, don’t think of using your background to scare me. There aren’t many people at Tiger Suppression Pass and if you die here, you die without anyone knowing, even if you’re one of Darklake’s princes! If you know what’s good for you, you’ll hand over your clothing and storage ring! I will consider leaving you with an intact corpse then!” Curly Mustache cut Lu Yun off when the latter opened his mouth to speak.","“Let me ask you something, how come there isn’t any resentment or yin qi in this pass when two million soldiers have died here?” Lu Yun asked curiously, ignoring the bandits.","“Huh?” Curly Mustache paused. What was the child asking this for? “Who am I supposed to ask about that?”","Curly Mustache was utterly confused. Tiger Suppression Pass was an ordinary place, made famous only because of the great battle between the two empires twenty years ago.","Just as Lu Yun said, any other locale would be a den of ghosts if two million cultivators had died there. But Tiger Suppression Pass appeared normal, completely sans malice.","“Chief, what are we wasting time with him for??” The skinny man next to Curly Mustache couldn’t sit still and approached Lu Yun in a flash of sword light.","“Heh heh, kid, you—” Terror filled the skinny man’s face. A fair hand was wrapped around his neck.","“A bandit of initial golden core? You train the most boring of methods, how dare you throw your weight around in front of this young master?” Lu Yun curled his lip. Not even the noble scions of Dark Orchid dared be this arrogant in front of him. How dare a mere golden core wandering cultivator saunter up to him for a robbery?","Curly Mustache’s eyes widened in dismay, but he wasn’t afraid of the lad since he was initial nascent soul.","“So you’re a tough mark. Let Xiuya go and we’ll let you go as well!” A keen light shone in Curly Mustache’s eyes.","“Let me go?” Lu Yun shook his head. “You people appearing so suddenly means that you own something like a space treasure, and a high level one at that. Give it to me and swear you loyalty. I’ll let you live then.”","“Hahahaha!!” some of the cultivators burst into uproarious laughter. What had the boy just said to two hundred cultivators above foundation establishment, a dozen golden cores, and one nascent soul powerhouse? He was completely insane!","“I think you want to die, kid!” roared a latter golden core bandit. He ignored Xiuya in Lu Yun’s grip and fired a ray of sword light from his mouth, wanting to take off Lu Yun’s head.","“What a fool,” Lu Yun snorted. His right hand was preoccupied with Xiuya’s neck, so he gripped the sword light with his left. It was an upper fine rank flying sword.","Crack!","He crushed it to pieces with a slight clench of his hand.","Pfft!","A treasure was directly connected to a cultivator’s heart and mind. Hence, the shattering of the flying sword dealt grave injuries to the cultivator.","Cultivators and immortals of Great Xia wouldn’t rely on treasures so heavily, Lu Yun thought as he looked at the suffering golden core bandit. As much as a treasure could increase a cultivator’s strength, over reliance on them led to stagnation of the self.","A Great Xia golden core cultivator would dominate all cultivators in this world, up to and including nascent soul. Far from over exaggeration, it was a sign of how fatal reliance of treasures was. As opposed to humans utilizing treasures, it was more like treasures wielding humans. Flying swords were also part of supplemental dao.","The cultivators of Great Xia, however, focused more on cultivation of the body. Treasures were external items, after all, purely meant to be a helping hand. Of course, this didn’t mean that Great Xia cultivators didn’t use treasures, just that they didn’t rely on them as much.","Certain heaven-defying ones still elicited a bloody battle for them.","According to Lu Yun’s understanding, the current world of cultivation was in the basic stage of cultivation. Great Xia had started to evolve beyond that to reach a higher stage. He’d also risen beyond the basic stage when he reincarnated through his lives. Even when he reached Great Xia, he was invincible among his peers and could challenge those higher level than him. The experience of three thousand reincarnations and the power of Hongmeng qi were not to be underestimated.","Thus, he didn’t pay any attention to the two hundred cultivators below him.","“Who are you?!” Curly Mustache’s eyes almost fell out of his head when he saw Lu Yun crush an upper rank fine weapon with his bare hands. He wasn’t able to do anything like that!","“You’ll naturally find out when you swear allegiance to me.” Lu Yun casually threw Xiuya away. Given the man’s cultivation level, he would be fine despite the drop of three hundred meters.","Whoosh!","A black blade swung at Lu Yun’s face—Curly Mustache made his move alongside the cultivators behind him. A messy array of flying swords and weapons shot at Lu Yun.","The young man shook his head and twisted his body slightly. Countless sparks flared around him and formed blades of fire that radiated in all directions.","Pfft pfft pfft pfft!","The blades of fire easily rebuffed the treasures.","“It looks like you will not submit if I do not demonstrate my might!” Lu Yun snorted and formed hand seals, turning the blades of fire into a crimson whirlwind. It was nine meters across and three hundred meters tall. Whirling with baleful fury, it swiftly sucked into a few dozen cultivators and spat them to the ground in an incapacitated state.","“You court death!” Curly Mustache howled and smashed his weapon at the whirlwind.","BOOM!","etvolare's Thoughts","Why yes, when I see a whirlwind of literal fire, my first instinct is to smack it with my blade as well. Wtf lol. This guy needs to be renamed to No Brains.","As opposed to humans utilizing treasures, it was more like treasures wielding humans. That's deep."]},{"number":2251,"title":"Chapter 2251: Chapter 2176.1: The Malice That Opposes the Heavenly Dao","paragraphs":["Chapter 2176.1: The Malice That Opposes the Heavenly Dao","The black blade raised a remarkable commotion when it crashed into Lu Yun’s fiery whirlwind, but a staggering consequence resulted instead. Curly Mustache’s fine rank weapon turned into a puddle of metallic water within a few breaths.","The man paled to see his treasure ruined.","“You have the balls to set a mid fine rank weapon against Aureate Bird Truefire?” Lu Yun curled his lip dismissively.","The fiery whirlwind was deployed from the fire of the Aureate Bird Cauldron. Also known as Sol Truefire, it was incredibly domineering and completely overpowered a regular fine rank treasure when reinforced by the Hongmeng true qi in Lu Yun’s body.","“Do you submit?” Lu Yun dismissed the whirlwind, leaving only him and Curly Mustache in the air. The others had been swept to the ground—while they were sorely injured, their lives were in no danger.","Right now, Lu Yun lacked people and his own secret forces. Though he vaguely felt that there was no point to him doing so, he still instinctively wanted to protect the Lu Clan. As useless as these bandits were, even trash could be used in Lu Yun’s eyes.","“The gentleman is undeniably strong. Wu Zhen submits.” Curly Mustache didn’t dare do anything else after seeing that his weapon had been destroyed and his men were unable to muster any resistance.","“Talk about your background. What’s a lofty nascent soul powerhouse doing as a bandit in Tiger Suppression Pass?” Lu Yun looked on with interest.","Wu Zhen glanced at the young man, then sighed.","“I was once the patriarch of the Wu Clan in the Skymoon Empire—vassal to the Tainlong Empire. After Tianlong lost to Darklake twenty years ago, rumors somehow circulated that my family colluded with Darklake and sold them intelligence regarding Tianlong, leading to my nation’s loss.","“My clan was exterminated for it and I managed to escape due to my latter golden core cultivation. Since arriving at the pass, I’ve stayed busy accumulating my strength in hopes of obtaining revenge.” Pain filled Wu Zhen’s face when he recounted his past.","The Wu Clan was once the greatest family in the Skymoon Empire, second to only the royal family. Being peak latter golden core, Wu Zhen stood a high chance of breaking through to nascent soul. He would be immensely valued in Tianlong Empire and his family’s standing greatly increased as a result.","Yet now, he’d been reduced to struggling for survival in Tiger Suppression Pass. Though he’d ascended to a nascent soul cultivator like he’d hoped for, he was a bandit.","“In that case, why don’t you throw yourself under Darklake’s banner and borrow them to enact vengeance? Isn’t that better?” Lu Yun asked with a half smile. Although peace reigned in the world, Darklake and Tianlong were irreconcilable rivals who continued to clash in their hinterlands.","“If... I throw myself under Darklake’s banner... I can join the army and have my revenge, but it doesn’t seem likely that Darklake is able to destroy Tianlong.” Dense killing intent suffused Wu Zhen’s eyes.","“You want to destroy Tianlong?” Lu Yun hadn’t thought that a mere nascent soul cultivator would harbor the ambition of destroying a third rank cultivation nation. “That’d be a bit difficult, and Tianlong’s superior nation would never permit you to do so.”","“How do you know if you don’t try?” Wu Zhen looked at Lu Yun and suddenly knelt in the void. “I know the gentleman comes from uncommon origins. If you help me obtain revenge, I will tell you the greatest secret of Tiger Suppression Pass!”","“The secret of Tiger Suppression Pass?” Lu Yun brightened, he was very interested in the local terrain. Not only was there no resentment despite two million souls dying here, but these two hundred bandits had the ability to suddenly appear in the sky.","“Your men are fine, you should help them first.” He waved Wu Zhen off, neither agreeing nor disagreeing.","On tenterhooks, Wu Zhen quickly landed and helped his men up. Lu Yun had shown them mercy—if he’d erupted with the full force of Aureate Truefire, all two hundred of them would be dead.","However, the young man was also aware that these bandits were wandering cultivators, versed in only unorthodox tricks and incomplete methods. Their battle strength was weak; he’d have a much harder time if they were geniuses from the various sects or clans.","Wu Zhen tended to all of his men after an hour and gave them pills and medicines to recover. Tiger Suppression Pass was sparse in ambient qi and once a battlefield—few passed through the area. Having made this area their home, the bandits normally operated on the fringes of Profound Wing Empire. They very rarely trespassed into Darklake Empire. Given Lu Yun’s blatant passage through their territory, the bandits naturally wouldn’t let him go free.","After Wu Zhen settled his men, he presented himself to Lu Yun again.","“Out with it, what secrets does Tiger Suppression Pass harbor?” Lu Yun sat lazily on the ground and leaned against a tree.","“So you’ve agreed?” Wu Zhen brightened.","“Tianlong Empire is enemies with my Darklake to begin with. It would be good for Darklake if you can become the emperor,” Lu Yun nodded.","“So you’re from Darklake...” The bottom fell out of Wu Zhen’s stomach when he heard Lu Yun’s response.","“So what if I am?” Lu Yun smiled.","Wu Zhen trembled, thinking back to the young man’s earlier prowess. Lu Yun took out a jade slip from his storage ring and tossed it to the man.","“Imprint your nascent soul in this jade slip and become one of mine. I will take revenge for you then and help you become the Tianlong emperor.”","“A nascent soul jade slip!” Wu Zhen shuddered. Those were only found in high rank cultivation empires. Some factions used them to curtail newly recruited subordinates or enslave people for the mines. Once his nascent soul was branded into the jade slip, it would take a simple thought from his master for him to fly apart into dust.","The jade slip was only applicable to those above nascent soul. Golden core and below didn’t possess such a part of them.","“Ah...” Wu Zhen hesitated.","“What, are you not willing?” Lu Yun sneered. “Either you imprint your nascent soul into the slip, or you die. I have a hundred ways to extract what I want from your memories.”","Wu Zhen wanted to cry, why had he run into such an unreasonable fellow? He had no other choice but to channel his mind into the jade slip.","“Master.” His expression became much more docile after the brand was made.","“Tell me about the secrets here.” Lu Yun put the jade slip back into his storage ring.","Wu Zhen chuckled ruefully. He’d wanted to lure Lu Yun there and use its strength to kill the young man. Who would’ve thought a nascent soul jade talisman would appear to completely knock his plans awry?","On the other hand, how would a wily old fox of three thousand reincarnations fail to see through Wu Zhen’s true intent? Lu Yun wouldn’t have brought out the jade slip had the man truly bent the knee.","“There’s an enormous seed storage at the bottom of Tiger Suppression Pass. Us Thundercloud Bandits live in that seed storage. I found its seed stone by accident when I first arrived at the pass. It’s the key to entering and owning the seed storage.” Wu Zhen was someone who appeared coarse on the outside, but was very shrewd at heart. However, with the nascent soul jade talisman in Lu Yun’s hands, he didn’t dare bring any of his schemes to play. He took out a crystalline structure the size of a fist and gave it to the young man.","“This is the seed stone that you speak of?” Lu Yun blinked at the object.","A seed stone was the heart of a seed storage—to possess it meant owning the entire storage. One had complete flexibility in movement—no wonder Wu Zhen was unwilling to swear fealty to Darklake and preferred to secretly expand his forces here.","“Correct, that is the seed stone. But for some reason, I’ve been unable to refine it no matter how I tried.” Wu Zhen smiled ruefully. If he had full control over the seed stone, he would’ve darted back into the seed storage instead of bowing his head to Lu Yun.","“This isn’t a seed stone,” Lu Yun shook his head. “Not even immortals would be able to refine this, to say nothing of you.”","“What...” Wu Zhen gaped.","“This is the key to a cross ark.” Lu Yun toyed with the crystalline stone, immensely surprised. “The cross ark is a wondroud weapon of Great Xia. What’s it doing here? Or is it...”","“The cross ark?” Wu Zhen asked blankly.","“The cross ark is a weapon of a cultivation dynasty. It’s not a treasure, but something greater,” Lu Yun explained patiently. “There’s an enormous section inside that can contain tens of thousands of cultivators. This crystal is the key to entering it.”","The cross ark itself wasn’t a treasure. The key was one with the ark, which meant that it naturally couldn’t be refined. And... Lu Yun’s eye twitched. There seemed to be something like the cross ark in his sealed memories, but he couldn’t remember exactly what.","He was a bit lost as he didn’t know what was in the sealed memories, only that he wasn’t willing to remember them. He instinctively suppressed them by force of habit, but certain things in this world constantly tugged at him, making him remember despite himself.","Of one thing he was certain, and that was the memories were not of this world or possibly even of this space and time. The dao character in his dantian shook, calming his mind and stilling the stirring memories.","Lu Yun suddenly understood many things.","He’d wanted to seal the memories and the heavenly dao was helping him, but something tirelessly tried to call them back. That thing was full of malice toward Lu Yun.","“No wonder this seed storage looks so strange and is filled with formations. So it’s not a seed storage at all,” Wu Zhen smiled ruefully.","“You wanted to borrow the restrictions and formations inside the cross ark to kill me, didn’t you?” Lu Yun smirked."]},{"number":2252,"title":"Chapter 2252: Chapter 2176.2: The Malice That Opposes the Heavenly Dao","paragraphs":["Chapter 2176.2: The Malice That Opposes the Heavenly Dao","“This humble one would never dare!” Wu Zhen turned ashen.","“Alright, stand guard outside with your men. I’m going into the cross ark to take a look.” Lu Yun infused the crystalline stone with Hongmeng qi before Wu Zhen could respond and disappeared with a flash. When he next appeared, he was inside an enormous space that was three thousand meters across.","“So it is a small cross ark. This one can hold thirty thousand cultivators.” Lu Yun assessed the ship’s internals, finding it very low on qi. There was much more in the barren outside, a sign that the ark was heavily damaged.","He sent his consciousness into the key and used it as a medium to inspect the entire ship.","“The core’s over here.” Lu Yun flashed to another space that held a ponderous object similar to a pill cauldron. It was the core of the ark—a pill cauldron named the cross forge. It was the center of propulsion for the ark and consumed spirit crystals to provide momentum.","Cross arks were enormous constructs that weren’t treasures, so not even immortals were able to manipulate one with their personal strength. They depended on these forges for movement.","“Although this is a small cross ark, its cross forge is an upper rank forge. This ark’s master has an uncommon background—he was very likely an immortal.” The more Lu Yun observed the ark’s core, the more he concluded that the vessel was immensely damaged. There was a terrible sword mark on the cross forge, like someone had pierced it through.","“An upper rank cross ark can certainly withstand an ordinary immortal’s full blow. Did a high level immortal strike it?”","The hulk of a cross ark was an immense treasure by itself. Given enough time, he would be able to repair it.","“The family’s strength will leap forward with this cross ark. It won’t be a problem to advance Darklake forward to another level then.”","Elevating Darklake empire wasn’t the desire of the royal family, but his grandfather Lu Tianling.","His grandfather’s enemy was the Origin Sect of Great Xia, it would be an utter joke to use a cultivation empire’s strength against the sect. Lu Tianling, however, seemed to have other plans. Though Lu Yun didn’t understand them, he would help his grandfather to the best of his abilities.","Lu Yun’s first task at hand was to comprehend heavenly dao. When one sought to do so with a human body, following one’s heart was of paramount importance. What Lu Yun wanted most was to help his grandfather seek revenge.","All valuables in the ruined cross ark had long disappeared, but its formations and restrictions remained powerful.","“Hmm?” A sudden thought struck Lu Yun and he shifted out of the vessel.","“Connate earth origin!” he roared, summoning a layer of yellowish-brown light from his body. Nearby rocks, sand, and dirt were forced to the sides by the energy.","Two beams of yellowish-brown radiance shot out from Lu Yun’s eyes. Covered by connate earth origin energy, everything beneath the land was laid out in front of him.","“This... is... a battlefield?” Lu Yun’s jaw dropped. Carcasses were strewn thirty thousand meters below Tiger Suppression Pass, even a few partial wrecks of cross arks could be found. They were completely ruined as their internal spaces were broken. None were intact like the one he was just in.","Lu Yun shook his head gently. The cross arks were three thousand meters below ground. Even if he had connate earth origin protecting his body, he wasn’t able to dive down that deep. His current cultivation was too weak.","“I have to get down there when I’m stronger. The lack of resentment in the pass very likely has something to do with the battlefield below.” Lu Yun thought for a bit and returned aboveground through his cross ark.","Sounds of fighting drifted into his ear as soon as he materialized.","“How dare you bandits stop this young master’s people! I’ve found your headquarters today and will leave none of you alive!” The furious roar was punctuated by agonized wails.","“Damn it, my new lackeys are dying!” Lu Yun glowered. He’d spent only an hour in the cross ark, but more than half of the bandits were dead and the rest were greatly injured.","A young man roughly twenty years old stood in the air, flanked by two nascent soul cultivators. Thirty-some golden core cultivators were assembled in a formation below and scything through Wu Zhen’s men.","Despite only being thirty odd people, they were highly trained and wielded lower fine rank weapons. Wu Zhen’s motley crew was a far cry from them.","Whoosh!","A golden bird appeared in the sky and wafted heat waves in all directions. Half of the golden core cultivators were swallowed in a single breath.","Who dares!” A keen light glinted in the young man’s eyes.","“How dare you touch this young master’s minions? Are you tired of living?” Lu Yun stood atop the golden bird and raised a provocative eyebrow at the young man.","“Hahahahaha!!” the young man sneered. “You’re not so simple yourself if you can instantly kill some random servants I took under my wing.”","The young man was handsome and fair skinned with a scarlet birthmark in the center of his forehead. The thumb-sized mark twinkled with red light as he laughed.","Lu Yun’s brow turned quizzical when he noticed the mark.","“But you’re the one who’s tired of living after saying that to me.” Instead of taking further action, the young man stared intently at the bird beneath Lu Yun’s feet.","“We’ll see about that!” Lu Yun smirked. Although he’d lived through three thousand lives, he was still the tyrannical good-for-nothing who loved to strut around. Rivers and mountains might be changed, but a man’s nature was hard to alter. Such was Lu Yun’s personality in this life.","He waved his hand and sent out blazing fire from the bird beneath his feet. It reduced the remaining golden core cultivators to ashes with yelps of pain.","“Sol Truefire...” The young man’s eye twitched. “We go!”","He was only golden core himself. Although he had two nascent soul guards by his side, he was no match for Sol Truefire. He immediately abandoned the fight and retreated.","“You want to leave after killing my men? I don’t think so!” Lu Yun directed the bird in chase.","On the ground, Wu Zhen swallowed hard. That young man’s thirty-some golden core cultivators had been sufficient to overrun all two hundred of his men, but they’d died in just a few breaths when Lu Yun made his move.","Sweat soaked Wu Zhen’s back when his thoughts traveled to this point. Had he really lured Lu Yun into the cross ark and used its restrictions against the lad, the only outcome would be Wu Zhen being casually executed after the fact.","......","“Who is that young man? He’s only latter foundation establishment, but he killed three dozen of my men in quick succession!” The young man sped to the west on the back of his sword, escorted by the two nascent soul cultivators.","“Damn it, this guy’s fast with a sword. My cultivation is too weak to get to him.” Lu Yun abandoned the chase when he saw their gap growing wider and returned to Tiger Suppression Pass.","“Master!” Wu Zhen quickly came up to him.","“What’s the situation?” Lu Yun swept a glance at him.","“There are eighty-seven brothers left...” Wu Zhen said dejectedly. These were brothers he’d spent a dozen years with. It quite pained him that only less than ninety were suddenly alive.","“Who were those people?”","“We robbed a young man with a decently illustrious background half a month ago in Profound Wing Empire. This young man is probably that one’s backer,” Wu Zhen cobbled together after thinking for a while and referencing what the young man had said.","“A young man from the Profound Wing Empire?” Lu Yun thought for a bit. “Alright, I’ll take care of this matter. Stay here with your men.”","Wu Zhen blinked; he’d thought that Lu Yun would take them with him.","“This is the key to the cross ark and some other items. Distribute them as you see fit. Remember, I want loyalty!” A cold light sparkled in Lu Yun’s eyes as he tossed a storage ring to Wu Zhen. Given that he held the man’s nascent soul jade slip, he wasn’t afraid of betrayal.","An overjoyed Wu Zhen hastily caught the storage ring. There were spirit stones, cultivation methods, formations, treasures, pills and medicines in abundance inside. It was sufficient supplies for Wu Zhen and his men for a hundred years.","Lu Yun also left a transmission stone to facilitate communication.","“There should be numerous bandits among the borders of the second and third rank empires. Your mission is to dominate them all. Find out a way to develop an intelligence network, one that can keep tabs on the general happenings of nearby nations. You were once a patriarch of a clan, so this shouldn’t be hard for you, no?” Lu Yun instructed.","Wu Zhen’s heart swelled with emotion. What the ring contained was more than one hundred times what the Wu Clan once possessed. With the cross ark as an infallible base, he could absolutely rise again.","After giving a few more instructions, Lu Yun left for the west in a flash of sword light.","Recruiting Wu Zhen was a pure accident. He had too few forces of his own—Wu Zhen was the only one apart from Bloodbath. The elder was sufficient for a third rank nation, but far from enough when the Lus’ enemy came from Great Xia."]},{"number":2253,"title":"Chapter 2253: Chapter 2176.3: The Malice That Opposes the Heavenly Dao","paragraphs":["Chapter 2176.3: The Malice That Opposes the Heavenly Dao","Being the disciple of the heavenly dao and having the experience of three thousand lifetimes under his belt, Lu Yun would be able to turn a pig into an immortal given enough time. Nurturing subordinates wasn’t a matter of handheld instruction. They had to grow through conflict and slaughter, so whether it was Bloodbath and his men, or Wu Zhen and the bandits, he left them to their own devices after giving them sufficient resources.","Lu Yun raised sword light and headed to the west. He slowly left the boundaries of Darklake Empire and entered Profound Wing Empire.","While borders were clearly delineated in the world of cultivation, there were no patrols between nations. Nations valued spirit veins and spirit stone mines. The cultivators of a nation were gathered near these resources, building cities to oversee them. Nations didn’t care about land that held no natural resources, and wars were often fought over spirit veins.","Tiger Suppression Pass, for instance, was an indeterminable distance from the Tianlong Empire, but it’d turned into the site of the final battle between two empires. For cultivators who could fly five hundred kilometers in one breath, borders were a bit of a joke. The only ones they would take seriously was if a formation protected one, but a formation that enclosed an entire nation was too mind-boggling to consider.","......","Iron Pagoda Mountain was a famous mountain in the west of Profound Wing Empire. It was shaped like a pagoda and embedded with high concentrations of valuable fine metal and ore. It was as its name.","Fine metal was uncommonly durable and ideal material to craft flying swords with. Iron Pagoda Mountain, however, was too durable to be damaged. Darklake once sent cultivators to excavate it, but to no avail.","As for fourth rank empires, they didn’t think much of a little bit of fine metal.","Unusual activity thronged around the mountain. Countless cultivators circled around it like groups of mosquitoes and flies. Three thousand meters tall, an enormous sword stroke scored the peak. It was the mark of a dao weapon.","Lu Yun concealed himself when he drew near the mountain and silently observed the surroundings.","“Hahaha, I hear you were recently dealt a huge loss in a third rank empire, Qin Qianxue!” At the bottom of the mountain, a young man in green robes pointed at another young man.","“Hmph,” the other snorted. “Don’t get too cocky, Jiang Feng. As lowly as they are, there are still crouching tigers and hidden dragons among them. That guy’s methods were plainly greater than mine—he probably comes from the same origins as us. It’s not embarrassing to suffer a loss at his hands.”","“He must be quite special if Sir Xue speaks of him like that,” Mo Qiyue said next to Jiang Feng.","“Is ‘White’ here?” Qin Qianxue asked Mo Qiyue.","“He’s not interested in this matter.” Jiang Feng shrugged.","Qin Qianxue looked at the Iron Pagoda Mountain. Innumerable cultivators attacked it with flying swords, but it remained unscathed. Not even a pebble dropped from it.","“Those fools. This mountain is very likely a treasure left behind by an ancient lord of the world of immortals. Are a bunch of cultivators going to shift it?” Mo Qiyue sniffed at the busily toiling cultivators.","“The Iron Pagoda Mountain is connected to too much, making it that only the younger generation like us can come here. The various factions are keeping each other in check and have forbidden immortals from taking action. The young man I met that day is probably here for the same reason,” Qin Qianxue mused.","Mo Qiyue and Jiang Feng looked at each other. “Seven Kills, Greedy Wolf, Army, Taisui, and Yinghuo have all manifested in recent times. Those of us from Great Xia are the closest, so we are naturally here first. But why are the others here so quickly as well?”","A ray of sword light streaked past them as they spoke, depositing Lu Yun in front of them.","“It’s you!” Qin Qianxue gasped as his two nascent soul guards went on the alert.","“Hahaha, ole brother Lu, you’re finally here! There’s such a fuss here that it’d be boring if you missed it,” Jiang Feng roared with laughter when he saw Lu Yun. Mo Qiyue also smiled broadly.","“Brother Mo, Brother Jiang, I’ve come late.” Lu Yun grinned at them and turned to Qin Qianxue. The young man remained quiet when he saw that his two friends were familiar with the newcomer.","“Ah... can it be ole brother Lu who delivered a loss to Brother Qin?” Jiang Feng immediately guessed the truth when he saw Qin Qianxue’s expression.","“Um...” Lu Yun said hesitantly. He’d listened for a while and revealed himself only when he understood their identities.","“This is our friend, Qin Qianxue,” Mo Qiyue explained with a smile. “Brother Qin, this is Lu Yun. He’s our brother too.”","“Lu Yun, Darklake... can it be...” Qin Qianxue’s eyes widened.","“Precisely.” Jiang Feng nodded.","“So it’s Brother Lu, greetings.” Qin Qianxue raised a cupped fist salute. “Brother Lu’s methods are unrivaled and I am not a match. However, please keep a low profile and do not make your identity or your capabilities widely known.”","Lu Yun blinked, then understood what Qin Qianxue meant. The Origin Sect. He didn’t know what kind of power the sect possessed since it hadn’t existed when he reincarnated into Great Xia. He didn’t expose his friends’ origins either. Although the trio were good friends with him, there was a complicated web of relationships and power struggles behind them. There were many things that they did not have a say in.","Looks like I need to pay Great Xia a visit when I’m done with Darklake.","There might be many things he couldn’t do in the future, but as he stood there now, these things had to be done. This was the training of the mind—comprehending all of life and the heavenly dao.","Qin Qianxue was a very proud person who’d taken it to heart that Lu Yun had scared him off that day. But when he saw that the Lu young master was familiar with Jiang Feng and Mo Qiyue, he was able to put it out of his mind.","Nor did Lu Yun bring up affairs of the day again when he saw Qin Qianxue drop the subject.","The three stopped discussing Iron Pagoda Mountain after Lu Yun’s sudden appearance. Night fell, and the Seven Kills, Greedy Wolf, Army, Taisui, and Yinghuo stars shone radiantly in the skies, forcing the other stars away.","It looks like the immortal weapon will be revealed tonight, Qin Qianxue thought to himself.","Many cultivators had spent numerous days at the mountain. They’d witnessed the mark left on the peak, but saw no sign of Yong Heyu. However, quite a few discovered traces around the mountain that indicated the man had gone inside the landmass.","Although it was night, activity still bustled around Iron Pagoda Mountain. Several soul projection cultivators mustered their strength for a joint blow, attempting to split the mountain open. It was bizarrely durable and didn’t move the slightest despite a dozen soul projection powerhouses acting in concert.","It was then that those assembled understood they’d underestimated this mountain all along.","RUMBLE.","Iron Pagoda Mountain suddenly trembled as a stunning ray of sword qi shot out from within. Horrifying sword qi quickly roiled over everything within fifty kilometers of the mountain.","“This is bad!” Lu Yun shouted when he saw the situation. “Leave!”","Sword light appeared beneath his feet as he fled outside the range of the sword qi.","“A blood sacrifice formation!” Mo Qiyue, Jiang Feng, and Qin Qianxue paled in unison. The latter two came from Great Xia and Mo Qiyue possessed an extremely mysterious background as well. They naturally recognized that someone had surreptitiously laid down a blood sacrifice formation fifty meters around the mountain!","There were hundreds of thousands of cultivators gathered around Iron Pagoda Mountain. Far from just foundation establishment, there were nascent soul, soul projection, and even powerhouses at higher levels. It was a mind-boggling move to sacrifice all of them!","Cutting rays of sword qi descended from the skies, leaving no time for even soul projection cultivators to react. Unable to defend themselves, they were churned to pieces by the light—even their nascent soul was reduced to a cloud of bloody mist.","Everywhere within fifty kilometers of Iron Pagoda Mountain had turned into killing fields.","Lu Yun clenched his jaw and wove his hands rapidly, gathering connate yang metal around his body to defend against the horrific sword qi. As sharp as they were, they were immediately defused when they touched connate yang metal energy.","Connate yang metal was the sharpest existence in the universe. Given Lu Yun’s weak cultivation, he gathered some bits and pieces that weren’t too strong. In his present level of accomplishment, he manipulated the energy of the five elements with the most primitive methods. It was like picking up a rock from the ground and throwing it forward.","But even so, the power of the five elements was so inordinately strong that they more than adequately defended him.","Once his cultivation reached a certain level, he would be able to use the five elements in many more ways. He’d be able to extract metal from a stone and craft all sorts of weapons. He might be able to hew the mountain open with just one blow of connate yang metal then.","His reaction speed was so fast that he ran out of the sword qi’s range within a few breaths. When he looked back, the ground was dyed red with blood.","Mo Qiyue, Jiang Feng, Qin Qianxue, and exceedingly few other powerful cultivators had managed to scramble to safety. The first three possessed lifesaving treasures, given their backgrounds. The others had either been hovering on the fringes or were so strong that they’d managed to wrest themselves to safety.","etvolare's Thoughts","I like the new kid, he's got his head on right. And really Lu Yun, a pig?"]},{"number":2254,"title":"Chapter 2254: Chapter 2177.1: Immortal Potentate","paragraphs":["Chapter 2177.1: Immortal Potentate","“Yong Heyu’s actions were calculated that day!” Lu Yun frowned ferociously. It was now apparent that even had Bloodbath not uprooted the Ling Clan, Yong Heyu would’ve found a way to reveal the aura of a dao weapon and gather cultivators throughout the land at the Iron Pagoda Mountain.","“Is a blood sacrifice needed to enter the mountain?” The possibility occurred to Lu Yun.","The survivors gaped in the next second. Although it was late at night, the sky was so radiant that it seemed no different from day. The earth was as if a sponge, absorbing the fresh blood from its surface with a speed visible to the naked eye. The blood soaked earth returned to normal in the span of a breath; there wasn’t even the scent of gore left.","“What a terrifying method! This isn’t a regular blood sacrifice formation!” A latter soul separation powerhouse was the strongest out of the survivors. He was in slightly poor form as he looked back at the mountain with apprehension.","“You, go inside and see what’s going on.” He grabbed a random soul projection cultivator and threw the hapless target within fifty kilometers of the mountain.","Whoosh!","Cutting sword qi flashed across their line of vision and quartered the cultivator before he even had time to scream.","“This isn’t the strength of a dao weapon!” The soul separation cultivator’s eyes widened. “Is it an immortal rank weapon?”","A dao weapon could instantly kill a soul projection, and very easily at that, but the mountain front of them lacked an owner and was simply releasing its sword qi in indiscriminate slaughter. A dao weapon could not deploy such strength without an owner. If it turned out to be an immortal weapon, then this wasn’t an affair that the soul separation cultivator could participate in.","If that was the case, not even the ninth rank empires had the right to be involved.","Regardless, the cultivator wasn’t willing to be dissuaded like this. There was still a dao weapon inside Iron Pagoda Mountain! Yong Heyu’s was at least mid dao rank and he was hiding inside the landmass!","“Hmm? The atmosphere is abating slightly.” Lu Yun keenly detected that the formation seemed to weaken somewhat after the sword qi killed the soul projection cultivator.","“You, take a look.” The soul separation cultivator’s name was Zi Lie and he was a wandering cultivator of a fifth rank empire. He’d rushed to Profound Wing Empire when he heard there was a dao weapon present in the world. This time, he pointed at a lucky nascent soul cultivator and instructed him to probe the premises.","Why would the cultivator listen to him? He raised sword light and ran for the hills. Zi Lie sneered and reached forward, forming a large hand in the middle of the air. This was the technique of a soul separation cultivator—splitting out the nascent soul and coalescing an external image!","The enormous hand grabbed the nascent soul cultivator and threw him into the mountain’s range.","Whoosh whoosh whoosh!","Numerous rays of sword qi sectioned him as soon as he set foot inside. He died before he even had a chance to scream, but the killing atmosphere around Iron Pagoda Mountain lightened further.","Many cultivators were highly alarmed by the development and quickly summoned sword light to flee for their lives.","“Do you think you can get away?” Zi Lie chuckled darkly. The hand in the air split into three and flew through the air, returning with a dozen cultivators in the blink of an eye and throwing all of them at the mountain.","“Some nascent soul, golden cores... Oh? Even foundation establishment are here?” Zi Lie looked at Lu Yun and the others with a malicious smile. “Juniors, head in there yourself,” he cackled. More than half of the atmosphere around the mountain had been dispersed.","“The difference in our cultivation is too great. I would be able to fight him if he was initial soul separation.” Mo Qiyue, Jiang Feng, and Qin Qianxue looked grave. Their nascent soul guards had already died to the mountain. Even though they’d made it out alive, they were very much worse for the wear.","Qin Qianxue was the weakest among them at latter golden core. The other two were initial nascent spirit. Yet despite their relative weakness, they didn’t fear anyone below soul separation. Unfortunately, Zi Lie was a latter soul separation powerhouse.","Apart from him, the other two soul separation experts at the scene had also survived. They hailed from fifth rank empires and could tell that the mountain would no longer be a threat to them if the killing atmosphere dissipated just a bit more.","By now, anyone could tell that there was more than a cultivator wielding a dao weapon inside Iron Pagoda Mountain. There was very likely the remains of an immortal!","The other two soul separation powerhouses hadn’t thrown anyone into the mountain, but neither did they stop Zi Lie either.","“Those guys are much more than they seem, they might come from the ninth rank empires or even...” muttered one of them—a frowning woman in purple robes.","“So many have already died here, including scouts from the ninth rank empires. Their deaths have nothing to do with us. Let’s see what this Zi Lie intends to do about them.” The other one, a man in blue robes, was plainly going to do nothing about the situation and reap gains at another’s expense.","Zi Lie leered when he saw the quartet remain unmoving and stalked in their direction.","“What a complete fool.” Lu Yun pursed his lip to see the man approach him. He wouldn’t bring out the Seal of the Multitude in front of the others—it was a connate treasure that would send even immortals in a frenzy.","He had another treasure that could be used.","Whoosh!","A gentle breeze fluttered as a man with a stony expression appeared in front of Lu Yun. He wore a longsword on his back and was clad in blue robes. Overwhelming killing intent shimmered around him.","“Lu Yi, throw this guy into the Iron Pagoda Mountain.” Lu Yun took a few steps back. Lu Yi was the talisman puppet that he’d refined out of the Origin Sect powerhouse. The man unsheathed his sword without a word and brought it down on Zi Lie.","Caught off guard, the latter hastily operated true origin to protect himself. Lu Yi’s blow came so fast and as a surprise that he could only block; there was no time to dodge.","Bam!","Lu Yi’s stroke bit into the protective layer around Zi Lie, its rampaging strength smashing through the hastily gathered energy. Zi Lie spat out a mouthful of blood and flew backward.","Damn, he’s strong! The thought flashed through his mind.","Lu Yi was just initial soul separation, but he’d undergone Lu Yun’s modifications and had been forged into something more like a treasure. His physical strength was beyond what a latter soul separation cultivator could endure.","Seeing that Zi Lie had been flung backward, Lu Yi pounced and grabbed the man’s ankle, flinging him in the direction of the mountain.","Zi Lie roared with desperation and summoned the separations of his nascent soul, slowing himself down with the three hands.","“Hmph!” Lu Yi snorted. He’d retained a trace of sentience after being refined into a talisman puppet and was a strange being that hovered between a living being and treasure. Or to be more exact, he possessed the advantages of both treasure and cultivator. The only drawback was that his cultivation would forever remain on this level. There was no possibility for him to grow stronger.","He deployed his own image in response to the three hands, one of a flying sword sparkling with frosty light. Since he was a sword cultivator, his image was naturally that of a flying sword.","The sword image flashed forward like lightning and sliced through Zi Lie’s hands. Lu Yi bounded forward again, grabbing Zi Lie and flinging him into the mountain’s range!","“Noooo!!” Terror filled Zi Lie’s eyes as rays of cutting sword qi descended from the sky and sectioned him. The sword qi immediately diced a meter tall nascent spirit as soon as it emerged from the remains of his body.","The death of a latter soul separation cultivator was far more effective than the soul projection and nascent soul cultivators.","Rumble!","Iron Pagoda Mountain trembled amid a series of loud rumbles.","“Hahaha, blood sacrifices are indeed the key to activating this treasure! Old guy, I’ve lured so many cultivators here on account of your wishes. Isn’t it your turn now?” A wildly arrogant voice sounded from the mountain—Lu Yun recognized it. It was Yong Heyu, the one who’d been at the side of the Darklake crown prince.","“No,” a stilted voice responded from the mountain. “Although I have regained my freedom, this is far from enough from activating the sword pagoda. You must kill everything within five hundred thousand kilometers and bring about a true blood sacrifice to fully activate it.”","“Within five hundred thousand kilometers!! Old guy, this is Profound Wing territory. I cannot slaughter my own citizens for this, but the neighboring Dark Empire or Darklake are good options...”","“Take care of the riff raff outside first.”","“We need to go!” Mo Qiyue, Jiang Feng, and Qin Qianxue raised sword light without hesitation, shooting for territory farther away. The two soul separation cultivators also instinctively fled for their lives.","“Lu Yun!” Mo Qiyue turned back, wanting to ensure that Lu Yun was with them. However, he saw the shadow of an enormous dragon dart out from the mountain and swallow the young man. Though he was immensely dismayed, there was nothing he could do for the moment but continue running."]},{"number":2255,"title":"Chapter 2255: Chapter 2177.2: Immortal Potentate","paragraphs":["Chapter 2177.2: Immortal Potentate","“Hahaha, Lu Yun?! So it’s you, young master Lu. You came to watch the show, didn’t you? Even the heavens are on my side!” The draconic shadow was Yong Heyu after he deployed the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons. He roared with laughter when he saw that it was Lu Yun in his grasp.","He hadn’t recognized Lu Yun at the Ling Clan, but with his wits, he quickly realized after the fact.","“It’s been a very long while, Terra Demon. Haven’t you become a brazen one, eh? You dare send people against me!” Lu Yun suddenly sneered. The shadow of a large seal floated over his body and easily blocked an attack from Yong Heyu.","The Seal of the Multitude was a connate treasure. With Lu Yun calling upon it, Yong Heyu couldn’t touch him, even though he was inside Iron Pagoda Mountain and aided by the mysterious person.","Meanwhile, the mysterious person was almost scared out of his wits when he heard the name “Terra Demon”! It was once a name known throughout the world of immortals in a certain era. In fact, it was the subject of many a nightmare. But since the world of immortals had long vanished, the name had also disappeared into history with it.","“Who are you?! Are you someone who survived from that time?! How do you know about me?!” shrieked Terra Demon inside the mountain.","Yong Heyu had been flung backward by the Seal of the Multitude. Cracks were developing on his dao weapon. Using a dao weapon against a connate treasure was no different from smashing an egg into a rock.","Whoosh!","Yong Heyu was drawn into the mountain with a flash of black light, replaced by a black shadow that approached Lu Yun.","“A connate treasure?! Who are you to have a connate treasure protect you??” The black shadow was the Terra Demon. He was flabbergasted by the seal around Lu Yun.","“Terra Demon, Terra Demon Immortal King, aren’t you something, huh! Do you even remember who saved you, who taught you cultivation, and who helped you become an immortal? Do you not recognize this seat even now??” Lu Yun saw only a tattered will in the black shadow, but its features were clear. It was one of his immortal kings from when he reincarnated into the world of immortals—the Terra Demon Immortal King!","“You... you are...” Terra Demon stared at Lu Yun. The young man was just a foundation establishment cultivator, but wielded a connate treasure and spoke these words from his past. Tongue-tied, he didn’t know what to say.","“Your... Grace...?” he ventured carefully.","“Who else would recognize you apart from me?” Lu Yun snorted. During his time in the world of immortals, he’d reached the peak of cultivation and was listed as one of the five titans of the world. He was the High Lord of the Northern Sky and called the wind and rain with a flip of his hand. Being one of the greatest in the world of immortals, not even the central immortal emperor had dared try to impose too many restrictions on him. The Terra Demon Immortal King was one of his many immortal king subordinates.","When the Mindful Immortal Potentate fell, Lu Yun had not yet become a high lord. That would come to pass several hundred thousand of years later. He’d sent Terra Demon to investigate the immortal potentate’s death and locate where the potentate’s pagoda had gone to.","So Terra Demon had indeed found it!","As for Lu Yun in that life, he broke through to the peak limits of immortal emperor not long thereafter and prepared to enter the next stage. However, what he set foot in next was the second reincarnation out of three thousand.","He’d been in his first reincarnation when he sought out the immortal potentate—his memories hadn’t been fully sealed then. Therefore, his command to Terra Demon must have something to do with the past him.","“Subordinate Terra Demon greets Your Grace the High Lord!” Terra Demon had sensed the aura of Lu Yun’s core origin—the same Lu Yun had experienced all three thousand Lu Yuns. Thus, the one standing in front of him was the first and truest Lu Yun.","As one of Lu Yun’s most competent subordinates, Terra Demon naturally detected his lord’s aura. Not to mention, it didn’t make sense that anyone other than the High Lord of the Northern Sky, invincible in the world of immortals, would be able to manipulate a connate treasure with the strength of foundation establishment.","“That’s enough, what happened after I left? Where’s the world of immortals?”","Where’s the world of immortals?","That was the biggest question in Lu Yun’s heart! He’d risen to immortality in all of his reincarnations, but never took the ascent protocol to the world of immortals. He didn’t even hear of that world.","“The world of immortals...” Terra Demon responded blankly. “Your Grace, I was died the sword pagoda after I found it. Thanks to protection from the origin of water as bestowed by Your Grace, I salvaged my will and fell into a deep slumber. I do not know what happened afterward.","“But in my sleep, I vaguely sensed the quaking of mountains and earth, the breaking of rules, the destruction of laws. The world of immortals... must have been destroyed.” Emotion filled his voice.","“But Your Grace, the High Lady was protected by the laws of water origin as well, so she must be fine after the demise of the world of immortals. See, Your Grace survived!” Terra Demon quickly added when he saw the less than pleasant expression on Lu Yun’s face.","The young man waved him off, fully believing the other’s words and loyalty. He’d raised Terra Demon from youth and knew his character like the back of his hand. If he wanted Terra Demon to commit suicide right now, the latter would do it without question.","As for this High Lady that he spoke of... the heavenly dao had likely shoved the woman at him. He didn’t want the woman and never touched her.","“How is the sword pagoda?” he asked instead.","“Your Grace, I attempted to claim the pagoda when I awoke one hundred years ago, but its core origin was so strong that I was unable to draw near it without my physical body,” Terra Demon sighed. “Therefore, I needed to nurture a cultivator and borrow his hand to activate the pagoda, then take possession of him and come back to life that way. Once I recovered my cultivation, I would claim the sword pagoda and go in search of Your Grace.”","“So Yong Heyu was one of your pawns.” Lu Yun didn’t fault his subordinate for inciting a blood sacrifice. Terra Demon himself was an inauspicious star of the cosmos. He brimmed with the air of violence that was greater than that of Seven Kills, Greedy Wolf, Army, Taisui, and Yinghuo. He’d been a keen sword in Lu Yun’s hand when in the world of immortals.","“Now that Your Grace is here, it won’t take any effort to seize control of the pagoda.” Terra Demon looked at the young man with great emotion.","“Hurry and take possession of Yong Heyu. The disturbance here has been so big that there will be many cultivators and immortals here before long,” Lu Yun frowned.","Terra Demon understood. He only had a lingering will left to his name and Lu Yun was latter foundation establishment. They wouldn’t be able to withstand stronger cultivators. Thus, he darted back into the mountain and sank into the unconscious Yong Heyu’s body.","Although Terra Demon’s will was tattered, it was one of an immortal king rather than an ordinary immortal. He’d also left behind many contingencies on Yong Heyu and perfectly primed him to be possessed.","Thus, Terra Demon easily took control of Yong Heyu and benefited from the young man’s hard efforts in cultivation. He’d surreptitiously helped the young man ascend beyond latter soul projection a long time ago, but used certain methods to conceal the breakthrough so that the heavenly book in the Celestial Realm Battlefront didn’t detect it.","When Terra Demon next appeared, he was a handsome young man three meters tall, dressed in white robes with silver hair and eyes. It was what his true self looked like. Since his physical body was lost and nascent soul crushed, his current level of cultivation was just that of Yong Heyu’s latter soul projection.","“This subordinate greets Your Grace!” Terra Demon knelt on one knee and bent his head. His waist length silver hair swept the ground.","“The world of immortals no longer exists and I am not the High Lord of the Northern Sky anymore. You do not need to hold to these rules of etiquette,” Lu Yun waved him off. Dense goodwill emanated from Terra Demon—the goodwill of faith!","Lu Yun was his faith!","“Let’s go to the sword pagoda.” The sword pagoda was what Lu Yun wanted the most. He thought of it constantly even when he was the High Lord of the Northern Sky.","The Mindful Immortal Potentate had withstood five immortal kings with it in his hands. He’d ensured they died with him, a testament to the might of this pagoda. More important was that Lu Yun vaguely sensed that the world of immortals hadn’t vanished due to a great cataclysm. There were certain unspeakable truths behind it.","Not only was the sword pagoda related to it, but it also seemed to be the key to unlocking his memories. That was the most important. With the key in hand, he could save it for the most appropriate time. Otherwise, he would forever drift through this life.","Terra Demon nodded and formed a hand seal with one hand. Both of them vanished at the same time. He knew the mountain like the back of his hand after one hundred years of preparation. The mountain itself was the sword pagoda, and the fine metal on its surface was one of its byproducts. Not even an immortal weapon would leave a mark.","“This... is...?” Lu Yun’s eyes widened as a massive ray of sword qi in front of him.","It was empty without end inside the sword pagoda, like it was a massive clearing. The only thing within it was this ray of sword qi nine meters tall. It was nine meters tall, one meter wide, three inches and three minutes of time. Completely unmoving.","It wasn’t particularly strong, but it gave one the feeling of eternity. Indeed, undying and eternal, it would outlast heaven, earth, and all living things.","“Your Grace, this is the core origin of the sword pagoda. It might also be a doorway to its true heart. You might be able to fully control the sword pagoda if you refine it,” said Terra Demon.","“No,” Lu Yun shook his head. “Where is the Mindful Immortal Potentate’s corpse and the core origin of the Seven Kills, Greedy Wolf, Army, Taisui, and Yinghuo Immortal Kings?”","Something was wrong—there was no sign of the immortal potentate and the five immortal kings suppressing him. All was empty inside the sword pagoda.","etvolare's Thoughts","Terra Demon's name is the first two characters for the Demonic Vine. The sword pagoda's characters are the same as the Sword Pagoda. Does everyone remember what these two were?"]},{"number":2256,"title":"Chapter 2256: Chapter 2177.3: Immortal Potentate","paragraphs":["Chapter 2177.3: Immortal Potentate","“The immortal potentate has fully perished and this subordinate borrowed the power of the stars to sacrifice the five immortal kings’ core origin to the sword pagoda. If not, it would be impossible to activate it,” Terra Demon answered honestly. “The Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons that I taught Yong Heyu came from this ray of sword light. It was not left behind by the Mindful Immortal Potentate.","“However... this subordinate feels that the five immortal kings don’t seem to have died. That core origin may not have been theirs.”","Lu Yun nodded. He’d thought that there would be some treasures from the six inside the pagoda. Instead, it looked like the ray of sword qi had swallowed them whole.","“Stand down, Terra Demon. I’m going to try to refine this sword qi.” Lu Yun waved the man off and added, “Don’t address me with Your Grace or High Lord in the outside world, just call me young master.”","“Yes, young master.” Terra Demon hastily retreated to the side.","Lu Yun took a deep breath in front of the sword qi. Hongmeng qi roiled in his body and the remaining goodwill in the Seal of the Multitude also ignited.","This sword pagoda had been something that even the central immortal emperor coveted. The Mindful Immortal Potentate hadn’t managed to fully refine it. As a minor foundation establishment cultivator, Lu Yun’s own strength was insufficient.","Thus, he called upon the seal without hesitation.","Rumble!","The Seal of the Multitude was held in his dantian. Although the goodwill was ponderous, it was still insufficient to truly manipulate the seal. All that floated upward was its shadow. Even its shadow, however, was superior to ordinary immortal weapons. It came from the heavenly dao, after all.","Tremendous aura surged forth—it was the first time that Lu Yun called upon the seal with his full strength. If it wasn’t for the fact that they were inside the pagoda, the disturbance likely would’ve already brought a Great Xia powerhouse to investigate.","The seal’s shadow enveloped the sword qi and Lu Yun teased out his Hongmeng qi, directing it into the sword qi.","Whoosh!","For some reason, the ray of sword qi trembled and erupted with keen rays, cutting through the shadow around it. They continued unabated and struck at Lu Yun.","“This is bad!” He frowned slightly and retreated, wanting to evade the terrible sword qi. Death was incredibly close to him—just one step away. He could feel the forceful killing intent from the sword qi.","Despite death breathing down his neck, he kept his composure. He’d died many times before and could face it with aplomb.","“This sword qi...” Brows furrowed tight, Lu Yun stared fixedly at the ray. He could sense that a ray of sword qi that could sever the shadow of a connate treasure would have been too much for him even when he was the High Lord of the Northern Sky.","“Young master!” gasped Terra Demon. He’d been keeping a close eye on Lu Yun and was moving at the fastest speed possible, wanting to take the blow for his lord.","But he was only latter soul establishment at the moment, how could he be faster than the sword qi? It was about to execute Lu Yun!","Boom!","Vast strength appeared out of nowhere and rebuffed the terrible sword qi.","“It’s only been a few days, my little junior brother, but here you are running afoul of this terrible thing,” rang out a surprised voice. Sky appeared in blue robes with blue hair cascading over his shoulders.","Lu Yun heaved a sigh of relief. “My greatest thanks to senior brother for saving my life. This would be the end of my road if you hadn’t gotten here in time.”","Terra Demon had rushed to Lu Yun’s side. “Young master, you’re alright! My deepest gratitude to this senior!”","Thump!","He fell to his knees in thanks.","“No matter, this is only proper since Lu Yun is my junior brother.” Sky smiled faintly and lifted his hand, gently raising Terra Demon back to his feet.","“Strange... the high lord was always alone when he fought in the world of immortals. He never spoke of a sect. Is he in one in this lifetime? But no, the lord’s senior brother easily blocked an attack from the sword pagoda... I once saw the central immortal emperor when His Grace was summoned for an audience, but this one’s aura pales far in comparison...” Terra Demon took another look at Sky and was dumbfounded by what he saw.","Sky was as unfathomable as the seas. Even though Terra Demon lacked his previous cultivation of immortal king, his consciousness remained and he could fully perceive the other’s terrible might.","Sky was the manifestation of the rules, thus lacking desire and emotion. He gave no thought to the emotions of others and didn’t try to hide himself. Lu Yun couldn’t sense Sky’s terrifying aura because he practiced the Nine Chapters of Dao. The “dao” character in his dantian also came from the same origins as his senior brother.","“Senior brother, do you know about this sword pagoda?” Lu Yun asked Sky.","“A sword pagoda? What an interesting name,” Sky chuckled. “It’s unbelievably terrifying and existed before I did. There is only a corpse of it now, or I wouldn’t have been able to save you otherwise.”","“Um... was this sword pagoda once a mighty powerhouse?” Lu Yun frowned tightly. Does it... have something to do with me?","“A powerhouse? You could put it that way. You’ll find out what it is in the future,” Sky sighed. “You better not run afoul of things like this from now on. You would be dead if it wasn’t for my coincidental manifestation and detection of its presence.","“Even though it does have something to do with you, it will still kill you if the time is not yet right!”","Lu Yun nodded. His senior brother hadn’t come because he’d sensed the young man was in danger, it really was a coincidence that he happened to be in the area. As the heavens toil ever onwards, so must one strive forward without end. If he depended on others in everything he did, he would never reach the peak. The heavenly dao had taught him what it should over the course of three thousand reincarnations. The rest was up to Lu Yun himself.","“But this thing coming to you now is a result of plans made by the past you. Everything happened as it is meant to.” Sky smiled and flicked his finger, sending a beam of blue light toward the ray of sword qi.","The ray shifted and twisted, trying to break the light.","“The past young master... did His Grace already foresee the events of today back in his time?” Terra Demon’s faith in Lu Yun grew even deeper.","However, Lu Yun knew what the past him meant—not the high lord, but a personage even greater.","Sky smiled without a word and beckoned the light back to him. “Try refining it now, junior brother.”","Lu Yun immediately sank his consciousness and Hongmeng qi into the sword qi.","Whoosh!","The sword qi jerked before settling down in his dantian, resulting in the sword pagoda itself shaking and streaking into Lu Yun’s dantian. It was a black pagoda that was unusually keen, like a sharp sword unsheathed. What surprised Lu Yun was that the pagoda stood on the same level as the dao character in his dantian!","“I will be returning to my post now that the matter is concluded. This is my first and last time saving you. The matters to come are up to you.” Sky faded into motes of blue light as he spoke, returning to his state as the rules.","“I could refine this because senior brother helped me. I wonder how the Mindful Immortal Potentate did it, or is this pagoda meant to target me?” Lu Yun pouted, not knowing that the immortal potentate hadn’t refined the pagoda back in his day. He’d simply borrowed its strength, just like how Terra Demon obtained the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons from the sword qi. His core origin was still that of an immortal king, despite having only his will left. Everything was fine so long as one did not attempt to refine the sword pagoda.","As for Lu Yun, even if he did once have something to do with the treasure, he was someone else now after reincarnation had suppressed his memories.","“But no matter what, I am the disciple of the heavenly dao. As weak as I am now, I will ultimately vault into that peerless realm. Everything will naturally be resolved then.” Although questions swirled in his heart, Lu Yun didn’t dwell on them. Many were things that the weak didn’t have the right to know about. Even if he found out, he won’t understand that level of existence. It was more useful to temper himself so that he could also become a peerless being.","He’d never doubted himself—confidence? He’d never lacked that. He thought very, very highly of himself. It was an attitude ingrained into his bones.","He also wasn’t a saint!","Please, he was perfectly willing to kill people, alright?"]},{"number":2257,"title":"Chapter 2257: Chapter 2178.1: Golden Core of Great Dao","paragraphs":["Chapter 2178.1: Golden Core of Great Dao","One night had passed since Lu Yun entered Iron Pagoda Mountain. Its sudden disappearance raised the attention of powerhouses in the distant capital of Profound Wing Empire. Numerous rays of sword light cut across the sky—all from heavyweights above combination level.","Combination experts covered thousands of kilometers in one breath. It’d only been a little over twenty minutes since the mountain disappeared, but dozens of rays of sword light descended upon the scene.","“Where is the Iron Pagoda Mountain??” boomed a middle-aged man.","Terra Demon creased his thin, silver brows.","“It turned into a flying sword and flew away,” Lu Yun responded when he sensed killing intent rise in Terra Demon. The young man no longer fought alone in this world. There was a massive Lu Clan behind him as well as a Darklake Empire. If the slightest hint of anything went awry, not only would the family be exterminated, but so would Darklake be wiped off the map.","“Turned into a flying sword and flew away?” snorted another combination powerhouse. “Take these two back with us and interrogate them closely. Iron Pagoda Mountain has become a very important site and is highly likely to be an immortal weapon. We must pursue every clue to the end!”","Terra Demon already stood in front of Lu Yun.","“Halt, all of you!” A soft shout broke the air as Mo Qiyue, Jiang Feng, and Qin Qianxue arrived with a dozen men. Their people were all combination powerhouses and there was even a tribulation heavyweight among them!","“You guys...” The first speaker was about to speak when those next to him grabbed him warningly. They were representatives from sixth and seventh empires here for the show. The newcomers on the scene were far beyond their capabilities, despite also being combination level.","“You’re still alive, ole brother Lu! That’s wonderful!” Enthusiastic as ever, Jiang Feng roared with happy laughter. Even the normally taciturn Mo Qiyue smiled faintly.","“But I say, I’m more curious how you managed to escape,” Qin Qianxue asked curiously. The trio had known that Iron Pagoda Mountain was extraordinary when they ran from it. They’d contacted their factions and swiftly assembled some forces from the ninth rank empires.","Mo Qiyue and Jiang Feng were equally curious, but guessed a thing or two when they saw Terra Demon standing in front of Lu Yun.","“Right, where’s the mountain gone to?” Qin Qianxue asked again.","“It turned into a flying sword and flew away.” Lu Yun had tempered his thick skin through three thousand lifetimes. Lying was no different from drinking water to him. The sword pagoda was too important and also relevant to his sealed self, so he didn’t want anyone to know that it was on him.","Seeing that their friend didn’t want to talk about it, Mo Qiyue and the others didn’t press the issue. They took their men and searched through the ruins. There was a massive crater several dozen kilometers across left after Lu Yun claimed the sword pagoda. It was cavernous and deep with no clue of what lay at the bottom.","“It’s the aura of treasures!” Qin Qianxue’s eyes lit up when the trio approached the crater.","Whoosh!","Light streaked out of the pit and shot toward the horizon. Those assembled blinked with surprise and a combination cultivator leapt into the air, closing his hand around the light.","It was a black shortsword with radiance swirling over it.","“A mid spirit rank weapon?” the cultivator started. This level of treasure wasn’t much in his eyes. Most combination cultivators used supreme spirit rank weapons, with some luckier ones wielding dao weapons.","“It really is a treasure?” Lu Yun gaped. He hadn’t thought there’d be more treasures beneath the pagoda.","Rumble!","The earth began to shake as rays of multicolored radiance shot out from the crater. Treasures streaked out shortly, protected by strange illumination and falling to the ground like meteors. Lu Yun grabbed a random blaze and came back with a lower spirit rank weapon.","“Um...” Mo Qiyue and the others were shocked. “What’s at the bottom to send out so many treasures?”","The highest out of the treasures shooting from the pit was but mid spirit rank, the lowest was qi rank treasure. But there were so many of them that thousands were ejected within the span of a few breaths.","“Get ‘em!” Lu Yun hesitated for only a split second before releasing his talisman puppet. His puppet swept through the premises, collecting everything that fell. Lu Yun’s foundations were in a third rank cultivation empire. A lower spirit rank treasure would be the pillar of support for the nation, to say nothing of thousands of them.","Terra Demon understood his lord’s intentions as well and began collecting the treasures as well. Mo Qiyue was only half a second slower than Lu Yun—he, too, leapt into action.","Despite his impressive background, he was a Darklake citizen and the Mo Clan was one of the nation’s most illustrious great families. His subordinates also grabbed everything they could lay hands on. These treasures were jokes to the higher ranked empires and Great Xia, but several thousands of them were sufficient to dictate the fortunes of a lower rank cultivation empire.","Lu Yun couldn’t use higher rank treasures for the moment and when he could, he could refine his own. Any that he seized now would simply draw the eyes of others.","Countless treasures spewed into the air like a volcano had erupted. They scattered down like a shower of rain, increasing in frequency, but low ranked as a whole.","Apart from Lu Yun and his friends, the others present were all combination cultivators. They wouldn’t lower themselves to fight for this level of treasure. Hailing from Great Xia, spirit treasures were trash to Jiang Feng and Qin Qianxue.","“I get why Lu Yun is doing this, but why is Mo Qiyue also collecting these treasures?” Qin Qianxue didn’t understand his friend’s actions.","Jiang Feng shook his head without judgment. “Qiyue must have his reasons for doing so. I’m more concerned with what might come from this pit next.”","“It’s been trash thus far. What, are you hoping for an immortal rank treasure?” Qin Qianxue pursed his lips.","Bam!","The ground trembled once more as a pillar of light shot for the horizon.","“A dao weapon!” Some of the combination cultivators immediately sensed the presence within the light. “Get it!”","They couldn’t sit still with the arrival of a dao weapon. Taking to the air, they grabbed for the pillar of light.","“So some real treasures are appearing. That one was an upper dao rank treasure,” Qin Qianxue looked on appreciatively. With their backgrounds and experience, they only needed to briefly sense the treasure’s aura to determine what rank it was.","The rate of treasures appearing slowed down after the dao weapon appeared. More than thirty combination cultivators fought each other in the air, grappling for the dao weapon.","Lu Yun and Mo Qiyue worked in perfect tandem and collected all of the lower rank treasures from the crater. Tens of thousands of treasures were ejected within twenty-odd minutes, but most of them were too low ranked to be worthy of consideration for the group assembled. In a mid or low rank cultivation empire, however, the sum would be staggering.","“I wonder what’s down there—maybe ruins from the ancient times?” Lu Yun stroked his storage ring and swept a glance down into the hole. The sword pagoda hadn’t landed here by accident either. It’d stopped emitting treasures, but was so deep that Lu Yun couldn’t make out anything in the gloom.","“I can sense overwhelming killing intent below. This must be a dangerous place.” Mo Qiyue walked over; they’d reaped incredible gains. He suddenly shifted to transmission, “Lu Yun, don’t let higher ranked cultivators know about the treasures you collected. As low ranked as they are, they’re not ordinary items.”","Lu Yun started. Mo Qiyue meant to evade Qin Qianxue and Jiang Feng’s hearing if he’d switched to transmission. He nodded without a word, knowing the truth of what the young man said. No one would find out anything since they’d claimed all of the lower rank treasures. Those from the higher rank empire or cultivation dynasty wouldn’t care about these.","“This is a highly sensitive matter and it might be ancient ruins or even the residence of an immortal,” Jiang Feng cautioned Mo Qiyue. “Qiyue, it’s not good for Darklake that these ruins have appeared here. You should try advising the Darklake emperor at an opportune moment that he should give up Profound Wing.”","Mo Qiyue nodded."]},{"number":2258,"title":"Chapter 2258: Chapter 2178.2: Golden Core of Great Dao","paragraphs":["Chapter 2178.2: Golden Core of Great Dao","Jiang Feng raised cupped fists at the two and left with his men. Qin Qianxue left as well, after taking another look at Lu Yun.","Although the two left, Lu Yun knew that a greater storm brewed.","A victor was determined between the combination cultivators up in the sky. A latter combination cultivator won the dao treasure and threw his head back with laughter. The treasure was a flag six meters across and bestrewn with starlight. Three hundred and sixty-five rays of starlight were a clear nod to the major cycle, and it seemed that the strength of the cosmos could be deployed with a slight wave.","“The Cosmic Flag? It’s the real thing, not an imitation!” Lu Yun happened to lift his head and saw the cultivator happily waving the flag around. “It was a king grade immortal treasure that belonged to Celestial Empress Myrtlestar of the East... What’s it doing...”","“Young master, that is the Cosmic Flag.” Terra Demon also recognized the treasure. There were nine grades to immortal rank treasures and king grade sat over all of them. The Cosmic Flag was the highest level of existence among king grade immortal treasures.","“Hey you, combination cultivator! Get down here!” Lu Yun couldn’t help but yell at the sky.","Gui Xie was still celebrating his new acquisition when he saw one of the untouchable young masters on the ground address him. He immediately landed without hesitation.","Gui Xie was a wandering cultivator with no home base, but he’d heard of some of the mysterious factions in the world. If he offended someone like this, the three ninth rank empires would quickly issue an arrest warrant for him. Survival would be nigh impossible then even if he fled to the corners of the world.","Thus, Gui Xie presented himself in front of Lu Yun without another word. He glanced at the tribulation cultivator standing behind Mo Qiyue.","This cultivator was from the Xuanhuang Empire. He was in charge of investigating Iron Pagoda Mountain and protecting these young masters. Since Qin Qianxue and Jiang Feng had returned to Great Xia, the cultivator remained to protect Mo Qiyue.","Lu Yun was not under his protection, but that didn’t stop Lu Yun from swaggering around in borrowed influence.","“What orders might the gentleman have?” Gui Xie asked respectfully. The tribulation cultivator hadn’t taken action earlier—the upper dao rank treasure wouldn’t have fallen into his hands if the powerhouse had. Therefore, Gui Xie wasn’t worried that Lu Yun would seize his treasure.","“I see that your methods are a mess and your true origin is much less than pure. You’re a wandering cultivator and I’m officially extending an opportunity for you to join me.” Lu Yun cut straight to the chase. While the Cosmic Flag was so tattered that it’d fallen to an upper rank dao treasure, it was still the treasure of Celestial Empress Myrtlestar. It wasn’t something that any random cultivator could claim.","Since the combination cultivator had easily directed the flag to recognize a new master, he must be far from ordinary. In that case, it would be helpful for Lu Yun to add the guy to his troops.","“Ah...” Gui Xie hesitated. With his cultivation level, he’d immediately receive a high position if he joined a cultivation empire, sect, or clan. He remained a wandering cultivator because he was used to freedom.","The world was his oyster so long as he didn’t violate the rules set by the ninth rank empires.","The tribulation cultivator behind Mo Qiyue frowned. He was well aware that Lu Yun was just the young master of a minor clan from a third rank empire. The young man wanted to recruit a combination level cultivator? Utterly preposterous!","But since Lu Yun was friends with Mo Qiyue, there was nothing the cultivator could say.","“Gui Xie thanks the young master for your kind intentions, but Gui Xie is used to freedom and cannot stand fetters. I am willing to leave behind this treasure in exchange for my freedom.” Gui Xie was roughly thirty years old and looked very ordinary. His worn blue robes weren’t a powerful treasure. As he spoke, he offered up the Cosmic Flag.","“You can go.” Lu Yun shook his head instead of taking the flag. “I hope you treat this treasure well and do not tarnish its name. If anything happens, you can find me at the Lu Clan in Darklake Empire.”","He took out a blank jade slip from his storage ring and etched certain things in it. Tossing it to Gui Xie, Lu Yun turned around and left.","Terra Demon looked intently at Gui Xie and snorted, “You have absolutely no idea what’s good for you. Be careful with my young master’s gift!”","The tribulation cultivator behind Mo Qiyue blinked, he’d thought that Lu Yun would make use of his presence to seize the treasure. How was this the scene playing out instead? What was in the jade slip that a good-for-nothing prodigal of a third rank empire had thrown to a latter combination cultivator? As confused as the tribulation cultivator was, he couldn’t be bothered to think things further.","There was one thing he overlooked the entire time, however, and that was the silver haired, silver eyed soul projection cultivator next to Lu Yun called him young master. Could a noble scion from a third rank empire possibly have a soul projection servant?","Gui Xie watched them leave with a complicated expression and scanned the jade slip with his consciousness.","“Heir to Celestial Empress Myrtlestar’s legacy, do not tarnish her name.” Lu Yun’s voice sounded as soon as the mind entered the jade slip. A surge of will burst out of it as a complete cultivation method emerged.","The Immortal Canon of Life and Death!","An immortal level cultivation method!","Gui Xie’s mouth dropped with shock. What kind of background did that young master have to pull out an immortal method without second thought!","Unbeknownst to him that this Immortal Canon of Life and Death wasn’t an ordinary level immortal method. It was the personal method of the Celestial Empress Myrtlestar of the East, one that reigned supreme in the world of immortals.","When Lu Yun was the High Lord of the Northern Sky, he was good friends with the High Lady of the Eastern Sky. Their friendship was forged through life and death. When he reached a bottleneck in his cultivation, Celestial Empress Myrtlestar lent him the Immortal Canon of Life and Death to help him break through to peak immortal emperor.","Nothing was known about Celestial Empress Myrtlestar’s current condition and her personal treasure had been demoted to an upper dao rank treasure. Lu Yun didn’t force the issue when Gui Xie proved unwilling to follow him. He handed over the Immortal Canon of Life and Death instead.","Poof!","The jade slip reduced itself into dust after conveying the full contents of the method into Gui Xie’s mind.","“Celestial Empress Myrtlestar...” Gui Xie came to a decision as he looked in the direction of Lu Yun’s departure.","Some combination cultivators waited in the shadows, hoping for the site of Iron Pagoda Mountain to spew out more dao treasures. Some weaker cultivars such as golden core, foundation establishment, and even qi refinement were present as well.","News of the crater shooting out tens of thousands of treasures became widely known and many cultivators gathered their courage to explore it. However, no one ever came back out.","......","“Lu Yun, your reaction earlier was a bit odd.” Mo Qiyue raised after they left Profound Wing Empire, thereby prompting the departure of the tribulation cultivation and associated six combination cultivators.","“Odd?” Lu Yun asked curiously.","“Based on your typical style, you would’ve robbed that Gui Xie blind,” Mo Qiyue cracked a rare joke.","“He didn’t offend me, what would I rob him for?” Lu Yun shook his head. That was the heir to his dead sister-in-arms. It was right and proper that he help Gui Xie.","Mo Qiyue didn’t believe anything that Lu Yun said; he saw things clearly. The Lu young master hadn’t said a word of truth from beginning to end. He couldn’t even be bothered to explain why there was a soul projection servant by his side!","“If you take him back to Darklake, his name and information will immediately appear in the heavenly book of the Celestial Realm Battlefront. Those from Dark Orchid will immediately be on your doorstep then,” Mo Qiyue said solemnly.","“Are you afraid of Dark Orchid?” Lu Yun curled his lip.","“The world of cultivation has its own rules, it’s not a matter of whether I’m afraid or not.” Mo Qiyue slowly shook his head.","Terra Demon also curled his lip with contempt. He had the consciousness of an immortal king! Even Lu Tianling could evade the heavenly book’s detection, to say nothing of him.","“The rules of the world of cultivation...” Lu Yun looked up at the sky.","“The rules aren’t set by a person or a faction.” Mo Qiyue pointed upward.","“The sky? That’s my senior brother...” Lu Yun mumbled to himself in a volume that only he could hear. “The one above him is also my master.”","The heavenly dao established rules on behalf of all and for the benefit of all. The sky existed to maintain the balance of the rules. Their existence was to represent all of life and contend against the will of the nothing.","It was why this civilization of immortal dao could expand to these heights. But now... the world of immortals was no more.","......","The three entered the perimeter of Darklake as they conversed. Lu Tianling used a certain treasure to evade the heavenly book, whereas Terra Demon used his immense consciousness to forcefully beat back the rules of the heavenly book.","Therefore, his name didn’t appear in its pages either.","“Interesting.” Terra Demon closed his eyes and carefully sensed his surroundings. “Young master, this world is more than it looks.”","“Oh? What have you discovered?” Lu Yun asked.","“That so-called heavenly book is a powerful immortal treasure that covers the boundless domain.” Terra Demon frowned. “Thankfully, we are on its fringes. If we were in its core, I would not be able to withstand it with my strength.”"]},{"number":2259,"title":"Chapter 2259: Chapter 2178.3: Golden Core of Great Dao","paragraphs":["Chapter 2178.3: Golden Core of Great Dao","“I see,” Lu Yun nodded. The Celestial Realm Battlefront was incomparably mysterious. Even a world of immortals in its prime wouldn’t have been able to craft such a vast and uncanny world.","No matter who entered, their cultivation was suppressed to initial nascent soul. Lu Yun didn’t think of asking his senior brother as, given Sky’s character, the only thing he would say was “you will find out when the time is right”. Lu Yun really couldn’t be bothered.","Dark City was much more deserted these days. There were thirty percent fewer foundation establishment and golden core cultivators compared to before Lu Yun’s departure. It was common knowledge in Darklake Empire that there was a location in the west of Profound Wing Empire with a newly formed treasure geyser. Countless cultivators formed a massive army that marched off in search of its fortune.","None of it had to do with Lu Yun as he’d already collected the greatest benefits.","Night, the Lu residence.","Lan’er’s faint snoring could be heard from her room.","The sword pagoda hovered silently in Lu Yun’s dantian. Though he’d refined it, he couldn’t use it. It was absolutely on par with the Seal of the Multitude.","“The Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons... Aha, here it is.” Lu Yun sent his consciousness into the treasure and tried to touch the terrifying ray of sword qi. Unexpectedly, he received an overwhelming amount of sword techniques instead. He could use none of them at the moment, not even if he mustered his full strength for one.","“I have indeed found it... Vast Dragon Seaturner, Peng of Kun, Starstream Stroke...”","Compared to the other techniques, the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons was the only one that Lu Yun could deploy as it was the weakest.","“The Mindful Immortal Potentate used the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons to dominate the world of immortals in his time. Then it seems that even he was unable to practice the other techniques,” Lu Yun sighed.","Whoever had invented these techniques was a veritable genius—the Vast Dragon Seaturner, in particular, was the improved version of the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons. It was the foundational move for all sword dao.","Bizarrely, Lu Yun somehow felt that he was complimenting himself.","Regardless, the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons were so immensely powerful that it took him seven days to learn its initial moves. A current of dragon-shaped sword qi collected in his dantian when he succeeded.","“So I see. The techniques within the sword pagoda aren’t that of regular dao or combat art. They’re different from the techniques of sword immortals. One can deploy them when one communicates with the sword qi in one’s dantian.” Lu Yun keenly sensed that the dragon-shaped current in his dantian seemed to be a replica of the ray of sword qi within the sword pagoda.","But since Sky had said that this was something from his past self, Lu Yun wasn’t much worried. Yong Heyu had so easily employed the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons likely because he’d formed a current of sword qi in his dantian.","Lu Yun slowly opened his eyes after he collected one current.","“It’s time to form my core...” He’d reached peak foundation establishment and was only half a step away from golden core. His spirit root had been tempered to an extreme through the aid of connate fire origin—it couldn’t absorb one iota more energy.","Although Lu Yun had consumed all of the goodwill stored in the Seal of the Multitude, he didn’t need that at the moment. While goodwill could offset the incredible amounts of spirit qi required by the Nine Chapters of Dao, the shackles of breakthrough were up to Lu Yun himself.","He held a milky paramount spirit stone in one hand and directed all of the Hongmeng qi in his body to the bottleneck.","Rumble!","The spirit stone crumbled to pieces and vast Hongmeng qi surged through his meridians like the floodwaters, gathering in his dantian. Aureate brilliance shone from the hazy dao character and boundless Hongmeng qi swiftly coalesced around it, ensconcing it until it became a hazy egg.","The golden core of great dao.","The golden core formed by the Nine Chapters of Dao was more than an ordinary golden core, it was one of great dao.","Lu Yun sensed the rhythm of heavenly dao as soon as his golden core formed and further understood the emotions and goodwill of the masses. His fingers flicked through hand seals, a steady stream of paramount rank spirit stones passing through his hands to crumble into dust.","His golden core was fully formed and consolidated after he exhausted one hundred paramount stones. He was in the second turn of the Seeing Dao chapter, initial golden core.","Another rumble exploded through his mind when his golden core settled. An imperceptible beam of light quickly descended from the sky and arrived in front of Lu Yun, splitting into two and entering his eyes.","Combat art of the heavenly dao—Eye of Nullification!","Lu Yun’s jaw dropped at the name. He... must have had a similar combat art in the past, one with a different name!","......","The days passed one by one as all remained calm in Darklake. It’d been one year since Lu Yun claimed the sword pagoda. Emperor Situ Wenxian of Darklake Empire was a decisive man. He immediately relinquished his claim over the Profound Wing Empire when he received word of the situation that’d developed. Profound Wing was an enormous vortex these days, sucking in ever-increasing numbers of immortals.","Although no one could map what was precisely in the crater, it could be certain that there was the legacy of an ancient immortal at the bottom. The three ninth rank empires were up in arms and had sent countless combination, tribulation, awakened, and even wandering cultivators to it.","The former Iron Pagoda Mountain had been renamed to Immortal Burial Valley.","It earned its new name after the ninth rank empires sent three wandering cultivators to explore it. None of the three returned.","The valley wasn’t a quiet locale. It erupted twelve times a year in the middle of each month. Under the illumination of a bright moon, all sorts of treasures, pills, medicines, or ingredients shot out from the crater. Most of them were low level, but there were always a few gems within that caused the combination or tribulation powerhouses to go mad with greed.","Immortal Burial Valley became well known throughout the entire world.","......","The breeze was brisk on a clear autumn morning. Terra Demon rushed into Lu Yun’s yard. The young man was partaking in breakfast through Lan’er’s service.","“What is it, Terra Demon?” Lu Yun put down the fried dough stick and soybean milk in his hands.","“Young master, I know what the treasures and pills found in Immortal Burial are.” Terra Demon’s expression was unspeakably odd.","“Oh?” Lu Yun shoved another dough stick in his mouth and began chewing slowly. This food item didn’t exist in the world of cultivation, but was something that he subconsciously remembered that he liked.","It didn’t exist in any of his three thousand reincarnations.","Two golden fried dough sticks and a bowl of soy milk from spirit beans were his unshakeable habit. His eating preferences had spread to the rest of the family—even Lu Tianling and Lu Xiaochi liked these two options.","“They’re all... immortal weapons, immortal pills, immortal medicines, and immortal ingredients!” Terra Demon garbled out. Lan’er was used to this kind of discourse and took out another set of bowl and chopsticks, serving the young man a bowl of soy milk and two dough sticks.","Terra Demon didn’t stand on ceremony. He grabbed the food and started munching his way through them. When in the world of immortals, the High Lord of the Northern Sky had been well known for being down to earth. He often ate at the same table with his men, which was one of the reasons whey they were so loyal to him.","“Some strange existence has consumed their core essence, which is why their ranks have declined.” Terra Demon swallowed a mouthful of soy milk. “Since their essence has been damaged, they cannot be repaired.” His tone was full of regret.","“Then let them be.” Lu Yun didn’t really care as he couldn’t use an immortal treasure even if it appeared in front of him right now. It would only bring trouble to the family. The tens of thousands of items he’d brought back from the valley were stored in the vaults.","“It’s likely that these items were all once from the world of immortals,” Terra Demon sighed, summoning an emerald ring to his hand. It was a lower spirit rank weapon.","“Isn’t this the Spiritlock Ring that you refined?” Lu Yun recognized it as one of Terra Demon’s most vaunted creations. It was a ninth rank immortal weapon that would immobilize even an ordinary immortal potentate. He’d bequeathed it to one of most accomplished disciples, but it’d returned to him after all these eons.","Lu Yun hadn’t paid a return visit to Immortal Burial Valley, but Terra Demon had gone a few times. The mid dao rank weapon that he’d given Yong Heyu had come from the crater, so it seemed likely that his old weapon had been recovered there as well.","etvolare's Thoughts","So obviously there's a huge overlap in names. Do you guys think that the Lu Yun of the three thousand lifetimes subconsciously recreated everything from his sealed lifetime?"]},{"number":2260,"title":"Chapter 2260: Chapter 2179.1: Terra Demon Takes a Disciple","paragraphs":["Chapter 2179.1: Terra Demon Takes a Disciple","Terra Demon had been the remains of a tattered will at the time, so he hadn’t sensed the abnormalities beneath the sword pagoda. And being a vaunted immortal king, he didn’t look twice at a dao weapon. Thus, he didn’t mention anything beneath the mountain.","Yet when Celestial Empress Myrtlestar’s Cosmic Banner shot out of the crater, he realized how serious the matter at hand was.","Lu Yun didn’t mind, the truth would always come out in the end. He was too weak at the moment, so the investigation could wait until he grew stronger.","Sorrow shone in Terra Demon’s eyes.","“Don’t worry, we can always bring it back to what it once was.” Lu Yun clapped his shoulder. The young man nodded in response.","“Young master, Ouyang Shengtian has come.” A seemingly reborn Lu Xuan set foot through the day. Eyes as radiant as the stars, he now practiced the Sword of Slaughter Record. His cultivation had grown to initial nascent soul and he brimmed with a dashing air. Although he tread the path of slaughter, he didn’t walk around with a bloodthirsty presence.","The true sword of slaughter didn’t reveal itself before it was deployed. It was meant to kill, not to intimidate.","“Ouyang Shengtian? Let him in.” Lu Yun nodded.","The Ouyang alliance with the Lus after Ouyang Shengtian’s possession completely upended everyone’s worldview. Of the three families that were set against the Lu Clan, the Ling Clan was completely nullified, the Ouyang Clan was now friends with them, which left only the Yuwens still holding on for dear life.","But the Yuwens had received support from the Nineheavens Pagoda and thus seen their strength leap forward. They showed signs of eclipsing the greatest family in the capital—the Mo Clan—and replacing them as the foremost faction beneath the royal family.","Lu Yun ignored the Yuwens and Ouyang Shengtian couldn’t be bothered to pay attention to them either.","“Hahaha, young master Lu, it’s been a while. You look as wonderful as ever!” Ouyang Shengtian entered the yard alone, wariness flashing through his eyes when he saw Terra Demon sitting with Lu Yun.","“Out with your shit, I don’t have time for this.” Lu Yun couldn’t be bothered with pleasantries since he knew Ouyang Shengtian was a wily old fox.","The young man chuckled and sat next to the two. Lan’er brought over more dough sticks and soy milk, but Ouyang Shengtian didn’t eat them. He didn’t know Lu Yun’s temper like Terra Demon did and he’d long forgone food thanks to his accomplishments in cultivation. It’d be one thing if it was legendary spirit grains and cuisines, but the soybean milk and dough sticks were just ordinary items.","“The Yuwen Clan’s opened a new pill storefront and taken over the entire Vermilion Avenue in the southern quadrant. It's a clear provocation of our two families.” A solemn look was in Ouyang Shengtian’s eyes.","With the decline of the Ling Clan, the Ouyang and Lu Clans jointly split it up. Its businesses became the property of the two clans. Given its weak foundations, the Lu Clan would face tremendous pressure if it took over the Ling Clan by itself. Things were immensely different, however, if the Ouyang Clan was involved—they were much more established in Darklake. Additionally, the Ouyangs and Lings had shared an underground alliance.","Most important was that Lu Yun knew the ins and outs of Ouyang Shengtian’s background. The young man was just resting in the Ouyang Clan for the moment. He wasn’t actually interested in a third rank cultivation empire.","He hadn’t been willing to have further doings with the Lu Clan, but didn’t have a choice after Lu Yun came calling one day with Terra Demon.","These days, the Ouyangs and Lus exercised a monopoly over the pill and medicine markets in Dark City. The Ouyang Clan was the market leader on the surface while the Lu Clan collected its profits in the dark.","The joint collective between the two clans immediately cornered the pill and medicine markets in Darklake Empire and created massive profits.","This time, the Yuwen Clan occupied the most prosperous Vermilion Avenue and opened a grand shop. Their prices were thirty percent lower than the Ouyangs and Lus, and their supply steady and significant. Their quality was even slightly better, so there was a drastic drop in business at the Ouyang stores just after three days.","Ouyang Shengtian was no ordinary person. He knew a little about the Yuwens and that they had secret backers, so he immediately rushed to discuss things with Lu Yun. There was no denying it—he’d been forced to join Lu Yun’s side. While he didn’t fear the Nineheavens Pagoda, their backer was someone he couldn’t afford to offend even before he’d taken possession of Ouyang Shengtian.","“Let the Yuwens and Nineheavens Pagoda hop around since they want to. The only thing they’re doing is helping Darklake reap more taxes.” Lu Yun didn’t mind. He’d gained a very competent helper after finding Terra Demon; the family had advanced at an astounding pace over the past year. He didn’t care about small fry like the Yuwen Clan and Nineheavens Pagoda.","“I’m just concerned that the Origin Sect doesn’t think the same way,” Ouyang Shengtian sighed. “They haven’t been able to sit still with the emergence of Immortal Burial Valley. They’re using the Yuwen Clan and Nineheavens Pagoda to control Darklake and Dark Orchid.”","Lu Yun tilted his head and looked at Ouyang Shengtian.","“I know what young master Lu’s ambitions are,” the Ouyang young master chuckled. “You want to be the master of the Jade Ruins Realm, don’t you?”","Terra Demon curled his lip. Master of the Jade Ruins Realm? Was that supposed to be viewed as ambition? When His Grace roamed the land, he had innumerable dynasties such as Great Xia beneath his banner. What would he do with a Jade Ruins Realm?","But the current high lord was a tiger down in the plains, removed from his mountain. He was a dragon in shallow waters... Ai. All the same, if someone wanted to bully the high lord, they did so with a death wish!","Ouyang Shengtian continued when Lu Yun remained silent, “The Jade Ruins Realm is now famous throughout the realms because of Immortal Burial Valley. The aura of an immortal treasure is emanating from the bottom. It will likely be ejected in the coming days.”","“So you’re saying that the Origin Sect will start with Darklake and Dark Orchid to control the entire realm?” Lu Yun naturally grasped Ouyang Shengtian’s meaning.","“The rules in the worlds of cultivation are so powerful that immortals tread lightly here. But it’s also an easy task for the Origin Sect to take control of the realm. Once it does, both you and I will be in deep water,” Ouyang Shengtian sighed.","“There’s nothing to worry about as long as immortals stay away. They can conquer the realm if they want, it’ll make things easier for us.” Lu Yun still didn’t care.","Ouyang Shengtian was speechless and had no idea where the young man’s confidence stemmed from. But since this was Lu Yun’s final word, there was nothing else he could say.","“Hahahaha!!” Overjoyed laughter traveled in from the distance as Lu Tianling kicked open Lu Yun’s door. “Yun’er, wonderful news, wonderful news!”","Ordinarily a genteel and refined man, Lu Tianling could be the coarsest of them all when the mood seized him. His laughter could be heard through most of the capital.","“What are you so happy about, grandfather?” Lu Yun asked curiously.","Lu Tianling had returned after half a year of absence and didn’t give an explanation of where he’d gone. Lu Yun didn’t ask, and Terra Demon performed the bow of a junior when he greeted the Lu patriarch.","“Senior Helian Shan has finally agreed to take your second uncle as his disciple, hahaha!!” Lu Tianling continued roaring with laughter.","“Eh... what did you say?” Lu Yun asked stiltedly.","“Senior Helian Shan, the law enforcer from the Xuanhuang Empire, has agreed to take your second uncle as a disciple! He is an awakened cultivator! The Lus only had three of them back in the day!” Lu Tianling clapped his hands happily. “Senior Helian Shan has come, so hurry and welcome him, Yun’er! We are going to set a magnificent banquet and celebrate for three days straight!”","“Long time no see, little friend Lu Yun.” Helian Shan’s voice echoed behind Lu Tianling. He was dressed in his usual black and the typical remote expression on his face.","One year ago, Lu Xiaochi joined ninth rank empire Xuanhuang through Fengxian Wu’s introduction and became one of their very important members. He gained the right to enter the Celestial Realm Battlefront and advanced rapidly in his cultivation. Now latter nascent soul, there were few opponents of his caliber in his cultivation level.","Helian Shan had paid extra attention to Lu Xiaochi on account of Fengxian Wu, then discovered that the man’s foundations ran deep and his powers of comprehension were astounding. The urge to take a disciple struck him and he visited Darklake this time to officially take Lu Xiaochi. He would join the law enforcers.","Lu Tianling was extraordinarily delighted—he wouldn’t pay attention to Helian Shan if the latter was a regular awakened cultivator, but the law enforcer had been specially nurtured by Great Xia royalty. He would be a preeminent personage even in Great Xia, and there’d been only three awakened cultivators when the Lu Clan had been in its prime!","Lu Xiaochi becoming a law enforcer’s disciple also meant that Lu Tianling had the chance of returning to Great Xia through legitimate means and rebuilding the family.","A beaming Lu Xiaochi followed Helian Shan. Although Lu Tianling had once taught him cultivation, the Lu patriarch paled far in comparison to the law enforcer.","Ouyang Shengtian sighed inwardly at the Lu Clan’s good fortune. They had a law enforcer for a backer now! That meant that the Origin Sect would no longer dare openly investigate Lu Tianling.","“You are Helian Shan?” Terra Demon frowned with arctic air."]},{"number":2261,"title":"Chapter 2261: Chapter 2179.2: Terra Demon Takes a Disciple","paragraphs":["Chapter 2179.2: Terra Demon Takes a Disciple","“A soul projection cultivator?” Helian Shan was about to address Lu Yun and ask after Fengxian Wu when a young servant spoke to him in an impudent tone. How dare he, and when had a soul projection cultivator appeared in the Lu Clan?","But on second thought, it made sense since Fengxian Wu resided at the Lus.","“I am.” Although Helian Shan didn’t know who Terra Demon was, the cold look in the other’s eyes irked him.","“How does a mere awakened cultivator have the right to be the second master’s teacher?” Terra Demon was a lofty immortal king, after all. He naturally wouldn’t give face to a tiny awakened cultivator.","Helian Shan stared in a daze, Lu Tianling’s smile froze, and Lu Xiaochi suddenly found the scene surreal. Ouyang Shengtian’s mind abruptly stopped working.","“Lan’er, you are dismissed.” Lu Yun patted Lan’er’s shoulder and pulled her back to her senses. She quickly took her leave and fled back to her room.","“Long time no see, Senior Helian.” Lu Yun nodded smilingly at Helian Shan.","“Hmph.” Helian Shan was an exalted law enforcer—even an emperor of a ninth rank emperor would treat him with respect. Who would’ve thought that he’d find such irreverence in a minor third rank empire?","“You do indeed lack the right to be my second uncle’s master,” Lu Yun continued with the same smile.","Helian Shan remained expressionless. He was an awakened cultivator with extreme mental fortitude. A few ants wouldn’t cause him to lose his composure, not to mention that Fengxian Wu was still in residence at the Lu Clan.","“Does Xiaochi have another master?” There was no emotion in Helian Shan’s voice.","“Yun’er!” Lu Tianling interrupted. “I know your master is an immortal, but immortals are hobbled by numerous rules in a world of cultivation...”","“Don’t worry, milord, the young master has his own plans in mind,” Terra Demon assured. He was particularly respectful to the Lu clan members as they were the high lord’s family in this life.","“Your master is an immortal? A wandering immortal or empyrean immortal?” Helian Shan blinked, understanding what Lu Yun meant. If Lu Xiaochi had the option of learning from an immortal instead, then he did indeed lack the right to teach the man.","But this realm had become off limits to immortals due to Immortal Burial Valley. If any immortal dared trespass without permission from Great Xia, they would be immediately obliterated upon discovery.","“Young master, this person’s potential is promising and he is suited to walk my path.” Terra Demon suddenly looked Helian Shan up and down.","“You want to take him as a disciple?” Lu Yun’s eyes widened with astonishment.","Terra Demon was very strict about who he took for his disciples. He’d only had two back in the world of immortals. Any other immortal king would have at least one hundred true or nominal disciples.","Terra Demon nodded while everyone found their conversation beyond comprehension. A soul projection cultivator wanted to take an awakened cultivator as his disciple? Had the world gone completely insane??","Lu Tianling felt his heart spasm painfully. He didn’t dare think about what was to come, just that it was now out of the question for Helian Shan to take Lu Xiaochi as his disciple.","“Hahahahah!!” Helian Shan finally broke out in furious laughter. “A soul projection ant wishes to be my master?!”","He was truly angry as this had gone beyond the limits of face slapping. It was pointed humiliation!","BOOM!","Raging aura exploded from his body. He punched straight forward without any bells and whistles, aiming for Terra Demon’s chest.","Ouyang Shengtian, Lu Tianling, and Lu Xiaochi paled with horror. Even the complex’s Major Cycle Nebula Formation shook from the blow. A furious blow from an awakened cultivator was too terrifying to endure!","“Your true origin is powerful and your strength is decent enough, but you utilize them in such a crude way. His... the young master once said that the times advance with progress, that the present is always stronger than the past. So why do you...” Terra Demon sighed as he watched the frightening blow. “You commit a sin for not respecting your master, and you commit a greater sin for being disrespectful in front of the young master! On your knees!”","Something flashed in front of the group and a thump rang out. Helian Shan suddenly knelt in front of Lu Yun while Terra Demon stood expressionlessly behind him!","Lu Tianling, Lu Xiaochi, and Ouyang Shengtian were too stunned to know how to react.","Terra Demon differed from Lu Yun in that the young man’s experiences were just a dream. They were gone after he woke up, leaving only the experiences of his memories. Terra Demon, however, was a bonafide immortal king. Despite possessing only a soul projection body, he didn’t need to exert any effort to manhandle an awakened cultivator.","Immortal kings were the peak of the world of immortals, second to only the five immortal emperors! [1]","No one below an immortal was a threat to Terra Demon, not even some of the weaker immortals. Since his nascent soul was damaged, he wouldn’t be able to contend against a truly strong immortal without absolute strength.","Helian Shan’s heart shook with shock; he’d clearly seen every move that the other had made. It was like Terra Demon had strolled through a garden, casually circling around him and kicking his knees down. A massive surge of strength had reared its head to force Helian Shan into his current position.","Although he’d seen the other’s moves and captured his footsteps with his consciousness, his body hadn’t been able to react. It was like the silver-haired young man in front of him didn’t come from the real world. He came from another, crossing through endless space and layers of planes to arrive behind him and kick him.","“Are you willing to recognize me as your master?” Terra Demon asked without the arrogance or contempt of someone in a superior position.","“Are you, are you an immortal?” Helian Shan asked in a shaking voice.","“An immortal? I guess you could say that,” Terra Demon replied noncommittally.","“Are you... Yun’er’s master?” Lu Tianling finally found his voice again.","“The young master’s teacher?” Terra Demon’s face flickered through a variety of expressions. Everything I know comes from His Grace’s hands. Although we weren’t formally master and disciple, our relationship was that of one. When did I become His Grace’s master?","He thought of the young man in blue who’d appeared within the sword pagoda one year ago—the high lord’s senior brother. His aura and presence had been as vast as the seas. It was something he hadn’t sensed even in the high lord back in his time.","What kind of existence would the high lord’s master be?","But Terra Demon knew that Lu Yun respected Lu Tianling immensely, so he simply shook his head and didn’t respond with any unpleasantry.","“The young master’s teacher is a domineering powerhouse of the realms. I am just the young master’s servant. There is no need to think more on that, milord.”","Helian Shan sucked in a sharp breath. This silver-haired young man who looked to be only soul projection, but was in reality unfathomably strong... was just a servant? Then how enormous was the faction behind Lu Yun?","It doesn’t seem impossible to stand up to the Origin Sect if he has this kind of background and power. Ouyang Shengtian was starting to care less about being tied to Lu Yun’s ship. An imperceptible light flashed through his eyes—he wouldn’t be able to fend off Terra Demon even in his prime. What the silver-haired young man displayed moments ago was the methods of an empyrean immortal.","Ouyang Shengtian was even more keenly aware that having seen some of Lu Yun’s trump cars, he only had two options left to him now. One, he could be utterly loyal to Lu Yun or two, Terra Demon could smash him to death on the spot.","He also finally understood what Lu Yun meant by the Origin Sect not being a threat as long as immortals didn’t come. With someone like Terra Demon holding down the fort, no one below immortal was a threat to the Lus!","Lu Tianling and Lu Xiaochi raised their brows at each other. It looked like the sudden addition of this incredible powerhouse was the work of Lu Yun’s master. Did his master not come from Great Xia? Or was he so strong that he could overlook all of the worlds of cultivation and the rules set by the heavenly book?","Great Xia powerhouses could not easily enter a world of cultivation without approval, but neither were they so bored that they would do so without reason. This particular world was protected by the heavenly book, but also curtailed by it. Qi was so sparse here that it was an impoverished backwater.","“Are you willing to accept me as your master?” An aloof Terra Demon circled around Helian Shan.","“My master is the chief enforcer for the Jade Ruins Realm and an immortal immortal. As strong as you are, you are far from him.” Helian Shan’s eyes were red from force of effort. He was trying to struggle to his feet, but an unknown method kept him kneeling at Lu Yun’s feet.","“An immortal immortal?” Terra Demon blinked and swept a gaze over Helian Shan. He shook his head. “You are not the disciple of an empyrean immortal—a nominal one at best. I do not sense the presence of an empyrean immortal on you and you’ve probably never even met your so-called master.”","Helian Shan’s heart shook, incredulity filling his eyes. How was the young man correct about even that?","“Kowtow to your master,” Lu Yun interjected. “You’re just a nominal disciple, your old master won’t mind.”","When he built a relationship with Helian Shan through Fengxian Wu, he’d done so with the intent of forging some sort of bond. But bringing the man under his banner would be even better.","1. I don’t know if the author is conflating immortal potentate and immortal emperor here, because Lu Yun was his liege lord back in the day. However, we’ve also seen mention of the central immortal emperor, so it stands to reason that there are indeed five immortal emperors. Yet Lu Yun was called an immortal potentate so... cue question marks? ☜"]},{"number":2262,"title":"Chapter 2262: Chapter 2180.1: Impending Chaos","paragraphs":["Chapter 2180.1: Impending Chaos","“Terra Demon could crush one hundred empyrean immortals with a single finger in his prime,” Lu Yun transmitted to Helian Shan. It was a staggering notion, but it might be useful to let the man learn a bit more about them.","Lu Yun had far more trump cards than this.","A Terra Demon in his peak could blow thousands of immortals to death with one exhale, to say nothing of one hundred empyrean immortals. Immortal kings were the peak existences of the world of immortals and empyrean immortals simply baby immortals.","Helian Shan stared at Lu Yun with utter shock.","Two faint dots of gold flashed through the young man’s eyes. Helian Shan suddenly felt that he had no secrets in front of the Lu young master.","“Disciple Helian Shan greets the master!” Helian Shan grit his teeth and turned his head with effort, but still remained kneeling in Lu Yun’s direction.","“A connate mortal constitution is destined to be barred from immortality, but walking my path means that setting foot through the doors of immortality are but a matter of time!” A smile finally broke through Terra Demon’s aloof expression.","Lu Yun didn’t find his statement surprising. A connate mortal constitution was the same constitution that Terra Demon once had, but he’d resolved it to help the latter become one of the peak existences in the world of immortals.","Helian Shan had the same constitution and would never become an immortal if nothing unexpected happened. He’d stop at the peak of awakened cultivation.","The law enforcer shook like a leaf when he heard Terra Demon’s last words. Being unable to become an immortal was the primary reason why the chief enforcer hadn’t accepted him as a disciple. How would he not be agitated to hear from his new master that the opportunity existed after all?","He didn’t doubt Terra Demon’s words as anyone who could identify his constitution with a single glance was far from ordinary. If he’d previously bowed his head out of fear for the other’s strength, he did so now with wholehearted acquiescence.","With that, Helian Shan became Terra Demon’s disciple. He’d come to take a disciple, but somehow became a disciple himself. Lu Xiaochi wanted to imitate his actions, but Terra Demon declined.","He could give Lu Xiaochi pointers, but take the high lord’s second uncle as his disciple? He would never dare!","Additionally, with Lu Xiaochi’s connate spirit root of the five elements and training in Lu Yun’s Major Five Elements Demolition Godslayer Record, Terra Demon didn’t have the right to be Lu Xiaochi’s teacher.","Activity quickly abated at the Lu residence that’d been ready to erupt in banquets and celebrations for three straight days. Everyone in the capital soon learned that the Lu second master had been ready to become a law enforcer’s disciple, but plans had fallen through. The Lu Clan immediately became the laughingstock of Dark City.","According to rumors from the Lu household, the vaunted law enforcer had changed his mind primarily because of the Lu good-for-nothing. The prodigal young master had been so arrogant that he’d offended the enforcer, making the latter leave in a huff.","With that, Lu Yun’s infamy was even greater than before. He dared offend eminent law enforcers! There really was nothing that the pestilence of Dark City didn’t dare do!","In the meantime, the Yuwen pill workshops operated and expanded with relish. Spirit stones flowed into the Yuwen Clan like water and the Nineheavens Pagoda supporting them gradually revealed itself. The Ouyang pill pagodas were completely eliminated from the capital and from the empire as a whole.","After the pill and medicine markets, the Yuwen Clan struck in all major industries relevant to cultivators. Other than the Mo, Lu, and Ouyang Clans, all other clans in the capital shifted to the Yuwens’ side—even the Zhao and Yu Clans.","Lu Yun remained oblivious to everything and went about his daily business. These days, he was very tight-knit with a group of cultivators from the northern quadrant as their greatest benefactor. He often visited these dregs of society because he wished to collect goodwill. When it came to helping the weak and poor... Well, he was no saint. He was here only to accomplish his own goals.","But thanks to his efforts, the living situation in the northern quadrant showed marked improvement. The Lu young master was still an irredeemable thug in their eyes, however, because he visited the northern quadrant disguised as another.","He was incredibly well known throughout the empire and after the Ouyangs allied with the Lus, there was no one who could keep him in check. If he swaggered into the northern quadrant, no one would be the least bit grateful to him. They wouldn’t even dare pick up spirit stones that he flung into the street.","Thanks to goodwill from tens of thousands cultivators, he was now peak initial golden core and a step away from mid golden core.","......","Mo Qiyue came to visit on this day.","“You’ve exerted control over the Ouyangs?” He looked at Lu Yun with surprise and incomprehension. He’d spent the past year in Great Xia as opposed to staying in Darklake, so he didn’t know what’d taken place before returning.","“But why expose yourself if you’ve taken over the Ouyangs? You could have them lie low in the enemy camp and be your spies. Wouldn’t that benefit you more?” Mo Qiyue was very curious as, after a series of exchanges with Lu Yun, he was certain that the Lu young master wasn’t the number one profligate that the rumors made him out to be. He was indeed a prodigal, but a wastrel? It was more like him wasting his opponents.","Lu Yun curled his lip; Ouyang Shengtian was a wily old fox. Who knew what he’d get up to if Lu Yun didn’t stabilize him as soon as possible? Have him be a spy for the Lus? Lu Yun would more likely get lost in a series of double crosses.","He could make use of Ouyang Shengtian, but never trust him. Perhaps the guy was an undercover agent sent by the enemy!","“Aiya!” Lu Yun smacked himself on the forehead with regret. “Why didn’t I think of that? I was just so concerned with increasing the family’s strength as fast as possible...”","Mo Qiyue looked dumbly at the young man, not knowing what to say.","“Ah, whatever, you always put on a good act,” he chuckled ruefully. “Where’s Miss Fengxian? I’m here for her this time.”","“Fengxian Wu? Does her family want her back?” Lu Yun blinked, then understood the situation. Given the appearance of Immortal Burial Valley, the Profound Wing, Dark, and Darklake Empires were about to be plunged into chaos. Fengxian Wu was just golden core, so her family would not be at ease leaving her in the Jade Ruins Realm.","Mo Qiyue had long been aware of Fengxian Wu’s presence at the Lu residence. An awkward expression had flashed across her face when they met at the Beast Colosseum; it was then that Lu Yun began suspecting Mo Qiyue’s identity.","That was why he hadn’t shown face to anyone but the Mo young master.","“Miss Fengxian Wu said she wanted to visit Immortal Burial Valley three days ago, so I sent Terra Demon with her. They’ve probably arrived by now,” Lu Yun answered after a pause.","“What?!” Mo Qiyue paled when he heard the response.","“What’s wrong?” Lu Yun frowned. Something was amiss. Immortal Burial Valley was a very fat sheep that regularly spewed out treasures, pills, and medicines. While none of them were anything high rank, they were still extremely valuable to any empire beneath sixth rank.","More importantly was that the items were all previously immortal items. They were very useful to Lu Yun, which is why he sent family members to collect them.","“Great Xia has decided to investigate Immortal Burial Valley.”","Those of Great Xia snorted at the valley’s name. A place being called Immortal Burial Valley simply because three wandering immortals had died there? A world of cultivation was a world of country bumpkins indeed.","Since the dynasty wished to investigate the valley, the royal family had to decrease the heavenly book’s influence over the Jade Ruins Realm to the lowest degree possible. That would make room for cultivators of other worlds and some of Great Xia’s own wandering immortals to surge into Jade Ruins Realm. All of that would send the realm into confusion.","“When?” Lu Yun’s face stilled. This would result in great changes to the land.","“Three months.” Mo Qiyue concealed nothing as these details weren't a secret to certain people. “The Human Emperor of Great Xia, eight kings, and thirty-six marquises have entered the Celestial Realm Battlefront to call upon the heavenly book. Its influence over the Jade Ruins Realm will gradually decrease starting from today and be completely nullified after three months. That is when Great Xia immortals will enter the realm.”","“So this means that a growing mess will engulf the realm starting from today?” Lu Yun narrowed his eyes. How interesting.","The heavenly book restricted immortals from entering a world of cultivation. Only when the book’s effects were nullified could immortals fully deploy their might in a world of cultivation.","Otherwise, the worlds remained the home of cultivators and taboo to immortals! After all, it wouldn’t be worthy of its name if immortals could come and go at will.","“Do you know who the Lu Clan enemy is?” Mo Qiyue sighed.","“The Origin Sect of Great Xia, how are they?” asked Lu Yun.","etvolare's Thoughts","Is he really still calling Terra Demon by that name in front of everyone lol. He... should probably change it, huh?"]},{"number":2263,"title":"Chapter 2263: Chapter 2180.2: Impending Chaos","paragraphs":["Chapter 2180.2: Impending Chaos","“Marquis Origin of the Origin Sect was once a slave of the Lu Clan. When disaster struck the family, he turned on his masters. After he seized the Lu marquis position, he hunted down the rest of the clan.","“Your grandfather’s line was lucky enough to escape and maintained a standing of a third rate Great Xia family. But afterwards, your grandfather stumbled upon an immortal weapon and an ancient immortal’s legacy in the Celestial Realm Battlefront. His cultivation advanced with giant strides and he showed signs of revitalizing the clan.","“The Origin Sect crushed the Lu survivors overnight when it received word of the bright future. Your grandfather managed to flee thanks to the might of the treasure, and you know what happened next,” Mo Qiyue couldn’t help but sigh. The Lu Clan was once so magnificent and awe-inspiring. Hailed as the leader of the thirty-six marquises of Great Xia, they were almost titled kings. Everything changed in the blink of an eye and further persecution from Marquis Origin meant that they were nearly extinct.","The matter had been general knowledge back in the day.","Mo Qiyue hadn’t known who Lu Tianling was at first; he learned of the complete history after making some inquiries at his sect.","The current Origin Sect rivaled the Lu Clan of old and Marquis Origin was one of the strongest marquises in the dynasty. Who dared take a celestial marquis to task for past crimes? Not to mention, the Lu Clan was so feeble that it almost didn’t exist anymore. No one would offend Marquis Origin for the disgraced remnants of a shattered family.","Lu Yun remained silent for a long while when he heard Mo Qiyue’s words. “The affairs of the world are inconstant and nothing is eternal. Where there is prosperity, so is there decline. My clan once soared at the peak of glory, but fell at the end. Such is the cycle of reincarnation that cannot be denied.","“But as a slave of my family, Marquis Origin repaid a debt of gratitude with vicious brutality. This grudge must be answered in kind!”","The everlasting cycle of living and dying was the only eternal truth of existence. Just like reincarnation, there was no existence that was forever or a void perpetual. Even the objective existence of nothing was not eternal.","Mo Qiyue fell silent.","......","Immortal Burial Valley had become the heart of Jade Ruins Realm and the eye of the storm. Its earth was blood red from constant violence and an uncountable number of cultivators had died over the past year. Great Xia’s decision to investigate the valley further raised a disturbance, resulting in higher ranked empires who hadn’t cared about it before also stirring to action.","It was like a keg of firepower ignited the second the heavenly book’s power over the realm was nullified. It had kept the realm under constant surveillance like a massive eye. Anything that happened was immediately recorded in its pages.","When the human demon Bloodbath went on a rampage in a fifth rank empire, it was immediately captured by the treasure and relayed to the law enforcers. That resulted in the ninth rank empires issuing an arrest warrant for Bloodbath.","It also suppressed any external immortal that visited the realm. If the immortal dared plague the world, then the heavenly book would activate and kill the offending immortal.","No one knew who’d created it. It seemed omnipresent and kept watch over the world like a miniature heavenly dao. With its power being weakened, the realm plunged into chaos.","Immortal Burial Valley.","“That woman grabbed the half step immortal pill that just flew out. After her!” Countless cultivators surged in a certain direction like the floodwaters.","The crater had just erupted moments ago, sending out a stream of pills and medicines. There was a half step immortal pill among them, a treasure that would command attention even in Great Xia.","Fengxian Wu had been very excited to see it. To think that she’d obtain an immortal pill on her first visit to Immortal Burial Valley! The half step immortal pill was bursting with uncommonly gentle power. If she refined it, she’d likely break through on the spot and form her nascent soul.","There were too many other cultivators present, however, a full one hundred thousand of them. There were numerous high ranked cultivators as well. Not even Terra Demon wished to meet them head-on, so he motioned to Fengxian Wu and fled in the opposite direction.","A moderately sized city had developed near Immortal Burial Valley over the past year. Untold numbers of cultivators had settled down in it, spending their days waiting for the crater to erupt. It brought forth a shower of treasures once a month—this instance was the thirteenth of the year. Each eruption incited bloody struggles in the valley. The worst of them had caused more than ten thousand casualties, but that hardly deterred would-be fortune seekers. Increasing numbers of cultivators arrived in the valley every day.","Only one item resulted from the thirteenth eruption—a half step immortal pill.","Boom!","One hundred thousand cultivators attacked at the same time, flinging a motley array of arts and treasures. Terra Demon’s eyes widened and he grabbed Fengxian Wu, disappearing in the sky.","They were dozens of kilometers away when they reappeared.","Pfft!","Terra Demon paled as he spat out a mouthful of blood. Though he was the nascent soul of an immortal king, his current cultivation was only soul projection. Simultaneous attacks from one hundred thousand cultivators were enough to break his bones to pieces.","“That group of lunatics would’ve smashed a real immortal pill with that reaction, to say nothing of a half step immortal pill!” Terra Demon’s heart pounded after he spat out blood. As fast as he’d run, the combined blow from so many cultivators had injured him with just its presence. A wandering immortal would’ve been vaporized by it.","“Are you alright, senior?!” Fengxian Wu threw out the pill when she saw Terra Demon’s condition and the horde of cultivators in hot pursuit. “Here it is, you can have it!”","“Don’t trust her! How would she so easily give up a half step immortal pill? She threw out a fake!” someone called out with the crowd. It drifted in and out of hearing, making it impossible to determine where or who it came from. That galvanized the hesitating cultivators and they focused on the duo again.","“You’re purposefully instigating things and deserve death!” Terra Demon snorted, sending out a ray of silver sword light with a lift of his hand. One agonized scream later, it returned to him with a keening nascent soul.","“Were you the one telling tales?” He regarded it coldly, reducing the nascent soul to dust. Despite one hundred thousand cultivators covering the land and sky, blotting out the sun like a thundercloud, he’d still killed who he wanted to kill.","“One of you already has the immortal pill. I will show mercy to none of you if you continue to pursue us.” Terra Demon wiped away blood from the corner of his lips. “The next to die might be you.”","Silver sword light circled around him like an argent snake. Overwhelming killing intent forced a collective shudder out of the cultivators. There were one hundred thousand of them, including a few awakened cultivators, but no one dared come forward.","Fengxian Wu was also stunned. She’d been slightly dissatisfied that Lu Yun had only sent Terra Demon to protect her, but she now understood that her guard rivaled a wandering immortal. If it wasn’t for her presence, he could easily retreat at will.","“There’s only one of him and one hundred thousand of us, we’re not afraid of him! C’mon guys, let’s band together and—” A shriek quickly cut off when silver light flashed by. The radiance returned with a dead nascent soul hanging on Terra Demon’s sword.","It belonged to a combination cultivator!","Silver sword radiance twinkled in Terra Demon’s eyes, pulverizing the struggling nascent spirit. Rays upon rays of sword light formed around Fengxian Wu, cocooning her with protection.","“Piss off or die.” Silver light blazed nine meters from Terra Demon’s eyes. His hair danced wildly as killing intent ballooned his aura.","Shocked, one hundred cultivators uniformly took a step back. They all recalled a story of a combination cultivator slaughtering one million cultivators in the powerful fifth rank Barren Empire, thereby causing its overnight demise.","However, being a fifth rank empire meant that Barren’s strongest powerhouse was just soul separation. Bloodbath had also been a combination cultivator. The one in front of them was just soul projection and he faced an army that included awakened cultivators.","Although some weaker foundation establishment and golden core cultivators could be found in the horde, most of them were soul separation and combination powerhouses. Nearly half of them were stronger than Terra Demon.","The masses parted and five awakened cultivators walked out together.","“We’ll spare your life if you hand over your treasure!” The five were dressed in varying outfits and nursed different ripples of power. Plainly, they were from different factions. One of them was an elder three meters tall who seemed to speak for the group.","Terra Demon was just a soul projection cultivator, but had picked out a combination cultivator from the horde and instantly killed them. Some now suspected that he carried a heaven defying treasure on him.","There were no human emotions to be found on Terra Demon’s face; he was enveloped by silver light.","“Die!” he sat out.","Whoosh!","He rushed forward, the silver flying sword in his hand churning toward the five awakened cultivators like an overwhelming stream of stars.","Rumble!!","The river of sword qi was so magnificent that it covered three hundred meters in all directions. It seemed like a leaping river, but was also immutable as a mountain. It crashed down on the five with domineering force.","The five looked on with dismay. Who would’ve thought that a soul projection cultivator would erupt with so much power?","etvolare's Thoughts","I like how Fengxian Wu cares for Terra Demon. She's got some empathy as opposed to being a spoiled little princess."]},{"number":2264,"title":"Chapter 2264: Chapter 2181.1: A Familiar Despair","paragraphs":["Chapter 2181.1: A Familiar Despair","“We cannot permit this person to live!” Among the five awakened cultivators, a dark-skinned man with bushy eyebrows frowned ferociously. “Where did Lu Tianling recruit such a perverse genius from? His strength and potential matches the finest of Great Xia! The Lu Clan will be trouble with him in their roster.”","This awakened cultivator answered to the Origin Sect banner. He yanked several hundred cultivators to him with a wave of his hand and threw them at Terra Demon’s river of sword qi.","Wails and screams crescendoed as the sky was dyed red. The other four followed his lead and swiftly threw several thousand cultivators at Terra Demon’s sword river.","As strong as he was, he was only latter soul projection. His full strength managed to kill three thousand cultivators before his sword river ground to a halt.","“Kill!” roared the Origin Sect cultivator. There was a black shortsword in his hand and he waved two rays of black light into existence around him before charging the enemy.","“The silver haired man has a heaven-defying treasure on him, which is why a soul projection cultivator can withstand the might of awakened cultivators!” someone called out from the crowd.","“That’s right, but as incredible as it is, it requires massive amounts of true origin. That man won’t hold on for much longer!”","The two voices sent the horde into a frenzy. Worlds of cultivation were never short of desperados and the mention of a heaven-defying treasure was enough to spur everyone into motion at the same time, hoping for a shot at the riches.","Safe within the sword light, color drained from Fengxian Wu’s face.","“Metal Origin Slaughter!” Terra Demon roared without a flicker of change in expression. The words formed a massive wave of sound that extended in all directions. Each character scythed into the cultivators as if keen rays of sword qi.","“Metal Origin Slaughter!”","“Metal Origin Slaughter!”","“Metal Origin Slaughter!”","Four successive shouts unfurled from Terra Demon, collecting as formless and intangible wisps of sword splendor in the void. The weaker cultivators were already bleeding from their orifices and dropping from the sky.","“The art of killing through sound!” gasped one of the awakened cultivators. Though he hastily dodged, numerous injuries already crisscrossed his body.","......","Two figures stood silently at the peak of a towering mountain outside Immortal Burial Valley.","“That subordinate of yours is terrifying!” Mo Qiyue sucked in a sharp breath as he watched Terra Demon cleave through one hundred thousand cultivators while protecting Fengxian Wu. The man had lost himself in the concentration of his arts.","“Seriously, what kind of person is your master?” Mo Qiyue turned to look at Lu Yun.","The Lu young master sighed. Though Terra Demon prowled through the battlefield like a tiger, he wouldn’t endure for too long. His was the nascent soul of an immortal king, one that consumed so many resources that Yong Heyu’s soul projection body couldn’t contain it. If the situation continued, it wouldn’t be much longer before the body collapsed.","“Being able to exert so much power at soul projection... I would say that only the perverse White is able to stop him,” Mo Qiyue continued when Lu Yun remained silent.","“White?” The Lu young master blinked; it was his second time hearing the name. The first was during his first visit to Immortal Burial Valley. When this place was still called Iron Pagoda Mountain, Mo Qiyue, Jiang Feng, and Qin Qianxue had mentioned this person.","“An absolutely perverse genius with only the cultivation of a nascent soul, but... ai,” Mo Qiyue spoke no further. “Go in there and bring back the princess.”","Three figures in black flashed into the masses as soon as he gave the order. Commotion from the horde had traveled far and wide, drawing more and more cultivators to the valley. Anyone who came attacked Terra Demon as they saw his performance with their own eyes. The more heaven defying he was, the more likely that he possessed a heaven defying treasure.","The five awakened powerhouses jointly formed a massive defensive circle that barely contained his Metal Origin Slaughter.","“Attack the woman behind him!” yelled the Origin Sect representative. He could tell that Terra Demon would be able to storm through the horde at will if the man was here alone. The man was constrained in everything he did because of the woman behind him.","Although the five awakened cultivators were from different factions, they’d reached an agreement that they could wait to fight over Terra Demon’s treasure after he died. The key thing was that he died first.","With the Origin Sect cultivator as the vanguard, the other four followed close behind him. Most of their power was concentrated on their leader.","“Break!” shouted the Origin Sect member. He sent out a ray of scarlet light that cut through Terra Demon’s art of sound and beelined for Fengxian Wu. They wanted to distract him and cause him to reveal weaknesses in a bid to protect Fengxian Wu. The five would then be able to kill him in a joint blow.","“What a strong attack, it must be a secret art!” Terra Demon creased his brow when he saw the light. Just as he was about to put himself in front of it, a figure in black arrived in front of him.","Pfft!","The scarlet light struck the figure square in the chest. The figure trembled before dispersing the light.","“The Scarlet Origin Light of the Origin Sect. Well well, very good!” The figure sharpened into focus as a man in black spirit armor and a black helmet. A black dragon seemed embossed on his armor. His voice was cold and although one couldn’t make out his features, his aloof gaze was clearly felt from the helmet.","“The Iron Dragons of Great Xia!” groaned the Origin Sect representative.","The Iron Dragons were the most elite group of cultivators that answered only to the imperial family and eight major royal families. Not even the thirty-six celestial marquises dared run afoul of these terrifying guards.","While the Iron Dragons were made of only cultivators, each of them was a preeminent powerhouse who could overpower some of the heirs of Great Xia nobility.","“Isn’t the Origin Sect more daring by the day! You dare attack even Princess Fengxian!”","Whoosh whoosh whoosh!","The other two Iron Dragons drew close as well, standing in front of Fengxian Wu and Terra Demon.","The three guards deployed their auras without reservation—they were close to the strength of immortals, not wandering immortals. The frenzied one hundred thousand cultivators collectively shuddered when the auras washed over them and halted.","“Princess Fengxian!” The Origin Sect cultivator was as pale as a sheet.","Princess Fengxian was King Fengxian’s most beloved granddaughter. After she left home due to certain things a year ago, her whereabouts became unknown. To think that she’d come to the Jade Ruins Realm!","One of the Iron Dragons sneered coldly and waved his hand, eliciting a bright dragon croon from the drawing on his armor. It charged the five awakened cultivators and ate them whole.","These five were on the same level as the Iron Dragons, but they didn’t even last one move in the exchange.","“You are not bad at all. Although you are only soul projection, you match us.” The Iron Dragons ignored the rest of the cultivators, turning to Terra Demon instead when he summoned the dragon back to him. All of them could see that if it wasn’t for Terra Demon’s dogged defense of Fengxian Wu, he would’ve killed the five awakened cultivators early on.","“Are you interested in joining the Iron Dragons?”","“No.” With this, Terra Demon understood that Lu Yun had arrived and nodded at Fengxian Wu. He streaked into silver radiance to reconvene with his lord.","The Iron Dragons weren’t displeased by his departure. They left Immortal Burial Valley with Fengxian Wu, enabling the one hundred thousand cultivators to breathe more easily. Mobility restored to the horde, they scattered in all directions.","Instead of returning to Mo Qiyue, the Iron Dragons boarded a flight treasure. Raising cupped fists to Mo Qiyue, they broke through the void and left with their precious guest.","Lu Yun heaved a long sigh of relief to see Fengxian Wu gone. It would’ve been an incredible headache if anything had happened to this young miss while she was in his care. He wouldn’t have sent Terra Demon with her if she hadn’t insisted on visiting the valley.","......","Great Xia, the Origin Province.","Bellows Mountain.","At only ten kilometers wide and several dozens of meters tall, it was a very small mountain even in a world of cultivation. However, it was the core of Origin Province. The Origin Sect, a Great Xia faction with one of the most premier marquis in residence, was located on this mountain.","A young man dressed in long golden robes, so handsome that he was almost uncanny, stood with his head tilted inside the sect’s great hall. He toyed with a golden orb the size of a fist.","“What is His Majesty the Human Emperor thinking to summon eight titled kings and thirty-six marquises for a backwater like the Jade Ruins Realm? He even disturbed the heavenly book for it,” murmured the young man as he creased his faintly golden eyebrows.","The heavenly book of the Celestial Realm Battlefront was the core of Great Xia. It was so important that disturbing it meant affecting the dynasty as a whole, not just that backwater.","The so-called Immortal Burial Valley was just a joke to the eyes of Great Xia nobility. There was at most the remains of one immortal inside, and even if it was the rumored treasure of an ancient immortal potentate, it wasn’t worth calling upon the heavenly book to do so.","The heavenly book was relevant to too many matters!"]},{"number":2265,"title":"Chapter 2265: Chapter 2181.2: A Familiar Despair","paragraphs":["Chapter 2181.2: A Familiar Despair","The uncannily handsome young man caressed the golden orb in his hand. Marquis Origin left it when he departed as he wasn’t confident in his chances of returning unscathed from the Celestial Realm Battlefront. Hence, the orb remained behind.","Bam bam bam!","Several figures flew backward from the hall’s doors—the guards to the palace. A tiny slit dotted each of their throats, their nascent spirits crumbled, and their bodies devoid of vitality. Their eyes, however, still sparkled with the watchful light of carrying out their duties.","Plainly, they hadn’t even known they were dead when death collected them.","The young man jerked his head up with shock and saw a white shadow float inside like a ghost. It was an eighteen-year-old young man dressed in clean white robes, a meter of hair flowing casually behind him. His face was tinged with an unnatural pallor, bestowing a different kind of air to his delicately shaped features. A blood-red flower in his hand made for a slightly jarring sight—it was an extraordinarily beguiling flower.","The flower’s petals were long and thin, so red that they seemed like it’d just fed on blood and was about to drip with it.","The newcomer’s eyes were without focus and his footwork strange. They created no sound as they connected with the ground and brought him to the young man in golden robes.","“Those of the Origin Sect nearly killed Fengxian Wu in the Jade Ruins Realm.” The young man spoke in a slightly hoarse, soft voice. He lifted his head and looked at Golden Robes with an unfocused gaze. “The Iron Guards have already killed that disciple and Fengxian Wu is unharmed.”","Slowly flushing deep red, Golden Robes stared fixedly at the newcomer’s cheeks.","“Does your Origin Sect really have nothing to do with the Origin disciple who attempted to assassinate the Human Emperor, but was killed in turn by his guards?” The young man mumbled to himself as he cocked his head.","“You go too far, White!” Golden Robes—Yan Beixing, eldest son of Marquis Origin—shot to his feet.","Assassinate the Human Emperor? He was the greatest powerhouse of Great Xia and his might dominated the realms. Who could possibly assassinate him?","Anyone else who spoke such ludicrous words would be dead for the offense, but White was an exception.","“What do you want?” Yan Beixing could tell that White was here to win one back for Fengxian Wu. While the two didn’t have a relationship, they were connected through her grandfather, King Fengxian.","“Is that the Lu inheritance orb in your hand?” The blankly staring eyes shifted toward the golden orb in Yan Beixing’s hand.","“The Lus?” Yan Beixing sneered. “So you want the inheritance orb? The Origin Sect has received official conferment from the Human Emperor and recognition from the heavenly book. We are one of the thirty-six marquis of Great Xia and as such, the inheritance orb belongs to us.”","White didn’t respond.","“Hmph.” Yan Beixing was an immortal while White was just a nascent soul cultivator. The difference between the two was as if heaven and earth, but Yan Beixing was very cautious of his visitor.","Whoosh!","White suddenly shifted in front of the young man. The breathtaking flower in his hand blossomed with a scintillating ray of blood light.","One petal, two petals, three petals...","Dancing gently through the air, blood-red petals enveloped Yan Beixing. Suffused with a unique beguilement, they were unearthly and preternaturally red. Deep-rooted fear flashed through the young man’s eyes.","White reached out and gently caressed the golden orb in Yan Beixing’s hand.","Snap!","The tiniest of cracks sounded as something seemed to break within it. A smear of blood floated out of the inheritance orb and dissipated in the air. White then gathered the petals together with a wave of his hand, condensing them into one petal that returned to his flower.","He left the hall with a turn.","Yan Beixing sagged with relief as sweat poured out of his brow. His uncommonly handsome face was frozen with fear.","“That pervert has the ability to kill immortals, but willingly lists himself alongside Jiang Feng, Qin Qianxue, and Mo Qiyue...” Yan Beixing’s eyes widened with horror when he looked down at the inheritance orb in his hand. “He... destroyed the Lu bloodline left in the orb...”","His eyes nearly spat fire, but he was unable to seek out White for revenge. The inheritance orb was a Lu heirloom to begin with, so there naturally were traces of the family’s bloodline within.","The Origin Sect was able to confirm Lu Tianling’s movements through the bloodline resonance of the orb and use the factions of the Jade Ruins Realm against him. Now that it’d been broken for no reason, the sect would find it very difficult to locate Lu Tianling again if he moved elsewhere.","They didn’t care about Lu Tianling, but they ardently desired the immortal weapon in his hand. The Origin Sect was a marquis-level faction, not a king-level faction. The law enforcers of the various worlds of cultivation had no need to pay them any attention.","“Servants, attend to me!” Yan Beixing roared.","......","The one hundred thousand cultivators gathered in Immortal Burial Valley had slowly dispersed. After Fengxian Wu departed, Mo Qiyue exchanged a few words with Lu Yun before leaving as well. A stony faced Terra Demon stood wordlessly behind Lu Yun.","Lu Yun approached the crater at the center of the valley and considered it in silence. He hadn’t been back since he left a year ago as the matter was too complicated. It wasn’t something that the current Lu Clan could participate in. If it hadn’t been for Fengxian Wu’s insistence on visiting, he wouldn’t have sent Terra Demon. While parts of the family had visited at various times, they hadn’t done so in such a high profile manner.","All of the cultivators here were now highly aware of Terra Demon’s might. They scattered when they saw him accompany a young man to the crater, deeply afraid that he would suddenly want revenge.","Lu Yun ignored them as purple radiance flashed through his eyes. The combat art of heavenly dao—Eye of Nullification!","Everything beneath the valley was made apparent to him and gravity filled the young man’s eyes.","“Although this Eye of Nullification isn’t as useful as the Spectral Eye, I can still see decently clearly with it.","“Eh? What’s the Spectral Eye?” Lu Yun shook his head. “We go!” He retracted the Eye of Nullification and left without hesitation.","“Is something amiss at the bottom, young master?” Terra Demon also turned grave when he saw the young man’s reaction.","“Amiss? Of course there’s something amiss!” Lu Yun took a deep breath. “Terra Demon, convey my orders to have the family’s members swiftly pull out of the area. The Lu Clan is forbidden from taking one step into Profound Wing!”","Terra Demon shook, it was his first time ever hearing Lu Yun speak in such a tone. He immediately executed Lu Yun’s command without hesitation.","“Senior brother... the sword pagoda suppressed those things. It looks like it wasn’t a treasure left by myself for a future me, but a treasure left to suppress them...” Lu Yun murmured at the sky.","A familiar, yet foreign despair suffused his heart. He seemed to see that in the near future, this world of immortal dao civilization would be swallowed by endless ghost zombies and turn into a land of death and despair.","It would ultimately be consigned to nothing.","“No matter what, we cannot remain in the Jade Ruins Realm. I need to find another place as soon as possible.” Lu Yun shook his head, then suddenly thought of something else. “The Human Emperor, eight kings, and thirty-six marquises have entered the Celestial Realm Battlefront to call upon the heavenly book. Has the emperor perceived something?”","Sky had immediately saved him when he ran into danger in the sword pagoda and helped him claim the treasure. None of it was a coincidence.","“But even so, will a mere Human Emperor be sufficient against those things?”","......","Fallen Leaf City was situated on the southern border of Dark Orchid Empire and sat at the foot of the biggest mountain range in the Jade Ruins Realm. It bordered Darklake Empire.","It was of moderate size, but it sat on a sizable spirit vein. Though it was just a small city in Dark Orchid Empire, the density of its ambient qi almost rivaled the capital of Darklake.","Fallen Leaf Mountain was also incredibly rich in resources, spirit herbs, mines, and low level spirit beasts abounded. Thus, it was a very busy city and the web of factions within quite complicated.","Lu Yun handed the family’s daily affairs over to Terra Demon and traveled alone to this border town. He’d originally planned to stabilize the family, raise Darklake to a fourth level empire, obtain the right to enter the Celestial Realm Battlefront, then leave the family to make some additional preparations.","But after he saw what was buried beneath Immortal Burial Valley, there wasn’t a moment to waste. He needed to improve his strength before anything else. With Terra Demon in residence the Lu Clan, the family was as solid as Mount Tai. They had a few treasures that Lu Yun left behind and Terra Demon’s own strength. Even empyrean immortals wouldn’t find it an easy time if they came."]},{"number":2266,"title":"Chapter 2266: Chapter 2182.1: Purplestar Silver","paragraphs":["Chapter 2182.1: Purplestar Silver","As for Lu Yun, the experiences of three thousand reincarnations had formed three thousand seals to suppress his past memories. If he wanted to increase his strength now, he needed to do so through his own efforts. Darklake was too small for him as it was a third rank cultivation empire. This was a step he had to take if he wished to understand the multitude.","Although forceful gales stirred the Jade Ruins Realm and utter mayhem would break out after three months, the current Lu Yun still didn’t have the courage to disturb what lay at the bottom of the crater.","He left most of his items at home for this trip, keeping very few on him. He wanted to enter Fallen Leaf Mountain to forge a new personal treasure for himself.","He’d been a sword immortal in his first reincarnation. It’d been the strongest of his three thousand lifetimes, so he wished to craft a flying sword for himself.","All was a-hustle and a-bustle inside Fallen Leaf City. More cultivators than could be counted passed through its gates. Lu Yun paid the toll of a mid rank spirit stone and strolled into the city. He was dressed in his customary long ivory robes with a cerulean blue overcoat. A paramount rank jade belt fashioned at his waist, he wore a cerulean blue ribbon to hold up his hair while waving a fan gilded with silver. As for his trademark lewd folding fan—he threw it into his storage ring after turning it into a picture.","He looked like a noble scion out for an adventure, so he quickly drew attention when he entered the city.","“Sir! This humble one is Wang Bu’er, is this your first time in Fallen Leaf City?”","Lu Yun only had time to take a few steps before a short, middle-aged man in a gray short-sleeved shirt sidled up to him. The young man lifted his head and looked sideways at Wang Bu’er before inclining his head.","“Since it’s your first time here, sir, you’ll be easily taken advantage of. Why don’t I show you around in turn for some spirit stones?” Wang Bu’er cut straight to the chase.","Lu Yun nodded and threw him an upper rank spirit stone. Wang Bu’er beamed and quickly gave thanks, but no goodwill emanated from him. That made sense as this was a consensual transaction. If even that was sufficient to create goodwill, then goodwill was too easy to earn.","It came as no surprise that people like Wang Bu’er existed in a place like Fallen Leaf City. They made their living showing outsiders around. Lu Yun had spent one of his lifetimes as one of these people, so he wasn’t disgusted by them.","It was honest work. While it didn’t require a lot of skill, they could hold their heads high and look others in the eye.","“Talk to me about the layout of the city and find me a place to stay,” Lu Yun tossed out.","Although Wang Bu’er was strictly at the bottom of the Dark Orchid totem pole since he was only mid foundation establishment, he was quick witted. He could immediately tell from the young man’s words that this noble scion was no child. The first thing one should do in a new environment was to get the lay of the land. Any other young gentleman on their first excursion away from home wouldn’t ask about this.","“In response to the gentleman,” Wang Bu’er explained as they walked, “The biggest in the Fallen Leaf City is the city lord’s residence. The city lord is a soul projection powerhouse who is nearly unrivaled in Dark Orchid.”","Wang Bu’er spoke with pride when he mentioned the city lord. The city lord was the pride of all the citizens. He safeguarded the city’s peace and tranquility, ensuring that they weren’t threatened by the spirit beasts in the mountain.","Lu Yun nodded slightly. Being a fourth rank empire, Dark Orchid’s strongest heavyweights would be soul projection. Having one in residence in a small city like this was indication that Fallen Leaf was more than it seemed.","“But the city lord more often than not spends his days in closed door cultivation. He only appears when there is a beast tide. If he is not present, the city lord’s residence very rarely intervenes in the city’s matters. Therefore, the strongest in the city are the various Fallen Leaf factions,” Wang Bu’er sighed. As wonderful as the city lord was, he was too far removed. He only showed himself if the city was in imminent danger.","“The strongest factions in the city are the Azure Dragons, White Tigers, and Black Tortoises. These three sects control, directly or otherwise, all of the trading companies, taverns, and shops in the city. Since it’s your first time here, sir, it’d be best not to offend any of them. Their leaders are all peak nascent soul!”","The two arrived in front of a moderately sized inn. It wasn’t the biggest or the most opulent, but it was very clean.","“Sir, while Cloudflow Inn isn’t the most luxurious in the city, its prices are certainly the fairest,” Wang Bu’er said with a smile. During their conversation along the way, he discovered that while Lu Yun emanated the strong presence of a noble scion, he wasn’t arrogant or overbearing. He was rather down to earth, so Wang Bu’er set aside his original reservations.","“Aiyo, Wang Er, got another good customer there huh? This gentleman must be an important person since he has a noble air between his brows! You’re a lucky one, Wang Er! Please come inside, sir!” The employee at the door was plainly familiar with Wang Bu’er and teased the man when the two arrived.","“My name is Wang Bu’er!” Wang Bu’er grumbled. “Zhang Ping, arrange an upper rank room for the gentleman. Here’s three mid rank spirit stones!”","He took out three spirit stones from his own storage ring and gave them to Zhang Ping.","Lu Yun had given Wang Bu’er a piece of upper rank spirit stone, the equivalent of one hundred mid rank stones. The man was normally just paid a few mid rank stones when he showed visitors around.","His gesture engendered a bit of good intention from Lu Yun. This was a world of cultivation, after all. It was quite uncommon to see a selfless person like Wang Bu’er.","An inn like this one costed one mid rank stone a day. Wang Bu’er didn’t know how long Lu Yun would be staying for, so he paid for three days in advance.","Zhang Ping led them to a seat by the window on the second floor after receiving payment. It was noon, so there were numerous cultivators here for a meal. There were five floors to Cloudflow Inn; the first two were similar to a tavern and rooms could be found on the other floors.","Dark Orchid was different from Darklake in that the food of a fourth rank empire contained rich qi. Although cultivators had no need of food, this kind of food was far from ordinary as the act of eating it was also partially cultivation.","A full spread of dishes soon covered the table. Wang Bu’er swallowed hard and respectfully stood in a stooped position next to Lu Yun.","Lu Yun took a bite at random. Given Cloudflow Inn’s size, there wasn’t much qi in its food, but it was better than nothing.","“What are you standing for? Sit down and eat.”","Wang Bu’er hesitated before taking a seat across from Lu Yun. He sat gingerly on one corner of the stool and joined Lu Yun in lunch. As they ate, he gave a full overview of the varying sized factions in the city, marketplaces, trading companies, and stores.","A commotion rose from the first floor halfway through their meal. Five burly men charged upstairs soon after and made straight for the third floor.","Sounds of fighting rang from upstairs after a few minutes. A haggard middle-aged man scrambled down from the third floor, his hands tightly gripping a small bundle.","The staircase to the first floor was blocked by another five men. As small as Cloudflow Inn was, it contained defensive formations that withstood the man’s cultivation of initial foundation establishment.","“Hand it over, old man, and we’ll leave you with a whole corpse!” A hulking man with a scar on his face leered, advancing menacingly on the middle-aged man.","Fear outlined the latter’s limbs and he sagged to the ground, scooting backward. He left a bloody trail on the ground as he moved. Many of the guests on the second floor vacated the premises, deathly afraid of bringing trouble down on their heads.","“We should stay out of the way as well, sir. These are people from the Darkwater Gang, an organization under the Black Tortoises. The Black Tortoises are a tyrannical force in the city, so it’d be best not to incur their wrath,” Wang Bu’er quickly whispered to Lu Yun.","Bam!","A man in black stomped over and kicked Lu Yun’s table over, then slapped Wang Bu’er across the face. The man was initial golden core and Wang Bu’er just mid foundation establishment. Half of Wang Bu’er’s face immediately caved in and his neck twisted at an unnatural angle.","“Heh, how dare you gossip about the Darkwater Gang behind us, Wang Bu’er!” the man sneered at Wang Bu’er. Although the latter had kept his voice down, it didn’t escape a golden core cultivator’s hearing.","Wang Bu’er flew backward and raised a series of ripples when he smashed into the inn’s defensive formation. Bloody froth bubbled at his lips and he slid to the ground, convulsing and gasping for air.","Lu Yun frowned slightly, walking over to Wang Bu’er and shoving a pill into the man’s mouth. Wang Bu’er’s injuries healed at a rate visible to the naked eye and he miraculously made a full recovery when he’d been on the doorstep of death just moments ago."]},{"number":2267,"title":"Chapter 2267: Chapter 2182.2: Purplestar Silver","paragraphs":["Chapter 2182.2: Purplestar Silver","The man in black lit up; he knew full well how much strength he’d put into that slap. At mid foundation establishment, Wang Bu’er completely lacked the ability to defend against it. There was no doubt about it, that slap would’ve taken the man’s life.","But the young man’s pill had brought Wang Bu’er back to life again! That meant the pill was at least seventh rank or even higher. A seventh rank pill was already a higher rank pill.","“Hand over your pills and medicines, kid! We’ll let you off the hook for it!” The man in black waved some of his men forward to grab their first victim while others advanced on Lu Yun. The young man’s clothes were only lower rank fine treasures—although they looked opulent, they didn’t originate from a major clan or sect.","But so what if the kid came from an impressive background? The relationships of factions in Fallen Leaf City were a complex web. Multiple interests were in play from all sides and the city swallowed numerous Dark Orchid youngsters every year. None of their families dared take the city to task for it.","Thus, the burly man acted without reservation and grabbed for Lu Yun.","“It’s usually this young master making trouble for others. To think that trouble dares provoke me today?” Lu Yun snorted and easily shifted to the side, kicking the man’s crotch.","“Owwwww!” Caught off guard, the man in black howled like a crying wolf. He flew backward and broke through the defensive formation on the ceiling with his head. He came to a stop wrapped around the rafters; no other sound was forthcoming from his mouth.","Those assembled sucked in a sharp breath. Who was this young man to kill a golden core powerhouse with one kick??","“Yutou? He killed Yutou!” The other gang members flocked together when they saw that the man in black was dead. The young man’s cultivation wasn’t strong—the ripples from his body pointed to only latter foundation establishment. However, he’d killed one of them with a single move!","“No matter who you are, kid, you’re dead meat after killing one of the Darkwater Gang!” snarled another golden core cultivator. Of the group blockading the first floor staircase, one had already left to report this to headquarters.","Lu Yun chuckled darkly and couldn’t be bothered to respond. His body shifted slightly to the side.","Bam bam bam!","What sounded like eggs cracking sounded one after another as a dozen gang members hung from the ceiling in the blink of an eye. They were alive, just crippled of their cultivation and manhood.","“Are you alright?” Lu Yun glanced at Wang Bu’er.","“My deepest thanks to the gentleman!” Wang Bu’er was fully aware that he’d misspoke and offended the gang, thereby dragging Lu Yun into his affairs. He was also immensely grateful that Lu Yun had taken out a pill at least seventh rank to save him.","Dense goodwill floated out of Wang Bu’er, but Lu Yun also sensed another strong surge from another direction.","“Long Aotian offers immense thanks to the gentleman for saving my life!” the middle-aged man with the bundle profusely thanked Lu Yun.","“Long Aotian?” Lu Yun blinked. “Hello Long Aotian, goodbye Long Aotian.” [1]","“What?” Long Aotian started with incomprehension.","“Eh, nothing,” Lu Yun smiled. “I didn’t do this to help you. I did this because they offended me.”","“No matter what, you saved my life! I wouldn’t live to see tomorrow’s sun if the gang laid hands on me!” Long Aotian shook his head.","“Sir, the Darkwater Gang will pursue you to the end of the world after you’ve killed one of theirs. You should leave Fallen Leaf City as soon as possible,” Wang Bu’er interjected.","“That’s right, you should leave right now. This humble one was targeted because I found a piece of Purplestar Silver. The Darkwater Gang is not a group that listens to reason.” Long Aotian shoved his bundle into Lu Yun’s hand as he spoke. He’d discovered a chunk of Purplestar Silver in Fallen Leaf Mountain and hoped to sell it for a good price. However, the gang set their sights on him as soon as he returned from the mountain and followed him to his lodgings.","Long Aotian had planned to concede and sell the silver for a low price as soon as he saw the men, but they beat him up without another word. The gang wouldn’t be satisfied with just the silver, they wanted his life as well.","He would already be dead if it wasn’t for Wang Bu’er murmuring at Lu Yun’s ear and drawing their attention.","“Purplestar Silver?” Lu Yun opened the bundle to find a chunk of metal the size of a fist. It was purple throughout and shimmered with silver radiance. “This is indeed Purplestar Silver. It’s not a premier ingredient, but it’s priceless beyond compare in Dark Orchid Empire.”","He threw the chunk into his storage ring and took out another one hundred pieces of paramount rank spirit stone. He put them in a storage bag as he could tell Long Aotian didn’t have a storage treasure of his own.","“I’m buying this silver for one hundred paramount rank stones. Of course it’s worth more than that, but I don’t have any more spirit stones on me.” Lu Yun tossed the bag to Long Aotian.","“Many, many thanks to the gentleman!” Being a cultivator at the bottom of society, when would Long Aotian ever lay hands on one hundred paramount stones? He didn’t know how much the silver was worth, but it was a wondrous treasure that could be sold for a decent sum.","Another large bloom of goodwill rose from Long Aotian.","Lu Yun had crawled up from the base of the hierarchy of power in some of his lifetimes, so he held utmost sympathy for these cultivators at the bottom of the totem pole. What sense of accomplishment was there in bullying the weak? If the disciple of heavenly dao wanted to bully someone, they would bully the strong.","“It looks like there are quite a few treasures in Fallen Leaf Mountain if something like Purplestar Silver can be found there. The Duskwater Gang must’ve gathered quite a few treasures during their years of operation. I’ll pay a visit to their vaults when I have time.” As Lu Yun’s thoughts ran wildly, the innkeeper ran over to address the situation.","He was an elder with graying hair and latter golden core. When he saw the gang members hanging from the ceiling like links of sausage, he nearly fainted dead away.","“Oh, oh dear... What do we do now?” Paling with horror, one could tell from his words that he was an honest man.","“Don’t worry, innkeeper. I take full responsibility for my actions. This young master will take care of the Darkwater Gang for you.” Lu Yun shook his head when he saw the man’s expression.","“Sir, I know you come from an illustrious background, but you can’t hold off the Duskwater Gang forever. They’ll come back around after you leave!” The innkeeper nearly cried.","Boom!","Countless customers shrieked and ran outside when the inn shook.","Boom!","Another explosion rang out. Lu Yun regarded the development with an unpleasant expression. The rest of the gang had come, but didn’t enter the inn. They attacked it from outside, trying to raze it to the ground.","“I do my fair share of bullying others, but not like this!” he sneered and summoned a folding fan into his hand. It was his prized pornographic fan. Snapping it open, the lewd scenes seemed to come alive. A man and a woman illustrated numerous unspeakable acts, replete with obscene sounds from body and mouth.","A curtain of pink light enveloped Cloudflow Inn, stunning the gang members outside. Most were nearly drooling and some noses ran with blood. Tents appeared and rapidly grew in height from their trousers.","Lu Yun’s illusory formation wasn’t something that a few golden core or foundation establishment cultivators could withstand. The strongest gang member present—a nascent soul cultivator—kept a tight grip on his mind and locked himself in place.","“Hmph, it’s your lucky day. I made this formation diagram with Sola Aoi, Yui Hatano, and others in mind. You get to experience it for free today!”","Wait a moment... who are these people?","Lu Yun shook his head fiercely, knowing that these names came from his sealed memories.","“Activate!” Lu Yun shook his hand and raised a burst of illumination from his fan, enveloping the Darkwater Gang members outside.","And then...","The citizens of Fallen Leaf City witnessed an utterly preposterous scene.","Two dozen gang members clasped each other tightly and ripped the clothes off each other. They fervently engaged in the most basic actions of human nature—even the nascent soul cultivator put up only brief struggle before joining them.","Countless jaws dropped.","“Tsk tsk, look at that ardor and enthusiasm!” Lu Yun clucked his tongue with appreciation as he stood by a window on the second floor.","The innkeeper, Wang Bu’er, Long Aotian, and others were flabbergasted. All they’d seen was Lu Yun take out a fan and wave it around before the scene outside took place.","Lu Yun’s folding fan was an illusory formation diagram that he’d refined in a spare moment. It was effective against those below soul projection or impatient and blundering cultivators. But to someone of steady heart and mind like Lu Xiaochi or Bloodbath, it was a joke.","Given the gang’s typical domineering, blustering ways, it was the perfect formation to use against them.","1. This appears to be a reference to a novel series titled “Hello Human Life, Goodbye Dragon Life”. Despite reaching twenty-one volumes, it has received only a manhua and is yet to be adapted into an animation. Netizens point to this as being a sign of how poorly written the series is. ☜"]},{"number":2268,"title":"Chapter 2268: Chapter 2183.1: Extermination","paragraphs":["Chapter 2183.1: Extermination","The Darkwater Gang was a complete joke in Fallen Leaf City after today. Two dozen of its men, including the vice gang leader, had fornicated in public in the most vulgar way possible.","“What’s going on here?!” A beardless man of roughly thirty years old rushed in with several hundred people. Most of them were foundation establishment with a couple golden core.","“Ying Wu, what are you doing?!” Gang leader Ying Xuanshui glared hotly at his vice leader. Ying Wu was holding a stocky gang member, rising and falling on top of him while hooting with pleasure. Another smaller and skinnier man behind him did the same thing to the lofty vice gang leader.","Bam!A glowering Ying Xuanshui kicked the skinny man aside. The man crashed to the ground, his condition unknown.","Bam!","Ying Xuanshui reached out and smacked the back of Ying Wu’s head. That was all it took to knock an initial nascent soul cultivator unconscious.","When the burly man found that there was no one behind him, he quickly turned around and saw the livid Ying Xuanshui. His coarse features assembled into a seductive smile and he raised his bottom to the air, rubbing Ying Xuanshui’s crotch with it.","The gang leader’s stomach turned and he almost vomited. He furiously stomped down the man’s butt, sending the wailing man careening to a nearby stone mound and fainting dead away.","Ying Xuanshui was a mid nascent soul cultivator and could tell that his men had fallen victim to some sort of illusion. He subconsciously glanced at the Cloudflow Inn in front of him. The pink haze enveloping it was explanation enough—this was obviously an uncommonly sophisticated illusion formation. Whoever touched the curtain of light was affected.","“To the friend inside, aren’t such filthy tactics against the Darkwater Gang despicable?” Ying Xuanshui directed his men to knock the two dozen gang members unconscious. Only that freed them from the influence of the formation.","Being the leader of a gang, Ying Xuanshui was a shrewd person who kept his cards close to his heart. He wouldn’t have come if not for hearing about the ludicrous acts that Ying Wu and the others were engaging in.","“Despicable?” a clear voice slowly answered. “Doesn’t the leader of the Darkwater Gang find these words laughable?”","The inn doors opened to reveal a young man in long ivory robes and cerulean blue overcoat. He waved a folding fan gilded with gold and set foot outside of Cloudflow Inn.","“Laughable?” Ying Xuanshui’s heart skipped a beat when he saw that the speaker was just a young man of seventeen years old, but commanded the cultivation of initial golden core. At the same time, the young man’s clothes were only lower fine rank treasures. This was most likely a noble scion from a third rank empire.","The gang leader’s heart settled back down as he concluded that the young man must have obtained his treasures and formation diagram from Immortal Burial Valley. Ever since the valley appeared, pills and treasures that were a rare sight in the lower ranked empires of Jade Ruins Realm became commonly seen.","“You say this young master is despicable, but I wonder if your Darkwater Gang is even more reprehensible?” Lu Yun smirked at the two dozen men in a shabby state being led away by the other gang members.","Ying Xuanshui’s face twitched. Although his men had committed those actions because they’d fallen prey to an ambush, it was an unequivocal fact that the actions had taken place. It wouldn’t be long before the gang became the laughingstock of Fallen Leaf City.","Despicable? Reprehensible? More like utterly disgraced.","“You court death!” Ying Xuanshui didn’t think much of Lu Yun after deducing the young man’s identity. He’d killed more noble scions of ordinary Dark Orchid clans than he could count. What did one from a mere third rank empire count for?","He promptly pressed down in the void and formed a massive hand with boundless true origin. It loomed over Lu Yun’s head. This was just an initial golden core cultivator! He would never hold off a nascent soul powerhouse, even with a couple of impressive treasures.","Lu Yun struck back in full when he saw that the other simply used true origin to manifest a giant hand against him. He waved Hongmeng qi out of his body and also formed a hazy gray hand, sending it against the one of true origin.","Plenty of spectating cultivators nearly broke out into laughter to see a little guy of initial golden core use a hand of true origin against a nascent soul cultivator. They’d seen people out of their depth before, but never one so delusional. The gap between initial golden core and mid nascent soul was more than heaven and earth in their eyes.","Boom!","A sharp collision sounded in the air as one of the hands was destroyed and the other continued with unabated momentum. Of course, this was only to be expected and the young man would be shortly...","Jaws dropped as Lu Yun’s hazy hand closed around Ying Xuanshui’s neck and held him up.","“How dare a nascent soul cultivator throw his weight around in front of me?” Lu Yun contemptuously lifted his chin and threw Ying Xuanshui to the ground.","Cowering inside the inn, Long Aotian and Wang Bu’er swallowed hard. Never could they have imagined that the lofty Darkwater Gang leader, a nascent soul powerhouse, would lack even the ability to rest the young man!","Lu Yun had been able to defeat an initial nascent soul Ouyang Shengtian when he was in foundation establishment and evenly matched the possessed genius. Now that he’d formed a golden core of great dao, the nascent soul cultivators of a mere fourth rank empire didn’t even register in his eyes.","Fengxian Wu could casually sweep away a dozen of them, to say nothing of Lu Yun.","He looked imperiously at the gang leader on the ground and suddenly broke into a gentle smile, sending shivers down Ying Xuanshui’s back.","“I am newly come to Fallen Leaf City and lack a few errand boys. You’re called Ying Xuanshui, aren’t you? Are you willing to serve this young master?” He was used to being called a young master in the Lu Clan, so this was the same honorific he adopted when out. These days, he was in the mood of recruiting whoever he saw. It didn’t matter if they wished to serve him or not. He lacked minions to run errands with.","“Hmph!” Ying Xuanshui was a hard man who shunted his head to the side with a cold snort. The other two hundred gang members also gathered around. Although they seemed to have provoked someone they shouldn’t have this time, they weren’t afraid since they had a mighty backer.","“So you’re not willing?” Lu Yun’s tones still remained gentle as he looked at Ying Xuanshui.","“My Darkwater Gang is under the banner of the Black Tortoises—”","Pfft!","Lu Yun kicked his head in before he could finish. Another kick to the dantian crushed Ying Xuanshui’s nascent soul out of existence.","Silence draped over the scene. The young man was... too abnormal and entirely too ruthlessly decisive. He’d been smiling one second and killed a nascent soul powerhouse in cold blood the next. Was it that easy to kill such a heavyweight? Could it be that Ying Xuanshui had been a paper tiger?","“I give you forty-five minutes to disband the gang, or this young master will kill you one by one.” There wasn’t much killing intent in Lu Yun’s tone, but it was foreboding all the same in the gang’s ears.","Two hundred gang members and another initial nascent soul vice leader stood frozen on the spot.","“Get out of here!” Lu Yun shouted, sending shudders through the crowd before they scattered. He sensed a decent surge of goodwill from all sides—there was both gratitude and admiration present.","The young man quickly grasped that killing a nascent soul cultivator with golden core strength instantly won him the worship of some weaker cultivators. Darkwater Gang was a tyrant of Fallen Leaf City, their reputation similar to his in Dark City. Now that he’d killed their leader and demanded this disbandment, the citizens were naturally grateful toward him.","“Young master, you’re in great trouble now! You should leave the city as soon as possible!” Wang Bu’er and Long Aotian ran out of the inn. While they were highly excited, they were more so enormously worried.","“Darkwater Gang falls under the Black Tortoise banner and Ying Xuanshui is the uncle of the Black Tortoise leader. They will not easily let you off for killing Ying Xuanshui!","“Their leader is a peak nascent soul powerhouse and he commands a dozen more nascent soul cultivators. There are also more than ten thousand Black Tortoise members. As strong as you are, sir, you will be overwhelmed with sheer numbers!” Wang Bu’er explained rapidly as he was well acquainted with the situation in the city.","“Disperse of the bodies for me. You can leave after that.” Golden light flashed through Lu Yun’s eye as he vanished on the spot. This was cultivation—comprehension of the many aspects of life, doing some good deeds, ridding the world of some tyrants, and collecting goodwill.","He... wasn’t being a saint, was he?","......","The two vice leaders of Darkwater Gang rushed back to their headquarters, surrounded by an entourage of two hundred gang members.","“What do we do now?” The awakened Ying Wu was at a loss. Although he’d committed unspeakable acts, there was no time to dwell on that since Ying Xuanshui was dead. But... that illusion had been pretty...","“What is going on, how did you provoke such a terrifying young man?!” The other vice leader, Ying Xiong, barely managed to force down abject fear.","Lu Yun’s last words had been tinged with goodwill, leaving an indelible mark on their hearts and minds. Thus, they didn’t even collect their dead leader’s body before departing.","“The men say that Purplestar Silver appeared in Cloudflow Inn, as well as a treasure that can raise the dead. I rushed there with our people, but the young man used a vicious formation against us!” As savage as Ying Wu’s expression was, it was more filled with fear.","Ying Xuanshui and Ying Xiong had rushed to the inn when they heard of what their fellow comrades were doing.","“Let’s go to second sister! We must have vengeance for the death of big brother.”","etvolare's Thoughts","Lovely, I'd like to wash my eyeballs now kthx."]},{"number":2269,"title":"Chapter 2269: Chapter 2183.2: Extermination","paragraphs":["Chapter 2183.2: Extermination","Ying Xiong was initial nascent soul and ready to cross over to mid nascent soul at any time. Lu Yun’s brand on his heart and mind was slightly weaker than the one on Ying Wu’s. After being attacked by the young man, Ying Wu’s current mentality was unbelievably fragile.","The golden core and foundation establishment gang members trembled when they thought of Lu Yun. The death of their leader with two kicks and the final blow from goodwill had caused deep trauma.","“That’s right, the Black Tortoises have a great number of experts. As strong as the young man is, he is only golden core. Big brother wouldn’t have died so easily if not for underestimating his opponent and failing to use his treasures,” Ying Wu forced out through grit teeth and spoke around the fear shaking his heart.","“Let’s go!” Ying Xiong set his jaw and stood up.","The second sister they mentioned was the dao partner of the Black Tortoise leader. It was due to this relationship that the Darkwater Gang could operate with such impunity in Fallen Leaf City. The Black Tortoise leader was peak nascent soul and half a step into soul projection. He would be the strongest of any third rank nation.","“You’re not going anywhere,” Lu Yun’s voice rang out. “Forty-five minutes is up. Since you haven’t disbanded, allow this young master to perform the deed.”","“You...” The two Ying brothers were scared out of their wits to see Lu Yun’s sudden arrival.","Whoosh whoosh!","Two rays of silver light flashed past, sending two heads of petrified fear shooting into the sky. Two headless bodies flopped to the ground as Lu Yun waved their storage rings to him, then burned the corpses in two balls of fire.","“There are quite a lot of treasures in the Darkwater vaults.” Golden light gleaming out of his eyes, Lu Yun headed in another direction.","Powerful formations protected the Darkwater vaults—formations that were jokes to the young man. Ones established by Great Xia cultivators might pose a challenge to him, but the ones from a fourth rank nation’s nascent soul cultivator might as well not exist.","Most formations were laid out according to the logic of the five elements in a continuous cycle of supplementation and counter. Others derived from this logic, such as illusion, slaughter, trap, or disorientation formations were based off of the five elements. One simply had to locate the nodes between the elements and break their cycle if they wished to dismantle the formation.","Of course, a formation with a complete cycle of the five elements would be considered a premier formation. The one safeguarding the Darkwater vault was just a protective one of metal giving rise to water.","When it came to formations, Lu Yun rather thought there should be ten formations of one potential, two principles, three essentials, four divisions, five elements, six directions, seven stars, eight trigrams, nine sectors, and ten orientations. It wasn’t just the five elements. If all ten could be combined together and ignite a grand influence over the world, that would...","Lu Yun shook his head, shaking his sealed memories back into place. Thankfully, it was just knowledge that’d slipped out and not memories. Many things would go wrong otherwise.","“Who dares trespass in Darkwater Gang forbidden territory!” Three latter golden core guards stopped Lu Yun as soon as he arrived in front of the vaults.","“While the gang’s strength doesn’t measure up to the former seven great clans of Darklake, they would be an elite faction regardless in the nation.” Lu Yun flashed in front of them, his fist moving like an illusion and spontaneously crushing all of their dantians and life force.","The Lu Yun of this lifetime didn’t show mercy or benevolence. Things were fine enough if others didn’t provoke him, but if they did, he turned into a mad dog that didn’t rest until he bit them to death.","He’d already given the gang a chance. If the two vice leaders had swiftly disbanded, he wouldn’t have bothered hunting them down.","Lu Yun sent out a surge of fire origin with one hand and directed it at the connection node between water and metal in the formation. Since fire countered metal, it immediately set all of the metal energy ablaze. As for water countering fire... an ordinary element of water evaporated when it met connate fire origin.","The entire formation collapsed when the five basic elements were dismantled.","Lu Yun was likely the only one who could employ this kind of method in Great Xia and the worlds of cultivation. It was similar to medicinal properties reformation—his own technique.","Darkwater Gang was just a tiny gang in Fallen Leaf City, so the formation safeguarding their vaults was but an initial third rank formation. It barely required effort to break, giving Lu Yun access a small vault roughly thirty meters across. Treasures and ingredients were randomly jumbled inside and there was a shelf in a corner that held roughly thirty storage rings.","Lu Yun swept all of them into the sword pagoda in his dantian without taking a close look. Apart from the ray of sword qi at its center, the sword pagoda was also a massive storage center. It was where he’d subdued the sword pagoda.","The space within was so marvelous that it could hold living beings in unbounded capacity. Lu Yun’s own storage ring likely would’ve proven inadequate to contain what was in the gang’s vaults.","After cleaning out what could be looted from the Darkwater Gang, Lu Yun scanned the entire area with the Eye of Nullification. He left content after determining there were no hidden vaults like the Lu residence.","While the gang’s wealth didn’t measure up to a trading company like the Ouyangs’, it was still quite stunning. There weren’t any rare or exotic treasures within, however. They’d probably all been turned over to the Black Tortoises.","......","“There’s a certain relationship between the Darkwater Gang and Black Tortoises. The Black Tortoises.. damn it!” Lu Yun suddenly frowned.","The Eye of Nullification broke through all obstacles. At his current level of cultivation, he could see for fifty kilometers in any direction, placing most of Fallen Leaf City in his line of vision.","But even so, he didn’t find it very useful. The Eye of Nullification only saw what was on the surface, it couldn’t see anything deeper.","Such as the information of the dead.","When he opened the eye to scan the Black Tortoises, the first to enter his eyes was the razed Cloudflow Inn. A deeply injured Long Aotian stood on top of the ruins while Wang Bu’er lay decapitated elsewhere.","“Speak, where is the young man?!” An aloof middle-aged man dressed in black armor grabbed Long Aotian by the collar. If it wasn’t for wanting information, Long Aotian would be dead as well.","“I don’t know!” Long Aotian exhaled explosively with a tragic air. They were out of the frying pan and into the fire. There was no hope of survival once the Black Tortoises had him in their grasp.","Long Aotian and Wang Bu’er came into sudden wealth with the storage rings that Lu Yun gave them. They’d planned to leave with Lu Yun when he came back. Unfortunately, the Black Tortoises came knocking before the young man did.","A woman with coldly beautiful features led the delegation—the dao partner of the Black Tortoise leader. Tears brimmed in her eyes as she sagged in front of Ying Xuanshui’s corpse.","“Big brother, I will obliterate whoever killed you...” she said emotionally as she trembled.","The man in black armor viciously slapped Long Aotian across the face when he heard those words. “Out with it, where did the murderer go?!”","“Kill him. The Black Tortoises will find him wherever he goes in this area.” Ying Yinshui stood up, whereupon she swayed and keened in a distorted voice, “Third brother, fourth brother! Whoever you are, I, Ying Yinshui, swear upon my dignity as a human being that I will exterminate you and yours!!”","Pfft!","She spat out a mouthful of blood while Black Armor paled. He quickly understood that Ying Yinshui had somehow sensed the deaths of her third and fourth brothers. She’d sensed Ying Xuanshui’s death not long after it occurred and rushed to the scene, finding Wang Bu’er and Long Aotian. Otherwise, the Black Tortoises wouldn’t be so quick on the scene even with receiving word.","Black Armor hesitated for a split second before turning his hand sideways like a blade and bringing it down on Long Aotian.","A chill gripped Long Aotian’s heart and he closed his eyes, waiting for death.","Pfft!","“AHH!!” A ghastly scream traveled into Long Aotian’s ears as the pressure lightened on his throat and he fell to the ground. He opened his eyes to see an apologetic Lu Yun and a wailing Black Armor with severed arms.","Lu Yun sighed as he looked at Wang Bu’er’s body. “I didn’t think that these siblings would have a Connection Talisman. This was my oversight.”","He originally intended to attract attention from the Black Tortoises through a disturbance at the Duskwater Gang. That would give Long Aotian, Wang Bu’er, and the employees of Cloudflow Inn enough time to retreat.","But Ying Yinshui had immediately come by due to the Connection Talisman.","“It’s you!” She realized as soon as she saw Lu Yun. The young man in ivory robes and a blue overcoat was the one who’d killed her brothers. “Kill him!!” she shrieked with a loss of all reason.","More than fifty Black Tortoise members had come with her, all greater than golden core. Three of them were nascent soul powerhouses, and all were on guard with Lu Yun’s sudden appearance. When Ying Yinshu shrilled her command, they immediately brought out their treasures and flung attacks at Lu Yun.","They’d gained a full understanding of Lu Yun’s actions before they arrived. If it wasn’t for Ying Xuanshui underestimating his enemy, he would still be alive now. In their eyes, a combined blow from sixty people was using a cannon to kill a mosquito.","“There’s something to the Black Tortoises, their concerted action shows signs of a basic battle formation.” Lu Yun raised his head to regard the flying swords with a frown."]},{"number":2270,"title":"Chapter 2270: Chapter 2184.1: Bloodline of Dragons","paragraphs":["Chapter 2184.1: Bloodline of Dragons","The battle formations of this world were not the formations of cultivators. They were the coordination of military formations and concerted movement of all parties reaching certain proficiency.","These kinds of battle formations were typically practiced by the army. The battle formations of mid and lower rank cultivation empires were lower rank battle formations. Their enhancement of battle strength was limited to less than fifty percent.","Lu Tianling’s army had been able to sweep all third rank empires and place Darklake as their head primarily because his battle formation was a mid rank formation that doubled battle strength.","The battle formation that the Black Tortoise disciples assembled was just the outline of one, but it already doubled their strength! This was definitely not something from a fourth rank empire!","Lu Yun also seemed to know some other battle formations that fell under immortal dao civilization. He just couldn’t recall them at the moment. Eyes narrowing, he watched as sixty treasures hurtled toward him in a nearly complete formation.","“Break!” he shouted, connate yang metal energy sparkling around his fingers. He pointed at a random wood attribute treasure.","Crack!","The wood attribute treasure was a mid rank item shaped as a gourd. It was the personal treasure of an initial nascent soul cultivator and was instantly pierced through by the white yang metal.","Rumble!","The battle formation sputtered as the gourd-shaped treasure was destroyed. Three fire attribute treasures immediately weakened and nearby water attribute treasures blossomed with strength. The flow of the five elements in the formation was completely knocked askew. It was out of control before it reached Lu Yun and fell to attacking itself.","Cultivators mostly depended on the five elements for strength. This relationship of complementing and countering each other was the most effective and direct way of enhancing strength. Thus, all formations or battle formations in the worlds of cultivation followed this logic.","With his Eye of Nullification, Lu Yun easily identified the gourd as the eye of the formation. Destroying it meant that the entire formation was negated.","The gourd needed to be destroyed first. If any other treasure was the priority and then the gourd, the method of attack would prove ineffective. The battle formation was constantly changing, as was its eye.","Lu Yun was able to find success due to his Eye of Nullification and command over the connate elements. Otherwise, even a formation grandmaster would find it difficult to easily dismantle the battle formation.","His destruction of the eye caused a subsequent collapse of the battle formation. He then punched a mallet-shaped treasure with his full strength, reducing it to shards. The fragments accurately connected with the other treasures and disabled them as well.","It took only less than one hundredth of an eye blink to defuse the treasure formation bearing down on him. Sixty treasures were sent flying every which way.","The cultivators observing from the shadows gaped. They didn’t even have time to understand what was going on before the sixty Black Tortoise disciples uniformly spat out blood. More than just coordinating the treasures, they were nearly one to direct the battle formation.","The formation was destroyed and the cultivators deeply injured from the backlash. Lu Yun took a step forward and punched the dantian of a mid nascent soul cultivator, obliterating it. He swiftly moved through them, reaping lives wherever he went.","Lu Yun was far from a benevolent soul. After three thousand lifetimes, he knew full well that whether it was the worlds of immortals or cultivators, these were brutal and ruthless places. Showing mercy to the enemy was being cruel to oneself.","There was no right or wrong in a place like this.","All of the ferocious disciples were dead after a few breaths. Lu Yun picked up storage rings from the ground and turned to Ying Yinshui with an eerie grin.","Her face was devoid of color—previously out of reaction to the death of her brothers, now from deep fear. This harmless young man of seventeen years had casually killed sixty of her men, the weakest of which was golden core. Was this the capabilities of a golden core cultivator?","“Ying Xuanshui’s younger sister and the dao partner of the Black Tortoise leader... Ying Yinshui?” Lu Yun smirked. “That’s a nice name, but why isn’t your surname Liu?”","“Liu? Why should my surname be Liu?” Ying Yinshui asked reflexively as her thoughts were a muddled mess.","Lu Yun shook his head at the woman’s expression and punched forward, sending her lifeless body floating backward like a drifting willow leaf. He grabbed the dumbfounded Long Aotian and left the city in a blaze of sword light.","......","A man approximately thirty years old in long black robes arrived on the scene after three dozen breaths. He looked expressionlessly at the body on the ground, not even a frown creasing his forehead.","“What is it, Wuheng? Heartbroken that someone’s destroyed your cauldron?” A man in a long purple shirt grinned merrily.","Wuheng shrugged wordlessly.","“It’s good that that woman is dead. The three girls are coming in a few days and you’d be in for some trouble if they saw her,” cackled the purple clad Zi Zhen.","“They’re going to be here soon, so where’s Huiying?” Wuheng looked around with confusion.","No one noticed them as they conversed. Black Tortoise members rushed to the scene and frantically dealt with the corpses, but ignored the two.","“The old guy in the mountain is acting up again, so Huiying’s gone to teach it a lesson.” Zi Zhen shrugged and changed the subject. “Shouldn’t you react with something when your ‘dao partner’ has been killed?”","“That young man was something.” Wuheng looked in the direction that Lu Yun left in. “He’ll rival the Human Emperor of Great Xia when he grows into his strength. It’ll be good to give him some more tempering.”","“Look at you being such a fan of talent!” Zi Zhen roared with laughter.","“Forget that.” A warm smile crept over Wuheng’s lips. “Let’s build a Red Vermilions sect for the girls when they come.”","......","Lu Yun rushed into Fallen Leaf Mountain with Long Aotian. The latter was deeply injured and kept coughing up blood. Plainly, his core essence had been damaged.","The Lu young master put him on the ground when they reached a clearing and scanned his injuries with the Eye of Nullification.","“Oh?” Lu Yun paused. There was more to Long Aotian than met the eye! “Well well well, you do live up to your name.” He smiled after seeing the truth behind the man.","“Sir?” Long Aotian trembled when he saw the look in Lu Yun’s eyes.","“You carry draconic bloodline!” Lu Yun stared at him like he’d found a precious treasure. “If you’d like, I can fully activate your bloodline so you can transform into a dragon!”","Long Aotian stared blankly at the young man, not knowing what to say. Draconic bloodline? Dragons were mythical beasts in all of Jade Ruins Realm and Great Xia! They were mysterious, powerful, and the epitome of strength. Even immortals would worship them if they encountered one.","Perhaps dragons did exist in the world, but few were those who’d met one. It was possible that only the Human Emperor of Great Xia had ever seen one, yet this young man said he possessed the bloodline of the dragons? What a preposterous notion!","Although Lu Yun was so strong that he could quickly defeat the nascent soul powerhouses of the Black Tortoises, Long Aotian wasn’t willing to believe that he had a draconic bloodline.","“Forget it if you don’t want to. I can simply heal your injuries so you can continue your mediocre life. But if you want, I can awaken your bloodline so you can become a true dragon. Although, I’m lacking a few things now so I need to gather them if I’m to activate your bloodline.” A jade-green pill appeared in Lu Yun’s hand as he spoke—the pill that’d saved Wang Bu’er.","He sighed when he thought of the man. Wang Bu’er hadn’t been the smartest, but he’d been honest and a good man. He would’ve been a good follower, but Ying Yinshui had killed him.","“You saved my life, sir, so no matter what you want me to do, I will do it without question!” Long Aotian didn’t hesitate as Lu Yun was incredibly strong. He was plainly an important elite of a great faction. Long Aotian was no fool.","“Take this pill and focus on your injuries first.” Lu Yun tossed the pill to Long Aotian. The man quickly swallowed it and sat down cross-legged to digest its effects.","They were forty kilometers away from Fallen Leaf City. Lu Yun looked back in its direction with the Eye of Nullification and, as expected, saw vast numbers of Black Tortoise disciples rush out in their direction."]},{"number":2271,"title":"Chapter 2271: Chapter 2184.2: Bloodline of Dragons","paragraphs":["Chapter 2184.2: Bloodline of Dragons","“That’s strange. Logically speaking, the Black Tortoise leader should be coming after me himself since I’ve killed his dao partner...” Lu Yun looked curiously at the Black Tortoise disciples.","“What, do you wish for their leader to hunt you down himself?” came a flippant voice behind him.","Lu Yun’s heart skipped a beat with surprise and he hastily whirled around. A young man dressed in white and roughly the same age as him had appeared at some point in time. He guzzled from a wine gourd in his hand.","Lu Yun had no idea when he’d arrived and turned the Eye of Nullification on him. However, the two rays of golden light failed to see through the young man. All he saw was a white haze of uncommonly keen light.","“Are you an immortal?” Lu Yun immediately realized. Not only was this young man an immortal, but he was likely a very strong immortal.","“Immortal?” The young man thought for a bit. “I guess.”","“Dao immortal? Immortal overlord? Or... chaos...?” Lu Yun asked offhandedly with a curl of his lip.","It was the young man’s turn to stare incredulously at him.","“You...”","Dao immortal came after immortal, then immortal overlord, and finally chaos immortal. As the High Lord of the Northern Sky in his first reincarnation, Lu Yun had been a chaos immortal!","“What about me?” Lu Yun hated being caught on the back foot. While he could tell that the young man meant no harm, it irritated him to see the other regard him with an amused expression.","What, are you supposed to be really strong? I’m a good-for-nothing on par with the heavens and the heavenly dao’s personal disciple. I can be considered a second generation heavenly dao! I’m not standing on lower ground in front of you!","Huiying looked dumbly at Lu Yun; meeting a strange young man here was the last thing he’d expected. The latter had easily spelled out the ranks of immortals when the strongest of Great Xia—the Human Emperor—was but a peerless immortal. Likely even the emperor didn’t know what came after his realm.","Black Tortoise members rushed to them before he had a chance to respond and surrounded them. They were about to erupt with fury when they took a clear look at Huiying. Shuddering, they stood down.","“Head of the White Tigers, to think that you would be here as well! These two are wanted by us Black Tortoises, so I would respectfully ask you to stand aside.” A young man of latter nascent soul spoke with a hint of fear in his eyes.","Huiying was well known in Fallen Leaf City for being the most bloodthirsty leader of the three sects. The Black Tortoise young man was deathly afraid of arousing his ire and bringing his own death down on him. Although he was no pushover himself, too many nascent soul cultivators had already lost their lives to Huiying.","Huiying took a deep look at Lu Yun and left with a shake of his head. The nascent soul cultivator relaxed to see him go.","“So there are indeed true powerhouses in this world, and many of them. Although the world of immortals has vanished, there are certain clues to be found.” A sharp light danced in Lu Yun’s eyes while he watched Huiying leave. Currently, what he wished to know the most was the whereabouts of the world of immortals. The woman he’d loved the most in his three thousand lifetimes resided there, so he wished to obtain information about her no matter what.","He’d purposefully listed the ranks of immortals to gauge Huiying’s reaction. Since Lu Yun had once reincarnated into Great Xia, he knew that the dynasty’s strongest heavyweight was peerless immortal.","As strong as that level was, it was only run-of-the-mill in the world of immortals. His lowest soldiers had been peerless immortals and had no right to learn of certain secrets.","His gamble had paid off.","“It looks like crouching tigers and hidden dragons abound in Fallen Leaf City. The leaders of the three sects are no ordinary people.” As curious as Lu Yun was, he wouldn’t seek them out now. Being just a golden core cultivator, he was no different from an ant to them. He would have the right to speak to them only when he grew strong enough.","“Kill!” The latter nascent soul young man didn’t hesitate after Huiying left. Several thousand cultivators assembled into a battle formation that resembled a black tortoise howling at the sky.","“An upper rank battle formation!” Lu Yun smacked his lips when he saw the shadow hovering over the formation. An upper rank formation enhanced battle strength at least ten times over. The shadow over it indicated that it was paramount level among upper ranks. He had absolutely no desire to set himself against an upper rank formation made of several thousand people.","“We’re leaving!” Lu Yun grabbed Long Aotian and waved a talisman in the air, vanishing on the spot. Being golden core, he could use the connate five elements to craft simple talismans. The Earthbending Talisman was made with connate yang earth energy and ordinary cultivators would find it impossible to trace.","Although he was out to temper himself with this trip, he wasn’t interested in dying. Neither did he imagine that he’d run into these kinds of issues as soon as he set out. Not only did he encounter an immortal stronger than normal, but he also met with an upper rank battle formation.","All that could be said was that... he was unlucky.","BOOM!","Fallen Leaf Mountain trembled the moment they vanished. Where they’d just been was now a pit five kilometers across.","......","“That was close!” Five hundred kilometers out, Lu Yun’s eye twitched and he licked his lips when he felt the mountain shake. “I’ll have to break them apart before they assemble their formation the next time I see them, or I won’t stand a chance at all.”","Lu Yun spat out bloody froth from his mouth. Although he’d utilized the Earthbending Talisman, the terrifying shockwave still caused some damage.","“I wonder how Bloodbath faced one million by himself, that madman.” Lu Yun wiped at his mouth.","Bloodbath had slaughtered one million cultivators from a fifth rank nation by himself, and there were parts of the army among the one million. While the nation had possessed only a lower rank battle formation, it was still incredibly frightening when assembled by one million cultivators.","Yet, Bloodbath killed all of them under those conditions.","Lu Yun knew that it was himself who was too weak. If he was nascent soul right this very second, he wouldn’t have to turn tail and run, even if he couldn’t immediately dismantle the formation.","The main peak of Fallen Leaf Mountain was eight hundred kilometers across. Lu Yun traveling five hundred kilometers with one talisman brought him out of the main peak. But since it was still part of the Barrens—a rather large mountain range—Lu Yun remained within the overall range of the Fallen Leaf Mountains.","Interestingly enough, local flora grew more lush when he left the range of the main peak. Trees towered at dozens of meters tall, some even hundreds.","“That’s strange, the ambient qi here isn’t that dense. It’s actually far less than that of the main peak. Why are the trees taller?” Lu Yun took a careful look around. There weren’t many spirit beasts present, just the occasional first or second rank beast. None of higher rank could be found.","“Long Aotian, do you know what’s going on here?” Lu Yun called upon the Eye of Nullification and found a similar case for fifty kilometers in all directions. The greenery was lush and vibrant, but there was no sign of life to be found.","“Is this... a forbidden zone?” Long Aotian was a long-time resident of Fallen Leaf City, so he knew of the certain happenings around the city.","“A forbidden zone?” Lu Yun blinked.","“Legend has it that the mountain range five hundred kilometers away from Fallen Leaf Mountain is deemed off limits by the Dark Orchid Empire. Spirit beasts are given leeway, but human cultivators die without a doubt if they trespass!” Long Aotian answered in a shaking voice.","“Off limits?” Lu Yun looked at the dense canopy overhead and leapt into the sky. He gazed out over an unending expanse of vibrant forest with no end to it.","“So this a formation.” He immediately understood. The so-called forbidden zone was an enormous formation of illusion. It was so big that his Eye of Nullification couldn’t see through it—not because it wasn’t strong enough to, but because its range didn’t extend to the full limits of the formation. The fifty kilometers he was in happened to be the formation’s blind spot.","Lu Yun landed and said to Long Aotian, “This isn’t off limits. Someone’s just playing with smoke and mirrors. Come with me.”","He set off in a certain direction, trailed by a terrified Long Aotian. As uncomfortable as he was, there was nothing else he could do.","“Purple Ginseng? This is nice and it’s eight thousand years old!” Lu Yun suddenly halted and looked raptly at where purple radiance flashed. Purple Ginseng was a seventh rank spirit herb and one eight thousand years was incredibly old. He placed a boundary around it without further ado and dug it up.","Spirit herbs like these were usually safeguarded by powerful spirit beasts. But thanks to this forbidden zone, there were only a few second rank beasts wandering nearby. It saved him a lot of trouble.","Apart from the ginseng, there were too many precious ingredients to be counted. His storage rings were quickly stuffed to the brim. Many of them were high rank ingredients, but more were low ranked ones.","Any other cultivator or pill master would collect only the high rank ones and discard the low rank. But to Lu Yun, these lower ranked ones were even more precious. In the three thousand worlds, he’d used countless lower ranked spirit herbs to replicate the effects of one of the ten legendary herbs—the Shennong Grass!","Thus, to him, even a first rank herb had its value.","The two wandered in the forbidden zone for three days, Long Aotian smiling wryly the whole time. His fingers were crammed with storage rings and another string hung around his neck."]},{"number":2272,"title":"Chapter 2272: Chapter 2185.1: Immortals Forbidden","paragraphs":["Chapter 2185.1: Immortals Forbidden","While the sword pagoda could also store items, time was not frozen within it. Certain ingredients would gradually lose their properties if stowed there. Thus, Lu Yun put everything he collected into storage rings. And since he would use them shortly, he had Long Aotian carry them instead of piling the rings into the sword pagoda.","He fully harvested everything within fifty kilometers after three days—be it the lowliest first ranked herb or the highest ninth ranked grass.","When he was certain that nothing existed within fifty kilometers, he sat down cross-legged in a clearing and had Long Aotian stand guard. Lu Yun retrieved the fist-sized Purplestar Silver that weighed several hundred kilograms and brought out a few other low ranked ores.","“Three parts zircon, two parts copper, four parts mica, and one part Purplestar Silver. Flaming Grass, Ripple Seaweed, Earthy Root, and Breezy Grass. Good, very good.” He smiled at the assortment on the ground.","Apart from Purplestar Silver, these herbs and ores were commonly found in Darklake Empire. He’d prepared all of them beforehand— Purplestar Silver was a happy surprise.","Lu Yun summoned a ball of connate fire origin and fashioned it into a ball of connate li fire. He threw the ingredients into the fire and slowly purified them in the flame. He then separated the medicinal liquid into four jade flasks.","After reaching golden core, he could summon energy from the connate five elements. Refining pills and treasures with connate li fire was an easy task. Thus, he left the Aureate Bird Cauldron at home. Sol Truefire was far more powerful in Terra Demon’s hands than his.","With the four flasks ready, he called another ball of connate yang metal into his hand and opened the Eye of Nullification, sectioning the ingredients to predetermined ratios. Connate yang metal being the sharpest thing in existence; it made quick work of the ingredients.","Sadly, he could only use the Connate Great Dao of the Five Elements to borrow the five elements for now. When the combat art stopped operating, so did the five elements dissipate. Thankfully, the combat art didn’t require much Hongmeng qi. He wouldn’t be able to split his attention otherwise.","After he cut the ingredients into what he wished and purified them, he recombined them. They were much smaller after impurities were removed and their ratios differed. All was within Lu Yun’s calculations.","He then dismissed the flame and placed the four pieces together, hoisting them into the air with Hongmeng qi. Forgoing the usage of a pill cauldron, he waved the jade flasks to him and smashed the flasks.","The four medicinal liquids combined with each other amid a series of crackling sounds. If there was a pill grandmaster present, he’d curl his lip dismissively at Lu Yun’s actions. These four spirit herbs were just ordinary low rank ingredients. They’d create a trash pill if mixed together.","Lu Yun directed the liquid to the four purified ores, resulting in a plume of smoke. The ores had been refined by connate li fire and were the purest specimens one could find. They gradually melted from the liquid, turning to liquid themselves that melded together.","Long Aotian goggled off to the side. Lu Yun hadn’t hid his motions from him, so the man had clearly seen everything. Combining ingredients for treasures with medicinal ingredients and perfectly making a new thing out of them?","Long Aotian found it difficult to digest the sight.","Lu Yun ignored him, grasping a ball of connate fire origin from the south and throwing it into the newly complete amalgamation.","Puff!","The consolidating liquid immediately burst into flames. After roughly twenty breaths, the connate fire origin faded away and left a piece of bright red metal in front of Lu Yun.","“Essence of li fire metal, not bad, not bad.” Lu Yun waved the palm-sized metal into his hand.","Essence of li fire metal was one of the most preeminent fire attribute materials there was. Even the Human Emperor of Great Xia would look at it greedily. Lu Yun had simply used some low ranked ingredients to create a piece that was completely without impurities!","The young man summoned connate li fire again, wrapping it around the newly refined metal. He formed a seal with both hands and sent out Hongmeng qi in a series of refinement seals, stamping them into the metal.","The shape of a flying sword began to take shape when Lu Yun suddenly bit the tip of his tongue, spraying blood essence over it.","Clang!","A red flying sword exuding hot air hovered in front of Lu Yun. Two thirds of a meter long, it was slender and as thin as gossamer wings. There seemed to be a tiny flame burning in the hilt.","“An upper spirit rank weapon...” Lu Yun breathed out smoothly as he looked at the flying sword that shared the same blood as him. Thank goodness he’d stopped in time. If he’d refined a dao weapon, that would’ve been a complete waste of the essence of li fire metal.","Apart from him being unable to command a dao weapon at his current level of strength, dao weapons had their own unique presence. Once he forged one, he wouldn’t be able to conceal it with the cultivation level of golden core. He’d be the focus of attention everywhere he went.","At his cultivation, he could at most master upper rank spirit weapons. While he could use higher level weapons, it’d be a bit of a waste and consume too many resources.","Since he’d added his blood essence to the process of refinement, the flying sword recognized him as its master the moment it took shape.","“As I refined you in a land off limits to immortals, let’s call you Immortals Forbidden.” The flying sword rang with a loud croon when Lu Yun beckoned to it, flying around the young man for a while before melding into his body.","“Now I will refine Dragon Transformation Grass for you. Shame I’m missing an ingredient, though.” Lu Yun glanced at Long Aotian with a smile.","The ripples of an upper rank spirit weapon naturally didn’t escape notice. He hadn’t expected that the young man would refine such a treasure in less than one hour! Was Lu Yun a master refiner to do it so easily? Judging from his words, he could turn out a dao weapon if he wished to!","Long Aotian wasn’t the least bit skeptical that the young man could create a dao weapon if he wished to. He’d used only an hour for an upper rank spirit weapon. Given enough time, a dao weapon seemed entirely possible!","Lu Yun took out a dirt-yellow talisman from his storage ring. It was one drawn by the power of connate earth. Although he couldn’t retain the power of the connate elements, he had no issue using them to etch talismans.","However, such talismans were extraordinarily difficult to create. Since they captured the strength of the connate five elements, several days were needed to draw each one. Lu Yun had used one earlier, leaving only two Earthbending Talismans left.","“Forget it, let’s refine the medicinal liquid first and then find the inner core of the blackwater snake,” Lu Yun muttered to himself and put the talisman back into his storage ring. He was about to take out more materials when alarm bells clanged in his heart.","Whoosh!","A long and thin vine burrowed out from underground, blurring so fast with movement that it was nearly invisible.","“Go!” Lu Yun swiftly sent out Immortals Forbidden and cut the vine to pieces.","Whoosh whoosh whoosh!","It seemed to be a precursor for other veins as several hundred of them surrounded the area in the blink of an eye. Madly waving around, they churned toward Lu Yun and Long Aotian.","Lu Yun could clearly see numerous mouths on each of the veins. If either of the two were hit by the vines, they would be instantly sucked dry.","“Metal Origin Slaughter!","“Metal Origin Slaughter!","“Metal Origin Slaughter!” Lu Yun roared in succession, sending out countless rays of keen sword qi from his body. He deployed the same art of slaughter that Terra Demon had used. Metal Origin Slaughter was an art of metal in the Major Five Elements Demolition Godslayer Record and Lu Yun was the one who’d taught it to Terra Demon. It was an art that coalesced connate metal energy into rays of sword qi that could be used for both defense and offense.","There were so many vines moving so fast that while Lu Yun could protect himself in the wake of their attacks, Long Aotian could not. The man was now very precious to Lu Yun as he had a trace of dragon bloodline in him, so nothing could be permitted to happen to him.","Thus, Lu Yun resorted straight to Metal Origin Slaughter.","Sound waves rolled out as infinite tiny rays of sword qi that shoved the vines aside.","“Let’s go!” Lu Yun grabbed Long Aotian and grasped an Earthbending Talisman in his other hand. Brown light enveloped them when he waved it in the air and the two vanished from sight.","Upon losing their target, the dense canopy of vines quieted down.","......","“So is this what is meant by a forbidden zone... We’d be in for it this time if it wasn’t for the Earthbending Talisman.”","The talisman could spirit Lu Yun to safety from the strongest illusion formations. The two reappeared five hundred kilometers out and heaved a long sigh of relief. They were where the Black Tortoises had forced them into the mountains. It was a barren area now as all greenery had been destroyed. They stood in a massive pit that was a dozen kilometers across.","“That battle formation was terrifying. It collected the strength of several thousand cultivators and enhanced it more than ten times over. Even a soul separation powerhouse would have to run from it.” Lu Yun gave a long exhale as he scanned what was before him. Thank goodness he hadn’t thought too highly of himself and refined quite a few lifesaving measures before he left Darklake. He would be in real trouble otherwise."]},{"number":2273,"title":"Chapter 2273: Chapter 2185.2: Immortals Forbidden","paragraphs":["Chapter 2185.2: Immortals Forbidden","Fallen Leaf City was turning out to be a very uncanny location. With the spirit vein beneath the location, it should’ve been under Dark Orchid’s direct control and a military outpost established here.","Yet strangely enough, sects ruled the city and the royal family sent only a figurehead of a city lord. Lu Yun should’ve realized something was amiss a long time ago. He frowned as he thought of the leaders of the Black Tortoises and Azure Dragons. These people were eccentric and their moods unpredictable. It was better to stay out of their way if possible. They must have their own goals in mind to be residing here—it might have to do with the massive formation of illusion in the forbidden zone.","Lu Yun didn’t look back when he left with Long Aotian. The Fallen Leaf Range could be found to the north of Fallen Leaf Mountain. It led to the Great Yellow Range and a few other small cities in the vicinity apart from Fallen Leaf.","They were much smaller, however, and less prosperous. There weren’t many cultivators, but being cities of a fourth rank empire, there were nascent soul powerhouses in residence for even small cities.","“The blackwater snake is a third rank spirit beast, the equivalent of a golden core cultivator. They should be common in Dark Orchid.” Lu Yun led Long Aotian to a city called Boulder Rise. It was a small city in Dark Orchid, but would be second tier in Darklake. Although it wasn’t as bustling as Fallen Leaf, it was still quite affluent since it was close to Fallen Leaf City. This city was occupied by the royal family and no sect was able to find a footing here.","Long Aotian was often in the area, so he was very familiar with the nearby cities. He gave an overview of Boulder Rise after they entered.","“Young master, Boulder Rise is the second largest city in this area, second to only Fallen Leaf. The empire values it highly and its city lord is apparently a descendent of one of the emperor’s brothers,” Long Aotian sighed with appreciation. Such a personage was unequivocally important in Dark Orchid, but he was here as the city lord of a small metropolis!","That also hinted at Dark Orchid valuing Fallen Leaf Mountain more than people would expect. Apart from Fallen Leaf, the city lords of the other four cities around the mountain were all ruled by descendants of the Dark Orchid royals.","Long Aotian peeked at Lu Yun when he finished speaking. If Lu Yun continued to clash with people in this city, it would make for a very sticky situation.","Lu Yun didn’t know what the man was thinking, but would definitely protest with every fiber of his being if he knew. Is this young master such a troublemaker in your eyes?","“Alright, let’s go to the markets first and save the rest for later.” Lu Yun didn’t plan on spending time in Boulder Rise. The enormous formation of illusion around Fallen Leaf Mountain filled him with trepidation, and he was beginning to suspect that someone had planted a herb garden in the one hundred kilometers of cleared land within the formation.","He’d harvested everything in it, which meant trouble would be coming after its master discovered the theft. An ordinary immortal couldn’t have possibly set that formation up. Thus, Lu Yun wanted to leave this dratted place as soon as he obtained the inner core of a blackwater snake. He’d come back for a look after he gained sufficient strength.","At the same time, inexplicable ease filtered into Lu Yun’s heart. With the leaders of the Azure Dragons, White Tigers, and Black Tortoises holding down the fort, whatever was inside Immortal Burial Valley would be somewhat restrained if they emerged.","Despite that, Lu Yun wasn’t in the habit of placing his hopes in others. He needed to do everything possible now to enhance his strength and develop his own faction!","Dragons were one of the strongest existences in the world of immortals. Dragon purebloods were born as dao immortals and became immortal overlords in maturity. The dragon race had answered to his banner when he reincarnated into the world of immortals—their patriarch, the Dragon Immortal King, was second to only Terra Demon.","Lu Yun was able to detect the hint of bloodline in Long Aotian because he’d once been the master of dragons. If it wasn’t for that, he would have no idea what the abnormality within the man’s body was, even upon taking a clear look at it.","The strand of bloodline was too thin.","Additionally, his predisposition toward dragons came from a name in his subconscious—Aoxue. While he had new people that he cared about in this lifetime, the ones from his subconscious had become his obsession.","Boulder Rise was less than Fallen Leaf, but it was also a hotbed of activity. Treasures and items, such as the inner core of third rank spirit beasts, that were rare in Darklake were common sights here. Some of the larger trading companies and shops in the marketplace had inner cores of third rank spirit beasts for sale, but those went for steep asking prices.","Foundation establishment cultivators could outright refine these inner cores and absorb the energy of the five elements within to strengthen their spirit root. They could also be used to refine pills and treasures. No matter the usage or place, the inner cores of spirit beasts were hot commodities.","Given their high prices, however, ordinary cultivators could only look wistfully at them. Inner cores were produced only in spirit beasts that were third rank or stronger—the equivalent of a golden core human cultivator.","A third rank beast wasn’t a target that an ordinary golden core cultivator could manage. The inner cores of spirit beasts were luxuries in all worlds of cultivation.","Crowds thronged the markets of Boulder Rise City, on par with those of the southern quadrant of Dark City. Sudden regret surfaced in Lu Yun’s mind—he should’ve visited Fallen Leaf’s marketplace when he was in that city.","Seeing as it was his first visit to a fourth rank cultivation empire then, he wasn't very familiar with the situation. It wasn't until he took in the marketplace of Boulder Rise City that he understood there was an unbridgeable chasm between the third and fourth rank empires.","This was all because cultivators of fourth rank nations could enter the Celestial Realm Battlefront. Resources found there were far in excess of what were available in the worlds of cultivation. Each nascent soul cultivator of a fourth rank nation could enter the battlefront—but this was limited to its citizens and required approval from the royal family first.","Lu Yun hadn’t given thought to joining Dark Orchid. For the moment, at least, it was completely infiltrated by the Origin Sect and had become a thorn planted next to the Lu Clan. Lu Yun’s primary goal for his visit was to shave down this thorn and gain more information about the nation.","Currently, he was dressed as a dashing young man. Long Aotian wore modestly luxurious accoutrements and looked like his follower. They didn’t raise much attention in the marketplace as master and servant duos were often seen.","“The Trading Company of the Four Seas?” Lu Yun suddenly stopped in front of a storefront. This was Boulder Rise’s largest trading company and his Eye of Nullification glimpsed an inner core of the blackwater snake within its vaults.","“This is the place.” He was about to set foot inside when three cultivators walked out of its front doors. Their eyes widened when they saw Long Aotian behind Lu Yun.","“It’s you, Long Aotian! We’ve looked high and low for you, but in the end you fall right into our laps!” Their leader was a latter foundation establishment cultivator and was supremely excited to see Long Aotian.","The two next to him were mid foundation establishment and also looked greedily at Long Aotian.","The man subconsciously shrank in on himself, then sneered back at them when he thought of something.","“What’s going on here?” Lu Yun asked as the three approached them.","“Sir, I ran into them when I discovered the treasure. If it wasn’t for me running off so quickly, they would’ve killed me and taken it from me.” The treasure he spoke of was the Purplestar Silver.","Purplestar Silver was so precious that even soul projection cultivators fought over it. Long Aotian didn’t dare reveal it as he felt Lu Yun was no match for soul projection experts.","“Hahaha, I say, found yourself a rich kid, haven’t you? You’ve become a rich kid’s dog, but do you think a kid wet behind the ears can protect you?” cackled the latter foundation establishment as he sized up Lu Yun.","“Wait, it’s you two! Us brothers risked our lives for that Purplestar Silver and you took it from us!” he suddenly cried out.","Passersby blinked and strange expressions crept across their faces. Most halted to look at Lu Yun and Long Aotian.","“Purplestar Silver? Where is Purplestar Silver?” An elder with white hair and a white beard rushed out of the first floor lobby, looking at Lu Yun with agitation.","“Grand steward, when we discovered Purplestar Silver, this master and servant duo took it from us through superior strength! You must uphold justice for us!” The latter foundation establishment cultivator immediately looked at Lu Yun and Long Aotian with a face full of fury when he saw the elder.","“Gentleman, no one can touch the things of the Trading Company of the Four Seas. Since your Purplestar Silver was wrested from our hands, please return it, or we will show you no mercy!” The elder glowered after hearing these words."]},{"number":2274,"title":"Chapter 2274: Chapter 2186.1: Red Spider Lily, Hell Flower","paragraphs":["Chapter 2186.1: Red Spider Lily, Hell Flower","Lu Yun’s expression remained the same as it was—he’d seen more than his fair share of similar situations. Long Aotian, however, flushed beet red and was beside himself with fury.","“You’re an absolute piece of motherfucking shit! I risked my life to scoop that Purplestar Silver out from the Jade Ice Lake in Fallen Leaf Mountain. When did it come from your hands?!” Long Aotian couldn't help but roar.","“Jade Ice Lake?” Lu Yun quirked an eyebrow when he heard the name.","“Jade Ice Lake? Can a puny mid foundation establishment cultivator like you enter the lake?” sneered the steward. “In contrast, latter foundation establishment cultivators stand a chance of making it out alive if they try.”","He looked at Lu Yun when he finished speaking. Being initial nascent soul, the steward could easily tell that the young man was initial golden core. However, this level of cultivator would still find it very dangerous if they ventured into Jade Ice Lake. Not to mention, Lu Yun was plainly dressed like a noble scion. A pampered young master like him would never risk his life in the lake.","Thus, the steward was much more willing to believe that this master and servant duo had robbed his men.","“This young gentleman is quite courageous to seize treasure that belongs to the Trading Company of the Four Seas. Return it with haste and I’ll take your youth into account. All that needs to occur for this matter to end is the crippling of your cultivation.” Greed shone in the old man’s eyes as a sardonic curve played on his lips.","They would have the Purplestar Silver no matter what. Since his three men said that it came from them, it was the perfect pretext for taking it. Purplestar Silver was priceless in fourth rank empires. It was premier refinement material that stood a high chance of turning a paramount rank spirit weapon into a dao weapon.","There was a master refiner in residence at the trading company. If supplied with Purplestar Silver, it was very likely that the faction would gain a dao weapon for themselves.","“Cripple my cultivation?” Lu Yun sneered to himself, but maintained a genteel smile. “Heh heh heh, I’d love to hear from the crowd. Would I, a vaunted golden core cultivator, not think to cover my tracks and kill all of them after taking treasure from some useless foundation establishment cultivators?”","The crowd began murmuring among themselves, but no one dared say anything in front of the eminent Trading Company of the Four Seas. This was the foremost trading company within Dark Orchid and its background stretched to the fifth rank cultivation empires. There was more than one soul projection cultivator among their ranks.","“Hmph, you tried killing us, but we three are subordinate to the Trading Company of the Four Seas and naturally have some lifesaving measures. You couldn’t manage to take us out!” The latter foundation establishment cultivator looked proudly at Lu Yun.","“You mean... I’m unable to kill you guys?” The young man’s smile deepened.","Standing next to Lu Yun, Long Aotian shuddered when he saw the expression. He’d seen this smile three times already, each followed by a bloody slaughter.","The grand steward of the Trading Company of the Four Seas? He might be a prominent figure in Boulder Rise City, but more nascent soul powerhouses than could be counted had already died to Lu Yun’s hands.","Long Aotian swallowed hard. What’d occurred in Fallen Leaf had already made its way to Boulder Rise. What might this grand steward think if he knew that the bloodthirsty demon of Fallen Leaf was the seemingly harmless young man in front of him?","“Hmph!” the steward snorted coldly. He’d seen too many noble scions like this young man. Their cultivation was the result of pills and medicines. Although the young man was of the golden core level, he could at most manage to bully those weaker than him. If he met someone of the same level, there was only a beating in store for him.","Pfft pfft pfft!","Red light flashed in front of the grand steward as three heads shot into the air. The three foundation establishment cultivators that’d been jeering their opponent flopped over as headless bodies.","“Aiya! I’m so sorry, my deepest apologies! I didn’t mean to! I just wanted to see if I could kill you guys... It looks like I can!” Lu Yun looked at the steward with a look of exaggerated horror. “Senior, I—I really didn’t think that I could kill three foundation establishment experts. I really didn’t do it on purpose!”","His acting skills were so bad and his words so ludicrous that they were a hefty slap across the steward’s face. As ridiculous as the scene was, no one could find it in them to laugh. The young man had been smiling gently at them moments ago, but killed three people in the blink of an eye! Was he a demon?","“How dare you kill those from the Trading Company of the Four Seas?!” Livid, the nascent soul grand steward’s eyes nearly spat fire. He was about to take action when someone gasped in the crowd.","“It’s him! He’s the young man wanted by the Black Tortoises of Fallen Leaf!” yelled a terrified man in gray. “He’s the one who destroyed the Darkwater Gang overnight and killed more than sixty Black Tortoise disciples. He killed the sect leader’s dao partner!”","“That’s right, it’s him! I saw him kill the Darkwater Gang leader with two kicks that day. Ying Xuanshui was a nascent soul powerhouse!”","“They say that the Black Tortoises sent a thousand disciples to capture him. They battled in Fallen Leaf Mountain and leveled everything within fifty kilometers. So he’s still alive!”","“No wonder the Black Tortoises still have an outstanding bounty for him!”","“The bounty’s three million paramount rank spirit stones for his head! Even information of his whereabouts or other clues will fetch one hundred thousand!”","Many cultivators looked at Lu Yun with eyes of greed, like they were seeing mounds of spirit stones.","“Three million paramount rank stones?” Lu Yun licked his lips. Was his head worth that much?","Three million was an incredible sum! The sum total of what he’d taken from the Ouyang trading company was just nearly one million. Here the Black Tortoises were, offering three of the Ouyang trading company for his head. It would tempt even soul projection powerhouses.","It felt like a bucket of cold water had been dumped over the steward of the Four Seas, however. Killing a mid nascent soul powerhouse with two kicks? He was a joke to the young man!","He turned tail and ran without another word, entering the trading company. The building’s defensive formation activated with a rumble—they lacked the courage to even face Lu Yun head-on.","As strong as the trading company was, they didn’t have many troops in tiny Boulder Rise. There was only one latter nascent soul elder in residence. They were renowned throughout the fourth rank empires, after all. No one dared cause trouble at one of the trading company’s branches.","“How could I possibly stop here after finding the inner core of the blackwater snake? You provoked me first and I’m not a saint, so why should I let you off the hook?” Lu Yun sneered at the formation. “A third rank defensive formation of earth giving rise to metal?”","Pale green light flashed from his hand and he pointed at the earth element in the formation’s core essence. Connate yi wood condensed to an imperceptible seed that sank into the formation. It quickly germinated and absorbed all of the earth energy within the formation. Lacking a fundamental part of its support, the metal energy within the formation quickly collapsed.","The third rank formation fell apart in less than half a breath.","“Come with me,” Lu Yun called out to Long Aotian and entered the trading company structure.","Currently, its customers were gathered in the first floor lobby while associates collected all of its treasures in an orderly fashion, ready to transfer them elsewhere.","“A brat wet behind the ears has all of you running scared. What an utter joke!” Contempt crossed the face of a twenty-eight year old man. Dressed in opulent upper qi rank robes, he watched the busy associates with boredom.","There were quite a few factions present in the lobby as well as cultivators with impressive backgrounds. They looked down their noses at the trading company’s actions, finding them a gross overreaction.","A loud bang sounded the next second—a sound that a crude porcelain object would make when broken. Sunlight filtered into the lobby as the front doors were kicked open.","“What?! Our defensive formation was broken?!” The grand steward trembled like a leaf to see Lu Yun and Long Aotian walk in.","There was a branch of the Trading Company of the Four Seas in Fallen Leaf City. Thus, the branch in Boulder Rise was well aware of what’d taken place in Fallen Leaf. Although there was a latter nascent soul elder holding down the fort in Boulder Rise, he knew that he was no match for Lu Yun. He himself could fend off Ying Xuanshui, but he couldn’t kick the other to death with two moves!","One could visualize the entire animal when looking at the single spot of a leopard.","Winds of change billowed through Jade Ruins Realm these days as countless Great Xia experts surged in. In return, the incomparably mysterious Great Xia Dynasty was no longer the mystifying unknown in some people’s eyes."]},{"number":2275,"title":"Chapter 2275: Chapter 2186.2: Red Spider Lily, Hell Flower","paragraphs":["Chapter 2186.2: Red Spider Lily, Hell Flower","The latter nascent soul elder of the trading company was beginning to suspect that this noble scion hailed from a high rank empire or from Great Xia. The Trading Company of the Four Seas had long witnessed the might of Great Xia cultivators, but to think that someone possibly from them would appear here today!","“Sir!” The grand steward shuddered when he saw Lu Yun break through the formation and ran up to bow.","“Heh, you can run pretty fast when you put your mind to it.” Lu Yun smiled lazily and gently slapped the steward’s mouth. Sweat beaded the man’s forehead. If he still couldn’t tell that this young man was no ordinary person after he broke through a third rank defensive formation in seconds, then he might as well end himself right here.","“Does this piece of Purplestar Silver belong to your trading company?” Lu Yun hefted an ore the size of a fist that was missing a corner. He waved it in front of the steward.","“No no, not at all. It was your follower who risked his life to fish it out of Jade Ice Lake. How is it ours?” the steward hastily shook his head.","“Hahaha, what a farce! Is this the Trading Company of the Four Seas who dominates Dark Orchid? You’re a complete joke!” The twenty-eight year old burst into raucous laughter to see the steward curry favor with a young man.","“No matter how we are, it is not your place to talk about us!” The grand steward whirled around with fury and released his aura without restraint. It crashed over the latter golden core young man, causing the blood to drain from his face as he stumbled a dozen steps backward and fell to a sitting position on the ground.","“How dare you, Qu Jing!” An incensed initial nascent soul elder next to the twenty-eight year old helped him up.","“Xu Feng, your Nineheavens Pagoda may be the number one sect of Dark Orchid, but you’re nothing in the eyes of the Trading Company of the Four Seas! We will show you no mercy if you further run your mouth in our domain!” Qu Jing sniffed as he looked at the sect elder.","“Do you represent the Trading Company of the Four Seas?” Xu Feng replied frostily.","“Grand Steward Qu Jing is part of the trading company’s senior council. Of course he represents us,” came a gentle and empty voice from upstairs. It echoed in the lobby before an eighteen year old young man floated down from the second floor.","Dressed in long white robes and as dainty as a sprite, he was utterly pristine like a snow flower in winter. His features were exquisite and his face clearly structured, but a hint of sickly pallor in his complexion gave him an unusual tenderness.","The only thing that invoked pity was that there was no focus to his eyes, like he was blind. He held an unnaturally brilliant red flower in his hands, its long petals as bright as blood. It bloomed with an unusual fragrance that set one at ease.","Lu Yun could tell with a single glance that the young man was very ordinary and latter nascent soul. However, the corner of his eyes twitched.","“Red Spider Lily... Hell Flower!” He stared fixedly at the flower in the young man’s hands. The Red Spider Lily, also known as the Hell Flower, grew on the banks of the River of Forgetfulness in the underworld of the three realms. It bloomed once every five hundred years and wilted after another five hundred. Also known as the Flower of Death, Lu Yun had hardly expected to see a legendary demonic item here.","Indeed, the Red Spider Lily was also known as the flower of demons. It fed on blood and souls. With such a diet, it would never wither. In the underworld, however, it was beyond sacred. It wasn’t often seen on the banks of the River of Forgetfulness and was ranked third among the top ten materials in existence.","There weren’t many who could recognize it. Lu Yun had happened to see it by chance when he reincarnated through the underworld. One who owned it was no ordinary soul. More importantly was that a strange spasm shifted through his heart when he saw the flower.","“Hell Flower... River of Forgetfulness... hell...” Lu Yun shook his head fiercely, his sealed memories churning with agitation. This time, the dao character was unable to silence them. Light flashed from the soul pagoda to suppress them when the dao character proved inadequate.","Hell Flower... River of Forgetfulness... these things...","“Young lord!” Qu Jing’’s eyes went wide when he saw the young man. The arrival of the trading company’s most mysterious young lord was most unexpected!","Another latter nascent soul powerhouse of roughly fifty years old stood behind the young man in white—the elder holding down the fort at this branch of the trading company.","“Qu Jing’s words can represent the Trading Company of the Four Seas. Those of the Nineheavens Pagoda can leave now.” The young man wore a stiff smile as his tone remained as gentle and empty as before.","“And what the fuck are you to represent the trading company?!” blustered the latter golden core young man who’d been thrown backwards.","“My words naturally represent the trading company.” The young man shook his head and snapped his fingers.","Bam bam!","The two floated out of the lobby.","“Sir, I have gained an understanding of everything that transpired. It is the Trading Company of the Four Seas at fault. You have killed those three, will you show mercy to Qu Jing on my behalf?” the young man spoke slowly as he turned his vacant eyes onto Lu Yun.","“I can, but I require some compensation,” Lu Yun answered evenly. This young man’s presence seemed very similar to someone he knew. No, it was exactly the same! In these sealed memories, this person was one of the people he was closest to.","The same person had appeared in this world. All was a function of reincarnation.","“What might it be?” The young man’s face twitched as he tried to smile radiantly. He gave up after a few abortive attempts.","“I want the inner core of the blackwater snake.”","“Qu Jing, fetch the inner core and give it to this gentleman.”","“Yes, young lord!” Qu Jing took out a black inner core from his storage ring and placed it in Lu Yun’s hand. He’d moved most of the treasures at the trading company into his storage ring before Lu Yun broke the formation.","“My thanks. Aotian, let’s go.” Lu Yun left as soon as he received the inner core, prompting sighs of relief from the other customers before they left as well.","“Lan Yu,” the young man in white said after everyone had left.","“Young lord!” The latter nascent soul elder hastily bowed.","“Withdraw our branches in the Fallen Leaf, Ice Moon, Iron Curtain, and Boulder Rise Cities. Move them to Dark City in Darklake Empire and partner with the Lu Clan,” the young man commanded softly. “They should see some reward for taking care of Little Wu for more than a year...”","......","“Sir, where do we go now?” Long Aotian felt like he was walking on air after they left the Trading Company of the Four Seas. This legendary faction had shown so much face to his lord that they’d clashed with the greatest sect in Dark Orchid!","On the other hand, Lu Yun knew that the trading company had suddenly turned so respectful for other reasons. If he had to go up against the young man with the Red Spider Lily, there would be nothing but defeat in the cards for him.","“Let’s take care of the trouble at hand first before we go to Jade Ice Lake.” Lu Yun looked behind him and sneered.","Long Aotian quickly realized that the Nineheavens Pagoda would soon swing by. The young master had humiliated them earlier. They couldn’t do anything to the trading company, but they could to Lu Yun.","Those two from the sect had arrived in Boulder Rise only today. They didn’t know what’d occurred in Fallen Leaf, but would think nothing of it if they did. They didn’t think much of the mere Darkwater Gang and Black Tortoises. Wiping out the gang? They could do that too.","The three million paramount stone bounty was the most important task at hand. There were plenty of desperadoes and others in Boulder Rise who meant Lu Yun no good. He exited the city being trailed by countless cultivators.","“Hahaha, the three million stones are mine!” Blade light flashed by without warning as a massive long blade cut down on Lu Yun’s head.","“You want to die, don’t you!” he snorted and pointed at the light.","Pfft!","Immortals Restriction shot out from his fingertip and rebuffed the weapon. Its owner didn’t even have time to scream before his head was separated from his body.","“How does a golden core idiot have the balls to make a play for me?”"]},{"number":2276,"title":"Chapter 2276: Chapter 2187.1: Jade Ice Lake","paragraphs":["Chapter 2187.1: Jade Ice Lake","While Immortals Restriction was just an upper rank spirit weapon, it was made from the essence of li fire metal. As such, its speed was unparalleled, as was its keenness. Ordinary golden core cultivators wouldn’t even be able to catch a glimpse of its shadow.","Lu Yun waved it back to him as a streak of light.","“An upper spirit rank weapon!” shrieked some of the cultivators following him when they obtained a clearer look at the flying sword.","Upper spirit rank weapons were premier treasures in fourth rank empires. The ultimate treasure of the Nineheavens Pagoda, the foremost sect of Dark Orchid, was an upper rank spirit treasure. Just one alone was worth far more than three million paramount stones!","The cultivators following Lu Yun revealed themselves, looking at him with blatant greed. So this was why the Black Tortoises had listed a bounty of three million for a mere golden core cultivator!","“Hand over your weapon and I’ll spare your life!” roared a bulky initial nascent soul cultivator with a tanned face.","Boulder Rise cultivators had only heard snippets of what’d happened in Fallen Leaf. They didn’t know the complete story and many thought the stories were exaggerated. How strong could a golden core young man possibly be?","Lu Yun shook his head slightly at the group. “I don’t want to randomly kill people, so you have one chance. Leave, right now.”","Immortals Restriction flared with a foreboding red light and exploded with killing intent.","“He’s just relying on the power of his weapon! How much of it can you bring to bear when you’re just initial golden core??” The tanned man abruptly brought out a black blade and whipped up a black tornado, aiming it at Long Aotian.","The man was very astute as he discerned that the young man must be extraordinary if the Trading Company of the Four Seas was wary of him. But the man next to him was just a normal foundation establishment cultivator. Attacking him would force the young man to respond, which would give him an opportunity to take both out.","The remaining three hundred cultivators also shifted to action when the tanned man moved. They brought out their treasures and flung them at the duo.","“Stand back.” Lu Yun remained expressionless as light blossomed from his sword. It now more resembled a blazing sun. “Die!!”","The sword radiance burst to nine meters long. He struck with a backhand and decapitated the tanned man before he had a chance to draw near Long Aotian. His mid fine rank weapon was also smashed to smithereens.","“I gave you guys a chance,” he growled. The sword radiance split into several hundred rays that were nine meters long each and sealed off the void.","The Five Elements of Absolute Slaughter—Fire Slaughter!","He’d used this technique against the nascent soul Ouyang Shengtian when Lu Yun himself was only foundation establishment. He’d sent the Ouyang genius scurrying for cover then. Now that he was initial golden core, had formed his golden core of great dao, and wielded an upper rank spirit weapon, he was more than ten times stronger than before. This move had previously resulted in only a dozen rays of sword light, now it was capable of hundreds.","Pfft pfft pfft!","Some of the weaker cultivators didn’t even have time to react before the crimson light cut them down and burned them to ashes.","The sword light recombined into one and returned to Lu Yun’s hand after a dozen breaths. Only five nascent soul cultivators still remained standing. They stared at the young man with shock—he’d cut down more than three hundred cultivators in a few breaths! Most of them had been golden core and nascent soul powerhouses. Was this still a cultivator of initial golden core?","“Hmph!” Lu Yun took a deep look at the survivors and stalked off toward Boulder Rise City.","A few hundred? They might pose a threat if they were golden core and nascent soul cultivators from Great Xia. But from a world of cultivation and with such a crude grasp of utilizing true origin?","Never.","The outcome would be the same even if it was Mo Qiyue or Jiang Feng standing in his shoes.","“Young master, why didn’t you kill all of them?” Long Aotian had long grown numb to the sight of Lu Yun killing numerous heavyweights.","“All of them? If I did, who would tell the Black Tortoises that I’m still at Boulder Rise?” Lu Yun grinned and sent a talisman into the two of them. They disappeared from sight. “Let’s go!”","He grabbed Long Aotian, raised sword light, and flew toward Fallen Leaf Mountain. He wanted to direct the Black Tortoises to Boulder Rise while he made visited Jade Ice Lake. If there was Purplestar Silver in it, then there must be Starnet Stone.","Starnet Stone grew alongside Purplestar Silver. While it was rare, it wasn’t particularly important refinement material. Or rather, one could say that it couldn’t be used in refinement at all. It was no different from a stubborn rock by the side of the road.","But in Lu Yun’s eyes, it was a priceless treasure. Not just because of its rarity, but because these kinds of ore could be fashioned into Proxima Metal. Proxima Metal was a key material in fashioning the cross forges that powered the cross arks.","Lu Yun had in his possession a battered ark with a completely destroyed cross forge. He wasn’t able to repair it due to lack of Proxima Metal. Now that he knew where to find Starnet Stone, he naturally wouldn’t pass up a chance to collect it.","Cross arks were key weapons in battle that could transport a million cultivators. Even immortals kept out of their way when encountering them.","As for how to design a cross forge or repair a cross ark, Lu Yun was the one who’d invented them. It was an easy task for him to create a new cross ark so long as he had sufficient materials and time.","Inventing the cross ark had come from his instinctual memories, from a time when they were yet to be fully sealed away. A faint image had lingered, which became the blueprints for the cross ark. Lu Yun now could fully combine the memories and experience of three thousand lifetimes together—he could craft something much more amazing than the cross ark.","They landed on the main peak of Fallen Leaf Mountain after roughly an hour. Jade Ice Lake was located at the mountain’s foot to the northwest, close to the land forbidden to immortals. It was a modestly sized lake at approximately ninety meters across. Waters beautiful as jade, they were also forbiddingly cold. Dangers lurked beneath the surface and unknown spirit beasts called it home. Not even nascent soul cultivators could be guaranteed a safe return if they ventured in.","Even so, many low level cultivators often explored around it—Long Aotian being one of them.","Night had fallen and the dense canopy at the foot of Fallen Leaf Mountain blotted out the stars in the sky. There was a clearing roughly five kilometers wide to the north of the mountain. Nothing grew there, sand and rocks were exposed to the open air. It was there that Jade Ice Lake could be found.","Its waters rippled beneath the starry radiance and a faint layer of fog circled over its jade-green waters. All was unusually quiet. Some spirit beasts occasionally called from the forest around the lake. There were no signs of cultivators to be found.","A black shadow suddenly flashed by and deposited two people by the shore.","“So this is Jade Ice Lake, it is as its name indicates.” When Lu Yun probed the water, he subconsciously identified it according to the scales of his subconscious. It was fifty degrees below zero and the barren clearing around it was a result of the lake’s influence.","Oddly enough, the temperature immediately returned to normal when one exited the clearing. Nothing beyond five kilometers was affected by it.","“Fallen Leaf Mountain is definitely a strange place,” he sighed to himself. Jade Ruins Realm was no ordinary world of cultivation either. There was a massive formation of illusion to the north of the mountain and now this lake. Most terrifying of all were the things suppressed beneath the sword pagoda.","He looked into the waters with the Eye of Nullification.","“What?!” he sucked in a sharp breath. The Eye of Nullification had a range of fifty kilometers, but it couldn’t see to the bottom of the lake! This body of water that was just ninety meters wide was over fifty kilometers deep!","He quickly found what he was looking for on the walls of the lake. There was a modestly sized vein of Purplestar Silver approximately twenty-five kilometers down, interspersed with plenty of Starnet Stone.","Lu Yun avoided wading into Jade Ice Lake without further thought as he could see countless snake-shaped spirit beasts beneath the surface. They were thirty meters long and the thickness of a water bucket. Four underdeveloped claws extended beneath their bellies as they silently hung onto the walls of the lake.","He wouldn’t have discovered them if not for the Eye of Nullification.","“So they’re remnants of jiao with a hint of the jiao bloodlines.” Lu Yun looked at the unmoving creatures in the lake.","Most cultivators, even immortals, thought that the bloodline of dragons ran through jiao, that they could transform into dragons.","It was an erroneous notion. Jiao were an individual race that was on par with dragons. The king of the seas in the world of immortals had been a chaos jiao with ten pairs of wings. It was a chaos immortal hailed as the Chaos Sea Emperor. The patriarch of the dragons had only been an immortal king, so their difference in strength was apparent at a glance.","But since pureblood jiao were few and far in between, there were only a dozen of them in the world. Most of them were intermixed with the dragon bloodline, hence being called scaled-dragons. That was the source of most people’s misunderstanding of them.","The chaos jiao in the world of immortals had died for mysterious reasons not long after Lu Yun became the High Lord of the Northern Sky. The denizens of the world only saw the upper half of his long body that tens of thousands of kilometers fall from the sky. No one knew anything else.","The black spirit beasts beneath Jade Ice Lake were pureblood, not scaled-dragons. They would transform into monster spirits as soon as their bloodlines were activated.","“Jiao and dragons are from the same origins in the world of immortals. No wonder Long Aotian can come and go at will since he possesses a trace of the dragon bloodline.” Lu Yun understood why the man had been able to safely retrieve Purplestar Silver from the lake.","“Sir, there are terrifying spirit beasts beneath that are mostly third or fourth rank. Many nascent soul seniors have been swallowed by them in the past,” Long Aotian quickly said when he saw that Lu Yun seemed ready to go for a dip."]},{"number":2277,"title":"Chapter 2277: Chapter 2187.2: Jade Ice Lake","paragraphs":["Chapter 2187.2: Jade Ice Lake","“Those spirit beasts show friendly faces to you instead of attacking, don’t they?” Lu Yun chuckled.","Though Long Aotian was surprised, he nodded. “This humble one depended on the lake for survival before I met the young master. But while the spirit beasts do not harm me, the waters are so terrifying that I can only venture in several dozen meters at most. The Purplestar Silver was a gift from the beasts in the waters. Please show mercy, young master, and don’t hurt them.” As simple and honest as Long Aotian seemed, he was also exceedingly prudent. While he was able to communicate with the spirit beasts in the lake and form a relationship with them, he didn’t tell anyone else about it.","It would be a catastrophic disaster for someone as weak as him if it became widely known.","“In that case, you’ll come down with me.” Lu Yun nodded with a smile.","Long Aotian started, then indicated his agreement. The young man grabbed his shoulder and the two dived into the lake.","Humm!","Lu Yun grabbed a handful of connate kui water origin from the north and used it to part the waters. The lake’s waters quickly shifted to the side when it encountered water origin energy, like a grandson meeting their grandfather.","The black spirit beasts went on alert when they detected an intrusion. Crimson eyes blinked open in the depths and scanned the trespassers. But when they saw that it was Long Aotian, their proud heads dipped in slight acknowledgment. Thanks to his proximity to Long Aotian, Lu Yun was overlooked by the beasts.","Their passage was free of obstacles and they easily made it twenty-five kilometers beneath the surface. The temperature here was much cooler than in the shallows. Even Lu Yun found it incredibly cold. If Long Aotian hadn’t been protected by Lu Yun’s Hongmeng qi, he would’ve frozen to death long ago.","Lu Yun also noted that the black spirit beasts at this depth had purer bloodlines than those above. He subconsciously glanced beneath him and found that he was still unable to see to the bottom.","“If Jade Ice Lake is five thousand kilometers deep, there might be pureblood jiao at the bottom,” he murmured to himself.","“Here it is.” Crimson light flashed from his hand and bit into the rock wall.","Schick!","A piece of wall sixty meters long disengaged from the rest. There was a minor Purplestar Silver vein inside, interspersed with numerous Starnet Stone.","This immediately drew the displeasure of the nearby spirit beasts. They raised their heads and howled with protest, but refrained from attacking Lu Yun because of Long Aotian next to him.","“The Black Tortoises are probably still looking for me above ground, which makes it a bit inconvenient to refine the Dragon Transformation Grass. I might as well try to do it here!”","Immortals Forbidden flashed forward again and created a massive hole two dozen meters across. Lu Yun cast a boundary at its entrance, blocking the lake waters outside. He then took out a few night pearls and embedded them into the wall.","“Sir, what are...” Long Aotian asked as he didn’t understand Lu Yun’s actions.","“It’s not safe up on shore, so I’m going to refine the grass for you here.” Lu Yun looked solemnly at Long Aotian. “You need to think carefully about this. Once you take the Dragon Transformation Grass and activate your dragon bloodline, you will no longer be human! You will also have to serve me.”","“Long Aotian’s life was this young master’s long ago!” Long Aotian snapped to seriousness, saying nothing about taking dragon form. He’d doubted Lu Yun’s words at first, but had thought things through by now. The spirit beasts in Jade Ice Lake were extraordinarily vicious and often attacked cultivators in the area. They treated only him differently, likely due to the dragon bloodline in his body.","“Meditate off to the side first and don’t make a sound,” Lu Yun nodded.","Long Aotian turned around and sat down on the other side of the cavern, closing his eyes in meditation.","“While the Dragon Transformation Grass is ranked last among the thirty-six earthly treasures, it is superior to any immortal grass. I hope I succeed in one try!” Lu Yun exhaled sharply.","In the lifetime he spent as a pill master, he’d done so as a cultivator, not immortal. He’d used the most run-of-the-mill spirit herbs to replicate the attributes of the Shennong Grass—number nine of the ten heavenly ingredients in the world of immortals. Compared to the ten, the thirty-six earthly treasures were much easier to handle. Not to mention, he could use the energy of the connate elements however he’d like now. The tools in his arsenal now were much stronger than before.","The Dragon Transformation Grass was useful only for dragons or those with draconic bloodline. There was a hint of barely detectable draconic bloodline in the inner core of the blackwater snake.","Lu Yun summoned a ball of connate li fire, then took out one hundred ingredients from his storage ring. He tossed them into the fire one after another.","Now that his memories of three thousand lifetimes were one, much of his disassociated knowledge was streamlined together. Although he’d never refined this grass before, he’d studied it when he was the High Lord of the Northern Sky. Combined with his memories as a pill master, it meant his mind swiftly flew through the calculations for refining the Dragon Transformation Grass.","“Chemistry...” The word suddenly flashed through his mind. “...what is chemistry?”","He cocked his head and thought for a long time before realizing it came from his sealed memories. Sighing, he put it out of his mind.","The basic theory of recreating medicinal attributes was to trace each attribute back to its origin. Once a foundation was set, one could create a brand new set of attributes through various combinations of proportion and shape.","While the ten heavenly ingredients and thirty-six earthly treasures were undeniably precious and rare, they were the combination of some of the most fundamental particles at the end of the day. He would be able to recreate their attributes if he located the particles that formed these ingredients and reassemble them according to the proper sequence.","As for why spirit herbs were stronger the older they were, it was because their basic matter accumulated in vaster quantities as time went on, thereby enhancing their effects. That meant that the legendary Chaos Purple Lotus at the head of the ten, even one that was one hundred million years old, was the same fundamental makeup as a tiny blade of grass by the side of the road.","It was a similar theory to the structure of formations. No matter how formations shifted, their fundamental principle was the relationship between the five elements. Even formations of whirlwinds or thunder and lightning that were beyond the five elements arose because of the five.","The methods used may vary, but the nature remained the same.","Everything would be so much easier with formula dao—the thought suddenly bloomed in Lu Yun’s mind. From dao came one, and one begat two, two gave birth to three, and from three resulted all living things!","Boom!","An explosion went off in Lu Yun’s mind as Hongmeng qi surged into motion and circulated through his body. He broke through to mid golden core as a natural development of things. Goodwill stored in the Seal of the Multitude burst forth and melded into his Hongmeng qi, pushing his cultivation to peak mid golden core.","However, that exhausted the reserves in the seal.","Long Aotian’s jaw dropped. What was this? Could one break through while refining a pill? While he couldn’t see through Lu Yun’s cultivation, the disturbance raised by the young man’s breakthrough didn’t go unnoticed.","Most mind-boggling of all was that despite his ascension, Lu Yun continued to busy himself with the fire and spirit herbs in his hands. He didn’t pause to operate his cultivation methods and consolidate his new level, as if cultivation had nothing to do with him.","Wasn’t the kid worried about a cultivation deviation??","Little did Long Aotian know that the true meaning of the Nine Chapters of Dao was to allow things to develop as they would. Lu Yun’s methods would operate even if he ate and slept, so a cultivation deviation was never a possibility.","He’d isolated three hundred and ninety-five spirit herbs; it was time for the inner core of the blackwater snake. He threw it into the flame and split out the strand of dragon bloodline.","“Combine!” he shouted and pulled several hundred balls of medicinal liquid together. They assimilated in a series of pops and crackles. Hand seals flew rapidly as the connate five elements changed swiftly, attempting to perfectly meld all of them together.","While they were the building blocks of the Dragon Transformation Grass, many of them conflicted with each other. There couldn’t be the slightest mistake in process or procedure. If anything went wrong, then the entire attempt was a failure.","Lu Yun entered a marvelous state as he unknowingly opened the Eye of Nullification, scanning every single particle with almost a meter of golden light. His swift hand seals continuously broke the liquid apart and reassembled them into brand new properties.","Glyphs flew out of his hands, ensuring that the newly formed properties could coexist harmoniously. A vast and bleak presence emanated from the ball of liquid.","Long Aotian shuddered as deep desire rose from his heart. He stared fixedly at the congealing liquid in Lu Yun’s hands. It was a pill with the properties of Dragon Transformation Grass!"]},{"number":2278,"title":"Chapter 2278: Chapter 2188.1: Dragon Lady?","paragraphs":["Chapter 2188.1: Dragon Lady?","The ball of medicinal liquid solidified into a cerulean blue pill after a rush of water origin energy. Lu Yun heaved a long sigh of relief. His first attempt at recreating the properties of one of the thirty-six earthly treasures after his awakening had been a resounding success! He’d even come across more understanding of dao.","This was the ultimate peak of dao and would be very helpful when he became the heavenly dao in the future. Naturally, he didn’t realize it at the moment.","“I have the Eye of Nullification, connate five elements, and Hongmeng true qi. It seems easier to refine higher level medicines and spirit herb attributes in this life than it was in my past reincarnations!” A smile floated onto his face.","The experiences, memories, and knowledge of his three thousand lifetimes were now in one body. His understanding of certain disciplines was greater than when he first obtained that knowledge. Although a myriad of methods existed in the world, they were all derived from great dao.","The methods used might vary, but the nature remained the same.","From dao came one, and one begat two, two gave birth to three, and from three resulted all living things!","After one understood the basic theory of origin, one could derive thousands of various daos. This was the enlightenment that Lu Yun had grasped while he refined the Dragon Transformation Grass. It was a theory that could also be utilized in the opposite direction. All things could become dao!","That was the most important piece of knowledge gleaned.","He was a part of “all things”. If the Dragon Transformation Grass could transform into all things, then all things could transform into Dragon Transformation Grass. He’d succeeded this time, but he might not the next.","There were too many attributes involved with the grass. If it wasn’t for his harvest of everything within that herb garden, he wouldn’t have so quickly refined the Dragon Transformation Grass. Even a clever housewife could not cook a meal without rice. If he’d lacked those spirit herbs, Lu Yun would’ve failed to distill the medicinal attributes that he needed.","“Oh?” As he regarded the cerulean pill in his hand, the young man jerked with shock. He hastily whipped his head around in the direction of the cave entrance.","A massive head had poked in at some point in time.","It was black all over and nine meters tall, a perfect plug for the entrance. Antlers that looked like withered branches stuck to its head and a pair of crimson eyes stared fixedly at the pill in Lu Yun’s hand.","“So pureblooded jiao do exist... but this one seems to have declined back to the empyrean immortal realm due to certain injuries.” His Eye of Nullification immediately plumbed the depths of the new arrival.","Pureblood Jiao were the same as dragons—dao immortals as soon as they were born. Adult jiao could become immortal overlords, but the one in front of him had declined to empyrean immortal. It was less than even a newborn jiao.","“Roar!” The gray jiao growled when it saw Lu Yun regard it and bobbed its head slightly.","“Eat this pill.” Lu Yun relaxed when he sensed that it wasn’t hostile. It’d come to prevent the Dragon Transformation Grass’ aura from expanding further.","Being an earthly treasure, the grass possessed an extremely strong aura. He’d chosen to refine it within the lake as a safeguard against its aura from spreading. However, it’d diffused regardless and summoned a pureblood gray jiao from the depths. Since it could spread downward, that meant it could very possibly extend upward as well.","......","Countless spirit beasts howled near Jade Ice Lake, having surrounded the body of water. Snake-type spirit beasts were the majority. Dragons were lascivious beasts and nearly all the worlds possessed creatures that carried draconic bloodline. The Dragon Transformation Grass was sacred to the race and also bore an almost fatal attraction to anything with a draconic bloodline.","The spirit beasts sensed the grass’ aura when Lu Yun refined it; there were plenty of their type in Fallen Leaf Mountain. Of course, most of them carried very faint traces of draconic bloodline. Most were heavily intermixed with other species, such as the scaled-dragons or hornless dragons. Their ancestors hadn’t been true dragons, to say nothing of descendants with just a drop of their bloodline.","Long Aotian’s bloodline was true draconic bloodline, something that none of these creatures could measure up to.","Hundreds of creatures with draconic bloodlines were gathered around Jade Ice Lake. The strongest among them was a fifth rank blackwater snake king. Blackwater snakes were the most pureblood of draconic bloodlines in worlds of cultivation, which was why Lu Yun had chosen its inner core to refine the Dragon Transformation Grass with.","Countless heads of black spirit beasts poked out of the lake’s surface and growled warningly, facing the creatures on the shore in a standoff.","Innumerable cultivators also crowded around, having detected the abnormality the moment something cropped up with the lake. Cultivators from the four cities around Fallen Leaf Mountain—Fallen Leaf, Rain Swallow, Ice Moon, and Iron Curtain—were present.","“These spirit beasts all possess draconic bloodlines. Since they’ve gathered here... has the last of the thirty-six earthly treasures, the legendary Dragon Transformation Grass, appeared in the lake?” mused a surprised elder that resembled a ball of flame as he had red eyebrows, a red mustache, and red hair. Bright red long robes rounded out the look.","“Master, do those legendary heavenly and earthly treasures really exist in the world?” An extremely ugly young man stood next to the elder. His lips were disproportionately thick, his nose smashed in, one of his eyes twice the size of a regular eye while the other was only the size of a peanut. His complexion was muddy and skin coarse, giving one an uncertain feeling of whether he was man or ghost. His voice also grated on the ear, like the sound of withered branches rubbing against each other.","However, no one dared look down their nose at him. Although he looked only fifteen years old, he’d already reached initial soul separation!","Soul separation was a divide between cultivators. Those who reached this level could project their own image and owned partially immortal bodies. They were hailed as earthly immortals.","The elder in red robes blazed with an aura that stretched for the skies. He didn’t bother concealing his aura as a high level cultivator and it was plain that they came from highly ranked cultivation empires.","“They must exist if they are recorded in books. There is none other than the legendary Dragon Transformation Grass that can attract all creatures with draconic bloodline in Fallen Leaf Mountain.” The elder swallowed hard. “Jade Ruins Realm is far from an ordinary world of cultivation if they even have this level of treasure!”","“Then what are we waiting for? With master’s cultivation, it’d be an easy task to venture into the lake and take the grass!” The gray-robed young man’s misshapen eyes gleamed with excitement.","“Calm down,” the elder chuckled ruefully. “Although the Dragon Transformation Grass is the last of the thirty-six earthly treasures, its true value isn’t any less than the ten heavenly treasures. The unfortunate thing is that it’s applicable only to dragons or those with draconic bloodlines. That is why it is listed last. Otherwise, it absolutely bears the potential to be listed at the head of the earthly treasures.”","“So master means that the grass is useless for us?” Disappointment flashed across the young man’s face.","“Dragon Transformation Grass is useless for human cultivators, but it can help those with draconic bloodline return to their origins! If we can capture a spirit or monster beast with draconic bloodline and use it to activate their bloodline, that will mean we have a dragon for a pet!” the elder chuckled.","“I see! Then allow me, master. I have my eyes set on the blackwater snake king. Tsk tsk, it’s on par with a soul projection cultivator!” The young man looked eagerly at the blackwater snake king on the banks of Jade Ice Lake.","“Don’t move for now,” his master shook his head. “There is much beneath the surface at play here due to Immortal Burial Valley. There are at least three people in the vicinity whose cultivation I cannot see through!”","“You’re already an awakened powerhouse, master! Is there anyone here who rivals you?” The young man jumped with surprise.","“It’s better to be careful!” The elder shook his head, failing to note the light flashing through the young man’s eyes.","......","Noon the next day, the sun directly overhead.","It’d been a full night and half a day since Lu Yun refined the Dragon Transformation Grass.","“Hahaha, so it is that thing’s presence, there’s no doubt about it!” Raucous laughter exploded from the sky as a black cloud floated over. A black aura immediately enveloped the premises, causing the spirit beasts and black beasts in the waters to snarl with unease.","“Monster spirit!” gasped the cultivators hidden in the forest.","Monster spirits were evolved from spirit beasts. Beasts that couldn’t take human form were called spirit beasts, or at most immortal or divine beasts if they reached immortality. Those that could were called monster beasts or monster spirits. Monster spirits were innately powerful, far stronger than human cultivators of the same level. Some with connate talents could even kill their peers.","“Hiss!” The blackwater snake king reared upward when it saw the black cloud descend. Its neck flattened and its tongue flickered in and out, rasping warning sounds.","The black cloud faded away to reveal a young man dressed in emerald green robes with emerald green eyes. He silently hovered thirty meters above the lake surface.","“It really is that thing! To think that the legendary Dragon Transformation Grass would appear here!” A long forked tongue darted out of his mouth to lick his nose. “And to think that I, Ancestor Bi Chen, would have a chance of transforming into a dragon!”","“Old Monster Bi Chen!” shrieked the red-robed elder when he heard the name. “Isn’t the tyrant of Barren Mountains in closed door cultivation in the mountain range? He broke through to become a monster immortal, what’s he doing here??”"]},{"number":2279,"title":"Chapter 2279: Chapter 2188.2: Dragon Lady?","paragraphs":["Chapter 2188.2: Dragon Lady?","Ancestor Bi Chen was a taboo of the entire Barren Mountains range. A monster spirit of peak awakened cultivation realm, he was well known for being the demise of numerous wandering immortals.","A few awakened cultivators from an eighth rank empire had once ventured into the Barren range and jointly killed a ninth rank monster beast about to take human form, digging out its inner core. When Ancestor Bi Chen found out, he dyed the streets of that kingdom red with blood. A tremendously powerful eighth rank cultivation empire perished overnight.","After that, the three ninth rank empires and law enforcers entered the mountain range to hunt down Bi Chen. They returned in abject defeat—all of the wandering cultivators dead and only a dozen returned out of hundreds of law enforcers.","Bi Chen then struck while the iron was hot, entering Firmament Empire—one of the three ninth rank empires. If it wasn’t for the chief enforcer suddenly appearing and blocking the monster spirit, there would only be two ninth rank empires left in this world today.","The chief enforcer was an empyrean immortal, but it still took three days to fight Ancestor Bi Chen to a standstill. In the end, they reached an agreement that cultivators above the tribulation level would not set foot into the Barren Mountains. Only then did the monster spirit cease his pursuit of revenge.","That was how the mountain range gradually became a forbidden zone in the Jade Ruins Realm.","“I wondered who it was that would know my name. So it’s the Primordial Empire genius Ji Lin.” Ancestor Bi Chen glanced sideways at the red-robed elder hiding in the woods.","“Junior Ji Lin greets Senior Bi Chen!” Ji Lin didn’t dare remain hidden after Bi Chen took notice of him.","“Mm.” Bi Chen inclined his head when he saw the human present itself.","Primordial Empire was one of the three ninth rank cultivation empires. It was first among the Jade Ruins Realms—the other two of Xuanhuang and Firmament paled far in comparison. Ji Lin was one of its geniuses and ranked number ten in the Jade Ruins Ranking of the Celestial Realm Battlefront.","The rankings didn’t encompass only the top ten awakened cultivators—but those of all cultivation realms, including wandering immortals and empyrean immortals. Everyone’s cultivation was suppressed to initial nascent soul in the battlefront, so competition was conducted on the basis of comprehension of dao and utilization of true origin.","Being ranked in the top ten meant that Ji Lin absolutely dominated those of his level. Apart from meeting old monsters like Bi Chen, he was essentially invincible.","“What, do you lot want to stop me?” Bi Chen looked coldly at the black spirit beasts in the waters.","“Hiss hiss hiss!” Although they felt the depths of Bi Chen’s horrifying might, they still raised their heads high and refused to back down. Other than the spirit beasts in the lake, all other spirit beasts cowered on the ground from the might of the monster spirit’s aura. The blackwater snake king was the only exception.","“Yo, isn’t this Ancestor Bi Chen of the Barren Mountains? What are you doing here terrorizing the juniors?” rang a flippant voice before the void twisted, depositing a purple figure over Jade Ice Lake.","“Lang Ye, master of the Demonic Spirit Tarn.” Bi Chen’s pupils constricted when he saw the man in long purple robes.","There were three major forbidden zones in the Jade Ruins Realm—Barren Mountains, Demonic Spirit Tarn, Cloudfog Valley. Apart from Cloudfog Valley, the other two were off limits because of powerful monster spirits in residence. Lang Ye was the lord of Demonic Spirit Tarn.","The chief enforcer, Bi Chen, and Lang Ye were known as the three strongest powerhouses of Jade Ruins Realm. There were some empyrean immortals present as well, but they were not exempt from the heavenly book’s rules like the chief enforcer was, so most remained in seclusion.","Even if they roamed the land, they would not be a match for the three given the influence of the heavenly book. The chief enforcer for the Jade Ruins Realm was the only immortal approved by the heavenly book.","Although Lang Ye and Bi Chen were only awakened realm, they were monster spirits with divine beast bloodlines. The talents and potential of their bloodlines meant that they completely matched human empyrean immortals.","“To think you’d come here as well, you’re not a descendent of the dragons. The Dragon Transformation Grass is useless to you.” Bi Chen looked at the newcomer without a flicker of change in his expression.","“Heh, although the grass is useless to me, there are a few juniors in my Demonic Spirit Tarn with draconic bloodline. The grass will create another powerhouse for my banner.” Lang Ye’s purple hair reached his calves and danced in the wind, the very picture of unbridled freedom.","Although most of the human cultivators here were from Dark Orchid Empire, they were familiar with Lang Ye of the Demonic Spirit Tarn and Bi Chen of the Barren Mountains. Both appearing at the same time shocked people so much that they didn’t dare breathe too loudly. When they heard the two speak of the Dragon Transformation Grass, they finally understood why there were so many spirit beasts gathered here.","The ten heavenly and thirty-six earthly treasures had long become myths in textbooks. Nearly everyone was familiar with their uses, but some of them were unrecognizable in the wild—such as White’s Red Spider Lily.","“So you mean to fight me for it?” BI Chen remained expressionless, aloof consideration in his handsome face.","“Such treasures are normally claimed by those with ability. I will not take it from you if the Dragon Transformation Grass shares a destiny with you.” Lang Ye shrugged innocently.","“Hmph,” Bi Chen snorted and ignored the other. Dismay suddenly marked his features. “Wait, something’s swallowed the Dragon Transformation Grass!”","He dove into the lake as a shadow, swiftly followed by Lang Ye. While the black spirit beasts in the lake postured in an intimidating manner, they couldn’t withstand the two monster spirits. Countless numbers died from the force of their entry.","The blackwater snake king reared in a show of force as well and moved to follow the two monster spirits.","“Hehehe, don’t be in such a hurry to run off, little snakey. You’re mine now!” A voice like a broken gong suddenly rang by the snake king’s ears as its body lifted into the air, grasped by a hand of true origin.","......","Twenty-five meters in the cave beneath the lake’s surface, Long Aotian roared a stunning dragon cry. Pale golden scales grew over his skin and two golden horns stretched out of his hair.","“Hoi hoi, you’re draconic royalty! A nine-clawed golden dragon, no wonder you’re called Long Aotian! You’re a dragon that soars proudly in the sky, alright! Hahahaha!!” Lu Yun threw his head back with laughter as he watched Long Aotian’s change.","Nine-clawed golden dragons were the legendary royal clan of the dragons, their most precious bloodline. Even the dragon patriarch in the world of immortals had been but a five-clawed golden dragon.","“I’m definitely making out like a bandit! Nine-clawed golden dragons can eventually become chaos immortals!” Lu Yun’s eyes creased into crescents from the magnitude of his grin. Chaos dragons were immortal emperor level characters in the world of immortals. He was now raising an immortal emperor!","At the same time, he wasn’t worried that Long Aotian would betray him after taking human form. He’d personally refined the Dragon Transformation Grass and imprinted his brand in it. Long Aotian would never think of betraying him after devouring it.","Dragons were a proud race, so if he didn’t employ certain methods, Long Aotian would almost certainly betray him when he grew into his strength. A nine-clawed golden dragon wouldn’t permit itself to be subordinate to a human.","As for the Dragon Immortal King under his banner in the world of immortals... he’d been Lu Yun’s spirit pet before he took form.","Despite the wondrous development, Lu Yun somehow felt that there was no future in what he was accomplishing. All he was doing was following the natural instincts of life and walking the path of what made sense. The rhythm of heaven and earth meant that all things inexorably proceeded forward. This was just a case of strengthening himself.","Even he didn’t know if he could see this road through to the end.","Piercing dragon croons rang from Long Aotian’s mouth and his clothes split open. No longer in human form, he was a golden dragon now.","However, Lu Yun gaped when he looked at the shifting dragon. He’d plainly seen a curvaceous body of plump peaks and rounded bottom when Long Aotian’s clothes burst apart. The dragon was a woman!","“Long Aotian... is a woman?! Such a domineering name... belongs to a woman??” Lu Yun smacked his forehead. How had he not discovered she was a woman after all this time?! He’d only looked at the woman’s bloodline with the Eye of Nullification, not her body. He’d thought she was a man at that time, so he wasn’t the least bit interested in looking closely at a man’s body. Thank goodness he’d planted a hint of his own brand in the Dragon Transformation Grass or it was only a matter of time before Long Aotian betrayed him.","He didn’t blame her for hiding this from him as it was quite understandable. But her personality would change after she became a dragon, so all bets were off the table then. She also carried quite a few secrets on her. Otherwise, he should’ve been able to see through her even without purposefully scanning her body.","Long Aotian’s transformation into a woman reminded Lu Yun of that person again... Aoxue.","Long Aotian swiftly shrank down after turning into a dragon, first to the size of a regular human being, then continuously smaller until she turned into... an egg!","Indeed, her nine-clawed golden dragon bloodline had been fully activated after swallowing the Dragon Transformation Grass and turned her into a true dragon. Her cultivation level, however, was too low at only mid foundation establishment. Activating her bloodline would also enhance her level of strength, but hers was the royal draconic bloodline. She had to revert to being an egg and hatch anew unless she was an empyrean immortal.","“ROAR!” The gray jiao blocking the entrance snarled with fury and shrank back.","“Jiao! There’s jiao here!” came a stunned voice. “And that’s a dragon egg, a real dragon egg!”"]},{"number":2280,"title":"Chapter 2280: Chapter 2189.1: Old Tree","paragraphs":["Chapter 2189.1: Old Tree","Bi Chen and Lang Ye hacked their way through the waters, alarming the gray jiao guarding the cavern as soon as they entered the lake. The two monster spirits glimpsed a majestic pale-gold dragon egg hovering in the water the moment the jiao withdrew its head.","“Why is it a dragon egg? Isn’t it supposed to be Dragon Transformation Grass?” Bi Chen asked blankly. “Or has a scaled-dragon with draconic bloodline eaten the grass and turned into a dragon egg?”","Bam!","In the split second they spent gaping at the egg, the jiao slammed its tail at the two interlopers. The spirit beasts in the lake were remnants of pureblood jiao, the equivalent of this one’s descendants. It flew into a rage at seeing a great number of them slaughtered by the two impudent trespassers.","“What?!” Lang Ye gasped with dismay, never imagining that something so terrible would be present beneath Jade Ice Lake. He and Bi Chen could match human empyrean immortals because they possessed the bloodlines of divine beasts. The gray jiao in front of them, however, was a bonafide divine beast.","“I’m leaving!” Bi Chen left without hesitation. A pureblood divine beast was frightening enough, to say nothing of one that was an empyrean immortal.","More importantly, the Human Emperor of Great Xia had already shifted the heavenly book and decreased its hold over Jade Ruins Realm. That meant this jiao was invincible throughout the land.","Splash splash splash!","The lake’s waters bubbled and frothed as the spirit beasts with draconic bloodlines flung themselves out of it just as eagerly as they’d dived in moments ago. After scrambling to shore, they split off in every direction.","The surrounding cultivators watched with jaws agape, having no idea what was going on.","BOOM!","A tremendous explosion rang out before they could grasp the situation. The waters suddenly exploded in a geyser of water three hundred meters high.","“AOOOUU!”","Two bedraggled figures fell from the sky while a massive gray entity three hundred meters long rushed out and coiled over the waters.","“That’s a... scaled-dragon!” several cultivators called out.","“A scaled-dragon the level of an empyrean immortal! What’s this terrifying thing doing here?!” The crowd was dumbfounded. Never had they imagined that such a beast would appear within the borders of a mere fourth rank empire!","“AOOOUU!” The jiao snarled at the sky and regarded the collapsed Bi Chen and Lang Ye with crimson eyes. They were just awakened level monster spirits, completely impotent before an empyrean level divine beast.","“Senior, this junior didn’t know that you were in seclusion here! I beg you forgiveness for the offense!” Lang Ye spat out purple blood and regarded the jiao with deep fear.","Humm!","Jade green light rose from the north of Fallen Leaf Mountain and shot toward the horizon. Trepidation appeared in the gray jiao’s eyes when it saw the radiance and it retreated into the lake after a glance at Fallen Leaf City to the south.","The cultivators heaved a collective sigh of relief and dispersed. Lang Ye and Bi Chen looked askance at each other.","“I saw a young human male next to the dragon egg just now!” A sharp look flashed through Bi Chen’s eyes. “If my guess is right, he’ll claim the egg...”","“Surely not!” Lang Ye knew what Bi Chen was planning from his expression alone. “Are you still not giving it up?”","“Give up?” Bi Chen licked his nose with a long and slender tongue. “I bear the bloodline of the hornless dragons. While the hornless dragons aren’t true dragons, they are still an offshoot. That egg holds a fatal attraction for me. If I can refine it, I will fully activate my bloodline and even transform into a real dragon!”","Greed shimmered in his eyes. It was impossible to suppress his inner desires given the pull of his bloodline.","“The young man was standing next to the dragon egg, so he’s certainly going to take it!” Bi Chen murmured to himself as he looked at Jade Ice Lake.","Lang Ye shuddered when he saw how fixated the other was. “I say, Old Bi, let it go. You’ll never succeed with that thing guarding it.”","“The young man won’t stay in the lake forever. I’ve already committed his appearance and presence to memory. He won’t escape my grasp when he emerges from the waters!” Bi Chen leered.","“Really, I recommend you forget it. He might not bring out the dragon egg with him.” Lang Ye had no desire to provoke the gray jiao—it was too horrifying. If it hadn’t been for it standing down due to reservation of something, both of them would already be annihilated despite being the strongest of the realm.","Although Lang Ye also had divine beast bloodline, he was no dragon. He didn’t care very much about the dragon egg. It’d be nice if he could obtain it, no big deal if he couldn’t.","“Hmph!” Bi Chen flicked a sideways glance at Lang Ye and then sensed the petrifying aura again. Blood drained out of his face as he quickly vacated Jade Ice Lake.","Lang Ye swallowed hard as well, knowing that their continued presence here was irritating the monster in the lake. He swiftly took his leave.","......","Lu Yun breathed a long sigh of relief as the Eye of Nullification told him that the two monsters on shore had left.","“Thank goodness for the gray jiao, or all of my hard work would’ve benefited another!” He could tell with a single glance that Ancestor Bi Chen possessed the bloodline of the hornless dragons and could refine the egg with the nine-clawed golden dragon. If Long Aotian hatched, she would firmly suppress Bi Chen through her bloodline alone.","But currently, she was an egg. Who was afraid of a zygote?!","The way things developed slightly surprised Lu Yun as his refinement of the Dragon Transformation Grass was within his calculations, but his advancement in cultivation was unexpected. It’d caused the grass to soar in power and raise the ensuing ruckus.","His Dragon Transformation Grass was far beyond regular specimens of its kind.","“Roar!” The gray jiao returned to the cavern and shrank itself to three meters long. It swam up to Lu Yun and roared softly at the human.","“You mean you want to take this egg to the bottom with you?” Lu Yun understood its words.","“Roar roar!” The jiao nodded. Although it was unable to take human form, it was highly intelligent—being an empyrean immortal. It would’ve known long ago if there was Dragon Transformation Grass in Jade Ice Lake. There wasn’t, so it came from the human male.","While jiao and dragons were close to each other, they were two different species after all. The gray jiao was not able to refine the egg and with its strength, it could take the egg from Lu Yun without the young man being able to do anything.","It sought Lu Yun’s approval and he didn’t sense any malice from it, so he didn’t refuse. Who knew when Long Aotian would hatch? He neither knew how to hatch a dragon egg nor had the time to look after it.","It was perfect that a babysitter had presented itself. He’d left his mark in Long Aotian’s body—she would be deathly loyal to him once she hatched. There was nothing to worry about.","The gray jiao jerked with shock when the human male tossed the dragon egg to it. It hastily reached out with foreclaws and caught the egg. Nodding to Lu Yun, it turned out of the cavern and dove into the depths.","“An empyrean immortal level divine beast! I’ll bet even regular true immortals aren’t a match for it!” Lu Yun appreciatively watched it go before walking out of the cavern and plunging back into the arctic waters.","“There must be something unusual below. Too bad my cultivation is so low that I’d be frozen to death if I head another hundred kilometers down.” Lu Yun knew full well where his limits were. The lake was very uncanny—there were pureblood jiao in residence! He even suspected that where the gray jiao lived wasn’t the bed of this bottomless lake.","He blurred into a shadow and broke through the water’s surface, but was in no hurry to emerge. Although he didn’t know what Lang Ye and Bi Chen had discussed, he’d seen the look in Bi Chen’s eyes. The monster spirit would never give up the dragon egg.","“Wouldn’t it be nice if I had an All-Hearing Ear ability? I’d know everything they were plotting.” [1] Lu Yun looked beyond the waters. He walked out only when he confirmed that there was no sign of Bi Chen and Lang Ye within fifty kilometers.","There wasn’t a cultivator to be found either. All of the spirit beasts had left. The only thing to be found in the vicinity were hundreds of dead black spirit beasts.","Overawed by the gray jiao’s aura, nothing dared approach within a dozen kilometers of the lake. Jade Ice Lake would turn into another forbidden zone sooner or later.","After thinking for a moment, Lu Yun moved the several hundred corpses into a storage ring. These spirit beasts bore the bloodline of the jiao. Perhaps he could use them and the logic he’d utilized for the Dragon Transformation Grass to refine a Jiao Transformation Grass.","Being descendants of the gray jiao, they laid untouched when the cultivators and spirit beasts departed. Thus, all of it benefited Lu Yun in the end.","He flew with Immortals Restriction after collecting everything and rapidly left the range of Fallen Leaf Mountain. The mountain was so eerie that he wasn’t willing to stay another second. He’d also detected the pillar of jade green light that’d made the jiao wary. It came from the zone forbidden to immortals.","“It’s him, the young man wanted by the Black Tortoises!” Some cultivators surrounded him as soon as he left the mountain.","1. Shunfeng'er is a Chinese sea and door god. The name literally translates to \"Wind Accompanying Ears\", a reference to his ability to hear any sound carried upon the wind. ☜"]},{"number":2281,"title":"Chapter 2281: Chapter 2189.2: Old Tree","paragraphs":["Chapter 2189.2: Old Tree","Fallen Leaf City had long disseminated Lu Yun’s physical appearance and aura to the cities and towns close to Fallen Leaf Mountain. Three million paramount rank stones was no small sum. Countless cultivators had assembled into teams to hunt for Lu Yun in the surrounding region.","Although he looked different now, when was physical appearance ever a consideration when it came to bounty? Any art of illusion could change one’s form, not to mention treasures like Transformation Jade and Talismans.","The bounties of the worlds of cultivations were based off jade slips that contained the target’s aura. Cultivators could familiarize themselves through the jade slip and use the aura to find the target.","Physical form could be changed, but one’s core essence and aura could not. Generally held within the body, aura seeped out whenever true origin operated and during the course of battle. It lingered briefly in the outside world.","Auras could be collected through jade slips fashioned from Destined Origin Stone and replicated. Any cultivator that wished to become a citizen of empires fourth rank and above had to register themselves at the various cities, leaving their aura behind on one such jade slip. This would serve as their form of identification in the world.","Although a wanted order did not utilize this kind of jade slip, it functioned essentially the same as one. It might even be more useful than the jade slip since all cultivators needed to do was to infuse the order with their consciousness to gain a sense of the target’s aura. If the target was in the vicinity, the cultivator would know through the aura that they were already familiar with.","This was similar to the arrest warrants in the world of mortals. One could first take a look at a drawing of the suspect to immediately identify the right person when the opportunity arose. Therefore, Lu Yun was corralled the moment he walked out of Fallen Leaf Mountain.","“That’s right, it’s him! That’s the walking three million paramount stones!” Some cultivators greeted him enthusiastically and flung themselves at him.","“What the... they don’t need to do things this way, do they? The Black Tortoise leader can crush me to death with a single hand, what’s with the bounty?” Lu Yun frowned as sword light flashed beneath his feet. He flew to the northeast.","They were still within Fallen Leaf City jurisdiction and he didn’t want to fight anyone here. No place would be safe once those heavyweights in the city realized where he was and gave chase. They were eccentric folks with unpredictable tempers and Lu Yun didn’t want to risk it.","Nearly one thousand cultivators followed him, so he summoned more power from Immortals Forbidden. It blurred into crimson light nine meters long and raced across the sky.","“Tsk tsk tsk! An upper spirit rank weapon in the hands of a mere golden core junior. Is it me who’s too lucky or you being too unlucky?” A cultivator less than thirty years old wearing long green robes suddenly came to a stop in front of Lu Yun. “I don’t care about the spirit stones, but I want that flying sword!”","He sent out a flash of sword radiance aimed at Lu Yun’s forehead.","“Hmph!” Lu Yun snorted. The man was latter nascent soul, hardly worth anything in his eyes. He wouldn’t fear a nascent soul cultivator from Great Xia, to say nothing of the ones from a world of cultivation.","He dodged with a twist of his body and tapped the green radiance.","Bam!","Silver light sparkled at his fingertips and disassembled the mid fine rank flying sword.","“You! Damn you for destroying my True Origin Sword!” The man paled and spat out a mouthful of fresh blood. “Die!”","The man summoned a black flag into his hand and waved it ferociously, dissipating a cloud of black fog that churned toward Lu Yun.","“Poison fog!” While he didn’t know what the black fog was, he could sense the enormous amount of poison inside. Highly cautious, he bade Immortals Forbidden to flare with light and turn into a miniature sun.","With a red sun beneath his feet, Lu Yun seemed as if a god descending from the skies. He barrelled toward the man in long green robes, exorcizing the poison fog without difficulty.","“You can’t do this!” The man was as pale as a sheet. “You can’t kill me! I am the city lord of Boulder Rise, grandson of Prince Sui of Dark Orchid. You—”","He vaporized into the void.","“Grandson of Prince Sui of Dark Orchid? Yeah, I’m your daddy alright.”","Prince Sui of Dark Orchid was a notable powerhouse of the empire. Since Lu Yun had come to this land, he was going to turn the nation upside down. He circled past Fallen Leaf Mountain after killing Prince Sui’s grandson and headed north.","The cultivators following stopped with shock when they saw Lu Yun killed a latter nascent soul heavyweight with one move.","“He... he killed the city lord of Boulder Rise! All of Dark Orchid will want his head now!” murmured a latter golden core.","“Not just Dark Orchid, Prince Sui is said to be the disciple of an immortal—the war god of Dark Orchid! He’ll be out for blood with the death of his grandson and I suspect that all of the neighboring countries will issue wanted orders!”","“THat’s right, Dark Orchid is the only independent nation of this world because of Prince Sui. That young man is dead without a doubt!”","......","Lu Yun didn’t care about a Prince Sui or a Prince Hey. Whenever one wanted to kill another for their treasure, one had to be prepared to be killed in return.","“So I have Starnet Stone now, but I need a few more items before I can refine Proxima Metal.” Lu Yun slowed down when he saw his pursuers drop off and debated how to locate the last of his ingredients. “They’re not rare or precious things, I should be able to find them in Dark Orchid.”","He suddenly paused. It was mid summer and the sun was beginning to set in the west. It was the hottest moment of the day, but he didn’t feel any hot air. The temperature around him was on par with Jade Ice Lake.","Whoosh!","A thick vine burrowed out from the ground and wrapped around one of his calves.","“This thing again!” Lu Yun stared, urging another flare of light out from Immortals Forbidden. It decimated the vine before the latter had a chance to tighten.","“I know I circled past Fallen Leaf Mountain, so what’s this vine doing here?” Lu Yun stood in the air with his sword emanating scintillating radiance. More views reached out of the void and surrounded him.","He refrained from making a move. There were too many vines and they were unusually durable. The one he’d destroyed seemed to have been bait. They didn’t do anything after they encircled him, just wove a spherical cage that kept him inside.","“Teleportation! These vines can teleport!” His Eye of Nullification immediately sensed that the vines shifted location after they confined him. “Has the owner of the herb garden discovered the theft and is bringing me back for an explanation?”","Various possibilities ran through his mind.","The scene brightened in front of him and his jaw dropped when he could see clearly. There was a wall in front of him, a brown wall so tall that its peak could not be seen. Various ancient patterns interlaced with each other on the wall and a dense sense of bleakness exuded from it.","“Little guy, you took my things without even asking beforehand. You’re a thief!” A wizened voice rang by Lu Yun’s ear.","His Eye of Nullification scanned the premises and found no one. There weren't even spirit beasts within fifty kilometers, to say nothing of people. There was only the tree.","Lu Yun lifted his head and gaped when he thought of something.","“This... this is a tree??” The wall in front of him was the trunk of an enormous tree that towered to the heavens!","“I am but a tree. Am I supposed to have arms and legs like you?”","“The junior greets the senior!” Lu Yun took a few steps back and bowed respectfully. A tree like this was at least one million years old! “This junior didn’t know that the herbs belonged to the senior. I will return them promptly.”","Lu Yun immediately took out several dozen storage rings.","“You can have the spirit herbs since you’ve harvested them,” the old tree responded. “But I desire something else from you.”","“Something else?” Lu Yun blinked.","“An unknown sacred wood treasure!” the old tree clarified eagerly. “There is an unknown wood attribute treasure on you as you bear wood energy even purer than mine. If I obtain it, I will be able to take human form!”","“Eh?” Lu Yun started, knowing that the old tree spoke of the leaf from the Builder Tree. It’d become one with him, however, and could not be separated. He would have to die before it could be bought out."]},{"number":2282,"title":"Chapter 2282: Chapter 2190.1: Hongmeng Spirit Fruit","paragraphs":["Chapter 2190.1: Hongmeng Spirit Fruit","As startled as Lu Yun was, he didn’t show it. Not a flicker of change marred his expression.","“Surely you jest, senior. Your cultivation soars to the heavens. Would this junior be able to pull the wool over your eyes if such a sacred item resides on me?” Lu Yun smiled faintly.","“Eyes? I have no eyes, but my instincts are never wrong.” The old tree’s voice was just as gentle, but now tinged with imperious certainty.","Whoosh whoosh whoosh!","Vines appeared in the air again and surged toward Lu Yun before he could respond. As the Eye of Nullification was active, he had a full grasp of the vines’ trajectories. Immortals Forbidden exploded with light almost as soon as they appeared.","The Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons!","Lu Yun immediately deployed his strongest technique. Sword qi of the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons rose from his dantian and melded with his flying sword. He was surrounded by countless rays of crimson sword qi and turned into a crimson dragon more than thirty meters long.","His cerulean sword dragon was more than ten times stronger than what Yong Heyu had brought to bear in Dark City. The dragon figure twisted eighteen times in a strange configuration, tearing the approaching vines to pieces.","The true meaning of the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons was not to utilize all eighteen moves at the same time. That would just infinitely weaken the technique. Rather, each of the eighteen turns meant a dao trajectory and ultimate truth of heaven and earth. That was the true meaning of the method.","There was only one move in the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons!","After he churned through the vines, Lu Yun shot up into the sky still in the form of a dragon. The core essence of this formation of illusion was still the basic cycle of the five elements. Specifically, the old tree’s power of wood. The tree was so massive and all powerful that if it wasn’t for the formation, it would be visible thousands of kilometers away.","He would have to kill the old tree if he wished to break the formation, but such a tree, even if it was completely ordinary, wasn’t anything that Lu Yun could destroy. Its torrential wood energy harbored infinite vitality, making it nearly impossible to kill.","In Lu Yun’s eyes, the tree was at least a peerless immortal, maybe even dao immortal. All he could do was run.","“There will be no place for me in this world if I let you get away from me!” The old tree finally flew into a rage and brought down overpowering aura on Lu Yun amid a loud series of rustles.","Pfft!","Lu Yun spat out fresh blood—this was the aura of a dao immortal! He was just mid golden core! His cerulean sword dragon form immediately dissipated upon being struck.","He was smashed into the dirt, thin cracks spider webbing his bones. If it wasn’t for his golden core being one of great dao and true origin being Hongmeng qi, he would already be pulverized.","All the same, it was a very arduous experience. He was crushed into the mud and severe agony wracking his mind. If not for his stalwart mindset, he would’ve already fainted from the pain.","“Damn it, it’s the Hongmeng Tree, number six of the ten heavenly treasures. It’s even sentient! If I make it out alive, I’m going to refine a Poisonheart Grass and send you to the afterlife with it!” As his thoughts traveled wildly, a dot of pale-green flashed through the gray Hongmeng qi in his body. The gray energy turned jade green and his terrifying injuries instantly recovered.","“It really is a sacred item of wood! Hahahah!” The Hongmeng Tree shook with laughter when it sensed the development in Lu Yun’s body.","......","Jade Ice Lake.","A black shadow floated up from the foggy depths as a pair of crimson eyes looked toward Fallen Leaf Mountain.","......","Fallen Leaf City, Azure Dragons headquarters.","Disciples cowered and shuddered with dread.","“Hahaha, I thought only the three girls were coming today, to think you’d come too, Leng Shan!” A young man in long white robes and a wine gourd made of white jade at his waist roared with laughter.","“Big brother Huiying, is your wine tasty?” came a sweet voice by the young man’s side. A young girl of sixteen years and dressed in downy-yellow robes looked hopefully at Huiying. Her large limpid eyes, nested amid exquisitely carved features, batted their eyelashes at him.","Huiying’s face fell and he wrapped protective hands around the gourd. “No, no, not at all. Big brother Huiying’s wine is the worst. Your big brothers Zi Chen and Wuheng have the best wine!”","It was Zi Chen and Wuheng’s turn to smile ruefully.","“There’s a good girl, Little Xun Luo. How about we compromise? You can have some, but don’t drink it all!” The aloof Wuheng couldn’t help but wave a white flag when faced with the girl. Xun Luo’s eyes curved into crescents from the force of her smile when she heard the response.","“Oh?” A young girl dressed in a green silk dress suddenly looked to the north, her expression shifting drastically.","“Never mind that, young sis Ying Xue. That old tree in Fallen Leaf Mountain throws a tantrum every now and then. Huiying just taught it a lesson a few days ago,” Zi Chen chuckled.","“The old tree? The Hongmeng tree?” Yu Luo creased her brow. Her long hair reached her waist and a red silk dress turned her into a fairy of fire. Wuheng looked dumbly at her and subconsciously swallowed hard.","“Yep, it’s that old tree alright. If it’s annoying you, Yu Luo, I’ll teach it a lesson for you!” Wuheng quickly said when he caught Yu Luo’s expression.","“Forget it, it’s not often that the seven of us get together. There’s no need to pay it any attention.” Ying Xue smiled and prevented Wuheng from rushing off.","......","The forbidden zone of Fallen Leaf Mountain.","Vine upon vine stretched out of the void. Each was several dozen meters thick and so long that their end could not be glimpsed. Lu Yun could offer no resistance and was rolled up into the sky.","The Hongmeng Tree was at least a peerless immortal—there was nothing that a mere golden core cultivator could do to it.","“So the sacred wood treasure has become one with your body! That’s even better, I only need to extract your blood to obtain it!” the Hongmeng Tree chortled. If it wasn’t for the fact that the treasure would wither with the death of the human, it would’ve already struck down Lu Yun.","Pfft!","A long wooden needle stabbed into Lu Yun’s chest and began guzzling his blood.","“Hahaha, this is indeed a pure sacred wood treasure! Hahahahaha!! Huiying won’t be able to do anything to me once I swallow it!” the Hongmeng Tree roared with laughter.","The tree detected Lu Yun’s aura the moment the young man set foot into Fallen Leaf Mountain. However, Lu Yun had been with Huiying then, so the tree hadn’t dared try anything. It’d kept a firm grip on its impulses, waiting for Lu Yun to strike out on his own before making a move.","“Hmph!” Lu Yun set his jaw and looked coldly at the Hongmeng Tree, inwardly quite calm. He was focused on communicating with the sword pagoda in his dantian. He wanted to use the sword qi within it to kill the tree.","However, it’d gone quiet. The ray of sword qi hovered silently at its core, completely inert.","“Oh?” Something else registered—while the Hongmeng Tree sucked away his blood, something else in his body wrested back a sliver of wood power.","“The Builder Tree is the first spirit root of the world and the king of trees. A mere Hongmeng Tree wants to take it? It won’t stand for that!” Lu Yun’s eyes brightened as a thought compared to him. His fingers flew through hand seals and operated the Connate Great Dao of the Five Elements. Tremendous power of connate wood gathered from the eastern direction, settling into his body. When the Builder Tree’s power of wood was fortified by connate wood, it exploded outward.","Wham!","Lu Yun turned jade green as his blood returned through the wooden needle. Not only that, but the power of wood within the Hongmeng Tree also came with it!","“What, what is this?!” the Hongmeng Tree shrieked with dismay. The tiny young human was quickly absorbing all of its strength! It couldn’t sever the connection even though it wanted to!","The young man was as if a bottomless hole, endlessly absorbing the power of wood from the Hongmeng Tree. The tree would be gravely injured if the situation continued and fall into a deep sleep.","“The Tree King... Tree of the World!” The Hongmeng Tree finally understood what the sacred wood treasure was, but all was too late."]},{"number":2283,"title":"Chapter 2283: Chapter 2190.2: Hongmeng Spirit Fruit","paragraphs":["Chapter 2190.2: Hongmeng Spirit Fruit","If Lu Yun didn’t have the Connate Great Dao of the Five Elements and was unable to summon connate wood energy, then the leaf of the Builder Tree would only hold overwhelming attraction for the Hongmeng Tree and no danger.","It was similar to Long Aotian in egg form and Ancestor Bi Chen.","But since the Builder Tree leaf had been roused with the power of wood from the Hongmeng Tree, Lu Yun took advantage of that to absorb connate wood energy and fully activate the leaf.","The Builder Tree, also known as the Tree of the World, was the king of trees and all of their ultimate banes. If it was to grow, it required swift infusion of vast sums of wood energy.","While Lu Yun could summon connate wood energy, he summoned too little each time. He could rouse the Builder Tree, but nothing else. This time, the Hongmeng Tree would supply the rest of the energy.","The leaf materialized in Lu Yun’s dantian and coalesced into a jade-green seed. It burst with scintillating light and furiously absorbed energy from the Hongmeng Tree like it was a vampire. The young man was undoubtedly receiving great benefits at the same time.","Boom!","A massive explosion went off in his mind as he spontaneously broke through to latter golden core and continued growing.","The Hongmeng Tree was at least a peerless immortal, possibly even dao immortal. Its wood energy was the equivalent of immortal force. When this level of energy streamed into Lu Yun, it was difficult for him not to ascend in cultivation.","“Mercy, Your Majesty, mercy!” The Hongmeng Tree’s voice grew smaller until it finally fell silent.","Crack!","A sharp snap sounded from the jade-green seed as a tender shoot unfurled from it.","Boom!","Lu Yun felt his body tremble when the shoot appeared and a marvelous enlightenment floated through his being.","“The strength of wood... is this the strength of wood? Its power, its rules, its world...” He gently probed the eastern void and grasped a ball of jade-green energy. It condensed into a physical object—connate yi wood!","He dismissed it as motes of light with a snap of his fingers.","“What a pity that I need to consume Hongmeng qi if I want to keep connate yi wood around.” Though he spoke with regret, happiness tinged his voice. He’d comprehended the great dao of wood the moment the Builder Tree germinated. With the aid of Hongmeng qi, he managed to retain connate yi wood in his body.","His knowledge of the wood element had reached incredible heights. The sprouted seed hovered silently in his dantian and took root in the void, standing shoulder-to-shoulder with the sword pagoda and golden core of great dao.","Humm!","He shook as his golden core spontaneously split open, leaving behind a baby the size of a fist! The golden baby sat cross-legged over the gray dao character and looked the exact same as Lu Yun. It was his nascent soul.","Lu Yun blinked with astonishment—he’d really benefited from disaster! Not only had he comprehended a hint of wood dao, but he’d also formed his nascent soul and broken through to the next level.","He’d stepped out of mid golden core straight into initial nascent soul. The sliver of his new understanding was also one of the great daos beneath heavenly dao.","But a nascent soul...","Lu Yun paused briefly, somehow certain that in his sealed memories, he’d never formed a nascent soul in the immortal dao he knew.","Boom!","Another explosion sounded in his ears as he stayed immersed in his new cultivation. Golden light flashed out of his nascent soul and entered his mind.","Heavenly dao combat art—Size Manipulation!","It was a combat art that allowed him to change his size as he wished. He could tower at thousands of meters and hold up the skies or be the smallest particle of dust that the eye could not discern. While some immortals could change their size, most of that was accomplished through manipulating their projected image or illusion. No one could truly change their physical body.","Size Manipulation, however, was perfect for concealment. He could become a particle of dust that evaded even the consciousness. This would be how he shook off his pursuers!","“Size Manipulation... I think I knew this combat art before!” Lu Yun’s lips curved upward.","He breathed with ease upon seeing the quiet Hongmeng Tree, then sat down with his eyes closed to carefully assess his new cultivation level. The goodwill stored in the Seal of the Multitude had been fully exhausted and he’d just reached initial nascent soul. It wasn’t time to forcefully raise his cultivation through goodwill.","“Hmm?” Lu Yun blinked, finding a change in his spirit root. Previously of pure fire, it was now a dual attribute of wood and fire. “Um...”","His spirit root had been an empyrean spirit root, but it’d still been of fire. It’d somehow shifted io dual elements now!","The Nine Chapters of Dao didn’t care what attributes Lu Yun’s spirit root was. It was a method of no affinity and worked with everything. Thus, his cultivation wasn’t affected by the change. All the same, it was quite a surprise.","“Should I collect sacred treasures of all five elements and create a perfectly elementally balanced spirit root?” Lu Yun smacked his lips and cackled, “The Hongmeng Tree is ranked sixth among the ten heavenly treasures and it’s right in front of me!”","The Hongmeng Tree, or more accurately speaking, its Hongmeng Spirit Fruit, were one of the ten heavenly treasures. He’d never seen it during his time as the High Lord of the Northern Sky, so to think he’d encounter one almost ten million years old in a world of cultivation!","He pushed off his feet and easily scaled the tree, darting up its enormous tree trunk. He saw jade-green branches and leaves roughly fifteen minutes later.","“There are indeed Hongmeng Spirit Fruit!” Lu Yun beamed, seeing golden fruit the size of a fist among the leaves.","Hongmeng Spirit Fruit was listed as number six as they were filled with profound mysteries and could be refined into the Overlord Divine Pill. This pill helped dao immortals comprehend the next level and break through to immortal overlords.","“Thank goodness it’s asleep now. When it was conscious, it wouldn’t divert much of its essence to the fruit. Now, however, most of its true origin naturally goes to the budded fruit.” Lu Yun grinned happily and moved swiftly among the branches, picking the fruit.","After thirteen days and the Eye of Nullification confirming that there was no more fruit did he stop. He was able to pinpoint the fruit so accurately because he’d coalesced his nascent soul and comprehended a hint of wood dao. Otherwise, he wouldn’t have plucked all of the fruit even if he’d been given a year for the task. The tree was ten kilometers wide and most of its branches hidden in unknown voids. The physical eye could not see them and the mind could not penetrate them.","Due to the Builder Tree germinating and comprehending a hint of wood dao, Lu Yun could sense the entire tree and use connate wood origin to direct all of the Hongmeng Spirit Fruit to him.","“Three hundred and sixty-five...” He shook his head. There were only three hundred and sixty-five fruit on such a massive Hongmeng Tree!","“Forget it, I didn’t see a single one during my reincarnation in the world of immortals, so I should be satisfied with suddenly owning three hundred and sixty-five!","“They contain the meaning of an immortal overlord and can help dao immortals break through. They are also useful for immortal overlords. If a cultivator’s body possesses the meaning of an immortal overlord...","“I’m going to study these fruit first and see if I can use other spirit herbs to replicate its properties.” Lu Yun smiled with anticipation.","He returned to the bottom of the tree and looked around, determining that there was nothing else of value. He knocked on the tree’s ponderous trunk. “I say, old tree, I’ll return hatred with kindness this time and show you mercy. Remember this if you have a chance to wake up.”","The tree had lost half of its core essence and sunk into a deep sleep. Who knew when it’d recover? Lu Yun would have already grown into his strength then and wouldn’t need to fear it.","The truth of the matter was, he wasn’t able to eliminate this tree at the roots even if he wanted to. Thus, Lu Yun raised sword light and left the area.","Although the formation of illusion was still present, it couldn’t stop Lu Yun and his Eye of Nullification. He quickly left the zone off limits to immortals.","A purple and black figure flashed by after he departed. Wuheng and Zi Chen appeared in front of the tree.","“How did the kid send the old guy into deep slumber?” Zi Chen gaped at the tree.","“No idea,” Wuheng shook his head with a rueful chuckle. “But he sure as heck doesn’t need any tempering from me. It’s not tempering for him at all.”","“Then what is it?” Zi Chen blinked.","“Playing house.”"]},{"number":2284,"title":"Chapter 2284: Chapter 2191.1: A Large Store Bullies Its Customers","paragraphs":["Chapter 2191.1: A Large Store Bullies Its Customers","Dark Orchid Empire encompassed three million kilometers of territory—an expanse that rivaled Darklake Empire. However, there were spirit veins that crisscrossed its domain, bestowing it with a much higher concentration of ambient qi than Darklake. Even the other fourth rank empires were less than Dark Orchid.","Ashflame City was one of the empire’s largest cities in the south. Also called the southern capital, it was the heart of the nation’s one million kilometers of territory to the south.","The city ran five thousand kilometers from end to end and there was a lower rank spirit vein beneath it. The concentration of qi in Ashflame’s environment was far greater than that of Darklake’s capital.","Compared to Ashflame, Dark City was a country village.","But to Lu Yun, one who’d journeyed through three thousand worlds, Ashflame wasn’t particularly impressive. He walked up to its largest restaurant—Immortal Gazer—and chose a seat by the window. He people-watched while sipping wine; eighteen exquisite dishes were arrayed in front of him. Made from spirit herbs and spirit beasts, not only were they delicious, but there was an abundance of qi within them.","Qi in most spirit herbs and spirit beasts was too violent and hard to be directly consumed, but these had been specially processed and cooked via unique means. Customers could perfectly refine and absorb the energy within.","But food was food, always less than pills made for specific uses. So while the chefs that could create these dishes enjoyed notable status in the world of cultivation, they were inferior to pill masters. All the same, true spirit chefs were far and few in between. In Darklake, only the palace had a lower ranked spirit chief on its roster.","The dishes in front of Lu Yun had been exquisitely prepared by one such chef. Ordinary nascent soul cultivators would gain the equivalent of three days worth of seclusion if they ate everything. It’d cost three hundred paramount rank stones and another two hundred for the private room.","Run-of-the-mill nascent soul cultivators would never be able to spend so much on a meal.","Lu Yun had killed the city lord of Boulder Rise prior to visiting Ashflame and taken his storage ring. There were more than one hundred thousand paramount rank stones inside, so he didn’t lack for spirit stones at the moment.","He ate leisurely as he scanned the streets with the Eye of Nullification, taking in everything within a fifty kilometer radius.","Immortal Gazer sat on the most prosperous street of Ashflame City. There were numerous large trading companies and stores nearby, so he should be able to find what he wished from this vantage point. Having located most of what he needed to refine Proxima Metal, Lu Yun was missing the final material of Frostmoon Ice. He’d come up empty-handed despite visiting several cities.","Frostmoon Ice was only a third rank item and a common sight in a world of cultivation. However, Dark Orchid was situated in the south of the realm where the fire element was most active. Being a water attributed item, Frostmoon Ice was uncommon here.","But since Dark Orchid was the strongest and most prosperous out of fourth rank empires, he should be able to find it if he searched carefully for it.","“I don’t know if you’ve heard, Ole Zhang, but something big happened at the imperial capital the other day!” Strains of conversation flitted into Lu Yun’s ears as he looked around. The private booths were protected by formations and offered privacy for the occupants, but enabled the customers inside to observe everything outside.","“Something big? What is it?” responded another cultivator.","“Someone razed our greatest sect, the Nineheavens Pagoda, to the ground! Apparently a combination level cultivator did it!”","“What?? A combination senior did it? There’s no one like that in Dark Orchid! Did the Nineheavens Pagoda offend a sixth rank empire?”","“No idea, but the combination senior didn’t get off lightly for it either. Some visiting powerhouses injured him before he escaped,” the first speaker sighed.","If this had happened a few years ago, the entire empire would’ve been turned upside down to hunt for the upstart. But after the appearance of Immortal Burial Valley, events like these were commonplace given that the empire’s stronger cultivators had all gone to it.","Lu Yun crinkled his brows when he heard this.","“Someone kicked over the Nineheavens Pagoda?” he was quite surprised. “Looks like they offended a cultivator from a higher ranked empire. That saves me some trouble.”","His smile deepened. He’d come to Dark Orchid to take care of the sect. The heavenly book would be rendered ineffective after a month and those from the Origin Sect would saunter into Jade Ruins Realms. Lu Yun planned to uproot their pawn first and eliminate a threat for the family.","Someone had beat him to the punch!","Thanks!","Hummm.","The formation of his room trembled and gave way to a small opening. A merry elder dressed in golden robes walked in.","“Is the gentleman satisfied with our humble establishment?” asked the elder as he looked at the barely touched dishes.","Lu Yun knew what was about to happen after glancing at the old man’s expression.","“It’s nothing special,” he grunted.","The elder paused, then deepened his smile. “You must be joking, sir. These dishes are from the hands of our renowned Spirit Chef Chen...”","“If I say they’re nothing special, then they’re nothing special.” Lu Yun leaned back on the soft chair. “What, you have something to say about that?”","“Since the gentleman is dissatisfied with our fare, please leave!” The elder’s expression abruptly cooled.","“Leave?” Lu Yun looked sideways at him. “Have I not paid you spirit stones?”","“This humble establishment cannot bear the weight of the gentleman’s stones. We will return them in full!” the elder responded casually.","Lu Yun knew what was going on here. They wanted to throw him out! It looked like Immortal Gazer was in the habit of bullying its customers.","Ordinary restaurants, even purely mundane ones, would ask before entering a customer’s private booth. But this elder hadn’t bothered with so much as a greeting before opening the formation. He plainly didn’t think much of Lu Yun.","It was noon and thus peak business hours. Immortal Gazer’s rooms were likely full, but a great personage had likely come. Thus, the restaurant sent a manager to have Lu Yun vacate the private room.","Therefore, the young man couldn’t be bothered with showing him a friendly face.","“Very well, you may return my spirit stones, but you must return them one hundredfold. I paid five hundred paramount rank stones, so you can return fifty thousand.” Lu Yun gently waved the wine cup in front of him.","“Fifty thousand? Are you joking??” The elder frowned ferociously.","“Get out.” Lu Yun tossed the contents of his cup at the elder’s face.","“You! You court death!” he flew into a rage.","“What’s going on, Manager Lang?” came a young voice behind the elder. A young man dressed in long snowy robes walked in with an entourage.","“Sir Sui!” The elder immediately put on a waning smile when he saw the young man. “Sir Sui, this kid refuses to vacate the room and is putting on a tantrum for it. But don’t worry, this humble one will take care of everything as soon as possible!”","“Oh?” Sir Sui glanced at Lu Yun.","The elder quickly took note of the young man’s expression and hastily called, “Men! Get in here and throw this impudent brat out!”","A dozen golden core men dressed in black stomped into the room.","“A large store bullying its customers...” Lu Yun looked at the elder and ignored Sir Sui.","“A large store bullying its customers? You’re not worthy of being bullied!” Their leader was a latter golden core and would be a pillar of strength in Darklake. But in a fourth rank empire, he was just a henchman for a restaurant.","Bam!","Lu Yun curled his lip and kicked the man’s stomach. He flew backward with an agonized cry. The table in the room was upended and the exquisite dishes smashed to the floor.","The elder’s eyes widened to see the man sent flying with one kick.","“How dare you resort to violence in Immortal Gazer!” The elder was also initial nascent soul. He flung himself forward and manifested a large hand of true origin.","Lu Yun had concealed his cultivation on this trip to Ashflame because he didn’t want to raise undue attention. But sometimes, the less one wanted something, the more it came for him. This is seriously...","In this lifetime, he was a domineering young master in the depths of his bones. Given that he was initial nascent soul, he ignored the large hand.","Bam!","The elder in golden robes bounced off like a rubber ball, shocking the rest of the men in black uniforms.","Clap clap clap!","Applause sounded at this time.","“This little brother is quite daring! You must be a genius from a third rank empire?” Sir Sui applauded with a shake of his head, but contempt tinged his words.","“Oh?” Lu Yun raised an eyebrow at the young man."]},{"number":2285,"title":"Chapter 2285: Chapter 2191.2: A Large Store Bullies Its Customers","paragraphs":["Chapter 2191.2: A Large Store Bullies Its Customers","Sir Sui smirked coldly. “The Immortal Gazer establishment can be found through the world of cultivation from ninth rank empires down to fourth rank. There’s a branch in every empire...","“Immortal Gazer itself is a premier faction in the world of cultivation. Apart from some new money upstarts of third rank empires, who would dare start a fight in one of their establishments? Even I don’t have such gall.”","It was indeed Lu Yun’s first time hearing this name. There was no such establishment in Darklake Empire. As for his three thousand lifetimes... forget it. Who knew what dilapidated corner the Immortal Gazer had been scrabbling in when he reincarnated?","The disturbance alarmed nearby customers. Many minds peered through the hole in the formation and watched Lu Yun with schadenfreude.","Lu Yun looked at Sir Sui. The latter’s age matched his appearance—less than thirty years old. But he was already mid nascent soul. If his strength didn’t come from a plethora of pills and medicines, then he was a genius.","“Who’s causing trouble in the establishment?” Grand Steward Tie Shanhe walked over with a stiff expression. It shifted as soon as he saw Sir Sui. “So it’s the little prince. Tie Shanhe has shown a lack of courtesy in not welcoming you earlier, please forgive me.”","Tie Shanhe was initial soul projection, but he still raised cupped fists to Sir Sui.","“Little prince?” Lu Yun’s eyebrows rose when he heard the term of address. He was reminded of the city lord of Boulder Rise that he’d killed before—the one who called himself the grandson of Prince Sui of Dark Orchid. Did this little prince have something to do with that one?","“Oh?” Lu Yun brightened as the Eye of Nullification showed him a piece of Frostmoon Ice in Tie Shanhe’s storage ring.","“Greetings to Grand Steward Tie!” Sir Sui quickly responded in kind.","Lu Yun remained expressionless as he wanted to see how this grand steward handled the situation. The elder in golden robes ran back, clutching his stomach. Lu Yun’s kick had caused significant damage, and that was with the young man showing mercy. Otherwise, the elder would be dead from one kick.","The elder added fuel to the flames when he recounted earlier happenings and glared coldly at Lu Yun.","“So it is this gentleman who is not satisfied with our cuisine, demanded reparations, and struck our people?” Tie Shanhe regarded Lu Yun frostily.","“Heh heh heh heh...” Lu Yun burst into laughter. “Is Grand Steward He not going to ask him why he entered my room without my say-so?”","“No matter what you say, you will die for hurting someone of the establishment!”","Tyranny! Utter tyranny!","Tie Shanhe took a step forward and pressed his palm down on Lu Yun’s forehead. A powerful force of constraint blossomed at the same time and enveloped the young man’s body.","The grand steward meant to kill Lu Yun with one palm strike!","Lu Yun sneered and shook himself all over, raising his head proudly.","Bam!","Tie Shanhe smacked Lu Yun’s forehead without holding anything back. But under Sir Sui’s startled gaze, the grand steward’s hand bounced off and the man fell backward as well.","“You, you!!” Tie Shanhe stared incredulously at Lu Yun. How had a seventeen year old young man repelled his strike?","The manager in golden robes rubbed his eyes fiercely, unwilling to believe the sight playing out in front of him. Tie Shanhe was a soul projection powerhouse, one of the most preeminent existences in Dark Orchid! How was he unable to jerk a young man around?","“Heh heh heh heh heh, so a mere Immortal Gazer dares strut around in front of this young master? If I say your food is subpar, then your food is subpar! Are you supposed to be an establishment of note? I will dismantle your building today and see what you can do about it!” Lu Yun imitated Tie Shanhe and stepped forward, raising his hand to smack it on the grand steward’s forehead.","Hummm!","Pale green light flickered into existence the second before Lu Yun’s hand connected. It was a lower spirit rank defensive treasure!","Bam!","Lu Yun’s hand continued unabated, smashing into the curtain of light like it was a sledgehammer.","Boom!","A muffled explosion rang out of the room as Tie Shanhe’s legs sank into the floorboards. Tiny cracks webbed through the pale green curtain over his head. If it wasn’t for a powerful defensive formation nearby, he would already be in the floor below.","“You!” Tie Shanhe spat out blood as he was injured alongside the damage to his treasure.","“A lower spirit rank treasure for defense? No worries, I’ll keep that in mind and make sure to kill you next time.” Lu Yun didn’t intend to let the matter go. It’d be one thing if Tie Shanhe hadn’t irritated him, but now that he had, Lu Yun didn’t intend to show mercy.","Tie Shanhe had plainly wanted his life just now, so the young man would answer in kind. Not to mention, the grand steward owned the Frostmoon Ice that he so urgently desired.","Crimson radiance flashed from his hand as Immortals Forbidden bloomed with a meter of sword light. It struck straight for Tie Shanhe’s head.","“Stop!” Sir Sui jumped with shock. How dares someone attack the Immortal Gazer grand steward in their own building? This faction was so terrifying that even his grandfather, Prince Sui, was very wary of them. If it was known that Tie Shanhe had been slain right in front of him, then he might as well evacuate from the empire right now.","Schick!","Fiery sword light appeared in Sui Ge’s hand as he blocked Lu Yun’s sword.","“Oof, he’s so strong!” Sui Ge paled and stumbled a few steps back. His move saved Tie Shanhe, but his expression shifted when he looked at his flying sword. It was an upper spirit rank weapon that his grandfather had personally requested for him. It commanded a lofty status even among upper spirit rank weapons.","But now, there was a nick the size of a grain of rice on it!","“You have an upper spirit rank weapon too!” Sui Ge looked greedily at the crimson flying sword in Lu Yun’s hand. Upper spirit rank weapons were very rare in Dark Orchid, each of them the pride of the nation. If he wasn’t Prince Sui’s most important grandson and tapped to be his successor, he wouldn’t have one either.","But the young man before him also held one and it was plainly of higher quality! How could a self-styled genius like Sui Ge resist?","“You want to bar my way?” Lu Yun looked coldly at Sui Ge, Immortals Forbidden balefully belching with light.","“Defeating a soul projection as a nascent soul, you definitely have a background of your own.” Sui Ge stared fixedly at the sword in Lu Yun’s hand. “As the grandson of Prince Sui of the Dark Orchid Empire, I will not allow you to run amuck through Immortal Gazer. Arrest him!”","He stood back as his four guards charged forward. They threw out four treasures of different colors that assembled into a strange configuration in the air.","They were latter nascent soul and their treasures paramount fine rank, but they came together with the aura that only soul separation cultivators could command. It was the heaven and earth image of a soul separation powerhouse!","The image of a pale green seal formed in the air and loomed over Lu Yun with fearsome aura.","“This is a joint combat art... Prince Sui does have a few tricks up his sleeves, eh.” Lu Yun looked sharply at the attack and slid to the side, evading the attack.","Tie Shanhe had recovered his wits and quickly formed some hand seals, directing the formations in the building to suppress Lu Yun. Matters would not end like this today.","Lu Yun felt something tighten around his body before the formations had him in their grasp. The image of a seal over this head also careened into him. Sui Ge and Tie Shanhe acted at the same time, sending out their flying swords like two murderous scaled-dragons.","BOOM!","Immortal Gazer shook from an enormous explosion. Most of the customers realized something was amiss and left, but some of the guests in the private rooms stayed for the show.","“Where is he?” Sui Ge looked around with an unpleasant expression. The private room they stood in was completely destroyed from the blow and there was a massive hole in the ground, but no sign of Lu Yun.","“Right here.”","Pfft pfft pfft pfft!","Red sword light flashed through the air at the same time and decapitated Sui Ge’s four guards before they had the chance to react. Even their nascent souls were churned to pieces by his sword light. Their treasures landed in Lu Yun’s grasp and he quickly grasped the situation after scanning them.","“I see, so they’re a set of four and come from Immortal Burial Valley...” The young man was disappointed. Any nascent soul cultivator that could bring the strength of soul separation to bear was worthy of his attention, but this was the reason why?","The treasures?","He could refine any number of sets if he had sufficient time. And here he’d thought it was some sophisticated joint combat art!"]},{"number":2286,"title":"Chapter 2286: Chapter 2192.1: Confiscating the Spirit Vein","paragraphs":["Chapter 2192.1: Confiscating the Spirit Vein","Immortal Burial Valley always produced exquisite treasures during an eruption. Lu Yun threw the four items into his storage ring for later study.","Sui Ge and Tian Shanhe gaped at Lu Yun when they recovered from their shock.","“How... how did you evade that?!” Tie Shanhe gasped. Although he didn’t know what kind of method Sui Ge’s four guards had attacked with, he’d suppressed the young man with the full strength of Immortal Gazer’s formations. Lu Yun, however, still escaped!","The establishment’s formations were incredibly powerful and could fully immobilize a soul projection powerhouse, to say nothing of a mere nascent soul cultivator.","Lu Yun didn’t look at the other two until after he killed Sui Ge’s four guards and took the treasures. He’d utilized Size Manipulation earlier and turned into a particle of dust, escaping through the cracks of the formation.","Immortal Gazer was a premier third rank formation. It could trap, kill, and defend. A soul projection cultivator would have no choice but to submit, but to Lu Yun’s Eye of Nullification, it was full of holes.","Employing Size Manipulation to turn into a particle of dust was almost second nature for him. He easily slipped through the formation’s cracks and killed the four guards before they could react.","“Let’s go!” Tie Shanhe didn’t hesitate when he saw that the establishment’s formation couldn’t do anything to Lu Yun. He grabbed Sui Ge, broke through the formation, and ran out of the building. He knew that Sui Ge was no match for the young man despite being mid nascent soul. They didn’t stand a chance even if they coordinated their attacks together.","Sui Ge could not die here. Prince Sui dominated the land and his patron was one that not even a fifth rank cultivation empire dared offend. He was the disciple of a true immortal. Although the prince showed respect to Immortal Gazer, he would cause enormous trouble all the same if his favorite grandson died here.","For that reason alone, Immortal Gazer had unequivocally taken Sui Ge’s side without missing a beat.","Tie Shanhe activated the formation again after their departure and bounced all of the customers out of the building. Only Lu Yun was left inside. Tie Shanhe then directed all of his true origin into a red disk that appeared in his hand.","Boom!","The building burst into flames like it was a furnace. Tie Shanhe had fully activated the formation underpinning its foundations. He wouldn’t rest until he killed Lu Yun!","The citizens of Ashflame City looked at Immortal Gazer with astonishment when its primary formation activated. It’d rumbled to life only once before—three thousand years ago. A soul separation cultivator from a seventh rank empire had thrown a fit in the restaurant. He was ultimately refined alive and his soul scattered to the winds.","The cultivator’s sect later came to demand an explanation, but their seventh rank nation suffered retaliation instead. It declined overnight and was now a third rank empire.","Such was the might of the Immortal Gazer.","“It’s a Nineheavens Brahman Formation, I completely missed it.” Golden light sparkled from Lu Yun’s eyes as he swept the premises.","Every formation and restriction within Immortal Gazer was lit up and emanating blazing flames. The entire structure burned with raging fire, but suffered no damage from the inferno.","“Where is it... Aha, a formation disk! I knew it, how could a fourth rank cultivation empire set up a ninth rank formation? They’re using a formation disk!” A smile crept over Lu Yun’s face.","A layer of fire origin enveloped his body. As fearsome as the Nineheavens Brahman Formation was, it couldn’t draw near connate fire origin. Lu Yun strolled through the rampaging formation like it was his backyard.","He could summon connate elements through the Connate Great Dao of the Five Elements, thereby ensuring that ordinary elements would not harm him. This was also possible because a soul projection cultivator oversaw the Nineheavens Brahman Formation. If it was a soul separation powerhouse instead, Lu Yun would have to flee for his life.","“Oh please, they’re completely ruining things by adding more to it!” Lu Yun shook his head with a soft sigh as he took in the formation around him. “The Nineheavens Brahman Formation ignites the origin of spiritual fire, but these Immortal Gazer fools have added a mess of supplemental formations to it. No wonder it’s so much weaker than it should be.”","Wrapped in a protective cocoon of fire energy, Lu Yun arrived beneath the restaurant. A fourth level defensive formation stopped the young man from progressing further.","“...do those of Immortal Gazer understand formations or not? A ninth rank formation disk being protected by a fourth rank formation? If the enemy can reach this place, what’s the difference between this formation and paper?” Lu Yun rubbed his forehead and broke the fourth rank formation with a few hand seals. An enormous flaming-red millstone appeared in front of him.","It ground onward with heat waves so terrifying that the young man frowned beneath the protection of connate fire energy.","“Nice formation disk! It’s been refined into something like a treasure, so treasure and formation are connected to each other. That’s a good idea! But this is a half finished attempt and not a true treasure.”","He stared at the formation disk for a long while before nodding with satisfaction. It was giving him some new inspiration. But if formula dao was present, combining treasure and formation would be very easy.","“Formula dao again!” Lu Yun shook his head with a rueful chuckle. “Let’s collect this formation disk first.”","The ninth rank formation disk was so strong that if it erupted with full force and deployed the Nineheavens Brahman Formation, even empyrean immortals would find nothing but anguished regret. But with a mere soul projection cultivator in charge, they were unable to fully utilize the formation disk. To Lu Yun’s eyes, the formation disk was just a sitting duck.","......","Countless cultivators gathered near Immortal Gazer—they’d never imagined that they’d be able to see the establishment activate its primary foundation. They weren’t the only ones, even the Ashflame city lord was alarmed.","“Has another soul separation powerhouse come to cause trouble at Immortal Gazer?” City Lord Luo Yulong murmured to himself as he looked in the restaurant’s direction.","Who knew what he’d think if he learned that the establishment had activated its formation for only an initial nascent soul junior?","“How is it, senior?” Sui Ge asked with dissatisfaction. Tie Shanhe pulling him out of the building was a loss of face. Sui Ge was very strong himself and a member of a mysterious sect. He learned from the hands of an empyrean immortal. Although he was only mid nascent soul, he was wholly unafraid when facing soul projection heavyweights.","Thus, Tie Shanhe dragging him away with their tail between their legs after one exchange felt very humiliating!","“He’s not dead yet!” Tie Shanhe glowered. How was a ninth rank formation insufficient against a nascent soul cultivator??","He took out a crystalline item from his storage ring and gripped it in his hand, slowly refining it.","Sui Ge’s eyelids twitched when he took a closer look. That was a lower rank spirit crystal! Not even his grandfather possessed one, but a mere steward of Immortal Gazer could easily take one out for refinement.","What he didn’t know was that Tie Shanhe was quite tormented by this decision. He only had so many lower rank spirit crystals—if it wasn’t for the Nineheavens Brahman Formation consuming too much true origin, he wouldn’t want to consume one either!","Spirit crystals were easier to refine compared to spirit stones. The qi they contained was much more pure and high quality, making them far superior to ordinary spirit stones. The energy contained within one lower rank spirit crystal was the equivalent of one hundred paramount rank spirit stones—in theory. No one was willing to exchange a spirit crystal for spirit stones.","Rumble!","A massive disturbance sounded from the building. Countless baffled cultivators watched as the opulent building... jumped upward.","Although it lifted only one meter, everyone clearly saw that it’d jumped upward.","Pfft!","Tie Shanhe spat out a mouthful of blood and sagged to the ground. The treasure he used to control the formation disk drifted away as dust.","“Someone’s touched the formation disk...” he muttered weakly with horror.","Boom!","Before anyone else could react, a crimson dragon rushed out of the top of the building and made a circle of the skies, diving after half a breath.","Crack crack crack!","The magnificent Immortal Gazer building toppled over as rubble from the collision.","“Hey, Tie! What can you do about this gentleman tearing down your establishment today?” The crimson dragon vanished and Lu Yun arrived on his sword. He sneered down at Sui Ge and Tie Shanhe.","The elder in golden robes closed his eyes and wished for death. He was the cause of events today. While the young man in blue would die when the executives made their decision, he wouldn’t be far off for his involvement.","“This is Dark Orchid Empire, you are not permitted to run wildly through it!’ Sui Ge was the foremost genius of the younger generation, how could he permit Lu Yun to strut around in front of him? He set foot onto his flying sword and rose into the sky to face the young man.","“Heh.” Lu Yun couldn’t be bothered with him. A flower from the greenhouse, while strong, was just a pretty facade covering nothing underneath.","He turned around and enveloped himself in a dense array of sword light. Transforming into a crimson dragon once more, he dove at Tie Shanhe on the ground.","Sui Ge wasn’t worthy of regard, Tie Shanhe needed to be taken alive. Lu Yun finally understood how preeminent Immortal Gazer was in the world, and how they must have certain ambitions to quietly set up a ninth rank formation in Dark Orchid.","Dark Orchid was so close to Darklake that if anything happened here, it would affect Darklake Empire."]},{"number":2287,"title":"Chapter 2287: Chapter 2192.2: Confiscating the Spirit Vein","paragraphs":["Chapter 2192.2: Confiscating the Spirit Vein","“How dare you!” Sui Ge’s ego took a large hit when Lu Yun ignored him. He raised sword light and chased after the young man.","“Eh?” Thirty meters away from Tie Shanhe, Lu Yun abruptly discovered that the void around him was turning viscous. The energy of heaven and earth seemed like a swamp, firmly miring him within.","Sui Ge’s sword light arrived at the same time.","“Hmph.” Lu Yun sent out his Hongmeng qi in a blast of brute force, barely evading the cutting sword light with a twist of his body. However, a section of his long blue robe drifted away.","“And here I thought you were some kind of amazing genius. You’re just a buffoon that’s all bark and no bite!” Sui Ge chortled to see his opponent nearly die from the blow. His sword light split into a dozen rays that aimed to cut down Lu Yun from all sides.","Hongmeng qi circulating madly, Lu Yun deployed eighty percent of his true qi to negate the formation trapping him in the air. Only twenty percent was left to withstand Sui Ge.","Whoosh whoosh whoosh!","Lu Yun’s movements were slowing significantly and most of his Hongmeng qi was preoccupied elsewhere. He, too, sent out a dozen rays from Immortals Forbidden to counter Sui Ge’s attack. Frowning, he didn’t say anything.","“That’s all you can do!” Sui Ge roared with laughter. “Great Move of the Wings, Rainbow Slayer! Die!”","Rumble!","Sui Ge’s flying sword flew out and turned into a massive pair of red wings in the sky. Each flap dislodged fiery feathers and sent them drifting through the void.","Whoosh!","Sword light resembling a rainbow cut through the air to arrive in front of Lu Yun.","“What beautiful sword light!” sighed numerous female cultivators in the city. All they saw was sword brilliance shooting across the sky like a rainbow. Sui Ge stood in the air, white robes draped around his tall and limber body. His handsome face brimmed with masculine energy and he conducted his movements with unbridled grace.","Sui Ge was the man of many dreams in Dark Orchid, the ideal dao partner. He mesmerized a host of fans as he blazed with high spirits and deployed a scintillating move.","“You sure know how to put on a show...” Lu Yun’s lips quirked upward. Although his Hongmeng qi was suppressed, he still had many tricks up his sleeve. He lifted his foot and kicked the rainbow arcing toward him, sending Immortals Forbidden beneath his shoe at the same time to protect his foot.","BOOM!","Ear drums across Ashflame shook from the collision as the resplendent rainbow of sword qi shattered in the air. Lu Yun flew backward from the massive recoil and crashed into the city streets.","“Not bad to withstand my Rainbow Slayer! Of course, you’re just relying on the might of an upper spirit rank weapon!” Sui Ge stood imperiously in the sky and sneered down at a Lu Yun with both feet sunk into the ground.","“Idiot.” Lu Yun curled his lip. If it wasn’t for the city lord ambushing him with the formation, he wouldn’t need a second move to kill Sui Ge.","This fellow, however, was blithely unaware and looked around with arrogant self-satisfaction. He was a clown in Lu Yun’s eyes.","“Die!” Sui Ge lost his temper to see disdain on Lu Yun’s face. How dare someone he defeated show this kind of attitude?! He was asking for death!","The flying sword returned to Sui Ge’s hand and burst with dazzling radiance, falling on Lu Yun once more.","Immortals Forbidden also answered Lu Yun’s summons and erupted with a meter of sword light, calmly blocking the attack. But here, the city’s formation exerted greater pressure. The twenty percent strength he was able to bring to bear was gradually being reduced to fifteen.","“City lord of Ashflame, I have no intention of being enemies with you. I just want to tear down a restaurant that likes to bully its customers and kill those who want to kill me. But since you do not answer to reason, I will not be polite either!” Lu Yun shouted with real anger.","“City lord?” Sui Ge blinked in the midst of deploying a strike with full force. He didn’t really understand what his opponent said.","The city’s defensive formation stretched for five thousand kilometers and was comprised of ten formations. The eye of the formation rested in the city lord’s hand. Each formation was a fifth rank formation and their assembly perfectly melded the power of all ten. Their might was enhanced tenfold.","That meant to say that the city lord was invincible within Ashflame. Even soul separation powerhouses had to respectfully bow their heads within this domain. Sometimes, the formation was activated with none the wiser.","Prior to this, Lu Yun hadn’t anticipated that the city lord would move against him. The combination of ten fifth rank formations and their increased might was far beyond the hamstrung Nineheavens Brahman Formation. If it wasn’t for the sheer quality of his Hongmeng qi being able to negate the effects in the air, he would likely be completely immobilized and be on the chopping board for Sui Ge.","The formations’ might continued to grow and suppress his cultivation. It was only a matter of time before he lost control over himself.","“Hmph!” Sui Ge also realized certain things, but was unwilling to admit that he was less than Lu Yun. Pressing his advantage to kill the young man was the most important matter at hand.","Lu Yun sniffed when the city lord remained silent and materialized a dirt-yellow talisman in his hand. He disappeared in a flash of light.","“Eh?” Ashflame city lord Luo Yulong frowned. How had the young man disappeared right under his nose?","But since he hadn’t shown himself earlier, he couldn’t be bothered to now. If it wasn’t for the ninth rank formation disk being so important, he wouldn’t have taken action to help Immortal Gazer.","......","Lu Yun reappeared fifty kilometers belowground, in front of a pale-gold spirit vein that surged like the river. A cold smirk played on his lips.","“Since you like to stick your nose where it doesn’t belong, I won’t hold back either. Ashflame’s spirit vein is mine!” Lu Yun leered toothily.","Ashflame was Dark Orchid’s largest southern city and hailed as the southern capital primarily because of the lower rank spirit vein beneath the metropolis. If Lu Yun took it, he’d be crippling the city beyond repair.","His hands formed seals to summon a black pagoda between them—the sword pagoda. His cultivation was still too low to utilize the ray of sword qi within, but the sword pagoda itself was a powerful spatial treasure that could store living things.","There seemed to be a world of its own within the sword pagoda. Other than the ray of sword qi at the center, the rest of the area was an unbounded space.","After Lu Yun formed his nascent soul, the sword pagoda automatically recognized him as its master. Although he couldn’t touch the ray of sword qi, that didn’t preclude him from utilizing the space.","The spirit vein in front of him was one hundred kilometers long. It traveled through the earth like a massive dragon, swallowing and releasing energy of heaven and earth. This one, however, was confined by a formation. It could neither move nor escape the range of Ashflame City.","Connate yi wood flashed from Lu Yun’s hand, breaking the wood based restriction and tearing an opening in it. The spirit vein seemed to come alive and swam toward Lu Yun.","He also could have broken the city lord’s formation with the connate five elements, but the Jade Ruins Realm was in complete shambles at the moment. He would be in grave danger if someone recognized the art he used.","Using a talisman of the connate five elements could be explained away as just a heaven-defying treasure. But waving the elements to him with a single hand... even the Human Emperor of Great Xia would come for him then.","Lu Yun didn’t want that kind of trouble, and thankfully he could act without reservation below ground. A golden immortal’s consciousness could not extend so far, not to mention formations and restrictions overlapped each other in this locale. Lu Yun wouldn’t have made it thus far without his talisman of connate yang earth. If he couldn’t manage it, then it was out of reach for awakened cultivators.","After a tiny hint of connate yi wood opened the formation, Lu Yun enlarged the sword pagoda with several hand seals. When its internal space was large enough, it exploded with a devouring force that swallowed the spirit vein.","It took three days for the sword pagoda to fully consume the spirit vein and safely store it inside.","“Heh heh heh, I was worrying what to supplement my cultivation with now that I’ve exhausted goodwill. This spirit vein comes in the nick of time!” Lu Yun waved another hand after claiming the spirit vein and stored the sword pagoda back in his dantian.","......","Ashflame City, within the city lord’s residence.","“Little prince, do you mean to say that the young man in blue that day was the murderer of the Boulder Rise city lord?” Luo Yulong’s face darkened. If he’d known that Lu Yun was that city lord’s murderer, he would’ve activated more than Ashflame’s trap formation to help Sui Ge. He would’ve called upon the city’s grand formation and obliterated the young man from existence.","Those from Prince Sui’s household were much more precious than the rest of the Dark Orchid royal family!","“The murderer who killed my second brother half a month ago was a young man dressed in blue, wielding a crimson upper spirit rank flying sword. If my guess is right, this is the one. Any who dares touch a member of Prince Sui’s household will die even if they flee to the ends of the world!” Sui Ge snapped out as he tossed a jade slip to Luo Yulong.","The city lord brooded after scanning it with his consciousness. It contained a recording of when Lu Yun killed the Boulder Rise city lord. This was what Sui Ge was here to investigate in Dark Orchid’s southern capital. Who would’ve thought that he’d run straight into Lu Yun here!","“I’ve already spread the news—Immortal Gazer experts will be here shortly and we’ll hunt down that young man.” Tie Shanhe was equally livid. The Ashflame branch had been completely destroyed and its ninth rank formation disk seized. They needed to catch this young man as soon as possible, or it would be his head on a pike soon.","Rumble!!","The city suddenly trembled as the ten formations enveloping Ashflame collapsed one after another.","“Someone’s disturbed the spirit vein!” Luo Yulong gasped."]},{"number":2288,"title":"Chapter 2288: Chapter 2193.1: Frostmoon Ice","paragraphs":["Chapter 2193.1: Frostmoon Ice","Ashflame City, the southern capital of Dark Orchid Empire.","The assembly of ten formations normally hidden in the void materialized in the airspace over the city. Not only that, but terrifying cracks snaked through their curtains of light. It was a clear sign that a lack of qi was causing the formations to crumble.","Luo Yulong, Sui Ge, Tie Shanhe, and some other soul projection cultivators shot into the sky, regarding the assembly with ugly expressions.","“Someone has dared touch the city’s spirit vein—there is no one in heaven or earth who will be able to save them!” snarled a stocky, dark-skinned cultivator at soul projection.","“No matter what, we need to stabilize the formations first. If they collapse, the city’s qi will immediately wash away.” Luo Yulong waved several tens of thousands of spirit stones out of his storage ring. They formed an enormous milky-white dragon that dove into the ground and returned a few hints of qi to the disintegrating formation assembly.","The other soul projection cultivators took note and also took out their spirit stones for repairs.","“As expected of the little prince, what a display of wealth!” Some of the cultivators looked on with envy when millions of spirit stones streamed out of Sui Ge’s ring.","A sum of millions of paramount rank spirit stones was no small wealth for soul projection cultivators. Of course, whatever they took out was for public use—Dark Orchid Empire would reimburse them later on.","They were repairing the formations both for the city and for themselves. Their foundations were firmly established in Ashflame. The metropolis would be worthless once qi fully dissipated from the city.","Eight soul projection cultivators and a mid nascent soul little prince managed to stop the array from crumbling after they brought out five million spirit stones.","RUMBLE!!","Before they could sag with relief, the ten formations hovering in the air spontaneously disassembled and turned to dust. All of the qi that’d been coalesced by the formations immediately flew outward. The lush Ashflame City turned as barren as the wilderness within forty-five minutes.","Some of the larger clans still had minor qi accumulation formations operating over their compounds. It retained a hint of vitality for the sprawling metropolis.","“Someone... has taken Ashflame’s spirit vein...” A pale Luo Yulong dumbly watched motes of energy scatter from his domain. The other soul projection cultivators were likewise flabbergasted. They’d lived in Ashflame for multiple generations, it was unbelievable and unacceptable that their preeminent home suddenly became a third-rate city!","Ashflame was the southern capital of Dark Orchid due to the spirit vein beneath its foundations. It continuously took in ambient qi and supported the ponderous formation assembly. The formations also gathered qi from the surroundings, thus maintaining a city that ran for twenty-five hundred kilometers.","But now... all of it was no more.","“Who dares sever the foundations of my Ashflame?! I, Xu Qiyu, will see that he is damned for all eternity!!” howled a middle-aged man who seemed otherwise scholarly and refined.","......","Lu Yun grinned merrily after he collected the spirit vein in the sword pagoda. Although it was only a lower rank spirit vein, it was an incredibly precious resource for him in his current state.","“I need to consolidate my cultivation first before I head up there and make trouble for the Ashflame city lord.” He sat down cross-legged and circulated Hongmeng qi. The lower rank spirit vein expanded in the sword pagoda and flowed into the young man’s body, using the pagoda as a medium.","Any other cultivator using a spirit vein to supplement their cultivation would explode on the spot. But Lu Yun practiced the Nine Chapters of Dao, a method from the heavenly dao itself. He needed hundreds to thousands times more qi compared to regular nascent soul cultivators. Energy from the spirit vein was immediately converted to Hongmeng qi when it entered his body.","His cultivation stabilized at peak initial nascent soul after a while, leaving Lu Yun only one step away from mid nascent soul.","“Goodwill is different from qi in that goodwill complements cultivation, but qi directly enhances cultivation. Regardless, it’s best to break through every cultivation level on the basis of dao comprehension and natural progression.” Lu Yun stood up, highly satisfied with reaching the fourth turn of the Seeing Dao chapter. He was much stronger than before and could certainly kill Sui Ge even if suppressed by the city’s formations.","“Let’s get that piece of Frostmoon Ice first before taking revenge.” He always sought an answer for every slight. Since the Ashflame city lord had voluntarily joined the fray, Lu Yun took his spirit vein in retaliation.","Besides, Darklake Empire needed to free itself of Dark Orchid control if it wished to raise its profile. On a fundamental level, Darklake and Dark Orchid were archrivals. Dark Orchid had become an Origin Sect pawn against the Lu Clan. It was only a matter of time before the two nations erupted in war. Taking the spirit vein of one of their cities was the same as weakening Dark Orchid, so whyever not?","......","Ashflame swiftly declined. Although numerous cultivators were still around, there were no signs of its former glory. Its heavyweights were preparing to move and oddly enough, numerous weaker cultivators rushed to the city when they received word.","Lu Yun didn’t bother changing his appearance before sauntering down the main street.","“Immortal Gazer... sure rebuilt itself in a hurry.” Lu Yun smirked at the towering building in front of him. It’d taken him three days to claim the spirit vein and another to raise his cultivation. Yet Immortal Gazer rebuilt itself within four days!","Bam!","He reached the front door and kicked away the associate outside before the latter could say a word.","“Old man Tie, this young master has come back. Get your ass out here!” Lu Yun’s voice roiled through Immortal Gazer as a wave of sound.","“It’s you! How dare you come back!” Busy setting up new formations in the new building, Tie Shanhe’s face jerked with shock when he heard the voice. He quickly took out a transmission spirit stone and sent Luo Yulong a message.","“I haven’t done anything unsavory, why wouldn’t I return?” Lu Yun relaxed when he saw that Frostmoon Ice still rested in the grand steward’s ring. He’d have to visit the north if he couldn’t find the material in Ashflame.","Dark Orchid Empire stood staunchly in the south. If he was to visit the north from here, he’d have to spend at least eight years crossing the entire world. The likes of him didn’t have the right to take a transportation formation.","Lu Yun wasn’t willing to waste time, so he struck as soon as he spoke. He flashed to Tie Shanhe and grabbed for the man’s neck.","Whoosh!","Sword light rushed by and slashed at Lu Yun’s hand. Frowning, the young man turned to the side and easily avoided the sword light.","“To think you’d come back, loser!” Sui Ge stood in the air with flowing white robes and frostily regarded Lu Yun. “You’re the one who killed the city lord of Boulder Rise, aren’t you?”","“Boulder Rise? Yes, that’s me.” Lu Yun sensed several powerful presences breaking through the air. Their part of the void was quickly placed under confinement. It wasn’t the effects of a formation, but the joint forcefield from seven powerhouses at least latter soul projection.","“Die!” Sui Ge roared, his crimson flying sword flaring with radiance and deploying Rainbow Slayer once more.","Derision played on Lu Yun’s lips as Immortals Forbidden erupted in turn, emanating scintillating red light like a miniature sun.","Bam!","Two ludicrously extravagant rays of sword light crashed into each other, dismantling the forcefield from the seven powerhouses.","Pfft!","Sui Ge spat out fresh blood as he was thrown up into the sky. HIs upper spirit rank flying sword disintegrated from the impact.","“How is this possible?!” Eyes wide open and incredulous, he was unaware that he’d been able to suppress Lu Yun that day only with the help of Luo Yulong. The city lord hadn’t revealed his involvement out of consideration for the dignity of the greatest genius in Dark Orchid.","“Die!!” Lu Yun’s target was Tie Shanhe. He brought his palm down on the man’s head after sending Sui Ge flying.","The man was ready and his lower spirit rank defensive weapon swiftly raised a curtain of light. At the same time, a treasure shaped like a club flew out to meet Lu Yun’s hand.","Bam!","Lu Yun sent the club flying with a vicious palm strike, but he also stumbled backward as well.","Whoosh whoosh whoosh!","The seven latter soul projection powerhouses also made their moves. Seven rays of cutting sword radiance darted for Lu Yun’s face.","“You court death!” Immortals Forbidden erupted with crimson radiance that enveloped the young man’s body before he shot into the air, transforming into a crimson dragon thirty meters long.","Swish swish swish swish swish...","The dragon twisted eighteen times in the bizarre fashion of the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons. The seven rays of sword radiance were rebuffed, forcing their beholders to reveal themselves in the void.","Lu Yun churned to action again and snaked toward the powerhouses.","“So strong!” Luo Yulong gasped with shock and flung out a green seal. It expanded to thirty meters long in the air and smashed down on Lu Yun.","BOOM!","Sword qi and seal smashed together, leveling all buildings within three hundred meters. Lu Yun was shoved out of his dragon form while Luo Yulong spat out a mouthful of blood mixed with pieces of organs. He fell down bonelessly from the sky."]},{"number":2289,"title":"Chapter 2289: Chapter 2193.2: Frostmoon Ice","paragraphs":["Chapter 2193.2: Frostmoon Ice","If it wasn’t for Tie Shanhe quickly snatching Luo Yulong out of the sky, the latter might have become the first soul projection cultivator to die from a fall—and a city lord at that!","Luo Yulong hastily took out pills when he reached the ground and poured them into his mouth, closing his eyes to digest them. Up in the air, the other six soul projection powerhouses worked in tandem to deliver another blow when they saw that Lu Yun’s dragon form was defused.","“That green seal is a nice item, it’s a mountain refined by a seed storage formation!” Lu Yun looked ardently at the seal that’d fallen to the ground. However, he had to ensure vigilance against the six remaining powerhouses.","He sent a dozen rays of sword light shooting out of Immortals Forbidden with a shake of his hand, negating their next attack. He then waved the green seal into his storage ring.","Whoosh whoosh whoosh!","Several thousand Ashflame city guards arrived and surrounded Lu Yun within a few breaths.","“Show him no mercy!” A livid Tie Shanhe roared after swallowing various medicines.","The guards moved without hesitation, deploying a joint attack. Thousands of rays of sword light formed a massive curtain of light that loomed over Lu Yun.","Ashflame’s guards were at least golden core. When several thousand golden core cultivators formed a battle formation, their sword light came down like a massive mountain. Even Lu Yun would be heavily injured if he was hit.","The young man twisted his body, leaving nine faint shadows in the void and evaded the mountain of sword light by the skin of his teeth.","Rumble!!","The mountain of sword light rammed into Ashflame City and obliterated everything within a one and a half kilometers radius.","“A mid rank battle formation that doubles battle strength.” A frowning Lu Yun appeared again over the city’s airspace.","......","“That is the Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragon... the methods of powerhouse Slaughterless who rampaged through the Celestial Realm Battlefront eight thousand years ago,” murmured a young girl in black as she looked up at Lu Yun in the sky.","The young man moved again, leaving nine faint figures in the void and rushing into the five thousand city guards. They posed such a threat that if he let them attack from a distance, he would suffer a one-sided beating. But if he threw himself amongst them, that disrupted their tempo enough that they couldn’t threaten him to the same degree.","“Scatter!” Their captain was an initial soul projection cultivator. He knew what Lu Yun wanted to do the second the young man charged them and gave the order for his men to disperse.","“Then I’ll kill you first!” Lu Yun set his sights on their captain as soon as the guards scattered and slashed through the air. The black-armored captain didn’t even have time to react before the attack was at his face.","Whoosh!","He was hewn into two.","“No, Yu’er!! Die, you bastard!!” A middle-aged man screamed with fury when the city guard captain died and threw himself at Lu Yun.","“Latter nascent soul?” Lu Yun raised a brow. This man likely had something to do with the cultivator he’d just killed, but who cared? Everyone in front of him was an enemy. He waved out another ray of sword light and sent it howling viciously at the middle-aged man.","“Housekeeper Hui!” Luo Yulong gasped and forced a burst of true origin out of his body, raising sword light to fly to Lu Yun. “Stop, you can’t kill him!”","Did Lu Yun care what the city lord was saying? Immortals Forbidden exploded with radiance and hacked the housekeeper into two before he had time to scream.","“You, you killed Housekeeper Hui... you’re a dead man walking!” Luo Yulong’s lips trembled as he stared dumbly at Lu Yun.","The young man collected Yu’er and Housekeeper Hui’s storage rings, then sneered, “If I am, then you’re walking before me.”","His sword flared once more and emitted a resplendent sun that careened toward Luo Yulong. The city lord was aghast, never dreaming that the young man would be so frightening that a latter soul projection cultivator had no recourse in front of him.","“It looks like only a peak powerhouse of soul separation will be able to take him down!” Luo Yulong didn’t have the courage to defy Lu Yun’s blazing sun. He would be able to capture the young man if the city’s grand formation still existed. But with the disappearance of the spirit vein and the collapse of the array of ten formations, he was no match for their attacker.","Bam!","Sword light the size of a small mountain cut into the sun just as it was about to reach Luo Yulong, pulverizing the attack. The five thousand city guards had once more assembled together in their battle formation and saved their city lord’s life.","Lu Yun leered and vanished with a shift of his right foot. Nine draconic shadows streaked through the air. The Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragon was an exceedingly strong body method that enhanced one’s speed to new heights.","Without the lead of a soul projection expert, the city guards were unable to determine where he was. He barrelled into them in half a breath.","Boom!","Sword qi sprayed in all directions as a crimson dragon flashed into existence among them. One hundred golden core guards died within a few breaths.","Pitter patter!","None of the guards dared stand up to Lu Yun anymore. They abandoned their coordination and ran for their lives. The young man didn’t hunt them down, instead turning his sword light onto Luo Yulong.","“We’re leaving!” Sui Ge appeared out of nowhere and grabbed the city lord. A treasure akin to a flying ship manifested beneath their feet and flew them to safety.","“An upper spirit rank flying treasure!” Lu Yun frowned in the direction of their getaway. As fast as it was, he could catch up to it if he wanted to. But currently, he wanted Tie Shanhe’s Frostmoon Ice more. With it, he would be able to create Proxima Metal and a cross forge, thereby repairing the cross ark.","Once he had a cross ark among his arsenal, he wouldn’t need to fear the Origin Sect. He would easily retreat with his family if they found themselves on the losing side.","Lu Yun looked around him—none of the other Ashflame soul projection cultivators dared meet his eyes. They scattered in all four directions, with the exception of Tie Shanhe.","“How dare you kill Housekeeper Hui, Lu Yun!” Tie Shanhe stood quietly on the spot, an eerie smile on his face while a thick line of blood dribbled out of his mouth.","“Oh? You know me?” Lu Yun blinked. He hadn’t given out his name since leaving Darklake and had even changed his appearance, but it looked someone recognized him.","“Hahahaha!!” Tie Shanhe roared with laughter. “You caused massive upheaval in Fallen Leaf and killed the city lord of Boulder Rise, Dark Orchid labeled you as a thorn in the nation’s side long ago. Why would it not investigate you? Prince Sui’s men will arrive in Dark City soon.”","Lu Yun pursed his lips and casually killed Tie Shanhe with a flash of sword light. He grabbed the man’s nascent soul as soon as it emerged and threw it into the sword pagoda. As a soul projection cultivator, Tie Shanhe’s nascent soul could travel for thousands of kilometers and live in the absence of his physical body.","“Frostmoon Ice!” Lu Yun broke Tie Shanhe’s restriction on his storage ring and smiled faintly when he found what he wanted. “Ashflame City is done. Let’s take a look at the city lord residence.”","He sped to the tallest building in the city.","“As I thought, nothing...” The premises were empty of people and treasure. While there were a few spirit stones left in the vaults, there weren’t that many of them. Lu Yun swept them into his storage ring and left.","Luo Yulong and the others were ready as soon as trouble struck the city. They’d shifted everything out and likely notified the emperor of Dark Orchid. The imperial family would send people here soon.","Lu Yun didn’t fear soul projection experts, but he was wary of soul separation. They could trounce him with image projections and sheer strength. He wasn’t a match for them yet. While Dark Orchid was known as a fourth rank empire, it had no superior nation. Who knew if they were like Darklake and playing the pig to eat the tiger?","He left as soon as he collected everything of value in the city lord residence. Right now, he needed to find a place to refine Proxima Metal and the cross forge.","“Halt!” A slightly angry voice rang in his ears when he was fifty kilometers from the city gates.","Lu Yun jerked to a stop, finding a sixteen year old girl in front of him. Dressed in a black silk dress, she was dainty and charming, but also full of hostility. He was quite startled to find that she was a soul separation powerhouse. Her real age was indeed as she appeared—not secretly thousands of years old.","“What might this miss be looking for in stopping me?” Lu Yun went on the alert.","“You said my spirit cuisine isn’t good?!” she shouted with irritation.","“Eh...” Lu Yun blinked. “You must be mistaken, miss. When did I say... eh? Are you Spirit Chef Shen of the Immortal Gazer?”"]},{"number":2290,"title":"Chapter 2290: Chapter 2194.1: Disciple","paragraphs":["Chapter 2194.1: Disciple","“Hmph!” The girl in black snorted and glared coldly at Lu Yun.","The young man felt a headache brewing. Why in the heavens did a mere Immortal Gazer boast of a soul separation spirit chief? Spirit chefs were not people to anger. When the Human Emperor of Great Xia celebrated his five thousandth birthday, one hundred and eight spirit chefs jointly prepared a feast of eighteen thousand dishes. Every immortal and cultivator in attendance found their cultivation taking a small step forward and their foundations further consolidated.","After that, spirit chefs were renowned throughout the world.","Turning his nose up at Immortal Gazer’s fare violated a spirit chef’s bottom line.","A thought struck Lu Yun as he noticed the young woman’s aura fluctuating—she seemed ready to fly into a rage. He raised cupped fists, “I am Lu Yun, might I know the miss’ name?”","“Heh heh,” she snorted coldly at the question. “How dare you ask about my name after saying my food is bad?”","Lu Yun shook his head in the face of her wrath. “Does the miss think that I used your dishes as an excuse to cause trouble at Immortal Gazer?”","Seeing as she was a soul separation powerhouse, it was impossible that she hadn’t heard his words. Therefore, he might as well not bother with any pretense.","“Is that not so?” she sniffed.","“Of course not.” Lu Yun stood with his hands behind his back and some pride on his face. “Although the miss’ dishes were full of qi, their taste left a little to be desired.”","“Hmm?!” Her slender eyebrows drew together, but she didn’t say a word.","“I happen to be a spirit chef as well.” Lu Yun smiled dashingly.","“You are also a spirit chef?” The young girl blinked, then regarded Lu Yun assessingly. The young man was dressed in long white robes with a blue overcoat. A medallion of fine jade hung from the purple belt at his waist. His flamboyant demeanor painted him as a good-for-nothing wealthy scion, no matter how she looked at him.","This person is a spirit chef?","Spirit chefs were only one step lower than pill masters in the world of cultivation, even Great Xia. Some higher ranked ones rivaled pill masters.","“You?” Disdain appeared on the girl’s face.","“Hahahaha!!” Lu Yun laughed loudly. “There is always a teacher among us if three people walk together. How do you know I’m not a spirit chef, miss?”","Whoosh!","He snapped open a large folding fan.","“Have you no shame!” The girl in black blushed hotly and hastily averted her eyes.","Lu Yun didn’t mind at all. He waved his explicitly graphic fan and waggled his brows. “If the miss doesn’t believe that I am a spirit chef, why don’t we have a contest?”","“A contest?” The girl looked at Lu Yun again only after he put the fan away, her face steadily grew darker. “How?”","“That’s easy. You make a dish for me and I’ll make a dish for you. We’ll taste each other’s dishes—won’t the victor be easily determined then?” Lu Yun chuckled.","“The dishes you tasted at Immortal Gazer were but the work of a few moments,” the girl sneered. “If I bring out my full force to make a dish for you, that means an incredible bargain for you!”","“How does the miss not know that it might be a bargain for you?” Lu Yun smiled. “We can add a wager to set the miss at ease.”","“Done!” The girl nodded. “If I win, you must teach me the method of the Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragon.”","“So that’s what you want.” Lu Yun abruptly understood. The girl knew the body method, but he didn’t mind. “And what if you lose, miss?”","“Lose? How would I lose to you? ...what, do you want to commit that shameless act?” The girl looked sharply at Lu Yun.","“Hmph, I am a noble man of my word. Not everyone is the same as you, you know.” Lu Yun curled his lip, refusing to answer the girl’s question. Seeing as his cultivation was less than the girl in black, all she had to do was smack him out of existence if she didn’t want to own up to her debt. Regardless, he wouldn’t lose.","“Hmph,” the girl snorted again. “If I lose, I’ll accept you as my master!”","“Why do I think I’m getting the worst of it no matter what?” Lu Yun grumbled.","“Do you think you’ll beat me?” she sneered.","“If your skill is at the level of what was displayed at Immortal Gazer, then you will lose without a doubt,” Lu Yun said innocently as he spread his hands out.","“When do we begin?” The girl couldn’t be bothered with more talk. She’d prevented Lu Yun from leaving because she wanted his Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragon. Since she could obtain it through a contest, she couldn’t be bothered with anything else.","When the Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragon shook the worlds eight thousand years ago, even the Human Emperor was alarmed. Sadly, no one knew of Slaughterless’ true identity. The girl in black only read about his body method in historic records. When she saw Lu Yun deploy an identical method over Ashflame, she silently followed in his wake.","Who would’ve thought that the young man would easily admit to it being the Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragon!","“Let’s do it now.” Lu Yun looked around; it was a barren field around him. Ashflame’s formations had collapsed upon the loss of its spirit vein. It took only four short days to turn its surroundings into a bleak wilderness.","The girl couldn’t be bothered with saying more, her opponent was only a nascent soul cultivator. While he was so heaven-defying that not even soul projection experts were his match, he was an ant to someone of the soul separation level.","If Lu Yun dared go back on his word, she would grab the young man and slowly torment him!","She summoned a golden pot that was one meter across. It was a mid dao rank treasure! It emanated the presence of a dao weapon as soon as it appeared.","Despite the girl being mid soul separation, she could fully utilize a mid dao rank treasure! Not to mention, she didn’t fear the local combination cultivators since she wasn’t from this world of cultivation.","She looked at Lu Yun before taking out a handful of spirit herbs and protein, placing them into the pot. It hovered in the air while she sent hand seals into the cauldron with both hands. The pot began shaking and rays of radiance circulated from it, enveloping the vessel.","She then flipped her right hand over, manifesting a blue flame that jumped like a sprite. Everything within thirty meters of it was dyed blue and waves of heat roiled over the two.","“The Fire of Heaven and Earth?” Lu Yun swiftly took a few steps back.","“So you know about it. You have some knowledge,” chuckled the girl. She gently waved the dancing flame to the bottom of the pot. When her hands formed seals again, her black silk dress turned blue and blue radiance streamed into the pot from her hands.","A faint, refreshing fragrance drifted out of the pot.","I’ll bring my full force to bear and cook a seventh rank spirit beast with seven rank spirit herbs. The kid’s receiving such a good bargain from this. But if he really does teach me the Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragon, it’s not such a loss to me either.","However, her expression shifted the moment as the strong smell of something delicious burrowed into her nostrils. She swallowed without meaning to and subconsciously looked at the other side.","A Spirit Glyph Sparrow had appeared in front of Lu Yun at some point in time. It was plucked, cleaned, and strung up on a lower qi rank flying sword. The sword hovered silently over the connate fire origin in Lu Yun’s left hand.","He held a jade flask with his right hand and slowly scattered spirit herb powder over the roasting Spirit Glyph Sparrow. As it turned golden crisp, not a single drop of oil dripped from it. All of its juices seemed to be locked within the crispy skin.","When caramelized brown began to creep over the bird’s skin a dozen breaths later, Lu Yun dismissed the fire from his left hand.","“Miss, my dish is ready, please have a taste.”","The girl put away her pot a while ago and trotted over to Lu Yun’s side.","“This is... a Spirit Glyph Sparrow?” She accepted the flying sword and took a deep sniff, then gently tore off a wing and took a smile bite. “Um...”","She stared blankly at it, then snapped back to her senses and quickly devoured the palm-sized bird. Only when she was certain there was not a sliver of meat left on the bones did she reluctantly lick her fingers.","A strange expression floated onto her face and she quickly sat down cross-legged. Her true origin operated fiercely and her aura grew with intensity.","Humm!","Lu Yun sensed the ambient qi within fifty kilometers surge furiously in their direction and gather on the girl.","“Is this girl... really destined to become my disciple?” Lu Yun blinked. He’d created no end of dishes like these for his grandfather and second uncle in Darklake. Their cultivation never changed, but a casually roasted Spirit Glyph Sparrow propelled this girl in black to break through!","She was originally mid soul separation, but a single bird had sent her to latter soul separation!","“You’re a spirit chef immortal?!” the girl asked in astonishment after her cultivation level stabilized.","“If you say so, then I guess I am so.” Lu Yun smiled faintly."]},{"number":2291,"title":"Chapter 2291: Chapter 2194.2: Disciple","paragraphs":["Chapter 2194.2: Disciple","Spirit cuisine was the same as spirit stones—items to supplement cultivation. Spirit cuisine differed in that it was eaten and digested into the body. Its qi was more gentle and easier to absorb compared to the energy within spirit stones.","Using spirit cuisine to break through depended on both the caliber of the fare itself and the cultivator’s fortunes. It was similar to cultivating with spirit stones in that ascension was not guaranteed.","However, spirit cuisine tended to be too expensive. The Spirit Glyph Sparrow that Lu Yun roasted would sell out even if he priced it at ten thousand paramount spirit stones. Of course, he didn’t intend to earn money that way. Cooking food was just a hobby, something to do for family in moments of leisure. He didn’t really want to become a spirit chef.","“How did you do it?! You used a first rank Spirit Glyph Sparrow to create a dish that was almost immortal fare...” There was no trace of the girl’s earlier contempt and derision to be found. The apples of her cheeks were red and grease from the bird ringed her mouth, presenting a rather adorable sight.","“Or is the powder you scattered over it from an immortal pill? There were hints of an immortal pill in that dish...” She smacked her lips. Although it’d been nearly four hours, some taste lingered in her mouth. Her brows knit together. “So you used an immortal pill...”","“What does the miss think of my spirit cuisine?” Lu Yun chuckled like he didn’t see her expression.","“You used an immortal pill to season the dish, so it overpowered the food. That was not spirit cuisine.” The girl’s expression was unpleasant.","“Can it be that you wish to do that deed?” Lu Yun blithely continued.","The girl fell silent without a word.","“Forget it, I can’t be bothered to lower myself to the same level as you.” He shook his head and turned to leave.","“Wait!” The girl blocked his way again. “Did you use the powder of an immortal pill just now?”","“Immortal pill?” Lu Yun curled his lip. “As wealthy as I might be, I wouldn’t waste an immortal pill on a spirit cuisine.”","He tossed the jade flask to the girl. She unstoppered it and took a slight sniff.","“Dew Grass, Skyfrost Fruit, an orchid, Flame Root...” She frowned after reeling off a dozen spirit herbs. “How is this possible? They’re all first rank spirit herbs, the lowest of the low with nothing special about them.”","“Magic happens when you scatter them over a Spirit Glyph Sparrow,” Lu Yun interjected.","She sent out a flying sword and knocked down a passing Spirit Glyph Sparrow, quickly dressing it and summoned a ball of true origin fire to roast it.","Mouthwatering fragrance quickly rose into the air.","“This is indeed the case... but it doesn’t measure up to the one you made. Are you actually a spirit chef immortal?” The girl finally understood. “Kong Mengqian greets the master and requests that you accept me for a disciple!”","She suddenly bowed in front of Lu Yun.","“Do you really want to become my disciple?” Lu Yun asked without a change in expression.","“Yes!” Kong Mengqian nodded emphatically.","“I know you have a lot of masters.” Lu Yun nodded, realizing that Spirit Chef Shen was an alias—Kong Mengqian was her real name. He could tell that she came from an illustrious background possibly even more prestigious than Fengxian Wu. She was a soul separation powerhouse at such a young age and a very competent spirit chef. He could also see the traces of no less than ten powerful teachers on her, and they were all stronger than true immortal.","“But I will be your only master after you become my disciple. Can you do that?” he asked solemnly.","“I only want to learn how to cook spirit cuisines from master.” Kong Mengqian frowned and lifted her head.","“In that case, forget it.” Lu Yun shook his head and left.","“I can promise you that I won’t take anyone else for a master after learning from you!” Kong Mengqian called out urgently. Lu Yun’s methods of creating such high level fare from low level ingredients were heaven-defying. She couldn’t let this chance slip out of her fingers!","“Then what about your previous masters?” Lu Yun asked.","“They were masters in name only,” Kong Mengqian answered.","With that, Lu Yun understood that her skills most likely came from family elders or servants.","“But if you become my master, you must teach me the Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragon,” Kong Mengqian added after some thought.","“I will naturally teach you everything I know if you become my disciple,” Lu Yun smiled faintly.","Kong Mengqian curled her lip. Although the young man was extremely talented, that was all he was. Those like him could be found like carp in a river in Great Xia—he was nothing special. As for the body method, he’d probably lucked out and obtained Senior Slaughterless’ legacy somehow.","“Let’s conduct the ceremony then,” Lu Yun chuckled.","“Here?” Kong Mengqian looked around them.","Lu Yun pointed at the sky. “Your martial grandfather is watching from above.”","“So martial grandfather has already returned to the heavens.” A resigned Kong Mengqian looked at a master weaker than her. But since there’s no martial grandfather, that means there’s no sect to restrict me. I keep my freedom and this young man weaker than me cannot discipline me.","Her disposition turned sunny again when her thoughts traveled here.","As strong as Kong Mengqian was, she was just a young girl of sixteen years old. She had a good heart and did things according to her personal preferences, but didn’t think of the consequences due to a lack of experience in this world.","Lu Yun’s tactics wouldn’t work on anyone else. If it was an experienced soul separation powerhouse in front of him, their first thought would be to capture Lu Yun and force him to reveal how he’d made the dish and the Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragon.","“Master, please accept a bow from your disciple Kong Mengqian!” The girl respectfully bowed to Lu Yun, but didn’t fall to her knees as she should.","Lu Yun didn’t mind. He was the disciple of heavenly dao, which made Kong Mengqian the martial granddaughter of the heavenly dao. If she dared betray him, the heavenly dao would likely send a chaos tribulation to smite her out of existence.","“Hahahahaha!! What wonderful news to hear that junior brother has obtained a fine disciple! This connate item has a shared destiny with your disciple, so it is her greeting gift!” Sky’s voice reverberated in Lu Yun’s mind and he felt something appear in his storage ring. When he scanned it, he found a tattered green bamboo staff.","“Um...” He brought it out and saw that it was one meter long with the thickness of a thumb. It was green throughout and looked completely ordinary.","“Your martial uncle gave me this treasure. It is your welcoming gift today.” Lu Yun flushed faintly after he introduced it. Of course Sky had given him a fine treasure, but it looked... very shabby. It was a pitted stick that a dog had gnawed on.","Kong Mengqian’s expression turned stiff and she stiltedly took the bamboo staff, murmuring, “This... this disciple thanks master...”","An ordinary stick of bamboo...","Her mind swept it again and again, finding nothing remotely treasure-like about the item. But since she’d made up her mind to learn from Lu Yun, she wouldn’t embarrass him. Thus, she solemnly placed the bamboo into her storage ring.","“Alright, you will follow me to Fallen Leaf Mountain first to handle a few things. After that is complete, I will teach you,” Lu Yun coughed.","Rumble!","A massive ray of sword light cut through the air and hacked a distant mountain into two. A figure tumbled out of the sky.","“Hahaha Gui Xie, finally out of strength to run? Now you can die!”","Another massive ray of sword light soared into the air and hacked at the remains of the mountain.","Whoosh!","An enormous black flag rose to meet it, scattering resplendent starlight across the void. Cosmic splendor streamed to it from a mysterious void and met the ray of sword light.","BOOM!!","When starlight and sword light collided, the halves of the mountain were annihilated to level ground. Gui Xie spat out a mouthful of blood and trembled like a leaf.","“Die!” The person in the air attacked again.","“Gui Xie?” Lu Yun blinked. Wasn’t that the latter combination powerhouse who’d received Empress Myrtlestar’s legacy? Someone was chasing him and had injured him to the point of death?","Empress Myrtlestar was Lu Yun’s friend, he wouldn’t let her heir die in front of him. He sent out a green seal with a wave of his hand and manifested it as a small mountain more than fifteen kilometers across. It was the seal that he’d taken from the Ashflame city lord, the mountain restricted by a seed storage formation.","KABOOM.","The small mountain was likewise sliced into two when it met the terrifying sword light, but it also afforded Gui Xie a second of breathing space and helped him evade the sword light.","“Help him!” Lu Yun darted toward Gui Xie with Immortals Forbidden beneath his feet, not waiting for his new disciple to answer.","“How dare two ants obstruct this seat?!” The person in the air was a young man in blue. He frowned at seeing Lu Yun block his sword light."]},{"number":2292,"title":"Chapter 2292: Chapter 2195.1: Nineheavens Brahman Fire","paragraphs":["Chapter 2195.1: Nineheavens Brahman Fire","Gui Xie’s attacker was a powerhouse of latter combination level. A snowy flying sword circled around him as he stood in the air, coolly regarding Lu Yun next to Gui Xie.","Kong Mengqian blinked, not having anticipated that her master, a nascent soul cultivator, would rush in front of a combination powerhouse. She swiftly understood that the one under attack should be Lu Yun’s friend, so she raised a ray of black sword light and followed close behind the young man.","Gui Xie was in poor shape as horrific wounds crisscrossed his body. He’d been almost beaten to pieces, and the worst of his injuries was a gash that ran from right shoulder to waist. It nearly bisected the man.","Lu Yun drew close to Gui Xie and shoved a pill into the man’s mouth when he saw that the powerhouse in the sky didn’t react.","The man’s wounds slowly took a turn for the better.","“Are, are you Sir Lu?” Gui Xie asked with bafflement when he opened his eyes and saw Lu Yun.","A dense current of goodwill surged from him into the Seal of the Multitude. Lu Yun’s lips curved upward when he sensed the rush.","“What’s going on? Why is he chasing you? Why are you being attacked by a combination powerhouse at your level?” Lu Yun could see through the man’s cultivation with the Eye of Nullification.","“How is he alive with all these injuries?” Kong Mengqian also arrived with a large pot in her hand. The spirit cuisine inside had finished cooking, but she dumped it without hesitation.","The powerhouse in the sky did a double take when he saw the pot in the girl’s hand. This was a mid dao rank treasure fashioned in the shape of a pot! What an utter waste!","His eyes gleamed anew when he resettled on the Cosmic Flag in Gui Xie’s hand.","Gui Xie shook his head and looked at his attacker. “Peng Hue, you can have the Cosmic Flag and my life. Let these two go.”","“Hahahaha!!” the man in the sky roared with laughter. “If I kill all three of you, that upper dao rank weapon will be mine and I gain another mid dao rank treasure!”","“So you want to kill us for our loot?” Lu Yun frowned. “Disciple, are you confident in killing him?”","Kong Mengqian rolled her eyes expressively. “Do you think combination powerhouses are cabbages by the side of the street? I am a spirit chef, not a battle genius. I can hold him off, but killing him is too hard.”","“Is a fifteen year old soul separation expert not a perverse genius yourself?” Lu Yun grumbled.","Kong Mengqian was latter soul separation and Peng Yue at latter combination. There was a major cultivation stage of difference between the two. Not to mention, the girl spent most of her time and effort researching spirit cuisine. It was already surprising enough that she could fend off someone stronger than her.","“The girl is a bit young, but she’s still a beauty, hehehe.” Peng Yue didn’t hear their conversation, but wouldn’t care if he did. He took in his fill of Kong Mengqian and leered lasciviously.","“You court death!” Being young as she was, Kong Mengqian easily lost her temper at offensive words. She cocked her hand back with the pot and shot into the sky.","Boom!","It grew to the size of a small mountain before she swung it at Peng Yue.","“Careful, he’s very strong! He’s not an ordinary cultivator!” Gui Xue called out when he saw the girl rush forward.","Peng Yue’s flying sword exploded with brilliance and slashed the pot. Kong Mengqian rapidly backed up with blood trickling out of her mouth. However, so did Peng Yue suffer from the collision. The girl was very strong and could fully deploy the might of a mid dao rank treasure, so the impact flung him backward for several dozen meters.","“Don’t worry, the girl isn’t an ordinary cultivator either.” Lu Yun took out a green pill from his storage ring when he saw his disciple stand her ground. “Eat this.”","He’d given Gui Xie an ordinary healing pill at first. Now that the combatants in the sky were preoccupied, he brought out a pill of his own making.","Gui Xie blinked, but swallowed the pill without hesitation or suspicion.","“Oof!” He flushed beet red as true origin circulated madly through his body. His injuries healed at a speed visible to the naked eye and were mostly gone after a dozen breaths.","“Is this a spirit pill?!” He opened his eyes with shock.","There were nine ranks to pills and spirit pill sat on top of them all. They were very rare in the worlds of cultivation; each one was worth cities. The Nineturns Profound Life Pill that Lu Tianling had obtained for Lu Yun was only a low ranked spirit pill, but it was one that the Darklake royal family had paid a great price to possess.","BOOM!","Another loud explosion detonated in the sky before Lu Yun could respond. Kong Mengqian batted Peng Yue away with her pot, but she also flew backward, drenched in blood. Lu Yun could tell that as fierce as Kong Mengqian was, this was only temporary. She would start losing in a prolonged exchange due to a lack of battle experience.","Gui Xie quickly grabbed the Cosmic Flag when he noted the situation and scrambled to his feet to help Kong Mengqian.","“Don’t rush!” Lu Yun stopped him in his tracks. “She’s just broken through and needs a powerful opponent to hone her skills.”","“Um...” Gui Xie paused. “Is the miss your dao partner, sir?”","“She’s my disciple.” Lu Yun waved off the rest of the conversation. “What’s going on? You’re peak latter combination realm and you cultivate the Immortal Canon of Life and Death. How did a mere latter combination cultivator injure you?”","The Immortal Canon of Life and Death was the method of Empress Myrtlestar from the world of immortals. Although Gui Xie had only practiced it for one short year, his true origin had fully transmuted to true origin of life and death. When he wielded the Cosmic Flag, he should be invincible among his peers.","“He’s not the reason for my injuries,” Gui Xie chuckled ruefully. “When I was in the Dark Orchid capital, I happened to overhear two Nineheavens Pagoda disciples discussing what they wanted to do to you. After asking around, I learned that the sect holds a grudge with the gentleman. I decided to teach them a lesson. Who knew that there would be an immortal in residence at the sect?! He inflicted most of the wounds that you see.”","“You destroyed the Nineheavens Pagoda?” Lu Yun blinked.","“Yes,” Gui Xie sighed. “Although I turned you down that day, I am not an ungrateful person. The method you taught me is unmatched and unrivaled, I must return the favor.”","“You’ve gone to quite a great deal of trouble,” Lu Yun sighed inwardly. Gui Xie... was a man after his own heart.","“Peng Yue was an old friend of mine, I once saved his life in the Barren Mountains. I didn’t think he’d kick me when I was down and covet my upper dao rank weapon! He ambushed me and injured me deeply. Thank goodness I ran into you here.” Gui Xie’s expression was unpleasant and goodwill continuously bubbled from him to be absorbed by the Seal of the Multitude.","“So he’s a complete ingrate.” Lu Yun lifted his head to see Kong Mengqian sent flying by another sword stroke. She was on the losing side now. “It looks like I need to teach my new disciple how to fight at some point. Time to help!”","He rushed upward with Immortals Forbidden. Gui Xie had mostly recovered through the aid of Lu Yun’s pill. He, too, waved his flag and shot upward.","Whoosh!","Lu Yun manifested a person next to him with a wave of his hand—his talisman puppet, Lu Yi. The puppet wielded a lower spirit rank sword and brought it down on Peng Yue’s head. The latter quickly dismissed the combat art he was about to deploy and defensively raised his sword in front of him.","At the same time, Gui Xie unfurled the Cosmic Flag and called starlight to him. They condensed into an enormous silver curtain that churned toward Peng Yue.","“Idiot! Don’t rely on the treasure’s innate strength. You need to combine it with your own methods!” Lu Yun couldn’t help but lecture when he saw Gui Xie propel the flag with his true origin.","“Heh heh heh,” Peng Yue cackled. “What does a cultivator from a low ranked world of cultivation know about combining treasure and dao methods? Illusory Dust!”","His lower dao rank weapon flared at his shout and struck downward with a dozen rays of sword light. They raced with plumes of smoke and light, obliterating Lu Yun’s talisman puppet. Peng Yue then ripped through Gui Xie’s curtain of light with another blow.","Gui Xie trembled and stumbled backward.","“Who would’ve thought that you’d recover so quickly, Gui Xie! Looks like there’s a few more treasures yet on this kid...” Peng Yue leered and threw out his flying sword. It exploded into thousands of tiny rays of sword light in the air and arced down at Lu Yun and the others.","“Ten suns in the sky, set fire to the heavens to cook the seas!” Kong Mengqian roared and threw out her pot. It expanded into a massive pot several dozen meters across and hovered protectively over the trio.","She then threw out a blossom of blue flames. They turned into a miniature blue sun that emitted with baleful heat waves. The heat melted the incoming rays of sword light."]},{"number":2293,"title":"Chapter 2293: Chapter 2195.2: Nineheavens Brahman Fire","paragraphs":["Chapter 2195.2: Nineheavens Brahman Fire","The Ten Suns Brahman Fire Incantation!","It was a powerful fire dao method that brought unparalleled might to bear when based off the Fire of Heaven and Earth. Kong Mengqian’s version summoned only one sun. If she could manage all ten, Peng Yu would be vaporized within a split second.","“The Fire of Heaven and Earth!” Peng Yue’s eyes widened before vicious greed swiftly filled them. “Die!”","He waved the sword radiance filling the sky into one ray and called his weapon back to his hand. The man bit through the tip of his tongue, spitting out blood essence and summoning a flare of sword light that was three hundred meters tall.","“Word Slayer, Break!”","Kaboom!","The sword light bit ruthlessly into the blue sun bearing down on Peng Yue. A massive explosion sounded as the man smashed into the ground and Kong Mengqian’s face drained of blood. She’d just reached latter soul separation and consolidated her cultivation through the fight with Peng Yue. That was how she barely managed to bring the Ten Suns Brahman Fire Incantation to bear.","Lu Yun flew out from his circle of safety beneath the mid dao rank pot and hovered in the air, sending hand seals into the void.","Whoosh!","Three breaths later, everything within five kilometers burst into flames. Roiling heat waves melted nearby rocks and soil into lava, creating streams of lava that ran in all directions.","“The Nineheavens Brahman Formation! How is this possible?!” Peng Yue was finally afraid. He stood a chance of escape with the earlier incantation, but this formation would result in nothing but death.","The Nineheavens Brahman Formation was a ninth rank slaughter formation. He would not escape from it if the formation wasn’t broken.","Lu Yun had surreptitiously inserted the formation disk beneath the ground when he spoke with Gui Xie and quietly set up the formation. It wasn’t until Peng Yue collided with the Ten Suns Brahman Fire Incantation that he activated it.","Peng Yue was a combination cultivator. If Lu Yun operated the formation ahead of time, the man would’ve easily detected the energy ripples from the array. He would’ve made his getaway before the formation was fully active.","And now, the Nineheavens Brahman Formation operated in full.","Lu Yun’s hands flew through hand seals as Hongmeng qi surged out of his body into the formation disk. Hidden in the void, the disk spun furiously while scarlet dragons of Brahman fire ripped through everything they saw.","Riding on his sword, Peng Yue darted left and right, unable to break through no matter what he tried. He couldn’t understand why a horrific ninth rank formation had suddenly appeared here! Thankfully, the cultivator in charge of it was only nascent soul.","If a soul separation powerhouse directed it, he would be ashes long ago.","“Gui Xie, let’s talk! It’s all my fault and I’m willing to pay you reparations. Please spare me!” Peng Yue smashed through a fire dragon that was thirty meters long, but the terrifying fire had already darted into his body. He had no choice but to scream for mercy.","“Spare you? Did you spare me earlier?!” Gui Xie jerked out of his shock.","Lu Yun couldn’t be bothered with Peng Yue. He manifested a lower rank spirit crystal with a flip of his hand and absorbed all of its energy, leaving not a shard behind.","BOOM!","Nine dragons combined into a massive one three hundred meters long while the formation flared with power. It pounced on Peng Yue.","“You can’t kill me! I’m a disciple of Wuxi Mountain! All of Jade Ruins Realm will burn if I die!” Peng Yue shrieked with panic. He might’ve been able to break the formation had he been at full strength, but he was at the end of his rope after fighting Kong Mengqian and enduring the Nineheavens Brahman Formation.","Bam!","Lu Yun didn’t give him a chance; he pointed his fingers and commanded the dragon to swallow the latter combination powerhouse. A gout of Brahman fire incinerated a meter tall nascent soul just as it showed itself.","“Wuxi Mountain...” Kong Mengqian repeated hesitantly. She took out a healing pill from her storage ring and swallowed it.","“Do you know what it is?” Lu Yun dismissed the formation and spent a few moments regaining his footing.","The girl shook her head without an answer.","It looks like this disciple of mine doesn’t listen that well yet. I’ll have to teach her in the future. Lu Yun put the formation disk back in the sword pagoda and took a pill himself. Being mid nascent soul, he’d suffered backlash from forcefully operating the formation. Fire poison was attacking his heart and he slowly refined it within after taking the pill.","He could’ve used connate fire origin against it if the poison wasn’t in his body. But since it was, he didn’t dare conduct fire origin into himself. Slowly refining it was the only way.","When Gui Xie saw that both Lu Yun and Kong Mengqian were deep in meditation to recover, he casually set up a miniature maze formation of the five elements around them. At the same time, he was deeply astonished that a latter combination powerhouse had died to nascent soul and soul separation cultivators. No one would believe this if word got out!","He’d yet to fully digest the effects of Lu Yun’s pill, so he also sat down cross-legged and continued to refine the medicine within.","......","Whoosh whoosh whoosh!","Three rays of sword light cut through the sky after twenty minutes and stopped where the battle had taken place.","“This... is...” A middle-aged man with a long beard gaped at the intersecting fissures on the ground. “This is the presence of the Nineheavens Brahman Formation. Didn’t a young man in blue take such a formation disk from the Immortal Gazer? Can it be...”","“There’s more than that here, there’s also the lingering presence of a dao weapon... look over there!” A middle-aged man in long red robes pointed at the ground. “Is that the dao weapon??”","“Let’s take a look!” the third man hastily concurred.","Lu Yun left Peng Yue’s lower dao rank flying sword and storage ring on the ground after killing the man. Since he hadn’t been in a hurry to collect it, the three travelers came across it.","“Piss off!” came a cold snort from the void.","The three paused and froze in the air.","“Who is it?!” Long Beard frowned. “Us brothers are the bodyguards of Prince Sui. We would request that you show yourself.”","“Prince Sui? Is that supposed to be something?” Gui Xie harrumphed. “Since you won’t piss off, then you can stay.”","A large hand broke through the void to grab the three.","“A combination powerhouse!” The three panicked and only had time to crush a jade slip before the hand swatted them out of existence.","“Are they really Prince Sui’s bodyguards?” Lu Yun asked slowly as he opened his eyes on the three storage rings that Gui Xie offered up.","Prince Sui was a legendary character in Dark Orchid as well as nearby third and fourth rank empires. He was essentially the faith of the Dark Orchid citizens. It wasn’t the royal family who wielded the greatest authority in the nation, but Prince Sui. Rumor had it that he was the disciple of an immortal!","“They should be.” Gui Xie nodded at the three “Sui” medallions from the storage rings.","“Is this Prince Sui someone important?” Kong Mengqian’s injuries were mostly healed.","“At the very least, he’s someone I can’t offend,” Gui Xie chuckled.","“It looks like he’s nearby, we should go.” Lu Yun rose and turned to Gui Xie. “What are your plans?”","“I was going to destroy the Nineheavens Pagoda first and then head to Darklake to join you.”","“Then come with me,” Lu Yun nodded.","Gui Xie was Empress Myrtlestar’s heir and possessed unbounded potential. He would be a great help and a peerless expert with some pointers.","“Gui Xie thanks the gentleman for your succor!”","......","The northern side of Fallen Leaf Mountain stretched for thousands of kilometers and was off limits to immortals. Lu Yun blithely walked in with Kong Mengqian and Gui Xie because the Hongmeng Tree was asleep. All was even more quiet than before in the formation of illusion.","Having just arrived in Jade Ruins Realm, Kong Mengqian was unfamiliar with the situation.Meanwhile, Gui Xie was a latter combination powerhouse and wasn’t the least bit phased by the forbidden zone.","Instead of heading to the tree, Lu Yun wandered through the formation and picked a few spirit herbs. He stopped only when all of his storage rings were full and a small heap was piled in the sword pagoda. Since there was a lower rank spirit vein inside, he didn’t need to worry about the spirit herbs losing their potency.","Although Lu Yun picked only low ranked spirit herbs, Kong Mengqian conscientiously followed in the young man’s steps. She was familiar with her master’s methods and how he could create nearly immortal fare with some first rank spirit herbs. She never dared underestimate them again.","“Alright, there’s something I must do, so you two go to the Lu Clan in Dark City and wait for me there.” Lu Yun addressed the two after they left the taboo area.","“Then please be careful, sir. Miss Kong and I will return first.” Gui Xie knew how mysterious Lu Yun was, so he didn’t ask further. As reluctant as Kong Mengqian was to obey, she had no choice.","After they left, Lu Yun raised sword light and flew to the south of Fallen Leaf Mountain. His destination was Jade Ice Lake.","The lake had become the mountain’s greatest taboo as a terrifying gray jiao lived inside. No one dared approach within five kilometers of the waters.","Lu Yun didn’t linger after he reached the lake, but plunged straight in. The black snakes of the lake were sentient and recognized Lu Yun. Thus, they didn’t obstruct him. Some even swam by to greet him.","He generously tossed them some of the pills he’d refined and fully won them over to his side. The last time he’d been here, he was golden core. Now he was mid nascent soul and impervious to the arctic temperatures of the water.","He still didn’t see the bottom of the lake after diving two hundred and fifty kilometers, but he saw the gray jiao’s nest."]},{"number":2294,"title":"Chapter 2294: Chapter 2196.1: Forge of Heaven and Earth","paragraphs":["Chapter 2196.1: Forge of Heaven and Earth","Jade Ice Lake was shaped like a water drop—narrow at the top, wide at the bottom. An enormous cavern was located two hundred and fifty kilometers beneath the surface. It was where the gray jiao called home.","It sensed Lu Yun’s arrival and poked its massive head out of the hole, nodding and looking quizzically at the young man.","“Senior!” Lu Yun quickly descended to a standing position in front of the jiao and raised a cupped fist salute. “This junior has come to invite the senior into the world.”","He cut straight to the chase as the situation in the Jade Ruins Realm was much more complicated than what he thought. Despite how strong Terra Demon was, there was only one of him. Thus, Lu Yun came for the gray jiao.","Immortal Burial Valley, the Hongmeng Tree, the massive formation of illusion that spanned thousands of kilometers, and the personages within Fallen Leaf City all pointed to Jade Ruins Realm being more than an ordinary world of cultivation. There were far too many secrets within this world.","As the Lu Clan had laid down its foundations in Dark City, it had no say in being dragged into this vortex. In that vein, Lu Yun sought to gather all the power he could.","“Roar!” The gray jiao heard Lu Yun out with confusion. It looked back at the cave, where a pale-golden dragon egg rested in the center.","“I’m sure the senior knows as well that the Jade Ruins Realm is about to fall to disorder. Countless immortals will be arriving shortly. You will not be safe with your heavily injured self in Jade Ice Lake.” Lu Yun naturally understood that the jiao was unwilling to leave the place it’d resided for an indeterminate period of time.","The divine beast fell silent and a thoughtful expression appeared in the depths of its scarlet eyes.","“Does senior not trust junior’s strength?” Lu Yun asked slowly. “Will senior take a look at my current cultivation level?”","The confused gray jiao subconsciously glanced at the young man. Its eyes went round with astonishment. The human male had been a golden core cultivator half a month ago, but was now mid nascent soul and his foundations were secure! There were no signs of instability or uncertainty.","“Do you recognize this, senior?” Lu Yun brought out a golden fruit the size of a fist.","“Roar!!” The gray jiao trembled with astonishment. Lu Yun’s increase in cultivation could be attributed to a fortuitous encounter, but the golden fruit was truly staggering. This was a Hongmeng Fruit!","Others might not know where Hongmeng Fruit came from, but the gray jiao had resided in Jade Ice Lake for an incredible period of time. Of course it knew where the fruit could be found. A terrible Hongmeng Tree lived in the depths of Fallen Leaf Mountain. It’d thrown a massive fit half a month ago, for which the jiao finally had an answer today.","“This is for you, senior.” Lu Yun tossed the fruit over. The jiao opened its mouth and swallowed it, keeping it for later usage.","“Roar!” It nodded at the young man and returned to the cave, likewise storing the golden egg in its stomach. It turned into a mini gray jiao one meter long and draped around Lu Yun’s shoulders.","A trace of a smile appeared on the young man’s face. He looked toward the pitch-black depths of the lake and shoved down his curiosity. Turning, he shot for the surface.","For some reason, the bottom of the lake made his heart quail. He somehow felt that there was a terrifying creature at its bottom.","“Or... der...” The gray jiao coiled around his left shoulder suddenly voiced two syllables.","“Hmm?” Lu Yun looked curiously at it. The jiao remained silent—it was exceedingly difficult just to pronounce those two syllables.","“Order?” Something bombarded Lu Yun’s mind and the seals of three thousand lifetimes almost loosened.","He didn’t linger after exiting Jade Ice Lake, instead raising sword light to return to Darklake. He was more than ten times stronger than when he first came. Therefore, his flight speed back was more than one hundred times faster than before. It took him only seven days to cross Darklake and arrive in Dark City.","The rules imposed by the heavenly book grew ever weaker. It would fully vanish in less than a month and no longer affect the realm. By then, Jade Ruins Realm would be engulfed with confusion.","Lu Yun quietly returned home, raising no attention at all. Of course, no one noticed as he’d said he was entering closed door cultivation when he left. He emerged back in public view at the same spot.","......","Terra Demon approached him as soon as Lu Yun returned to the clan residence.","“Young master!” He was briefly taken aback by the gray jiao on the young man’s shoulder, but quickly set it aside.","Lu Yun was good friends with the dragons and jiao when in the world of immortals. After the ten-winged chaos jiao died, he sheltered both races. Thus, it was no surprise that a pureblood jiao had appeared with the young master.","The gray jiao lifted its head and nodded at Terra Demon, shared sympathy in its gaze. Given its uncommon background, it could read some of the man’s personal details.","Terra Demon couldn’t resist an eye roll. Who has anything in common with you?! I’m very satisfied under His Majesty’s command! But it’s also your good fortune that you can find shelter with His Majesty!","“Has anything major happened lately?” Lu Yun sat at the stone table in the yard. Lan’er was already asleep as it was late at night.","“A true immortal has arrived in the Yuwen Clan,” Terra Demon replied somewhat solemnly. He was peak soul projection, but could at most withstand empyrean immortals. True immortals were stronger than empyrean immortals and thus more than he could handle.","Although he possessed the nascent soul of an immortal king, it was so heavily damaged that it wasn’t even a hundred millionth of his strength in his prime.","“True immortal eh... That’s a bit troublesome.” A golden fruit appeared in Lu Yun’s hand. “This is Hongmeng Fruit, hurry and refine it.”","“Thank you, sir!” Terra Demon was overjoyed.","Sixth of the ten heavenly treasures, Hongmeng Fruit entailed the meaning of immortal overlords. It was exceedingly useful for helping dao immortals and immortal overlords walk the path of cultivation.","Terra Demon was once an immortal overlord, but his nascent soul was shattered and his comprehension of that profound meaning nearly dispersed. Thus, the Hongmeng Fruit was of critical importance to him.","He quickly received the fruit and carefully put it away in a storage ring. The High Lord of the Northern Sky is who he is, alright! He is able to find such a heaven-defying treasure as the Hongmeng Fruit even when wandering among a low level cultivation world!","“We need to get rid of the true immortal at the Yuwens before the heavenly book fully loses power. Refine the Hongmeng Fruit and we head out to kill that true immortal after three days!” A sharp light flashed through Lu Yun’s eyes.","The heavenly book’s hold over the Jade Ruins Realm would vanish after a month, leaving immortals free to do whatever they wished. That would be the perfect time for the Origin Sect to move against the Lu Clan.","Therefore, he needed to make use of this month to fully consolidate his hold over the capital. All unstable factors had to be expelled. The true immortal likely wanted to eliminate the entire family in traveling to Dark City at this time, but little did he know of Terra Demon’s capabilities. The nascent soul of an immortal king detected his presence the moment he arrived!","The heavenly book was still nominally in effect at the moment, preventing him from doing too much. If he set a toe out of line, he would be punished by the treasure.","“The Yuwens have banded together with the Zhao, Yu, and remnants of the Ling Clan to fully suppress us. We would truly be in danger if it wasn’t for the Trading Company of the Four Seas supporting us from the shadows,” Terra Demon sighed. A true immortal arriving in the capital forced him to set aside quite a few of his plans. It wasn’t that he was afraid, but that too much came into play when an immortal fought. Everything within five hundred kilometers would be leveled and the capital reduced to rubble.","Terra Demon had refrained from action due to concern for the innocent. On the other hand, the Mo Clan... had vanished after withdrawing from Darklake Empire three months ago.","“The Trading Company of the Four Seas?” Lu Yun blinked.","Terra Demon nodded. “They say that their young lord is friends with the young master, so they’re here with their young lord’s orders to help.”","“It’s him...” Lu Yun’s thoughts turned to the unseeing boy with a Red Spider Lily in his hands, always perfectly pristine from the world. He hadn’t minded that Lu Yun had kicked in his trading company’s doors and nearly stomped it to the ground.","“I see.” Lu Yun nodded. “The Trading Company of the Four Seas is no small entity. They’re probably helping us because of Fengxian Wu.”","Terra Demon understood. So that was why the trading company spared no effort in helping the Lu Clan. If it wasn’t for them, the family would’ve collapsed a while ago. And no matter how Terra Demon swept their actions with his consciousness, he never found them doing anything untoward.","“Ah, young master, there’s another thing that has to do with your two friends,” Terra Demon mentioned after some thought. “Before the Yuwen, Yu, and Zhao Clans moved against us, your friends Zhao Chenguang and Yu Shuai came to notify us. The Yuwens caught them and are holding them captive.”","“I see.” Lu Yun’s expression was calm. He sniffed a conspiracy.","Yu Shuai and Zhao Chenguang had come in secret, but were captured by the Yuwens instead? How had they come up with such a flimsy excuse?","Yu Shuai and Zhao Chenguang were nearly forgotten members of their families. Although they were the sons of the patriarch, their potential was poor and they weren’t valued in the slightest. How would they possibly know about an operation as crucial as moving against the Lus?","Confining the two was likely the next step in the plan against the Lu Clan. They were up to their old tricks of using the good-for-nothing Lu Yun!"]},{"number":2295,"title":"Chapter 2295: Chapter 2196.2: Forge of Heaven and Earth","paragraphs":["Chapter 2196.2: Forge of Heaven and Earth","The Origin Sect took no further action against him after he killed their soul separation cultivator. They must have grown wary and sent a true immortal this time in a bid for caution.","Terra Demon gave an overview of everything that’d recently happened in the capital before leaving. After Lu Yun recollected himself, he headed for the family’s secret vault.","......","The Lu young master had modified the secret vault to be based on talismans of the connate five elements as well as a massive seed storage formation. Previously thirty meters across, the vault was now a massive space roughly half a kilometer wide. Large qi accumulation formations abounded within, creating an ambient concentration of energy so intense that it was ten times denser than Fallen Leaf or Ashflame City.","The gray jiao swam down from Lu Yun’s shoulder and circled through the area, immensely satisfied with the place. Meanwhile, the young man took out one specimen from all of the spirit herbs in his storage ring and planted them in the vault.","“Skynet Stone, Frostmoon Ice, Essence of Copper, Silverscar, Purplenight Gold, Transformed Spirit Grass, Waternet Root...” After completing this task, he took out another set of ingredients and placed them in front of him. A summoned ball of connate li fire melted them all.","The gray jiao located a tiny pond made from a talisman of connate kui water and spat out the meter-tall golden dragon egg. It coiled over it and stuck its head out of the water, looking at Lu Yun’s actions with curiosity.","His cultivation level was much higher than when he refined the Dragon Transformation Grass and his command over connate li fire and other ingredients was much more proficient. Golden light sparkled in his eyes as his fingers fluttered through hand seals. The seals melded into the liquid of ingredients and distilled what was useful from them.","The gray jiao’s eyes went wide when it saw the flames in Lu Yun’s hands. Connate li fire! A young man of nascent soul cultivation could casually summon this connate flame! Not even the most preeminent chaos immortals could manage the deed.","While the flame in Lu Yun’s hand was exceedingly weak, it was connate li fire without a doubt.","The jiao nodded to itself—it hadn’t followed the wrong human. Perhaps this young man really could help it recover and take another step forward.","The ingredients gradually merged together in the void and a faint smear of silver floated out of the bundle. Proxima Metal was about to take shape, but here, Lu Yun hesitated.","“Proxima Metal is the key ingredient for a cross forge, but other materials are needed to refine the forge as well. While I have a broken cross ark in hand...” Lu Yun’s hand seals suddenly changed and rays of blue, red, white, black, and yellow light gathered from the void.","These were the pure connate five elements and they immediately fused into the solidifying ingredients. The hint of silver instantly vanished—the connate five elements were the guiding force of these materials now.","“Too much connate metal origin, out!” Lu Yun threw out a ball of golden energy.","“Needs more connote fire origin, come!” He grabbed in the southern direction and threw a ball of connate fire origin into the materials.","“Connate water and wood origin need to be increased! That’s enough connate wood origin!”","His hand seals were now the movements of treasure refinement. He was going to refine the core origin of Proxima Metal and the connate five elements into a cross forge.","......","Humm!","Rumble!","A soft rumble sounded overhead as a red cauldron with simplistic design appeared in front of Lu Yun. It billowed with a vast presence. Although it was only one meter tall, there was astounding capacity inside. It ran six hundred meters from end to end.","Lu Yun didn’t add a seed storage formation; the cauldron had somehow given rise to something similar itself. He looked at it with clarity in his eyes.","“The connate five elements are the foundation of this world’s core origin. When they come together to form the same space, it manifests the rules of heaven and earth. The rules then manifest light, shadow, wind, thunder, time, life, and ultimately the world...”","Thunder and lightning roared within the cauldron, a byproduct of the five elements.","“To think that this world would be like this... It seems to be different from the world of my memories, but reaches the same goal through different means.","“The nothing...” Lu Yun’s spontaneous comprehension of this world propelled his mentality to soul separation. His actual cultivation remained at peak nascent soul.","“Heh heh heh, a cross forge? Let’s call this the Forge of Heaven and Earth.”","Albeit named differently, it functioned the same as a cross forge, but was many times more powerful than a regular forge. The heart of a cross ark’s propulsion system, this forge was bigger than some of the larger cross arks.","Lu Yun took out a lower rank crystal after he put the forge away and held it in his hand, slowly absorbing and refining it to replenish his Hongmeng qi.","......","The gray jiao settled down in the Lu secret vault. It focused on hatching the dragon egg while also recovering from its injuries. If there was anything Lu Yun needed from it, the jiao wouldn’t hesitate to help.","It was morning the next day when he left the secret vault.","“Grandpa, you’re already an awakened powerhouse??” Lu Yun jumped with shock when he saw Lu Tianling.","Lu Tianling was equally startled. He kept a heaven-defying treasure on him that enabled him to conceal his cultivation. Even the heavenly book could see through it, but his little grandson had identified his true cultivation with one glance.","“You...” Lu Tianling’s jaw dropped as he didn’t know what to say.","“Heh, don’t worry grandpa. There is none other than your grandson who can see through your true cultivation,” Lu Yun chuckled.","“Oh you! Eh, wait, when did you form your nascent soul and reach mid nascent soul??” Lu Tianling was about to respond when he took note of Lu Yun’s cultivation and was shocked out of his intended topic.","A seventeen year old nascent soul cultivator?! He’d been delighted for several years when Lu Xiaochi formed his at thirty! His grandson had exceeded the master by so much that they weren’t in the same plane of existence!","Genius?","The so-called three gentlemen of Dark City would seek immediate reincarnation into their next lives if they were compared to his grandson! There weren’t that many seventeen-year-old nascent soul cultivators in Great Xia either.","Besides, what kind of place was Great Xia? It possessed an abundance of qi and precious treasures—it wasn’t surprising for there to be teenage nascent out cultivators.","Yet Lu Yun had grown up in a third rank cultivation empire and still formed his as a teenager. What was this if not heaven defying?? And he’d only been foundation establishment a year ago!","“Hahahaha!! A seventeen year old nascent soul cultivator! My grandson coalesced his nascent soul at seventeen years old! HAHAHAHA!!” Lu Tianling threw his head back with laughter, laughing so hard that he flushed beet red. Being an awakened powerhouse, he could naturally see that Lu Yun’s cultivation was completely stable.","“But haven’t you seen my disciple, grandpa?” Lu Yun asked curiously to see his grandfather so excited.","“Disciple?” Lu Tianling tried to set aside his agitation.","“Haven’t Gui Xie and Kong Mengqian come home?” Lu Yun frowned.","“Milord, bad news! ...young master?” A flustered He Wuheng ran in and paused when he saw Lu Yun. “You’re back, young master? Wonderful!”","“What is it? What’s going on?” Lu Tianling frowned.","“In response to milord, the Yuwens beat up the second master moments ago and Senior Bloodbath went to save him. He was also gravely injured and they’re both held captive.” He Wuheng glanced at Lu Yun and continued solemnly, “The Yuwens say we must pay five hundred million upper rank spirit stones in three days to ransom them, or else...”","“Or else what?” A threatening glint appeared in Lu Yun's eyes.","“Or else Senior Bloodbath and the second master will not live after three days.”","“What is going on here?” Lu Tianling took a deep breath.","“Someone came to cause trouble at our trading company this morning, so the second master went to handle it. However, someone beat him up for it. The one who injured the second master and Senior Bloodbath is a latter nascent soul cultivator,” He Wuheng said slowly.","“I understand now, leave this to me,” Lu Yun sighed. “If there’s a single hair missing from second uncle or Senior Blood’s head, I’ll exterminate the Yuwen bloodline from this world.”","A tyrannical air bloomed from his body while Lu Tianling wordlessly opened and shut his mouth.","“Ai, I’ve gotten old, so I leave the matters of the family to you guys!” He looked at his grandson with gratification.","“Don’t worry, grandpa. The Origin Sect will fall and the Lu Clan will surpass Great Xia,” Lu Yun said calmly.","“You...” Lu Tianling stared at Lu Yun, unable to find words for a proper response.","“Be at ease, grandpa, I’m not a child anymore. I learned of certain things long ago.”","“Good, good, wonderful! You’ve finally grown up, Yun’er!” Lu Tianling laughed with joy.","......","The Yuwen trading company was now the biggest in Darklake Empire. It monopolized more than seventy percent of the empire’s business. It’d acquired numerous training companies throughout the nation—whether by money or force.","Only the Lu trading company could stand up to them now. The Ouyang Clan had long become a Lu vassal.","The Yuwen headquarters stood in the middle of the most prosperous southern quadrant of the capital. This was Darklake’s hub of commerce.","Two enormous flags were raised in front of their headquarters and two people hung from it. Drenched in blood, they had more bones broken than anyone could imagine. Tormented to within an inch of their lives, they barely looked human.","It was Lu Xiaochi and Bloodbath."]},{"number":2296,"title":"Chapter 2296: Chapter 2197.1: Empyrean Immortal","paragraphs":["Chapter 2197.1: Empyrean Immortal","“The Lus lord it over everyone simply because they’re a big store! They sell trash pills and also bully and insult their customers! That’s why I personally took these two down and hang them before the public. But since they’re Marshal Lu Tianling’s foster son and follower, I won’t do anything to them. I will release them as soon as the Lu reparations arrive.”","A young man of twenty-four years old stood beneath the flagpoles. He wore long turquoise robes and a gentle smile on his face. White teeth gleamed out of red lips.","Cultivators gathered to whisper and point at the two dangling men.","“General Lu Xiaochi is an honest and upright man who accomplished many great deeds for Darklake! He is highly revered by the people and not someone a brat like you can insult!” A golden core cultivator in yellow robes couldn’t bear the sight. He flew up to release Lu Xiaochi when—","Whoosh!","Sword light flashed by and pulverized his dantian. He drifted weakly to the ground, staring incredulously at the young man in turquoise.","“You...”","“A Lu sycophant?” The young man curled his lip. “What a crude excuse. Everyone saw what happened in the Lu storefront earlier. Lu Xiaochi, honest and upright? How do you not know he’s a hypocrite who plays the act well?”","The crowd took a collective step back after seeing the young man cripple a golden core cultivator with one move. No one dared stick their necks out.","“A crude excuse? Well said.” The crowd gave way to a young man in long white robes. Waving a folded fan, he strolled out of the assembly. The corner of his eye twitched when he saw the dangling men, but he refrained from brashly leaping into action.","“What do the matters of a Lu establishment have to do with the Yuwens?” Lu Yun sneered.","“I couldn’t stand the injustice and simply acted for what is good and proper.” The young man didn’t think anything of Lu Yun.","“Then why does the Lu Clan need to pay compensation to the Yuwen trading company?” Lu Yun pressed.","“Because the customer that your family oppressed is now recuperating in my business.” The young man finally realized that the young man in white should be a Lu family member.","Yuwen Zhuifeng had departed from home at a young age due to a powerhouse accepting him as a disciple. He was here paying a home visit with his master, so he wasn’t fully aware of certain Darklake matters.","“Have them come out here then, and release my second uncle and Senior Blood.” Lu Yun’s lips stretched in a familiar smile. If Long Aotian was here, she’d immediately know that blood was about to flow.","“Heh heh heh heh heh,” Yuwen Zhuifeng chuckled. “So you’re the prodigal son of the Lu Clan. What, you’re used to bullying others through superior force and now think the Yuwen Clan is an easy target after you’ve destroyed the Ouyangs?”","He changed the subject, refraining from further discussing the customer.","“You’re right, I love bullying others through superior force and numbers. That’s what I’m going to do to your family today, what of it?” Lu Yun pushed off his feet and reached Bloodbath and Lu Xiaochi before anyone realized what the young man intended. He swiftly released them and threw the two flagpoles at the Yuwen trading company building, destroying its formations.","“Here I am, bullying you. What you gonna do about it?” Lu Yun tossed two healing pills into the men’s mouth and checked their wounds.","“You...” Yuwen Zhuifeng scowled, on guard as he hadn’t seen how Lu Yun managed the string of actions. He was also livid that the Lu young master had stabbed the flagpoles into his family’s business headquarters.","“Be careful, he has people ambushing his opponents for him.” Bloodbath sat down cross-legged when he slightly recovered.","“I know,” Lu Yun nodded. Lu Xiaochi likewise caught his breath and glanced at his nephew.","“Be careful.”","Whether it was Lu Xiaochi or Bloodbath, both knew that with Lu Yun’s personality, today’s matter could not be resolved in a peaceful way. The young man wouldn’t stop until he killed the person in front of them and razed the Yuwen trading company.","“What about me?” Lu Yun stepped forward. “We Lus love lording it over people and love bullying others. So what? You want reparations from us? I can consider burning some paper money for you after you die.”","Logic and reason? He wasn’t in the practice of dealing with that. Lu Yun couldn’t be bothered to play along with the other’s sanctimonious act. Anyone could tell that it was the Yuwens framing the Lus here.","“You court death—” Yuwen Zhuifeng was about to launch into a speech when he saw Lu Yun ball his fists up and charge. He hastily swallowed the rest of his remarks and raised his hand, meeting the Lu young master in his advance.","Bam!","Lu Yun was so fast that Yuwen Zhuifeng felt his eye socket ache when his hand was halfway up to his face. He suddenly felt lighter on his feet and flew backward, smashing into the Yuwen trading building.","The structure’s formations were already broken and the two flagpoles pierced through the building foundation. The entire structure collapsed after Yuwen Zhuifeng was thrown into it. Whatever customers and staff were inside came out moaning with agony.","“What is the meaning of this?!” A middle-aged man with a dignified air rushed out of the ruined building and leveled a vicious glare at Lu Yun.","“Heh heh, weren’t you hiding inside and peeking the entire time? What’s the meaning of coming out only now?” Lu Yun showed a complete lack of respect. “But since you ask, I’ll let you know that today, I’m here to loot and kill!”","The young man grinned brilliantly, but the look in his eyes was extraordinarily cold.","No one in the crowd lingered when they saw the pestilence of Dark City in fine fettle. Cultivators scattered in every direction, despite not understanding why Lu Yun’s cultivation level was suddenly so high. Regardless, the young man in front of them was indeed the good-for-nothing of the Lu Clan.","Lu Yun didn’t wait for the Yuwen nascent soul cultivator to reply—he flew forward and stepped on the man’s head, grinding his head into his body.","What a pity that this nascent soul powerhouse, a domineering heavyweight in Darklake, died ignobly to a single stomp from the Lu young master. The nascent soul of cultivators at this level could not leave their body, so death of the physical body meant death of the person.","“Father!!” Yuwen Zhuifeng screamed when he crawled out of the rubble to see Lu Yun kill that member of his family. He flung himself at the young man. “You will die for this!!”","A jade-green greatbow appeared in his hand, one without a bowstring. The young man raised the weapon and came howling for Lu Yun’s head.","“So that was your old man?” Lu Yun chortled and commanded a flare of light from Immortals Forbidden, slashing it at his opponent.","Bam!","A bow and sword crashed in the air. Lu Yun’s hands went numb from the impact and it was his turn to fly out.","“DIE!!” Yuwen Zhuifeng stood where the Lu young master had been and shifted like he was drawing back on the bow. Surprisingly enough, a string of pale-gold light actually appeared on the greatbow!","All wood energy within five kilometers surged toward them and formed a jade-green arrow of light on the bow within half a breath.","Twang!","The bowstring vibrated, sending the jade-green arrow sailing across the horizon.","Thud!","It pierced Lu Yun through, much to Bloodbath and Lu Xiaochi’s dismay.","“Yun’er!”","“Young master!”","Moments away from throwing themselves forward, the two jerked to a stop when they saw the young man flip around and land gently on the ground.","“A fine rank weapon that uses the connate five elements?” The Lu young master licked his lips with appreciation. “My World Tree happens to lack fertilizer as connate wood origin is too much for it. The sapling is too small to digest that level of energy, but pure connate wood is perfect!”","He could’ve easily dodged the arrow if he wanted to, but just when it was about to touch him, he noted a shift in the World Tree rooted in his dantian. It redirected the arrow of light to it and swallowed the projectile.","“Yo, your arrow is as floppy as a noodle. There was no strength behind it! I’ll stand right here and be your target. See if you can shoot me down!” Lu Yun crossed his arms and sniffed dismissively at his opponent.","“You!” Yuwen Zhuifeng was well aware of the greatbow’s power. He’d once used it to heavily injure a soul separation powerhouse!","Being no fool, he could tell that Lu Yun carried an incredible defensive treasure since the arrow had failed to harm him. It negated the greatbow’s might, so he put it back in his storage ring and unsheathed a flying sword glittering with arctic energy.","“Do you actually think you’re a match for me without that bow?” Lu Yun sneered at the change in weapon. Yuwen Zhuifeng had been able to send him flying solely because of the greatbow. The Yuwen young master wasn’t weak, but he was no match for Lu Yun.","“Hmph!” Yuwen Zhuifeng snorted, sending his true origin into the blade of frost. He brought it down on his opponent’s head.","When Lu Yun raised his right hand this time, however, overwhelming pressure abruptly bore down on him. Even the circulation of his Hongmeng qi was affected.","“So I see.” He stared coldly at the ray of sword light while Hongmeng qi operated furiously in his body. Ordinary true origin would be suppressed by this boundless pressure and be completely locked in place.","But he was no ordinary cultivator and he practiced extraordinary methods. Hongmeng true qi was also more than ten times higher level than ordinary qi. As colossal as this pressure was, it couldn’t do anything to him."]},{"number":2297,"title":"Chapter 2297: Chapter 2197.2: Empyrean Immortal","paragraphs":["Chapter 2197.2: Empyrean Immortal","An ugly smile appeared on Yuwen Zhuifeng’s face while hatred brimmed in his eyes. He’d left home at a young age, leaving behind his parents and family. This had been a long anticipated visit after many, many years of absence and he’d come back to see his father trampled to death right in front of him. How could he bear it?!","He was rage incarnate and wanted nothing more than to swallow Lu Yun alive!","“DIE!”","Magnificent splendor intensified the closer the sword light drew to Lu Yun. But in the next moment, Yuwen Zhuifeng saw the scene clear in front of him. The immobilized young man was suddenly gone.","Pfft!","Yuwen Zhuifeng felt himself rise into the air with a crisp snap, going higher and higher. He caught a hazy glimpse of a body falling forward before his consciousness went black.","Lu Yun kicked the falling head away and rummaged through his opponent’s corpse for the young man’s storage ring and mid spirit rank flying sword.","“Ai, I would’ve needed to expend some effort to kill you, but you relied too much on your backer. Placing your hopes in others ultimately leads to your own downfall instead.”","Yuwen Zhuifeng was quite strong; he was even slightly stronger than Sui Ge. But he trusted the powerhouse behind the pressure too much and didn’t expect that Lu Yun would suddenly strike back. That was how the Lu young master killed him with one stroke.","“You! You killed Feng’er!” A terrifying aura washed over the scene as an elder with a white beard wearing long black robes appeared in front of Lu Yun. He frostily regarded the Lu young master.","“You’re that guy’s master?” Golden light flashed through the young man’s eyes. The old man was an empyrean immortal!","To think that there would be more than a true immortal in Dark City! He looked to have come last night, after Terra Demon entered seclusion to refine the Hongmeng Fruit. Hence, the latter failed to detect this immortal’s arrival.","“I’m right here, you can take revenge for your disciple now.” Lu Yun proudly lifted his chin.","The empyrean immortal was taken aback at how devil-may-care Lu Yun was. Shouldn’t any cultivator be terrified at the sight of an immortal? Hence, he quickly thought of something else.","“I am an empyrean immortal of Jade Ruins Realm. Although the heavenly book suppresses my cultivation, it will not do anything to me if I truly take action.”","“Then hurry up and get on with it.” Lu Yun curled his lip. “I want to go home for dinner. Or don’t tell me, a lofty empyrean immortal doesn’t dare take revenge after this young master killed your disciple right in front of you?”","An empyrean immortal’s aura was vast and profound. Everyone within five kilometers, including Bloodbath, was pressed to the ground. They didn’t have the strength to lift their heads.","Lu Yun, however, faced the vaunted personage with ease and confidence. He was wholly unconcerned with the pressure from an empyrean immortal, like he faced a mortal instead of someone much more superior to him.","The Jade Ruins Realm was a world of cultivation—a place for cultivators, in other words. The rules as set by the heavenly book meant that any cultivator who ascended to empyrean immortal was restricted by the treasure.","Most chose to leave a world of cultivation after reaching immortality, setting out for Great Xia or other places meant for immortals.","Immortals from other locales were monitored by the heavenly book when they entered the world. Any who dared to cause a disturbance in the Jade Ruins Realm were punished by the treasure. Even immortals originally from the realm were treated as outsiders if they later returned.","Thus, someone calling themselves an immortal of the Jade Ruins Realm meant this was someone who’d never left the world after reaching immortality. In other words, someone who didn’t have the courage to set out for other places.","Empyrean immortals were invincible in a world of cultivation, but they were the lowest of the low in a world of immortals like Great Xia. An empyrean immortal without an illustrious background or patron might die or be enslaved at any time.","Based on this one’s style, Lu Yun could tell that he was a coward who immensely treasured his life. Therefore, the more at ease Lu Yun was, the greater his background and backer potentially was. It would make the immortal incredibly wary.","“You may go upon leaving my disciple’s body and personal effects,” the immortal finally said after his expression flickered through a variety of changes.","“Pfft.” Lu Yun curled his lip and walked up to Lu Xiaochi and Bloodbath, gently caressing their shoulders. Hongmeng qi surged into them and freed them from the immortal’s pressure with a shudder.","“Let me leave you a word of advice,” Lu Yun suddenly turned back. “Leave Dark City as soon as possible. The murky waters here are not for the likes of you.”","He ignored the immortal and left with his people.","......","The Yuwen trading headquarters were a pile of rubble and whatever was left had been collected by the sword pagoda that Lu Yun surreptitiously sent out. He didn’t leave anything behind for the Yuwen Clan.","Yuwen Zhuifeng’s master watched the trio leave, raising his hand a few times and putting it back down. Ultimately, he swept a glance at his late disciple and vanished into the air.","The gray jiao stuck its head out of Lu Yun’s sleeve, disappointment writ large in its eyes. It’d wanted to test its strength against the empyrean immortal!","It was like Terra Demon—foreign to the Jade Ruins Realm. But its nascent soul was strong enough that it forcefully hewed through the heavenly book’s power and forced it back. While the jiao would also be restricted by the book if it wanted to take action in this world, it wouldn’t suffer to the same degree as immortals.","Lu Yun heaved a sigh of relief. While he wasn’t afraid of the immortal, certain trump cards would be exposed if they clashed. It would help his enemy take preemptive action. An ace like the gray jiao rivaling a true immortal was something he wanted to keep secret for as long as possible. It would lose effectiveness as soon as the enemy detected something like that existed.","The cowardly empyrean immortal had plainly been a pawn in the hands of the Yuwen true immortal, sent to test the Lu Clan.","......","“Father, your son has been unfilial and caused you to worry!” When Lu Xiaochi saw Lu Tianling sitting in the main hall after they returned, he immediately fell to his knees.","“Never mind that, you’re all back safe!” A faintly smiling Lu Tianling heaved a long exhale to see all three of them back.","“An empyrean immortal as timid as a mouse was used by the Yuwens this time,” Lu Yun interjected. “He was so cowardly that he didn’t dare do anything to me.”","“An empyrean immortal?” Lu Tianling gasped with surprise.","Even Lu Xiaochi and Bloodbath were shocked as their senses had been obstructed when the empyrean immortal’s aura overwhelmed them. They didn’t begin to recover until they returned to the Lu residence, so they weren’t very clear on what’d taken place.","“No wonder there was such a presence coming from the southern quadrant. An empyrean immortal has come,” Lu Tianling mused over the unwelcome revelation. So immortals were already moving against the family!","“Don’t worry, grandpa, he didn’t do a thing. If he did, I would make sure he’d never twitch a finger ever again.” Lu Yun laughed easily when he saw the expression on Lu Tianling’s face. “Don’t forget whose disciple I am, grandpa. My master won’t agree to an immortal disturbing the peace in the capital. Not to mention, He Shanlian should be arriving in a few days. Who will dare touch us then?”","Lu Tianling relaxed only when he heard the law enforcer’s name—he quickly thought of Terra Demon. Although the Lu patriarch had never seen this personage in action, the unconscious projection of the latter’s aura still made Lu Tianling, an awakened powerhouse, jolt with alarm.","It wasn’t the aura that a cultivator could emanate.","“Master, young master, there’s two people outside. One of them calls themselves your disciple!” A servant quickly rushed in with a bow.","“Let them in!” Lu Yun’s eyes lit up.","“Understood!”","Kong Mengqian and Gui Xie walked in soon after the servant left.","“Young master!” Gui Xie called out respectfully when he saw Lu Yun.","“...master!” Kong Mengqian clenched her teeth and reluctantly performed a grand gesture of greeting.","“Good, good, very good!” Lu Yun understood why they were late when he saw Gui Xie. The man had broken through to tribulation realm! The two were most likely undergoing a tribulation somewhere when they were yet to arrive.","“Yun’er, who are...” Lu Tianling asked with confusion. Who were these people? One was tribulation level and the other latter soul separation.","A sixteen year old soul separation cultivator?","The Lu patriarch felt a distinct lack of sufficient mind capacity for use.","“Gui Xie greets the patriarch. Gui Xie has received great favor from the gentleman and has come to show my gratitude,” Gui Xie said before Lu Yun explained.","While Lu Tianling looked to be latter nascent soul, his vast aura stunned Gui Xie to no end. He didn’t believe that Lu Yun’s grandpa was only a nascent soul cultivator!","“Kong Mengqian greets... the martial great grandfather!” the girl nearly cried. “I am master’s disciple.”","......","The Lu Clan set up a grand banquet to welcome Kong Mengqian and Gui Xie. It was beyond Lu Tianling’s wildest dreams that his grandson had accepted such a young soul separation cultivator! With his ability, he could tell from a single glance that Kong Mengqian must come from a distinguished background. Her identity was even more mysterious than Fengxian Wu’s.","After helping Gui Xie and Kong Mengqian settle in, Lu Yun returned to the secret vault. He took out some paramount rank spirit stones and redecorated the area, then took out the Nineheavens Brahman Formation disk.","“The Nineheavens Brahman Formation... If I etch the runes for the Connate Great Dao of the Five Elements into it and turn it into a formation of connate li fire... What will happen then?”","Lu Yun gave it some thought, but ultimately dismissed the idea. His current cultivation was insufficient for spending an entire month etching the runes for a combat art. Not to mention, the Connate Great Dao of the Five Elements was a heavenly dao art. He might not succeed even if he was an immortal himself.","“I should focus on how to refine the formation disk into a treasure...”"]},{"number":2298,"title":"Chapter 2298: Chapter 2198.1: Undercurrents","paragraphs":["Chapter 2198.1: Undercurrents","Lu Yun wasn’t the only cultivator who’d ever had the impulse to refine a formation disk into a treasure—it conveniently enabled one to deploy formations with a wave of their hand. At the same time, he was likely the only person who dared do so.","The creator of the formation disk seemed to have the same thought, but didn’t dare see it through. If the formation disk of a ninth rank formation exploded, it would destroy everything within five hundred kilometers.","Formation disks differed from treasures in that they needed to be arranged for ahead of time so they could absorb the energy of the elements and meld into the environment. It also took some time for a formation disk to activate.","Typically speaking, formation disks were just formations that could be moved elsewhere at any time. When Lu Yun utilized the Nineheavens Brahman Formation to kill Peng Yue, he first used the Connate Great Dao of the Five Elements to collect the origin elements. That was how he set up the formation in such a short period of time and operated the array.","This method was available only to him. No one else could manage it.","If formula dao was present...","Lu Yun’s cheek spasmed. He really wanted to bring formula dao into this world! But if he did, his suppressed memories would recover since formula dao was not of this time. The heavenly dao would be the first to destroy him then.","Heaving a sigh, Lu Yun called upon the Eye of Nullification. Connate li fire floated over his palm as he took out countless materials from his storage ring. He conducted a series of experiments to assimilate, distill, and otherwise study the connection between formation disks and treasures.","He stopped after a full day and night passed.","“A ninth rank formation is on par with an immortal weapon... If it’s fashioned into a treasure, that will inevitably affect the formation’s strength.” Lu Yun shook his head. He’d found a way to craft the formation disk into a treasure, but that would decrease the formation’s power. If the treasure’s rank was too high, it would also be too difficult to deploy its power.","Lu Yun sat cross-legged on the floor and settled into meditation.","“Hmm?” He brightened and took out the Forge of Heaven and Earth. The radiance of the five elements shimmered over his fingers as they flicked through hand seals.","BOOM.","The formation disk exploded into motes of scarlet radiance and flowed into the forge. The Forge of Heaven and Earth shuddered and absorbed all of the illumination, like a whale drinking water. Scintillating scarlet runes crept over the forge’s surface.","Lu Yun had destroyed the formation disk and used a special method to split out the formation’s attributions from the disk. He sent them into the Forge of Heaven and Earth so it would have the attributes of the Nineheavens Brahman Formation.","A cross forge was the heart of a cross ark, the equivalent of a cultivator’s nascent soul. His forge was an enhanced version. Since it was a hub of energy, all it needed was a sufficient amount spirit stones to release the formation from itself. It could even bring the full might of a ninth rank formation to bear.","......","Another day and night passed before Lu Yun’s fingers paused. The Forge of Heaven and Earth remained the same as before—one meter tall, deep blue throughout, and runes of five colors intersecting over its surface.","Thunder and lightning roared inside it while nine hundred and ninety-nine crimson dragons almost three hundred meters long snaked through the air. Due to the thunder and lightning inside the forge, these fire dragons also bore a hint of the power of thunder! It was a very pleasant surprise for Lu Yun.","“The Forge of Heaven and Earth isn’t a treasure, but that’s even better! Enormous true origin and cultivation is needed to wield a treasure. As long as I have sufficient spirit stones and spirit crystals, I’ll be able to utilize the full strength of the Forge of Heaven and Earth! I have an immortal weapon at my disposal.” A smile curved his lip.","Ai, it was something from his sealed memories again. Although the memories were sealed, the instincts of his soul could not be erased. The cross forge was an instinctive creation from the remnants of those memories.","This Forge of Heaven and Earth...","A typical cross forge required a corresponding cross ark to deploy its strength. The inside of his forge, however, contained the framework of the five elements. That made it possible to be independent of a cross ark’s existence.","With the Nineheavens Brahman Formation assimilated into it, it could also attack. As long as there was sufficient fuel to power it, it could bring the formation’s entire might to bear.","Lu Yun studied his creation with immense satisfaction before putting it back in his storage ring. He then dragged out Tie Shanhe’s nascent soul from the sword pagoda.","After all this time, the latter’s nascent soul was greatly shriveled. While there was a lower rank spirit vein inside the pagoda, his nascent soul was so firmly constrained by Lu Yun that it didn’t receive one iota of energy. He would fade away after a few days.","“So it was indeed you... who took Ashflame’s spirit vein... and you have a spatial treasure... that can store living beings...” Tie Shanhe weakly lifted his head, then realized something and quickly sat down cross-legged to absorb the qi in his surroundings.","Although only a nascent soul remained of him, his instinctive desire to live remained. There were three options available for a nascent soul. One, rebirth through possession. Two, become a wandering immortal. Three, find a treasure that could reshape a physical body for him.","Each option was exceedingly difficult.","“There is no future for you after killing Wuxi Mountain disciple Hui Chang, even with all these treasures,” Tie Shanhe said before Lu Yun had a chance to respond.","“Wuxi Mountain?” Lu Yun blinked. Hadn’t Peng Yue said he was from there as well? Who would’ve thought that Housekeeper Hui in Ashflame would be another one of their disciples?","Tie Shanhe smiled ruefully. “Even Great Xia’s titled kings don’t dare set themselves against Wuxi Mountain. You, a mere nascent soul cultivator, killed one of theirs. If they find out, you, your sect, and your family will be annihilated.”","“So what if I killed one of theirs? They’re just a Wuxi Mountain.” Lu Yun rummaged through his memories. He seemed to have heard this name when reincarnating through Great Xia. But back then, he’d been overlord of all and even the Human Emperor greeted him respectfully. Though he’d heard of Wuxi Mountain, Lu Yun hadn’t paid much attention to them then.","“Forget it, they’re not important.” He laid a restriction on Tie Shanhe’s nascent soul. “From now on, you are my gardener. Look after the spirit herbs in this area.”","“Um...” Tie Shanhe’s eyes widened and he stared dumbly at Lu Yun. “Are you not at all afraid of Wuxi Mountain?”","“Pfft.” Lu Yun curled his lip and ignored the man.","He’d set up a great number of restrictions in the seed storage formation of the secret vault. Tie Shanhe was able to walk around only in the spirit herb garden. He couldn’t reach any place else.","When Lu Yun saw the gray jiao napping next to the dragon egg in a pond, he couldn’t help but ask, “Senior, why don’t you refine the Hongmeng Fruit?”","It was placed next to the dragon egg, as if lending its aura to nurture the egg.","“Roar!” The jiao shook its head. Although it ardently wished for the fruit, it was in no hurry to refine it.","Lu Yun shook his head with resignation and took out another fruit, giving it to the gray jiao. “Senior, this junior’s family is about to face off against our enemy. There will be certain things that we request your help with, so it’s best if the senior recovers as soon as possible.”","The gray jiao’s head crashed into the water with absolute astonishment at the second fruit. It took a while for it to compose itself and accept it.","The young man had an endless supply of the sixth item of the ten heavenly treasures! Were these Hongmeng Spirit Fruit weeds by the side of the road?","Little did it know that Lu Yun only needed one fruit and a bit of time to study it if he wished to replicate its effects with other spirit herbs. Thus, he didn’t think too much of the heavenly and earth treasures.","Directly refining the Hongmeng Fruit meant that much of its medicinal effect would go to waste. Only when it was made into pills or spirit cuisine could it be fully utilized. Sadly, Lu Yun’s cultivation level was too low to process ingredients of this caliber.","Reforming medicinal properties was an entirely different matter from refining pills or cooking spirit cuisine. Only the method was needed for the former, whereas cultivation was also needed for the latter.","......","Terra Demon didn’t cause a disturbance when he emerged from seclusion. After two days, he was initial soul separation. Lu Yun relaxed when he saw that the Hongmeng Fruit had been fully refined.","Terra Demon’s strength underwent a complete change after obtaining the meaning of an immortal overlord from the fruit. Even his immortal king nascent soul was beginning to recover.","Kong Mengqian found Lu Yun as soon as he left the secret vault.","“Master, isn’t it time that you taught me something? Like how to use low level spirit herbs to cook immortal level spirit fare, and the Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragon!” The girl pouted as she grabbed Lu Yun’s arm. Goosebumps rose all over Lu Yun.","“Have you refined the bamboo that I gave you?” He raised his eyes to her face.","“No, not yet...” Her face spasmed when Lu Yun mentioned the bamboo.","“Refine it first. There’s three hundred and sixty-five restrictions on it. I will satisfy one request for each one you refine and teach you one thing.” The smiling young man freed his arm from Kong Mengqian’s grasp. Although the girl was only sixteen years old, her body was well developed. While Lu Yun was no upstanding gentleman of sound moral character, he wouldn’t take advantage of his own disciple.","Not to mention... he really wasn’t interested in other women.","Sky had sent down a gift when he accepted Kong Mengqian, indicating that the heavenly dao acknowledged this martial granddaughter.","“If you refine all three hundred and sixty-five, I’ll teach you anything you want.”"]},{"number":2299,"title":"Chapter 2299: Chapter 2198.2: Undercurrents","paragraphs":["Chapter 2198.2: Undercurrents","“Three hundred and sixty five restrictions... in an ordinary stick of bamboo? Is this what the sect uses to test disciples?” Kong Mengqian’s eyes shone with expectation. “Then you need to keep your word, master!”","She skipped off. Meanwhile, Lu Yun held his head. He probably should’ve taught his disciple how to respect others first, hmm?","“Maybe the issue’s with my cultivation. It’s so low that my disciple is more like a younger sister.”","“When do we begin, young master?” Terra Demon approached the young man. They were to destroy the true immortal in three days, of which two had passed.","Lu Yun tossed a storage ring to him. “Here are one hundred and eight Transfer Talismans that I refined over the past two days. They can be assembled into a talisman formation. Go place them where the true immortal is.”","Terra Demon left to carry out his orders. With the nascent soul of an immortal king and the fortification of the Hongmeng Fruit, a minor true immortal wouldn’t discover him if he set his mind to staying invisible.","Fighting a true immortal in the capital would level the entire city. Thus, Lu Yun wanted to move the man elsewhere first before killing him.","The only thing he was worried about was if the Origin Sect would send out higher level immortals against him. He could manage empyrean, true, and even august immortals. As immortals were divided into nine ranks, those three indicated lower rank immortals. But once a mid rank immortal appeared, Lu Yun’s hands would be tied. He’d have to flee with the entire family if that was the case.","......","The Zhao Clan, one of Darklake’s seven great families and oldest aristocracies.","Everyone of note in the family was gathered in the visitor’s hall, including representatives from the Yuwen and Yu Clans.","“What are your thoughts, Patriarch Zhao?” The patriarch of the Yuwen Clan, mid nascent soul Yuwen Zhi, merrily stroked his beard. “Patriarch Yu has already decided to give us Yu Shuai.”","“There is no room for discussion in this,” Zhao Hongtu shook his head. “Chenguang is my son. As useless as he is, he is still my son.”","“We don’t want his life,” Yuwen Zhi chuckled. “Plus, your son is already golden core, isn’t he? Golden core at less than twenty years of age... and that is someone useless in your view!”","“Zhao Hongtu’s son is Zhao Hongtu’s son! He will not be one of your bargaining chips, no matter what!” The Zhao patriarch’s cold snort indicated the end of the matter.","“Brother Zhao, wise are those who recognize the times we’re in!” Patriarch Yu Chengze on the other side tried to convince his friend. “Seniors from the Nineheavens Pavilion have already arrived and it is the end of the road for the Lu Clan. Chenguang and Shuai’er will only be guests at the Yuwens’ for a few days, nothing will happen to them...”","“Shut up!” Zhao Hongtu sneered. “Yu Chengze, how dare you run your mouth when you can’t even protect your own son? Seniors from the Nineheavens Pavilion? The Nineheavens Pavilion of the Dark Orchid Empire has already been razed to the ground by a combination powerhouse! The ones here are defeated losers!”","Yu Chengze shut his mouth as Yuwen Zhi’s expression cooled. The latter closed his eyes and spoke no more. An awkward atmosphere descended on the scene.","A Zhao servant suddenly ran in. “Senior elder, the matter is done. Young master Chenguang has been delivered to the Yuwen Clan.”","“What?!” Zhao Hongtu surged to his feet. “What did you say?!”","The servant ignored Zhao Hongtu and remained looking at the highest ranked senior on the other side, Zhao Lingyue.","“Hongtu, you are no longer suited to be the patriarch. Upon deliberations by the council of elders, we have removed you from your position. The family will be overseen by the council from henceforth.” Zhao Lingyue was a very old man with white hair and so many wrinkles crossing his face that his skin looked like shriveled bark. But it was this latter nascent soul elder whose cultivation was second only to Zhao Hongtu.","“Hongtu, you are indeed unfit to be patriarch.” More people walked in after the elder spoke. They were all soul projection powerhouses—the heavyweights of the Zhao Clan who’d joined Dark Orchid after breaking through.","Their speaker was Zhao Hongtu’s grandfather, Zhao Lingfei.","“Grandfather, you...”","“Greetings to the patriarch!” Zhao Lingyue and the other elders rose to their feet and bowed in unison.","“Despite his average potential, Zhao Chenguang was able to successively break through in a short period of time and form his golden core. There must be a reason for anything out of the ordinary. This matter must be fully investigated,” Zhao Lingfei said coldly. “Additionally, Lu Tianling of the Lu Clan is controlling the emperor and seeks to overthrow Darklake Empire. Such a viciously ambitious character should be hunted down by all! We Zhaos will naturally not shirk our duty.”","Yu Chengze smiled ruefully at the stunned Zhao Hongtu. The same circumstances had taken place with him as well, but the seniors of his clan didn’t strip him of his patriarch position. They’d only forced him to submit.","For clans such as the Yus and Zhaos, someone broke through to soul projection once every thousand years and was brought to Dark Orchid Empire.","Today, these family seniors returned to their original clans and immediately assumed the reins of power. The position of family patriarch had long been turned into a mere figurehead. Not only did the seniors of the Yu and Zhao Clans return, but so did those of the Ouyang, Yuwen, Ling Clans, and even Darklake royalty!","“Grandfather, Marshal Lu Tianling has rendered great deeds to the nation and committed no faults. The battle of Tiger Suppression Pass twenty years ago...”","“Shut up!” Zhao Lingfe sneered. “You do not need to speak of these things and you no longer need to worry about family affairs. Focus on cultivation and break through to soul projection so you can follow me to Dark Orchid.","“Zhao Lingyue, you will handle the family’s affairs from now on.”","“Yes, senior patriarch!” The elder hastily bowed.","“Why do I feel like this isn’t a very nice course of action?” rang a clear voice. Light flurried in front of the assembly’s eyes as a young man dressed in long ivory robes walked in through the door.","“Who are you?” Zhao Lingfei frowned at the newcomer.","“Lu Yun?” Yuwen Zhi recognized the young man and subconsciously rose to his feet.","“So you are Lu Tianling’s grandson? Good timing, this saves me some time.” Zhao Lingfei reached out a hand to grab Lu Yun’s head.","The young man snorted and waved his in return, sending the old man flying with a wave of dense qi.","Bam!","The hall shook when Zhao Lingfei stopped. He was embedded in the wall.","“I should be the one saying that. Since you’re all gathered together, this saves me some time.” Lu Yun curled his lip and smiled at Zhao Hongtu. “My late arrival has caused Uncle Zhao some suffering.","The others on the scene sucked in sharp breaths to see Lu Yun casually rebuff the mid soul projection Zhao Lingfei. Zhao Hongtu, however, was unperturbed. “Please spare my family’s seniors, young master Lu.”","“But of course,” Lu Yun waved off his concerns. “I will not touch the Zhao and Lu Clan out of consideration for Chenguang and Yu Shuai.”","Zhao Hongtu breathed out more easily upon hearing this, while Yu Chengze looked at his fellow figurehead with bafflement.","“But the Yuwens must die. I said I would exterminate their bloodline if there was a single hair missing from my second uncle’s head. I, Lu Yun, am a man of my words.” He turned a cutting glare at Yuwen Zhi.","“You...” The man was flabbergasted. If the mid soul projection Zhao Lingfei was no match for the young man, then a latter nascent soul cultivator would just be a baby to Lu Yun!","Hum!","Lu Yun formed a massive hand from Hongmeng qi with a push of his hand and smacked Yuwen Zhi into a cloud of bloody mist.","The Yu and Yuwen Clans gaped; Zhao Lingfei struggling down from the wall was also horrified. Smacking a latter nascent soul cultivator into bloody mist with one slap?","Not even latter soul projection powerhouses could manage such a feat!","Meanwhile, Zhao Hongtu was as pale as a sheet. He inwardly celebrated that he’d visited Immortal Burial Valley a few months ago and personally witnessed Terra Demon holding off one hundred thousand immortals.","Otherwise, he would’ve made the same decision as Yu Chengze this time.","Lu Yun swiftly dispatched the rest of the Yuwen clan members who’d come with Yuwen Zhi.","“Uncle Zhao, Uncle Yu, it would be best to not let your family walk around too much these days. Your clans do not have the right to participate in the upcoming turmoil, and you may face annihilation if you do not handle the situation properly.” Lu Yun swept a look at Zhao Hongtu. “I will save Chenguang and Yu Shuai.”","He turned left without a trace.","“Was that... really Lu Yun?” Yu Chengze swallowed hard.","“Of course it was. If it wasn’t for a trip I made to Immortal Burial Valley and seeing their steward hold off one hundred thousand immortals by himself, including a few awakened powerhouses... I would’ve made the same decision as you,” Zhao Hongtu chuckled ruefully. “To think that young master Lu would also be a heavyweight so far ahead that we are unable to look upon him!”","“What?!” Yu Chengze’s eyes went round. “One versus one hundred thousand? Isn’t that the ability of real immortals? The Lus have an immortal with them...”","......","Lu Yun visited the Yus after leaving the Zhaos and found that Zhao Chenguang and Yu Shuai were indeed missing. They’d been taken to the Yuwen Clan.","He didn’t care about the situation at the Yu Clan. If it wasn’t for Yu Shuai, he wouldn’t be bothered with this family. They knew his stance, so it was up to them how they handled it.","In either case, he wasn’t planning on sitting around. He was going to counterattack the Yuwen Clan.","“Brother Ouyang, long time no see.” When Lu Yun arrived at the Ouyang Clan, he found Ouyang Shengtian being harassed by some family elders.","“Hahaha, well met young master Lu!” Ouyang Shengtian heaved a long sigh of relief to see Lu Yun. “Help me settle these old guys.”","“There’s no rush,” Lu Yun waved a hand. “Bring me all the spirit stones in your family vaults, I’m borrowing them and will return them after the fact.”"]},{"number":2300,"title":"Chapter 2300: Chapter 2199.1: Emptying the Nation’s Coffers","paragraphs":["Chapter 2199.1: Emptying the Nation’s Coffers","“What?” Ouyang Shengtian’s eyes shot wide open. “All of the Ouyang spirit stones?”","“Shengtian, who is he? Why can he barge into the family’s heartland without prior report?!” demanded an elder with a goatee.","“Should I kill the old guy?” Lu Yun raised his hand with a smirk.","“Don’t!” Ouyang Shengtian shook his head rapidly. “Great grandfather, just ignore this. Young master Lu Yun is my friend...”","“What?? He’s that good-for-nothing Lu Yun?” Ouyang Biegui huffed and puffed, glaring at the newcomer. “You’re the one who wasted old brother Lu’s family foundations!”","“Huh?” Lu Yun was very confused. The Lu and Ouyang Clan had been arch rivals before Ouyang Shengtian became who he was. But the Ouyang soul projection forefather from Dark Orchid called Lu Tianling... old brother Lu?","What was going on?","“Your grandfather once saved my great grandfather’s life. Although my great grandfather broke through and headed to Dark Orchid, he never forgot this great debt of gratitude. When he detected that the soul projection cultivators of the Yuwen, Ling, Zhao, and Yu Clans were traveling back to Darklake, he decided to come as well.” Ouyang Shengtian smiled ruefully.","“...My grandfather saved the Ouyang forefather’s life... so the Ouyang Clan decided to destroy my Lu Clan?” This was the last possible turn of events on Lu Yun’s mind.","“Hmph! I would kill Ouyang Baitian and Ouyang Baiyi myself if those two were still alive,” Ouyang Biegui snorted.","“Don’t be angry, great grandfather. Aren’t the Ouyangs and Lus allies now?” Ouyang Shengtian quickly mollified. The “great grandfather” term was rolling more easily off his tongue.","“Hmph!” harrumphed a livid Ouyang Biegui.","“Alright, set that aside for now. Lend me all of the Ouyang spirit stones.”","“Um...” Ouyang Shengtian and his great grandfather looked at each other.","“Alright, I will!” The Ouyang young master decided after brief hesitation. He sent his men to the vaults and took out all of the family’s spirit stones. He’d long consolidated power over the entire clan, a fact that did not change with Ouyang Biegui’s return.","The Ouyang family wealth was immensely impressive after accumulating for thousands of years. They took out thirty million upper rank spirit stones for Lu Yun to use!","Thirty million upper rank spirit stones were the equivalent of three hundred thousand paramount spirit stones. It was an incredible feat for a family of a third rank cultivation empire to possess such riches!","Lu Yun accepted the stones without a pretense of courtesy. He scanned the storage ring that Ouyang Shengtian gave him and threw it into his own, leaving without a word.","After his departure, both Ouyang Shengtian and Ouyang Biegui quieted down.","......","Darklake Empire’s royal palace sat in the heart of the capital. It occupied one hundred and fifty kilometers. Magnificent and spectacular, it was the core of the nation’s power.","It was under heavy guard at the moment with one sentry every three steps and a patrol every five. All of its countless formations operated and none of the maids, eunuchs, or even royal descendants could freely walk around.","“The royal family of any cultivation empire is not to be underestimated.” Lu Yun easily penetrated the palace given that he was protected by talismans of the connate five elements. As he stood at the peak of mid nascent soul, he could break through to latter nascent soul at any time. It was also much easier for him to utilize the connate five elements in creating talismans.","The Eye of Nullification scanned everything within fifty kilometers. But everytime he used it, he was reminded of another art of the eye. It was very similar, with the difference of his being far inferior.","That art could read the information of life and death.","The great formation of the palace rivaled the array of ten in Ashflame City of Dark Orchid Empire. Even soul projection powerhouses would have an unpleasant time if they barged in.","Great changes occurred after Darklake royalty returned from Dark Orchid. Emperor Situ Wenxian was confined to his quarters and Lu Yun’s good friend Situ Yun also lost his personal freedom.","Crown Prince Situ Jie was acting regent and wielded sole authority, but he was also a puppet. The seniors of the family held the true reins of power.","Lu Yun dove into the earth beneath the palace and traveled through it with a shimmer of hazy yellow light over his body.","“Here we are, this is the place.” He burrowed out from the ground, arriving in front of the national coffers of Darklake Empire, the sum total of its wealth. No single clan or sect could compare to a government. The country reigned supreme and its subjects were too numerous to be counted.","Darklake Empire had existed for nearly ten thousand years. What kind of wealth would there be after this period of accumulation?!","The national coffers were a massive seed storage formation, each of its one hundred kilometers partitioned into different areas.","“My my my, there’s more than thirty million paramount spirit stones and some hundred million upper rank stones...” Lu Yun grinned toothily. The formations here were so domineering that any other nascent soul cultivator would already be eviscerated.","“Who dares trespass in the empire’s treasury?!” An angry roar echoed as a man in white appeared with a flash of sword light.","“Uncle Wu, it’s me, Lu Yun.” Lu Yun smiled merrily at the man.","“Young master? You..” Wu Wei gaped at Lu Yun, not knowing what to say. He was a member of the royal family’s secret force—the Hidden Dragons—and assigned to the vaults.","“The Hidden Dragons haven’t been exposed, have they?” Lu Yun asked.","“No,” Wu Wei shook his head. “His Majesty immediately scattered the Hidden Dragons to various locales when he detected something amiss in the capital. The enemy has not noticed our existence.”","Lu Yun nodded, not knowing what his grandfather had done to hide some cultivators from the heavenly book. Dark Orchid was completely in the dark that Darklake Empire possessed a troop of soul projection powerhouses.","If the heavenly book couldn’t detect it, then the true immortal in Dark City was even less likely to realize unless the Hidden Dragons stood in front of him one by one.","Emperor Situ Wenxian possessed keen instincts and was ready before the various clan elders returned from Dark Orchid. He dispersed the Hidden Dragons to appear as if he was under house arrest.","“That’s good,” Lu Yun nodded.","“Ah yes, what are you doing here, young master?”","“I need spirit stones!” Lu Yun responded seriously. “All of the spirit stones in the nation’s vaults!”","“Um...” Wu Wei frowned slightly. “Is this the marshal’s command?”","“No,” Lu Yun shook his head. “Don’t ask further about this, Uncle Wu. I have great use for them.”","“Very well then!” Wu Wei nodded. Although the spirit stones in the vaults were quite important, Darklake Empire teetered on the brink of disaster. A single misstep could lead to the nation’s fall, such as exposure of the Hidden Dragons. Dark Orchid’s retaliation would be sure and brutal if it learned of a vassal nation’s secret cache of soul projection heavyweights. It might even declare war on Darklake through another vassal nation.","If such a situation developed, then Darklake would not survive being beset by all sides.","Lu Tianling’s original plan was to slowly develop in the shadows and turn the Hidden Dragons into a contingent of cultivators who were at least soul separation. He hadn’t imagined that the Human Emperor of Great Xia would disturb the heavenly book and negate its power over the realm!","Wu Wei formed a hand seal and released all of the formations in the vaults. “Young master, those traitors will sooner or later turn their sights toward the vaults. You might as well take everything in it so it won’t end up in their hands.”","A nation’s fortune was so vast that all of the spirit stones, rare treasures, and pills were innumerable. It totaled two hundred million paramount rank spirit stones!","Lu Yun gestured with his fingers without another word and sent out the sword pagoda from his dantian. His cultivation was so low that he couldn’t utilize the sword pagoda’s true strength—he could only use it as a spatial treasure.","Regardless, spatial treasures were very rare in worlds of cultivation as their refinement process was too complicated. One needed to gather the power of the five elements and use them to manifest space. Only premier master refiners could forge such treasures.","While there was space inside Lu Yun’s Forge of Heaven and Earth, it was filled with the power of thunder and lightning, as well as the Nineheavens Brahman Formation. It wasn’t a spatial treasure because the forge wasn’t a treasure at all.","The sword pagoda swiftly expanded in the vaults and turned into a massive tower three hundred meters tall. Not a particle of dust remained in the vaults one hundred kilometers across after a round of terrifying suction force.","Wu Wei’s jaw dropped. He’d taken out some storage rings and was ready to help, but the young master had needed only three dozen breaths to empty the treasury!"]}]);
